camssa:8a020f01-dca2-4bbc-beb4-59d639c1c0e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There is a reference study on the de facto implementation of the EIF components. In this study, the\r
specification's effiency is not totally addressed, due mainly to the lack of dedicated resources. Nonetheless, there are assessments produced by arbitrary stakeholders (public representatives) from different Member\r
States directly addressing the specification's efficiency (see 'EIF evaluation and strategy' initiative), although\r
these ones are not finely structured.\r
\r
EIF components evaluation, page 8:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/29d694d4-4696-11ec-89db-01aa75ed71a1/languageen\r
\r
EIF evaluation and strategy, Feedback section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/law/better-regulation/have-your-say/initiatives/12579-European-Interoperability-\r
Framework-EIF-evaluation-and-EU-governments-interoperability-strategy\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e91ed99-dd26-436c-a497-fe116726a8c3 .

camssa:8b2a28d8-6120-4019-baf0-ceeea5fffab7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISA and ISA2 Programmes have been promoting the creation of domain-specific and cross-sectorial\r
communities, openly creating and sharing their results within the European Union. There are two relevant\r
assets coming from this community: the ISA2 Action Plan and the final study on the ISA2 Programme\r
Evaluation, where attention was made to analyse and highlight which goals and achievements have been\r
accomplished.\r
\r
ISA2 Programme reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en\r
\r
ISA2 Programme Action reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/actions/improving-digital-skills-public-sector_en\r
\r
ISA2 Programme evaluation, final study report, page 47:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/news/study-supporting-final-evaluation-isa%C2%B2-programme-now-available_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c5efe37-d1ef-4267-bcf8-6493d76ab52c .

