camssa:9ed1ae98-423f-4d23-baf6-a4fefc53712b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The EIF specification started in 2004, and up to date constitutes the most relevant interoperability\r
programme of the European Union. Every year Member States publish their National Interoperability\r
Frameworks (NIF) with regards to the EIF recommendations. Therefore, this specification is wide-spread\r
used.\r
\r
EIF first release, 'European Interoperability Framework for eGovernment Services' document:\r
http://www.dlorg.eu/uploads/External%20Publications/\r
\r
NIF reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/nifo_en\r
\r
ISA2 Programme (EIF major releases):\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/actions/continuously-updating-european-interoperability-strategy_en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01ac9c61-c8e0-4c9b-b20d-dfb70609b88d .

