camssa:013d0d58-316b-4926-8599-d3fa25b3da43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of CSV is not related to security and privacy of the data exchange. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47dadbd4-e0d9-48cf-a9c1-e0dd94c007e6 .

camssa:01424e99-dacb-44f3-84b3-3a2fbce8e743 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "\"The publiccode.yml specification can indeed be associated with the European Interoperability Reference Architecture (EIRA) building blocks, particularly those related to metadata and data models. As a structured metadata schema for public sector software, publiccode.yml aligns with EIRA's Metadata Management and Data Model building blocks (and potentially others), which support the standardised description and interoperability of digital resources across public administrations. By providing a common model for software documentation, publiccode.yml enhances data discoverability, exchange, and reuse, all essential for effective interoperability within the EIRA framework.\""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b9ce2a5-df5c-419b-b5bf-4f743c11441d .

