camssa:02e6f4da-f8f0-493c-a078-893fda153afb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Although the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification does not make any reference to interoperability issues, the CEN/TC 428 results are aligned with different models and frameworks, and attention has been paid to ensure that these relationships are well defined and published. For example, according to Joinup's Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation, an update of EN-16234-1 e-CF is in progress, which is intended to add references to the SFIA (Skills Framework for the Information Age) model.\r
\r
Joinup-2021 Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation reference, Education, Digital skills and Digital learning section:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/education-digital-skills-and-digital-learning\r
\r
Skills Framework for the Information Age (SFIA) reference:\r
https://www.sfia-online.org/en?msclkid=3c1ee036b64d11ec990d0b2d87d7154a\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5981fdd3-0387-4d1f-ac1b-a0bd2b9d3266 .

