        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "81.05%AssessmentScoreAverage",
        "84.44%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:0313cc2b-f9e7-41d7-b188-3f8b97e777f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The roles, state and properties that are defined in this specification do not form a complete web language or
format. The implementation of WAI-ARIA relies on the context of a host language, like HTML, and can be
partially implemented.

WAI-ARIA Authoring Practice reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices/

WAI-ARIA User Agent Implementation Guide:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-implementation/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e2a8d60-9c30-45b8-a25d-4d7677ebdadc .

camssa:0313ed4a-87e2-4e99-ade1-e2156f3126ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0317ca4b-e048-4063-b1de-74da0d9f7615 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL allows for flexibility in implementing web services. Service providers can choose which operations and features to implement based on their specific requirements. It can define the messages, port types, bindings, and service elements that make up the service contract. However, it does not mandate the inclusion or implementation of every defined operation or feature.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53862953-8ef9-418e-b821-aa9393378bf0 .

