camssa:032e935b-5a15-4d0e-ab74-2b50b907e4e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the OpenTelemetry specification itself does not directly simplify the delivery of European public services, it provides essential tools and practices for enhancing the observability, reliability, and performance of digital systems underlying these services. OpenTelemetry can improve the delivery of public services as monitoring telemetry data can help improve the systems used to provide citizens with public services.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7904e4f-967c-4f14-b2e6-543402e1d890 .

camssa:03307f65-5377-41df-8bbd-5444994120e7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03366ffa-0bc1-4814-a721-f2e1a5048bbf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:0337dfe7-6eab-4c7c-b623-93af68e8913f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML last update was in the 2000s and is compatible with the way browsers renders HTML5, aside from
that the specification might hinder the implementation of CSS and other component that improves the
accessibility of users with disabilities. XHTML does not ensure compliance with accessibility standards, such
as WAI-ARIA. XHTML does not include features like proper semantic elements, alternative text for images,
and ARIA roles, which prevents it from any type of adaptation.

Moreover, the Regional Government of Bizkaia developed his website to promote the integration of groups
with disabilities into the Public Administration of Bizkaia. This organisation used XHTML 1.0
recommendations and CSS2.

XHTML 1.0 implemented in e-accessability project:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/einclusion/document/eaccesibility-public-administrationbizkaia-bizkaianet

WAI-ARIA Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/

CSS2 Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2683773a-a2cd-4a44-ba75-98aa0485da92 .

camssa:033c8ad3-1adf-4544-bccf-60e8d8c13f13 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0340383e-e9e8-462a-a8bf-28a9f2622da7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-73a8058bec757a2fdb0f8513c2f11841e982cbef76c3be82af67707c294da8b8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:034239f6-96f8-43f1-a2cd-4bd583f2a58e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:465fd844-45ef-48a8-80e5-ee8f8ad43849 .

camssa:034c1bd3-125f-4a1c-be67-c3298116f602 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:034e9970-54f5-45da-bf18-02bf1590629a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS classification is not dependent on any other specification, operating system or web platform; therefore, NUTS is platform-agnostic.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cebfe30-d88b-481e-9ad2-45bcc21fcd9a .

camssa:034fd5e3-8cc6-4cd7-b2b3-c962db24f3a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the NFV home page, services are deployed by complementing Software Defined Networking (SDN) and NFVI. The NFVI specification highly recommends to adopt other protocols for security and other function aspects. Therefore, NFVI is not technology-agnostic.\r
\r
NFV reference: \r
https://www.etsi.org/technologies/nfv/nfv\r
\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c18670b3-2c81-46c1-b85a-f390a1553254 .

camssa:0357075e-acba-4b1d-aa28-24b2c3b9459c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:035da302-4161-4ecf-9245-8655708c7de2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:036387ac-ba89-43e2-a66b-a4f8c97e3332 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After carrying out research on the efficiency and effectiveness of PNG, no study or documentation assessing the specification has been found to justify this criterion. \r
However, there are many articles comparing PNG with JPG characteristics in terms of effectiveness and efficiency, for example:\r
\r
JPEG vs. PNG:\r
https://www.digitaltrends.com/photography/jpeg-vs-png/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac299c42-3f63-4eda-a5fc-2d461896f65a .

camssa:036be90d-04f2-4a91-9ec7-2fcaac7091ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, NUTS can define the interoperability aspects of the Controlled Vocabulary ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110					'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b41b521-da93-4f43-aa9c-a3a337f6a989 .

camssa:0372967d-46a5-4728-be52-5133daca7c85 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:0373e705-6939-4524-85b7-154b670713c1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0375e3f4-07e0-4273-953d-1a77df8c095c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:037740d5-3110-4851-bd31-c83916b31597 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cce03af6-5694-474b-a402-a68ba59c75a0 .

camssa:0377eff2-fa5b-4f4a-8708-a6f02efa6299 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTP is not related to  e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff1b19b5-cbd3-413d-846c-df3a06228202 .

camssa:0379e7bb-a5b4-42f4-870a-cc35aac0c105 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA enhances the interoperability capabilities of multiple components, as the specification describes well-defined messages and protocols in different use cases. This allows components from different vendors to be combined and services to be managed seamlessly.\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Artifact Processing and creating Portable Service Templates section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969502'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:90f3eba0-28b3-40a9-8082-37e23042e825 .

camssa:037d9711-0d77-4b1d-aac4-5c01bf4e6fd5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-aa6ea51e02f049efbd153499fb071e07c5f49ba6a0343203440380497057d70e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:037e134e-9487-4355-8ca6-e8e89010aa4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS is not a European Standard as it is not mentioned in any European-level open repository nor catalogue. \r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6eabd5d0-4e2a-468b-8f84-33a8a36604d4 .

camssa:037fdce6-cbae-4175-8e4b-37b5aa8bca71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XACML specification primarily focuses on providing a framework for fine-grained access control, which 
indirectly contributes to the secure exchange of data. However, it does not directly address the mechanics of 
data exchange such as encryption, secure transmission protocols, or data integrity.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d331c2c5-4e23-42e7-adff-84b9298a119f .

camssa:03860d4e-c649-4d28-8738-91ce73ada6ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not allow any extension to be made.\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fcad67d-2add-488d-bb58-42c177b8af49 .

camssa:038689f9-0334-46f0-8802-d802612b799a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8954ddabf37f4899562b9ea4c8f0bbf204f3e48c9203043bc231f368092396a2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:0388aaaa-a404-4923-9f0b-cb20bd3124dc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While MIME itself does not provide means to enable access control mechanisms, they can always be implemented at the email server, application or network level.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5873c8b-d5cf-4145-a7af-480ea760b829 .

camssa:038988f9-3ca3-491b-bf8e-ee93510fe29c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:038c5bb2-6dbc-464d-ba46-3e7c6dce08a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """MIME is being used to specify the media types supported by the Europeana collections. Europeana is a cultural initiative that works towards the preservation of the patrimonial heritage. \r
\r
Europeana Media Types: \r
https://pro.europeana.eu/about-us/mission"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb9891eb-4af9-4fb7-9de9-2312872b9516 .

camssa:039a32b2-164a-4d2b-b80a-f2d5ff3ef860 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:039cff7c-5d5f-4d66-8b01-53a9d50d18d9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03a090cd-902b-4257-947f-3515a098bdb4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ISO 369-2 is intended to server as a code to identify a language name. Although this collection can be mapped against this same collection to test the specification's implementation conformance, the specification does not publicly provide conformance testing requirements (see ISO 639 reference); the user may opt for their own techniques or for third-party software conformance services. \r
\r
ISO 639-2 reference:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#13\r
\r
ISO 639 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/4767.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9246390b-041b-43f8-9ea6-0fac66494c2c .

camssa:03a4f86e-6caa-4aac-baf9-73595df7b0d3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML5 is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, HTML5 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Human Interface" and "Representation" ABBs from the EIRA Semantic and Technical views.\r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54433662-8666-4c34-8a9f-b41682435173 .

camssa:03ab9e22-c4a7-47fb-91f2-848f6e7d307f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03ac9ad4-e35a-427a-8e75-87f09a4ccdde a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03af1042-435c-430b-a73c-8732faa1c74a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData follows REST principles and there exists some kind of data protection, but it is not an integral part of the specification. In this sense the specification relies on the security considerations of the HTTP specification.

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832

HTTP specification security considerations:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-9 '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e97e165-d40b-43ce-96ef-932ba08484db .

camssa:03b729e0-d38c-4dc3-bc94-618960eb6208 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f41cca0d171e6f64dbc2bdeae9fbc87f2ea51ac00185b22114d59ab8a06e78d0 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:03ba6aee-903a-42d6-8921-74eafb97076d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:03c0c3b1-c5a9-4f5a-baf8-d625737326b0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:03c8b152-ecdc-42dd-a983-6cf472e9ae0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DCAT-AP specification has a section on which multilingual aspects are covered. This section provides a mechanism for  indicating the language(s) in which the metadata is available. This is done using the ""dct:language"" property, which can be used to specify the language(s) of the metadata, and also provides guidance on hou to use language tags in metadata fields.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4715a6d4-7ac6-406c-80dc-21fb8ff56c0e .

camssa:03cdabbf-ec5b-463b-8801-cc55e227b6fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As an internet standard, IPv4 promotes a common framework for communication. This can help facilitate agreements between organisations to define a unique method for communicating. Moreover, the IPsec protocol allows organisations to share information safely.

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c584422-79a4-4892-aed3-c1b0123de4d4 .

camssa:03d639bd-d7ab-418c-b6dd-290427d86d49 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03d87ad5-78ce-4fbd-bc84-a9163765e3ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard is designed to be implemented and used in any domain, allowing its usability in different sectors and applications. In this context, AES is designed to protect data; thus, the standard can be implemented to protect data of any type.

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6630176-76c3-48e6-be53-184fce2ef56a .

camssa:03da57a3-4f59-4633-9539-72e01e9155bd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03de8cfb-64ea-4d2c-a344-b5f6eed11c60 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03e0387f-a565-4b97-b638-aa866183b432 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML allows for partial implementations as long as users meet key requirements. In comparison to
HTML5, XHTML requires a much more structured document which adds difficulties when performing partial
implementations.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/#C_2'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d633a01b-377a-43d2-a884-b10deaa5efa7 .

camssa:03e4c668-6fbe-4ef8-9fcc-e27883e4223d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is a protocol focused on the transaction of data involved in the email exchange. Even though it is related to data exchange, and it is aimed to ensure the delivery within email services, it is not involved in data portability amongst systems fostering the European Public Services."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2395f0c8-c64c-493f-82b8-6735ef36857d .

camssa:03e800d5-3e7b-47ac-a4e1-93dd2e191183 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:03eec8a0-ce0c-4129-bfe9-790f38f32876 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DID Rotation project refers to the process of updating or changing a Decentralized Identifier (DID) while maintaining the continuity and integrity of the digital identity it covers. This procedure is essential for various reasons, including enhancing security, adhering to emerging standards, or transitioning to a more sophisticated infrastructure. This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program.

DID Rotation project:
https://www.ownyourdata.eu/en/did-rotation/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2a97b2a-e66e-41ef-bb74-6540211720d5 .

camssa:03ef8d2a-7299-463c-94b5-e1b2245bd8ee a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:03f11e8f-b52b-4508-a815-c942b0e6e448 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

