camssa:04153fac-b1af-4ebe-902c-829283a451f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Syslog is not designed specifically for modeling business processes. Syslog's primary purpose is to facilitate 
the transmission and storage of log messages, typically related to system events, errors, or activities. It doesn't provide the necessary features or structures for representing business processes in a visual or diagrammatic way.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4bb8116f-7896-4197-87da-e528bdf01c26 .

camssa:041af2d8-abeb-41ab-a960-42e9de6686ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No royalties are to be paid for the usage of the specification.\r
XBRL GL was developed by an international consortium with a major focus on financial regulators and\r
administrators; the specifications are freely licensed and royalty free. The only restrictions are those imposed\r
by XBRL’s intellectual property policies and trademark rules.\r
\r
https://xbrl.us/home/about/legal/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d928cc6e-c848-4c5f-acca-c2baa0b8fca2 .

camssa:041dd943-bbfd-420a-be9f-c12fd7923232 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Every new version of the specification goes through a defined process with open and public consultations. Request for comments are not restricted to the RDA members but are open to all."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3cfb75dd-0632-4e43-8def-6ed491f9d08b .

camssa:041e3888-3e5e-4049-8dc9-5f6590f2aa9e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not allow any kind of customisation.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5263ce85-7040-466f-a49c-61e90cfbd26b .

camssa:04214bef-31df-4494-888f-5bceeeb64663 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData services return URLs to identify resources that may be later requested by clients. Where possible, data reusability increases by exploiting the information found in the route part of the URL, or by easing datasets management. However, data reusability might be limited. There is no evidence of any European solution confirming this aspect.

OData reference on extensibility:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358848'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d697ae3-cdce-4935-9529-802a8a48b19a .

camssa:0421a34c-b738-44eb-92f6-a2941b5f3a8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is tied up to REST APIs communication. Although the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) service declares its own data model in a machine-readable form, which allows customers to interact with the service on a generic basis, the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) relies on REST APIs in order to be implemented.
In this sense the specification has some dependencies on some data formats used by the AAS, mainly with the OPC UA format, that is present in other specifications that usually are implemented along the main one. 
So, the specification is not technology agnostic.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b0ae8fd-2e89-45d8-8568-528a999ae151 .

camssa:04234b1e-aa62-4f2c-bac0-e819b06faa4e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NUTS classification has been developed by a lage community within the European Commission (EC) and all the EC patents are available with any restrictions related to royalty-free basis.\r
\r
EC reference, Regulation (EC) No 1059/2003 document:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1405939838475&uri=CELEX:32003R1059'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f985485-3c53-46a3-acae-94893f9276e0 .

