camssa:0440bcf1-2fbc-41d5-ac41-abf38c00e39f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification can enable mechanisms to ensure that data has not been modified and that it is accurately transferred between public administrations or organisations and citizens. In this context, the specification supports authentication methods that enable data encryption and ensure that data has not been modified since its initial form when sent by the sender. In addition, there are some mechanisms such as message authentication code (MAC), which allow for checking whether data has been altered while in transit. This mechanisms can help to enhance data accuracy and guarantee that transferred data is the same as that sent by the original entity.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

AH and ESP protocols:
https://netseccloud.com/ah-vs-esp-understanding-the-core-differences-in-ipsec-protocols

Message Authentication Code mechanism:
https://www.twingate.com/blog/ipsec'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58fcb2f5-d326-4abd-8432-265e203fdef7 .

