camssa:05cbe3eb-5c53-491f-82d8-2f52d832d302 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL has been used in several use cases developed in the context of data protection related solutions as \r
SPECIAL (Scalable Policy-aware Linked Data Architecture For Privacy, Transparency and Compliance), an \r
H2020 European project which involves ODRL for compliance check.\r
\r
Approaches for GDPR compliance utilising Semantic Web: \r
https://harshp.com/research/publications/035-representing-activities-processing-personal-data-consent\\x02semweb-gdpr-compliance\r
\r
SPECIAL Deliverable: \r
https://www.specialprivacy.eu/images/documents/SPECIAL_D17_M17_V10.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c48f2b2a-cc17-48f8-aa0f-847c276c7cbd .

camssa:05ccd762-7e61-4698-998f-f486326e9d73 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Standards are developed by groups of experts called technical committees. These experts are put forward by ISO’s national members. If a user interested in getting involved, they ought to contact their national standards body. Companies and individuals are not eligible to join ISO as members.\r
\r
ISO Technical committees: https://www.iso.org/get-involved.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:799a359c-5d3f-4fb5-8f7d-8c006140c9ab .

camssa:05d326a5-848c-489b-bc95-cd01e9046112 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OpenTelemetry is developed by the Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF), an organisation based in the US that hosts and promotes open source projects for cloud native computing. Moreover, OTel does not appear in any of the main European standard development bodies, therefore, the specification is not a European standard.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cfd84edb-8aa6-46a1-942f-8882032b912c .

