camssa:06822fa5-b532-49c9-8533-f1dc7f200f86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of the specification aims to foster interoperability between public administrations and cross-border exchange of wheat-related data. \r
Although the specification is not applicable to several business domains, the several implementations are evidence that there is a need for the exchange of wheat-related data across borders.\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0979912-3424-4ced-92a3-2088ac1b93fc .

camssa:068a4cd3-2304-4f6d-a31f-0516e43c7c68 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WS-Security is a SOAP extension, concequently it cannot be reusable for other purposes."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe480879-5e87-4164-a8c5-4618379e7d09 .

camssa:06912017-4fc2-4724-bd97-f0adf786ddbc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching through different catalogues, no evidence of the Extensible Forms Description Language specification being included in the catalogue of any Member State was found.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef5cc242-81bc-44c7-a65f-e3dc9ad9a066 .

camssa:069dbce5-eb7c-46b0-9c84-25535e9e3fa8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ebXML RegRep is an enabler of digital service delivery channels as the specification contributes to the adoption of Collaboration Protocol Agreements (CPA), which describes how trading partners engage in electronic business collaborations through the exchange of electronic messages (see OASIS CPA reference).\r
\r
Open source CPA toolkit reference:\r
http://ebxml.xml.org/news/open-source-cpa-toolkit\r
\r
Joinup CPA toolkit reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-security/solution/cpa-creation-toolkit\r
\r
CPA reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ebxml-cppa'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4978a593-c09b-4cb7-b1d9-97815c2f1f7b .

camssa:06c0eb53-4ec1-4468-b92d-5e054c0d92f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:06c13b6c-125b-4fe5-bbfe-ec18cffe8a45 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:06c13cb2-64db-4221-aadc-46cb09df8f78 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XAdES is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eaa65c7d-1e13-413d-98bc-cab73e5114c5 .

camssa:06c2253f-54bb-4dce-942d-e026697b66ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI ARIA provides a set of attributes that can be added to HTML elements to convey additional information to assistive technologies about the roles, states, and properties of those elements. The Spanish "Accessibility Observatory" offers a methodology to ensure the monitoring and evolution of eaccessibility services, and includes WAI-ARIA as one of the elements reporting the current status of eAccessibility in digital public services. The WAI-ARIA specification is implemented in this methodology and scopes comprehensibility of website contents when combined mainly with HTML.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/#intro_ria_accessibility

PAe reference, Survey Methodology PDF:
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/en/pae_Estrategias/pae_Accesibilidad/pae_Observatorio_de_Accesibilidad.html?idioma=en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4061dc45-786e-4c9f-8928-b3a09efe8b71 .

camssa:06c7a992-8e6b-47cc-a417-54c2d4b85601 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TGF emphasises the importance of comprehensibility in the design and delivery of administrative procedures and services, and provides guidance and best practices for achieving this goal by promoting user-centric design principles such as user testing and feedbach to ensure that services are comprehensible and meet the need of users.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f40e0e83-7ad9-4855-9c32-6640ca335bb4 .

camssa:06c8fe09-1f16-4a37-8f65-f4e6469e23a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the OASIS Patent Policy apply to all OASIS specifications, including SMP.\r
\r
OASIS Case Study Guidelines:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/casestudies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31a80b80-72c7-45b8-b263-ab98dde31957 .

camssa:06c91b91-cf7b-45f5-be79-ddf982682408 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP provides for the establishment of authenticated and/or encrypted transport through security layers such as TLS (Transport Layer Security) and SASL (Simple Authentication and Security Layer). These layers can be tunneled through one another, allowing for both authentication and encryption.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf

SASL Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2444

TLS Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c6b54a4-a9fe-4556-a329-37a3d41aef21 .

camssa:06cd171b-18c1-4b29-bbdd-96a9f9302763 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OASIS has defined a clear process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. Moreover, there is a public review in the TC process.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f67a9ade-9e77-4c66-b7d8-9852e37c3c63 .

camssa:06d53c83-7c26-4ac4-828f-05471d787050 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, Linked Data and Open Data repositories and initiatives are a key point, and public administrations are putting efforts to develop a cross-border environment for open data exchange and reuse. \r
\r
Many initiatives and projects are raising using RDF as a foundation to collide their purpose and objectives. The creation of Linked Open Data solutions can be considered as innovative solutions as they help to evolve the eGoverment."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4743c07-5791-4155-9bbc-0229e13fd9f9 .

camssa:06d973bc-deb0-49f4-a169-1f4602fcb138 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:06dd69e1-e635-4769-a92c-9afb2958ffc3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:06dfc3e3-57ef-4ac4-850f-639ef3fadafe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As XML is used to encode all communications all over the internet, XSD fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of administrations by providing validation of exchanged data.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23e3e770-c790-4817-819c-16b42985330c .

camssa:06e1ac11-6997-48e9-89c6-35b7af5c4b26 a cav:Score,
