    cav:value "100" .

camssa:06e9b428-a853-48a7-9b70-2c44d88a8a2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UDDI is a sector agnostic specification that can be used under any business domain. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:213bde98-78ce-497b-897f-053386add132 .

camssa:06eb40ee-0112-4d21-a638-2e266877b4f2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:06f07a65-1e9e-4814-b1d2-728d92f7f108 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the specification is to facilitate the exchange of structured data. By allowing to make the data available to other persons or organisations, this Core Vocabulary reduces the administrative burden.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35f15736-715d-4fdf-8a97-5c0aa63ef7a9 .

camssa:06f9afc2-a1ac-4dee-ab11-ee11c79b9dc8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ed5ed50-616b-403b-a0f3-f83bbd1ca6d6 .

camssa:0706e84c-0d65-4e43-a661-f7e7d67852aa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:070978ef-079b-4fd9-92a4-52f8aad1c73d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0709e17f-c9a2-4335-9b9e-4368b1d9926d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 639-2 has been adopted by different specifications and used in different contexts. According to the Summer Institute of Linguistics (SIL), regristration authority in charge of the ISO 639-3, ISO 639-3 and ISO 639-2 are complementary and compatible, although having been conceived for different purposes. Moreover, the IETF BCP 47 language tags (generally used when working with HTML and XML) has included all ISO 639 codes in their code suite, indicating market acceptance.\r
\r
ISO 639-2 Registration Authority reference:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/develop.html\r
\r
SIL reference:\r
https://iso639-3.sil.org/about/relationships\r
\r
IETF BCP 47 langage tags reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/search/bcp47'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c575265-ce04-4e54-8b57-c4a949af9fe1 .

camssa:070a2b7b-8e6d-43be-8fc3-1f999cbd8dff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:070b7339-3039-43bd-9df2-67fc65b9fe45 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:070bcdf4-2451-4177-8390-e713f52c1635 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-21276471c1781fa2c7e78c8e03851e076b840beddbf5cf64f53b54b8855a01b8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:070c687e-d005-417a-b33f-f38135f26634 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification allows for the registration of information, making it accessible to other organisations or users. Additionally, the specification supports the use of the Collaboration Protocol Profile (CPP), which provides information that can also be stored and accessed by other users.

ebXML information reuse:
https://www.tutorialspoint.com/ebxml/ebxml_quick_guide.htm

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0caacdf-952c-4871-bdfe-5699a8b3450c .

camssa:070f7f04-4417-4d7e-8ca6-a59deb40b96d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML has been used in OpenModel project. In this project, YAML is used as structured data format in which AiiDA workflows are based. AiiDA is an open-source Python framework designed to assist researchers in automating, managing, preserving, sharing, and replicating complex workflows and the data involved in contemporary computational science. The development of this project is focused on the high level API which facilitates the ability to dynamically generate AiiDA workflows based on a YAML structured data format. 

OpenModel project:
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/953167/reporting'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27221fec-0239-4763-92d9-51577005392b .

camssa:071036bb-2cf2-4ea2-89e8-8fb687402314 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By allowing the encoding of data and information through the different information systems and the internet, UTF-8 fosters the visibility of administration services and eases the decision-making of public administrations. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7dd6cb92-edbd-452f-9e52-27ceea2d251d .

camssa:0710f207-5bc1-48dc-a4fd-387122e797e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-BPEL is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d57980d3-06a4-4f05-aa69-d8fd3b80aa52 .

camssa:071ae95a-dc7b-42a2-85c1-f7e731eb813f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain way. The implementation of OpenPM2 can help projects from any business domain to ensure the proper development while increasing efficiency and effectiveness. \r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:adf0af1e-9e8d-4994-9847-770040a1124e .

camssa:071b6a13-0838-4fcc-8fc0-6020b7f19728 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"According to the official schema.org blog, the specification addresses e-accessibility to some extent. The specification worked along with the IMS Global Learning Consortium's Access For All Specification and the Accessibility Metadata Project in order to provide accessibility of content for a wide range of users. Therefore, the specification can enable e-accessibility when combined with a set of recommendations taken from such collaborations (see Schema.org Accessibility Properties for Discoverability Vocabulary reference).\r
\r
Official blog for schema.org reference, Content Accessibility post:\r
http://blog.schema.org/2013/12/content-accessibility.html\r
\r
IMS Global Learning Consortium's Access For All Specification homepage reference:\r
http://www.imsglobal.org/activity/accessibility\r
\r
Accessibility Metadata Project reference:\r
http://www.a11ymetadata.org/about/\r
\r
Schema.org Accessibility Properties for Discoverability Vocabulary reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/2021/a11y-discov-vocab/latest/#intro\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:596a5461-8e5d-4cff-97af-ba2d0c440d23 .

