camssa:07310aee-e720-40fd-b3dc-f1fb07b03cbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. This Core Vocabulary fosters interoperability between public administrations, easing the exchange of business information. An example of this is business registers, which describing legal entities eases its reuse and exchange helping to implement the Once-Only Principle. \r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee7b1d40-ee5f-4bc9-be8d-083219ec534f .

