camssa:0779bb4d-5ebe-4a02-8ef1-7c99485fcb69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"OGC standards appear in Joinups 2024 ICT Rolling Plan. When a specification is included in Joinup's ICT Rolling Plan, it usually means that it is of current relevance and has significant implications for interoperability. This naturally attracts the attention of developer communities, generating debates and discussions to explore its effective implementation, impact and possible improvements.

OGC Community:
https://www.ogc.org/about-ogc/community/

ICT Rolling plan 2024: Smart sustainable cities and communities:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/smart-and-sustainable-cities-and-communities-rp2024\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:713bd549-bc52-41d4-85ce-31f7a02e783c .

camssa:077b1601-7ea0-40d2-a00e-fd792688729a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion of XHTML within any European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7159d4b9-a67d-4e6b-871e-2c2eb89ca46f .

