camssa:07920066-0699-4509-bdc0-360fd6b5e178 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary has been used to develop some European projects, for example, ESPD-EDM (European Single Procurement Document - Exchange Data Model) which is the technical representation of the legal European Single Procurement Document. It is used to support interoperability between ESPD services provided all over Europe.\r
\r
ESPD documentation:\r
https://docs.peppol.eu/pracc/espd/edm/\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5cc32b0e-5e7a-42fa-ab19-dbc0e0291a72 .

camssa:079c057a-6079-419b-b26d-afde1cccb6ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'while ISO/IEC 19944-1 does not specifically address data processing accuracy, it provides a foundation for organizations to establish data governance practices and security controls that indirectly promote the use of access control mechanisms.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ad71b6a-d52a-496b-b4f5-11f7707f84d6 .

camssa:079e2f92-13e3-48c5-856a-7ab4b7b5ae93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:625d17ba-9bd3-4bee-bcda-2381c701fb90 .

camssa:07a283d8-9e44-4a9e-9a08-628830b21ead a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'E-ARK CSIP does not specifically address data processing accuracy mechanisms, nonetheless, it indirectly support such issue by promoting best practices that may contribute to the maintenance of information accuracy such as metadata documentation, preservation planning and the recommendation of standard file formats.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d64016ae-e315-4b50-bd5d-50657e54b78f .

camssa:07a2e800-41d0-4f4a-b3c8-779e8feff48f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XSD 1.1 is not related to define organisational interoperability aspects. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
XSD Reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d230e29-fa01-49ce-92b8-7bc99c690dd3 .

camssa:07a399a3-704d-412b-927e-565cbceca3d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are several parts in the specification from 1 to 4 that we can find on the official ETSI webpage.\r
REM services enable cross-border recognition between existing national legal systems related to electronic \r
registered delivery services. Also, the eIDAS regulation is one of the top directives and regulations for the \r
digitalisation of the European environment.\r
\r
ENISA recommendation:\r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/events/tsforum-caday-2018/presentations/C03_Rock.pdf\r
\r
ETSI Web:\r
https://www.etsi.org/\r
\r
eIDAS Regulation:\r
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73d002eb-07cc-47af-8765-480e70b35af1 .

camssa:07a8508d-3c12-4f39-8b77-ef052ac65995 a cav:Score,
