camssa:07bf1b49-a23a-42a3-9349-8edb987c9877 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied. \r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef154f15-0db5-4ed9-b222-16404ccf980a .

camssa:07c02b5e-e731-4740-a7f5-bc161b36953f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:07c921aa-1ecf-4610-be4c-7d48d2f8af8e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although Ogg’s purpose is not to foster the visibility of administrative data or services, it can help to enhance the visualization and visibility of public administrations by providing multimedia content. In fact, the specification helps to store and eases the visualization of media content in any platform of a public administration.\r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4d54d10-346c-4dc3-bd9b-3b1ceea30616 .

camssa:07ca28b8-aab0-498f-8661-ff802e23afd0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3c0edf049cd95575b46d688ed31be0ccce7a5822c5bcc22adf05d491f01f2780 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:07cd7f4e-23c0-4457-9691-0dc66a020baf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SHACL was designed to enhance the semantic and technical interoperability layers of ontologies expressed as RDF graphs. RDF is a European Standard used by public administrations in projects for sharing Linked Open Data. This means that the validation carried out with SHACL on RFD graphs fosters their use for the publication of data as Linked Open Data."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9898dde7-ee06-4805-b4d4-4482f7f14b81 .

camssa:07d075fc-e5e8-4407-ba53-defa666f03f5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:07d24702-07d3-4bb7-ad65-05c6080b8cfd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Not enough information has been gathered to determine that the specification impacts positively or negatively to long-term preservations. Therefore, it seems that the specification's purpose is not related to the preservation of electronic resources.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c43d8091-673e-4fe0-a59e-0f6e73c7f981 .

camssa:07d44c97-abd5-4421-8180-702b4d83f238 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No, the specification is not a European Standard.\r
\r
XSD Reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87590999-e32b-4f0d-82df-27e479d8a1c5 .

