    cav:value "100" .

camssa:07da32d3-f7cc-4a97-bc2f-bbdf2f24f725 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification extends XML standard. In this context, XML is platform agnostic, therefore ebXML can also be considered  as a platform agnostic specification.

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23ceced1-46cf-45cd-90a4-82088d7bb095 .

camssa:07da4e94-0229-4cb6-b433-d42c2105abe8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Time Stamping Protocol (TSP), utilizing TSA authentication mechanisms, can enable entities to access certain fields or restrict access, and validate signatures with Time-Stamp Tokens. The assignation of precise timestamps to each transaction or data modification ensures that the sequence and timing of data changes are accurately recorded. This is an important capability for establishing when data was altered or accessed, which can help verify its authenticity.

TSP/TSA IETF reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d840eec-5a7e-4bb0-b9a5-7bd869ab2cb3 .

camssa:07dbd27b-9419-46b7-99bb-6ba38c86f493 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a67ecbc29e70e62b18dba3ae4f8d1f91d5b3196777dbf8b58c6713cd517eb768 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:07e3d3d7-8662-44c8-98b8-92a31107b37d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:07e5abf4-5d06-46f5-8052-5d4e44fbf2b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS has many functionalities that can simplify the delivery of European public services.  One of the most notable aspects of OAS is its conformity with REST architectural style, which means it allows for the connection of components in microservices applications.  This OAS characteristic, is a key enabler for the simplification of European public services, as it eases the digitalisation and accessibility of RESTful APIs design, documentation and functionalities. \r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f92da92e-300d-405a-a691-1e529b9bbf64 .

camssa:07e60b3f-7b6f-4a48-9adc-207a923145d1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:07e8f804-db25-4695-9fe2-4e3d973f9576 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the design goals of YAML is data portability between programming languages. An example can be found in the processes and models section, where it is explained that one measure to maximize data portability is separating properties needed for serialization and presentation. Once it has been done, YAML representations of application information will be consistent and portable between various programming environments.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#32-information-models'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4df5e511-a809-4aa4-bbda-8d6f72f8db99 .

camssa:07eaec36-0f1b-45e6-a8fe-bd2287d5c688 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NFVI specification is composed of different virtualised resources that activates depending on the task. Nonetheless, this does not imply that the NFVI specification can be extended.\r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:319e187f-6cad-4e05-97dd-fd0100f67904 .

camssa:07f04f6c-ad9a-41ec-b246-da07d723ce91 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:07f098e8-c5ff-4ef5-b71a-4f2a8ea7a95d a cav:Score,
