camssa:098519ee-bace-4d42-908a-18c9e35cbf38 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The fifth part of the MIME specification defines the conformance criteria to define a certain level of implementation that allows the useful interworking of messages with content that differs from US-ASCII text.\r
Moreover, there are some free online validators for MIME to check the compliance of MIME messages with the IETF standards.\r
\r
MIME Part Five: Conformance Criteria and Examples\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2049\r
\r
MIME online validator:\r
https://www.mimevalidator.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4388a24a-5367-465a-a106-34ffd3853ef9 .

camssa:098ec403-4800-45c3-a6b7-2e6f8f7a6c76 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IndexedDB API can play a supportive role in enabling digital service delivery channels, particularly for web-based services. While IndexedDB itself is not a comprehensive solution for service delivery, it offers a crucial set of capabilities that can help optimise the performance and functionality of digital platforms used in delivering public services.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:469a5a52-a0eb-46b7-9c00-70d8a9e19755 .

