camssa:09a1fc42-3e05-4f52-b925-51ff7ffdb856 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Initially IPsec was designed to be part of the IPv6 specification, but as security became important, it was finally designed to be an independent internet protocol for security. Therefore, this specification is technology agnnostic.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

IPsec in IPv4 and IPv6:
https://networkengineering.stackexchange.com/questions/37025/ipsec-in-ipv4-and-ipv6'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c60cf75-c3c2-48c3-80dd-b391060db6a4 .

camssa:09a8907c-4d99-4450-b313-a6013d4cbf06 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV is included in the ICT Standards List identified for its use in eProcurent at Joinup. Despite the specification cannot be downloaded directly from the European Platform, CSV is a IETF specification that can be reused for free. \r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4180"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a001f6e8-f81f-47e5-938f-5b8e90372768 .

