camssa:09ebd2ca-40fc-44d1-9bdf-adbc362fde23 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES is a group of extensions to Cryptographic Message Syntax (CMS) signed data which purpose is to make advanced electronic signatures. One profile of CAdES is CAdES-LTA, it is a signature conformant which has one or more long-term-validation attributes that guarantee the preservation of the authenticity of the signature. Moreover, a resulting property of CAdES is that electronically signed documents can remain valid for long periods, even if the signer or verifying party later attempts to deny the validity of the signature.\r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e35e7e1d-21b1-45ad-857c-ab88615bdece .

