camssa:0a92365a-eb5a-49d0-bbb9-eba3710b5c45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA primarily focuses on improving the accessibility of web content, including interfaces, it does not inherently enable the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services in terms of structuring or organizing data. WAI-ARIA is more concerned with providing additional information to assistive technologies about the semantics and behavior of user interface components.

The inclusion of WAI-ARIA in the French "General framework for improving accessibility" (RGAA) within e-accessibility policies reflects a commitment to making digital interfaces more accessible to people with disabilities. This specification facilitates effective interaction for individuals using assistive technologies like screen readers, speech recognition systems, or keyboard commands.

Web Accessibility ARIA:
https://doit.illinois.gov/initiatives/accessibility/guides/web/introduction-to-aria.html

Cornell University:
https://it.cornell.edu/accessibility/developers-learn-how-wai-aria-can-improve-accessibility

RGAA reference:
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/publications/rgaa-accessibilite/methode-rgaa/criteres/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b944d49-fd70-4a17-96f3-ff55cc29ca8c .

