camssa:0ac2a080-c9ae-498f-83e3-484676b62b69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not related to the prevention of data portability. Therefore it neither prevents nor supports data portability. ECLI implements Dublin Core Ontology, as ECLI is a uniform identifier that has the same recognizable format for all Member States and EU courts.\r
To make it easier to understand and find case law, each document containing a judicial decision should have a set of metadata as described in this paragraph. These metadata should be described according to the standards set by the Dublin Core Metadata Initiative.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/\r
\r
ECLI Information:\r
https://e-justice.europa.eu/175/EN/european_case_law_identifier_ecli?init=true '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e103fc23-3bb7-4dd9-aad6-11b12f564e87 .

camssa:0ac7c093-6c76-4fa7-91fb-ee8fe28ada31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XAdES Baseline Profile is a business sector agnostic specification which is reusable beyond the domain for which it was developed. Specifically, implemented to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8cba0729-a26c-49ed-9a0e-f65056a5619b .

camssa:0ac9f901-b4f4-4dd0-a260-6e7434513ac0 a cav:Score,
