camssa:0bf8a938-d2ac-4fe5-87aa-75115f67526e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2960a076-1ccc-4d68-9f93-89c30cede966 .

camssa:0bf8e586-9e73-4c5e-b3ba-a48cf33ee343 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the key features of the ESPD is the digital signature functionality, which provides a mechanism to\r
verify that the document has not been tampered with, and that the information contained within it is authentic\r
and accurate. The digital signature ensures that the data has not been modified or altered in transit, and that\r
it is the same data that was originally sent. It is important to note that the e-signature functionality is something that is built on top of the ESPD model, and each Member State is responisble of implementing it on their respective procurement digital services platform.\r
\r
Commission Decision (EU, Euratom) 2017/46 of 10 January 2017 on the security of communication and\r
information systems in the European Commission:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1548093747090&uri=CELEX:32017D0046\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f2c8e3f-db01-43fe-b0b1-7584c0efd642 .

camssa:0bf96cd4-350a-45e8-8d8d-b90d278968d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XML is to store, transport and exchange data through interoperable systems. Additionally, the specification provides the means to validate XML documents using XML schemas.\r
\r
XML Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/                                        \r
Fog and Edge Computing in 5G’ ENISA report: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/fog-and-edge-computing-in-5g  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72dd4b61-7a3a-43a1-8e1a-8a92d41d6ee3 .

camssa:0bf980ab-be9f-4713-af1b-ecfb02c777af a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0bfd5043-340d-4585-9e4b-8d01c693faa3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0c00bfa6-7280-42cb-b9c9-adf4235ba875 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData is a protocol of querying and sharing, and as such is not supposed to offer long-term preservation of data. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
OData reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c4443e1-9c5b-4cda-adb1-0a196fe354ea .

