camssa:0c36c607-8429-49b1-941a-ffe59a511b47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OpenTelemetry explicitly addresses and guarantees data accuracy through data sampling. The idea behind sampling is to control the spans sent to an observability backend, resulting in lower ingest costs. Different organisations will have their own reasons for not just why they want to sample, but also what they want to sample. Consequently, end-users can focus on interesting traces for them (e.g: frontend team may only want to see traces with specific user attributes).

OTel Sampling: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/concepts/sampling/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:382c4a7b-1471-412e-a835-679ea3d99676 .

camssa:0c3a48d3-82e2-42a1-b9fc-c9917de3d9c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT specification ensures data processing accuracy through mechanisms like templates, which define rules for matching XML elements and applying transformations. In XSLT, functions and operators are type-safe, meaning data types are strictly managed. If incompatible types are used together (e.g., adding a string to a number), an error occurs, reducing the chances of inaccurate transformations

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffcb5f9b-19be-4215-a76c-aa7ea8e3cf3b .

camssa:0c3a8e29-99da-4e9b-91ff-3926d4699183 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e46f1a4a060cc7e143e32e4833c94af9164c37bc0d4c844bd1fa974ffb2ac225 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0c42c0ce-c046-4c28-9acc-8b4a82d54a59 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ORDL can be mapped to the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, ODRL is associated with the "European Legal Interoperability Agreeement", "Legal Agreement, "Legal Interoperability Agreement" and "National Legal Interoperability Agreement" ABBs from the Legal View, "Semantic Interoperability Agreement" ABBs from the Semantic View, "Technical Interoperability Agreement" ABBs from the Technical Application View.\r
\r
EIRA:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira/solution/eira/release/600\r
\r
ELIS Solution:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis\r
\r
ELIS v6.0.0:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b14536dc-6997-4a56-9c55-7a14bf74c221 .

camssa:0c4317ef-9aeb-4e33-89d9-1a4a52cdd24d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has a validation schema to test conformance. Also automated check rules can be\r
implemented.\r
\r
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43922d34-7c8f-4fea-a9f9-e50ad0a3550a .

