camssa:0c8334e3-7253-4a5c-837f-7c888a37fac1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being an international standard that encompasses the internal security framework of all private and public administrations, ISO/IEC 27001 helps to create digitally by default services that reduce the administrative burden on both sides, public administrations and stakeholders.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 27001 reference website:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/54534.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4b27cf37-1edb-4253-a70e-19fa084be09b .

camssa:0c892d5d-1e33-45c9-9251-b8e754f5fb69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e48ea7a9-1876-477e-804c-b62b999431d4 .

camssa:0c94f70b-fcc0-4de7-8189-237deda8d037 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Cryptographic algorithms are the basis of e-signatures encryption. ETSI TS 119 512 is furthermore developed for trust service providers for the storing and retrieval of information and data that require a high degree of security in their processing and exchange. 

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa6df682-3d85-41d8-a9e0-35b309367086 .

camssa:0c96ffc6-af06-479f-ac96-ee4d694647e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI EN 319 532-3 has the support of various communities listed in the following link as "Supporting \r
Organizations", including Universities, private and public companies.\r
\r
Portal ETSI reference:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/webapp/workprogram/Report_WorkItem.asp?WKI_ID=56725'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42705b09-61f0-4cfa-b4ba-ea72eb9bb386 .

camssa:0c9b2454-30fd-4843-95a0-594fe583c766 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0ca91c74-ddf2-4d0b-a0cd-fb05d5f68875 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP is included in the national catalogue of Belgium, Denmark, Sweden and Malta. The National Interoperability Framework of these countries is aligned with al least 2 out of 3 sections of the EIF according to NIFO factsheets.\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022\r
\r
Belgium National Catalogue:\r
https://www.belgif.be/page/specifications.en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e8ec040-5575-49d8-9fdf-39c21216ec5b .

camssa:0caae820-bc94-4180-a217-7a3d6f4a881e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ODRL does not dictate the use of specific communication protocols. For secure data processing, especially \r
during data exchange, it's important to implement secure communication protocols, such as HTTPS, to \r
protect data in transit.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76b6ab31-109f-4018-9406-6d6a07884724 .

camssa:0cab1b1f-af47-4904-b089-c1dbb55ddded a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalRuleML is aimed to define a common data and metadata model towards the maximisation of information reuse. It provides a set of requirements and aspects that foster modelling data supporting data exchange and semantics. \r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c4eca62-6fd5-4557-889f-2d8c6ad3a0ae .

camssa:0cb08a41-5734-4bae-a10f-e87bea849780 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0cb412c1-bf1d-4873-8e44-4ed1b7d41bf0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:0cb42df5-756e-457b-a511-a9bb09165536 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT is not a European standard. The specification was developed by the W3C as part of its work on XML technologies, which are used worldwide for web and data interoperability.

XSLT W3C Homepage:
https://www.w3.org/community/xslt-40/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c51c3ca2-5cc1-4f04-858a-d26b4cf67f6f .

camssa:0cb4674c-0d43-40b0-a1e5-9525e4866602 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0cb4756c-48dc-4bc4-a944-fd8a8790877e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TGF does not assume any particular language or script and is designed to be language- and script-neutral. This means that it can be applied in any linguistic or cultural context, and can be adapted to support multilingual content and user interfaces.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9f47f76-010d-47e1-acf0-a333a09e73e5 .

camssa:0cbbc16f-0ccb-4858-8675-9ac71b338e81 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML5 is one of the main pillars for Open Web Platform, a full programming environment for cross-platform applications with access to device capabilities; video and animations; graphics; style, typography, and other tools for digital publishing; extensive network capabilities, among others. Moreover, developers can have stability in to implement and plan through HTML5.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d16ccc0d-6636-4cc9-a5f4-06fdd88f679b .

camssa:0cc3cdc2-6bd3-4ba7-a5b8-43e3fdf246a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary specification significantly facilitates organisational interoperability agreements by providing a standardised framework for describing location data. This standardisation ensures that different organisations can seamlessly exchange and understand location information, reducing semantic conflicts and enhancing collaboration.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d6e812c9-029a-4538-b87f-655cdd3b0497 .

camssa:0cc6444a-dbeb-4d8c-8a96-9412e845f54f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML can be used to document the steps involved in administrative procedures in a structured way. By breaking down procedures into hierarchical tasks, it can improve clarity. Moreover, YAML can help listing rules and services.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f8c62e5-e4a8-49af-aa6f-b5df6576fa56 .

camssa:0cc68f16-c628-40ce-b909-ba91f2e3b96e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0cc6d6c6-1de2-4b2d-a8b7-6cf545e1a733 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of YAML is not related to ensure the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

YAML specification: 
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf0040c2-2488-4886-909f-8ccf6e522b34 .

camssa:0cc897df-7457-4158-9e90-bf42f29e019d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI ES 119 612 has the support of various communities listed in the following link as "Supporting Organizations", including universities, private and public companies. The ESI technical committee provides public support to members and non-members alike, with different conditions depending on ETSI membership status. This support helps to increase the use of the specification and the specification itself by detecting weaknesses in implementation or any other relevant aspect of the specification's functionalities.

ETSI oranisation:
https://www.etsi.org/about'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c55d79f7-0c97-4139-a752-606cf6eeb423 .

