camssa:0d04e8d2-bbf1-466c-a8a6-577c27572433 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is place in the very beginning of the Digital Public Service Life-cycle, specifically in the analysis where requirements are set. At this stage, the solution includes and remarks the need for the Organisational Agreements and  the Organisational Interoperability Agreements. The Organisational includes a set of relevant aspects and agreements that are key to ensure interoperability at organisational level, these building blocks are, for instance, agreements on privacy, agreements on reuse of infrastructure, agreement on data sharing amongst others. By providing this granularity, the EIRA helps public administrations on the process of defining solutions and the organisational agreements that will need to be put in place. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:411a98b2-5811-4397-8cbb-30ecf3721ed1 .

camssa:0d05bd52-53fb-442e-9a83-f0128394220f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:0d0ab151-7a62-4e99-b935-ab66c77e5262 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary does not enable the long-term preservation of data/information/knowledge (electronic records included). The main purpose of the specification is to define a standardised way of describing organisations that have gained legal entity status through a formal registration process. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cac1087b-0917-457c-9308-0f20538f6449 .

camssa:0d14df04-f603-4764-8d36-429741c41418 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0d15a808-c270-462b-819c-c35e6c52f3b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI TS 119 612, operates under the ETSI Intellectual Property Rigths (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
ETSI ownership of IPRs section: \r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5635f1f-3f94-43ee-9f75-3c2bc0b10f81 .

camssa:0d1a0d61-fcb7-4b00-a635-02d3a56c2fd6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are platforms to share results and information about IPv6. The IPv6 Forum is a world-wide consortium of worldwide leading Internet vendors, Industry Subject Matter Experts, Research & Education Networks, with a clear mission to advocate IPv6 by dramatically improving technology, market, and deployment user and industry awareness of IPv6. 

"IPv6 Forum" reference:
https://ipv6forum.com/?module=News&type=user&func=display&sid=9'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b00e07e-2307-4713-be69-b82f3f87928e .

camssa:0d1b4200-094b-4227-9c5f-9335c52d8616 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTTPS is maintained by IETF which is an international community developing open standards.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/about/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0fb1c95-f3e3-414c-a235-02abd0f57af3 .

