        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV has not been found to be included in any open repository or catalogue of standards at national level.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98834089-bc62-4696-b62e-8ea1c5771940 .

camssa:0df54607-b453-4a7d-8612-dce8db56edb7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST has been included in the catalogue of Finland and Slovakia. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
\r
National catalogue of Finland: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Finland%20Factsheet%20Validated.pdf\r
\r
National catalogue of Slovakia:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/NIFO%20-%20Factsheet%20Slovakia_2016_v1_0.pdf\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6129c3ae-1719-49d2-b5fc-230712cfce68 .

camssa:0df916b3-368a-4f94-8b28-492b27911196 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the BFO is an upper level ontology that is designed for being used in supporting information retrieval, analysis and integration in scientific and other domains, currently there is no sharing of data among users due to the wide variety of applications.
BFO is the core element of  the European Materials Modeling Ontology (EMMO) used to organise the top level ontology that leads to a better integration of business processes related to material processing. 
https://emmo-repo.github.io/


BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1b59774-df8a-4d53-a64b-2d59cfbd35de .

camssa:0dfc5d60-2bf5-4b6a-b5d4-c9dff7c82df9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related to the definition of a data model. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc959"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed038d5b-4259-4892-a024-a8e451cc269f .

camssa:0e0024fb-fb31-4427-8246-2258ef58bbbd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e00cbc2-4f39-4c3f-8478-237cbddf52e4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e01fbd2-e7de-4476-8c32-adadd7cff2b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML supports XML namespaces, which allow users to use elements from different vocabularies within the
same document and has strict syntax that prevents the user from customising their product. In this sense,
HTML5 offers a larger set of possibilities when creating web interfaces.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/#well-formed'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9a1af93-8c2d-4225-80ef-eb80c9eff334 .

camssa:0e03520b-a150-442d-949b-5b3b80f148c3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e08a925-904c-40a6-977b-9f3159674b1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ITPE conducts conferences and webinars within various communities using the specification to give a voice to anyone who wants to give their opinion on the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification, including national participation.\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, Events:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/events/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c8629e4-1181-4cb8-b1c1-2a0ad12beb2e .

camssa:0e0b1033-23eb-4b01-9b66-f3a1e8411f23 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching the different national catalogues, there has not been found any European Member State recommending ETSI TS 119 612.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3df2a92-236e-4d4d-8480-a34870310bac .

camssa:0e0bddaf-06f8-4747-a397-8a8bbce7a6ec a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e0e281c-262a-41fc-88ec-ef4ee7d61d1d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e1176f8-8c15-4e4b-8625-62a93651221a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GraphQL is a generic and flexible engine that defines a schema syntax, query syntax, and a query execution reference for centralised databases. It is therefore domain-agnostic and is designed to be used in any domain.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:999cbc20-84c2-4f66-8bf2-a1348a6d383b .

camssa:0e168dfa-7042-43bc-8d41-a91fab4faa35 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"NUTS introduced the ISO 2-letter codes in 1999, a specification designating country codes (for example, BE3 for the Walloon region in Belgium, where BE corresponds to the ISO-2 letter code of Belgium) (see EUROSTAT reference, History of NUTS section, 'NUTS 1981 - MUTS 1999' document). However, the NUTS classification is not dependent on the ISO 2 specification, and the UK code ('UK') is a clear counterexample to the ISO standard ('GB' according to ISO 2). Therefore, NUTS is technology-agnostic.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, History of NUTS section, 'NUTS 1981 - MUTS 1999' document:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/history\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:38c26646-6805-45b4-8b0c-34c5b10d1308 .

camssa:0e189531-cef1-40f4-81d4-10ad4128fd45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although HTML is aligned with the first levels of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee's 5-star schema for Open Data, it does not support the different principles of Linked Open Data.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
https://www.w3.org/wiki/LinkedData"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0ef82e2-878b-450f-97ee-b9499e38dbce .

camssa:0e257cf0-47b3-4f5f-af00-85cc47624134 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"All specifications developed by the Publication's office of the EU are royalty-free and its IPR policies are\r
alligned with the FRAND principles.\r
\r
Publications Office of the EU IPR:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/about-us/legal-notices/publications-office-of-the-european-union-copyright\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c98ae9d-3121-4c52-8eb8-7f54431c361e .

camssa:0e28a7c5-c8ed-408d-9e19-acee0f4a02dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:0e2f3e75-838b-4bef-b492-73f58244a90b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 10 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to the Croatia, Estonia, France, Germany, Malta, Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Spain and Sweden.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc896b65-3ebd-4cb8-8383-086755f99f8d .

