camssa:0e50c0d0-73fc-4719-883a-83daa2a16bf2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is maintained and developed by the CEF eDelivery Team and all the information related to the specification and its implementation can be found at CEF’s webpage.\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/eDelivery+SMP+-+1.10"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0239d019-df16-4d8b-9f4b-c582a3a5c641 .

camssa:0e59aea2-3151-4dad-b70c-cc24ec1c2967 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard does not directly model business processes, its contribution to
standardizing geospatial training data for AI/ML applications indirectly supports more efficient, reliable, and
collaborative business processes within organizations that depend on geospatial analysis and AI/ML technologies.

OGC TrainingDML-AI:
https://www.ogc.org/standard/trainingdml-ai/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0da73bdf-1b67-445a-bc4e-7d893235fd00 .

camssa:0e5c077c-8f42-4ef2-9807-4591d20879e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Dataspaces provide a way to integrate heterogeneous data from multiple sources. In many organisations, data is often scattered across different databases, systems, and formats. Dataspaces help create a unified view of this distributed data, enabling more effective analysis and decision-making. By integrating data, sharing and collaboration is easier. This can improve communication and data portability.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol Specification: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db6dbd5f-4970-4ea3-8b0b-4f00ab96bd69 .

camssa:0e5ca165-dc58-4134-90e9-9aab6b93ac8f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e5ca3ae-2b5c-4bdb-889b-e226928126fd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:0e5fe544-2b03-4710-8fe0-0d3cbacea6ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The header parameter of the CSV specification indicates the presence or absence of the header line. Some valid values for this header are "present" or "absent", which can enable data processing accuracy.\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:440bcb5e-44af-433e-b380-0445d7a215e1 .

camssa:0e616020-cc72-4df6-ab22-12e291da2de3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:0e6189c9-ff12-4612-aaa0-deccd1e3ffcf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification foresees that it can be implemented separately. Being a reference model based on layers, it offers the users the possibility to work with any amount of layers. This can be seen on the Microsoft implementation, where only 5 of the 7 layers are in use.

Microsoft and OSI:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/network/windows-network-architecture-and-the-osi-model

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd336cdc-c97d-4665-a992-9249542f14cb .

camssa:0e61b510-fedb-4d93-b34a-8b205aaf201d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI EN 319 532-3, operate under the \r
ETSI Intellectual Property Rights (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free basis.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights Policy, ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bb17e89-779e-47c9-9da4-6ff93571a31f .

camssa:0e61bbc1-8cae-4607-b18e-9bc615e615c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In accordance with ISO/IEC JTC 1 and the ISO and IEC Councils, these International Standards are publicly 
available for Standardization purposes. 

Publicly Available Standards: 
https://standards.iso.org/ittf/PubliclyAvailableStandards/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc4f4d61-04f1-4534-a405-19c13555f2c6 .

camssa:0e636be5-576a-4ced-be78-f287cf4460d8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP specification allows customisation for flexibility to accommodate diverse use cases and evolving technologies. HTTP relies on a set of "methods" to indicate the intended action to be performed on a resource.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Semantics, RFC 7231 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7231'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c44dd404-9ba5-4e9b-bc4b-97bd161690fc .

camssa:0e67a9e5-3740-4f06-a8a8-694e09d684a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Different existing reports point out the benefits of implementing ISAE 3402 in terms of efficiency. An example \r
of such assessment can be found in the following link. \r
\r
Report on ISAE 3402:\r
https://isae3402.co.uk/sites/default/files/Whitepaper_ISAE_3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:334d21b8-4294-42c7-abce-8fc7bb849a12 .

camssa:0e69dee3-8893-4273-be54-6ff4ede29223 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is currently only available in English and Portuguese.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html

Portuguese version:
https://mba.eci.ufmg.br/legal/bfo-pt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c96c0edd-842d-434e-a5e5-547d420930d7 .

camssa:0e6e2bec-2acf-42f3-8112-ff3548a6acce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching through different catalogues, no evidence of the Indexed Database API being included in the catalogue of any Member State was found.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e39dc9d1-e335-4df5-b5e7-24ebcc03d33a .

camssa:0e702846-e05e-4329-b89e-4308b54cec86 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
