camssa:0e773440-bf49-4d1e-9a16-dc02f4ae7561 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By providing a standardised way to validate RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs, SHACL ensures that data conforms to specific shapes and constraints, making it easier to share and integrate data across different systems and platforms.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8ab552f-864a-4eb8-b8df-0fe1cc04a267 .

camssa:0e77f047-436e-4573-b6aa-336730ad9e49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Customisation is an important part of the GraphQL functionalities. For instance, in order to introduce additional semantic meaning, the specification supports the addition of custom scalars,  or even to define custom directives beyond those provided by the specification.\r
\r
GraphQL custom scalars:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Scalars.Custom-Scalars\r
\r
GraphQL Custom directives:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Type-System.Directives.Custom-Directives'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4aa02ff-f0c5-4d1a-807f-e6eead6494e8 .

camssa:0e79e769-38f9-4e7a-aebc-d219e446eb38 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:0e7b6f55-e439-499c-afc6-736ec5f19167 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:0e7b9a34-9c51-4c8c-87e0-4a2d6dbf81a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Web Services Description Language (WSDL) itself primarily focuses on describing the interfaces and operations of web services, and it does not provide specific mechanisms for ensuring the secure processing of data. Security considerations, including secure processing, are typically addressed at other layers of the web services architecture and are influenced by the implementation choices made by service providers and consumers. \r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a6bf2a5-7b46-4e9c-82a9-93c3cb706add .

camssa:0e91754a-42cc-4d4c-8a72-8e475823fea4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 is a sector domain agnostic specification that can be used independently from the business domain.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/   '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8bc14de-c964-4730-b4b5-044d1eccf146 .

camssa:0e91b959-6375-4c42-a7f1-11ab40417ea6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0e93ae4b-5d06-405b-a102-716cfd7c0276 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the GITB TDL is not related to long term preservation of electronic record. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specifcation. \r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00e833cd-76de-451f-ac79-7b034a81bd7b .

camssa:0e95cddf-e2c4-4afd-98fc-dd3ba92742a1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0e9aca8b-f0dc-48f8-8373-de09e1237ac1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2beb4d81-b4e1-4635-9889-a1fe8f86f0ea .

camssa:0e9c09c2-6a5e-43c5-860d-72cdb005d1f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData queries and shares data accross different systems via RESTful interfaces. RESTful APIs may be platform-agnostic, without any dependency on the environment or programming language being used; however, this use case is not always applied. Therefore, the specification is not platform-agnostic.\r
\r
OData reference: \r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/odata-v4.0-part1-protocol.html\r
\r
RESTful reference, Use cases section:\r
https://restfulapi.io/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d62b2cd-f629-4162-9c35-391452284e67 .

camssa:0e9ca296-87c4-46eb-bb3a-438911496a7e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although it is mostly suited for public administrations, ETSI TS 119 512 protocols can be implemented in any business domain. For example, the specification uses different preservation schemes that build the so called preservation profiles (see eIDAS reference).\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a02b6857-15fe-4168-adc1-258bbb5f998b .

camssa:0e9eede7-df42-422b-8ae2-bef57b0190df a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0ea09930-fb2e-4672-9d3a-e25179287113 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REM provides an e-mail service and security controls and mechanisms to protect transactions. Also REM \r
Signature enables the secure exchange of data between both parts.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference, section 6.2.7:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9faca844-f951-4b20-9ece-5af8f554b537 .

camssa:0ea190ef-bff4-45a7-854a-690ce4c95ea8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:0ea6e806-313a-4c34-a739-3c32273ee1b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 27001 is included in the Catalogue of standards of Norway. \r
\r
Norway catalogue of standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2a5cde0a-6b1a-4761-a80b-63a42ba237d8 .

camssa:0eac7301-4a2c-4ba9-8aab-4fb535499ec3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DCAT-AP is not related to the modelling of business processes, therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:56758502-d14f-4f2f-be32-9b9efc4d9966 .

