camssa:0ec8134d-afce-463b-a829-212609b608a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/\r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce3c452f-c249-43f9-a624-934ac66e5df7 .

camssa:0ecdc61f-cad8-433c-8cca-615accc24b45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As part of the ""IP Stack"", IPsec has been selected by several public administrations for secure data exchange over the internet. By allowing the secure exchange of data, the specification fosters the visibility of data across borders.\r
\r
An example of its implementation is the TESTA project, which provides a secure cross-border data communication network service for public administrations.\r
\r
Interoperable Delivery of European Egovernment Services to Public Administrations, Businesses and Citizens \r
(IDABC) Reference Link:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/idabc/en/document/2097.html\r
\r
TESTA Service:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17ac10d9-7829-41e0-811f-77c8497d47f1 .

camssa:0ed09c84-e252-46d5-8968-22fad8300ac5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT is not a European Standard in the sense of a formal standard developed and recognized by the European standards organisations.                                        \r
\r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/         '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b08c0c8f-761f-46b6-b067-39d3858bd33e .

camssa:0ed5fca8-65ee-4137-912b-9a3857f27ce1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0ee24356-ac8c-49c0-a4f7-203a83cc4f1d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A significant amount of the data collected never gets leveraged because of the challenges in interpreting data models and API standards for utilizing the data across platforms. This specification enables close to real-time (right-time) access to context/digital twin information coming from many different sources (not only IoT data sources), thus scoping comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data, and services.

GS CIM 009: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/CIM/001_099/009/01.07.01_60/gs_CIM009v010701p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac78282c-4be5-4fcb-8568-9c118b2b0623 .

camssa:0ee372b4-f675-446d-a225-ced4887c7386 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0ee9e1f8-5f20-4522-b6d6-a4af7bbe141d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As defined on the TC standardisation, only TC members are involved in the development of ISO standards. A review is carried out to arrange the consensus firstly within the TC members and subsequently is reviewed by the different ISO member bodies. However, it cannot be considered a public review, because only TC members can participate.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2f7e101-11ee-4bff-8a3d-794a15ae2c49 .

camssa:0eec9fc2-4ab7-40b9-8e0f-84e8c31b1f8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is a key enabler for the metadata exchange. It is part of the eDelivery Building Block defined by CEF, which aims to foster data exchange and reuse across borders enhancing the interoperability in Europe. Moreover, eDelivery SMP 1.10 helps in the decision-making process by allowing data exchange between administrations.\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/Benefits+of+eDelivery"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16b73c51-9952-44c8-9514-d6d2b43dc177 .

camssa:0ef29b81-ed82-4624-b610-904bd8c577ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SHACL can significantly enhance policy-based access control systems by defining precise rules for data access and modification. These rules can be specifically designed to protect personal data managed by public administrations, ensuring that only authorised personnel can access or alter this sensitive information. By implementing stringent access control policies, SHACL helps mitigate the risk of unauthorised access and data breaches.
In addition SHACL can implement access control mechanisms to regulate data access, using SHACL-ACL, thereby enhancing security.

"SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43458-7_4

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:49ed1ed4-6d7b-4365-bd11-2f962eb3300c .

camssa:0ef4dedc-9de3-4f19-ac61-db58f8b1e310 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0ef939e4-e3c0-41d5-8ec1-534a7adf1671 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0efd6641-c3f0-4e39-b2ee-4f747e3769c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No up to date mechanism to assess the IPsec conformity has been found. The existing  conformity tests provided in the past by the IETF IPSec working group are outdated.\r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hoffman-ipsec-testing-01"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d487c068-8bb3-45a7-9a95-677961e01cbb .

camssa:0eff2c4f-4e9d-4dee-b790-d5d9d259444d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SFIA Foundation intends to align the SFIA specification with different models and frameworks. At present, there are some workgroups that prove this trend, for example through the development of the EU ICT Role Profiles (see SFIA reference, Tools and resources section, Standard skills profiles subsection, European Union-EU ICT Role Profiles, CEN/CENELEC Workshop Agreements (CWA) 16458-1:2018 European ICT Professional Role Profiles – Part 1: 30 ICT). However, there is no explicit provisions to achieve this end.\r
\r
SFIA reference, Tools and resources section, Standard skills profiles subsection, European Union-EU ICT Role Profiles, CEN/CENELEC Workshop Agreements (CWA) 16458-1:2018 European ICT Professional Role Profiles – Part 1: 30 ICT:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/tools-and-resources/standard-industry-skills-profiles/european-union/eu-ict-role-profiles'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff37aba0-cd00-4fc5-84c4-ea193330492d .

camssa:0eff3a7b-5777-487c-9c64-d0d47015614f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, HTTPS has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ffc8150-5bf8-4ab8-b65c-85ff5607666a .

camssa:0f03e798-234c-462e-9f5b-de34241a173f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:0f03f966-295c-40b8-8031-e566ca83c20e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME extends the format of email messages to support text in ASCII and non-ASCII characters, as well as attachments of audio, video, images, and application programs.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:225bba13-c3eb-4b45-8f7f-51168f62785d .

camssa:0f0b0ff5-5697-4cc3-b053-1ca1900898b3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:0f0f9377-65f6-4c8f-a1de-989f6802cd71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPSV-AP is a reusable and extensible data model for harmonising the way public services are described in a machine-readable format. So it describes the public administrations and eases their visualisation and comprehensibility.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1fcb2e9-48ac-4737-9ace-e7aa01fc4ecf .

camssa:0f1016c8-ddea-4e6b-864b-66ae5d6b3ff7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to business process modelling, therefore this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
W3C specification reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89144247-7a88-47aa-bca5-b74b099e32d6 .

camssa:0f13fb9d-2f02-42d7-9628-5f929a74230b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33b5b305bcc0a995fd3c592dc8a6f52d0749a6e817aa85844f3e4f31c7dea344 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0f198539-488c-49fc-b480-d6d49e71c825 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, WAI-ARIA can define the interoperability aspects of the Human Interface ABB of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9dd753e0-587f-4a01-bfab-e2fedf635bbe .

camssa:0f1b5656-8583-4c93-90fd-8c741b8528c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, IPv6 is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. IPv6 is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on the IPv6 specification (RFC 2818).\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:738cb119-b31f-4d25-930e-2ec597c498c9 .

camssa:0f1fd1d0-cbc0-4bb3-8d09-1cd076c046ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 can be found for free in several European websites, for instance joinup, the European Open Data Portal, or the Publications Office website. \r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127 \r
\r
OpenPM2 Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/open-pm2-project-management-methodology"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb636049-6099-4561-bc22-ef019081c7e4 .

camssa:0f20308b-b5d7-414d-bea7-efba24bc25c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML provides a set of components enabling users (data users) to store and work with any type of electronic content, fostering the comprehensibility of administrations' rules and processes. When combined with other specifications, ebXML can enable the exposure of interfaces. For example, the specification in combination with the ebXML Business Process Specification (ebXML CCTS ISO/TS 15000-5:2005) fosters interoperability between eForms and ESPD services (see ESPD-EDM UBL adoption reference).\r
\r
ebXML reference, Conformance section:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__53396_365468741\r
\r
ESPD-EDM UBL Codes and identifiers reference:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_technical_handbook.html#_compulsory_attributes\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7df29a1b-dd94-406b-951a-e80a4cd13efd .

camssa:0f2205b3-69b7-4bba-885f-dde40f2851f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Schema.org is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, schema.org can define the interoperability aspects of the Ontologies Catalogue ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:604db0d3-c5fc-455d-b66c-574756e1a97e .

camssa:0f2429dd-2f5e-4d44-b160-c69406b532de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 focuses on the technical specifications for Ethernet and does not specifically address privacy aspects. However, any implementation of Ethernet technology must comply with broader privacy regulations and standards in the EU, such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

Additionally, the ICT Rolling Plans do recommend the use of Ethernet due to its widespread adoption, reliability, and performance. These plans help guide the development and deployment of ICT infrastructures across Europe, ensuring they meet current and future needs.

Rolling Plan for ICT standardisation:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation

GDPR Regulation Reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32016R0679

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:287a1d52-7432-42bc-851e-13131549d6c1 .

camssa:0f25060f-16f2-4653-8e34-a260b039af2b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EIRA includes mechanism to ensure that security and privacy is ensured when designing digital public services. It is done by providing architecture building blocks and organising them as viewpoints that address these specific topics, and also by considering all LOST views, ensuring traceability from legal requirements to technical. 

To go further in detail, there are specific enablers related to identify the requirements for identity and access management, which are the building blocks that will ensure that access to data is controlled. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2ce4c458-9f02-4748-99ea-044fbba75ec9 .

