        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:0fe7546e-e16d-4cb2-9adb-ec7bc8abd4a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 allows time-stamp authority to be used. Typically, a time-stamp authority includes mechanisms to authenticate people who wants access to timestamped information. Thus, using time-stamp authority, it is possible to implement authenticity mechanisms to access shared information between organisations, for example.

ETSI TS 119 512:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.01_60/ts_119512v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d4878e5-0466-45a7-8b68-a09f0d72a9f7 .

camssa:0fedd705-bde6-426d-9fcd-84ff7dda8436 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1cd71a7b6d54631ba58cc8b0655a443d696f49ec74a0f4cccc871de7789d6a60 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0fee6cec-780b-4b8e-8bd7-5c7b397b9c9f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:0fee711c-8ea8-4c55-bfb2-38c8c0a06488 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalDocML has no requirement recognizing and executing the content on the receiving end. The receiving agents must ignore executable content coming from unsecured channels and/or unknown sources. However, the specification is XML based and it provides a set of common elements that are used to validate the information and the structure of the information exchange. This fact contributes to the trustworthy data exchange between parties.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php\r
\r
Akoma Ntoso Media Type Version 1.0:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/akn-media/v1.0/csprd01/akn-media-v1.0-csprd01.html#_Toc417907373"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:954fe959-671c-4fac-98ce-3e2eb00d4f95 .

camssa:0ff7a8b4-106f-4ff3-9496-9ee400183714 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT is recommended by five states, some one those are the Netherlands and Spain, which includes DCAT in their national catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
Netherlands National Catalogue Reference: \r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst \r
\r
Spanish National Catalogue Reference:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:9e2c2877-5103-4934-8440-c60ba2e10c48/Catalogue_of_Standards_NIF_Spain.pdf \r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68b4303a-a52e-45e1-a9c5-c2e33e12a97f .

camssa:0ff86ebd-2cef-4763-ad3b-3f8e5964b0d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Standard for Public Code gives public organizations a model for building their own open source solutions to enable successful future reuse by similar public organizations in other places. It includes guidance for policy makers, city administrators, developers and vendors. This fact can help organisations to make their information and rules available while improving the decission-making process. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8fdc9a07-c0e0-4c0e-9a0f-9031c6948264 .

camssa:0ffab52d-0e2a-415f-aa35-770ae5441302 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A public review is part of the decision-making process defined by the change and release management policy.\r
\r
DCAT-AP change and release management policy:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/document/change-and-release-management-policy-dcat-ap'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:009eeb7d-2cb7-48c9-b11c-770e37a5c08e .

camssa:0ffd773c-fac0-4342-9a5c-57aafb23f232 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/692f5c19-99da-47f3-b40a-0bb6efd516f5"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:0ffde750-d288-4550-b766-f47f2599dbe1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is available for its implementation in any business domain. By contrast, when there exist\r
some difficulties to connect to the certificate status service provider, certificate-using systems could\r
implement CRL (certificate revocation list) processing logic as a fall-back position.\r
\r
OCSP reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7049f8c9-a4b6-446b-979f-d61e8e70240d .

camssa:1000eb1e-3152-4566-b223-37fd184c9f5c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26c3fa9eb08207b2dfbd8d7c3852f0c9db3fdc50491d24db5b2f2eb1acf68732 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:100aed64-f98c-4279-b38a-da9acab9b9a1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:100c0f69-2ea0-4f49-a00e-4605bb7e2d93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 5 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. These Member States are Estonia, Germany, Spain, Sweden and UK.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00fb27ba-7334-4893-8d76-598bccfa7bed .

camssa:100c9ca7-b8c1-42a7-bc98-e4260c287fe7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:100ea844-776e-4afb-8103-ad137a30b1c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UDDI Specification Technical Committee was composed by members coming from the most important IT companies as are IBM, Microsoft, SAP or Oracle. \r
UDDI is along with SOAP and WSDL stack the pillars for the implementation of web services. UDDI is a key enabler for creating an effective service ecosystem. Additionally, the main market share companies support the use and implementation of UDDI, so it is demonstrated its maturity and market acceptance."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3a8445e-c8b6-4dc7-9325-6f20ad1bfb66 .

camssa:10123f58-c5a1-4bf7-a61e-af1100cbb510 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived. \r
             \r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2021/Process-20211102/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:429977e0-04f1-40ec-85c6-55e978e131a4 .

camssa:10287d04-2023-4f1a-abfa-59fa5d28bf30 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3c0edf049cd95575b46d688ed31be0ccce7a5822c5bcc22adf05d491f01f2780 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:102d075e-9e94-47f4-886d-b3e7b1a9100b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of DCAT-AP it to support the evolution of European Public Services by enhancing the searchability and discoverability of datasets across borders. DCAT-AP is an interoperability enabler.\r
 \r
See:                                                                                                                                       \r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/dcat-ap-key-european-data-publishers-reach-data-consumers-and-create-european-open-data-ecosystem_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89c68649-f888-4dde-a5af-1a2bb8fa9051 .

camssa:102dab31-88c6-4949-a71a-9264fabd3d4b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:102e0bf2-46a0-49d7-af29-8e715abe056b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:102e76bb-c5fe-4818-9122-548ffa55b101 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-52e41801b0db7274d934a229fee15e657273655d70d448d16706fcbe0e4f9746 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1031140b-bef7-4b35-95f5-4f003021a523 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a vocabulary to describe assets within a Repository, it provides concepts and properties identifying the content creators and other informative metadata such as dates involved in the release of the solutions described. These facts increase the reliability of the exchanged data. _x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
ADMS Specification W3C:_x000D_\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:327347da-6360-49dd-aea0-b737d7b5c11b .

camssa:103255cd-cb4e-476c-8a53-fca56f7b05f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """According to the 5-star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, FTPS as an internet protocol for the exchange of data, supports the first level of maturity which corresponds to make data available as structured data.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b3ece3a-7803-4685-8696-4046739cf101 .

camssa:10368df3-7538-4196-ba9f-29cf925d1317 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f41cca0d171e6f64dbc2bdeae9fbc87f2ea51ac00185b22114d59ab8a06e78d0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1038e855-9eb8-4bfc-a94e-9d12f380d765 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "JSON is a text format that is completely language independent.  The specification uses conventions that are familiars to C-family of languages, including C, C++, C#, Java, JavaScript, Perl, Python, and many others. For these reasons, JSON is an optimum data exchange and interchange language."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a95d4871-320a-4573-a719-678240e15da1 .

camssa:103a2f5e-f23a-441d-a520-caad001a44b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By allowing to gather different objects signed with electronic signatures in one single ZIP file fosters the implementation of the once-only principle. Moreover, it is included in the context of the Connect Europe Facility’s (CEF) as one of the specifications covering the eSignature Building Block. At the same time, it is implemented in the Digital Signature Services (DSS), across borders initiative which aims to enhance the interoperability and data reuse. \r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/Services+eSignature"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d51c113b-45d0-49af-985f-b9c4c9cb636c .

camssa:10401ee3-c748-46ea-b6df-f03ae7e7d51c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ETSI TS 119 612 is not related to the long-term preservation of data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e61fa75-3e01-4236-ad9e-e15e193220a1 .

camssa:10409b33-d23c-45f1-904e-dbbff9ce848f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:1043f58a-7722-43d9-b7ed-dfc2e0ee29c8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-093c1e09f5a65e4cba0247dcab5a8f4854f3e512db336b1855b9a4c48d3659e0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:10445f42-0baf-4bdc-9573-27c54c07e149 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DID specification is highly usable beyond business-specific domains due to its standardized, interoperable, and decentralized nature. Its applications span government, healthcare, education, finance, IoT, and more, providing secure, verifiable, and user-controlled identity management.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/

DID use cases:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-use-cases/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2b04d37-9ea5-4b98-a5e9-c2a38fff58c6 .

camssa:104728f9-fbb4-456b-a0f6-d1b0f874093e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTP is used as the main protocol for file exchange  by many public organisations. By allowing public administration to share information with others, it  fosters the visibility of data (e.g. Administrative rules, processes etc.) and facilitates public administrations decision-making. \r
\r
An example of implementation supporting this fact would be CIRCABC, a project with the purpose of enhancing the collaboration, communication and document exchange between different European Union's stakeholders. \r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/circabc.pdf \r
https://circabc.europa.eu/faces/jsp/extension/wai/navigation/container.jsp"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:146818bd-56b9-49a5-8d5e-6e1125a46341 .

camssa:104d5dec-d931-4dd0-8e5d-8f99d3218c09 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:104f406e-fae5-4db2-a131-ac75ddcdaf0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:670f4f1d-b2ed-4fbf-862c-c34d8e0078ac .

camssa:104f5d02-723d-4208-b4ce-14ea74822297 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

