camssa:111fe34d-c7db-4717-9de2-0b6521e27503 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of DNS is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:463f4a62-c444-4af3-b364-b325f0c07c70 .

camssa:11216121-f265-4026-bbff-20a6fcc8aa0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"CSV is one of the main points on the publication of Open Data. Using the specification 3 out of 5 stars from Tim Berners Lee's schema for open data are supported. \r
\r
Moreover, some initiatives for the publication of European Organisations data as open data, consequently Linked Open Data have their datasets stored in CSV format. An example of it is the EU Open Data Portal. \r
\r
CSV can be considered a facilitator to publish public administrations data as open data. As 5 Stars Open Data model of Tim Berners-Lee states, CSV makes sure content is available on the web, structures data and makes it usable in a non-proprietary open format.\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180\r
\r
EU Open Data Portal:\r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/home\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af909d78-cd70-4abb-aeee-f2a772716d29 .

camssa:1129b226-f2f6-444a-aecc-b730e65e6dc2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of CPOV is to provide a reusable data model for describing public organisations in the European Union. The CPOV helps to identify where responsibilities and functions are duplicated or overlapped. So, it helps to comprehend the administrative rules and data of public administration.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf4c4bbb-dc7f-42e9-890c-abbbb15ce932 .

camssa:112aa1bc-10cb-4460-967d-f0cf5ffb27b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5372fb8-7403-4951-b9fe-ccc92ee4b891 .

camssa:112cf94f-15c4-49a4-83bc-2d262ae5a917 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:11302a64-ebe2-466e-842a-5fc083beb23e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e8c3529a6146f0b0d269112be717ba4e9c5979ea4f43f57d217c0f998d26ce17 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:11302d23-d845-44ca-bc57-08ff4b2fce5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL allows the expression of permissions, prohibitions, and obligations related to the use of digital \r
content. When used in systems that involve the exchange of digital content, ODRL can be employed to define and enforce secure access controls, ensuring that only authorized entities can access and use the data.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfcd9bf8-b70f-4ce6-a9db-ddd53e9f7e93 .

camssa:1131ebb0-1034-4977-bfad-f199c6de4529 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8eb17470327d32b3bb523447fe72ee5c60ddb03e81dae318b485fbe05f48a844 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:1132f4c5-c5ab-472f-8d7f-d638894f7169 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WS-BPEL is one of the main pillars for Open Web Platform, a full programming environment for cross-platform applications with access to device capabilities. Moreover, developers can have stability into implement and plan through WS-BPEL.\r
\r
The specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9032d017-a789-4f23-8c3c-a0996186a163 .

camssa:113ab436-ad9c-46f9-8e4d-45ea55ffaa10 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7400d45-a5ac-477c-8eba-add44c478c39 .

camssa:11468342-7d82-4f53-bfff-9a6718822d52 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:114a8415-c84c-444d-94fb-072bb3bf51f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is independent from any particular software, hardware, or operating system. So, it can be \r
said that EuroVoc is independent of any specific technology.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c7f64cf-3384-4e50-bf55-23ae86968383 .

camssa:114d77f9-b415-4791-913d-3e76158ac4e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a367166c-f243-40d3-8465-4e5e4ec770b2 .

camssa:1150135b-bd92-4e50-845d-0d9caa4656c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-138786a6e7517e10b94e83ec3b3e7ac79b4c49dcbeaef8d8e993c8df0d173529 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:11550a56-2503-4eb3-8a3f-ea619303cc2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XACML specification ensures that access control policies are not only well-defined and consistently enforced but also transparent and auditable, meeting the needs of administrators and compliance requirements.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d594b206-9e3e-4ff5-8ea0-542e08ee2abb .

camssa:1158afd8-00e9-43a8-8d9b-3492f9e9c5f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Implementing SMP within a eDelivery environment does not hamper the interoperability of systems since SMP is compatible with the scalability of networks and users. The development of these environments can be sustainable and adapt to the user needs without harming implementations.\r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505000"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05590830-f6ac-4625-b35f-8e26a7c0fd02 .

camssa:115930a7-b920-4fc3-bcec-2c4d859fb9c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OWASP defines and evolves specifications on a community-driven basis, where all the stakeholders have the opportunity to contribute to the development of the specification.\r
\r
The assets of the specifications are publically available on Github and all users can create issues or add modifications.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf \r
\r
Contribute page: \r
https://owaspsamm.org/contributing/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5a88e0e-41cd-4420-8112-6a8aee228674 .

camssa:115a7685-1a3d-4820-bf3a-a297fde5f081 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
