camssa:11629d6d-c758-4199-a851-035caa74261c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV enables expressing machine-readable metadata about use and processing of personal data based on legislative requirements such as the GDPR. Modelling of the GDPR concepts by the DPV contributes to the once-only principle given that it is meant to be an interoperable vocabulary for representing information about the use and processing of personal data.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bfd5043-340d-4585-9e4b-8d01c693faa3 .

camssa:1162b75e-8451-44ce-95a9-f5906b895b82 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. This Core Vocabulary fosters interoperability between public administrations, cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff28a7b5-3ceb-487a-afab-484ab2917516 .

camssa:11695f16-bde2-4075-bf1e-85d9df24be9c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI TS 119 512, operates under the ETSI Intellectual Property Rigths (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free.\r
\r
ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:924fd4de-6482-455f-bf69-f129445f08c3 .

camssa:116a49b7-af2d-40dc-8e9b-46120f9de694 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Assessments of the efficiency of CIM NGSI-LD API primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. A 2021-paper focuses on enhancing the semantic capabilities of the oneM2M architecture by providing solid contributions to the oneM2M standards. During the study phase where possible approaches to a discovery and data aggregation solution are analysed with respect to the use cases and requirements, there are also looks to the query and discovery mechanisms already available, starting from the ones defined by CIM NGSI-LD API.

ETSI SmartM2M Technical Report 103716: https://inria.hal.science/hal-03261059/document'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:494a5a2c-9cb3-4f83-82c8-e6d3296a4993 .

camssa:116dee6d-3c86-4882-9f17-b0b7b9877391 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although FTPS is an alternative of FTP for a secure communication internet protocol and it has been supported by some commercial file transfer tools, SFTP is easier to implement and it works better over NATs and firewalls without the issues that hamper FTPS implementations. So, it does not have a complete market acceptance.\r
\r
FTPS - Obsolescent Secure FTP:\r
https://www.ssh.com/ssh/ftp/ftps\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:770d962a-6398-4e18-a2b9-56e4d56890a0 .

camssa:11753d80-fb8b-47a8-970c-ed8f85d434b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) is a solution used to encrypt data, making it more secure against attacks or attempts to access data in an unauthorised way. In this context, the standard not only addresses data protection but also interoperability and collaboration. Moreover, AES has been assessed in many papers and discussed in terms of how it can be implemented in different contexts. Finally, it has been integrated into solutions such as VeraCrypt.

VeraCrypt AES project:
https://veracrypt.eu/en/AES.html

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df9b3819-ad57-40ab-a66c-bdccd6f376cd .

camssa:117601f7-e782-4a5e-b084-847304adf139 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e18b1d5c-14e5-4308-ba86-2daf7e8b9211 .

camssa:11849f93-87f4-4013-a0c5-8de3b865eefb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was produced in 2004, and it has been followed at European level. These Best Practices have been evolved together with the application profile used in the European Platform for the reusability of interoperability Solutions, Joinup. \r
\r
W3C Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3b7e486-4509-4a15-973b-5f6bf4f54c57 .

camssa:1184f56d-bcfd-4d6d-8dab-1b97ce8009ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SFIA is not related to the secure processing of data. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a126d972-9039-44fe-8e85-df7b98861613 .

camssa:11867401-80e5-4550-85ce-f9e0b5f3c49e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'FTP is developed and maintained by IETF, a widely recognised open international community developing standards to enhance the internet. \r
\r
IETF Reference: \r
https://www.ietf.org/\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2b3bca2f-c9cc-403a-b5f4-073f172211cc .

camssa:11926352-4b7d-457d-b962-7f035775555b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:1192e94c-c459-41ed-bfc0-a7c8b2c08f31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XSLT is a language for transforming XML documents. Therefore, it fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of public administrations data and services as it facilitates the visibility of the documents. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b16c874b-efc7-4c02-a64e-c6cc198b71eb .

camssa:119607b7-c092-4893-a723-495bafa9f2d7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17bea234285e6e633e4e21105358610ad5f5f0eaaf82f4bd50cb64ec11538984 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:119d3672-6c09-4f56-9a9a-f73998a43303 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the primary focus of W3C Verifiable Credentials (VC) is on secure and privacy-preserving credential exchange, they can play a role in supporting and enhancing the modeling of certain business processes. Verifiable Credentials provide a standardized way to express and exchange claims, and this capability can be leveraged in various business contexts.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee495d47-b829-4d8e-b2f0-289bcdf96b8b .

camssa:11a5a3c2-f897-4002-9fba-ccd0c51bbbbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 establishes a common methodology for the development of processes. The adoption of this methodology can positively impact the organisational interoperability between organisations developing services or products under this methodology since they would be acting and carrying out similar steps that would allow the cooperation between them. Cooperation in cross-border projects is a powerful feature enhancing efficiency and effectiveness.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b8c51a1-7be3-40a2-9c8a-5ca4a363ab34 .

camssa:11a80d4a-9b62-4400-aeb2-af9d914f0193 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI TS 119 612 specification establishes mechanisms such as digital signatures that allow to ensure data authenticity and integrity. In this sense, such mechanisms allow public administrations and organisations to share data in its original form. 

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6ebac84-3232-49cf-b3c1-dca9241ce672 .

camssa:11ae4ba8-edc4-4d9a-bfb2-31dd79f3c27b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:11b02d3e-7ade-429e-bb4a-6a0f5cd68145 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8954ddabf37f4899562b9ea4c8f0bbf204f3e48c9203043bc231f368092396a2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:11b05feb-82ff-4fc7-a4f8-401dceb48e40 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:11b18bde-ae79-48c2-8db8-a17b1d29ce69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Shape Expressions (ShEx) language provides a structural schema for RDF data. This can be used to document APIs or datasets, aid in development of API-conformant messages, minimize defensive programming, guide user interfaces, or anything else that involves a machine-readable description of data organization and typing requirements.\r
\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6ac2a3c-f808-4639-bd2e-b6a4417fe5a6 .

camssa:11b306aa-483b-4e53-a9a5-9349951cb731 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "60" .

