camssa:12363b11-5530-461a-a9dc-aa555e0662cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The use of HTTPS not only ensures that the communication between the user and the service is protected, but also provides the exposure interface of the message that will be sent to the requester.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e00cbc2-4f39-4c3f-8478-237cbddf52e4 .

camssa:1236b119-e709-4e7d-8155-a76c318cc24e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSS v2.1 is dependent from HTML, its main function is to describe how HTML elements should be displayed on web documents.\r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2cf62404-7a5d-441a-8408-9f69392e7e3c .

camssa:123daf35-ccbc-4a50-81c3-d6e207df0d77 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 covers data transmission, media access control, and network performance; however, it does not directly address security. Its design, though, facilitates the implementation of robust security measures alongside higher-layer protocols and practices, enabling secure data exchange.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cddfabaa-2ad3-4d4a-a500-f4b0a9ca4e3a .

camssa:12406136-8503-48d2-b59d-861880df920d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that uses CAdES (ISO 14533-1:2014) nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification. However, the specification CAdES from ETSI, is involved in some cross-border projects as "Analysis of standards related to Trust Service Providers" developed by ENISA (European Union Agency for Network and Information Security) which is a centre of network and information security expertise for the EU, its member states, the private sector and Europe’s citizens. \r
\r
ENISA project:\r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/tsp_standards_2015/at_download/fullReport\r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81a2308c-5c43-41bf-ba9f-9d48b98b4b41 .

camssa:1241f7a0-7c17-4e2a-a69f-533bc7662d93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of HTTPS is not related to the provision of access control mechanisms. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf6b9183-aa81-4c4b-9eae-9bb95e0cba1d .

camssa:12450ce0-9183-4431-b4e5-99972d31a21b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of FTPS is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:010443c2-3d1d-4ef5-8a52-149e4658ebca .

