camssa:134c761f-d999-4a12-8bab-eefefb8c4308 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The LegalDocML is developed by OASIS using the technical commities (TC). The goal of the TC in charge of LegalDocML development is to collect requirements from the community of the stakeholders who create, manage and use legislative and legal documents  in order to extend and refine the standard.\r
The main objective of the OASIS community is to promote individuals, organizations, and governments come together to solve some of the world’s biggest technical challenges through the development of open code and open standards\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php\r
\r
OASIS home page: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7784689b-1e44-47c3-a3a9-bd9e1cbbad61 .

camssa:134e61ca-863b-442d-8158-b183cf8e738c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documents assessing and documenting DQV features and providing 
possible improvements of its performance among other aspects. 
In "DQAF: Towards DQV-Based Dataset Quality Annotation Using the Web Annotation Data Model" it is proposed to use the DQV specification for a Dataset Quality Annotation Framework (DQAF).
Furthermore, there are ducumentation such as "Introducing the Data Quality Vocabulary (DQV)", which makes and assessment of DQV and explains its components as well as how it works. 
 
"DQAF: Towards DQV-Based Dataset Quality Annotation Using the Web Annotation Data Model" reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/7799649

"Introducing the Data Quality Vocabulary (DQV)" reference:
https://www.semantic-web-journal.net/system/files/swj2079.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82e59c52-8f4c-4d6a-95d3-38f6e7ad32e7 .

