camssa:13dd03db-6090-447a-ba0b-5f8a0e40159a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Following the completion of the research into conformity tests and certifications, an open-source tool has been identified that enables the testing of implementations with time-stamping commands. This tool is designed to ensure that the implementations are developed in an appropriate manner.

TSP certification tool:
https://www.freetsa.org/index_en.php

OpenSSL:
https://www.openssl.org/docs/manmaster/man1/ts.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b85eff2d-00f5-48f5-9f3f-ffcf95f9886c .

camssa:13df14e3-cf69-4bbf-867d-718743c33217 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is a specification that provides a core vocabulary that allows the description and representation of \r
information in a standardised and machine-readable format fostering the data exchange and the \r
interoperability of organisations and resources using it. Moreover, the specification offers serialisation in \r
common formats for open data publication and shareability such as RDF or JASON-LD. \r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b75d7b6a-c8c8-41d4-8e50-0def658d83dc .

camssa:13df518b-eae6-44f3-b948-c0402170c18c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:13e22dc4-ab60-4c7b-a3b5-bab4b24dd417 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ADMS is not related to restricting access to information or data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39d4068d-c0a7-4d26-95b3-5bc7e3902d0e .

camssa:13e8acbd-09d8-454d-ad33-0a24d6471edb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of Core Location Vocabulary is not related to the long-term preservation of data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0582c06e-1ad1-41c6-8946-beeae69ce701 .

camssa:13f3590c-3d59-4349-8ee7-b247c9c2da1d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:13f38b87-7e82-4cf7-ba85-fa1da0f579bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. Moreover, there is a public review in the TC process.\r
 \r
The specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:260a12e4-a098-4db9-8a8e-300bbd2216fe .

camssa:13f70a8f-c787-4c42-8285-df7d647a0fe2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification accommodates extensions, particularly through its structure for country-specific customisations, which allows jurisdictions to incorporate fields aligned with local regulatory, legal, or operational requirements. This flexibility ensures that publiccode.yml can adapt to diverse administrative contexts while maintaining a standardised core, promoting both local relevance and broad interoperability. The specification thus supports extended functionality in a manner that upholds international compatibility and adaptability to specific national needs.

Publiccode.yml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Publiccode.yml section 2, Country-Specific Extensions
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/country.html#country-specific-extensions'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b2b5d39-e3fd-411f-9c0e-7606626cb95d .

camssa:13f8a41a-79d6-4143-9652-e9d4149a709e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'If a DID method specification is written for a public-facing verifiable data registry where corresponding DIDs and DID documents might be made publicly available, it is critical that those DID documents contain no personal data. Personal data can instead be transmitted through other means such as Verifiable Credentials [VC-DATA-MODEL], or service endpoints under control of the DID subject or DID controller. 

DIDs restriction of access W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#keep-personal-data-private'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed27e1f4-5d7b-4d6a-ace5-efd5aef49d33 .

camssa:13fa7956-4f80-4605-882b-04c7ca5fab16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:997c6e35-0be3-4de4-9e32-b5fb58af1daa .

camssa:14024396-d4ef-49d1-92bf-1285e06ecc6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are no Member States recommending SMP in their ICT National Catalogues.\r
 \r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e710cb27-2134-4d5d-9476-ec6185bca987 .

camssa:140a6884-8e0d-460b-b66b-b70056dbc1ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTP is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0ad58487-bf0a-4215-95ac-ad094f550215 .

