camssa:1417bcda-7f34-447f-9765-057147601aab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies  \r
Technical reports:\r
https://www.w3.org/standards/history/shacl """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:211d69aa-1cd6-494b-be91-a404e27089d4 .

camssa:14185d82-e8e0-48d8-83a5-a16febb86c17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JSON is a lightweight specification that allows data exchange between different applications fostering interoperability and data visibility. The specification is scarcely used for document exchange. Therefore, JSON adoption does not hamper the interoperability and scalability of systems. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.json.org/xml.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:745e9eea-1187-4c1f-b5b5-5b3aa28039a8 .

camssa:14196608-b14d-4b17-8ba3-96f00cd76313 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification can be considered a European Standard as it is listed in the European Union Observatory for ICT Standardisation (EUOS). The EUOS will thoroughly monitor the global Standardisation landscape, providing a comprehensive and accurate coverage of the most important ICT Standards, Working Groups and Technical Committees that affect the key ICT topics of the Digital Single Market and the EU ICT Rolling Plan for Standardisation.\r
\r
EUOS: https://standict.eu/euos'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:578ea8cb-ddd8-4bef-9d57-084605d476b8 .

