        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-2614723a75c6a002b733f97562482608046dd2e6da97e3073312dbbdaf482279 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:144b55aa-25c3-4ac2-8159-db8f25a060de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6743319b-ad8c-41f1-b27c-90f9ea206da6 .

camssa:1452e241-21a8-45e2-9cc0-8876e264a346 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1275ea52-7ce6-44e2-8b67-6a7869c07b6d .

camssa:1456aeb5-1aa9-476f-b316-5d6094563ff1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Better regulation provides a set of guidelines to guarantee that policies and laws development, implementation and evaluation are properly established. At this point, the Better regulation toolbox includes a set of recommendations, best practices and requirements whose purpose is to ensure and enhance the cross-border application and organisational interoperability as much as possible.\r
\r
Betterr Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd310247-311e-4098-b6a5-ae2cca6a1792 .

camssa:1462d68e-33b5-4c88-a1bb-d5399c14349d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'iCalendar can support the visibility of certain administrative procedures, rules data, and services by providing a comprehensive set of mechanisms to enable the exchange and management of  calendar-related data such as envent descriptions, services availability, and location information.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ac519aa-6d4d-49ce-9f2a-50259db5aa58 .

camssa:146818bd-56b9-49a5-8d5e-6e1125a46341 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-105c699a138c27ab9a1af9174253cd7488b278f700acdbb1bdbcc3e0b9c5ec3d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:14703c13-849d-46f6-962e-e820bdc1cdcd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XFDL is based on XML, which is inherently a portable data format. XML allows data to be easily shared across different systems and platforms because it's a text-based, standardised format that can be parsed and processed by a wide range of applications.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:468a8bc2-2914-40da-b550-e286bbfcbc65 .

