camssa:154f02a2-e7d3-4cdd-9e4a-6d8b0a653647 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML was the first standard markup language to develop web resources. HTML files are used to exchange information through the web, and they foster data portability between systems and applications.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:efb513c8-a0b4-4b28-9788-ab7da75d5df4 .

camssa:154fbf95-c144-479b-88a0-acd6b40006f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary can help to facilitate the modelling of business processes. The Core Vocabularies can become the basis of a context-specific data model used to exchange data among existing information systems. 

Core Vocabularies:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/core-vocabularies

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:821df186-ddab-4714-b825-488828c6f6f7 .

