camssa:15c46b0f-cf05-4204-851e-5cefd6d72e5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is independent of any specification and can be implemented without any dependency on platforms.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d29bee3-2190-4f5f-bf9d-70519819f9f1 .

camssa:15c9ada7-e65c-4334-88d8-215a02fe65cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification can indeed foster the creation of collaborative communities that share software information on national and European platforms. By standardising metadata for public sector software, it allows for easy exchange and visibility of projects, which can encourage collaboration, co-creation, and reuse among different administrations and sectors. This structured approach aligns with EIF Recommendation 32, as it provides a consistent way to document and share software, promoting transparency and joint development efforts at various levels.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

EIF: 
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aeb2aa83-9887-4ae8-a06d-3f3e473002f3 .

