camssa:15f3e448-abf2-4f72-8ddd-88fe07d43531 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are some comparative reports of SFIA and other ICT skills and competence frameworks such as the e-Competence Framework (see SFIA reference, Tools and Resources section, Collaborations subsection, 'SFIA – e-CF Comparison & Mapping Review' document), which indirectly assesses the SFIA specification's effectiveness.\r
\r
SFIA reference, Tools and Resources section, Collaborations subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/tools-and-resources/collaborations\r
\r
SFIA reference, Tools and Resources section, Collaborations subsection, 'SFIA – e-CF Comparison & Mapping Review' document:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/assets/documents/e-cf/sfia-e-cf-comparison-mapping-report-v1-0.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf15ef6e-80eb-4f4f-99f1-3a29686b2df4 .

camssa:15f4a8ed-d7a4-46a8-af41-9e4a38913cd0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39ffef052c31580b50b418f3991e9de7db4dc182fcf96f5a447d7f8e09560612 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:15f96005-0a02-4219-84fd-a18f05677c41 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TGF is an open framework that is freely available for use and adaptation by governments and other stakeholders, without any licensing or patent restrictions. The TGF is based on open standards and interoperability, and its development has been guided by principles of openness, transparency, and inclusivity. The TGF specification is published and made available under a royalty-free license, which allows users to copy, distribute, and transmit the specification, and to adapt it for their own use, as long as they give appropriate credit to the original source.\r
\r
OASIS IPR policy:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0a12953-12c4-46ca-a001-02a5f37e5a81 .

camssa:1600957f-f968-4eca-a7cd-d3cd0d46945f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 offers some provisions on the portability of documents containing digital signatures.  This can be provided by preservation and validation services, whose main functions are to authenticate and preserve the chain of evidence of official documents. Nonetheless, ETSI TS 119 511 only specifies the requirements of these functionalities, while its companion document ETSI TS 119 512 provides the protocols to implement these services. Therefore, ETSI TS 119 511 supports the evolution of European public services.\r
\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d9c1e10-f91f-4b5b-918f-78b137f39f3c .

camssa:1604da80-1152-4f1c-b513-1dfa2b5b8503 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

