camssa:162035dd-5027-497f-bdeb-065c7d8a062d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'When it comes to services related to the access of any kind of archives, OAIS can simplify the delivery of public services insofar it provides a framework from which to model archiving systems that facilitate the comprehension of information to the designated community, as well as it also guides on the processes to follow for the accessing of information in the context where it applies.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7dbb78d-1076-4f6f-9ee8-0416cb1947c0 .

camssa:162c6136-b211-47b9-8f47-fa63d88268d7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:162f6ce7-f4a3-455c-9539-4764b441e968 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was initially developed in 2017 with its initial version 1.0. It was used as the basis for the development of European Specifications and building blocks enhancing the development of public services. However, the version analysed is 2.0 which was released by January 2020. For this reason the specification is not sufficiently mature for its use.\r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f6aa9b2-d800-44c3-9250-bef0342527dc .

camssa:163341d5-c386-4fa7-a1bd-46f7a978dd77 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating and Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all of the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:\r
- Technical excellence;\r
- prior implementation and testing;\r
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;\r
- openness and fairness; and \r
- timeliness.\r
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fbcab81b-1296-4753-a322-0e05d74c38ee .

camssa:16353261-9b6d-4b99-887c-b2064fed92d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "TLS 1.2 is independent of any specification and can be implemented without dependencies with technologies or platforms. Moreover, IETF is a neutral-vendor Standard Developing Organisation that has developed the technical specification independently of any vendor product."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11302a64-ebe2-466e-842a-5fc083beb23e .

camssa:1637d9e9-8167-4b9e-a396-4018dbb68268 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISAE 3402 is not related to enabling digital service delivery channels, therefore, this criterion \r
is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b943ad4e-cac3-4625-af80-6cc22c89ce75 .

camssa:164900d0-8e81-406c-a6d4-3bb41edfca31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C provides a Markup Validation Service for free to validate CSS, and (X)HTML using style sheets.\r
\r
W3C Markup Validation Service:\r
https://validator.w3.org/\r
\r
Online CSS validator:\r
https://jigsaw.w3.org/css-validator/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a66f975a-bd43-4f28-97b4-4b72a5856738 .

camssa:164f594c-838d-4958-8419-696f43382dc1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI TS 119 512 specification complements ETSI TS 119 511 and specifies protocols for trust service providers providing long-term data preservation services of digital signatures and of general data. Moreover, the preservation service may include a long-term storage, or a temporary storage. Thus, long-term preservation can be guaranteed with long-term storage service of the specification.

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb9e78d8-455d-4c1f-9bf0-d1c377cdc53d .

camssa:1664b43d-c65d-420a-ac1d-46491ea44b62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are document of the European Comission assessing the suitability of XAdES specification.\r
\r
See:\r
 https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html#_xades_profiles"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7af2b21-0def-4284-bdd1-246b9a2226b0 .

