camssa:16678ac9-d19c-4de1-bbb0-007816186235 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Several projects, such as "A Prototype Cross-Border GML Data Service," have created new opportunities for integrating cross-border spatial data services using Geography Mark-up Language (GML) and XSLT for schema transformations. Additionally, the INSPIRE Directive and its related regulations form a key cross-border EU initiative, supported by the ISA programme.

Schema Translations by XSLT For GML-Encoded Geospatial Data In Heterogeneous Web-Service Environment:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/237698411_SCHEMA_TRANSLATIONS_BY_XSLT_FOR_GML-ENCODED_GEOSPATIAL_DATA_IN_HETEROGENEOUS_WEB-SERVICE_ENVIRONMENT

Infrastructure for Spatial Information in Europe:
https://ies-svn.jrc.ec.europa.eu/projects/registry-development/wiki/Re3gistry_1_0_documentation#_cp3
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:961849b3-f0ce-4488-835a-373937d84d33 .

