camssa:16e7e71f-a6d8-49f0-a911-2cfffb0dfee0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The goal of ETSI TS 119 511 is to provide the  legal framework for the conformity of the Electronic Signatures against European regulations.  ETSI TS 119 511 cannot be understood without its companion documents, insofar the suite of specifications ESI forms the basis for the conformity assessment of trust services following the eIDAS regulation.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e3e6a70-34b8-4b41-b512-d753fc325404 .

camssa:16e81b2d-5d08-4a2e-bccd-ba12ee633c0b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After researching there has been no success finding any assessments about the specification effectiveness.\r
\r
How the specification can help ensuring trustworthiness of information:\r
https://script-ed.org/article/blockchain-based-electronic-time-stamps-and-the-eidas-regulation-the-best-of-both-worlds/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2d3b5c9-2469-43cb-b4ab-b1d5ad86e3aa .

camssa:16ecd14a-a943-4163-a58d-7631813d3df3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c967c90bfc7bc13426924eca012de349ae51d4e8f652fe64bfbec2cccc8c8146 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:16edf3b3-b22c-4bae-88a7-720e87dab7cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI, the SDO/SSO that created and currently maintains the specification, explains that most ETSI test specifications are developed according to the well-proven methodology defined in ISO/IEC 9646. This standard, which covers the entire test development process, provides an excellent basis for the production of high-quality test frameworks and specifications.

ETSI Conformance Testing: 
https://portal.etsi.org/Services/Centre-for-Testing-Interoperability/ETSI-Approach/Conformance

ISO/IEC 9646: https://www.iso.org/standard/17473.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55b7738e-558b-489a-8f9c-0daeb2f30460 .

camssa:16eec4e1-b2cb-4f97-a195-c9eb33df4edd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The implementation of the specification fosters interoperability between administrations across borders. Moreover, it is a European interoperability solution component included in the eDelivery building block. The purpose of the building block is to enhance the eGovernment in the context of the interoperability and the reuse of administrations’ data. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0e2d3df-99e9-4925-a73d-a64684ef3c2f .

camssa:16efbb14-1cac-4241-8f97-2da10f1dde23 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:16f35b84-c08f-49a1-bead-478a5b8a41cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ESPD has not been found included in the catalogue of any Member State.\r
\r
CAMSS List of standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2dd88ac-eda3-40c8-b431-8b28d0549ad1 .

camssa:16f586b0-b436-4871-b15e-9b2ac40c3ef0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES has sufficient market acceptance for its use in the development of products. In the following link there is an example of integrating digital signatures like CAdES in a framework.\r
\r
Digital signature service:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d7009cc-6e06-4479-8b52-99086d90744c .

camssa:16fcd010-9606-481a-b172-a83d569377ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, OpenPM2 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Service Delivery Model" ABBs of the EIRA Organisational View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31c9c169-a5ae-4251-8bd2-3da3cd2eda1d .

camssa:16feb7b3-3638-498f-ac97-1c154c1ff152 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:16ff4ea5-b030-4366-a2be-3aa156b9513c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:170529d1-642b-4b98-854c-af3d1a4e3d53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "HTTP has ben in use by the World-Wide Web global information initiative since 1990. That fact evidences that the standard has the sufficient market acceptance and is sufficiently maturity.                                                                   See:                                                                                                                                        https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2616"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55a3f134-4b2b-4b6c-9dd4-5667029a5300 .

camssa:17068a97-9ec8-4934-9071-791fd5d0e98f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """In the maintenance and development process that the Publications Office has developed there is no public consultation foreseen in the development process of the specification. However, it is worth to note that users can contribute to a previous phase.\r
\r
EuroVoc\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc\r
\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8681c60f-9fd9-4357-812d-7e33d686bc3a .

camssa:1708cfc0-9f0e-4395-aae0-24b18fa6b89e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs is used in Self-sovereign identity (SSI) in eIDAS project. This, is the next step beyond user-centric identity. Both concepts are based on the idea that a user must be central to the administration of his/her digital identity, which requires not only a user’s ability to use an identity across multiple locations but also true control over that digital identity, creating user autonomy.

SSI eIDAS: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ssi-eidas-bridge'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94210199-e0d0-428d-ae8b-6b3382f63ee6 .

camssa:17142722-dcbe-427c-9bd5-9d908d04155d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SFIA is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, the specification can define the interoperability aspects of the Interoperability Skill ABB of the EIRA Organisational View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/v110 '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ae12003-327e-4d9d-b9d4-2e2d98eb4dab .

camssa:1720fac8-b031-441f-8729-f27abc75dea9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1725dd31-0cb3-458d-aa16-3466f8c16975 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1726a784-3ec4-49ce-8a61-ab1b0678afe5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"JSON is a specification used for data exchange between different platforms, this fact facilitates the visibility and comprehensibility of administration's data. Moreover, it eases the communication between administrations enhancing the decision-making process. \r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dfa3b449-c140-415e-a940-63d118d9a562 .

camssa:1728548a-f6a3-4161-b663-330b0d8c21e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV enables expressing machine-readable metadata about use and processing of personal data based on legislative requirements such as the GDPR. Modelling of the GDPR concepts by the DPV contributes to the once-only principle given that it is meant to be an interoperable vocabulary for representing information about the use and processing of personal data.\r
\r
DPV specification: \r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa5fff9d-65fb-46c9-90b8-31b9a0bff163 .

camssa:1729523e-a934-45fa-9bad-bca32a937eea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of GraphQL is not related to enabling the secure processing of data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47852c0c-da95-44a9-8c04-1e2e2ca75a41 .

camssa:172cf8cc-e3dd-4f38-bdfd-8bed65fd962b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10762e12-6f86-4774-961f-39f6fb47bf2e .

camssa:172fe1c9-9ce0-4ef0-af3a-0f19c51b4dff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e9e0cf4a339c837607828404dd0e9b360d643528fcc1df488a95ca67166acea3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1731d94d-fa2b-4cf6-aa4d-425adf2363f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2cedd44f05183dae5548108bdeace2c092b84c7c5d89c475b0741ddae7fc7b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1733a9df-f784-4575-aa16-76689760d240 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1739f203-3ec5-4f16-ac47-ab40e0e45ac0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NIST asserts rights outside of the United States. The public is granted the non-exclusive, perpetual, paid-up, royalty-free, worldwide right to reprint works in all formats, including print, electronically, and online, and in all subsequent editions and derivative works.

NIST IRP and F/RAND principles:
https://www.nist.gov/open/copyright-fair-use-and-licensing-statements-srd-data-software-and-technical-series-publications#:~:text=To%20the%20extent%20NIST%20may%20assert%20rights%20outside,and%20in%20all%20subsequent%20editions%2C%20and%20derivative%20works.

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f360980a-88aa-46cf-8f93-c3a89e551000 .

camssa:173a03ad-d928-47be-bc19-74ae11a011ec a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
