    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:17806bce-b491-48e8-b9d7-696d28a73c11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS is included within a national catalogue of recommended specifications. It belongs to Ireland. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of this Member State is partially aligned with the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. There is middle-low performance in the Interopearability Governance, Legal and Organisational layers, and there exist some shorcuts in the Conceptual Model with regards to Internal Information sources and services, Base Registries and the conceptual model, compared to the EU average.\r
\r
National catalogue Ireland: \r
https://data.gov.ie/pages/opendatatechnicalframework#recommended-standards-for-open-data\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85a2a440-75c7-4109-b082-a9bf3301b355 .

camssa:1781b34b-fe04-4c3e-84b0-09bf0da5684d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17864a25-121c-4062-9bc5-8564eea1f13c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of TSP is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. 

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:453aae9f-4728-43bf-9578-9a30ac95cc71 .

camssa:1788e821-439e-4b84-a7c6-06e6235ab000 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a64b01ca9e737c550b205ba3a8a46b3fcfc9447b648ba8ef15d62d3ada26141 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:178d6a71-ac26-474c-8b0c-eac023e89c69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """One of the main purposes of the specification and the OASIS TC in charge of its development is to be extensible, that is to allow modifications to the models within the AKOMA NTOSO framework so that local customisation can be achieved without sacrificing interoperability with other systems.\r
\r
Moreover, the European Commission includes in its Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation and the related standardisation activities of the same rolling plan. Referencing it as a good candidate to support the eGovernment.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:520faf2e-bb25-41ba-aa6f-72b6c03f7c21 .

camssa:178f89a0-6d6a-4a7a-96ca-5ab2fd6ba5b1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XACML is the basis of the Policy Management impelemented by the cross-border project SEMIRAMIS. This 
project aims to provide e-services with the required underlying secure authentication and management approach.

Semiramis home page: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:882eb2f1-7d3e-4f19-a1e8-a1b93bf5c853 .

camssa:178fa1d0-cee2-467f-a733-a36be15bc8d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is included in 9 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. This Member
States are Cyrpus, Estonia, France, Germany, Greece, Norway, Poland, Slovenia and Spain.

National Catalogue of Cyprus:
https://dits.dmrid.gov.cy/dmrid/dits/dits.nsf/all/B83AA8E4EB4EFD19C225855800288B10/$file/Cyprus%
20eGovernment%20Interoperability%20Framework_new%20EIF_v2.0-To%20Publish.pdf

National Catalogue of Spain:
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio
/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f4360a2-266d-4ce9-8e57-7cc343a7ba5b .

camssa:17924540-8020-4b39-8f0c-851b41113262 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ab118934e7af3d561b9036668a1de9f17c020207e8ebb0ed33d9405e12eeef4c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1792763a-aeb3-4dda-85f3-d8918600ac34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though no explicit evidence has been found of any implementation of the ODF at the European Level, there are several recommendations from the EC and member states for the usage of the specification when sharing or collaborating between and with administrations.  \r
\r
No formal project has been found where ODF is used for this purpose. \r
\r
EC recommends supporting open document format: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/open-source-observatory-osor/news/ec-recommends-supporting-open \r
\r
UK Sharing and collaborating with government documents \r
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/open-standards-for-government/sharing-or-collaborating-with-government-documents """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:968ad4ec-9777-48bc-a46e-d01f5dcff856 .

camssa:179dd5dd-f073-459c-a43b-ddaabafb729b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAIS reference model provides means for the restriction of access to information or data through its access control mechanisms. Access controls are a fundamental part of the OAIS architecture, and they allow archive managers to control who has access to the digital objects and metadata stored in the system.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d065e3a3-5983-4308-b5ae-fb089d6d2a64 .

camssa:17a131fe-db29-4a50-b7a4-58b1d203dc2a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17ac10d9-7829-41e0-811f-77c8497d47f1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17be0020-cb48-475a-a9c7-c7585d724746 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the time of elaborating this assessment, this specification is not included in any EIRA ABB in the current EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS)._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:28227288-c3a0-49a8-b106-7c84f97f223e .

camssa:17bea3a6-5490-48f4-885b-c95271d4618a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Changes to the YAML language itself will be made using a Requrest For Comments (RFC) process. The project has an active core team but they do all changes publicly and take some direction from issues and pull requests. Despite this, the working group is still working out the final details of this process, so for now there are no details about how it will be this public review.

Contribution to YAML:
https://github.com/yaml/yaml-spec/blob/main/.github/contributing.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03ac9ad4-e35a-427a-8e75-87f09a4ccdde .

camssa:17bf0995-8fc0-48a1-b9d3-c0776be67a43 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17c1da9a-dc00-44c8-b39a-06d0450a8e7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 specifies policy and security protocols for trust service providers providing long-term preservation of digital signatures and of general data using digital signature techniques.  The specification performance is closely related to the different specifications involved in electronic signatures across borders. In the context of the European internal market (see article below) , it can be considered as an asset for the creation of solutions enhancing the interoperability between administrations and businesses when eSignature, and long preservation of electronic records is needed. \r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 Working group:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/webapp/workprogram/Report_WorkItem.asp?WKI_ID=61427\r
\r
Article: Towards a standardised preservation service for qualified electronic signatures and qualified electronic seals:\r
https://dl.gi.de/bitstream/handle/20.500.12116/20980/proceedings-01.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34b01e06-ae8b-42be-9c0f-2cc37208e769 .

camssa:17c87903-ec7c-4c89-a4c6-5d2d1eca9ea9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17d46a7c-4cba-40e3-a0ea-66515c764822 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1624157830122d60825aa5aa88ab70d0b140b2e7e510086699f9a9773efef6bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17d53b4f-e3fe-4f17-9b88-1581cdf4514a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 was developed with the purpose to support the development of projects within European Institutions and to ensure maximum efficiency and effectiveness. Currently, it is used for the development of a huge variety of projects underlying from the different General Directories, concretely the DIGIT, who is the corporate author.\r
\r
The fact of being a tool used for European Institutions for the development of different types of projects ensures its market acceptance and usefulness for developing products and services, specifically public ones. \r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f945ce84-a5f4-457b-ae85-46edfafae774 .

camssa:17d614e4-7fc1-4529-b60d-5b69bb98f58f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS is intended to serve as a device to identify administrative zones in the EU and non-EU regions. There is no possibility to extend the coding system as NUTS was conceived for a unique purpose.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b701194-2a5a-4566-8bb4-d47a81d3fd4a .

camssa:17d7ab41-ff0f-4dc0-ba66-7d8431c0f464 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The RDA specifications address and will facilitate interoperability between public administrations and repositories, public and private providers. The 4 specifications listed here as well as the others in the evaluation process are all components necessary and essential for data sharing, access, re-use, preservation, citation, etc. All of them contribute to data interoperability in the new digital economy irrespective of the organisation who implements / uses them."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4bba979d-5255-4725-b1f6-0929b8a38673 .

camssa:17d98ca8-09b7-46c6-9234-80a7bd6e4d53 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17de6f93-02b5-40c4-8504-420d7fdaf8e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family of documents provides a general-purpose framework for representing and exchanging provenance information, which can be applied across various domains and industries. Therefore they are domain-agnostic.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76b154f9-59c5-449f-a2ac-c41ae19f483d .

camssa:17e3a9ef-abd1-47b9-a5af-f0bd5fd47572 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17e48646-a5dc-40bd-ae67-cde3a27b6fef a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17ebd672-7170-4b4f-b9f1-e00bc07d477a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GITB TDL is a language created to express test cases against any given specification. Therefore it can be used in any domain.\r
\r
JOINUP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/detailed-information#domainagnostic'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eec2e5f9-334d-44ce-9a79-6755794e84d9 .

camssa:17eda2a1-9a41-494e-9376-9c59999cf3db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is part of the Electronic Signatures and Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications and is dependent on some of the protocols and semantics they convey, therefore, this specification is not technology agnostic (See Annex B for an example).

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:858c02f6-7249-4031-bd1e-c8c64d0d1304 .

camssa:17f4b09f-301e-4047-94a2-e7c613f63d3a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The flexible approach of UBL makes it an adaptable specification, that can change based on future business and administrative needs, therefore supporting the evolution of European Public Services.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:728f3080-47ef-4752-a06d-70638ececa79 .

camssa:17f78711-104a-4cf0-ac65-33c90dfd94ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After carrying out an exhaustive search concerning LegalDocML validation, conformance and certification, no tool has been found available for free for these purposes. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6d49c0d-f527-4d74-8c9d-b056b6590281 .

camssa:17f997a4-3ece-4358-aa49-ce2f31120b3a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:17fd140d-c6ec-4fa0-8b7f-8c2c74b46f64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 is a sector agnostic specification that allows its implementation independently form the business domain. 

IPv4 domain-agostic reference:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4842-8603-6_3'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47ba6446-92bd-47e9-9b5e-fb67ea35094c .

camssa:18001327-0ef2-448a-9004-1d619cfeda0b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTTPS was adopted as web standard in May 2000 by IETF. Moreover, Google is promoting the usage of HTTPS for the improvement of security in terms of transfer data. In the latest report of Google about the usage of HTTPS, it shows that the usage of HTTPS is increasing significantly. \r
\r
See:\r
https://transparencyreport.google.com/https/overview?hl=en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abf90fee-e954-4638-a05f-4fd54b796829 .

camssa:18008cf3-622e-4eba-89d2-471b2ff1d458 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 restricts access at the connection establishment phase by verifying the identities of the communicating peers. Once a secure and authenticated connection is established, TLS 1.3 ensures the confidentiality and integrity of the data exchanged within that session.

TLS 1.3 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07e3d3d7-8662-44c8-98b8-92a31107b37d .

camssa:180132b3-316a-4897-bca0-cc33af311d1c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:18041247-9684-41bf-825b-541188f284c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TIFF fosters the interoperability between systems by having a TIFF Tag Interoperability IFD (Image File Directory) which has multiple tags that store the information to ensure the Interoperability.\r
\r
TIFF Tag Interoperability IFD reference:\r
https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/tifftags/interoperabilityifd.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07aba0cc-fc4f-4f51-acf4-031e32dd0fb5 .

camssa:1809c0c1-e7e7-4a89-b24e-76b0f2f3afd9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:180eab58-6517-425a-b854-6972b0fef958 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI TS 119 614-1, operates under \r
the ETSI Intellectual Property Rights (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights Policy, ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eddbc8d7-12ea-4129-8b54-ab3a365ff67c .

camssa:180eee59-9c2f-45a0-9478-de9e962727aa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4a006ad6785e066d16c13daf48a60ee43ec33d1de1b06613c8e656ccf330a6d5 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:18197009-b893-4932-8950-4e98d9bc6fce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XSLT has an open-source framework processor (XT-Speedo), so it is independent from any technology or platform."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8edc36eb-2ab5-4e24-b94a-8c46f4bec11e .

