camssa:1885ff8c-881f-424e-af46-519b7cc4b670 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Even HTML 5 is fostering the first level of maturity provided by Tim Berners-Lee's 5 stars schema for publication of Open data, it is not supports the principles to be considered as fostering actor on pubilishing Linked Open Data. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e88f246f-9a8b-41e3-a18c-1684ac35b64b .

camssa:188e1dcc-0856-4eb2-a464-4bb901e76ab9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. Moreover, there is a public review in the TC process.\r
 \r
OASIS guideline:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26\r
The Akoma Ntoso review process: \r
http://www.akomantoso.org/?p=141"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:becfd42b-e8f3-4ec8-82d9-50409a0a1ef4 .

camssa:1892791a-f2b6-4c83-be2a-5cf7433e0daf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1896ef1e-391f-4b3f-ba5e-5179d9df746f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Linked Data Event Streams could be used to maintain and open up reference datasets to foster interoperability by advocating the reuse of the identifiers for which they are the authoritative source. LDES provides a robust framework to ensure that data can be easily shared, understood and used across systems. Therefore, it could contribute to enabling data portability.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba764abd-c910-4eb5-9d14-f6748a3edd44 .

camssa:189811c0-088f-4ebc-b119-29793b11ed98 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:189fd8e3-5693-4f4d-9110-e5f8c07315c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The current version of the specification was released back in 2018 and has been tested with real implementors to demonstrate its usefulness and application. For certain industries and scenarios, ODRL has been successfully implemented to manage digital rights and permissions effectively. It is particularly well suited for applications involving content distribution, intellectual property management, and digital rights management.\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core\r
\r
W3C Working Group Github space: \r
https://github.com/w3c/odrl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d352542e-2323-40f6-8429-5e1289211a21 .

camssa:18b60cb8-808b-4bf6-9bbb-3481501e42f3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a0101cb11c30c1bbf94adb74479472f2a40c53ccc4b442180fece91506c20a9d ;
    cav:value "2" .

