camssa:18ca80ac-c375-4d29-918f-6c68f97826c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not related to the publication of public data as open data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f8aaec17-6519-42c4-896c-657894b786e1 .

camssa:18d16cf3-465c-4638-9827-0b3ca4820c26 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:18d1cce6-6b60-4ed4-9dab-2adc407f7a8f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification provides a message format that allows vendor-specific extensions to be provided in a 
structured way. Structured data is a feature introduced in the syslog protocol that enables the inclusion of additional, machine-readable information within syslog messages. This mechanism allows for extensibility, as custom key-value pairs can be added to provide supplementary context or metadata related to the log event.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89b1e722-66c3-4fb1-af86-70b1c0bcfad6 .

camssa:18d68a34-c0b5-4e76-9dec-07623db43bf6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:18d74db9-1452-4627-b0c4-e356a2590967 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing documents and studies about the XACML performance in different environments. 
The research article "Approaches for Testing and Evaluation of XACML Policies" concentrates on the examination of XACML policies, offering various methods to enhance their efficiency.

Approaches for Testing and Evaluation of XACML Policies:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication
/279192661_Approaches_for_Testing_and_Evaluation_of_XACML_Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cae2175d-4464-4db2-9244-c7dc75c71854 .

camssa:18d9cdf6-d25a-445c-a47b-ead042990ca1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, IPv6 is  a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. IPv6 is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4322a8cf-c984-4f29-b8f9-d0f2cbb6b16b .

camssa:18dde53e-4fcb-4fa2-a45c-ff46931fb271 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:18de216e-d414-45fe-9cb1-1025406c6792 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By providing a standardised method for the description of legal entities, RegOrg helps to ensure that the information provided and exchanged is properly structured. At this point, it helps the trustworthy data exchange between citizens and businesses, and administrations. \r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:139d3de5-4811-4aba-8238-74d221075cba .

camssa:18e13c39-d7b9-4208-a695-295fd49f6d3f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """EuroVoc is used for the EU Open Data Portal, the site where EU Institutions publish their datasets for their reuse. In there, it is also used the classification of EuroVoc in order to improve the shareability, researchability and interoperability when processing the data. It helps to link data under knowledge domains. \r
 \r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:692f87e4-8d43-4409-8db5-3b88db136caf .

camssa:18e16300-d604-4779-86d1-2508495034a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Verifiable Credentials was included in the European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI), the first pan-European, public-driven blockchain initiative of its kind. EBSI VC/VP data models build upon W3C Verifiable Credentials, which defines the standard way to present credentials/certificates on the internet in a common digital way, improving the efficiency, interoperability, and readability of all documents/certificates.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials Privacy Considerations: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/#privacy-considerations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4224c4a-85f3-486b-8ba7-dd826d102291 .

camssa:18e81fe8-6160-4198-8de0-3ccb7a2b76c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As it is mentioned in the specification's documentation, ETSI TS 119 612 allows the extension in various parts, such as Scheme, TSP and XML Schemas. This can be checked out in the section "5.3.17 Scheme extensions".\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c47397ff-b269-4229-a1aa-56135d9f8850 .

camssa:18e90214-1e68-4f07-8d0f-5545339d9d78 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5b29a4581c52656a3bcf08224b259c29610cb540c56af4512ebe0ded3adeeac1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:18f3f110-0ac6-4eba-8ec9-bee4c9fe2f5b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fef5941bab92019b7692f8544de94715a42ed9ff76d89cbec4fb6f9821611925 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:18f4ce4f-8561-4c6c-a37f-079446374835 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the Indexed Database API is not itself customisable, some elements can be modified. For example, object stores, which are the primary storage for data in a database, can be changed.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc2df252-784f-4d56-b568-87100391882a .

camssa:18f592a4-a8ec-4e37-a163-bd4c65d2cd77 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of TSP is not related to organisational interoperability.  Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. 

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48757f55-7b11-47f8-90a2-f923fa8d5c91 .

camssa:18fbd401-0135-4a0d-9645-1cda520b3b64 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1902a7db-40f4-47f4-9f1b-dd5c84265953 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are platforms for sharing results, information, and discussing IPsec. One of these platforms, where people can discuss implementations and new versions of IPsec, is the Netgate forum. Many entries addressing issues with implementing IPsec and discussions about IPsec can be found there. In addition, IPsec is also available in the Joinup repository (Interoperable Europe Portal).
 
Netgate IPsec forum:
https://forum.netgate.com/category/17/ipsec'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e6e61a72-29d9-47b6-9828-588c8b282e53 .

camssa:19055d6e-28da-4ee6-99e1-d1a80c9b5497 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:1905c148-ac97-4e75-8fe5-0b529239a720 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL, as a specification, does not inherently address administrative procedures, rules, or data visibility. Its main purpose is to facilitate the interoperability of web services by defining the contract between the service provider and the service consumer. \r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d17a607-a2d4-47d1-be6e-78d6ef077ec8 .

