camssa:194b6363-695d-4a40-800b-d96be57eb2e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XAdES is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84fbe6be-e84f-4c8d-97de-69265fe2690e .

camssa:1952db46-0f8f-4aad-b64b-8186aab210cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """EuroVoc is a public asset developed by a European Institution and can be accessed and reused without any payment conditions. Therefore, it can be considered that the specification is licensed under royalty-free basis and (F)RAND basis. \r
\r
EuroVoc reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:266901cc-e7f6-43a6-a3d9-647bbaa651e1 .

camssa:195c9a59-c060-4492-a5eb-30357934c982 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is to provide communication security regarding privacy and data integrity. It can be concluded that TLS 1.2 collaborates in a way to proper data portability. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3f247a6-a9f2-4504-b7cf-df80e7057ba2 .

camssa:195f1185-9545-467e-a2f5-2c304e409e82 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol enables the interaction between participants of a Dataspace. All data follows a series of requirements so that they can be reused as needed. The Dataspace Information Model, which forms the foundation of this specification, enables the interaction between participants of a Dataspace and specifies how they should do it in the most effective and efficient way.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol Information Model: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/model'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:199224fb-a5ab-43b5-9e4d-69263df4be62 .

camssa:19612439-8c11-46b0-b9cd-5b8d2f2c678c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Assessments of the efficiency of DNS over HTTPS (DoH) primarily involve evaluating the performance, 
scalability, and practicality of implementations. For instance, a 2020-paper related to the 3rd International Conference on Information and Computer Technologies (ICICT) describes the impact of DoH on cyber systems. The assessment explains that DoH is one of the latest enhancements implemented to address security against malware and other vulnerabilities, which proves the specification's efficiency.

On the Impact of DNS Over HTTPS Paradigm on Cyber Systems: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/9092077\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2129e28b-4012-459f-a8de-60cb742ce07d .

camssa:1967de57-f3f2-493b-b515-80b8650c5ba4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c2a96e0-e907-4f7d-b4be-f5e705213795 .

camssa:196b8f24-0ae9-469c-9575-b2f0de58ba14 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:196ddb03-6ee8-4027-bac3-3be4d6ef0c0a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the publication of data as linked open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable for this criterion. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c289e20-f924-45cc-90f4-76b32e46d777 .

camssa:196fdf5d-03d4-4313-b08e-113a302314fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SOAP 1.2 is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:63a35833-6fd1-4233-ae7d-8b6a4246a683 .

camssa:19726cf2-d119-460d-a25b-784b6ec22014 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SMTP can be implemented in any platform and it is independent of any technology.\r
\r
SMTP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5321"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:777d8cfc-2823-4fc4-b67c-fee14a771c4a .

camssa:1972bb9a-4c71-4a9b-bd34-81ad6110641f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of LDAP is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable specification. \r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3837aa32-75d8-4b89-b166-cfef992a2330 .

camssa:1975e10e-c551-482f-84c5-98e5e6c80d59 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UTF-8 was launched at the beginning of 2000s, and currently is one of the three encoding methods recognised by Unicode or web languages. It demonstrates the maturity and the market acceptance for development of products and services.\r
See: \r
https://w3techs.com/technologies/overview/character_encoding/all """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0a5b807-ce1c-4cb6-9eac-efdb3f391b73 .

camssa:197613fe-8bc1-45b0-8ab9-97831dbb50a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SMP specification describes also the binding of the specification with the REST interfaces for the Service Metadata Publication within a 4-Corner network. Therefore, the specification fosters the availability of interfaces containing information from the different parties involved in a 4-corner network.\r
\r
Specification Reference, section 5 mentioning REST binding:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505042'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cef0aa2f-ed87-45dc-a31f-d240361a40e5 .

camssa:197c4974-9ba6-4604-93c8-d7feb60e85c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Users can create domain-specific extensions or profiles of DQV that focus on particular domains or industries. These extensions can include domain-specific terminology, quality metrics, and constraints that are not covered by the core DQV vocabulary. By defining domain-specific extensions, users can ensure that DQV aligns with the terminology and requirements of their particular domain.

Data Quality Vocabulary: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1fb9f3bf-5ff7-4778-9d84-d1c66e102204 .

camssa:197db3e7-f235-463e-95a3-09f9150baa96 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:1985aa79-2fe7-45fd-9947-1e7ecc035d3f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:198a46ff-7085-47a9-beab-d6b9e0f2710a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"WAI-ARIA is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a82535d-54b9-4c72-8b07-9ccd2e615bf5 .

camssa:198d6ff9-6640-4728-9cd0-5cf9c3221e8e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP does no directly help for the provision of application programming interfaces (APIs) or Web services.\r
\r
However, DCAT-AP aims to ensure consistency by providing a standard description of the catalogues and datasets published by data portals across Europe. This description makes datasets more searchable and accessible for data reusers and encourages the data providers to use open data portals for dissemination of reusable data."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8228df91-a871-4b9d-a3ee-8b6a1c99ab95 .

camssa:1991a8ce-869c-4d3d-8bb9-1b559c892cb1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:19920595-7c7e-48fa-9a4d-64ea141385b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While OpenTelemetry is not directly related to enabling the secure processing of data, OTel configuration should ensure sensitive configuration information is managed securely. Sensitive information should be stored securely such as on an encrypted filesystem or secret store. Environment variables can be used to handle sensitive and non-sensitive data as the Collector must support environment variable expansion. In addition, the Collector should be configured to obfuscate or scrub sensitive data before exporting. 

OTel Security Best Practices: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/blob/main/docs/security-best-practices.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3fab1493-7c8c-4008-89a1-5fb26a56a4bd .

camssa:199224fb-a5ab-43b5-9e4d-69263df4be62 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:199a610e-b12d-48d1-b9da-fc48648a7b98 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The OASIS TC in charge of LegalDocML operates under the Royalty Free on Limited Terms IPR mode as defined in the OASIS Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) Policy.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ac73930-2d6f-4f2a-aecb-ac2cd48086ca .

camssa:199a9cc1-fe4d-4828-b28e-586991c80720 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although PDF/A supports the first level of maturity from the Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for the Open data, it is not supporting the main principles for the publication of data as Linked Open Data. \r
\r
PDF/A reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/38920.html\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/50655.html\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d4dfc53-265b-4c19-b3e6-3d3bc54ebfdc .

camssa:199d580c-df97-46a0-a3cd-aa0572d30d1a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By defining schemas for XML documents, which are involved in the data exchange across borders, XSD utilizes a limited reuse and implementation of the once-only principle. \r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e90d7598-a46a-4ffe-af4c-1b75538f7c64 .

