camssa:19da9f5c-8347-4d43-93db-d1b43401e10c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The OpenPM2 is the open version of the Project Management Methodology developed by the Commission back in 2007 and that has been evolving according to the experience gained over time. Within the PM2 Alliance, different stakeholders have the opportunity to contribute to the development of the specification in the different domains.\r
\r
PM2 alliance and advisory committees: \r
https://www.pm2alliance.eu/advisory-committees/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c232c02f-93e4-4e0e-b02d-8086d3e36bb8 .

camssa:19dec9d8-c49a-46a1-a0e4-c62ed65644a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpopse of Indexed Database API is not related to enabling the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7619d41-3b03-4e49-9967-15efed832ea5 .

camssa:19e6c986-d925-4feb-9b20-978db2e85391 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"DNS facilitates the visibility of public administrations. As an example of ensuring their visibility, DNS might\r
enhance the transparency of public administrations' networks. The European Commission is developing its\r
own DNS service, the DNS4EU, which will allow the access to global Internet and will comply with EU\r
regulations.\r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1034  \r
\r
Domain Names - Implementation and Specification:                             \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035    \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da3196f3-9a77-4ae1-abf8-b14ec6f590bf .

camssa:19e89c9b-d673-43e9-be9a-306b57dea3e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV is a commonly used format for data exchange. It allows to provide data in a simple way. Moreover, as is structured data and non-proprietary format it eases data consumption by different stakeholders. \r
\r
An example of initiative relaying on CSV to provide data to users is ESCO, that allows the download data sets in CSV format. \r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/esco/portal/escopedia/Comma-separated_values__40_CSV_41_#ESCO_data_in_CSV_files"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1354514a-23cc-4322-962b-7573b6b1b85e .

camssa:19e8b34d-0e35-4951-a298-3307b4f94c7e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c8137c2-4d85-4384-9f20-6d9960391cee .

camssa:19e905fd-e7e9-4161-b315-7901ae876b9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DNS is widely used for EU cross-border projects. For instance, it is used by TESTA, the data communication network service operated by the European Commission.\r
\r
See:                                                                                                                                                https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/testa_overview_-_july_2018.pdf \r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34bc9945-9584-4746-ad21-91aa0ec0ab51 .

camssa:19eb9851-a412-4f2c-8be4-e6cc1e00f3ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA does not allow for partial implementation. In fact, the Cloud Service ARchive (CSAR) is an archive format that is meant to guarantee the availability of all specification artefacts as well as the successful execution of services. In other words, in order to support the execution and lifecycle management of a cloud application in a given environment, all corresponding artefacts have to be available in that environment, preventing partial implementation.\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Cloud Service Archive (CSAR) reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969474'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82a05db9-5241-491c-ba7b-5e2258b2b79e .

camssa:19ef297d-0bbe-4e0f-9cf3-b444b31b4f3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PAdES is a set of restrictions and extensions to PDF and ISO 32000-1 making it suitable for advanced electronic signatures. One profile of PAdES is PAdES-LTV (Long Term Validation), it is a signature conformant which has one or more long-term-validation attributes that guarantee the preservation of the authenticity of the signature.\r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html\r
\r
PAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:80888485-464e-446e-9801-cfda593f6d3e .

