camssa:1ad24aa9-0d10-4b60-805b-3844c38935d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"NUTS releases do not foresee public reviews. Any amendment to the NUTS classification is a Member States' competence (see European Commission reference, Regulation (EC) No 1059/2003 document, provision 13). In case of any revision concerning the NUTS classification, the Member State in question has to replace historical data set by time series according to the new classification within a two-years period (see European Commission reference, Regulation (EC) No 1059/2003 document, Article 2(5)). EU adoption of the new classification and its duration are subject to a feasibility evaluation.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, History of NUTS section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/history\r
\r
European Commission reference, Regulation (EC) No 1059/2003 document, provision 13:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1405939838475&uri=CELEX:32003R1059\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:33d44f1a-6f77-4d1a-b536-458b179bf050 .

camssa:1ad35a3b-6672-4117-b569-e249140d942d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 639-2 has been extensively used in the library industry and can also be used for any domain that requires the expression of language in codes. The EU Official Language codelist and the SCL-language classification provides the outline of standard code lists for languages in Europe. They draw on the ISO 639-2 alpha3 codes (among others) with a focus on European languages.\r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5\r
\r
Language codelist reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/language\r
\r
SCL-languages referece:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eu-semantic-interoperability-catalogue/solution/scl-languages?f%5B0%5D=solution_content_bundle%3Aasset_distribution'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72489ca0-5ed8-4487-b218-e74c61d49f6c .

camssa:1ad83542-8854-4d2f-a019-e295e13e099b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:1adb92eb-14b0-464e-b7ce-fa11a1cca4a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT is a W3C standard, indicating its endorsement and support by the W3C organisation. As a result, the specification is subject to ongoing management and maintenance by the W3C.    \r
                                                                                                                                                                                  DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/     '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c0f9187-ceba-40a3-a809-69d971288687 .

camssa:1ae09c9e-e7a7-4cce-9df3-1c3c6f0ff608 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:1aed7d99-4b44-4083-92cf-3fdd465a028f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Internet Protocol is a necessary specification for the implementation of the once-only-principle as it allows cross-border communications over the internet. For example, the mobile IPv6 protocol provides mobility support for IPv6. It allows you to keep the same internet address all over the world, and allows applications using that address to maintain transport and upper-layer connections when changing locations. 

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460

Mobile IPv6 protocol:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/aix/7.1?topic=protocol-mobile-ipv6'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f650696-d14c-4910-a3e9-597b2e08e108 .

camssa:1af3c1c9-88a1-49c9-be39-166517870fa4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39e72d0c-5f96-479a-bdac-1acdef9fe3ef .

camssa:1af75cc9-370a-42e9-a753-6b8616c471e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GraphQL has the mutation functionality. However, despite the fact that there are some extensions for GraphQL to query linked open data (GraphQL-LD), there has not been found any evidence proving the capacity of the specification to publish open data.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://graphql.org/learn/schema/\r
\r
GraphQL-LD:\r
https://comunica.github.io/Article-ISWC2018-Demo-GraphQlLD'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a75b23f-625c-48d8-a08f-48442eb00b63 .

