camssa:1b6fa8b4-987c-4df1-baff-805a3dce49a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI TS 119 612 specification can enable mechanisms to ensure that data has not been modified and that it is accurately transferred between public administrations or organisations and citizens. In this context, the specification supports authentication methods, such as digital signatures, which ensure that signed data is in its original form, and it is accurate.

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53e44ae8-efac-40bc-a113-70e55969139c .

camssa:1b705f64-7d1d-4100-a2fb-7add7200ca58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV XML specification allows for an XML serialisation of a PROV model, a fact that explicitly proves that the PROV family of docuents can provide means for the long-term preservation of information.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60834ea2-a23a-4428-921d-f326c2b36257 .

