camssa:1f815ebf-8b6a-4d99-a67a-eabe1ce205f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 has a specific section called "Session Layer" whose purpose is to provide the means necessary for cooperating presentation-entities to organise and to synchronise their dialogue and to manage their data exchange. One of the services provided is token management, which allows the presentation-entities to control explicitly whose turn it is to exercise certain control functions.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ddfd76b0-620c-4631-a216-76a83d4bd89f .

camssa:1f9050eb-3232-45ac-9564-dabd0304155f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Since its first release, ISO/IEC 19944-1 has been widely accepted and adopted by major stakeholders and Member States given that it extends a standard that has already been recommended by many cloud-computing organisations such as the Storage Networking Industry Association (SNIA), and standardisation bodies such as UNE. \r
\r
UNE digitalisation report:\r
https://www.une.org/normalizacion_documentos/Informe%20Transformaci%C3%B3n%20Digital_20201127.pdf\r
\r
SNIA Best Practices for Cloud Security and Practices:\r
https://www.snia.org/sites/default/files/Hibbard_Best-Practices-for-Cloud-Security-and-Privacy_V2_Final_0.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69827f15-1914-49df-8a97-8620322e10d7 .

camssa:1f996f2a-7334-4f0e-8c31-53207e83e823 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being in a low maturity level of development DPV is being developed under the guidelines proposed by W3C. Consequently, DPV is still not a standard nor is it in the W3C standards track, and it is not a European Standard.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:317ed3e5-cc86-4529-97b8-06751e234bd9 .

camssa:1fa23532-bb08-46a7-99a1-53ca4bb7388b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As defined on the OASIS Technical Committee (TC), the OData TC are involved in the release lifecycle of the specification. External contribution to this committee is possible through open channels. Up-to-date, the OData TC has announced three public reviews; however, the topic selection of these reviews is independent of the external contributors.

OData OASIS Technical Committee reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/comments/index.php?wg_abbrev=odata

OData OASIS Technical Committee, Overview reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=odata#overview

OData TC third review reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/2023/07/19/invitation-to-comment-on-odata-extension-for-data-aggregation-v4-0/

OData TC fourth review reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/2024/04/08/invitation-to-comment-on-four-odata-v4-02-specification-drafts/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf5cd5e1-2e51-4da1-a831-94465dc9dbdd .

