        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:202465db-29c1-45fa-8882-53c2698ee3f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is designed to be platform-agnostic, which means that it can be implemented on any platform or operating system, such as Windows, Linux, or macOS. The specification is based on open standards and uses XML-based schemas to represent legal documents, which can be processed by a wide range of software systems and applications.\r
\r
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb8799ae-3abc-4b4f-9580-9497bde2c6a2 .

camssa:20292e7e-984b-49d8-9781-abad438d3e0a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2034c3af-7ef1-47cf-9493-6b9119c35c35 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been constantly evolving to adapt to users needs and to ensure the effective development of projects funded with public funds. Besides, its evolution is translated into several releases where improvements have been put in the focal point. The current version was released more than two years ago, by mid-2018. This fact together with its first publication in 2016 provides enough maturity for its use in the development of public products and services. \r
\r
Additionally, it is worth to note that this OpenPM has been evolved from previous Project Management Methodology, and therefore it contains a high level of lessons learned to improve its added value.\r
\r
OpenPM2 first edition reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/0e3b4e84-b6cc-11e6-9e3c-01aa75ed71a1/language-en\r
\r
OpenPM ISA2:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/open-pm2_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94161d80-9267-4e3c-9a7f-948abf6d5d26 .

camssa:203500ed-feda-48d7-9839-6f5235a533c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, IPsec is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. IPsec is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on the IPsec specification (RFC 4301).\r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4301"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe7cc5b5-4220-4b25-b0de-fa8618e95b07 .

camssa:2036d00c-7901-42c7-a6e5-1710248b007d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Dataspace Protocol can simplify the delivery of European public services as it offers a framework for the management of International Data Spaces, which aligns with Europe's vision of data. It standardises secure environments for data exchange between government entities, service providers and citizens, improving interoperability and data flow, etc.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7691fdaa-dfc7-4b84-8b51-47d5b11fcde8 .

camssa:203a2cdf-8383-4c2a-a3da-ad2525a26deb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is not related to the publication of public data as open data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4239bb0a-fe7b-4a28-bd2f-998699dc1eb3 .

