camssa:203a9574-6c6f-44d5-acda-4a2277e43723 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the PROV family of documents does not explicitly address data protection, its use in systems or applications can indirectly support data protection efforts through transparency, accountability, auditing, consent tracking, and security incident investigation. However, comprehensive data protection requires considering broader factors beyond the scope of PROV.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/\r
\r
PROV-AQ Security cosiderations:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/NOTE-prov-aq-20130430/#security-considerations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:482d9c5e-e4e6-4b5b-a6b9-4c16513e8719 .

camssa:203ce508-21b8-45af-8f00-79fe1fe81a00 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox provides a set of guidelines to guarantee that policies and laws development, implementation and evaluation are properly established. Therefore, the Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox includes a set of recommendations, best practices and requirements whose purpose is to ensure and enhance the cross-border application and organisational interoperability as much as possible.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e03520b-a150-442d-949b-5b3b80f148c3 .

camssa:203ef15e-bd03-492b-9738-e00cf1d5099c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:204494ff-72f4-4d48-a71e-eb3fd2bf4bf3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of UTF-8 is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore this criterion is not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad1cf1b2-1aad-43aa-b26b-90b624070410 .

camssa:204499ed-15ee-45a1-be60-b9bc70fd5ecc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ESPD hasa been developed by the Publications Office of the EU. The specification can be accessed\r
through the European platdorm Joinup, and also through the Ted Developer Docs.\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
Ted mainpage:\r
https://ted.europa.eu/TED/main/HomePage.do\r
\r
ESPD joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eprocurement/solution/european-single-procurement-document'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:caff0d87-d46a-4f24-9d92-68e09f3a4322 .

camssa:204b0c14-94dc-42df-b3c2-5bc8ee43bcd3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:204d5556-bb4a-4bf6-bd2b-f8a3bc2fe28d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Together with other models or initiatives like eCertis, the ESPD fosters the cross-border participation in procurement, increasing competition and supporting economic growth. eCertis is a tool that helps to understand what kind of evidence can be used to fulfill a specific public procurement requirement in a European country.\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
European single procurement document and eCertis:\r
https://single-market-economy.ec.europa.eu/single-market/public-procurement/digital-procurement/european-single-procurement-document-and-ecertis_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:afdf10d2-d36d-4107-86d0-f59d97d62900 .

camssa:2055cc80-5be5-443a-9f06-740c6ed34e80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As the internet protocol stack, it allows connections and data exchange all over the internet. The internet protocol is the main enabler element to perform communications over networks. This fact together with its long haul demonstrates the market acceptance and the maturity for its use development of services and products. Moreover, the European Regional Internet Registry has a high number of IPs available in order to provide them when necessary.\r
\r
Even though, it is worth mentioning that IPv6 it is being gradually adopted by suppliers, vendors and public services. However, there are existing translation and transition methods between both versions that allow the normal connection between nodes using different Internet Protocol versions\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.ripe.net/publications/news/about-ripe-ncc-and-ripe/getting-ready-for-ipv4-run-out"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07b09f42-f317-410a-be88-ed08d31ca5d8 .

