camssa:218da1bf-a588-48f7-9467-79260596743e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP can contribute to the secure exchange of data by providing a foundation for implementing basic security measures. For example, The Cache-Control directives, offer a mechanism to restrict the unintended storage or reuse of sensitive information. For instance, the "no-store" directive prevents caches from storing sensitive data, contributing to data security. However, they don't provide a complete framework for secure data processing.

HTTP/1.1, RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-http-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b951c642-0501-4436-84c2-4407412accc8 .

camssa:218f8a3e-e34a-43e6-a47e-839e90b1595d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As an organisational enabler, EN 16234-1 e-CF aims to provide a standard that includes some other essentials for any IT professional, such as their basic skill set, their education and training qualification and certification, and the ethics around worker development. In this sense, the specification is not only usable beyond the business-specific domain, but also is designed to be implemented in any other domain.\r
\r
Joinup-2021 Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation reference, Education, Digital skills and Digital learning section:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/education-digital-skills-and-digital-learning'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe0424a0-a48f-4431-8338-fb0f928e926c .

camssa:2196ac84-88ce-4b86-8c32-6f43ff625984 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as a "Request for Comments" (RFC) document. During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory. IETF therefore makes available the working documents to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c784406-64e9-413c-88e5-7651c1733a20 .

camssa:21a0f3ee-6a0a-49c5-88a2-4bf49af1bee7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 specifies the policy and security requirements of the preservation services schemes applicable to a given preservation storage model which outlines how preservation evidences are to be created and validated by defining the relationships among the preservation schemes, preservation profiles and they are related on a given business-specific trust service. \r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d5e29f7-3414-49ee-933a-cc10115be093 .

camssa:21a47f29-4faf-446f-a7aa-9180c96e2767 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This specification contains a specific section that addresses interfaces, APIs and interoperability regarding cloud services. By promoting an international standard for cloud services, the specification enables the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services. The standard guides the structuring of these interfaces to facilitate interoperability, taking into account different aspects like transport protocols, data formats, and principles for effective communication and integration.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fb367d3b-9918-41be-85e7-2320f00e5ed9 .

camssa:21a95f3f-9a24-4e84-8836-7e970baf9f73 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:21b189b0-b934-406e-ad81-4fe028713951 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ShEx is not related to the long-term preservation of information; therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:423b1770-b5fd-4dd6-b6cf-febb8a07f603 .

