camssa:22c29d43-c616-4aa1-9d26-0d2ea5768ee8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XFDL specification is based on an XML structure, providing a standardised format for data collection and form submission. However, there are other modern technologies, such as HTML5, which are easier to implement. Finally, the specification does not simplify the delivery of public services.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:746a35a7-9aeb-48b4-979a-963c69486614 .

camssa:22c8f86f-752a-4c69-b2e3-dfcd651a8f40 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Insufficient information is available to conclusively determine whether this criterion is met. Furthermore, the
specification does not appear to be designed with the explicit goal of enhancing data exchange security and
privacy. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:958f8fa7-a6d9-4494-b188-e9e1fec0db19 .

camssa:22ca9310-c8c9-4c17-b153-f73b80cb84e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NFVI is intended to be used in virtualised ecosystems. Because the NFVI is a distribution set of NFVI-nodes in multiple locations that supports the locality and latency requirements of NFV use cases, the specification also provides network connectivity, and therefore can be implemented in different business domains.\r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/ \r
\r
ISG NFV Deliver, Terminology for main concepts:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/NFV/001_099/003/01.06.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fabcd2d5-6c46-413f-8d05-b1d7f84b7ebe .

camssa:22cfceed-7579-47a6-a7dc-232eb2cc6501 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:22d11489-fe87-4e35-b216-430b0182d4be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SHACL is a specification developed and maintained by W3C and identified by the MSP for its use in public procurement in Europe. As the specification is available for free and on a FRAND basis, this reduces the administrative burden."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df420ce1-a47f-417e-ad7a-1ed82811b592 .

