    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:23206baa-739a-44c0-94b6-292488d6275a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Back in 2021, The AMQP Technical Committee (TC) released specifications for public review, during which they actively invite and encourage feedback from stakeholders.

AMQP TC Release Announcement:
https://groups.oasis-open.org/communities/tc-community-home2?CommunityKey=969c2da1-55c4-4bba-92d2-018dc7d3efe9#announcements

Invitation to comment on three new AMQP specifications:
https://www.oasis-open.org/2021/04/01/invitation-to-comment-on-three-new-amqp-specifications/

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc4a0b62-b824-4d31-81e0-7bd54824c759 .

camssa:23246f93-3ff6-439c-8ec9-60c8273ad20a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:232965b5-dbc4-4ab6-a9b3-3cdbd1dcf764 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is included in Belgium national catalogue of recommended specifications.\r
\r
Belgium National Catalogue:                                                                             https://www.belgif.be/page/specifications.en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e73089c-05c9-43f4-b491-b8e9b8049f3d .

camssa:23297820-2291-43c3-8940-2977d5b965c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "As a document exchange format, PDF is a valuable tool for sharing information through the internet. Allowing to share data and information the standard foster the visibility of administration data and services. Additionally, it eases the decision-making process within administrations. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9550a31f-2909-4dce-842d-722365675e97 .

camssa:232a751c-0faf-4383-a316-e5b42aa26d01 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of CCCEV is to ease the creation of a repository of reusable criteria in machine-readable formats. The CCCEV together with other common vocabularies fosters the publication of datasets representing criterion, evidence and evidence issuers. \r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary \r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f281a47c-3f46-40b1-8ce0-5ea504252a0f .

camssa:232e8fb8-0bd3-43f1-84c6-511a8ec50d3b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPsec is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not 
applicable to this specification.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fde39493-8620-43e2-847e-3534fe5b55bf .

camssa:2331fae7-b2c5-41a0-b54c-0304c75db704 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, IPv4 is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. IPv4 is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2490a59b-2f63-43a5-9fe8-02d6280027a0 .

camssa:234227c7-8237-4083-bd7b-f3ff0d1e3cb1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary is designed to support the exchange of information between organisations or persons (more generally Agents) defining Requirements and organisations or persons responding to these Requirements by means of structured or unstructured Evidences.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ee52453-7787-45cd-b2e2-9c1eccf7bf54 .

camssa:23496f22-0565-4898-9d75-57d2a737a456 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:23497635-25a5-436c-81a7-8df43ebc8687 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ELI is adopted as a system to make legislation available online in a standardised format. ELI progresses toward making legal metadata more reusable, it should lower the barrier for data consumers to retrieve the ELI metadata from an ELI provider. A way of achieving this is by legislation publishers describing and publishing ELI datasets.\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:92f3f8e9-b738-41b7-9df5-10790a0d5ac1 .

camssa:234be327-7ec0-4828-980f-cb4c837c4417 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is currently implemented in several initiatives in the public sector. This is a key point that reflects the market acceptance of the specification by the public administrations and institutions in Europe. \r
Some implementations of the ADMS are Metadata Registry (MDR), ADMS-enabled description of a vocabulary implemented in PoolParty Thesaurus Manager 3.1.0, and the Implementation for the XRepository of the German Federal Ministry of the interior. \r
\r
ADMS in Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a38425f5-87d1-4000-baa6-59a3c329af45 .

camssa:2350e415-6904-4892-91c4-70cb3191a3ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Council Conclusion where ELI is defined sets out conclusions involving how Member States are called on to implement ELI to properly allow other administrations, business and citizens access the legal documentation. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
Council Conclusion\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ea95006-505b-4d74-ad38-03e57208c534 .

camssa:235189f0-6ca2-4f65-ab5a-27e4548e5788 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing documents and studies assessing WSDL performance and its features. The main topic are effectiveness while discovering, automatically classify web services or the poor query results. \r
\r
Improving Web Service descriptions for effective service discovery:\r
https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82569095.pdf\r
\r
Towards Effective Service Discovery using Feature\r
Selection and Supervised Learning Algorithms:\r
https://thesai.org/Downloads/Volume10No5/Paper_25-Toward_Effective_Service_Discovery.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85fd6453-54c5-4a47-a558-130ad9d2de21 .

camssa:2352dd8b-832e-44bb-b372-f77f952d8e1a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2353cf34-1ce5-4933-8f2c-9793b1346220 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'E-ARK CSIP can indirectly scope comprehesibility of administrative procedures and services by promoting the use of descriptive metadata. Descriptive metadata can provide information about the administrative context of records, such as their origin, creator, date of creation, and other relevant administrative details. This metadata helps users understand the administrative procedures and services associated with the records.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b730c576-3571-4e1d-acba-b8869ff61395 .

camssa:2354c20e-91e0-4e16-811e-5b1a6a43853b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the time being TOSCA provides a default XML or YAML-based file dedicated to its implementation (that is, the Cloud Service Archive -CSAR, or TOSCA metadata file, and the TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML Objective section). In this sense, the specification is not technology-agnostic.\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Cloud Service Archive (CSAR) reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969474\r
\r
TOSCA reference, TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML Objective section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969412'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f3ef7fc-bac2-475c-b611-3d40762a023f .

camssa:23579df7-0d78-452a-8f65-c6e5788800ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

