    cav:value "1" .

camssa:23601f09-4ca6-4485-8523-aa6c7bc7489f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL provides a flexible and expressive framework for access control by allowing the definition of sophisticated policies governing the use of digital content. Implementers can leverage these features to \r
create access control mechanisms tailored to their specific use cases and requirements.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15caa2cd-2868-4e76-b16c-3910874f7485 .

camssa:23644a59-2d92-4fd2-b322-d1743c95530a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA enhances web accessibility, it is not designed to handle authentication and authorization concerns. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e989fa4b-cee8-4536-b28e-25a691a8d4f6 .

camssa:2365125a-9b1c-4c7e-a3a8-543ada341a3a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "65%AssessmentScoreAverage",
        "79%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:236b435e-5f5e-4c62-abdc-5da1baed9a4a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-BPEL is not related to the  delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b106fa9f-16cf-4c5c-b867-f38072e469ed .

camssa:236cf159-64c4-408c-934f-b9669ed861f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT is publicly available for implementation and use for free on Github. \r
\r
See:\r
https://github.com/w3c/dxwg/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d4ac5ada-c993-448f-a512-42e8d82a6573 .

camssa:2373b1f7-c9af-4e00-9ccd-9031643e35ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 6.4 of the specification is dedicated to the Authorization and Access Control. The role of authorization in the context of access control is to ensure that a custodian can verify that a requestor is allowed to perform a requested action. Access may be restricted by requestor identity, by requestor location, by requestor role, by date and time and so forth. As part of the access control policy the custodian may require that the requestor proves she has authorization. Authorization may be granted directly based on attributes of  the requestor or may be granted only after 3rd party verification of authority. 

ETSI Context Information Management (CIM); Security and Privacy:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/CIM/001_099/007/01.01.02_60/gr_cim007v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b6436fd-ead4-4067-b258-484ddc71233d .

camssa:2373d7d3-d335-4e60-ab4d-3a984fad28ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "As a protocol for data exchange, HTTP allows the exchange of information with interfaces of public administration systems."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7aeeebb-f658-4378-af96-52127f635fd1 .

camssa:23763a96-126d-422c-9ea4-2098da798a0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93d9977f-9074-45a0-a79a-1a7c02afd5a6 .

camssa:237e6439-e9bc-486b-b2c0-6b78ffb946e1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2380086e-7a41-4355-8b54-dcf420188044 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are Directives regulating participation on the development of standards. Participation is limited to \r
membership approval and sometimes the payment of a fee.\r
ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has \r
adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop \r
standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation \r
through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The \r
decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical \r
feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
\r
ETSI Portal reference: \r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/esi/esi-activities'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54283783-8437-46d9-90f4-37f827e3340c .

camssa:2382aa52-c8f0-4e0d-abc9-89764fa271e4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
