camssa:23980330-d096-454a-a943-babc6a3decca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, ISO 3166-1 can define the interoperability aspects of the Data Set ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:642337ad-6885-41ab-9eab-a2cc8b6c2e59 .

camssa:239b4e73-963b-4748-8fea-16e7f9136dc1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:23a05452-248a-4410-a98c-f5ce290a0ff8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'FTP is an exclusive protocol created solely for transferring files, but it lacks security for the transmitted data.\r
\r
Nevertheless, there are extensions available for FTP that address this issue by providing secure information delivery. One such extension is FTP over TLS, commonly referred to as FTPS, which employs Transport Layer Security (TLS) to safeguard FTP communications over a network.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\r
\r
Securing FTP with TLS Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:045db7bd-9329-4151-84b0-20d1afea7fa8 .

camssa:23a2ac29-0c04-43a0-ad38-6bfd05a42331 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:23a2f6b9-1222-4e76-8562-8e4dcaee5ce3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:23a39989-71d3-4c5e-aded-2f2b6f32bed0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISAE 3402 is mainly focused on establishing quality control processes in private sector companies, \r
administrations could benefit from implementing it for those procedures that require payments. This would \r
allow public administrations to clearly define and expose how their procedures are carried out and therefore, \r
enhance transparency and comprehensibility of data.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 website:\r
https://www.isae3402.com/ISAE3402_overview#'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f90b1a8-e587-4b05-9bd8-6a889fde790a .

camssa:23a91089-937f-4f90-b419-58412fd8e997 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While DoH enhances the confidentiality of DNS queries, visibility into administrative procedures, rules data, and services is more closely associated with other technologies and standards. For visibility into web services, you might consider protocols like HTTP, HTTPS, or APIs that define how data and services are accessed and interacted with over the web. 

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b52655ae-041f-4ba6-b8fa-67456cd97465 .

camssa:23ae3c91-e0f7-4c8e-aa9d-ff2b91235af0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The EN 303 645 specification addresses the most significant and widespread security weaknesses. Due to the large consumer IoT landscape, it is inevitable that the applicability of the provisions (recommendations) will depend on the device, which gives the specification a degree of flexibility (see 'Reporting implementation' section). In this sense, the specification allow for partial implementation.\r
\r
EN 303 645 reference, 'Reporting implementation' section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ffd3edb-fddc-4313-ae6f-a72a0af38583 .

camssa:23b6f994-bce7-4a58-beef-8bdc07dd53d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition.\r
\r
XAdES function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS, campliant with the European Directive of electronic signature of the European Parliament and the Council. Concequently it can be concluded that through this functions it promotes the once-only principle"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:12dcb470-8eb6-4bfb-8987-58c5cd4b1236 .

camssa:23bc3965-9815-4f75-a1df-94dcfd9c402e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:23bf2ea4-f82f-4583-81a9-caf0cd6a8ffa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the Advanced Encryption Standard cannot be found in any repository of standards at European level, the standard is mentioned in the "Cryptographic security: Critical to Europe's digital sovereignty" document, from the European Parliment, as a main cryptographic algorithm. In addition, the Advanced Encryption Standard can also be found in the eDelivery specification.

"Cryptographic security: Critical to Europe's digital sovereignty" document:
https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2024/766237/EPRS_BRI(2024)766237_EN.pdf

eDelivery specification encryption:
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=866025549

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68dc4298-244c-42df-bd51-a8e65a9abd01 .

camssa:23c28180-dbf5-4461-9d12-c6e307fd37f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion of ADMS within any European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:115add6a-aaa1-48ea-b3e9-a1f33142939f .

camssa:23c669df-d65d-482e-b579-57773f941d00 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like the IPv6 specification, IPv4 can utilise many mechanisms, some included in IPsec and others not, that can enhance data accuracy. Examples of these include the authentication of agents involved in data transactions, access control lists to deny unwanted access, and the AH and ESP protocols, which help transfer data securely. All of these mechanisms combined can contribute to achieving data processing accuracy.

IPsec protocol:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/network-layer/what-is-ipsec/

AH and ESP protocols:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/zos/2.1.0?topic=ipsec-ah-esp-protocols

IPv4 ACL:
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst2960l/software/15-2_6_e/configuration_guide/b_1526e_consolidated_2960l_cg/m_sec_acls_cg_danube_2960l_cdb.html

IPv4 authentication agent:
https://community.rsa.com/s/article/IPv4-IPv6-Authentication-Agents-aa7bd0d4'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86494834-b35c-458e-97a1-19b826e38268 .

camssa:23cd740f-d4d0-4d47-83b0-4818fe3e11fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of UDDI is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20cba500-79a6-4b6c-87a1-013dfabd04eb .

