        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The European Union considers the IPv6 as very important to "ensure the cross-border interoperability of online services and the digitisation of European public\r
administrations for the ISA2 goals"\r
See: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/ipv6_framework_for_european_governments_0.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2d048047-c21a-4123-a0f3-ca03ef71231c .

camssa:24c4648a-9fe0-4ba2-94e7-05a4009090db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are no Member States recommending W3C Best Practices in their ICT National Catalogues as it is a document related to the publication and usage of data on the Web designed to help support a self-sustaining ecosystem.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b45d904-9202-4395-9e96-8ad09e6ee27d .

camssa:24c54ad3-4f62-417c-bd64-0a7833081642 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "ASiC Baseline Profile is part of the electronic signature stack of specifications, this group of specifications are aimed to ensure the availability and validation of signed data. Therefore, the implementation of eSignatures involving ASiC Baseline Profile fosters secure and trustworthy data exchange. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:edb9ca22-38ce-4127-9dd7-97592efe84f5 .

