camssa:250847f9-8b21-4e82-bfe2-507f422aaa55 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can support the semantic layer by offering a taxonomy for business data on transactional\r
level.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS), these semantic layer would comprise the following ABBs:\r
\r
Semantic View:\r
Representation\r
Applicable Profile\r
\r
Technical View:\r
Data Transformation Component\r
Data Transformation Service'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0538df6-a2aa-4e09-8a3d-df593b1e7273 .

camssa:250ac407-1673-4cba-9e66-89e071a0dfa5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of Ogg is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f3d7d9d-d070-4c0d-bde7-030c1d87bc1e .

camssa:250f94cf-4d1f-4f0c-ad12-a7f59077eb58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There is no evidence of available studies directly assessing the specification's effectiveness. However, there are some use case evaluations submitted by (non-)European administrations where effectiveness is analysed. It is the case of Croatia, which sponsored a study (through the Ekonomski institut, Zagreb) on the implementation of NUTS in its territory (see EconStor Publications reference, NUTS implementation document); and more specifically, on the implementation and suitability of NUTS level 2, which raised a lot of debate at the time of the study.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics\r
\r
EconStor Publications reference, Croatia's NUTS implementation document:\r
https://www.econstor.eu/bitstream/10419/115958/1/ERSA2003_096.pdf\r
\r
Ekonomski institut reference, Ivana Rasic document authoring:\r
https://www.eizg.hr/about-us/employees/researchers/ivana-rasic-phd/218\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e590303-d597-4666-8c17-13cbac59cebd .

