camssa:276a5f5e-c03e-46a0-86f2-6a70d34fc53e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. XACML addresses and facilitates interoperability between public administrations, cross-border services, and impacts positively the development of eGovernment. This is because it has been designed to evaluate and control access by ensuring the compliance of security policies. Also, the project SEMIRAMIS, uses this specification to ensure secure channels for the exchange and reuse of information. 

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html

SEMIRAMIS project: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:06e64369-f5ec-4783-b35f-6ad314cf2fb7 .

camssa:276a8f49-6705-4959-a07c-e7eafe0c7d96 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The standardised terms and concepts within SAREF can facilitate clearer communication and understanding between systems, which is beneficial for secure data exchange protocols. When different entities use the same standardised terms and classifications, it can reduce ambiguity and errors during data transmission, contributing to more secure and accurate exchanges.

SAREF:
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b801af07-b8b1-4f23-b6ed-0434c60abd63 .

camssa:277208f6-8a7a-4b49-a072-74861e144933 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

