        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2773428e-3593-4ee2-a303-c59eed5f2c68 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval process so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the Request for Comments (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications. \r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.  \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/  \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b942545-8824-434f-bbab-a03be62e8a31 .

camssa:277644e1-ab38-4f5d-b9c0-9c223e7dd7ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification aims to accurately communicate user interface behaviors and structural information to assistive technologies within document-level markup. The Spanish Public Administration, under the initiative of the Observatory of Web Accessibility, is currently modernizing the mobile user interfaces across all its services.

WAI-ARIA reference, Abstract section:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/

PAe reference, 'Proceedings of the Observatory of Web Accessibility' section:
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/en/pae_Estrategias/pae_Accesibilidad
/pae_Observatorio_de_Accesibilidad.html?idioma=en
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:984c6b2e-3e2b-4e01-9cac-ad335dc1ee33 .

