        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:279417d8-df84-4d1a-aab5-fcd2ef03b7c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As can be seen on the Oracle documentation about ebXML MCD implementation, the specification can implement additional functionalities such as Message Control Documents (MCD), which serve as an interface between a back-end system and WebLogic Integration Business Connect for processing business messages. In this context, this implementation is optional and can be carried out incrementally to achieve new functions.

ebXML MCD implementation:
https://docs.oracle.com/cd/E13215_01/wlibc/docs81/admin/xml_protocols.html#1032357

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee115734-111f-4829-9130-7888085734be .

camssa:2797f211-e5f1-4887-a904-8ef817fd34da a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:279847ae-4b8c-4ded-8ba4-1a90ecd37378 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e63f7d67-5299-48c8-9d55-90dc7b3db54e .

camssa:279da99f-7f71-4bd3-a579-aad23722edd5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec enables implementation of different profiles, which involve a set of specific requirements depending on the context of implementation: integration into the native IP stack, or "underneath" an existing implementation of an IP protocol stack.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0ab40b45-5273-4879-976c-80c2dc19bcd6 .

camssa:27a70fac-8629-4dc1-8472-83e55190eb2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More 
specifically, IPsec can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data Exchange" and "Virtual Private Network" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/v610'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f61926e-72bd-4ba0-b4f5-d76629302ac3 .

camssa:27a94d1c-8509-4bc7-865a-e6354eb8b3b4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not related to long term preservation of electronic records. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CCCEV reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5eba8af-61f4-4128-8e77-8034b8646ee4 .

camssa:27a98a2a-f4ff-4d86-8265-aae8166c2798 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EuroVoc is related to the delivery of multilingual public services. It contains terms in 24 EU \r
languages, plus in three languages of countries which are candidate for EU accession. By establishing language equivalences between identical concepts expressed in different languages, it allows documents to \r
be indexed in the language of the documentalist and searches to be made in the user’s language.\r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c369c35-435d-47e9-965d-098e6abca48e .

camssa:27af33cd-d978-4a83-81fc-d741a82194ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a reference architecture, the specification covers all LOST views, which means from legal requirements to how technically are there implemented. This can help to ensure that EIRA covers from administrative procedures and actors involved, the rules at legal, semantic, and technical level. Also, how to handle data and requirements related to data, data models and services themselves. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4aac888-5d88-4d76-8acf-d09414bc8bb4 .

camssa:27b12722-3cfc-4d4c-931a-89a7714427d2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:27ba2e5d-32eb-4807-84e8-8635e64231f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ISAE 3402 is part of the International Federation of Accountants (IFAC) standard providing companies in the \r
financial sector with an independent assessment tool on user entities' controls over financial reporting. The ISAE 3402 auditing tools, therefore, are ony meant to be used as a whole.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd489410-5eb0-4500-bcc2-ee2636820bdd .

