camssa:2826442e-fe15-41d9-a8f4-6b6c4f609e80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) develops solutions to help European public administrations perform cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks. 

Specification development process by the ISA Programme:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications

Detailed document ISA Programme:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:431e5a81-7d8d-4630-a81f-6a90a7e50ad9 .

camssa:2829d702-9784-4fcf-a9c6-4eb3eb1e1fc1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV has been found to contribute to the development of the SPECIAL project (Scalable Policy-aware Linked Data Architecture For Privacy, Transparency and Compliance), a European-funded project that aims to advance the state of the art by delivering technology to reconcile the contradiction between Big Data innovation and data protection compliance requirements.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

SPECIAL project:
https://specialprivacy.ercim.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:640fa8f8-24cf-4d52-bdd0-637aa20d4e5a .

camssa:2831b2b3-50ed-478f-8d54-b9b166460dac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NIST organisation offers a guide on how to contribute to the development of new solutions. Tools and use cases can be contributed via GitHub pull requests, while feedback can be provided via GitHub issues. Contributed tools and use cases can be hosted directly in the NIST repository, or they can be hosted elsewhere online and linked to from the NIST repository.

NIST collaboration space:
https://www.nist.gov/itl/applied-cybersecurity/privacy-engineering/collaboration-space

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7e1b5b0-3902-42c1-9aa3-6c5d0c954e23 .

camssa:2834514f-d035-4bf7-9c76-815d1910d84e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS is to help to the development and documentation of APIs, with any kind of restrictions related to the domain it is to be applied; therefore, OAS is domain-agnostic and can be implemented in any domain.   \r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c01c265-a1ed-471e-916e-df4fefc446a3 .

camssa:2834ccce-c228-40c2-b502-59f3db39cc9b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By establishing a common method to model rules for accessing and consuming digital content, it can help administrations to describe intellectual property rights for their information fostering the digital readiness of the materials and services provided. In this sense, the specification can help to reuse and exchange valuable information and services increasing the digitalisation of administrations reducing the related administrative burden. \r
\r
Moreover, it is a powerful tool for the development of legislation and its compliance with privacy aspects, as it demonstrates the SERAMIS project. \r
\r
SERAMIS: \r
https://cordis.europa.eu/docs/projects/cnect/2/612052/080/deliverables/001-D55v4GDPR.pdf\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5dd29cb-48ba-4c1b-a574-d9bd6572acce .

camssa:283b54d3-e2c8-4e9d-a644-284c6d969609 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca8ae615-78e0-41aa-a98e-b8233ca5631a .

camssa:283c992a-8e71-47d7-a223-75daeee3a070 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of REST's architectural properties is the modifiability of components to meet changing needs. The REST constraint "code on demand" applies when returning executable code is needed in order to support a part of the application. Therefore the server can extend or customize the functionality of a client by transferring executable code: for example, compiled components such as Java applets, or client-side scripts such as JavaScript.\r
\r
REST "code on demand" reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/#code-on-demand\r
\r
REST R. Fielding dissertation: Chapter 5\r
https://www.ics.uci.edu/~fielding/pubs/dissertation/rest_arch_style.htm'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4602d3ed-3132-43b6-804e-918a5a63ea5f .

camssa:284aeebb-58fb-473b-9df7-0968b1f544e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

