    cav:value "100" .

camssa:28821789-497d-41c6-b855-9ff2f219fd60 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the moment of performing the assessment, no initiative at national or European level has been found to use UTF-8 to cover privacy aspects.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:30c1f5d7-005d-4035-8175-b78bca41a2c0 .

camssa:2883c39e-83f6-4e01-af6a-640c7c4fda44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UDDI public registers allow to have a public register of web services in a human-redeable manner and it also guarantees a framework to describe, discover and integrate web services. Therefore, UDDI can contribute to comprehensibility of data because it allows access to different web services in an open way, although it is not its main purpose. 

UDDI OASIS reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/uddi-spec/doc/spec/v3/uddi-v3.0.2-20041019.htm#_Toc85907967

UDDI techtarget reference:
https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/definition/UDDI-Universal-Description-Discovery-and-Integration'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9557724-d818-48ef-8e81-73c664257ca8 .

camssa:28880cd4-4d3d-4ba7-a39f-c27c99857cb8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No evidence has been found of the specification being included in a formal interoperability agreement between organisations involved in the European public services provision."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c0a0406-54c9-4971-9372-cbecb2bfac19 .

camssa:288f92f4-5b6d-4501-96f6-be3d7ea52c6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SVG is developed by the W3C community, an international organisation aimed to develop open standards and specifications.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec1d42d5-aa69-4d7f-8ddb-27958cf95e29 .

camssa:2893a140-4e36-4511-affc-b0e4f7d4789d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8a34a40e5bc5436b3530d898d75a57cf0488591887b31a5169499fe78952d84c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:289b5122-7fd8-4b04-8a49-60dca726cb17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The once-only principle is an e-government concept that aims to ensure that citizens, institutions, and companies only have to provide certain standard information to the authorities and administrations once.\r
\r
IPSec is a set of open standards and protocols for securing the exchange of data packets over a computer network. By allowing the secure exchange of standard data, IPSec reduced the need to provide the information several times Therefore, IPSec eases the implementation of the once-only principle. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:719ba576-d0e4-490e-8d5c-683ba1ad3d80 .

camssa:28a31766-4c18-4fce-8586-bbcc6eea8cc2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XACML is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:61ba39d2-4706-414f-81d6-0729477b8a48 .

