camssa:2921ad9e-20f7-4061-aa1e-491626752ede a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Understanding data exchange as the publication by the administration of data for its later consumption by citizens, the specification facilitates the trustworthy data exhange in RDF format by providing the means to validate RDF data graphs.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:838a4d71-82fd-4843-ba74-683fe71be723 .

camssa:2924e453-6542-4ec4-a009-cc6d6116165d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19c639047dab46befb5839503733c8f1e7ed8278f788a089d11d2caee84a8f7c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:29271daf-8903-4141-88f7-7457a8c423cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows extension. It provides a framework that enables the addition of new functionality beyond the core features defined in the standard.\r
\r
SOAP 1.2 introduces the concept of SOAP features and SOAP modules, which are mechanisms for extending the SOAP framework. SOAP features define optional capabilities that a SOAP node may support, such as message transmission optimization, reliable messaging, or security features. These features can be defined and implemented by extending the SOAP specification.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aeb0540c-c72b-4a2f-9f8e-eca0237ac657 .

camssa:2929b2b1-c4dc-4f58-8523-52ad6bb8a3b9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4a006ad6785e066d16c13daf48a60ee43ec33d1de1b06613c8e656ccf330a6d5 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:292d7057-704f-42d9-a691-713f86547542 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "RDA Research Data Repository Interoperability Recommendations is a common format for research data. It is an area of application which is not covered by any other technical specification being under consideration to become a European standard. This conclusion has been drawn from the examination of all the programming mandates addressed to CEN, CENELEC and ETSI to the date, CEN’s webpage , CENELEC’s webpage , CEN-CENELEC’s webpage ICT section , the EC Information Providers Guide, Directive (EU) 2016/2102 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 October 2016 on the accessibility of the websites and mobile applications of public sector bodies , the standards and tools for exchange and processing of actionable information inventory of ENISA  and the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c41f1a98-20f4-4f64-8b45-752d43a6529c .

camssa:292def1c-5d86-4415-8a53-130688e8e9a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of ETSI TS 119 432 is often evaluated through various means, including practical implementations and pilot projects. For instance, a 2020-paper about learned lessons from implementing an android client for the Cloud Signature Consortium API highlights the ETSI protocol as the one to be respected for communication between SCA/SIC and SSA/SAM.

Learned Lessons from Implementing an Android Client for the Cloud Signature Consortium API:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-41025-4_15'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8494cd54-0daf-45b8-b7a8-b6babdf5ae0b .

camssa:293175de-92ec-4125-834d-09b2fce0d5a6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-73a8058bec757a2fdb0f8513c2f11841e982cbef76c3be82af67707c294da8b8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:2932ce53-903d-4cde-941f-7a4116b04363 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL is implemented for data validation purposes by DCAT-AP,  which is a specification that describes public sector datasets with the aim to enable cross-data portal search for datasets, and make public sector data easily searchable across borders and sectors.\r
\r
DCAT-AP is used in the Open Data Support service initiated by the European Commission."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:97f02c28-604f-4566-aacb-abf7c5f2b388 .

