camssa:29b28d0c-9231-4b5f-a173-d97aa0d3d581 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPv6 is not related to the modelling of business processes. IPv6 is primarily a network protocol designed to facilitate communication over the internet, and it does not inherently focus on modelling business processes. 

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26ce4271-9264-4e7b-9eb5-de462be96d24 .

camssa:29b72b66-5eaa-466b-91c6-03f103a455b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SVG does not define a cross-sector reusable data model. It defines a common XML schem using XML based tools. By being written in XML, SVG builds on this strong foundation and gains many advantages such as a sound basis for internationalization, powerful structuring capability, an object model, and so on."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b20db4c-71a4-4a11-8d36-b6af0bd34da0 .

camssa:29bbac22-1d1e-44ef-994b-c17a09553775 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:29bc4066-f167-4178-bae7-26b2ce65340a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'When it comes to the preservation mechanisms, ETSI TS 119 512 specifies a data structure "EvidenceExchange", which contains preservation objects and preservation evidences to support seamless export and import from one preservation service to another one using evidence records, As an example, ETSI TS 119 512 is implemented in Germany and its TR-ESOR middleware, therefore proving it can support the evolution of European public services.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf    \r
\r
TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/EN/Service-Navi/Publications/TechnicalGuidelines/TR03125/TechnicalGuidelines_03125_node.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bac0c4b-0cb0-404a-95d8-544db118cce5 .

camssa:29c403f2-0abe-4638-8598-a9459f961b1c a cav:Score,
