camssa:29f797a8-a64d-42d0-ae15-f8efe01e3c05 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"As ECLI implements DCMI, where ECLI is a uniform identifier that has the same recognizable format for all Member States and EU courts, it can be significant of the specification's effectiveness, if used together with other specifications.\r
\r
\r
ECLI Webpage:\r
https://e-justice.europa.eu/175/EN/european_case_law_identifier_ecli?init=true\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:271014da-7802-4ea9-b61c-fdb267478bd6 .

camssa:29f97d71-a850-4d8b-8e18-00afcc97232a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3eaf0fa4-b8de-4998-abe9-c221062069f6 .

camssa:29f9e0ba-0c46-4bdc-852c-b855bd46e58a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no such assessments addressing the effectiveness of the specification. This might be due to the early-stage development of the specification.\r
\r
Besides, the ARIA initiative proposes tools and methods to evaluate e-accessibility. In this sense, in the future there might exist such reports.\r
\r
WAI-ARIA github, issue tracking:\r
https://github.com/w3c/aria-practices/issues/\r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73b8d983-bf03-4a66-a13f-26932c8fcfbe .

camssa:29fa5d8a-a073-42b8-9461-51d9df8ad194 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By allowing the exchange of datasets metadata, DCAT-AP increases the searchability, visibility, discoverability and reuse of existing data, including information on processes and administrative rules. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3656498-4828-4a74-8b43-ff1cb9fea437 .

camssa:2a01b36c-5216-4a52-aa0f-65f82d2bd2b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Overall translation is done to the tags in the optional message content such as "Entity Name" or "Postal \r
Adress", although information in free text shall be written in UK English.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d8fc5bb-be8a-420d-9f31-bb973750138a .

camssa:2a0664db-b659-4b89-b4b7-7ec4ae73d7a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ESPD supports data portability between systems and applications that are used to implement public\r
services by providing a standard format for collecting and sharing procurement-related information. The use\r
of a standard format for procurement-related information enables the exchange of data between different\r
systems and applications, which can help to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of public procurement\r
processes.\r
\r
ESPD Business handbook\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52408060-3437-49bc-8889-d1ee2c7f34f6 .

camssa:2a09bd9a-8fbf-4578-a670-d37251181e65 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0229101dfe08cbe58da1e454363d30a8178a2e120466c8db23965488cae5c8b1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2a10a068-33c1-4828-9925-d087524635f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of TLS is not related to the publication of public data as open data. The main purpose TLS is to provide a secure channel between two communicating peers. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

TLS Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68f0f046-958e-4989-b467-748632b130eb .

camssa:2a121c86-062a-4719-8f16-5c5a22138845 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of UDDI is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

UDDI OASIS reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/standard/uddi/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eba2d9f3-76f0-4858-9e24-8e8813d75af4 .

camssa:2a14eb3a-cd45-49b4-aae6-611505af3d63 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The first version of the EN 303 645 specification was published in 2019 and up to date has reached version 2.1.1. The specification's predecessor was TS 103 645, prior to its designation as a European Standard (EN) (see EN 303 645 homepage reference, OUR ROLE & ACTIVITIES section). All the specification releases can be found in the TC CYBER website or at the EN 303 645 homepage.\r
\r
EN 303 645 homepage reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/technologies/consumer-iot-security\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2578e95-9204-4f28-b054-c233a8a3befc .

camssa:2a1797ad-7f1a-466c-b568-d8ad04808320 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML’s structured format allows to exchange data between different systems and services, facilitating interoperability and integration. Moreover, public services can use YAML to define workflows and automation scripts, improving efficiency and reducing manual intervention. This is particularly useful in public services where multiple agencies and systems need to work together.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5dde6e3-3c4b-41a8-a7c5-6d057b15e32d .

camssa:2a1e1b62-ac62-493a-b244-fc9f8dc6c1fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAREF is not related to providing an access control mechanism. Therefore, this criterion is 
not applicable to this specification.

SAREF: 
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c87adbd-c3e3-4564-987d-1caaf2a29c46 .

camssa:2a26ee0b-5863-420d-b2d6-32b2fc5fd173 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org can be deployed in any platform since the specification can be coded into RDF and JSON-LD, which are compatible with the vast majority of information systems. Therefore, the specification is platform-agnostic.\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Getting started section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/gs.html\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github reference, 'Improving schemas' section:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/blob/main/README.md\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:366aa7f3-48b4-4afd-ac19-b8a4fa80422c .

camssa:2a308149-d27f-45aa-9681-ab6cba1eda0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the time of elaborating this assessment, this specification is included in the "Machine Learning" ABB under the Technical Insfraesctructure View and "Artificial Intelligence" ABB under the Technical Application View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6065e564-77ee-4252-9815-41a4bb3431a2 .

camssa:2a32edb2-569b-4b35-953d-7931c965b1b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:2a3507e4-f922-476f-80ae-e7eeaca30913 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML is designed to be extensible. One of the extensions available is the Core schema which is an extension of the JSON schema, allowing for more human-readable presentation of the same types.

Core Schema YAML:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#103-core-schema'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23a2ac29-0c04-43a0-ad38-6bfd05a42331 .

camssa:2a38d445-8a98-4a15-8b6a-e1456fffa049 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fef5941bab92019b7692f8544de94715a42ed9ff76d89cbec4fb6f9821611925 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:2a428fc0-796c-40d6-8d9e-065dbf28b583 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Dutch National Cyber Security Centre prescribes the use of TLS 1.3 in the latest version of their Security Guidelines (advice on purchasing, drafting and reviewing configurations): \r
https://www.ncsc.nl/documenten/publicaties/2019/mei/01/ict-beveiligingsrichtlijnen-voor-transport-layer-security-tls\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:717b7843-deaf-4bd2-b125-8820fed5bd60 .

camssa:2a4980bc-ea51-4457-8192-207b57d4910c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP is recommended by Italy, The Netherlands, Sweden, Belgium, and Spain. These Member States extended DCAT-AP to meet the specific national needs.\r
\r
See: \r
https://datos.gob.es/sites/default/files/doc/file/report_dcat- \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2a88e09f-7189-4aaf-9b8c-823c1fe979a1 .

camssa:2a50b24a-cb10-49e1-9827-7bef6e2a1bea a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2a50bcb9-4d15-4f60-8e76-fffc64557d82 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs allows to control digital identities, as well as authenticate identities without dependence on centralized authorities. Therefore, DIDs simplifies administrative processes allowing people to manage their digital identities, and also supporting the principle of digital-first. 

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6d7bc5f-879c-49c9-98ff-a46760e2667e .

camssa:2a5a8bf8-7cfe-4968-8e69-f9e04cb68f79 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae5426df-1468-4d10-801a-ed2a82c6e4ff .

camssa:2a5cde0a-6b1a-4761-a80b-63a42ba237d8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2a600b05-0730-4c18-8b45-59e974ec79bb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d921feb8-3f32-4c21-8bab-b87d3e1fcf0a .

camssa:2a6581a0-bc32-46b4-8c55-46beaba4b109 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2a670c20-6a48-485c-9713-991bbb659814 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/66c7661b-8efe-4769-a12d-f9efb652c9f2"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:2a680e15-04ea-4d53-b55e-e4bd59ad06c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OpenTelemetry specification allows extensive customisation to meet the specific needs and requirements of different applications and environments. OpenTelemetry provides SDKs for multiple programming languages where each SDK is designed to be modular, allowing developers to include only the components they need. On the other hand, developers can define custom spans and add custom attributes to spans to capture specific details about their application’s behavior.

OpenTelemetry - Create custom traces and metrics: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/zero-code/net/custom/

OpenTelemetry - Building custom components: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/collector/building/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce241152-463e-4691-a314-7d109700fd52 .

camssa:2a6a9d91-235e-48bd-8b5b-a106db1d2b22 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI fosters a community of nations working together to standardize legal information, and it encourages the
sharing of this data on national and European platforms. This makes it easier to exchange and reuse legal
information across borders

EU Open Data Portal Data sets:
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/data/group/eli?groups=eli

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

5-star linked open data:
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c25fe9fe-a71b-4eaa-ae20-43345dc8f693 .

camssa:2a6af11c-86b4-4365-92ed-26136e308348 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Even though there have been several implementation at different levels of EIRA and its specialisations, there are no studies so far evaluating the effectiveness or efficiency of the specification. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0631537f-f9ab-42e1-aa9a-c417fbf015f2 .

camssa:2a726cd7-9171-4d94-9efe-eec88e0719c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Data on the Web Best Practices Community Group continues the work started by the Data on the Web Best Practices Working Group in investigating topics such as data versioning, subsetting, data access and metadata. It will promote discussions about Data on the Web challenges and best practices, evaluating its benefits and any drawbacks. In doing so, the CG will collect new evidence of the DWBP implementation globally and will offer additional material to promote the adoption of DWBP, while needs for further standardisation will be identified. Needs for further standardisation will be identified.

Data on the Web Best Practices Working Group: 
https://www.w3.org/community/dwbp/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dea33121-7638-4b88-9951-075bed38a340 .

camssa:2a8137c8-bc6c-4ac1-be4b-43972e8e95f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The implementation of XHTML relies on the specific business requirement which is not necessarily aligned
with the reuse of information. The reuse of information might be limited to the definition of variables and this
is much more strict in XHTML in comparison to a more flexible languages, such as HTML5.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c61b7647-625e-4701-97e5-8f34e5db28e6 .

camssa:2a852ddc-49c2-40d3-98c5-85d6637bed79 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2a852f2b-f1f3-403c-8638-48f24ae6720a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the OAIS reference model does not in itself facilitate the reuse of relevant information, it provides a framework for the management and preservation of digital objects over time, which can enable the reuse of information by ensuring that it remains accessible and usable over the long term. The metadata and descriptive information associated with digital objects can also be used to facilitate their discovery and reuse.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53390702-2473-4012-92c9-26fc43e6376b .

camssa:2a88e09f-7189-4aaf-9b8c-823c1fe979a1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b4f0d1b7f1d41c70797fa200c6fc73ac01f2f1659319e5cb1cebe8f5e79c1fcb ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2a8ac55c-f5f6-40af-ab44-f27b2ec84eb9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6f7b3377cc1836eb056d44786260085e36fc1d6856a3aa3d37fe017e16cfc319 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2a8b7d5c-41a1-4926-92b5-47ab0bd87b21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, WAI-ARIA can define the interoperability aspects of the "Human Interface" ABB and the "Public Administration Single Window" of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e40f8853-9daa-4cc2-a19d-27f6f76d4447 .

camssa:2a97011c-8803-4fd6-8abf-62fccc44c847 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 provides a collection of codes for the names of countries, dependent territories and special areas of geographical interest, regardless of any specific domain. Therefore, the specification can be used in any domain.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffd1ee32-0e6e-4c41-8f19-42ae0c8d36aa .

camssa:2a99ba34-373d-4611-9583-d9bf03d610bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any article or study assessing the efficiency of the ISO/IEC 19944-1.  \r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6e3ff8f-cb70-4d7a-abad-9fe1ac0639e2 .

camssa:2aa52a14-20e5-45a9-9c3f-4ae57525ebfe a cav:Score,
