camssa:2aa7fd8c-3f9d-4f22-9665-795d8b518338 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
IETF Reference: \r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:023642e5-4409-498c-96a3-885c9f96c25d .

camssa:2aacc273-b67d-4a94-9b45-1f9f3ee95fea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Such means as providing an access control mechanism can be provided as SOAP extensions using the SOAP extensibility mode. The SOAP Messaging Framework does not directly provide any mechanism for dealing with it directly.\r
\r
SOAP Reference, section 7 Security Considerations:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/#secconsiderations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b311ea6f-cb6f-41d2-ac76-3342ecc55491 .

camssa:2ab3d88e-e7c5-42b1-822d-275e463b7128 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2ab4de72-f6ce-4155-9439-7bd5bc245ffb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPsec is not related to the exchange of data and therefore, it can not ease the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
IPSec reference, What IPSec Does:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-7'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5364e961-5f8d-411f-a203-c1db3ae79201 .

camssa:2ab85a48-fdee-4cc6-9479-5bf26d3d5368 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SMP 2.0 specification developed by OASIS does not directly address the authenticity and authentication of roles or agents involved in data transactions but can contributes to enabling authenticity features as described in section 5.6.2.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference, section 5.6.2 about contribution to enabling authenticity features:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505052'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e160535-de32-4a90-b1b8-dc638c09a73c .

camssa:2ab91735-4bc8-4a9e-b39b-94b0b3c021f2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a64b01ca9e737c550b205ba3a8a46b3fcfc9447b648ba8ef15d62d3ada26141 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:2ad05a49-ba25-4fb5-b933-be3275b94654 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Xforms 2.0 includes data structures and models that can be considered as reusable models for establishing data policies, the data involved and the processes involved. \r
\r
Xforms 2.0 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/xformsusers/wiki/XForms_2.0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6bc7f01-e16d-46ea-bcb3-01bdc64a929c .

