    cav:judgement "The purpose of XAdES is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a28be4c2-0418-4f52-aedb-0631c23b6b3b .

camssa:2aea4287-a73a-49cd-895a-03bf8b1f4c1e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI TF is the body in charge of the maintenance and development of the specification. In the ELI
Governance document, it is defined how and by who the specification is evolved.
Member States are open to participate in the evolution of the specification only with soft requirements like
having implemented the specification at a national level and having the knowledge to contribute to the
evolution of ELI.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

Governance Rules:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/governance_rules.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6440be23-54c0-425b-bf92-2a74345eac19 .

camssa:2af1beb0-100c-4bc2-9d13-d49d8385ec49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """In the context of eSignatures and Seals, the European Commission has stated an Implementing decision where urged the Member States and other Public services providers to recognise CAdES, PAdES, XAdES, and ASIC as formats for electronic signatures purposes. \r
\r
See: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32015D1506"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:936d7fa1-6f8f-4d29-99f9-330f399cbef7 .

