camssa:2bc82f87-a4ca-4b99-bd6c-9c6072fb8fb8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The iCalendar specification has many known implementations, and currently being used by some of the top leading technologic companies such as Apple or Google. From this fact it is evident that the iCalendar has widespread market acceptance, as well as it is being used for the creation of innovative solutions.\r
\r
iCalendar implementations:\r
https://microformats.org/wiki/icalendar-implementations\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:157413bf-466d-48fb-bf74-a14943312b55 .

camssa:2bd1b244-da80-4ba3-adb7-4b93bd418a3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The simplification of the delivery of public services is not on how they are deliver, it starts with the analysis and design phase of these services. There is where EIRA is meant to focus and support the simplification of European public services. 

The holistic approach of the specification ensures that there is a translation between legal requirements into the technical implementations. By providing different perspectives to different aspects such identification and access management, EIRA can help public administrations to develop services considering simplification by design. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:befd0b06-9a63-46c9-b8e2-53261cf8a1ae .

camssa:2bd1cfec-d859-4e1e-aab3-25411ba625ad a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2bd3bc41-b393-4220-82d9-adcd556ce1eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related to fostering visibility and comprehensibility of administrative rules, processes, data, services and decision-making of a public administration. . Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:99eaad1e-c2ae-4315-a603-9ab015baeb9a .

camssa:2bdbe80e-dbad-4e40-a38a-a463232407c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The syslog protocol provides a standardized framework for logging messages, and to a considerable extent, it supports the reuse of relevant information when needed. Some aspects of the syslog protocol that facilitate 
information include structured data, standardised message format, integration with logging systems, etc.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b326623b-9c2e-464f-8141-303a72287911 .

camssa:2be39d21-527b-41b1-b8b5-b3184e9663ad a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-138786a6e7517e10b94e83ec3b3e7ac79b4c49dcbeaef8d8e993c8df0d173529 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:2be58c8b-6c6c-4823-9b0d-518fbe414243 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPSec is maintained and developed by IETF which is an international community developing open standards\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.ietf.org/about/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4301 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec56c048-1439-4389-9acc-64f4092f03b8 .

camssa:2be8cc33-4030-456d-aca7-065ae8955b09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF is a vendor neutral standard developing organisation and HTTP is independent from any technology or platform.\r
\r
See:                                                                                                                                       https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2616"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:868ccd56-65be-4b7e-ac49-2b21d1edf818 .

camssa:2beb4d81-b4e1-4635-9889-a1fe8f86f0ea a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2bf21426-bc73-46bd-b0d1-846f5b082a90 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2bf70d86-a121-4ae7-9e89-0637c6c2917e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Each test performed by the specification has a tag EUMS (European Union Member State) that varies \r
depending on the Member State or not Member State using the specification, so although not explicitly \r
recommended, there are Member States that use it.\r
This is supporting eIDAS implementations especifically for validating the requirements from ETSI TS 119 \r
614-1 V1.1.1\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e83e948-7988-4ba1-8dd1-650cc5436b9a .

