camssa:2c127171-f6eb-4756-b119-f9aa56e7fe3d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of OWL2 is to allow accessing, importing, sharing, and reusing public ontologies. The data described by an ontology in the OWL family is interpreted as a set of "individuals" and a set of "property assertions" which relate these individuals to each other. _x000D_\r
Following this logic, the specification helps to improve the comprehensibility of the administration’s data. By allowing to infer knowledge from sets of data and information, OWL provides meaning to the represented data. Therefore, it fosters the comprehensibility of administrative data while helps the decision-making process of administrations._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
OWL2 W3C reference:_x000D_\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:753f33af-5081-4b36-b11c-db8795005f49 .

camssa:2c1e8102-56d9-4591-a4c5-53b97cda80cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2c232dc1-a605-41d0-8e07-6350aaff7d42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EuroVoc was developed for the first time in 1982 and has full support from the European Union, since it was \r
developed to support and help European and National institutions on their functions. The thesaurus \r
categorises knowledge domains close to the European Institution. Therefore, it can be considered with \r
market acceptance at eGovernment level for the development of products and services.\r
\r
EuroVoc over the time: \r
https://op.europa.eu/es/web/eu-vocabularies/th-dataset/-/resource/dataset/eurovoc?target=About#Time\r
\r
Eurovoc: \r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f4d81ef-8821-413f-8ebb-fa04b1b5fa47 .

camssa:2c24fd48-9887-48b9-bd77-9a68966e802b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSS is a simple mechanism for adding style (fonts, colours, spacing...) to web documents, but by itself, it does not publish data on the web. It also does not comply with the other levels of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee's 5 stars for open data nor the principles of the linked open data.\r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/\r
\r
Five star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02590019-567e-4a15-95c9-dfcd027c9413 .

camssa:2c29006e-6b4c-4d4c-887a-ff75800293e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TrainingDML-AI standard aims to maximize the interoperability and reusability of geospatial training data. It provides detailed metadata for formalizing the information model of training data. This includes aspects such as how the training data is prepared, how to specify different metadata used for different ML tasks, and how to differentiate the high-level training data information model and extended information models specific to various ML applications.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09510ab2-dc6e-4eb5-a664-28aa8f863c68 .

