camssa:2d0364f0-6ceb-49a9-9270-0111cfa83c91 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML provides a set of components enabling users (data users) to store and work with any type of electronic content, fostering the comprehensibility of administrations' rules and processes. As well as providing an electronic data interchange model (that is, the ebRIM and the ebRS core components), the specification contributes and promotes to the comprehensibility of public services' implementations (see ebXML reference, Conformance section). For instance, there there is the ESPD-EDM on EU procurement, which relies on the Universal Business Language (UBL) and facilitates the implementation of the ESPD service over the Member States.\r
\r
ebXML reference, Conformance section:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__53396_365468741\r
\r
ESPD-EDM ebXML reference:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_technical_handbook.html#_adoption_of_ubl_2_3\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1c1e2341-9883-43bf-a67d-88d1d98f2388 .

