camssa:2e0e8577-82d7-4c33-b29f-e00306d3d3a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification was started in 1999 as a joint initiative between the United Nations Centre for Trade facilitation and Electronic Business (UN/CEFACT) and Organization for the Advancement of Structured Information Standards (OASIS). A joint coordinating committee composed of representatives from each of the two organisations led the effort. In this context, four different versions have been launched since 1999, and each release can be found in the OASIS web. The current and latest version (4.0) was launched in 2012.
However, the specification has joined ISO recently, and in future releases it is possible that release management will not be available publicly.

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html

ebXML RegRep ISO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/83479.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04cd295b-b224-4479-8bab-9b657e2a74fc .

camssa:2e172fc0-b6f4-4586-81fb-fb9168528c48 a cav:Score,
