    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2e452eaf-0f35-497e-a97a-c76aa7a05761 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NGSI-LD Information Model prescribes the structure of context information that shall be supported by an
NGSI-LD system. The NGSI-LD Information Model is defined at two levels: the foundation classes which correspond to the Core Meta-model and the Cross-Domain Ontology.  The latter is a set of generic, transversal classes which are aimed at avoiding conflicting or redundant definitions of the same classes in each of the domain-specific ontologies.

GS CIM 009: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/CIM/001_099/009/01.07.01_60/gs_CIM009v010701p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1dd46a5f-ecb5-4e3a-a893-bc0aea309e29 .

camssa:2e541cec-3bf5-4834-8367-45d80d6f778e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2e56bc16-f828-4339-a8b0-51ee79f1b635 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2e585964-7b6b-4383-aa12-d493552326d8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS could be used in a multilingual context beyond a statistical purpose. The specification could be useful in determining the linguistic and dialectical areas when establishing a specific European public service.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74d89de6-d37e-45b0-9cfc-411586d24611 .

camssa:2e5a2dc0-a091-48f0-ad7b-fb4ff1a5580b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is currently implemented in several initiatives in the public sector. The ODF helps to avoid vendor lock-in, which is part of the recommendations of EIF. Additionally, LibreOffice implements natively different versions of the Open Document Format. This is a key point that reflects the market acceptance of the specification.  \r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office\r
\r
ODF in a UK government project:\r
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/open-standards-for-government/sharing-or-collaborating-with-government-documents """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7444c37e-67fa-4773-9672-0af62ab65995 .

camssa:2e5e906b-91f9-437a-9e43-019bd8a9dec3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:2e5f5da9-f7c4-45d7-8b28-9c837ffc0085 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """One of the pillars of ELI is the usage of URIs templates patterns that ensure that resources are accessible in a persistent way over time. This fact fosters the long-term preservation of electronic documents ensuring their availability. Moreover, since it provides access to legal documentation in a machine-readable format, it also fosters its reuse and evolution towards other formats ensuring the evolution of European Public Services. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ac139d6-a716-44c4-848f-ed1da59bd45f .

camssa:2e61844b-cf9f-464a-983b-a4695cdd7852 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-105c699a138c27ab9a1af9174253cd7488b278f700acdbb1bdbcc3e0b9c5ec3d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2e6353e2-dd6e-4cb4-99bd-9454a69e3089 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:2e75fe60-a5f7-4b09-a4e0-79e10be957ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c03fa05-848a-485a-ad9b-c8f50c46f465 .

camssa:2e7654ce-cef4-429f-9607-618509de22fc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:2e7dbbcd-cb8a-4e17-b2db-3c9afe07f0d4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:2e81d54c-259c-407d-a5ed-eb873b9ef81e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:2e84d1f2-cfcd-4827-8c47-23403701928d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XACML is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, XACML can define the interoperability aspects of the "Access Management Component", and  "Access Management Service" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:595ad340-5bce-4f7f-b56a-8c7435238a8d .

camssa:2e8b02dd-e3df-44ca-b818-1910ca25b51c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, the IPv4 is widely adopted as a key point on making data, information, and resources available on the internet.  However, it is worth to point out that the new version recently is being gradually adopted including several innovative solutions. Furthermore, there are already transition mechanisms to connect nodes using different versions of the Internet protocol. \r
Nevertheless, the European Commission has endorsed the adoption of IPv6 in new initiatives in order to ease the transition to the new version of the protocol. \r
See: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/LexUriServ/LexUriServ.do?uri=CELEX:52002DC0096:EN:HTML"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:327917cf-e2cd-4e94-bf6e-d0802c0af8c0 .

