camssa:2f474e93-ea0c-46ee-89c7-a3a9ed46b148 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, HTML5 is supporting the first level of maturity the which corresponds to make data available on the internet. \r
\r
HTML5 is the center of the Open Web Platform, it allows programming application.\r
\r
See:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11cfd60d-bf85-48e3-b0ee-bde0a81b5d82 .

camssa:2f4812c8-8764-4bf6-8cc6-58c720bcaacb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose Member State NIF has a high performance on interoperability according to NIFO factsheets.

NIFO Factsheets:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ac13829-80b1-4f27-bdf2-3772277a209c .

camssa:2f492f01-e507-4fc5-8422-fbd99f629701 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has one major release published on the 6th of September of 2023. At the same time, the specification has a GitHub where change and release management is published.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes

LDES GitHub: 
https://github.com/SEMICeu/LinkedDataEventStreams
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04682fd6-59b5-40e8-86e6-cb5cd596e13e .

camssa:2f495f78-73ef-4114-aa72-0be876f9ffec a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:2f4c2377-3c07-48cc-b8d9-6f5b1c3b2435 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of IPv6 is not to enhance visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services, but can contribute to it. For example, the specification provides a larger address space compared to IPv4, enabling more hierarchical addressing. This can simplify network management and enhance visibility, making it easier to organise and categorise network resources.

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e31409e-4244-4614-a738-11477fe806d6 .

camssa:2f4d77df-3b6f-4f32-a5a2-1e72ce0d4a2e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification contributes to enchance and simplify the process of drafting legal documents. This fact helps to save time and resources by removing administrative burden that have been related to regulation drafting over the years. An example of this is the LEOS software. \r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php\r
\r
LEOS: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/justice-law-and-security/solution/leos-open-source-software-editing-legislation\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55e1d5ac-e150-4858-b372-dde8cd001362 .

camssa:2f53476a-9544-426d-807c-b0958ebc5f22 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:2f548dde-ad82-4d62-8760-a14f4f0cd002 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CIM NGSI-LD API is developed and maintained by the European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI). Its development involves contributions from industry experts and collaboration within ETSI working groups, particularly ETSI Technical Committee CIM. This standardisation body provides a foundational level of support for the ontology. ETSI takes into account the impact of users as they improve their standards and their relevancy. 

ETSI Technical Committee CIM: https://www.etsi.org/committee/cim'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37b4f218-fbb7-484f-b850-04fbb1c44127 .

camssa:2f585471-5375-472b-8d5c-bcc3d6591a3e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:2f5a783e-86c6-4bfa-a147-dff18d423292 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAREF is not related to ensuring the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. 

SAREF: 
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fca13e5a-b4d8-4897-835b-189fb006cca0 .

camssa:2f5c372f-fa6a-4840-b9a8-f308758cdd20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The EuroVoc Hanbook contains important information about the concept scheme, disambiguation of thesaurus terms, their relationships, EuroVoc maintenance etc. thus, defining requirements to conform to the specification's implementation.\r
\r
EuroVoc Hanbook:\r
https://publications.europa.eu/resource/cellar/a2723a83-574f-11eb-b59f-01aa75ed71a1.0001.01/DOC_1\""""@en ;
