camssa:3075f995-3f72-4fcc-826a-1e87ad448780 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no mention of OData in any official document stating its conformance in regards to Regulation 1025/2012. It does not appear in any of the main European standard development bodies, therefore, the specification is not a European standard.

ICT technical specifications:
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technicalspecifications_en

CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb37485c-cd02-4ada-8cd0-36a984f3121c .

camssa:3078b259-4f20-4657-a745-dd7f15b89e0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating and Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all of the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:\r
- Technical excellence;\r
- prior implementation and testing;\r
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;\r
- openness and fairness; and \r
- timeliness.\r
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca351c46-118d-47fe-9df0-6b2b3cdc3570 .

camssa:307989d6-0197-49a7-97fa-55d0063aa3ba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:307ce1b4-2974-4bbc-9553-9222ae44a6c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is not directly related to data protection, as its main purpose is to specify protocols for trust service providers providing long-term data preservation services for digital signatures and general data. Data protection considerations are overlooked given that they are addressed by its companion document ETSI TS 119 511 (Policy and security requirements for trust service providers providing long-term preservation of digital signatures or general data using digital signature techniques)\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a6924d7-78f2-47d8-bd10-4705b64f2e8e .

camssa:307cffa1-defb-4792-b6f7-e38851acd360 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-838030847fa0adf54939e3feaac0ac2510924c54035e1cb671b223b54b02fd70 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:307de662-5e4b-4ef7-823a-8251b1269d32 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification enables the visibility of administrative procedures as ISO 19941 is about cloud computing interoperability and data portability. Integration and portability of administrative data is crucial in enhancing its visibility.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3854da72-0f5e-4eab-8b69-0449c4ee5274 .

camssa:307eb231-cc9b-4ee9-a50e-92cd5ae2d61e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41c8cb43-7a0a-44a1-acba-96d6e89cfa2b .

camssa:308816d6-425b-410f-be5c-bf1dca582d5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is used to encode all communications to web services. Therefore, it fosters the availability of public administrations interfaces.\r
\r
Additionally, the benefit of using XML is that web services are not tied to any one operating system or programming.\r
\r
See:\r
https://esentool.ted.europa.eu/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0a0d9eab-23ea-43dc-95f8-175ca24fb171 .

camssa:3089ee61-da0c-4c72-9f74-e027352a7cbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI registries can implement enhanced security measures to ensure controlled access and protect personal data. For instance, the WebSphere Application Server facilitates access to UDDI records based on user categories, ensuring that sensitive information is accessible only to authorized users.

IBM security reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was/8.5.5?topic=curs-configuring-uddi-registry-use-websphere-application-server-security'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6718c2a6-1846-430c-992c-4d53b014d4fc .

camssa:308dd275-657f-484b-b847-9220376a0481 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The German Climate Computing Center (DKRZ) has used the recommendation to deploy an operative service that enables data users to create custom research data collections (\"data carts\") as part of the global Earth System Grid Federation (ESGF): https://esgf-data.dkrz.de/projects/esgf-dkrz/datacart_pid"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1fda560b-1fca-4b5a-a8f1-3a18841df5e7 .

camssa:3093d8e2-49d5-49b7-af97-5b59fcfa5534 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification is included in the solutions catalogue of ICT Standards for Procurement created by the European Commision. The European Catalogue will contribute to these objectives by offering a one-stop-shop for procurers on guidelines for procurement, including on vendor lock-in, on the use of standards, and a lifecycle costing scheme that accounts for the often neglected interoperability costs. It will streamline the numerous guidelines and provide for a platform of exchange and dissemination.\r
\r
ICT Standards for Procurement: https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72b3fb59-ba28-4c03-a02e-278185aaa372 .

camssa:3095180a-f552-46e1-a9bc-a1c0973e0e18 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
