camssa:30e02b51-199a-4616-a055-b7fa324db0c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML complies with the five principles of Open Data since it publishes data in a structured, machinereadable
format, is XML-compliant for easy viewing, editing, and validation of documents, and supports new
elements and extensions to ensure interoperability across different environments. Built on open standards,
XHTML is compatible with open-source tools and facilitates the publication of data under open licenses,
eliminating the need for proprietary software.

XHTML Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/#xhtml'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39cd326b-291c-4aae-a74c-89d548cd9b18 .

camssa:30e2dbb6-342e-43d3-bc3e-c1ab02afe91f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is at the core of multiple usecases complied on the IDTA initiative. Some of them are Collaborative Engineering and Product Carbon Footprint. Both use the AAS as way to facilitate the traceability of data (carbon footprint or desing changes) among partners and the creation of communities/working groups associated with this tasks.

Product Carbon Footprint use case
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/use-cases/product-carbon-footprint 

Collaborative Engineering use case:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/use-cases/collaborative-engineering-the-technological-basis-for-the-digitalized-value-chain

IDTA use cases:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/use-cases

IDTA Github
https://github.com/admin-shell-io 

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf8b3172-0202-473a-8b3a-dbfdd5adeae4 .

camssa:30e2f7f5-17dc-42ff-bfda-577d92e40716 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:30e93f9f-c17a-4e12-b3f6-474c8c933693 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. So it can be said that JPEG is independent of any specific technology or platform. \r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9643eaf8-e735-4b29-b458-85f4b6961b4d .

camssa:30edd65a-ee73-4ce3-bbb5-4f7d526a57f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'However, the E-ARK CSIP can indirectly support the publication of data on the web in structured and machine-readable formats. By following the CSIP guidelines, organizations can create well-structured information packages that include descriptive metadata. This metadata can provide valuable information about the content of the package, making it easier for users to discover and understand the data within. Moreover, the specification also outlines the the importance of using open standards such as XML.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03307f65-5377-41df-8bbd-5444994120e7 .

camssa:30f8b839-5b88-481c-8d47-7e35cbbb2785 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:30f92875-9eb9-4459-98dd-8328c9555889 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CAdES is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:812ebe71-b5ab-4ae8-a1d9-74855ef785ca .

camssa:30fa1117-8c6e-4906-b5a5-ae333b8bc4a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The OASIS Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the OASIS Patent Policy apply to all OASIS specifications, including SMP.\r
\r
OASIS Case Study Guidelines:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/casestudies"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f82adc9e-d740-4c71-b477-a6f09174247f .

camssa:30fb7a0d-a10f-4634-99cc-f2928a750ad7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No evidences have been found of the specification being included in a formal interoperability agreement between organisations involved in the European public services provision."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d05bd52-53fb-442e-9a83-f0128394220f .

camssa:3107fc3a-6ee8-44fe-a7fd-6ed67cf5f7fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 16234-1 first appeared as a common framework of professional digital and IT competences, skills and knowledge in 2008, known as CEN Workgroup Agreement (CWA) 15893-1:2008 (see CEN Workshop on ICT Skills reference, List of CWAs section). EN 16234-1 v2.0 of the standard was launched in 2010 (known as CWA 16234-1:2010), and a third release in 2014 (CWA 16234-1:2014). In 2016, EN 16234-1 e-CF (EN 16234-1:2016) was adopted as a European Standard (see CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.1). The official lastest version of the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification was published in 2019 (EN 16234-1:2019), which corresponds to version 4.0. Although the specification meets the requirements for a mature specification, there is no documentation on its development processes. \r
\r
CEN Workshop on ICT Skills reference, List of CWAs section:\r
http://relaunch.ecompetences.eu/cen-ict-skills-workshop/\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.1:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93f90788-3649-42be-9231-bef7f61008a5 .

camssa:31110f2d-6da0-4092-b4fe-605552f85f43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SFIA is intended to serve as a device to represent the skills and competences of any ICT professional workforce which largely benefits the reuse of relevant information in all information systems. There is no evidence of any relationship between SFIA and the One Time One Principle (OOP).\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52ed161d-efc0-40e3-9003-2bbf3d194abf .

