camssa:318cf785-4809-414d-a5c6-f9c5bdd98bfb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the XBRL specification explicitly notes that security, privacy and confidentiality are not directly in\r
scope for XBRL, the chief architect of XBRL GL developed the structure of XBRL GL based on more than 10\r
years working with the XML security efforts of the W3C and is a named contributor to the XML Encryption\r
specification. In particular, personally identifiable information is segregated and standardized to simplify\r
encryption and other protection efforts.\r
\r
This issue of data protection is dependent on other specifications or technologies like the XML Encryption. \r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2caf84b-ef83-4c92-b767-e70c812a3145 .

