        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) has established Working Groups. These Working Groups are open to the participation of everyone interested in semantic solutions working for public administrations in the Member States or in EU institutions.\r
\r
SEMIC working groups:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac6ccbd1-a58a-4932-861e-b2a079524f97 .

camssa:31a24510-6035-434f-bd6e-04349a974a20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA has the Web Accessibility Initiative - Communities of Practice (WAI-COOP) platform for sharing results and best practices. Therefore, the specification encourages the creation of open information about the specification and encourages relevant communities from the EU to share their results; therefore, this platform also extends at national level.\r
\r
WAI-COOP reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/WAI/about/projects/wai-coop/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82c5da75-3333-43c6-972d-c52c0e40aa05 .

