camssa:31fde9f1-3203-4019-8ce3-7bb8a95ffccd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is in a very early stage, has been implemented and it is being implemented in Italy and Germany. However, at the moment of performing the assessment, there are no assessment of the specifications efficiency. 

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Italian National Software Catalogue:
https://developers.italia.it/

Open CoDE:
https://opencode.de/en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cf3516f-a4f6-47ff-a3ca-ab35e55acf10 .

camssa:32030902-da62-4a33-99f8-be15c6b8043a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-31bf959b6c4a983ec70eb87e0177f2739575ebce42c7c3b95b9012ef3bfe673e ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:320ab39e-6baa-4ba0-8b7b-792dec86f7a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, CPOV can define the interoperability aspects of the "Core Data Model" and "Data" ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications camss/solution/elis/distribution/elis-v600xlsx'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23a2f6b9-1222-4e76-8562-8e4dcaee5ce3 .

camssa:32163dcd-3d37-4028-8673-6a02a73e99ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 is not related to enabling the long-term preservation of data (electronic records included). 
Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21517b68-1b99-4809-a141-e8356c12e91b .

camssa:32172b77-6194-430b-9743-517e2d6de016 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:32198a37-a116-41db-8f55-f5a5c3688e44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including ADMS.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8789f4e6-3bb7-4c0b-b48d-56386df9f876 .

camssa:321becce-b7c2-46bf-bb43-255a0622be01 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The use of precomputed responses allows replay attacks in which an old (good) response is replayed prior\r
to its expiration date but after the certificate has been revoked. Deployments of OCSP should carefully\r
evaluate the benefit of precomputed responses against the probability of a replay attack and the costs\r
associated with its successful execution.\r
\r
OCSP reference, section 5:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8b8c136-13f8-4022-93bf-e0ae957a3065 .

camssa:321cb71b-8a0f-4f1c-b862-6dd62f13fc0a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:321f4962-8355-40f9-a11f-fc6ad4ff84c2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:32205ebd-23c6-4c61-8034-7a7eb89881a2 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/4ddf45b0-4f8e-412a-917d-f1d4379713e3"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:322330bc-b7c3-4b4e-886d-01706704ff1d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification refers to the Dynamic Attribute Provisioning Services so, it is inherently abstract and can be \r
implemented and/or used in any domain as long as it fulfills the requirements. Therefore, its use goes beyond a specific business domain.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76f5ba58-6a32-43ab-926e-3c3aefec9427 .

camssa:32242ef2-1ff0-4734-ad32-7df2843ad88d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the official documentation, ISO 3166-1 was first published in 1974, and subsequent editions in 2003, 2013 and 2020. ISO 3166-1 is the Part 1 of the ISO 3166 family of standards, which was divided in three parts in 1997. Part 1 was created on the basis of country names obtained from the United Nations. In 2013 the specification was integrated in an ISO "standard as a database" (see ISO 3166-1 reference, Country Codes on the Online Browsing Platform), easing its accessibility on the web and integrating all the specification's supporting processes (e.g. change history of country codes). Besides, the specification has published documentation on its supporting processes (see ISO 3166-1 reference, Public Information on ISO 3166-1).\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference, Introduction section:\r
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:72482:en\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference, Country Codes on the Online Browsing Platform:\r
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#search/code/\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference, Public Information on ISO 3166-1:\r
rg/livelink/livelink?func=ll&objId=16944257&objAction=browse&viewType=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dbebfef9-0670-4854-a33c-971ab3ffdb2d .

camssa:3233e014-fe5f-4575-a3c3-b41859044af6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5b29a4581c52656a3bcf08224b259c29610cb540c56af4512ebe0ded3adeeac1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:323751f8-5d81-4204-be0a-78d08557489a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 19941 is chosen as one of the specifications recommended for the creation of dataspace infrastructures in the Data Space Support Center, which typically supports this type of projects. \r
\r
DSSC: https://dssc.eu/space/SE1/185794608/Data+Interoperability+standards+and+technologies+landscape'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e77fb2f9-275f-4e5e-a76f-4efd0141b0d3 .

camssa:3237cb99-da7c-4d7d-95db-ee9b116b4be7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is more about the "what" and "how" of a web service—what operations it supports and how to communicate with it. The Web Services Description Language (WSDL) is primarily focused on describing the interface and operations of web services, emphasizing the contract between the service provider and consumer. It provides a standardized way to specify the location of a web service, the operations it supports, the format of the messages, and the protocols for communication.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3942504-0ef8-4988-bcc7-e229557895fb .

camssa:32387785-d0e0-4153-a7e4-f49ee29e8db8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to foster the availability and comprehensibility of public administrations services or the decision-making process."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a52cb1ce-54df-4f59-a920-3ad551fc84b3 .

camssa:3239ae25-45b5-4e94-9cfb-ef019f305918 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:3241a3c4-ad18-42b5-b910-decdde1f039f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Standard for Public Code aims to be a reference resource for making public administration efficient when creating public services and products reusable. Its usage can benefit European Institutions of a common method for the development of software solutions to be deployed all around Europe. The flexibility and capacity to adapt the code for a specific purpose and the general guidelines for its creation and documentation can foster the creation of software solutions supporting multilingualism. Moreover, it could be used together with other already existing resources as the CEF Translation Building Block to ensure multilingual service delivery.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f817c4d9-bbbd-466f-b156-7c5fed6a783c .

camssa:32477a75-394d-4a58-982f-b36d8dfa190d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification purpose is to enable communications over the internet. IPv6 is the new version of IPv4 which is a widely used protocol therefore it is not dependent of any specific platform or technology. Thus, the adoption of IPv6 does not hamper the interoperability. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:810c4a0b-a712-4a23-a0bf-706cac9b2348 .

camssa:324ac1c2-3de2-4925-99c5-76c969207ac3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of a location, represented as an address, a geographic name, or a geometry. By describing locations (addresses, geographical names, etc) in a common way using both human and machine-readable format, it allows the publication of information as open data for its consultation and reuse. In addition, the specification resorts to the usage of an open standard such as JSON-LD. In addition, this vocabulary is also aligned with the 5 stars of tim.berners.

Tim.berners 5stardata:
https://5stardata.info/en/

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:77beebf5-ec0d-465e-bc16-fb99a72cea25 .

camssa:324e1187-7091-4fa5-b0b5-9da9bd657183 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a document format, PDF/A helps to make data available on the internet. This fact demonstrates that the standard is supporting the first level of maturity from Tim Berners-Lee's 5-star schema for Open data.  \r
\r
PDF/A reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/38920.html\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/50655.html\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/es/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab88c0bc-9b2a-4601-8d10-08496371c1bb .

camssa:324f869d-5293-446c-859f-0e1bc0c40705 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:32558a41-eaf2-4a8b-9b5d-f4872b6e560d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of PDF 1.7 is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48501d08-bb15-41fc-a54d-7c586784a251 .

