        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:326b7b21-8076-4a69-abc4-4c5c43c22131 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a1a97870-0098-41f3-b6ab-bb765c2ef786 .

camssa:3271566a-2357-4040-81e8-291f3cf0610a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:327347da-6360-49dd-aea0-b737d7b5c11b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:3278d0d7-9fc7-4bc1-b40a-f8f5745df762 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org opted for a flexible data model and introduced 'hosted extensions' (see Schema.org Hosted Extensions reference), as a way of adding more detailed descriptive vocabulary building on the schema.org core vocabulary (see Schema.org reference, Organization of Schemas section, Extensions subsection). The specification allows extension and encourages users to share their work through through the GS1 Web Vocabulary platform; external extensions are, however, out of the scope of the schema.org development community.\r
\r
Schema.org Hosted Extensions reference:\r
https://schema.org/docs/extension.html\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Organization of Schemas section, Extensions subsection:\r
https://schema.org/docs/schemas.html\r
\r
GS1 Web Vocabulary platform:\r
https://www.gs1.org/voc/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58f7f2a8-2a8f-4de4-a56d-2fe4af80f6aa .

camssa:327917cf-e2cd-4e94-bf6e-d0802c0af8c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cf1de0bf03a8ee372af0deddf9ef5c4609f5a7bb9c7e001c89d887c6789eaf56 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:32842db5-d653-47a7-961f-4f8fe338ddbc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML facilitates organisational interoperability agreements, since one of the specification's objectives is to boost interoperability within organisations. For example, ebXML enables the creation of Collaboration Protocol Agreement (CPA).\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
Joinup CPA toolkit reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-security/solution/cpa-creation-toolkit\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16ff4ea5-b030-4366-a2be-3aa156b9513c .

camssa:32871aa3-1221-4916-adf1-906ea74da7e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """In some cases, the specification uses ambiguous and misleading terms such as “data-data” and “literature-data” which hampers the understanding of the recommendations. \r
The specification has been adopted by different organisations and initiatives and it demonstrates that the specification has sufficient completeness and consistency for the use and development of products and services.\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad724efb-5ef2-4672-b02c-1beeabefd1f3 .

camssa:3289a4df-0b99-4143-9be5-a739f732da5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAMM was defined with flexibility in mind so that small, medium, and large organizations using any style of development can customize and adopt it. It provides a means of knowing where your organization is on its journey towards software assurance and understanding what is recommended to move to the next level of maturity. So it can be said that SAMM can be applied and developed in different domains and purposes without harming the interoperability of functionality of systems.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/ \r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0627925-07d0-49f9-bf98-4648d014eb97 .

camssa:328d60bb-e7df-4adf-9734-37e349b573a7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:328f8a69-c623-420c-8cf3-1262e1698147 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in the different official European websites and repositories, there is no evidence that the GITB TDL is included in an open repository/catalogue of standards at a national level.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:78a191c2-869e-4242-bce2-690f2020a8c4 .

