camssa:3410f410-4936-4c30-a05e-17632b829f8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition.\r
\r
Zaragoza's City Townhall using HTML5 exemplifies the promotion of the once-only principle work towards unifying the services  offered regardless of the platform.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0373e705-6939-4524-85b7-154b670713c1 .

camssa:34146c05-5691-4f7f-a8b1-e04aa259a27d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In the Introduction of the documentation, is it explicitly named that in some European Union Member States \r
(Italy, Belgium, etc.) regulation(s) and application(s) are being developed, if not already in place.\r
Also as mentioned in a previous criteria, Italia is using ESI/REM for their own purposes, reference in the \r
following link:\r
\r
REM Services- Criteri di adozione degli standard ETSI- Italy Policy IT: \r
https:// www.agid.gov.it/sites/default/files/repository_files/rem_services_-\r
_criteri_di_adozione_degli_standard_etsi_-_policy_it_1.0_28_maggio_2021.pdf\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b09cc35-bd1f-40b2-8ace-df24a8e7a24b .

camssa:341820a2-fc54-4640-afa0-9af47ff6cdce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:edf560c5-b90a-4ee4-81dd-05026c2bccf1 .

camssa:341b2057-a78c-4108-9685-0cab884a8258 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) provides protection against unauthorized changes to DNS information by encrypting DNS queries and responses, thereby ensuring the integrity of the data during transmission and preventing DNS spoofing and tampering. However, the HTTPS connection does not provide the response integrity of DNS data provided by DNSSEC.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c522a2c-6c23-412c-9492-d3dab1ea164e .

camssa:342d5c69-d02a-4845-b92c-f03e891bd227 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "100%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage",
        "81.28%AssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:34307c54-093b-4be8-9960-e54b2a4627df a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is not yet been included in an open repository/catalogue of standards at national level.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c45b1e1-42a8-4db0-821f-5bce5c1d6e16 .

camssa:34309d93-2f2b-4fc8-8144-67c538870c8d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3435c988-0998-4e30-80ff-2b20a2c6300d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of EN 303 645, operates under the ETSI Intellectual Property Rigths (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free.\r
\r
IPR Policy, ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2aa7f84d-bf80-4912-8ae0-722dd9b46aff .

camssa:343d87b7-9445-4264-996a-ddf9fdd29708 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Assessments of the efficiency of this asssessment primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. The European Committee for Interoperable Systems wrote a paper in 2016 highlighting how important portability and interoperability is in the cloud computing field. ISO 19941 is mentioned as an example of a cloud solution that vendors can adopt, showing how efficient the specification can be.\r
\r
Special Paper on Cloud Computing - Portability and Interoperability: https://www.ecis.eu/wp-content/uploads/2010/10/ECIS-Special-Paper-on-Cloud-Computing-Portability-and-Interoperability-16-06-27.pdf\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3bc5ea8-b9de-427e-8abf-909f6076e4ba .

camssa:3441b7d1-323d-4a10-8cae-71f4c32a930d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """In accordance with Common Patent Policy for ITU-T/ITU-R/ISO/IEC the ISO 32000-1:2008 is licensed under (F)RAND basis and Royalty-free basis. Although  there are terms included that allow patent holder to apply specific costs. It is defined in IPR disclosures that can be found at ISO's webpage. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.iso.org/iso-standards-and-patents.html\r
https://isotc.iso.org/livelink/livelink/fetch/2000/2122/3770791/16231513/2008-04-20_AdobeSystemsIncorporated_32000-1.pdf?nodeid=17314064&vernum=-2 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4ef8c24-23b9-4e16-b040-e2840b8691bd .

camssa:34421f67-61f5-4fc5-910a-6f9fc92c7b85 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification contains specific requirements regarding the different facets of cloud interoperability and data portability, which can be implemented incrementally or separately, even though it is advisable to implement all of them in order to be aligned with the ISO completely.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b100de4-7a36-43c7-894e-e3004db65efe .

camssa:3444d50d-9ea9-477b-bf0f-4490e83c9ea1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ESPD Data Exchange Model (ESPD-EDM) is designed specifically to enable the integration of the\r
eESPD service into national e-procurement solutions and/or pre-qualification services, therfore, facilitating\r
the modelling of e-procurement business processes in each member state that applies it.\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
European single procurement document and eCertis:\r
https://single-market-economy.ec.europa.eu/single-market/public-procurement/digital-procurement/europeansingle-procurement-document-and-ecertis_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2581d14e-686f-4db4-89bc-131e25bdd296 .

camssa:3449f64a-b5a9-467f-97c6-dbd2fae93cf7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Domibus is open-source and can be used and implemented without any restrictions related to (F)RAND principles. Moreover, it is released under the European Union Public License, which entails Royalty-free IPR policies.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4cba89e-ec9a-403b-aa60-eb4d2f3a0d0b .

camssa:344dc0e0-db1a-4b52-b2ea-7d2d3d5c2b61 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OGC-TrainingDML-AI and some other OGC specifications have been found being implemented in the EO2HEAVEN (Earth Observation and ENVironmental modelling for the mitigation of HEAlth risks) project, moreover, the Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC) works globally, including in Europe, to create and promote geospatial data and technology standards.

OGC Implementations:
https://www.ogc.org/resources/implementations/

Project: EO2HEAVEN (Earth Observation and ENVironmental modelling for the mitigation of HEAlth risks):
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/244100/reporting

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f15e870b-c455-4916-889a-40f117612e6c .

camssa:344e2555-b1f9-483a-8922-9a091e50d92f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3457123b-a698-4ca8-9eb8-6bc391bb7431 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'With the goal of facilitating a seamless audit trail, XBRL GL is designed to provide an unambiguous linkage\r
from underlying events and activities to reporting information and can therefore be used as necessary to\r
increase visibility and provide greater comfort in the trustworthiness of underlying content. The XBRL\r
specification itself is uniquely designed to provide definitions, descriptions and linkages to regulation,\r
practice and guidance for reported data. XBRL GL Profiles, XBRL Formula, and other rules communication\r
languages, such as ISO Schematron (as leveraged by Turkey) provides a means for those responsible for\r
communicating procedures and requirements in a standardized manner, facilitating “data quality at the front\r
door”.\r
\r
https://specifications.xbrl.org/specifications.html\r
\r
https://www.edefter.gov.tr/edeftermevzuat.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1415355d-4278-47f7-80e3-43cd5391b0e2 .

camssa:345ab9b9-3b6f-441f-bf0d-666aa4f7683a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a standard protocol, DNS helps to ensure interoperability when it comes to define processes for setting internet domain names, thus easing interoperability between devices, applications, data repositories, services and networks, this is why, among other reasons, it appears as one of the setting standards for the "Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications eligible for referencing in public procurement"\r
\r
Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications eligible for referencing in public procurement :\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32014D0188'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a1359cc1-d8a0-4f57-b12e-3e36e9d4c26f .

camssa:345ff1c1ee41beeb38f7831271d4d1e090aeaa8bb2e41599bdcf2e6a2d1ef290 a cav:Assessment,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assesses cssvrsc:282fbf529fb851a9da3ed39f48d235c69fd1da93947dfd668889fb8191777920 ;
    cav:considers camssa:66bc951c-4143-446e-abd5-1e87534accac ;
    cav:contextualisedBy sc:44119b394568e5be30da9b83729a3cba1f19eadd53373d5cc6ff6a73fd3e26e8 ;
