camssa:347b5c7b-699c-40c4-bf6d-6605ea51b0f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a protocol which allows the data exchange over the internet, IPv4 contributes to the information and data exchange between administrations. Therefore, avoids the non-digital exchange of data reducing the administrative burden.\r
Additionally, as it is available for free contributes to the reduction of administrative burden."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f19591cd-1d3f-4bc6-afec-6c8124bfa1ca .

camssa:347bcec7-144d-437e-ab3d-0bb8538169ff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:347fc07c-90fe-4246-a17c-cdf53b642087 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification can significantly facilitate the simplification of public administration processes while supporting the digitalisation and modernisation of public services. By establishing a standard for documenting public sector software, it enhances interoperability and encourages reuse among various administrations. This shared framework helps to mitigate administrative complexity, enabling public entities to adopt, adapt, and integrate software more efficiently, thus reducing duplication of efforts and promoting consistency. Consequently, it aids in the seamless delivery of European public services, aligning with the EIF’s objectives for simplification and digital responsiveness.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Italian National Software Catalogue:
https://developers.italia.it/

Open CoDE:
https://opencode.de/en
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8b75c8b-e794-43be-bf13-0cbf32762b7e .

camssa:34836d24-7e0a-4c5f-89b1-d2d5e16a91b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISO 639-2 is not related to the publication of public data as open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ISO 639-2 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/4767.html\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b88d07c-1e0b-4716-9b88-6196c058240e .

camssa:348c8228-7a07-4fcd-9789-5f98ad698df2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-396b6535162f7bba7733ebcc30d2e467321ce07cd8e48b86ab8201acf27031f9 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:349022ed-9c4c-4922-bab0-65a6fd4579a0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-73a8058bec757a2fdb0f8513c2f11841e982cbef76c3be82af67707c294da8b8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:3491ab5b-a4e7-4409-a92d-c82440b464b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI is in continuous development with the primary goal of facilitating and improving interoperability when
exchanging legal documentation among different Member States. Presently, it has already been successfully
implemented by 20 countries, including Finland, Italy, Luxembourg, Norway, Portugal, and Spain, with the
latter fully incorporating the system, while others are in various stages of partial or ongoing implementation.
The ELI documentation includes valuable resources that offer insights into use cases and implementations
by various stakeholders, providing visibility and guidance for those engaging with the framework.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

ELI Testimonials:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/testimonials.html

ELI highlights:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/index.html

ELI Implementation Overview:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/implementation.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05e7d1e9-0382-4961-a94e-72b300a46118 .

camssa:34932ca9-88c2-455b-9dab-f34c784bad99 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:34943aa9-c612-4cfe-a1c1-78aa6f75b105 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IPv6 has a 25% of share in internet-connected network advertise. 49 country report 5% of the traffic through IPv6 and 24 countries exceed the 15%.\r
See:\r
https://www.internetsociety.org/resources/2018/state-of-ipv6-deployment-2018/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2d520d6e-a5c0-4a90-93ba-b12ec9a4d1bf .

camssa:349495c0-fb85-4b64-94c8-04c8903b4e1e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No formal agreement has been found established between organisations or administrations involved in European public service provision including the usage of PDF 1.7. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:921aa5b4-901f-4c50-908d-c153b3353615 .

camssa:3496efaa-f255-4a8f-93ea-94acf372459a a cav:Score,
