    cav:value "1" .

camssa:34c1692b-728f-4c7b-915f-d6c15596eea8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP makes communication between clients and servers better, by establishing the basis for various digital channels, including websites, mobile applications, and APIs. It supports a wide range of content types, such as text, images, audio, and video, enabling public services to deliver diverse forms of digital content effectively.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Semantics, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-routing-http-messages'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:848c65ab-0b94-40dc-b6d3-ad8a088d34b9 .

camssa:34c1ee74-460e-4dc9-b0c8-3eae6394d58f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI TS 119 512, operates under the ETSI Intellectual Property Rigths (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
ETSI ownership of IPRs section: \r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94c85a84-1ec1-4e8d-9b6d-419f15b5bfcd .

camssa:34c6913f-300a-469f-ae3c-3319f3922e9f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:34cee433-b177-4bcf-aca0-edd4db0ac97b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:34d3f5b0-d636-4148-b4d9-bfa9ca47cafb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c431cc9b-a890-4020-a622-c5741e7ce51e .

camssa:34e0e7c2-1fe5-4e47-b8aa-f74c7ebfdd8a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Every new version of the specification goes through a defined process with open and public consultations. Request for comments are not restricted to the RDA members but are open to all."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0457ca93-6071-49e9-94ec-e1ffccbd5d2a .

camssa:34eafd5f-78bc-49ca-8b6a-b8cdf5db5374 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"A Linked Data Event Stream is a collection of immutable objects described in RDF (such as version objects, sensor observations or archived representations). LDES aims to allow clients to replicate the history of a dataset and efficiently synchronise with its latest changes, it improves the public administration's comprehensibility.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7aab757-910a-4b7c-8b79-e8f72e347cd5 .

camssa:34ef07f7-11f7-4760-b54a-e19dc4725149 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The implementation of SMTP does not hamper the scalability and interoperability of systems. For example, SMTP allows to synchronize a Smarthost server which helps to synchronize any number of machines so you don't have to configure SMTP on each machine. The Smarthost server will manage all email accounts.\r
\r
Advantages and disadvantages of an SMTP:\r
https://blog.mailrelay.com/en/2017/04/25/what-is-smtp-advantages-and-disadvantages-of-an-smtp-server """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcb54963-1050-4f7d-a392-1cf379015aec .

