    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3571f5e4-1fd5-48a3-8388-3e0b28bb7ca9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of SMP seems to not be related to fostering the e-accessibility. Moreover, no information regarding this topic has been found to answer positively or negatively to the criterion. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505000"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6969a1ca-f4ac-47b6-adb6-4b95db55524f .

camssa:357342bd-7fd0-4380-8fac-516f4fa40b89 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Most of the public administration services use HTTP Cookies to measure site traffic in order to improve its operation and administration and, with the user's consent, to evaluate the performance of government information campaigns and improve user experience, therefore, we can say that HTTP Cookies enables the exposure of interfaces. \r
\r
French government website: \r
https://www.gouvernement.fr/en/coming-to-france\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#creating_cookies\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5bfc581a-f577-4e92-a5f3-0ab1f312427e .

camssa:357fe506-c64c-4820-a045-20f80068bbc5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'An ebXML RegRep stores any type of electronic content, such as text documents, images, sound or video, and provides a set of protocols enabling data transfer among systems. ebXML is an active asset in the development of The Once-Only Principle Project (TOOP project). Therefore, the specification enables data portability between systems supporting the evolution of European public services.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
TOOP project reference:\r
https://toop.eu/info'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:800a2564-5ae9-4810-a6c8-b5c192b0218d .

camssa:35879774-cb76-4535-90b3-2704c3b7f86c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7dc95fe9-a5b1-4925-ab1a-4cd07a3fcc72 .

camssa:358cdc06-f17a-455b-9f99-2870d909994b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:358d5ad4-7ab4-4773-a4eb-b5a3c5772b95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By allowing communications over the internet, IPv4 contributes to the exchange of information between public administrations. Therefore, it reduces administrative burden.

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58ba9d55-260a-4d65-bf74-1fd4f2d9eb8a .

camssa:358e3230-f1cc-4d41-812b-0d91531cf430 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:358ee6a6-5b3a-4ff4-8c98-4d4c3cb5605a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG does not define a reusable cross-sector data model, but it defines a standardised manner to deal with images while sharing, creating, or editing.\r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:25a5c883-4710-439b-a2b7-904ad2c346e0 .

camssa:35a06d49-62d3-401e-9d8b-429abfd3a4a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of TLS 1.3 specification is to enable a secure and trustworthy exchange of data by providing a set of cryptographic mechanisms and protocols that, when implemented and used correctly, enable a very high degree of security for data exchange over a network.

TLS 1.3 Cryptographic Negotiation Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-4.1.1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51a0fcfd-17cd-48b8-98bb-7f2ad53647a0 .

camssa:35a23558-9ae9-4ffd-a637-c9291f47d295 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 is independent of any specification and can be implemented without any dependency on platforms.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2779e9b3-9993-4e6b-856d-34c49d62691c .

camssa:35aac1a3-159b-427a-81e6-07922fb4f784 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:35aadecc-6d2c-48b2-84d8-e1ec5a884594 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to the publication of data as Linked Open Data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:721acc2b-ef34-4835-ac6e-8646718cbb9e .

camssa:35b305c5-42d3-4c46-928c-90f7794a889e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-396b6535162f7bba7733ebcc30d2e467321ce07cd8e48b86ab8201acf27031f9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:35b52383-1c25-4684-accd-670ed2983cc1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The majority of web browsers and applications are using TLS 1.3 which offers significant security and performance enhancements over TLS 1.2, including a faster handshake, symmetric encryption, which provides both confidentiality and integrity and streamlined cipher suites (a combination of authentication, encryption, and message authentication code algorithms used to negotiate the security settings for a network connection). 

Consequently, it is widely adopted by major corporations: AWS uses it in their Application Load Balancer, Google Cloud supports it since 2020, and Microsoft integrates it into SQL Server 2022 and Windows 11. This adoption reflects TLS 1.3's superior security and efficiency.

At the time of doing this assessment, there is currently a draft from February 2025 pending to review. This draft aims to refine and improve the existing TLS 1.3 standard, ensuring it remains secure, efficient, and interoperable in the long term. 

Google Cloud TLS 1.3 Reference:
https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/networking/tls-1-3-is-now-on-by-default-for-google-cloud-services

Windows TLS 1.3 Support Reference:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sharepoint/security-for-sharepoint-server/tls-support-1.3

AWS Application Load Balancer Reference:
https://aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/application-load-balancer/

TLS 1.3 2025 Draft Reference:
https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-tls-rfc8446bis-12.html

TLS 1.3 2018 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:869a20a3-2b03-4035-bd30-e6b6c54010fa .

camssa:35ba73b0-f9ca-448d-82b8-01b9975474ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XSD 1.1 is not related to guaranteeing the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in data transactions. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5867e20-1b37-46b9-80ed-db7cc3df5cc7 .

camssa:35c2090e-5f07-4ec5-9e6e-6e70a121af09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By making legislation open and accessible in a machine-readable format it fosters the creation and delivery of new public services. Moreover, it establishes a standardised terminology to ensure that when legal text or information is translated the nature of the document is not harmed nor modified. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
Study on how users of legislation access transposition information:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/ELI_usability_study_results-final.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6df05962-8d38-4edf-97a2-7634268241e6 .

camssa:35c36519-c10e-4fa7-a102-8b9ed7623435 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no such assessment addressing the efficiency of the specification. This might be due to the early-stage development of the specification.\r
\r
Besides, the ARIA initiative proposes tools and methods to evaluate e-accessibility. In this sense, in the future there might exist such reports.\r
\r
WAI-ARIA github, issue tracking:\r
https://github.com/w3c/aria-practices/issues/\r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59d7973e-9c94-4008-9533-0e2834ddf0c6 .

camssa:35c3ce2a-1878-4f57-adb4-15f4b52a8ecf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There exists assessments addressing the efficiency of the DCAT specification.\r
\r
Referenced Article: \r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1570826818300532'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b30db651-3283-4cfb-9233-4b3639e3610f .

