camssa:36671bef-bf99-49af-bc1f-24ad98e91b12 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CSIP addresses the implementation of authenticity features within information packages. It provides guidance on the documentation of relevant metadata to ensure the authenticity and trustworthiness of digital information.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5fa088c8-fa87-420b-8dae-808513254de2 .

camssa:3667e188-e9e7-48c9-bd91-899ba6b11079 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Modelling data with RDF-based vocabularies is known to enhance digital public services.  An example would be the Core Public Service Vocabulary (CPSV) which is a data model describing public services aiming to enhance interoperability between systems and therefore simplifying the delivery of public services.\r
\r
Core Public Service Vocabulary:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary\r
\r
RDF Description services:\r
https://www.w3.org/1999/11/02-RDFServices/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:241f8a66-1294-4249-90f1-ab8895d59790 .

camssa:366aa7f3-48b4-4afd-ac19-b8a4fa80422c a cav:Score,
