camssa:36dbd15c-2dd8-4cf1-96f1-cc77f980d985 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Better Regulation Toolbox is an internal European Commission resource designed as a complement to the Commission's Better regulation guideline. It provides more specific and operational guidance to those involved with different elements regarding EU legislation, not being possible to be modified but adopted in a manner that aligns with the constraints and needs of the local context.. 

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec7f77d5-66b8-4457-92a4-0efc71fcac6d .

camssa:36e95e8a-69b7-4d1a-8f96-81f4d33b20e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification type system defines a set of commonly used types for interoperable data representation. This ensures that data is exchanged in a consistent format, regardless of the underlying system.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a890ec9-139e-4a82-b346-39337b07ce5c .

camssa:36e9a742-cb34-4c22-b916-5645506c14e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'All OpenTelemetry Specification contributions will be licensed under its Apache 2.0 License. It is a permissive license whose main conditions require preservation of copyright and license notices. Contributors provide an express grant of patent rights. Licensed works, modifications, and larger works may be distributed under different terms and without source code.

OpenTelemetry License: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/LICENSE'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7532871d-14de-43be-a5c8-24e1c985b263 .

camssa:36ee04b0-d53c-4780-9d89-7079361176ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/\r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1daa1127-fa9c-40c8-b677-740d0bd788d8 .

camssa:36f4a987-40b8-4557-ba01-249922db2d04 a cav:Score,
