camssa:37be8cbf-2c17-465d-be82-50acfc0b93d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ISO 3166-1 can enable scope the comprehensibility of administrations when combined with other specifications, notably when referencing to public services' data models and recommendations (see EU Vocabularies reference, Authority tables section). The Core Person Vocabulary recommendation of the Semantic Interoperability Community (Semic) is a clear example of spatial data understanding at European level, as in combination with ISO 3166-1 a person or organisation's identity can be traced in detail.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html\r
\r
EU Vocabularies reference, Authority tables section:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/authority-tables\r
\r
EU Seminc Github reference, Core Person Vocabulary, Location section:\r
https://semiceu.github.io/Core-Person-Vocabulary/releases/2.00/?msclkid=7f4a3d0ca9ca11ec99845e3a63e37998#Location\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a384e590-8f86-45e5-bbfa-65db804fda7d .

camssa:37bef870-8604-4c77-8690-168b07c244b5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1624157830122d60825aa5aa88ab70d0b140b2e7e510086699f9a9773efef6bd ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:37c09407-03ed-4bf0-a6c9-eafe57b0483e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODF is a business agnostic document format that can be reused in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3003f570-ce53-4bf9-9ea4-4d84193409e7 .

camssa:37c27460-02ee-4dbb-8ec3-f433e0d7ed80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Extensible Forms Description Language is an extension of XML and does not rely on any specific technology. Therefore, it is technology agnostic.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a13ae310-2ef3-4a1a-8d77-87a7ebc9744a .

camssa:37c40096-d3b1-4231-a069-5694f6db8361 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17bea234285e6e633e4e21105358610ad5f5f0eaaf82f4bd50cb64ec11538984 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:37c6e9e1-c2fd-428f-929f-a5d74d3c8c16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There can be found many articles and research papers addressing e-procurement and assessing the efficiency and effectiveness of the ESPD in the context of the digilalisation of e-procurement process. A sample of these assessments can be accessed below:\r
\r
Improving Electronic Public Procurement Using the Once-Only Principle: Connecting the Greek Electronic\r
Single Procurement Document System to the Once-Only Principle Project's Infrastructure, Implementing the\r
eProcurement Pilot:\r
https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3494193.3494226\r
\r
Employing the Once-Only Principle in the Domain of the Electronic Public Procurement:\r
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-44322-1_18\r
\r
E-Procurement in the European Union:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sebastian-Bobowski/publication/329322569_EProcurement_\r
in_the_European_Union/links/5c86d5d392851c831973a589/E-Procurement-in-the-European-\r
Union.pdf\r
\r
Accelerating Transparency and Efficiency in the Public Procurement Sector for a Smarter Society:\r
eNotification and ESPD Integration for Developing E-procurement:\r
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-19-3112-3_25\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:097249d1-669e-499e-9426-2978b9fab53c .

camssa:37c88adc-1dfa-4ac7-8c61-0306f7d681e9 a cav:Score,
