camssa:383998a2-9f60-4890-8a7b-3ae382b8b7d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is the basis for the creation of digital public services, and it provides the common and basic components for it, but any Solution Architecture Template or Solution can extend them to ensure that their needs are covered. The Interoperability Architecture Solutions Validator can help to ensure that extensions are aligned with modelling guidelines and requirements of EIRA. Examples of extensions of EIRA are any of the eGovERAs, from the Business Agnostic to the Domain Specific. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c5b08341-5cbd-4a21-823f-5c342f4e39b8 .

camssa:383f15f6-806b-46df-858d-ee6fb617dc06 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:38448fb4-e2b8-4740-8931-d8d46bbe475d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SOAP 1.2 is not related to the  delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b9a013b-8cd5-4792-8cec-92dfd608e415 .

camssa:3846b8f9-35bd-4e30-b39f-8b5feb753cb9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification does provide an access control mechanism for the credentials. A credential's repository is a program, such as a storage vault or personal verifiable credential wallet, that stores and protects access to holders' verifiable credentials. This helps minimize the risk of exposing unnecessary information, reducing the potential impact of unauthorized changes or disclosures.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/ \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d880fc2-d788-4fc8-89bb-ffbd51c21c5c .

camssa:38478d46-622c-47e5-b966-1b3d0ad9b6dc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ESPD Github repository hosts all feedback given by stakeholders. As it is stated in the ESPD release\r
notes, changes and updates of the specification are carried out following Member States and stakeholders\r
comments in the Github repository issues workspace.\r
\r
ESPD Issues in Github:\r
https://github.com/OP-TED/ESPD-EDM/issues\r
\r
ESPD release notes:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/release_notes.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3b56f5c-8228-4dc1-8632-8bdc0b16da35 .

camssa:384ab72b-00ef-4b46-8fba-c21a2573ea3b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec is a set of open standards and protocols for securing the exchange of data packets over a computer network, including data confidentiality, integrity, origin authentication and anti-replay. However, there is no specific provision to this end.\r
\r
IPSec reference, Where Can IPSec Be Implemented:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-11'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7d728d4-6600-41e3-968a-4405a9613025 .

camssa:384b8a18-cebd-4b28-b6b6-0cb9f40e7562 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification enable the processing of data but not its security. To cover security aspects or issues, it is possible to enable external mechanisms like encryption or implementing security mechanisms on the systems processing the YAML data. 

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6905f043-5ffb-4a3b-87b6-a3fdb693ba21 .

camssa:384d0629-3449-497a-8ae7-c8f68bceefb8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:38512a2b-97a3-45af-bb79-8bfddbc6db03 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:38537bdd-3a9f-4ba9-a9a7-b5e98a7e4403 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog has published documentation regarding change management (section 6.3.4) and release management following the IETF internet standards process. The process of creating a standard under IETF is clear: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience are taken place. Furthermore, The IETF welcomes the critical evaluation of protocols and has provided guidance for it. 

Syslog Protocol Change Control: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424#section-6.3.4

Standard process IETF: https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Protocol Vulnerabilities IETF: https://www.ietf.org/standards/rfcs/vulnerabilities/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7102c199-ec8f-46dd-b6d6-6de87ca991c5 .

camssa:3854da72-0f5e-4eab-8b69-0449c4ee5274 a cav:Score,
