camssa:38a5d127-1773-42ac-bdac-485efac3675d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Extensible Forms Description Language specification can enable e-accessibility by its XML structure. In this context, the specification allows to structure data in a consistent, predictable way that can be easily interpreted and processed.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bc3ce9b-e15c-4187-b3f7-52abd2a8f4a8 .

camssa:38b03a39-3afc-4fbf-8608-e5c5c848b39a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Domibus can be integrated into the flow of business processes where secure communication and data exchange are required. Moreover, Domibus can perform data transformation as part of the message exchange process. It can help ensure that data exchanged between systems aligns with the requirements of the business processes involved.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb2cbca0-8917-4c6d-9a3f-0005872f1e1c .

camssa:38b0fda1-1bf6-45d2-9c20-5120d24a17cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39e7870e79b2999a8b61c97f0c356312b88174320d6464fce5639e57ec0de011 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:38b1d43a-a340-4a99-bd47-50c8b0f4bcd9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) develops solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks.\r
\r
Specification development process by the ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications\r
\r
Detailed document ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42f9438c-7389-4d74-9ba3-eece831d8823 .

camssa:38b2d2b0-4a52-4a5b-9bb1-76f0bc5d9345 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP has not been found included in any European or national initiative covering privacy aspects.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:454728f0-c73e-4783-be14-43bd4b8117eb .

camssa:38b8967a-2824-4798-a036-5df1699149fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ccd72cb1-d901-4b93-b834-38bad1ea099b .

camssa:38bdb0e3-8713-48bd-a440-5985414381eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Publiccode.yml is included in the Italian repository for public documents, which includes standards and specifications. The repository in not explicitly dedicated to standards and specifications, but was created to be a reference. Therefore, this can be considered and official and feasible source. Moreover, the specification has serve as the basis for the creation of the Italian Catalogue of Software. 

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a303b79a-b7cc-4cbf-8a10-7061f806c04c .

