camssa:38c2ad80-1e66-484e-a93f-09f476f6971e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This document does not define a cross-sector reusable data model, but it defines a Best Practices on how to publish data on the web.\r
\r
W3C Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae5642b7-fe45-47d5-8d26-ac4655cfaa1f .

camssa:38c7b39a-700a-4302-9ae4-45df2d5c5ce0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPsec is not related to  e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
IPSec reference, What IPSec Does:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-7'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0e04963-e673-470a-b707-7ce04f9b1387 .

camssa:38c8124f-f8f5-4147-86ca-a65974fbfc72 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:38cd54f4-c1e3-4cb3-9f4f-6ac32c74e681 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Enryption Standard allows implementations to support at least one of the three key lengths, established by the standard guide. A "key length" refers to the size of the cryptographic key used to encrypt and decrypt data, measured in bits. In this context, the standard allows optional support for two or three key lengths, but it's not required to support all three.

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfbf8fe3-6cf0-44e0-b2d6-6fe7077bca85 .

camssa:38d673bb-95d9-4702-860a-9c4d5ef8b292 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This Core Vocabulary Application Profile offers the possibility of describing public services in a standarised way easing their reuse and discoverability. It can be translated  into Federated Catalogues of Public Services that can be accessed across-borders. As the "Evaluation Study supporting the interim evaluation of the programme on interoperability solutions for European public administrations, businesses and citizens (ISA²)" states, there are several MS like Italy or Finland that are using CPSV-AP to create Public Services Catalogues.\r
\r
JoinUp Webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/\r
\r
Evaluation Study supporting the interim evaluation of the programme on interoperability solutions for European public administrations, businesses and citizens (ISA²): \r
https://www.ceps.eu/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/NO0119341ENN.en_.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa205bf8-431f-43e2-b47d-f55c33be1f6c .

camssa:38dc0659-de64-49f3-ad95-f8d572a37dbd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No evidences have been found of existing studies or documentation assessing HTTP Cookies in terms of effectiveness to justify this criterion.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f206eb27-6555-4cbe-adb8-d440661185d3 .

camssa:38e138d4-267b-4ea3-8506-19ff2f6c8830 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Transformational Government Framework (TGF) is technology-agnostic, meaning it does not promote nor endorse any specific technology or vendor solution. Instead, it provides guidance and best practices for the design and delivery of government services using open standards and interoperability principles.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f343a0b-0793-439a-9e23-3b87539d86e0 .

camssa:38e38d37-e252-4881-a796-beb98e89f7da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP, as a cross-border and cross-sector vocabulary increases government-to-government reuse of data and therefore can prevent citizens or businesses from providing standard information several times. Like all common vocabularies, DCAT-AP facilitates the implementation of the once-only principle. \r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/dcat-ap-key-european-data-publishers-reach-data-consumers-and-create-european-open-data-ecosystem_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a661845-300a-4645-aa41-7c1e86a1e412 .

camssa:38e8b5cc-a9ab-423e-af4b-1e295893cdfe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:38eab310-b7f7-4c5f-8c21-40b7e44cfda4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SHACL can describe the interoperability aspects of the Data Validation Service or Data Validation Component ABBs from EIRA's Technical View."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5eb068ff-26d5-472d-8357-1642bb4d9f19 .

