camssa:39396932-6446-458d-8258-c4f03b2831d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XML is to store, transport and  exchange data through interoperable systems. Moreover, XML defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a human-readable format and machine-readable format enhancing the reusability of data and stimulating the interoperability of systems and services.  \r
\r
Additionally, W3C develops its specification independently from any vendor. Thus, the adoption of XML does not hamper the data portability of data expressed with it. In fact, the adoption of XML fosters data portability, especially between REST APIs.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d243b47e-f823-4aac-8ae7-b60fef422713 .

camssa:39455a90-eb2d-4947-a261-43b6c554a124 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-58010a47630ff9ea23336bf3fc558deff59905e0292551fcabc95740082cb378 ;
    cav:value "1" .

