camssa:3970dc66-bbb9-406d-9176-222407c1f3b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The standard for Public Code gives public organizations a model for building their open source solutions to enable successful future reuse by similar public organizations in other places. The open-source for public code can, therefore, be considered as an asset in the creation of innovative solutions. The reusability and capacity to adapt and develop in such different ways ensure its reusability improving the effectiveness and efficiency. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b103e9f1-e3b8-45c9-b587-a939eaf01d0d .

camssa:39714bde-e66b-4c08-ad04-d1812615a269 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although at the moment of elaborating the assessment, the specification is widely used, the specification in itself does not foster the creation of innovative solutions. \r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6db4cf89-1a64-409a-a72a-357852f9eb71 .

camssa:397384b5-f002-42f5-a162-a7db4dbf6b1e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is intended to identify a country, dependencies and special areas of geographical interest. There is no possibility to extend the coding system as ISO 3166-1 was conceived for a unique purpose.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:803a70b9-8b0f-4967-a764-6b15b010f6d7 .

