camssa:398b75ed-5901-4c07-af92-83f5ce30bccf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Access to the Indexed Database API is controlled by the browser's security mechanisms. For example, scripts can only access the Indexed Database API if they are from the same origin/domain. This prevents unauthorised cross-origin access to the stored data.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d50bafa4-9a41-4bae-9c26-4bd4f443d925 .

camssa:398c1f37-bc9a-4ab1-8ba1-88cc70a47c6d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3991de48-7d93-4374-a58d-c67ad6fb2510 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Genericode, being a flexible and modular standard, allows for partial implementations based on specific use cases and requirements. Its modular structure allows developers to implement only the components that are necessary for their particular use case. For example, if an application only needs to represent simple code lists without metadata, it can choose to implement only the core elements of Genericode without incorporating metadata-related features.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:856313e1-30d0-4bfa-b5e3-3cf28fe8b435 .

camssa:399863a8-7053-4e27-833e-7b176e8a1258 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is used by XML Gate, the EU DG SANCO single entry point for Member States submissions of structured data in XML format via web services. \r
\r
See:\r
https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/sanco-xmlgate/Login.jsp"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:97165dfe-fdd3-42aa-a3ce-19ba579b3429 .

camssa:3999caef-46f5-4334-b012-13f6dffd5732 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a88757c-3b21-4e4a-b7da-4f8886a27522 .

camssa:399c7db1-c947-4d62-8afd-e241dc43f866 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has a section dedicated to conformance. Conformance requirements are expressed with a combination of descriptive assertions and RFC 2119 terminology. The key words “MUST”, “MUST NOT”, “REQUIRED”, “SHALL”, “SHALL NOT”, “SHOULD”, “SHOULD NOT”, “RECOMMENDED”, “MAY”, and “OPTIONAL” in the normative parts of this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119. However, for readability, these words do not appear in all uppercase letters in this specification. Furthermore, Interoperability Test Bed (ITB) can also be used to test LDES.

LDES GitHub: 
https://semiceu.github.io/LinkedDataEventStreams/#conformance

RFC 2119: 
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2119

ITB LDES: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/news/itb-support-digital-flanders'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04a047b6-866b-4637-ab3b-280e83735449 .

camssa:399d5876-cf45-4d73-9a7a-10c8f9eae4e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, LDAPv3 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a5e8bf6-a638-4d7e-9037-3e90615185c4 .

camssa:39ab8254-8df8-4a41-8ead-cfb960698d2a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including ADMS.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0fedd705-bde6-426d-9fcd-84ff7dda8436 .

camssa:39ac5650-7f3e-4f27-a5f5-c044e2f3a439 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAML 2.0 is available for its study and use at OASIS’s webpage. Therefore it can be reused by the organisations, administrations, open communities, etc. that developed it.\r
\r
See:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0980ce47-25e4-45ef-b621-5530782592ff .

camssa:39b019c9-c77e-42f7-b6d9-7efbce89d9ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UTF-8 is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications, concretely of the Netherlands and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e6490ab2-e709-4d08-8be5-99bd6c12879b .

