        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) was defined in 2001 and is a cryptographic protocol for certifying timestamps using X.509 certificates and public key infrastructure. Therefore, it is demonstrated that TSP has enough maturity for its use in the development of products and services.\r
