        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of genericode is not related to providing means for restriction of access to data. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:80960817-8d98-467f-9b50-9b77c002a1ba .

camssa:3af46121-bd30-41cf-adcd-240f17b10863 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although no formal agreements have been found on the usage of TIFF, there are different projects and initiatives at European level, that use TIFF files for the data exchange. Some examples of Agencies and projects involving the specification are the European Environment Agency and its Evaluation map of Europe, which is available on TIFF format. Also, the initiative founded by the European Commission, OpenAire, which is aimed to foster cooperation among researchers over Europe and the discoverability of their data. This initiative defines guidelines for data management in the context of H2020 Programme: Guidelines on FAIR Data Management in Horizon 2020.\r
\r
OpenAire Preservation Guidelines:\r
https://www.openaire.eu/data-formats-preservation-guide\r
\r
Elevation Map of Europe:\r
https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/data/digital-elevation-model-of-europe\r
\r
Digital Elevation Model over Europe:\r
https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/data/eu-dem"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1429f827-fbfa-4fa8-a9b5-0972e9a8e4d5 .

