camssa:3afe97b2-3369-4cb3-85f5-6153e39475c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Web Services Description Language (WSDL) itself primarily focuses on describing the interfaces and operations of web services, and it does not provide specific mechanisms for ensuring the secure processing of data. Security considerations, including secure processing, are typically addressed at other layers of the web services architecture and are influenced by the implementation choices made by service providers and consumers. \r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5da3934c-0c53-40d4-86cf-688548846bb5 .

camssa:3b014fa9-2184-41da-9a3d-6751423a646f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The syslog protocol encourages collaboration in the field of message logging as it was created by IETF, a non-profit and open organisation dedicated to standardisation. IETF encourages collaborative efforts that extend beyond the specifications themselves and include discussions, forums, and knowledge-sharing platforms where users can exchange ideas, experiences, and best practices related to syslog. For instance, IETF has created discussions lists for their specifications that improve the development and specification of Internet technology through the general discussion of technical, procedural, operational, and other topics for which no dedicated mailing lists exist. 

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5478d453-08d1-4364-a84b-4e727b761b78 .

camssa:3b0318e1-e172-4966-914c-e53e72c67300 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:3b0adfd2-8fe8-43f7-9b2c-d0fc490ef490 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OGC Training DML-AI has been found included in the 2024 ICT Rolling Plan standards catalogue. More specifically in the Smart and sustainable cities and communitiessection, where it appears as one of the  geospatial standards underpinning the INSPIRE (Infrastructure for Spatial Information in the European Community) directive and CityGML, an international standard for spatial data exchange.

ICT Rolling plan 2024: Smart sustainable cities and communities:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/smart-and-sustainable-cities-and-communities-rp2024'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b82fdc01-a29e-4fa6-8991-27e78d7ee4dc .

camssa:3b0f1663-aae2-4db1-8e1b-227f7967602c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPv4 is included in 2 national catalogues, which belong to Member States which comply with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the EIF according to the NIFO factsheets. These two Member States are the Netherlands and Sweden. \r
\r
See:                                                                                                                                               \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets      """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9787be10-2784-4b84-801f-2375e12ecc28 .

