camssa:3b57477a-3000-4527-bdb3-ca35eb5647f1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'It could serve as a valuable facilitator of European organizational agreements regarding geospatial data by
providing a common framework for data management and exchange. This support can help reduce barriers
to interoperability and promote collaboration among entities involved in geospatial data processing.
Additionally, integrating machine learning capabilities within this framework could further enhance data
analysis, decision-making, and innovation in geospatial applications across Europe.

OGC TrainingDML-AI:
https://www.ogc.org/standard/trainingdml-ai/

OGC TrainingDML-AI Implementations:
https://github.com/opengeospatial/TrainingDML-AI_SWG/tree/main/Implementations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a24acb4-8e3a-4f78-b02f-290d47578c3e .

camssa:3b63f412-64f0-48b0-9811-615109d73194 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary specification provides classes to describe elements, such as geometries, which can be understable by different languages. In this sense, this vocabulary describes other information, such as administratives territorial units, or  times, whih are defined in codes and numbers, making them understable in any language.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58a646fe-1ea2-4e54-ae9a-a7481da4d41b .

