camssa:3badc716-3a9c-4127-825a-245d809756fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS is a vocabulary based on DCAT for the description of Assets, specifically interoperability solutions). In this sense, the ADMS helps the publication and reusability of solutions and their data.\r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:508ef958-88a8-4980-9ef1-634f0a663801 .

camssa:3baecba7-2d01-4f76-bb00-109d754e307c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog itself is not designed for the purpose of facilitating the publication of data on the web. Syslog is a standard protocol used for the collection and forwarding of log messages from various devices, applications, 
and systems in a network. It is commonly used for system management and security auditing.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a76d1dd3-9725-492f-9679-7c497998b1c0 .

