camssa:3bdad4c7-4514-4e5a-817a-b2e9e16181f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI allow publishers to restrict access to logs. It is possible to enable the WebSphere Application Server to obtain more security, especially in the areas of data authorization and confidentiality in a UDDI registry. Using WebSphere Application Server, UDDI can classify users into two groups: one in which all users have access and another in which only users authenticated to WebSphere Application Server have access. On the other hand, at UDDI it is also possible to register privately.

IBM security reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was/8.5.5?topic=curs-configuring-uddi-registry-use-websphere-application-server-security'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2225caf7-6514-46bf-9d26-547c84a5ee36 .

camssa:3be207c5-fffd-4f19-a5f9-00b33c384649 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The widespread adoption and use of the ESPD in public procurement processes, along with its integration\r
into e-procurement platforms and tools, suggests that it has sufficient market acceptance for its use in the\r
development of digital solutions. Moreover, The use of the ESPD has been mandated by the EU for all\r
public procurement procedures since 2018, which has helped to increase its adoption and acceptance in the\r
market. In addition, the ESPD has been integrated into several e-procurement platforms and tools, which\r
demonstrates its suitability for use in digital solutions.\r
\r
ESPD Business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7de01dcf-7f90-4edf-b33f-df40e130cfd7 .

