    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3d1a65e7-dc5b-4069-b399-c655eb1585e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification mentions in section 5.3.3 that cloud services employ an identity and access management system to control access to the interfaces offered by a cloud service and also to control access to resources inside a cloud service. The authentication of the role agents involved in the data transactions is likely to be in the hands of the Cloud Service Provider (CSP).\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:61ec990f-f35f-47f4-86d5-5ff598f89dfd .

camssa:3d1cd831-25bc-4905-a9eb-3f414f7e33ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is designed to plug directly into existing business, accounting, legal, auditing, and records management practices, eliminating the re-keying of data required by traditional fax, scanned-image and paper-based supply chains and in doing so provides an entry point into electronic business for small and medium-sized businesses.  Therefore UBL actively supports comprehensibility as is the case of the ESPD project.\r
\r
Developer community OASIS. UBL functionalities:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ubl#functionality\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
ESPD reference, Legal framework and context section:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_business_handbook.html#_i_1_1_legal_framework_and_context'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ccba2207-d1d7-4931-b6b0-523763e668b8 .

