camssa:3d471b88-c73e-448a-8cc6-802235abf0e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI allows to publish data in a public registry and can be useful for other people who is looking for solutions. However, UDDI is not intended for data exchange and does not provide many mechanisms to ensure a secure and correct exchange of data. Therefore, data exchange is possible, and there are some mechanisms to guarantee security, but it is not its main purpose.

UDDI OASIS reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/standard/uddi/

IBM  security reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was/8.5.5?topic=curs-configuring-uddi-registry-use-websphere-application-server-security'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a592098-70d9-4d42-8d4d-04bf49c3b5f6 .

camssa:3d50ef29-2ca0-4294-b823-702ae1f6fd80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion \r
of ISAE 3402 within any European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4773543-c5f0-49f3-8b2e-478ce304addc .

camssa:3d551056-0782-49f9-bd74-470fc6839809 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By focusing on citizen-centric service design and delivery, and leveraging digital channels and technologies, the TGF aims to improve the visibility and accessibility of administrative procedures and services, and to enhance the overall user experience for citizens and businesses.  An example of it is the promotion of the health profile.\r
\r
TGF Specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html\r
\r
TGF health profile:\r
https://lists.oasis-open.org/archives/tgf-comment/201406/msg00001.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:49ae01d5-884f-4cc0-a863-85388dc83161 .

camssa:3d564ddc-d9bf-46e0-acfd-5fe15c2ed393 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, HTTP Cookies is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. HTTPS is therefore available with any restrictions related to (F)RAND.  \r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bea3dfc-2b38-4b73-a219-3ef56e847f13 .

camssa:3d601324-e18b-48e8-aa53-2fe8e31933a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'[TO BE CHECKED] The specification is intended solely for documenting metadata related to public code projects and does not aim to support or regulate secure data exchange. It lacks provisions for security or privacy frameworks and does not establish protocols for handling sensitive data or ensuring secure communications. Therefore, its scope does not align with the data exchange security and privacy requirements outlined in EIF Recommendation 15.
Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cedc0e27-bfd0-42d6-9471-ffe8701b342d .

camssa:3d61f75e-443c-4dd2-a69e-a99b7e1e89f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bfac99f-4a58-4e29-9379-db18c783601c .

camssa:3d645417-eae5-44ef-bbe5-eee6fa62662b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0c9dd43038136296b52f50e05f9d6eef39f7b8018517224007990b15be2eb19e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:3d69cb22-4920-4a46-9c02-95d12c95e98f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XACML is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the 
specification.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a521f81c-8f38-4c36-aaf8-8f79b4146625 .

camssa:3d6a4edf-cd9c-4211-b43d-17ca718a682d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT is recommended by the Netherlands and Spain within their national catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst \r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:9e2c2877-5103-4934-8440-c60ba2e10c48/Catalogue_of_Standards_NIF_Spain.pdf \r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9755c11-26dc-4b80-9618-334100b5ea53 .

camssa:3d6c8238-4996-46dc-a174-7c2dc27d5c46 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear Technical Committee (hereby TC) process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process.\r
\r
OASIS guideline:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa4938fa-3db4-45f0-b2f3-a5e357761e59 .

camssa:3d6da601-9920-4aa1-9865-46c9c97a0af3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP cookies is the most widely used standard protocol serving essential functions on the web such as storing stateful information on the user's device or tracking the user's browsing activity. For example, the Google Analytics JavaScript libraries use HTTP cookies to "remember" what a user has done on previous pages and interactions with the website.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265\r
\r
Google Analytics reference:\r
https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/analyticsjs/cookie-usage?hl=es#analyticsjs'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37598dc2-24d5-4510-a93f-ac1df5ceb7d6 .

camssa:3d73de31-a5e0-443e-9b77-6a79d7d1cda1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG is an international standard worldwide used as an image format. It is supported as a standard way for the treatment and exchange of image files.\r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7405df9e-8c3d-4b28-990b-e5bdf397a9cd .

camssa:3d75890b-8a6e-4426-9195-1cc061482144 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'iCalendar enables the sharing and exchange of scheduling and event information between different systems and applications. This reusability ensures that calendar-related data can be easily imported, exported, and integrated into various software, promoting interoperability and reducing the need for data duplication or manual data entry. As a result, relevant information can be efficiently reused when needed, streamlining processes and enhancing data consistency across different platforms and services.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7f2ef4d-61cb-4d44-9002-8c3599e377f4 .

camssa:3d78370d-221a-4ded-9535-ee8b09bc684f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
