camssa:3dc56857-3a84-4488-8b10-94d7c875cb99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the description of the specification states, the Core Location Vocabulary is an extensible data model. In this context, the specification can be extended to achieve new functionalities, such as validating data with the SHACL shapes validator.

SHACL shapes validator:
https://semiceu.github.io/Core-Location-Vocabulary/releases/2.1.0/shacl/core-location-ap-SHACL.ttl

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:56716059-b979-4976-9c2e-d469af99163c .

camssa:3dcb28b9-5de0-4f18-b108-69c0983b7f6d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA specification allows for extension. Developers can extend the set of roles, states, and properties defined by WAI-ARIA to accommodate specific needs in their web applications.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87180812-d57a-4bd0-9451-ffbf5f1a199a .

camssa:3dcd48c8-f9e3-48c8-a3a2-01ef5307699b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UTF-8 is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, UTF-8 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data" ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46ae596b-691c-4a35-a5d4-512c8103fa63 .

