camssa:3e271d3c-a6e1-46bf-ac6f-b424dfae2c47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 does not directly facilitate the publication of data on the web, but it contributes to the broader goal of providing a common conceptual framework for the development and understanding of network protocols and communication systems.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe06cf14-5a05-42f2-9944-d8df01758fd3 .

camssa:3e2e1c29-8ca6-42f0-9f09-669c24e4ed04 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification includes several authenticity considerations. In this context, although the specification does not implement TLS, it recommends it. In this sense, only pages using TLS with certificates that identify them as being from the same domain can access their respective databases. As a result, unauthorized pages cannot access these databases and are thus protected.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7a09792-a8d2-4686-9b8d-b1b692ceb2c0 .

camssa:3e2eb89d-f282-40b8-a04a-cb95f9225468 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:3e328e20-8dad-4662-a823-e8d89f8dcd4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The European Union (EU) Member States are currently implementing the INSPIRE Directive and related regulations, included in the ISA programme. This projects includes the usage of XSLT included in a catalogue of standards at EU level too.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ies-svn.jrc.ec.europa.eu/projects/registry-development/wiki/Re3gistry_1_0_documentation#_cp3"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d645417-eae5-44ef-bbe5-eee6fa62662b .

camssa:3e331eb9-2de2-4477-a1a3-ad1fde959971 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ISO/IEC 7498:1 primarily focuses on providing a conceptual framework for network communication. It does not explicitly address the exposure of interfaces to access public administration's services. The OSI model is more concerned with the abstraction of functions into layers to facilitate interoperability and communication between different systems.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd338812-8c89-47d8-bb74-1f0b6e593362 .

camssa:3e3c5403-2f29-430f-991f-b1080c462508 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification makes use of optional classes that allow it to be more flexible towards the purpose it is working for. An example can be the Participation class that allows to define roles within a certain context.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b87aa1c4-2056-4565-a219-0e9d76b07b0d .

camssa:3e3ce58d-7599-4fd3-9e8b-057537d267fb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """9 Member States are recommending PNG in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are Croatia, Estonia, France, Germany, Greece, Norway, Poland, Spain and Sweden.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e242fd2-8ce6-4ac2-afb0-0100a36583e1 .

camssa:3e3d519a-8e0b-4853-94e5-513e822e0b81 a cav:Score,
