camssa:405be78f-a313-4280-8aa1-e0a7a7e1def8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Conformance to HTTP implementation means it is correctly mapped and aligned with the vocabularies it
defines. HTTP can define conformance requirements relying on manual methods and general guidelines for assessing conformance by the usage of the keywords:  "MUST," "SHOULD," and "MAY". Httplint is an online tool that performs various checks on HTTP/1.1 headers returned by a server. It checks the syntax and content of almost all HTTP/1.1 response headers, and also warns about missing headers and suggests improvements.

HTTP Lint:
http://zamez.org/httplint

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Semantics, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc291eb1-649e-4c24-93ec-b0bb6be6dcf4 .

camssa:405c3bcc-382d-461e-a94d-c5f72fbbf51e a cav:Score,
