camssa:406532a4-8a1e-464e-8daa-93f0734db533 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the second star corresponds to make data available as structured data, an area of application of SOAP 1.2.\r
\r
In addition, SOAP 1.2 serialisation provides several advantages, especially if the Semantic Web is not just about providing metadata for existing web pages, but also about exchange of content that is machine-readable.  \r
\r
See:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/dbf2/6496e5b3087b708d4c00883c6470b53ff8d8.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa421656-c5fa-404e-8a78-21e504a75a92 .

