camssa:40a8a120-93ef-4fd1-a301-2930a7193c80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CAdES is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e7bcb32-2fd1-4777-bc0c-1862ebe3251c .

camssa:40b9552c-bbab-4f1c-a82e-521a6e18ccaa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the main purpose of the specifications is not the preservation of information it can be used in the context of eArchiving. An example of this aim is DCAT and DCAT-AP, data catalogues vocabularies built around RDF and which are used with the purpose of describing datasets included in data catalogues. The enrichment by means of metadata according to RDF schema could help to the long term preservation of digital documents.\r
\r
DCAT specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e03a6c7c-e0b2-40f7-9847-dfcbdadeb8b0 .

camssa:40c354db-0718-4186-814c-3e548f812bf8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:40c484e3-c765-4a8a-b551-e1b5a0f51fca a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:40c890e9-bfd3-4dd8-a38c-e677e64a46c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "DNS does not hamper the scalability of the systems implementing it. In fact, by allowing the association of a name to a domain, the maintenance and identification of domains is facilitated."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:707891a2-bf7f-425e-9bd7-6d28086e29e7 .

camssa:40ca87ac-3882-4e8e-8e78-4e33b879e457 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SMTP is publicly available for implementation and use, and therefore for everyone to study, for free on IETF webpage.\r
\r
SMTP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5321"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f8350d01-0047-4e6c-8ad9-1bc8757dc24b .

camssa:40d29e4e-27c7-4e04-adfb-c48e6457dfda a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI.org, which is now associated with OASIS, is comprised of more than 200 major software developers and e-business leaders. Since 2000, UDDI has released three versions for different main purposes. Moreover, the specification is in constant development by its community, and there is documentation available in uddi.org. Therefore, it is demonstrated that UDDI has enough maturity for its use in the development of digital solutions and services.

UDDI OASIS reference:
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/uddi_v3.htm#_Toc85907974

UDDI evolution reference: 
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/the_evolution_of_uddi_20020719.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04c6cbec-9b19-41e6-968b-a48c47aeb680 .

camssa:40d47ba3-81db-4ff1-95a8-20b97ae332ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XAdES is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e5d7ec3-bb2e-4de9-965c-23bd95615126 .

camssa:40d7c213-0872-4126-b77b-d15d27b3b79a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are no Member States recommending Standard for Public Code in their ICT National Catalogues.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fb4c4bb7-c737-411f-a7cc-56e48420d1fc .

camssa:40d813a5-c230-41a6-a890-75cd33680771 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:40d9d9f4-7e15-45b8-9497-27429f6c9996 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP provides communication between clients and AD, which means it is responsible for transporting highly \r
sensitive information. For that matter LDAP can be developed to meet high performance security standards, \r
including those related to data processing. An example for that could be the layer/transport layer security \r
(SSL/TLS) encryption can add vital protection to information shared through LDAP and enhance the security \r
of organizations’ communication channels. \r
\r
LDAP Authentication methods and security mechanisms:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4513.txt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a801ee02-b10e-4fca-8368-d729f8462251 .

camssa:40dba7a7-82a9-46a9-bb04-cf7fae4b636d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:40dce5a8-4ace-4724-98f5-12f6f24b29cf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:40e02e71-82f6-47f4-b921-b85134ff6c9e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2cedd44f05183dae5548108bdeace2c092b84c7c5d89c475b0741ddae7fc7b2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:40e11190-1b93-4b6b-b52a-cae28c437431 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
CAMSS Assessments Library: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-assessments-library"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52d1dc9e-e832-4308-b794-17b01e0273ff .

camssa:40e1ebb9-cd15-486e-bbbe-7674e0ccc3fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The SOAP 1.2 is included in the  European Interoperability Architecture (EIA) study explores the need for a European interoperability architecture facilitating the establishment of European public services (cross border eGovernment services). WS-Security is a SOAP 1.2 extension so it can be mapped in EIRA too.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/isa_2.1_eia-finalreport-commonvisionforaneia.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35b305c5-42d3-4c46-928c-90f7794a889e .

camssa:40ecf29d-dad3-4f0b-ab5d-c7addfff4d6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The DCAT-AP vocabulary supports the attribution of data and metadata to various participants such as resource creators, publishers and other parties.\r
\r
In addition, it also supports the association of rights and licenses with catalogued Resources and Distributions.\r
\r
Such metadata improves the reliability of data exchanged between citizens, businesses and public administrations. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a236072-8d3f-49d8-a059-90e0d38df685 .

camssa:40f66b7e-6e51-4aae-b534-7fd5c0bd9938 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to the Netherlands and Spain. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dcd6b25b-578e-4f8e-a797-4f43bf9e8509 .

camssa:40fe35ad-9e60-4853-b741-692d07cfc083 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are pieces of evidence that state OData is wide-spread and used (see OData ecosystem reference).
Although there are some market alternatives to OData, such as GData (Google) or OpenAPI, it is worth to note that there is some evidence of OData as an innovative solutions creator. Moreover, the specification has a dedicated Github tailored by the Microsoft community.

Stackshare-OData reference:
https://stackshare.io/odata/alternatives

OData ecosystem reference:
https://www.odata.org/ecosystem/

OData-Microsoft Github reference:
https://github.com/OData

GData reference:
https://developers.google.com/gdata?hl=es-419

OpenApi reference:
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6455634a-e5a3-437e-b606-5fd941df8a7d .

camssa:41103622-3c50-4d21-98e2-59858f7a42e3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:4112c53b-cf4c-432e-b725-155b5e72b0ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Any cross-border project using internet, uses HTTPS.\r
\r
An interesting example is the TESTA network service – which stands for Trans European Services for Telematics between Administrations – provides a European backbone network for data exchange between a wide variety of public administrations. It is an ISA2 solution which has been designed to support the needs for a whole range of application architectures relying on protocols such as HTTPS. \r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e1e1d60-51b9-4281-a9e8-a1b601fda466 .

camssa:411a98b2-5811-4397-8cbb-30ecf3721ed1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4123a5cc-a118-4019-957a-312a7bb1aeac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4125df51-923a-4569-8408-a50dd552447f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

