camssa:41d4dd15-19c5-4810-b561-31decad35a7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """EuroVoc was developed for the first time in 1982. It has been constantly evolving to adapt user's needs. Moreover, there are several releases since it was developed that justify its maturity and its use in the developement products and services. \r
\r
\r
EuroVoc Releases: \r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4063991-b4f1-4330-a8a4-26aeaa4203e6 .

camssa:41db18cb-104c-4873-9036-b79b72a42ca7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ELI is a business-specific specification that is focused on the identification and definition of metadata for legal documents at the European Level. Even though it could be extended or modified to fit other business requirements, there are no implementations that evidence this fact. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
ELI Technical Documentation: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/technical_information.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:750825b8-0c87-41b8-a078-c2395c1f6b19 .

camssa:41dc4b3b-c0bf-4f29-8c35-21ea28f83e4e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are many free online tools that perform numerous checking in order to verify the conformity of the ETSI Advanced Electronic Signatures which includes XAdES.\r
\r
XAdES conformance testing:\r
https://signatures-conformance-checker.etsi.org/pub/index.shtml"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37110617-ed65-4f2e-abe0-1b9f3a98c74d .

camssa:41dd06e3-9418-47b8-afca-5dd6d9776bfa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org may enable digital service delivery channels. European Legislation Identifier (ELI) is using schema.org in some of its use cases, increasing the access to legislative documents. ELI is adopting the schema.org Legislation vocabulary.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
ELI-Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eli-european-legislation-identifier/solution/eli-legislation-extension-schemaorg/about\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Legislation vocabulary:\r
https://schema.org/Legislation\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df3e81b2-e474-4212-aa9a-bf5e9ab1204d .

camssa:41dfb22a-2c8c-4bb3-a98c-9c593c755cb8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:41e16105-98f6-470f-a2a5-afd91ce56696 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:41e715ea-c05e-493f-90f6-f2bf52d94ea7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is made by W3C, which is a non-European international SDO. Therefore, it can't be considered as an European Standard.

World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) reference:
https://www.w3.org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5fdb1727-e1f3-4854-9eda-85aed76837be .

camssa:41e84c1b-9550-4433-a68d-906404f491c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ETSI TS 119 432 foresees enabling access control mechanisms. Digital signatures can work as access control mechanisms to private data. The authorised signer's use of its key for signing requires users to provide multiple proofs of their claimed identity before being granted access to the needed set of resources. Nevertheless, the way in which the user identity verification process is carried out by the service provider or any suggestion concerning the usage of multi-factor authentication mechanisms is out of the scope of the present document.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f47072bb-dc87-4b80-88fd-081bd6d875d9 .

camssa:41edecf5-6136-4260-b19e-57eee20422d0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:41f4f642-66c4-4745-8ab0-343701624df2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:41f57b21-2111-4fac-8997-1926056b81c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:41fa3f19-c94c-4f27-aacf-b7a5c2582c8e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:41fed22a-8cf6-45c3-9a51-3a6177a1196e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UTF-8 was launched at the beginning of 2000s, and it currently is one of the three encoding methods recognised by Unicode or web languages. This fact demonstrates the maturity and the market acceptance for development of products and services.\r
\r
Usage statistics for character encodings for websites: \r
https://w3techs.com/technologies/overview/character_encoding/all \r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3da73b90-8c6f-4dc5-a2f3-5d474b8c8359 .

camssa:4201244c-80bf-4160-bd62-4df5bba4b14c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the moment of performing the assessment, Ipsec is widely used, including for the development of innovative solutions and especially when Virtual Private Networks are required. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4adbf946-a743-42c1-80c4-1ab290422280 .

camssa:4205f486-0784-4a32-ab55-553f4f3726b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Some evaluations indirectly evaluate the efficiency of the specification. For example, this document offers a survey of current literature and examines open-source dataspace connector implementations that adhere to the International Data Spaces (IDS) standard. The selection of the IDS standard in this context serves as an indirect demonstration of its relevance and efficiency compared to other alternatives.\r
\r
A Survey of Dataspace Connector Implementations: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.11282.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42cfed70-9a2c-4e08-90f4-2da4b66ca855 .

camssa:420892ea-d0b3-496c-820d-46cc9c492e8b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:420946e1-0ec1-40db-883c-9b31f3eda09c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 protocols are designed in a way that can be implemented separately depending on the preservation goals (see section 4.2) or the storage models (see section 4.3).  Partial implementations therefore are allowed in this specification.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a59471ae-9816-4f47-a402-08668d752f53 .

camssa:4210d002-58bf-437b-a40b-a39141bdb87c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org is a (structured data) mark-up schema that helps search engines understand the information on web pages and potentially provides richer search results. Therefore, the specification addresses data portability. At European level, the DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe (DCAT-AP) will be mapped to schema.org, resulting in DCAT-AP-SDO (Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe); apart from aiming at improving data portability within European Data Portals, the DCAT-AP-SDO schema will support the evolution of European public services by enhancing data discovery networks on the web as its precursor DCAT-AP did (see ISA Programme reference, DCAT-AP and public sector databases).\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
DCAT-AP reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dcat-ap\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\r
\r
ISA Programme reference, DCAT-AP and public sector databases:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe_en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab1f446e-4a9b-4df6-8f9b-d4756a4eb5fe .

