camssa:423267e5-40dc-44e1-967c-e116eb9e480c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As defined on the TC standardisation, only TC members are involved in the development of ISO standards. A review is carried out to arrange the consensus firstly within the TC members and subsequently is reviewed by the different ISO member bodies. However, it cannot be considered a public review, because only TC members can participate.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:089bbf12-1934-49e2-b3be-a64d9c45511e .

camssa:4234e937-b736-4273-8c39-c1bd89772168 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """3 Member States are recommending WS-BPEL in their ICT National Catalogues. They belong to Cyprus, France and Germany.  \r
  \r
CAMSS List of Standards:   \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94c6901d-5122-425f-9703-d52a8dddddcf .

camssa:42352bd2-b1ae-41f9-9f2f-8d18b77ee16e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of CPOV is to provide a reusable data model for describing public organisations in the European Union. It manages a public portfolio that facilitates the discovery of which public authorities and departments are responsible for given areas of the public task. Therefore, CPOV provides a standarized frame which facilitates interoperability, and the visibility of government data. 

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d1fa039-24c8-415f-9300-575324bdf669 .

camssa:4238d166-cefc-4762-a535-4037330776b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS supports the evolution of European Public Services by enhancing the discoverability and reuse of interoperability solutions. \r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:059dedbb-73c1-41af-8498-5b97f3012635 .

camssa:4239bb0a-fe7b-4a28-bd2f-998699dc1eb3 a cav:Score,
