    cav:value "80" .

camssa:429a932e-5003-44cd-8f84-7ac79bf5e235 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification addresses semantic aspects thus data security and data privacy issues are addresses by\r
other means. The specification does not prevent the use of any security means.\r
As noted previously, the chief architect of XBRL GL designed the Specification was deeply engaged in the\r
W3C’s security specifications development. While XBRL GL itself does not inherently enable secure\r
exchange, it has been designed with secure exchange in mind.'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:596c118e-60af-408b-b32f-de82b43edf87 .

