        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As it happens with all Core Vocabularies, the ADMS specification can be extended for specific purposes on determined use cases, as it is a profile of DCAT.\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6bc200f6-7f9f-4953-b7bb-9a29872b9fb4 .

camssa:4371b5cd-ea2a-46de-af34-445a27b52bf7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification does not specifically address the protection of personal data managed by public administrations. Its primary focus is on standardising the metadata related to public sector software to enable efficient reuse and sharing across administrations. While it supports interoperability and transparency, it does not include provisions for safeguarding personal data, nor does it offer guidelines related to privacy or data protection standards in public administration systems.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b250bb0f-ef08-4d39-a90d-5dea9581a3da .

