camssa:4419a89d-1599-43cb-89cd-814fafd1bda1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The message-level security standards employed by ebXML rely on XML Security operations such as XML Signature and XML Encryption. As described in the Oracle document about security features, the XML Encryption mechanism allows for the encryption of digital content, making data more secure and trustworthy.

ebXML security:
https://www.oracle.com/technical-resources/articles/enterprise-architecture/ebxml-security1.html

XML Encryption:
https://www.w3.org/Encryption/2001/

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9b10d05-2eae-4e2a-8d0c-cc33d88f1945 .

