camssa:445ae117-5c73-4742-8d00-3f09085f64da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification is included in the GRID4EU project. The GRID4EU project focuses on how distribution system operators can dynamically manage electricity supply and demand, which is crucial for integration of large amounts of renewable energy, and empowers consumers to become active participants in their energy choices.

GRID4EU project:
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/268206'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf5c5ec4-1319-42be-8d73-bb0e6ca1d9f4 .

camssa:445fbd93-eb15-4f05-b9ce-bcbe5e46f4f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 specification is distributed from the ETSI platform. ETSI supports European regulations and legislation through the creation of Harmonised European Standards. ETSI’s mission is to provide platforms where interested parties come together and collaborate on the development and promotion of standards  for Information and Communication Technology (ICT) systems and services.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43b91d58-2800-46df-914d-b37ded56778c .

camssa:445ffa71-98e0-4c06-8834-b0f7af3c5fc7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of PAdES is not related to the visibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html\r
\r
PAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d1bf820-7341-40fc-a9d4-5e571a8dbf6b .

camssa:44600fd3-a43c-4bf0-9dd6-f9e0810ba426 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTPS is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae05729a-7d7c-4024-9c2f-5ea49f220940 .

camssa:446536b4-7fc2-4ef8-884a-24b6b4838734 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAREF releases do not foresee a public review. Releases and extensions are just published while reviewing is done internally by the ETSI Technical Committee SmartM2M.

SAREF Technical Specification: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/103200_103299/103264/03.01.01_60/ts_103264v030101p.pdf

ETSI Technical Committee SmartM2M: https://www.etsi.org/committee/smartm2m'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:441681ad-de5c-435c-98ba-3053230cda60 .

camssa:44667361-aff0-4e28-8bf7-021bf9a27d0e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:447e7dd5-a722-46a9-b8ac-59ade06adf8f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "JSON is defining a set of rules to format data in order to ensure the proper data exchange between applications and platforms. Even defining rules, it can not be considered as a data model in itself, therefore, JSON is not defining a cross-sector data model. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15461af6-459e-4076-a007-3ef6bb486724 .

camssa:448762b4-5e5a-423d-bac0-abeabe753e08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CPOV is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, CPOV can define the interoperability aspects of the "Core Data Model" and "Data" ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc36ed24-8ac3-496e-b36d-6e8ec6f370e9 .

camssa:4489a651-c287-4e28-8379-ca762562d530 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of ETSI TS 119 612 together with other specifications. The "eIDAS Regulation and Its Impact on National Legislation: The Case of the Slovak Republic" study, focuses on the critical analysis of the adopted eIDAS Regulation, its impact on the existing e-signature legislation and the amendments adopted, which are necessary to unify the legal framework for electronic signature of the Member States of the European Union. Moreover, the legal aspects of the e-signature are analised.

"eIDAS Regulation and Its Impact on National Legislation: The Case of the Slovak Republic" study:
https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3387/12/4/187'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b119c8d6-1fcb-44bb-a4e5-1446a29be36f .

camssa:448e1d51-0941-465e-81fd-358645227ab3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There is no evidence of available studies directly assessing the efficiency of this specification. However, there are some use case evaluations submitted by (non-)European administrations where effectiveness is analysed. It is the case of Scotland, which publicly depicted the implementation process of NUTS and explicitly shows the way in which the specification can be adapted to disparate territories.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics\r
\r
Scotland government reference, Scotland's NUTS implementation document:\r
https://www.gov.scot/publications/review-nomenclature-units-territorial-statistics-nuts-boundaries/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa87cae2-bb13-4e25-bbef-0769c8cb9431 .

camssa:4491bead-bd8d-45d7-8ea8-d853fba45d2a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39ffef052c31580b50b418f3991e9de7db4dc182fcf96f5a447d7f8e09560612 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:44934ce6-841e-47f6-a77c-d3980ebe557b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:449375e1-9305-4783-b112-e6ac48a28c8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of WAI-ARIA involves various methods, such as usability studies, user testing, and evaluation against established accessibility standards. As the specification undergoes evaluation, numerous cases and studies investigate its utilization in web content for e-accessibility purposes.

ACM Digital Library reference:
https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3412841.3442066

WAI-ARIA Practices reference:
https://wai-aria-practices.netlify.app/aria-practices/

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/

'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:645997d2-e7db-4169-ada1-802acad685ef .

camssa:449930d8-9534-41c6-89ca-4f05014feca9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV is publicly available for implementation and use, and therefore for everyone to study, for free on IETF webpage. \r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4180 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7129a8cd-2a93-4be6-92e7-9ddfa1df60fb .

