camssa:44a45417-abae-4410-a79a-94e11a0e48dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition. SOAP addresses and facilitates the exchanging of information within cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb630361-0efa-4257-8b29-917752109ded .

camssa:44a5a486-e889-4cb9-8d7f-94fd0960a019 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:44a65e4a-ac99-41a7-a37d-1bd450800137 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although there are no specific studies or documentation about the "Standard for Public Code", there are several studies concerning the importance to include open source solutions and software to public administrations and their benefit to administrations, businesses and citizens.\r
\r
Adopting open source software in public administration: The importance of boundary spanners and political commitment\r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0740624X15000258\r
\r
A study on the introduction of Open Source Software in the Public Administration:\r
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/0-387-34226-5_16\r
\r
Open source software for the public administration:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228770161_Open_source_software_for_the_public_administration\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1d22412-2cc2-4b45-890f-de2010d13aa1 .

camssa:44ab305c-aafa-444d-947f-e1f967bc834e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Not enough information has been found to answer positively or negatively to this criterion. No information related to the governance process of the Better regulation has been found to support the answer to the criterion. \r
