    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:44e8de94-30f5-43d6-a63e-017020ffd69c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State that includes WAI-ARIA in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories 1. Conceptual model for integrated public services provision, 2. interoperability layers, and 3. interoperability principles.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe96db11-4699-4d0e-b8a5-1318d8ad067f .

camssa:44f62873-db5a-43fe-9c3f-f044272cb1a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Each of the specification approval phases (TAB, Council, Public RfCs / Consultation) allow for objections and appeals.\r
See: \r
https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/creating-and-managing-rda-groups/working-group-outputs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ee49673-6e62-4308-b0ca-b15c1cd5c971 .

camssa:44f75ed0-6a4e-40f4-b887-a6b3414ce9dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML can enable the exposure of interfaces, particularly in the context of APIs and other service configurations. By using YAML to define and document interfaces, developers and administrators can clearly communicate the structure, endpoints, methods, and parameters of their services. Some API specifications use YAML to define the structure of API requests and responses.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/

OpenAPI definitions in YAML
https://swagger.io/docs/specification/basic-structure/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d34315bd-f613-4beb-a405-2f6557c6742f .

camssa:44f7f2ce-3ddf-446c-a02c-f6b1026bc0e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2b846455-6ca4-4f15-ab3d-e68457badf42 .

camssa:44f94fcf-0449-4d46-9d12-80332e7ff16b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'File transfer is an essential component of many information exchange processes in public services. FTP can be used as a means to transfer files between different systems and entities involved in public service delivery. It provides a standardized protocol for file transfer, enabling interoperability and efficient exchange of information. In this sense, it can be said that the specification simplifies the delivery of European public services.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03f11e8f-b52b-4508-a815-c942b0e6e448 .

camssa:44fa8dae-5334-461c-a9e1-b8b4f5687db8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ELI is used for the EUR-Lex, the site where EU Institutions publish their datasets for their reuse. In there, it is used to improve the shareability, researchability and interoperability when processing legal data developed by the different Member States. \r
\r
EU Open Data Portal Data sets: \r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/data/group/eli?groups=eli\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba1e2475-cd5b-489f-ac7b-7931646d4093 .

camssa:44fac17a-c43e-46b4-842b-a9fb132f0765 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of NFVI is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview section 4:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a11e6e77-8f48-4e3a-8b75-c5415636bc75 .

