camssa:473b43e5-014c-4819-a155-17b7af951e27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows the exchange of authentication and authorization data between parties. It is mainly used to ensure single sign-on (SSO) and by doing so, it secures the exchange of data.  It extends SSO across security domains independently from any platform which prevents non-interoperable proprietary technologies. For instance, a relevant implementation of SAML 2.0 is SAML Web Browser SSO profile. \r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Web Browser SSO Profile Reference:\r
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was-liberty/core?topic=authentication-saml-20-web-browser-single-sign'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1b6b5c3-5ef1-42bf-9be4-43d5c7552207 .

camssa:473cfae9-c3fd-4400-946d-45b3413195a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAML 2.0 is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, SAML 2.0 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Identity management Component", “Identity Management Service”, “Access Management Component”, and “Access Management Service” ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:379ec3de-bf47-4ac4-aa67-29af2af269b6 .

