camssa:477df04d-c202-4762-a184-aaee7532de63 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The HTTPS specification itself does not have a validator or conformance-checking tool associated with it. However, there are several tools and practices available to assess the implementation and conformance of HTTPS in a web application or server configuration such as the SSL/TLS Certificate Validation.\r
\r
Validation methods for TLS/SSL certificates:\r
https://www.digicert.com/faq/public-trust-and-certificates/what-are-the-validation-methods-for-tls-ssl-certificates'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7dab5c8-f32b-4c9f-a2be-40a528231558 .

camssa:47852c0c-da95-44a9-8c04-1e2e2ca75a41 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:47892d88-796f-4c21-8e02-5cf3c2f0df27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no conformity test from the OASIS, but there are free online documents that will help you validate the UDDI specification when it is implemented. It is also possible to test UDDI with IBM UDDI Test Registry, to experience the registration process, but without putting the web service in an official register.

IBM Test UDDI reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/es/rsas/7.5.0?topic=standards-universal-description-discovery-integration-uddi

UDDI v3 reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was-zos/9.0.5?topic=services-overview-version-3-uddi-registry'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75f88629-3181-4332-ba17-272ba010cd31 .

camssa:478bc545-bf56-4436-b758-b64a13a317af a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSD 1.1 is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
W3C Consortium Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca551cde-383c-4f6b-9334-2468e17d2d51 .

camssa:478bde10-781a-4f02-8a85-251cf12f183b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of YAML is not related to data integrity. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.  

YAML specification: 
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c0b6b0e-72ef-421b-bede-e440659c2ec1 .

