    cav:value "1" .

camssa:47ec8fe8-cca7-404d-88a7-16e10dfe656f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While TSP itself does not encrypt or secure data, it provides an essential layer of trust and verification to data transactions, enhancing security when integrated with other security measures. The examples below demonstrate how adding reliable timestamps to data operations supports the secure exchange of information by ensuring transparency, accountability, and the integrity of data records.

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a5c15738-e80e-447b-8076-699e53249a94 .

camssa:47f2664d-6a4e-4833-82da-21f12aeeb0a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification supports data driven service interoperability like opening of data and reporting.\r
\r
Danish business registry sharing all annual financial statements in XBRL as open data:\r
https://datacvr.virk.dk/data'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:295d2f63-5093-4561-9c27-656738cd4e5d .

camssa:47f52a32-bd9b-49d5-97a8-0167f3e9ca34 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:47f81fdc-b1a4-4fa1-9b5e-1adb8368124d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP does not directly address secure processing of data, but it can promote best practices for metadata description and publication that indirectly contribute to the security of data processing. By providing metadata elements to describe the technical details of data services, it can help data publishers provide information about security measures. Additionally, using standard vocabularies and identifiers can facilitate interoperability of data services that require secure access to data. Finally, it is often used with other standards and guidelines, such as FAIR principles and DMP guidelines, that provide additional guidance on how to ensure secure processing of data.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:732d5eb1-4323-48ec-ad62-0c2268de27a7 .

camssa:47fc2e09-2192-4bfe-9f95-a29e027e3ba2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAML 2.0 is publicly available for free on OASIS Webpage.\r
\r
See:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:180eee59-9c2f-45a0-9478-de9e962727aa .

camssa:47ff12ff-9b51-4ed9-8a8e-e7202c3078f1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LDAP is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, LDAP can define the interoperability aspects of the “Service Registration Service” and “Service Registry Component” ABBs of the EIRA Technical Infrastructure View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e803e6c-3fe5-4292-abcc-561edafedb77 .

