camssa:485e9ecb-476f-47fa-9e0e-f71aca659734 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There is no Member State that includes SAMM in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7dc8bd2-fcf8-45ba-835e-56592497cba4 .

camssa:4862ec98-8979-41a6-96e6-46ae69579ed8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ESPD cannot be customised given that it is based on the Universal Business Language (UBL) which is immutable.\r
\r
ESPD Business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
UBL specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17510bb6-6354-490f-bfcb-b7cc25e0d051 .

camssa:48638c43-13b0-4be2-9dba-8ee74a3e740b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not indicate that relevant information is allowed to be reused, meaning that all information needs to be provided whenever it is needed.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c53cbe0a-aa57-4b4f-86cb-32f8d74f2e0c .

camssa:48692aa0-375c-4d8d-b60d-89fda5011931 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of this Core Vocabulary is to support the exchange of information between organisations that define criteria and organisations that respond to these criteria by means of evidences. This Core Vocabulary helps to comprehend the administrative rules and data of public administration.\r
\r
CCCEV reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:890e87f6-aab7-4e21-9c14-477e4688e11b .

camssa:486be9f7-6d24-4b61-81c9-0e2c9aa01ee4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:486cde93-e850-4ec3-8ea4-92ef297a8b1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Genericode encourages collaboration as it was created by OASIS, a non-profit and open consortium dedicated to standardisation. Both members and non-members of the Code List Representation TC are welcome to participate in the unmoderated Code List Representation Developer Mail List by subscribing at the OASIS mail list manager if any discussion about genericode arises. Furthermore, there is a public GitHub with the development and maintenance of the documentation and artefacts associated with OASIS genericode.

OASIS Code list Representation TC: https://groups.oasis-open.org/communities/tc-community-home2?CommunityKey=7558fd85-f7ac-4dd7-b57b-018dc7d3f6f7

Code List genericode GitHub: https://github.com/oasis-tcs/codelist-genericode'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e35519e3-2142-4b0b-911d-05e1203d0490 .

camssa:486ce953-3a8e-4a1d-b23d-1de555c70f55 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8eb17470327d32b3bb523447fe72ee5c60ddb03e81dae318b485fbe05f48a844 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:48708765-4e5c-4f2e-9791-31e535c7db46 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:48710b4b-17b5-4d47-8edf-f4a43a4b87be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML is a superseded specification that evolved from HTML4 using XML and became a W3C
recommendation on 26 January 2000. It has seen several updates, including XHTML 2, which was
recommended on 31 May 2001. However, HTML5 has largely replaced XHTML, retaining many of its
strengths, such as stricter syntax, while offering improved features, better browser compatibility, and a more
modern approach to web development.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/

XHTML 2 Reference:
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/introduction.html#history-2

HTML5 W3C Reference:
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e39b93c9-7ad4-40bd-898c-a3c2bb8ba611 .

camssa:48715bce-08ff-490d-a612-5e1ba2d54770 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In UDDI, each register must establish its information protection policy, establishing nodes, which protect the data. Each register can have one or more nodes, and contribute to accessibility of web service metadata. Moreover, nodes can use authInfo elements, which are optional elements in API calls for publication, research and subscription API sets, with the objective of control the access.

Access control UDDI reference: 
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/uddi_v3.htm#_Toc85908215

AuthInfo elements UDDI: 
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/uddi_v3.htm#_Toc85908057'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9fce1cc-4dd1-41fd-96f2-e2ceaa7c224e .

camssa:4871a934-a018-4b32-99a6-25250a8c46f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Such means as restriction of access to information/data can be provided as SOAP extensions using the SOAP extensibility mode. The SOAP Messaging Framework does not directly provide any mechanism for dealing with it directly.\r
\r
SOAP Reference, section 7 Security Considerations:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/#secconsiderations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f72bec7-80a6-43a5-92f6-3dc4382fd6a5 .

camssa:48757f55-7b11-47f8-90a2-f923fa8d5c91 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:48792274-5ed5-4ffc-9222-2e02cb905369 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification uses the TestBed service to validate GraphQL queries against GraphQL schemas and contributes to enabling the delivery of European public services. Test Bed offers support for projects using GraphQL by launching a new GraphQL validator to validate queries against their target schemas. The validator is based on the GraphQL reference implementation and expects as input the query to validate as well as the target schema.\r
\r
TestBed & GraphQL reference: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/news/new-graphql-validation-service'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:56214d71-3d67-419b-9a2e-85e45c2bc118 .

camssa:487928af-d08f-4f47-81ac-97d5fc4a13c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS is being used by the TESTA (Trans European Services for Telematics between Administrations) network service, a cross border project that provides a European backbone network for data exchange between a wide variety of public administrations.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818\r
\r
TESTA project:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da311624-0509-49bb-8fee-29e0b5e5716c .

camssa:487cb37c-e773-42ce-9407-28599b9c5627 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is included in two Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. These\r
Member States are Malta and the Netherlands.\r
\r
National catalogue Malta: \r
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243\r
\r
National catalogue The Netherlands:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:866f81e0-e2d4-4905-85aa-b6d2f0513a06 .

