camssa:48a06de2-f6d6-4d6c-b792-60a8b448af56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of WAI-ARIA is not related to the secure of data exchange. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2010f0c6-65ec-4a97-a6ce-722ebb5a1483 .

camssa:48a1389f-6cde-443d-bcb0-6e0ab99036e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of TSP is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ae45c9b-59bd-4f07-9beb-e2853fea06f6 .

camssa:48b20630-1055-4636-a966-dfa0016b0435 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The E-ARK CSIP Specification is not related to multilingualism. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8eb2d1f8-526c-4efd-9d09-e3a5e897bd72 .

camssa:48b3e7b8-c560-41c3-918e-873c878e4545 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:48b68fa7-73d6-412f-8665-f02452421d25 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI is a business-specific specification that is focused on the identification and definition of metadata for
legal documents at the European Level. While it has the potential to be adapted or expanded to
accommodate other business needs, there is currently no evidence of implementations reflecting such
modifications.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

ELI Technical Documentation:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/technical_information.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f12cc81a-5b50-4454-86ca-2e4cc36fd62f .

camssa:48bab4fc-46a4-40a4-bb8f-992ab60cd67c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Vocabularies can be used as the foundation of common export formats for data in base registries like cadastral, business registers or public service portals. The Registered Organisation Vocabulary as well as the Core Business Vocabulary can be used to describe and ease the publication of information as open data. There is an example of the publication of data as Linked Open Data: "Greek Tax Authorities business registry published as linked open data using core business and core location".\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary/about\r
\r
Core Business Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-business-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e20fd592-8802-493e-ada1-5d9028900f5a .

camssa:48bb2a55-5ab8-4f68-9bfc-5980ee603ac6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary facilitates the process for institutions publishing data about public organisations. This Core Vocabulary fosters interoperability and impacts positively on the development of eGovernment. Moreover, CPOV facilitates the reusability of public information, and contributes to the only-once principle, by allowing data to be shared and integrated into different systems and platforms.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0013994d-d5bb-47e3-a2e0-ff719eef24a5 .

camssa:48bdc266-a2f3-4274-b816-2a5a9a100b16 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:48c61780-84c4-4a3f-a50d-cc65991f7c65 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has been developed to support some requirements that are not mandatory but recommended. For example, some security layers such as the SASL can be implemented, but is not required to run the specification. 

LDAP SASL reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2444
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42cfe6df-6364-4948-a2fe-7f3e68a5d4ee .

camssa:48cbf2df-3033-41b5-a6ed-04a868c360b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:48cf6927-6dd6-48d8-b471-51cd6c31bc17 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/e5aca567-a9dd-4ba8-9bb7-deb43ff3342a"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:48d457a0-8d25-4c63-809c-df88d9fc9f48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The protocol for remote digital signature creation aims to scope comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data, and services as it can help define the services required for remote digital signature creation, such as signature generation, key management, and timestamping. In addition, it may define the administrative procedures involved in remote digital signature creation, such as user authentication, authorization, and key management. 

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a2cb34f-4e10-4772-a7d7-0d8f359e8042 .

camssa:48dc7caa-0d46-4623-89d7-ebf8e1f210a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """12 Member States are recommending ODF in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are Croatia, Denmark, Estonia, France, Greece, Ireland, Malta, Netherlands, Norway, Slovenia, Sweden and UK.\r
 \r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e52e03b7-c6ae-4aa0-81f8-21b0ca21104c .

camssa:48dd57f7-bf70-42ce-9a67-2a594cca1522 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of CPSV-AP is related to the delivery of multilingual public services. All datatype properties with datatype “text” where the value for that property may exist in multiple languages, the property has multiple instances which are tagged with a language identifier for each language in which the value for that property exists.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
