camssa:49bb136d-25d9-42d1-b1a9-b9dc4fb8f926 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP is still excellent with authenticating Linux-based applications including many open source solutions, for 
example: OpenVPN, Jenkins, Kubernetes. It is often used to complement Active Directory (AD) as a directory services protocol. Therefore, it is demonstrated that LDAP has enough market acceptance for its use in the development of digital solutions and services.

LDAP used with OpenVPN:
https://openvpn.net/vpn-server-resources/openvpn-access-server-on-active-directory-via-ldap/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89e6c4cf-3bae-4209-b2a5-38c1402a88dc .

camssa:49c0ace4-2e84-425c-9c5b-1d3412249d47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO provides in the documentation the requirements for automatically establishing conformance measurements (section 4.6.5 Validating conformance to BFO). 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42952de5-aa97-49aa-9efa-3f96fb74cac3 .

camssa:49c204b9-7f27-4152-8d74-3970bee16942 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:49c274e1-9163-4241-90e3-5cb9241fa7a3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 6.6 of the specification explains that in the context of the CIA paradigm the role of integrity is to give assurance to user B that on receipt of data from user A that what he receives is exactly as sent by user A and that the data has not been manipulated by user E. In addition, there is a close relationship between integrity and availability with the defining characteristic that the system delivering data is complete and has itself not been corrupted nor manipulated by user E. Integrity is therefore a key characteristic of non-repudiation services.

ETSI Context Information Management (CIM); Security and Privacy:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/CIM/001_099/007/01.01.02_60/gr_cim007v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95e9a014-9b0b-4a0b-8cea-cd74e3a41721 .

camssa:49ca30d1-6126-476e-871d-b7ec48e96ae4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification is supported by ISO. In order to participate in creating standards, the user must be part of their national standards body (assuming their country is part of ISO). Other groups working on ontologies based on the BFO include it as a de facto element. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6c0aa05-2b27-4d30-b6b7-8adc9e7d47ac .

camssa:49cd16bc-217c-4430-8b51-d5b0c5c66561 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence found of the creation of any community along with the sharing of their data and resultson European platforms. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
IPSec reference, What IPSec Does:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-7\r
\r
IPSec reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:848a1a7d-d483-4c67-be7e-6fe096a0496a .

camssa:49ce380b-2c99-4722-8160-5c3b148565bb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software or platform. The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary can be used by any organisation.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e99388e6-366b-4807-a7a9-8d68fa36666e .

camssa:49e749aa-56f8-4523-93dc-cb1977e3382c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-31bf959b6c4a983ec70eb87e0177f2739575ebce42c7c3b95b9012ef3bfe673e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:49eb8328-8b73-49e1-bbf3-67dcd294957e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SHACL is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to the specification.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a5805985-117d-434b-9492-dc98918b174a .

camssa:49ebf568-9883-46ea-ba80-1d5634eef6a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SHACL specification is included in SHAPEness project. And in this context, the SHAPENESS is utilised by the European Plate Observing System (EPOS). The SHAPEness features have proven to be a valuable solution to easily create and maintain valid graphs according to the EPOS data model. In addition, the Test Bed project can be highlighted, as it offers a reusable SHACL validation service, allowing RDF content validation through SHACL shapes.

SHAPEness project in European Plate Observing System (EPOS):
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-39141-5_23

SHACL Test Bed:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/news/shacl-validator-updates

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5137db2-2aa8-4ceb-a419-dc9bab86cdb9 .

camssa:49ed1ed4-6d7b-4365-bd11-2f962eb3300c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:49f3c6a6-3749-4e76-8d8c-26200e053d26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is independent from any particular software, hardware, or operating system. So, it can be \r
said that ISO 19941:2017 is independent of any specific platform.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ccf726a3-ea2c-486f-8d8a-213fdf32aada .

camssa:49f66292-3b66-4b55-bea9-c7a23924c274 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:49f6928e-4c02-4f36-83aa-23ab15e7675d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 16234-1 e-CF framework is intended to serve as a device to represent the European e-Competence Framework, which focuses on skills and competences of the ICT professional workforce. EN 16234-1 e-CF has a self-contained structure and behaves as a single-purpose device; therefore, the specification does not allow customisation.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecdc3a6b-43da-4ec5-aa29-b17ccea5415b .

camssa:49ff4522-a39f-4bc3-8349-863e51bf2571 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is free to use. There are no royalties or fees required to use the specification, as it is licensed under the CC0 1.0 Universal license. This licensing framework places the specification in the public domain, permitting unrestricted use, including reproduction, modification, and distribution,  without any royalties, fees, or conditions.

Publiccode.yaml Licensing:
https://github.com/publiccodeyml/publiccode.yml/blob/main/LICENSE'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c85ddbc0-1d19-4cee-91ef-68243d15cd7e .

camssa:49ffdc1d-3aa5-46d4-87f1-fe6477352c6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML is an open file format published with an open license to use as the user sees fit. With that said, most of the subsets, tools and libraries for YAML have assorted licenses that are slightly more specific. For example, the YAML CSS Framework is published under the CC-BY 2.0 Creative Commons Attibution license, which simply requires an attribution link to the originating site.  

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf93202e-500c-4708-bf0b-4952d9a9b66a .

camssa:4a021f32-0771-4a07-8750-7c71dfb4dfaa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7451c94-95bb-4076-a6c4-e247dee11743 .

camssa:4a04093b-7bdf-4437-ad9e-c99566b8c806 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a05c468-72ab-45b2-90c3-a4f8bc0fcdb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a document exchange format, PDF/A is a valuable tool for sharing information through the internet. Allowing sharing data and information the standard foster the visibility of administration data and services. Additionally, it eases the decision-making process within administrations. \r
\r
PDF/A reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/38920.html\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/50655.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b90c83d3-0138-4b3e-9fec-b9519d78afe0 .

camssa:4a05f2e5-2659-496a-9a3d-a43ccddcd948 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of ADMS is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e784a604-971a-400f-81e2-12785c53ba4d .

camssa:4a0bc111-a99d-438f-9816-303d7f319f38 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a0dcb59-21e1-497b-8ca7-79f6a65fd82b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAREF is not related to providing means for restriction of access to information/data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. 

SAREF:
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aec26d49-06ee-4c49-b874-102203545f15 .

camssa:4a1126fb-8970-43c5-8d09-5d71d5a49071 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData allows for including custom transformations (that is, query options) that the user explicitly requests, which are not necessary defined in the OData specification. However, these extensions are restrictive or limited to a specific functionality.\r
\r
OData reference, 2 Overview and 6 Extensibility:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752211'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0003303-1b50-41fe-8d26-5f1745bda071 .

camssa:4a12441e-2a79-4aa6-8260-359e60248b58 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:4a19f973-0c9c-48a3-8cf3-1c6b936b0919 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML specification is not platform-agnostic, is dependent on certain environments and platforms, such as
compatible web browsers for proper rendering.

Browser Compatibility Reference:
https://www.lambdatest.com/web-technologies/xhtml

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3474a05b-e52f-4f6b-84e7-ce1615a3c7ce .

camssa:4a1f88f7-6e09-4ead-92ac-0d2a43224c43 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:4a229936-816b-4188-9a15-90db47098560 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON itself does not provide direct customization options. It has a predefined structure and syntax that follows a specific set of rules. The basic building blocks of JSON are objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, and null values, and it does not support custom data types. Nonetheless, indirect customisations can be applied, as their basic building blocks can be flexibly used.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:995f61dc-e91a-4c51-ba1e-db0b175ea192 .

camssa:4a2aad87-6a04-406f-8470-5245f1ff2598 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a2fa461-f18c-43af-b71b-c1ed03061094 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4a30ebbd-4135-4e73-a483-68af8fc759e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is independent of any platform and can be implemented without dependencies with technologies. Further more, BFO is designed to support information system interoperability per se.  

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d9ee543-a0a2-4c7a-8d71-863611e093fc .

camssa:4a34f8a2-07ee-456a-be8b-02f65359846d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a37b0e2-178a-4183-a621-c81f9c621e3a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a39fc43-0bf2-4fbc-9919-b7a0006cdba1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d7be9f0dd52944e6c25f5469c86355a42ae446838bd9759b4986d21f7db4814b ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:4a48194d-8062-4cbd-8d3a-ce8d387429bb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Domibus is currently being used and implemented by a large number of projects involving large-scale message exchange in the context of public services delivery. An example of projects using Domibus to deliver public services is the MAPA project, or the e-CODEX platform, which provides easy access to cross-border justice for citizens, business and legal professionals all over Europe.\r
\r
Domibus implementation in MAPA project:\r
https://mapa-project.eu/2022/01/F\r
\r
DomibusConnector Suite for e-CODEX:\r
https://www.e-codex.eu/node/47'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:732c0433-c412-4e18-97ed-da670987b7b7 .

camssa:4a4b841e-de07-4be2-8e07-c49338638ddc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is a completely free of charge specification provided by the European Commission, and there is no fee or IPR limitation to use it. Moreover, the tools used for modelling and working with the EIRA, are open source and can be used without paying. Moreover, apart from using the specification with no limitations, the action provides support for implementing it free of charge. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef252ba3-f091-4f53-9902-dbe94ef070d5 .

camssa:4a4e2506-2f69-4dcb-98af-fb04c23d5b43 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a50eb9c-283b-4884-9bd5-dcafea33f26e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT is included in five national catalogues, with the Netherlands and Spain as examples. The Netherlands have the highest performance of all Member States, complying with all 3 sections of the EIF according to the NIFO factsheets.\r
                                                                       \r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards                    '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c878d048-b11d-42e0-8414-85a2c36e30b3 .

camssa:4a592098-70d9-4d42-8d4d-04bf49c3b5f6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:4a598131-fb79-4962-bf98-162e4aede136 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a5ea23e-5353-4a9a-9ddf-eba3f67a290b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv6 is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, IPv6 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data Exchange" and "Firewall" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v610'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ca9425c-6244-4bfe-bd8f-a6c1ea87c4b2 .

camssa:4a5f4b20-079b-4a28-982d-2ee03f4d4d45 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4a5f5954-aa0a-4a9d-b60b-1e68450115b7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:4a659650-39f2-4e80-ba7f-82ad0b7df326 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the time of elaborating this assessment, FTPS does not foster the creation of innovative solutions. Since its publication in 2005 as an extension of FTP, it has been used to secure the ordinary protocol FTP. However, another FTP extension with the same purpose as this specification, is raising its usage and FTPS is getting obsolete.\r
\r
FTPS - Obsolescent Secure FTP:\r
https://www.ssh.com/ssh/ftp/ftps\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc94c549-94e3-4bdd-a8a0-b8a7a96eca08 .

camssa:4a69cf22-a8e5-4bfe-8179-900b5127841d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:4a6dacfd-8570-4328-9273-7fa615f6ec2e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main purposes of OAIS is to provide a framework from which apply long-term preservation of information techniques in archival information systems.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf"'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62020b4c-c934-4d2e-a78f-6d82018d16fb .

