camssa:4ac74713-73b5-4d1f-b21b-a74382a37eec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP mentions the importance of protecting personal information in server logs and the potential risks associated with transferring sensitive data. (See section 11.1 at HTTP/1.1 RFC 7).

HTTP clients are often privy to large amounts of personal information (e.g. the user's name, location, mail address, passwords, encryption keys, etc.), and SHOULD be very careful to prevent unintentional leakage of this information via the HTTP protocol to other sources.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c52c50ac-3c6e-4c86-835a-e357e2113b30 .

