    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4af0839a-f0e3-4bf1-8d82-15fd3fc127f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the specification is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b9ce59b-b789-4aac-812b-15750f657d2f .

camssa:4af17120-48e4-4d90-add7-c69b75b65cd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of PAdES is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html\r
\r
PAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d41919c2-243a-4a76-aa1e-b5ded475fbec .

camssa:4afe96ca-0a3b-4f49-97f9-86c1d964f435 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main features of the TSP is that it allows for the maintenance of accurate and consistent timestamps, thus helping in creating a reliable record of data changes and states over time. Users, therefore, can access historical data effectively and ensures that any reused information reflects its proper sequence and integrity. Allowing the reuse of existing data that has been certified, the specification can avoid administrations asking for same certified references in procurement, for instance.

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5bb191cf-c06a-4e43-b153-e9ea61615706 .

camssa:4b02ff58-70a7-478d-aea0-272df3a4f2d6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c09094de9d71f12686896827a205db683b6df58fa363bc5be2a7d99989e7dd0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4b03baf6-ee5d-4598-91fa-c727302480d3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Version 1.1 of the specification is referenced within Joinup as one of the assets for the licensing of datasets. However, the link provided allows users to access the whole text of the latest version, therefore it is accessible for free from the European Platform Joinup. \r
\r
Rights and licences for Datasets: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-implementation-guidelines/discussion/mi6-rights-and-licences-datasets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98fd6812-8e7e-4a76-a2d8-d56c3d9ba323 .

camssa:4b04f15c-c9f7-419c-a649-38c5688f72eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XHTML is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, XHTML can define the interoperability aspects of the "Representation" ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4954f780-2bec-43c9-a5dc-ae2344705a1f .

camssa:4b0a9ec8-d5b1-4881-bab6-3ed95ee9022d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPv6 is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a35bf41-174e-425e-ae7c-b75fb5bf94b2 .

camssa:4b1a517a-bbde-4e4a-aa9c-84cd0205cd4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification has been included in many European projects focused on privacy aspects. One such project is Demo 4 from the GRID4EU European project. In this project, the IPsec protocol is mentioned as a mechanism to transport information from primary substations to secondary substations. Moreover, the IPsec specification is also used for transporting electrical network data and control messages.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

IPsec in GRID4EU project reference:
http://www.cired.net/publications/workshop2014/papers/CIRED2014WS_0107_final.pdf

GRID4EU project reference:
https://ses.jrc.ec.europa.eu/eirie/en/data-collection/grid4eu-demo-4-increase-medium-voltage-mv-networks-hosting-capacity-der-introducing'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50934a68-a734-4a19-8f6c-307abc82c95f .

camssa:4b1c1042-5f4b-41be-b8ec-2f367f25c616 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4b24d0a2-98fd-41ff-a40d-4fc33c06d924 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4a006ad6785e066d16c13daf48a60ee43ec33d1de1b06613c8e656ccf330a6d5 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4b27cf37-1edb-4253-a70e-19fa084be09b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4b2afaf6-c966-4c8a-b855-6f30c974a034 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 319 422 defines requirements for a common electronic delivery service in the framework of the eIDAS Regulation. It also provides a profile scheme that is of interest for the eIDAS Regulation.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66d43090-4d50-4df8-bf03-a0fba1e7677c .

camssa:4b2d963e-ee46-4860-a032-006fe210884d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4b2f344c-1f9e-41c3-8086-c64e9e59348f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There are no evidences of existing studies or documentation assessing the standard or specification in terms of effectiveness and efficiency to justify the criterion."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98f75a46-ad8e-4d9c-8da3-6366f99157c1 .

camssa:4b30cc13-0b9e-4c2e-aa37-c3e5601a4efb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By allowing the exchange of datasets metadata, DCAT-AP increases the searchability, visibility, discoverability and reuse of existing data, including information on processes and administrative rules. \r
\r
DEU data provider manual:\r
https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:19a71bf1-97e3-4720-bb9d-e3d1d9932214 .

camssa:4b32ec04-41cd-49df-bc0c-1f00689ebef4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4be59ccf-54a2-41a8-a8b7-3907a9f8a3f1 .

camssa:4b368e1e-a1a8-4938-92d3-22edba0eebe0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog, as a logging protocol, is not inherently designed for the purpose of exposing interfaces to access public administration services. Syslog is primarily used for the collection and transmission of log messages between network devices, systems, and applications. However, syslog can indirectly contribute to the management and monitoring of public administration services by providing a standard in logging security events, providing an audit trail for security-related activities. This is essential for public administration services to identify and respond to potential security threats.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:92c8a80f-bdda-492f-9788-9fe2779c0a01 .

camssa:4b3ed4f8-089e-4cad-bfd8-c2aabbeada6b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, YAML can define the interoperability aspects of the “Container”, "Container Registry", and "Containers Manager" ABBs of the EIRA Technical Infrastructure View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87604251-5025-48dd-92e1-31f7c370b097 .

