camssa:4b6e6776-698e-43e2-967f-c6870b388cda a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF is a vendor neutral SDO. However, FTP relies on the default data connection ports provided by TCP to ensure that all data exchanged is sent correctly to the proper destination.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc959\r
\r
Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc793'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d7dec6a-9478-4a27-9475-d62a919ea9e1 .

camssa:4b721122-efb0-46aa-b468-06c40e9260f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"EN 16234-1 e-CF provides a common European description of the knowledge, skills and competences of the ICT professional workforce in any sector of activity. According to Joinup's Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation, the use of the specification will increase the development and promotion of ICT professionalism, digital skills and e-learning in all sectors of society and industry.\r
\r
Joinup-2021 Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation reference, Education, Digital skills and Digital learning section:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/education-digital-skills-and-digital-learning\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:803b905b-8b48-43d6-a246-900091402d62 .

