camssa:4c13d1c3-8d14-48e1-a3db-02e284d3687c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, the specification is not associated with any ABB from the latest version published of the ELIS v1.0.0. \r
\r
However, ELI is associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS) on-going version 1.1.0 that will be published in 2021. More specifically, ELI can define the interoperability aspects of the "Legislation Catalogue" ABBs of the EIRA Legal View, and "Ontology" ABB from the Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07d075fc-e5e8-4407-ba53-defa666f03f5 .

camssa:4c2a6155-ea32-499b-99da-7e8f61bdf775 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the PM2 alliance gathers the inputs from different stakeholders, there are no disclosures of a public-review being part of the decision-making process. The OpenPM in the end is produced and published by the Center of Excellence for Project Management Methodology, which congregates individuals and organisations coming from several and diverse area of knowledge. \r
\r
The Center of Excellence also coordinates the PM Support Network (PSN), which in turn contributes to the development of communities and professionals executing projects using the methodology.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127\r
\r
PM2 alliance and advisory commettees: \r
https://www.pm2alliance.eu/advisory-committees/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:99a454ab-63a0-4b4a-b54e-e0a8b1476df9 .

camssa:4c2faf4d-8003-40d7-946b-94a0e12a2d5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Vocabularies can be used as the foundation of common export formats for data in base registries like cadastral, business registers or public service portals. The Registered Organisation Vocabulary as well as the Core Business Vocabulary (it is the same vocabulary but it was renamed) can be used to describe and ease the publication of information as open data. There is an example of the publication of data as Linked Open Data: "Greek Tax Authorities business registry published as linked open data using core business and core location".\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary/about\r
\r
Core Business Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-business-vocabulary\r
\r
Greek Tax Authorities business registry published as linked open data using core business and core location:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/registered-organization-vocabulary/news/core-business-and-core-locati"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5cfd6bd2-2adb-4501-b173-0384e1e4a5dd .

camssa:4c34b6b2-739a-4a95-8464-bb31fc5ca357 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification was originally designed to be associated with business processes. In this sense, the ebXML working groups included a section dedicated to "business processes." Additionally, the "XML and Global Business Exchanges - an invitation" document states that the specification aims to be a global initiative to develop an open technical framework, enabling XML to be utilised in a consistent and uniform manner for the exchange of all electronic business data. However, it does not state that the specification cannot be used in other domains. Therefore, although it is designed to be implemented in a business context, it can be considered domain-agnostic.

ebXML business domain:
https://xml.coverpages.org/ebXML.html

"XML and Global Business Exchanges - an invitation" document:
https://xml.coverpages.org/ebXMLInvit.pdf

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1aa5ddd7-dee9-4894-83b7-36d9328d5aba .

camssa:4c3f676a-cb49-4ae5-a5e1-32d7d96fe795 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is intended to identify a country, dependencies and special areas of geographical interest. There is no possibility of partial implementation of the specification, as the specification has a single purpose.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8c31b9f-aedd-4180-9197-4f4a721972ca .

camssa:4c458263-90ac-4caf-8ccb-3d16134cea22 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4c47412a-6526-49fb-8887-cbc0f74549ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already studies and documentation assessing the specification in terms of effectiveness and efficiency. The topics are different, for instance, there is a study assessing the capabilities of XML Schema for the defense against Signature Wrapped Attacks. \r
Another field of documentation is the XML Schema clustering, and its effectiveness for the improvement of user results.\r
\r
ResearchGate XML Schema Validation Reference:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/252053794_On_the_effectiveness_of_XML_Schema_validation_for_countering_XML_Signature_Wrapping_attacks\r
\r
ResearchGate Effectiveness & Efficiency Assessment Reference: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/254858700_XML_schema_matching_balancing_efficiency_and_effectiveness_by_means_of_clustering'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:44d05425-ce4a-4dd4-8a5e-f2c7a0c8e2e5 .

camssa:4c47ff97-7ff9-4738-8c59-19d18a8b88e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The fact that the specification describes the model for being serialised and represented in a machine\\x02readable format fosters the exchange and reuse of information and its translation to other languages different from the original in which was developed the initial resource. Therefore, ODRL can be useful to ensure the availability of access datasets licensing and the related services in different languages, easing the multilingualism of digital public services. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4819d2d-415d-4e67-bced-35274a5dae3b .

camssa:4c53b409-fe57-4ae3-a1ac-739a52705316 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After carrying out information retrieval, no document or study has been found assessing the OpenPM2 in terms of efficiency or effectiveness."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:563b9fff-3d5f-4aec-82c9-ee7fe0e2e8f4 .

camssa:4c5490f7-c534-44d6-bc13-30bc2875744a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e8c3529a6146f0b0d269112be717ba4e9c5979ea4f43f57d217c0f998d26ce17 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4c54e308-b6e4-4cfd-903a-2398dee4913d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary does not ensure and enable data processing accuracy. The main purpose of the specification is to define a standardised way of describing organisations that have gained legal entity status through a formal registration process. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e3511d3-a41e-45ec-87c4-78944727cf46 .

camssa:4c56261f-c9d2-42c2-b24d-e183b7139233 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XAdES is included in 7 national catalogues. They belong to Member States which comply with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the EIF according to the NIFO factsheets. \r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50e2c285-6b5a-43df-a7ed-cdb18df60f85 .

camssa:4c58f6a5-0bfd-4d94-bd33-e09df92dd293 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"FTP is used as the main protocol for file exchange by many public organisations. By allowing public administration to share information with others, it fosters the comprehensibly of data (e.g. Administrative rules, processes etc.) and facilitates public administrations decision-making. \r
\r
An example of implementation supporting this fact would be CIRCABC, a project with the purpose of enhancing the collaboration, communication and document exchange between different European Union's stakeholders. \r
\r
CIRCABC Reference: \r
https://circabc.europa.eu/ui/welcome\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:670c9d29-f658-40a1-89e0-9b6b750fb825 .

camssa:4c5ac0b6-db55-441b-a5de-8f92713373dc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does dwell in data portability between systems/applications or supporting the implementation/evolution of standards since it is designed to support the interchange of information among different information systems. But its main focus is the model, it contributes to data portability but it is up to the users to develop it. 

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7b17ab0a-7d3e-419e-bbb2-404bd902fd9b .

camssa:4c5bc6a8-42ae-4927-bb78-d747e1e688c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog provides with security features for the exchange of data. According to section 5.1 of the specification's protocol "all implementations of this specification MUST support a TLS-based transport". The syslog protocol operates at the application layer, and its focus is on the transmission and reception of log messages. The content of syslog messages is typically sent in clear text by default. 

Syslog Protocol Section 5.1: hhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424#section-5.1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:813922dc-9e7f-4afa-ae6b-86e32a80ff4f .

camssa:4c66fd08-5179-4901-a3c3-5eeb44ac4610 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "None"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:4c670d68-a143-4306-9944-001cb3e26007 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx can be very useful for data portability as it is a tool that allows for the communication of data structures associated with some process or interface.  Moreover, ShEx also allows for the serialization in different human and machine-readable formats, use cases that ease the transfer of data between systems, at the same time it eases comprehensibility for humans.   An example of the ShEx implementation would be the Hercules ASIO project, whose objective is to create a Research Management System (RMS) based on semantic open data that offers a global view of the research data of the Spanish University System (SUE), to improve management, analysis and possible synergies between universities and the general public. Therefore, supporting the implementation of European public services.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues\r
\r
Hercules ASIO project:\r
https://github.com/HerculesCRUE/ib-shex-lite'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73c6a719-247c-4dc7-81b3-aff77f0d6622 .

camssa:4c6905a7-d7d3-48cc-a7bd-c2a56913f8fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF standards are free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. The specification is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e01e0379-6d88-40ef-a160-8fdc5038575a .

camssa:4c738472-6379-4290-8c68-109659de545b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Belgium is recommending CPSV-AP in their ICT National Catalogues.\r
\r
Belgium national catalogue:\r
https://www.belgif.be/nl/specifications"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82041b72-845f-45ba-a110-166432c5a5dc .

camssa:4c7586c3-d17a-4ad4-84ab-4f37216527cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP is included in 1 national catalogue of recommended specifications. It belongs to Spain.\r
The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of this Member States is almost fully aligned with the\r
European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework\r
Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio\r
/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1dec1d94-50d7-4340-82e5-b7020c8bd295 .

camssa:4c78179f-795b-4864-983c-832bc775f2e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5513b49-82c1-4b1e-8353-8933e3bce563 .

camssa:4c78ae67-ae18-4723-ad62-12d82a44191a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "60" .

