    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4c9951cf-92c5-4899-a98b-1156f8d8a85f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec allows data portability between systems and is compatible with both IPv4 and IPv6. Moreover, IPsec works with AH and ESP headers, which facilitate data transfer between systems. Therefore, IPsec can use these headers to enhance data portability between applications. 

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

IPsec in IPv4 and IPv6:
https://networkengineering.stackexchange.com/questions/37025/ipsec-in-ipv4-and-ipv6'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e31c7d69-a499-4faf-b077-964eb93eb10b .

camssa:4ca010ec-a097-45ef-97f3-508aa998663f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4ca9425c-6244-4bfe-bd8f-a6c1ea87c4b2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4caacdaa-ddc5-42a6-81ec-6754d39666c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Data Privacy Vocabularies and Controls Community Group (DPVCG) is in charge of mantaining and developing the DPV, it is a fairly open group that welcomes participation regarding extensions and refinement of terms.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:28ed0e75-85ac-4ab5-9a0f-a730d7cf063c .

camssa:4cac315d-64f6-42f7-9f79-968cdd1deb0b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33ea90f5c1bb01d4398c57d03a25934dc5722d5ddbc98a43911ea4fb302ec54c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4cac8438-2286-4718-81fb-e6aa67288a79 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4caf6116-c8f2-4d4d-9a16-2cac161c1d12 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although Ogg’s purpose is not the long-term preservation of data, it can be used to store multimedia content. \r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:008d0fee-3a4f-49a1-93ec-aac8d44bc2cd .

camssa:4cb09e85-d10b-40ea-87be-49bae2bae3c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39ffef052c31580b50b418f3991e9de7db4dc182fcf96f5a447d7f8e09560612 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:4cb3f249-95cb-4a1e-a11d-7b778b274979 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML, developed by the W3C, is not classified as a European Standard. However, it significantly
contributes to the foundation of web technologies widely used throughout Europe. By providing a consistent
way to structure web documents, XHTML has helped improve digital communication and made it easier to
exchange information.

XHTML W3C reference
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b5934e9-f0c6-45a6-bd3b-c3502183cdf8 .

camssa:4cb7802b-0fb7-4ca6-b908-7a57778b30cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CSS v2.1 is to give format to web designs, thus, the use of the specifications does not hamper the scalability of systems. By using CSS v2.1, administrations, citizens or businesses can visualize data over the Internet. If the environment grows or changes, CSS can be adapted without creating harm over the solution.\r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f43b0b80-09a2-446b-9ff3-fb0bcf782aa0 .

camssa:4cb7c981-fb40-4c4a-8b62-f31f8c0525d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of ODF is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db8826c0-57c1-4d83-aa99-7702ed0d4acc .

camssa:4cb84244-507e-4635-bb92-3cee3b8dae52 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The HTML5 Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including HTML5.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea93ca05-ec67-4325-abde-938887caf960 .

camssa:4cc2515d-5677-4fc4-a12e-576c51cb2eb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition. In this sense, SHACL addresses and facilitates interoperability between public administrations, cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment. This is due to the fact that it has been designed to enhance the semantic and technical interoperability layers of ontologies expressed as RDF graphs, and RDF is a European Standard used by public administrations in projects for sharing Linked Data."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f7f2b03-79a4-48b0-962e-5c2a5afc8c7f .

camssa:4cc56a9b-db10-4adf-a8fb-ac66fe02d8c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is an Extensible Mark up Language (XML) based specification.  XML is a markup language and file format for storing, transmitting and reconstructing arbitrary data, and it emphasizes simplicity generality and usability across the internet.  For that matter, XML supports at least one of the five stars of Tim Berners-Lee scale.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0740414a-8da5-49c0-86b3-04c82699d208 .

camssa:4cca4481-cacf-440a-854f-5e0cc946e3f6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4ccd5705-d117-47fc-9210-816c05add975 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)  is widely used and implemented in the context of application, transport, internet and link layers as FTP or IP. Moreover, there are several implementations of the specification that support the market acceptance of TSP.\r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52c7cd97-92ab-4a36-9ecd-1a3af95712b0 .

camssa:4cd06cd4-11f0-48ad-9be0-92ed2b8f69aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog focuses on the transmission and reception of log messages in a standardized format. However, syslog can indirectly contribute to organizational interoperability by providing a standardised communication format, thus improving cross-platform compatibility and secure information exchange.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2053e90-f749-4fd5-872e-2086d3d145db .

camssa:4cdab712-67e1-438c-847e-50e9e59523a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XHTML is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
XHTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ce96e30-baec-4343-af0a-9e9c9fe596f1 .

camssa:4ce00c1d-86ff-49fd-8737-6b637f073b7f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4ce82551-b4ac-4652-a5c9-52cf26054e1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP is included in European Union Agency for Network and Information Security (ENISA). This organisation is a centre of network and information security expertise for the EU, its member states, the private sector and Europe’s citizens. ENISA works with these groups to develop advice and recommendations on good practice in information security. It assists EU member states in implementing relevant EU legislation and works to improve the resilience of Europe’s critical information infrastructure and networks. 

ENISA Privacy and Data Protection by design Reference:
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/privacy-and-data-protection-by-design

HTTP /1.1 Access Authentication, RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html#section-11'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7234e714-8807-478b-ae8d-5cff65cbb670 .

camssa:4ce96e30-baec-4343-af0a-9e9c9fe596f1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33ea90f5c1bb01d4398c57d03a25934dc5722d5ddbc98a43911ea4fb302ec54c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4cea824a-1e1e-43f7-8bac-dd785eabd508 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is designed to support possible customisations depending on the business-specific needs and requiremets.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf    '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b4ff8a1-9d2e-49f2-9f69-9b6a791181d4 .

camssa:4cefea9d-f0ab-41e0-a6e6-399f54469402 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XACML is publicly available for free on OASIS Webpage.\r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fd068e3b-7096-46d0-8eb3-832ab404315e .

camssa:4cf07008-ca53-478f-a921-123c78a2af4e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4cf88e93-f628-4dc1-8084-46df96b5cf16 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4cfd90ab-077c-45a7-a413-9c965ef5e816 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived. \r
            \r
W3C Process Document reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/2021/Process-20211102/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0749752-dd2c-4e34-99e5-ebeb7905f641 .

