camssa:4d1406cc-4c8e-4a91-978d-bbdc386acaee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of IPSec is to secure communications over a Network; therefore, the specification does not focus on the facilitation of digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
IPSec reference, How IPSec Works:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-9'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09f9c067-9022-4c46-8fc5-937e866bfc3c .

camssa:4d18731f-6d06-46cb-8867-4ece93f462aa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4d19a471-165e-4079-9107-d9e4390e8f9f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a protocol for mantaining and accessing Directory Services, LDAP is a useful tool to display of user \r
information in a readable manner. comprehensibility of data therefore is supported by the fact that it permits \r
to access user information in the network in a structured, human-readable manner.\r
\r
LDAP Directory Information Models:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4512\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc9867e8-a50f-454c-9def-9d86de88b988 .

camssa:4d1b17f0-9c91-4bda-b844-bd2e96f41ab8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As WS-BPEL is a language used for the composition of web services, WS-BPEL helps and fosters the visibility of administration data, and services. Moreover, it eases the decision-making process by ensuring the data exchange and reuse. \r
\r
The specification: \r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6604232f-6b4e-44b9-b37d-3a8022eb59a1 .

camssa:4d1bf820-7341-40fc-a9d4-5e571a8dbf6b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4d1ce26f-1ce1-4072-942a-427f987a69a1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4d25a8e2-09df-42fb-9445-84e280a3d32a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While genericode itself does not directly enable the exposure of interfaces to access public administration services, it can indirectly contribute to the interoperability and integration of systems that provide access to public administration services by promoting consistency, compatibility, and semantic clarity in data exchange.  By utilising genericode-compliant code lists, agencies can ensure how data is represented and exchanged between services and external systems.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2eb600fd-fb60-494f-ac60-a7d414e6a406 .

