camssa:4d6585ba-c0f9-4de4-8822-7141e4abdd5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of GITB TDL is not related to the comprehensibly of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#what-is-the-gitb-tdl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:24c09b65-1ed3-4c4f-8155-ba2a25b517b4 .

camssa:4d676378-de7c-4ee4-83dc-8cdc8e067ce6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4d697ae3-cdce-4935-9529-802a8a48b19a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:4d6c9420-00c1-47f0-a283-a4662048a42f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog has been selected for its use in the European Data Protection Supervisor (EDPS). It is the European 
Union’s (EU) independent data protection authority and they aim to monitor, advise, intervene, and 
cooperate in personal data and privacy matters regarding EU institutions. It is mentioned that SYSLOG is the 
administrative management tool for training at the European Commission in three fields: informatics, 
language and general.

EDPS: https://edps.europa.eu/_en

Training SYSLOG: https://edps.europa.eu/data-protection/our-work/publications/opinions-prior-check/training-syslog-commission_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:65d5eb7f-0782-494c-bfc9-3fd002d0f8f3 .

camssa:4d7a1e6e-0a68-44df-8f3d-3e99812eb928 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has\r
adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards.\r
\r
ETSI standard making:\r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7fa1c9d-b8f7-40a7-9325-04be262ebee3 .

camssa:4d7dec6a-9478-4a27-9475-d62a919ea9e1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4d7fe1a2-3530-4188-b364-4f0ec9d861dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In 1992 there was the SAS (Statement on Auditing Standards) 70 and then there was a transition to the\r
ISAE 3402 / SSAE16 which is based on the SSAE 16 and is an analysis and evaluation standard\r
(assurance). Finally, the standard was published by The International Auditing and Assurance Standards\r
Board (IAASB) in December 2009.  Therefore we can state that ISAE 3402 has a widespread market acceptance.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 history:\r
https://www.isae3402.com/ISAE3402_history'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d07f1ced-88f5-4b21-b143-5be60d732c21 .

camssa:4d8043cd-92d7-45c6-9a27-d033c796c44a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4a006ad6785e066d16c13daf48a60ee43ec33d1de1b06613c8e656ccf330a6d5 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4d841c01-fbc7-4874-8284-5cf85bae41cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:4d8a6a16-a0c4-490d-a464-2e99937b0024 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DPV is not related to the authenticity and authenticathion of the agents involved in data transactions, therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffdf3aef-4988-44ec-a5c8-545a87da4d85 .

camssa:4d8f1902-fa63-47a0-8c02-61113530a6a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of RegOrg as a data model does not hamper the scalability of systems. The use of existing data models for the development of common information systems facilitates the development of those systems and improves their interoperability. Moreover, RegOrg facilitates information exchange between business registers.\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e367fadc-2210-4eaa-9c07-2c944a5109d6 .

camssa:4d95f99d-bde7-4506-9323-fa86effb6d5a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are several existing documents and studies assessing SAML 2.0 features and capabilities and effectiveness. Broadly speaking, the studies are focused on the capability to enable Single Sign-on and its benefits. \r
\r
Researchgate analysis on SAML2.0 Reference:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221609828_Formal_analysis_of_SAML_20_web_browser_single_sign-on\r
\r
Researchgate on Single Sign-on Auth Reference:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/45872317_Web_single_sign-on_authentication_using_SAML'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df4351f6-beb8-498f-9d47-2df93cf9f9aa .

camssa:4d9be542-8ff2-49e2-a2e4-fee26efe4399 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:4da57071-a4b2-453e-8bc2-a89d3d8a84d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is a key enabler for digital transactions across borders ensuring the trustworthiness of data being exchanged. This fact helps to avoid the non-digital data exchange allowing the reduction of administrative burden. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f2f0c239-a1c5-4849-92c9-98730aa1e035 .

camssa:4da8bf2e-7f87-4f03-a06f-7d1ffd6a5f77 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TS 119 614-1 is a testing conformance suite that can be applied in any domain and context where the \r
exchange of documents is required. Therefore, the specification is usable beyond any business-specific \r
domain and can be used in any kind of organisation.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:362b22f6-cea3-4006-ad41-877dc0bf873c .

camssa:4db1d06d-de7b-423d-ba29-c1ee01b05efd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4db7988e-a2b7-4cbb-a7c6-32673127c332 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:4dc0245b-15ab-4f2f-9723-d2b5d69ef261 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:4dc3d83e-b23e-480b-b16d-e61ae1113734 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'FTP allows public administration to exchange information and therefore to avoid requesting standard information to citizens or businesses several times. \r
\r
FTP is used by MAGA, an initiative from the Flemish Region of Belgium consisting in a common platform for data reuse between administrations.\r
\r
Magda Solution Reference: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/magda-platform/about\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\r
\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3fa4c52-5e70-4bc2-92d5-0e13686db68b .

camssa:4dc64b93-125d-46ca-815d-37fa5869e1f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SHACL specification documentation states that the only mandatory implementation is SHACL Core, while other components can be implemented separately. In this context, SHACL Core includes essential features for representing shapes, constraints, and targets.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27c5a0ed-174b-4b5f-a16a-81888d91ea4c .

camssa:4dc73f63-713f-4988-ba7a-7effb6bd5b11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SFIA is not related to data portability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:78deed63-760a-47e1-bd01-3efb57061a59 .

camssa:4dca544d-ab35-4692-b3e9-d1c18a60c2a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 9 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. Some examples of Member States including IPv6 on their catalogues are Spain, Sweden, France or Germany. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8950d795-4cb9-4da0-bf0c-bf3331f643a6 .

camssa:4dcc2189-5685-4916-8648-fe6ae9e81fd6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4dcf3e4e-38cb-4aaf-86c6-6e4b153a5daa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although MIME itself does not provide means for data confidentiality, its security extension mechanism (S/MIME) is a powerful tool for implementing data confidentiality features in email communication. It leverages cryptographic techniques to protect the content of emails and attachments, ensuring that sensitive information remains confidential and secure during transmission and storage.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
S/MIME specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:231c69c0-5d4d-49ac-97e6-476cd6ae1781 .

camssa:4ddb8efc-4b24-4334-bdc4-11eaa0f153f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By using LDAP, the system administrator is prevented from providing several authentication accounts for accessing distributed directories, the user does not have to deal with several credentials. This fact helps to adapt the specification to user’s needs without hampering the scalability of systems._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60dc5122-1957-4006-9bf9-f0fb535e59f6 .

camssa:4dde5686-63d3-48c7-b90f-95e00f20d59a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "RDF is built around specifications as XML or URL (URI). Even though, both web standards are well known and widely extended avoiding interoperability hampering."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c5490f7-c534-44d6-bc13-30bc2875744a .

camssa:4de450fb-c7b8-4b62-be8a-4f1b55d0f709 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV is independent of any specification and can be implemented without relying on other technologies.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0722702c-6909-49e2-95f2-3f096971e2f7 .

camssa:4de85f7d-046d-4b1d-ba5c-39030aac985f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4ded25f9-85a4-4f10-b971-63d6c56ad0d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ddcde46e-a948-4cfd-876d-757b0466dff7 .

camssa:4ded5b9c-b31b-4602-8e62-0ff7aa82e987 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As one of the official European Organisation for standardisation, ETSI standards are compliant with the European Standardisation Regulation 1025/2012. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/about/etsi-in-europe"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d433bd2-536d-41be-82ce-ac56850826ae .

camssa:4df5e511-a809-4aa4-bbda-8d6f72f8db99 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4dfae94b-8a5f-4658-bde9-c5a66d23d068 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Universal Business Language (UBL) Standard, version 2.1, has been designated by the European Commission as one of the first consortium standards officially eligible for referencing in tenders from public administrations. Still UBL is not considered a European standard although it is recoginzed as such.\r
\r
COMMISSION IMPLEMENTING DECISION of 31 October 2014 on the identification of Universal Business Language version 2.1 for referencing in public procurement:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/ES/TXT/?qid=1657095448506&uri=CELEX:32014D0771'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cffc87bb-5e8b-4c03-92fc-db4c205e8927 .

camssa:4dfddde1-d2e3-41d0-b596-8e21d3ecdaf9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CPOV is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:270e499f-d945-489d-89b6-9f6b293bff31 .

camssa:4e000cc2-4f0f-4c36-8536-6a09c804426f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification cannot be implemented partially. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bce2add5-c396-446c-8337-ead76ae775a2 .

camssa:4e048d65-e113-40f6-aa84-87176c3741ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 allows for extension to accommodate additional requirements or specific use cases beyond its scope. Extension enables organizations to address unique data management needs, industry-specific considerations, and emerging technologies, while maintaining compatibility with the core principles of the standard.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fbaa783-37e5-42d2-a6cc-298b29a2d27f .

camssa:4e05c61c-07ac-4489-a096-87fcd3102bf5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4e05dd2e-2141-41b0-ae97-447772e5f3aa a cav:Score,
