    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:4e064930-1a8a-4a55-b40c-a2972684d626 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Executive Committee has to review and co-ordinate the progress of the TCs and, from time to time, review the terms of reference given to Technical Committees. \r
\r
In addition, the Technical Committee shall review and approve the minutes of the preceding meeting. The minutes, after approval, shall constitute the official record of the meeting of a TC\r
\r
See:\r
http://www.ecma-international.org/memento/policies.htm"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:938c7fb5-55bd-4f31-bfba-3d0baebd801e .

camssa:4e082547-48bc-45d1-9dc6-88c94948c0d0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:4e0a88ab-ba6c-454c-ac95-9a655de9c462 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs are persistent and can be updated and reusable in many situations. In this way, if the controller of a web page or any other web resource wants to assign it a persistent, cryptographically verifiable identifier, the controller can give it a DID. Furthermore, in the DID document, the author can include the "alsoKnownAs" property pointing to the current URL of the blog, and make DID upgradable.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#assigning-dids-to-existing-web-resources'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e971b6b-8eb8-497c-a5ed-845b7b85b06a .

camssa:4e12b812-850a-486d-a737-dfecfcb5fdfb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4e246ac7-92c8-475a-806f-04421c7a5431 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI’s Intellectual Property Rights Policy is based on Standard Essential Patents (SEP). The policy implemented by the standardisation organisation seeks to reduce risks and ensure that the standards are available under (F) RAND basis and Royalty-free, it means with no cost or fee to be paid when possible. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0233d8e6-3e5e-4593-801a-15edef8d1ac5 .

camssa:4e2766e3-fa61-4b1a-a8b3-849f8d0fc2dd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4e286979-c04b-45ed-b6cf-01111209e4ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Examples of public institutions or organisations are provided in in the criteria 1. (e.g EMBL European Bioinformatics Institute, and Australian Center for Plant Functional Genomics)"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:235ffe36-012c-4654-b01a-7b0aa49a3263 .

camssa:4e29cdbf-7ea8-46e7-8222-fcc2e10d2d14 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
