camssa:4e6ca639-6de7-4fac-9825-6961bfdb81c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XHTML appears from the reformulation of HTML4 using XML. XHTML 1.0 became a World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) recommendation on 26 January 2000. There have been multiple updates with new versions of XHTML, for example in XHTML 1.1 became a W3C recommendation on 31 May 2001. There is a development of XHTML5 which is an XML adaptation of the HTML5 specification. This fact proves that the specification is mature enough for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
XHTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9eecd417-04e5-4576-8a3f-d950b3fcd870 .

camssa:4e73089c-05c9-43f4-b491-b8e9b8049f3d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4e733230-7cbd-4969-b984-ceb1618d0079 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not related to enabling long-term preservation of data/information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b07c6e66-267c-4962-9a58-ffea31e87b63 .

camssa:4e738c05-baf2-409f-a91f-d98edb98606a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows for customisation. The specification is designed to be modular and flexible, which enables implementers to develop their own extensions or customisations to meet specific requirements.\r
\r
Implementers can customise the specification by adding the elements they developed or extensions that have been modified, attributes, or namespaces to the existing XML schema. They can also develop their own modules or components that extend or modify the behavior of the specification.\r
                                                     \r
AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:12801bf4-10a4-4492-bf10-554eb1aca0bf .

camssa:4e73ad0c-8db0-4083-bac3-ab555066a5f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP is meant to serve in the Internet of Things domain. Moreover, the specification is also available for its\r
use within a public administration service, for example in PDF signatures.\r
\r
OCSP reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560\r
\r
Adobe OCSP reference:\r
https://www.adobe.com/devnet-docs/acrobatetk/tools/QuickKeys/Acrobat_SigRevCheck_KeyAll.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:70f09d0a-cbb9-4ce6-b14d-eb8d4f7098bc .

camssa:4e73fd3e-ed18-42f2-ad90-be295fee0e8e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ab64f97c21ac8b84c75d6f52a89765b1c8fd1856d2d2060926d05e94f306a88d ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4e7536cc-afad-423d-8004-67a9178e5558 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Extensible Forms Description Language (XFDL) is a useful specification for creating, processing, and rendering electronic forms and documents. Moreover, it can also be useful for addressing some issues related to conducting electronic commerce on the Web. However, other newer and easier-to-implement specifications have been developed to perform these functions. Therefore, although XFDL is still in use for addressing functions related to e-commerce, it is not the preferred specification.

XFDL for e-commerce:
https://drdobbs.com/web-development/xfdl-the-extensible-forms-description-la/184411136

"Sustainability of Digital Formats: Planning for Library of Congress Collections" repport:
https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000580.shtml

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:249a209a-975b-4fb6-bd5b-fe4ef75af817 .

camssa:4e77ffa7-5ef8-4f18-a35d-38792e5c80c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is the Accessible Rich Internet Applications Working Group (ARIA WG) which aims to develop technologies that improve the accessibility of web content for people with disabilities, which includes the continued development of WAI-ARIA. Participating in the WG requires a W3C account.\r
\r
W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
ARIA Working Group reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2021/Process-20211102/#groups'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5925dde3-0faa-43d8-b322-1995cfbbdbf6 .

camssa:4e7bcb32-2fd1-4777-bc0c-1862ebe3251c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:4e8f06af-828d-4407-8159-2804e28c391a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI is an initiative aimed at improving the interoperability of legal information within the European Union. It
provides a common framework for identifying and referencing legal documents across different jurisdictions.
ELI is often used as a best practice and guideline rather than a formal standard.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ccfe3cc-5844-420d-96bf-0edcd2cf7c69 .

camssa:4e9412f1-5991-4cea-b9c2-1993f6df533c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4e98f946-e5a2-4c81-ad7a-bc20a488aa8a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard includes mechanisms that help guarantee data accuracy, such as data encryption. By encrypting information, it can help ensure that data has not been altered by an unauthorised user since it was sent.

Geeksforgeeks AES reference:
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/advanced-encryption-standard-aes/

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47689ee3-c52b-46aa-a8de-b87cc2b057a9 .

camssa:4e9b643d-a55b-4d28-afac-388d0dcaea0d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:4ea670db-5268-4874-8306-0aa40baf143d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1624157830122d60825aa5aa88ab70d0b140b2e7e510086699f9a9773efef6bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:4eaa4509-c1bb-4542-bb19-5fd47d4c0531 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary states that a publisher may use any of the terms defined in this document encoded in any technology although RDF and XML are preferred. This indicates that while RDF and XML are preferred, the specification does not mandate their use, making it usable across different technologies.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:182246aa-cbf3-4bd5-b52e-b09660e38e1e .

camssa:4eae2a9b-c18a-4f6b-8d4e-38176b842222 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
