camssa:50674dc0-8c0e-45cc-bbc0-724b896c77db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-BPEL is not related  to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76bb69ff-9e3a-4d1a-a6c0-628d5ff774a1 .

camssa:506c2c13-d500-43d5-b67b-d03774c55450 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The first drafts of XBRL GL were developed in 1999 by the chief architect who contributed the work to XBRL.\r
Development and implementation of pre-recommendation status versions followed shortly after (See\r
http://www.xbrl.org/business/companies/breathing-new-life-into-old-systems.pdf from 2004, for example).\r
The standards process within XBRL led to the first official version in 2005.\r
The Specification was not developed in a background. Its chief architect and other participants also\r
contributed to virtually all other Specifications in overlapping space, including UN/CEFACT Accounting and\r
Audit artefacts, OECD Standard Audit File for Taxation (SAF-T), ISO/TC 295’s Audit Data Collection\r
specification ISO 21378:2019, AICPA Audit Data Standards, and others, each focusing on some specific\r
area or compliance. This collaboration was to encourage harmonization and help in proving the capabilities\r
of XBRL GL.\r
\r
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2007-04-17/GLFramework-REC-2007-04-17.htm\r
\r
All versions: https://specifications.xbrl.org/spec-group-index-xbrl-gl.html\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:212c4401-e63b-4038-9de8-1b39c9fa33b9 .

camssa:506c5488-6ae9-40db-8160-9e59d3cf0078 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS, as a vocabulary for the description of assets included within a Repository (Catalogue), it can be used to define Interoperability Solutions catalogues, beyond the eGovernement scope. \r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d850fb8f-481c-45c9-bfad-771019e87553 .

camssa:506cd4d9-b876-477a-a81b-c9f8ab35669c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard itself does not define a formal access control system with explicit roles and permissions. However, the encryption it provides acts as an effective access control by restricting data access to those who possess the decryption key.

Geeksforgeeks AES reference:
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/advanced-encryption-standard-aes/

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:468c3821-a64a-4700-b79b-4f77d6f06836 .

