        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose Member State NIF 
has a high performance on interoperability according to NIFO factsheets.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c36541c2-2490-4959-9e01-3a651142aec8 .

camssa:509e7db2-c935-42b1-9e7b-e3d130d89a92 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """' Given that a verifiable credential often contains personally identifiable information (PII), implementers are strongly advised to use mechanisms while storing and transporting verifiable credentials that protect the data from those who should not access it. Mechanisms that could be considered include Transport Layer Security (TLS) or other means of encrypting the data while in transit, as well as encryption or data access control mechanisms to protect the data in a verifiable credential while at rest.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials Privacy Considerations: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/#privacy-considerations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7446669-67e2-4911-a047-55eb3a04a223 .

camssa:50a87cb0-d012-4672-bfcd-27d9da47bc2a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:50ac5eb8-e1de-4e07-b761-1b8f0201b908 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:50acb0e6-4d21-4c88-bbf9-9929ee304301 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 is a messaging protocol for exchanging information in a structured way, it uses XML for its message format. As the protocol is a messaging system for exchanging information in a structured way, it helps to promote the visibility and comprehensibility of the administrative rules. In addition, it is a key enabler for web services reuse across borders along with UDDI and WSDL. \r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  \r
\r
Differences in SOAP Versions:\r
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSAW57_8.5.5/com.ibm.websphere.nd.multiplatform.doc/ae/cwbs_soapverdiffs.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9bc8bdcd-9e70-4d98-be98-00a2885a04ab .

camssa:50b1233b-7c26-4d9e-b793-43d99bf3bcbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WS-BPEL does not directly conform with the main conditions to publish data as open data. However, this specification can be used for the consumption of open data by the definition of web services business process. \r
 \r
WS-BPEL OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html \r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db3102ef-48fb-4c1c-ae2e-568e69e94193 .

camssa:50b383fb-5907-4b2c-baa3-fceed7040a50 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:50b3b0b1-89fc-4c21-b3b0-6e8984381e48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Various EU Member States have  are considering adoption the specification as their standard for the creation and publication of legal documents in a machine-readable format. \r
\r
AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:014d755d-f733-4e9e-a62c-b474352f281c .

camssa:50b56dd4-c596-4232-b535-1932a07a13aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not foresee any support for multilingualism. Nevertheless, it does mention that cloud computing services may have operational policies such as requirements for support of minority user languages.\r
\r
Some territories also have strict laws and regulations around correct use of character sets in user \r
interfaces (notably Asian characters and their usage), legal requirements to support mandatory “official” \r
languages (some of which might have few real speakers).\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d46f2088-e17f-4b67-86c0-345e39de374b .

camssa:50b5b799-60b3-4ebc-b71e-449f46809f20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XAdES does not provide a cross sector reusable data model per se. The specification provides a set of conformance level for the basic features in the context of the European Internal Market. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e2919f3f-924d-46a8-aebf-bbe3fb042a6f .

camssa:50b6c643-0b3c-4b17-ae5a-f2c9e0aba645 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAIS can indirectly help ensure data processing accuracy by promoting metadata quality controls, data integrity checks or preservation planning.  Nonetheless, OAIS specification does not give specific provisions to perform them.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c97bc689-716f-44b9-9b9f-9346da7ed47d .

camssa:50b6dbd1-a6ab-40cd-b3e1-c8a17827da3d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """12 Member States are recommending HTML in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are Croatia, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Greece, Malta, Norway, Poland, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden and UK.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05bf7fa6-b78a-4776-b8f0-156cc306cbab .

camssa:50b8dfd5-a8b4-4b30-9b0f-83f39b69e957 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org may contribute and promote the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data and services on the web. The specification promotes schemas for structured data (e.g. services, data) enabling potential users to find and use such data as services or relevant information. Up to date, there is no evidence of schema.org as a promising enabler of visibility, but there are ongoing projects such as the Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe (Schema.org profile of DCAT-AP, or DCAT-AP-SDO) that are working in this direction.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'Documentation' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/documents.html\r
\r
DCAT-AP reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dcat-ap\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:14d82d5c-6167-475e-baf8-8fdb3aa0e033 .

camssa:50bd9f45-b172-4dc4-9cc5-ecc57acc76de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion of PDF/A within any European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8fc4aca6-b4b0-40dd-9a8c-5f44ab26c3f4 .

camssa:50bddd40-9481-4848-9ae8-6e71003cbf51 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C Best Practices is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
