camssa:5119134f-862c-4673-8f02-213475b066e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDA specification and recommendation processes are open from inception. Individual membership to RDA is free and open to all, as long as individuals subscribe to the RDA Guiding Principles (https://rd-alliance.org/about/get-involved.html):\r
• Openness – Membership is open to all interested individuals who subscribe to the RDA’s Guiding Principles. RDA community meetings and processes are open, and the deliverables of RDA Working Groups will be publicly disseminated.\r
• Consensus – The RDA moves forward by achieving consensus among its membership. RDA processes and procedures include appropriate mechanisms to resolve conflicts.\r
• Balance – The RDA seeks to promote balanced representation of its membership and stakeholder communities.\r
• Harmonization – The RDA works to achieve harmonization across data standards, policies, technologies, infrastructure, and communities.\r
• Community-driven – The RDA is a public, community-driven body constituted of volunteer members and organizations, supported by the RDA Secretariat.\r
• Non-profit - RDA does not promote, endorse, or sell commercial products, technologies, or services.\r
\r
Organisations may join RDA as members for an annual fee. Full details are provided at https://rd-alliance.org/organisation/rda-organisation-affiliate-members/rda-organisational-membership.html\r
\r
RDA Specifications, upon delivery, are assessed by the RDA Technical Advisory Board (TAB) and feedback / comments are given. All outputs go through an open and transparent Request for Comments process of 1 month on the RDA web platform. Details on the process are available at - https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/creating-and-managing-rda-groups/working-group-outputs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f10ed034-fe68-491d-809d-33c440c13e59 .

