camssa:51ce547c-af7a-4a54-a649-8c28e8c2804c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612  is a component derived from the actions implemented based on the Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market. This regulation aims to enhance interoperability when it comes to the trust services of e-signatures in the European context.  \r
\r
Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3f27c0a-8253-4837-8e68-54072cc42b49 .

camssa:51d0e8b2-93b0-463f-97e7-9a574b0db310 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is not a European Standard itself. Instead, it is a standardized language for expressing permissions, obligations, and constraints for digital content and services. Instead, ODRL is an open standard that has been developed by a community of stakeholders with a focus on providing a common framework for expressing digital rights.\r
\r
ODRL Community Group Home page:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/odrl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:18358d21-ee03-4120-b5f3-2b54ea602dab .

camssa:51d17dfd-402b-4f34-9884-7ecb4fa82866 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent from any specific tecnology. However, its serialisation is carried out using three different formats such as RDF, JASON-LD, and XML. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50772a30-8373-474e-abd8-8a34456f2685 .

camssa:51d20131-aadf-480b-a008-1de5aa8fbc3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While PROV can provide valuable insights into the lineage and relationships of administrative procedures and services, the comprehensibility of these elements requires consideration of other factors beyond the scope of the PROV family of documents.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ad31151-f96a-483e-9f07-5c397fb45e40 .

camssa:51d2c71f-ad2e-4f19-96c1-3026a90c6865 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a64b01ca9e737c550b205ba3a8a46b3fcfc9447b648ba8ef15d62d3ada26141 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:51d64ea3-e7a1-4ce3-9671-5933a88108d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:444be9d8-22c1-4f9c-b566-2c6d102d41e1 .

camssa:51daa74c-2b78-4692-8657-3f3046b69852 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification aims to provide a format for long-term storage and access to parliamentary, legislative and judicial documents that allows search, interpretation and visualization of documents. Therefore, LegalDocML can support and foster the long-term preservation of electronic records, especially legal texts.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2893a140-4e36-4511-affc-b0e4f7d4789d .

camssa:51db6043-0221-450b-8418-414fc4efe6e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of CIM NGSI-LD API is often evaluated through various means, including practical implementations and pilot projects. For instance, a 2021-paper by ETSI is intended to complement the NGSI-LD information model normative specification, it is also intended to be complementary to the NGSI-LD Primer, which mainly explains how to use the NGSI-LD API in a more “hands-on” practical way, especially for the initial use cases considered location, which demonstrates the effectiveness of CIM NGSI-LD API.

Guidelines for Modelling with NGSI-LD: 
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Gilles-Privat/publication/349928709_Guidelines_for_Modelling_with_NGSI-LD_ETSI_White_Paper/links/6047dca2299bf1e07869576b/Guidelines-for-Modelling-with-NGSI-LD-ETSI-White-Paper.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03f2f826-9625-4d3e-83db-830bc13f7a6b .

