camssa:525b5eda-0073-4bac-b287-6e5e6a9b9480 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/\r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f306e486-f257-476a-ac25-691a745ca878 .

camssa:525d795f-b991-4264-a0ed-27bb59ebd65d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:525deced-0ddd-4066-a506-c703cb23dffb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e5a9e0d-a895-44d9-a3ab-3c9c059eb0b4 .

camssa:5262337d-3830-4de1-9ee7-8928430f432c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Joinup offers several services that aim to help e-Government professionals share their experience with each 
other. Joinup supports them to find, choose, re-use, develop and implement interoperability solutions. DQV
is mentioned in some Joinup entries as a discussion topic, although is not distributed in the platform.

DQV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/access-base-registries/solution/abr-bregdcat-ap/discussion/issue-06-quality-datasets'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b04f157-b4c3-4341-ba8b-99277f22a1cd .

camssa:526251de-dd2e-42c1-8002-9c681e3a7eac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the publication of data as Linked Open Data. Therefore, e-Delivery SMP 1.10 is not fostering the publication of Linked Open Data. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ae6907f-22e9-4991-9d54-353f97c15b48 .

camssa:5263ce85-7040-466f-a49c-61e90cfbd26b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:52666104-a763-4bc2-bdbe-dda07b8b5611 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard provides a standardised method for protecting data by encrypting it in a common format. This standard facilitates collaboration by ensuring data is encrypted and decrypted uniformly. An example can be found looking at VeraCrypt project. The aim of this initiative is to encrypt partitions or storafe devices, in an automatic and fast manner.

VeraCrypt AES project:
https://veracrypt.eu/en/Home.html

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d8fdbd8f-7035-442e-b601-6377ef523213 .

camssa:526aae0b-7891-40e0-869b-99daacd0004d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Besides CELAR and Indigo projects, the European Union is committed to the development of open source utilities that can be used in industry as well as in research. It is the case of the RADON project, where TOSCA is used as the project's Infrastructure as code (IaC) format centerstage.\r
\r
RADON project reference: \r
https://radon-h2020.eu/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c891427-ce70-4dd9-ae5c-be7e55e8fd3f .

camssa:526dcdc5-bdba-4bdc-9026-557455b558c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Registered Organization Vocabulary is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of a legal entity. It facilitates the information exchange between business sectors and organisations, fostering the digitization of the administrations' transaction. Therefore, it reduces the administrative burden by avoiding the exchange of non-digital documents.\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dee73599-438a-4afe-96d5-0aec259f0806 .

camssa:5272fb48-cfd3-4d73-bc02-64179b4e1b19 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

