camssa:52a8a29b-614e-4bdc-a0f6-69435637643d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The XACML specification includes data structures and models that can be considered as reusable models for establishing data policies, the data involved and the processes involved.\r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4bfca259-9a63-45b1-8cc2-55d18a06c53e .

camssa:52bbc652-25e5-411f-a5e0-ce911cca4b63 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There are no existing European standards with market uptake covering the same area as RPKI."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:858b4448-0ac9-4d17-b2c6-0db3f8684f70 .

camssa:52c07ff3-7374-4fea-958f-993ef287747f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP can facilitate digital communication and online services in several ways. It helps reduce network usage and latency when accessing online public service portals, ensuring faster and more efficient service delivery. The caching mechanism allows for the storage and reuse of data, which decreases the number of requests sent to servers. This not only improves performance but also reduces the load on the server side, enhancing reliable access to public services.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Caching, RFC 9111 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0aa8fef-de66-43b2-98c0-fc5c5d1b1157 .

camssa:52c29a5f-47c2-4eef-81eb-b32d1e7f8b0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are already existing tools for testing the implementation of XACML polocies. The Security Pool Policy allow to check for enhancements in a XACML implementation. Also, a tool known as WS2 Identity Server is available under its own licence to allow the testing of XACML implementations. \r
\r
WS2 Identity Server\r
https://docs.wso2.com/display/IS541/Using+the+XACML+TryIt+Tool"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ac71950-769d-4f79-944c-fd367a99092f .

camssa:52c440bc-3a7e-449a-ab04-c86aca9eb780 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:52c4592e-755c-4fd7-8ad2-8de61792e53d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification offers a standardised format for exchanging messages between users. In this context, the ebXML specification also facilitates business collaborations through the exchange of XML documents in a standardised format.

ebXML interoperability:
https://www.tutorialspoint.com/ebxml/ebxml_quick_guide.htm

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e2673e68-76ec-45d3-be80-4de8afd90be7 .

camssa:52c7cd97-92ab-4a36-9ecd-1a3af95712b0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

