camssa:52dbcd39-5c36-4be8-bfb8-83f1680bb9da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Extensible Forms Description Language is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, Extensible Forms Description Language can define the interoperability aspects of the "Forms Management" ABB of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v610

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27ffa3f0-b327-4c38-aa8e-b6f2224db0c4 .

camssa:52dcee3b-9f86-4e05-852d-040d6dd3d33c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DPV is not related to data processing accuracy, therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a77dea6d-9216-4574-9354-d6f6fd4cd663 .

camssa:52dd6ea0-9966-4b4e-b798-be953022129b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI specification is supported by the ELI Task Force, which includes representatives from multiple
European countries. The ELI TF, which consists of European countries that have implemented ELI, is
responsible for defining ELI-related specifications and ensuring their future evolution.

This community is public and its work, including the ELI specifications and best practice guides, is freely
accessible.

ELI Task Force reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

ELI Best Practices reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/digital-skills-public-sector/solution/interoperable-europe-academy
/european-legislation-identifier'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:271b4719-fa24-448b-b4b0-5096073d1b47 .

camssa:52e2081a-fded-4890-8f7a-cdf16f93c0ad a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:52e45326-dcc4-4e5f-bee1-074e2db1f8ba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:52ed161d-efc0-40e3-9003-2bbf3d194abf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:52ef632e-5f6a-46b1-b57d-2aec46c7ebe9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. The ODRL \r
community provides forums for discussion, collaboration, and sharing of best practices related to the \r
implementation and use of ODRL.\r
\r
W3C Consortium home page: \r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/\r
\r
ODRL Community:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/odrl/\r
\r
W3C Working Group Github space: \r
https://github.com/w3c/odrl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba71b6df-0ba0-4bd2-950f-f85bf4d5edfd .

camssa:52f06d6f-abbb-4405-9cff-7615dd60b004 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XML is to store, transport and  exchange data through interoperable systems. Moreover, XML defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a human-readable format and machine-readable format enhancing the reusability of data and stimulating the interoperability of systems and services.  \r
\r
Additionally, W3C develops its specification independently from any vendor. Thus, the adoption of XML does not hamper the data portability of data expressed with it. In fact, the adoption of XML fosters data portability, especially between REST APIs.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f30e9fc-19f9-4b46-9ce7-dacb46681b7f .

camssa:52f07f56-cf19-4d27-984c-fa604d886a2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"IPv6 can work with VPN's to guarantee restrictions who can access to information. One example is the OpenVPN, which supports IPv6 natively, and is highly configurable with extensive control options. Moreover, the ACL functionality in IPv6 helps to establish an access control.

Access Control Lists for IPv6 reference:
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/routers/ios/config/17-x/sec-vpn/b-security-vpn/m_ip6-acls-xe.html#GUID-C7F3B9EF-CD1E-45E4-8A48-F301C746FAC1

OpenVPN reference:
https://support.openvpn.com/hc/en-us/articles/17891771293083-Access-Server-Enable-and-configure-IPv6-to-transport-IPv6-packets-through-the-VPN-tunnel\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:351e8ea9-1053-407f-8cfd-46c6c6cce87c .

camssa:53029994-cd98-435d-ba89-272d8b119cd4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of ISO 639-2 is not related to the exposure of interfaces to access public administrations' services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ISO 639-2 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/4767.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f29ac8b7-9575-4fab-a043-2a3a60cf8893 .

camssa:5306393f-23e5-427e-bfc9-9a8c350801ed a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:530f52f8-7eb4-44e5-8f17-95f39dc4b35a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the sum of all hardware and software components that make up the environment in which the NFV is deployed, the NFVI addresses security aspects through different standardised modules.\r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview section 6.7:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36d62d99-ae39-45a1-8cf5-448631dac2c3 .

camssa:5311262a-1b88-42b1-8718-d826dcf4f721 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As SMP is maintained by OASIS which is an international community developing open standards, it encourages people to join and contribute to the development and maintenance of old and new specifications and share their data once a specification its finished on European platforms and the eDelivery User Community.\r
\r
OASIS Community Reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/join-2/\r
\r
eDelivery User Community: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/EDELCOMMUNITY/eDelivery+User+Community'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca4b55ca-cd36-45f2-96fa-bfdecbbf5346 .

camssa:53121666-356c-4426-a2d8-13f7a17de294 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OGC TrainingDML-AI is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose
Member State National Interoperability Framework has a high performance on interoperability according to
NIFO factsheets.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef65b38a-9496-486e-bb04-ebdbf4ac1ac9 .

camssa:53160156-032d-4731-8b13-b6396a23a70a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is maintained by the Platform Industrie 4.0 and has a dedicated working group which is open to contribution on github.

Asset Administration Shell (AAS) Github 
https://github.com/admin-shell-io/aas-specs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:67d119d1-4121-4b58-8475-f05fadb0e9c9 .

camssa:5318f7da-f10c-46ca-a637-ccb862a2b854 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5320e6c3-f3b8-4aa6-b508-2b1b2b7f1a43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "'The XML specification itself does not directly address the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations or any specific data privacy concerns. XML is a markup language designed for the structuring and representation of data, allowing for the exchange and storage of information in a standardized format. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.'"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1c03d883-3480-4500-b98f-97eeefb6e7e0 .

camssa:532c4997-1928-45e7-8cee-747c5814483c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 is recognised by the Multi-Stakeholder Platform on ICT Standardisation of the European Commission.
This recognition also underscores the role of TLS 1.3 in advancing trusted communication within European cross-border services, aligning with the EU’s commitment to robust cybersecurity frameworks.

European Multi-Stakeholder Platform on ICT Standardisation:
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/multi-stakeholder-platform-ict-standardisation

Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2017/2288 of 11 December 2017 on the identification of ICT Technical Specifications for referencing in public procurement Reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32017D2288'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a435d152-2fcc-4992-b1af-549dedd60ade .

camssa:5333ecc1-9b05-4a95-8639-36479d3e76de a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:53390702-2473-4012-92c9-26fc43e6376b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:5342a9ef-699a-413b-af58-d1e76e6f2db6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs is included in the EUOS, the EU Observatory for ICT Standardisation. Moreover it is also included in the Data Space Support Center (DSSC) Standards catalogue, where it covers the trust layer.

EUOS repository:
https://www.standict.eu/standards-repository/decentralized-identifiers-dids-v10-core-architecture-data-model-and

DSSC standards catalogue:
https://dssc.eu/space/SE1/185794711/Data+Sovereignty+and+Trust+standards+and+technologies+landscape'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6b17fbd-fd35-44fa-9811-ee830342bd27 .

camssa:53489aac-91de-4a94-8f6c-12cc04cb3121 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDA specification and recommendation processes are open from inception. Individual membership to RDA is free and open to all, as long as individuals subscribe to the RDA Guiding Principles (https://rd-alliance.org/about/get-involved.html):\r
• Openness – Membership is open to all interested individuals who subscribe to the RDA’s Guiding Principles. RDA community meetings and processes are open, and the deliverables of RDA Working Groups will be publicly disseminated.\r
• Consensus – The RDA moves forward by achieving consensus among its membership. RDA processes and procedures include appropriate mechanisms to resolve conflicts.\r
• Balance – The RDA seeks to promote balanced representation of its membership and stakeholder communities.\r
• Harmonization – The RDA works to achieve harmonization across data standards, policies, technologies, infrastructure, and communities.\r
• Community-driven – The RDA is a public, community-driven body constituted of volunteer members and organizations, supported by the RDA Secretariat.\r
• Non-profit - RDA does not promote, endorse, or sell commercial products, technologies, or services.\r
\r
Organisations may join RDA as members for an annual fee. Full details are provided at https://rd-alliance.org/organisation/rda-organisation-affiliate-members/rda-organisational-membership.html\r
\r
RDA Specifications, upon delivery, are assessed by the RDA Technical Advisory Board (TAB) and feedback / comments are given. All outputs go through an open and transparent Request for Comments process of 1 month on the RDA web platform. Details on the process are available at - https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/creating-and-managing-rda-groups/working-group-outputs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e89457f-368c-4bac-a565-8dc4821f1786 .

