camssa:53f6ab91-3615-464a-aff6-8ac4e96a7493 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a specification created to provide a standard-way to express credentials on the Web, there are several features that ensure the alignment with this definition. One example is the credential metadata, which contains crucial information about the credential itself, such as the credential type, issue date, and expiration date. Another example would be proofs like a digital signature, ensuring that the credential genuinely originates from the claimed issuer and has remained untampered. These facts increase the reliability of the exchanged data.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0101e66f-0c20-496f-b1a0-56cd33e928e0 .

camssa:54071ec1-08c5-4826-98f7-a918c28ccf69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a protocol for mantaining and accessing Directory Services, LDAP is a useful tool to display of user information in a readable manner. Comprehensibility of data therefore is supported by the fact that it permits to access user information in the network in a structured, human-readable manner.

LDAP Directory Information Models:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4512

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ebfdcee2-3d65-4a0b-813b-3d5c829c0e66 .

camssa:5410f1b7-6db1-4ec1-ab32-ba510b592f76 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:541575c1-35ed-4980-9eee-cfceef25badd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of XSLT is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f2b4208-d6f1-4daa-8068-52f220b4e2bd .

camssa:54228b13-1ae6-4863-85f6-e22b05d13c49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAMM provides an effective and measurable way for all types of organizations to analyze and improve their software security posture. Applying the model, the organisation can develop and improve software applications in terms of security. Therefore, the specification can be used within the creation and maintenance of innovative solutions since security is a key aspect.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb5e0aea-acb8-4857-83c2-b68650700593 .

camssa:54283783-8437-46d9-90f4-37f827e3340c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:543268af-a4cf-4ccc-b96e-71a438c5144e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:5432da2f-892f-43dc-87e9-dcc356775876 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAMM is a set of criteria that supports all types of organizations in developing and improving software solutions. It supports the complete software lifecycle and is technology and process agnostic, allowing its maximum reuse.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/ \r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3149acb-fb78-42f4-8751-c8ffd10e69fd .

camssa:54363e84-0839-40f8-87a9-f04f9c86f3b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is intended solely for documenting metadata related to public code projects and does not aim to support or regulate secure data exchange. It lacks provisions for security or privacy frameworks and does not establish protocols for handling sensitive data or ensuring secure communications. Therefore, its scope does not align with the data exchange security and privacy requirements outlined in EIF Recommendation 15.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3aae87b7-863e-48cd-b8b1-39738ea53daf .

camssa:543dab72-7607-44f8-90be-ec1c33ef217c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:54401036-a70c-4aec-b015-920103dff074 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UTF-8 is maintained by IETF which is an international community developing open standards.\r
\r
About IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/about/\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eea3810a-d28a-4e08-bc3e-569880c83181 .

camssa:54433662-8666-4c34-8a9f-b41682435173 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5839144ecfb6c41a2c3cf5c1e86a6b3ad7a9e3ec9c4efa5650a6e7b9e3586335 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:544562d6-417b-4083-9046-dc398bf54ca4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSD 1.1 is an open specification that can be used independently from other technologies or platforms. However, XSD 1.1 is defining datatypes which depend on definitions in XML and Namespaces in XML. This fact is not hampering the adoption of XSD as XML is worldwide adopted. \r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f96252f8-6987-4a0b-b734-2f48b4c5fbb8 .

camssa:5449dc55-761c-4966-8f24-731936993810 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the Core Location Vocabulary is to capture the fundamental characteristics of a location, represented as an address, a geographic name or geometry. It was developed from November 2011 until February 2012. It had some updates, and it was finally published in May 2012. This fact shows that CLV is mature enough for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da526670-b4a8-426b-a40a-a39ed13f4583 .

camssa:544ebee9-6753-40f1-9b4e-d9d8e8233dc6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No overlap has been detected with European standardisation organisations activities at EU level.\r
This conclusion is based on the work programme of CEN  and ETSI  as published on their respective websites, and on the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf68d5ed-788d-4398-b00a-7e72fa2a9dba .

camssa:5450ded7-cc15-4493-9f8d-f0350db9b0b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:545103d8-303b-4782-b19d-f6b21c5a969c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ASiC is included in the Dutch national catalogue of recommended specifications. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of the Netherlands is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da7708fd-eb3a-4ba5-a93a-4f9624220470 .

