        "65%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:5452f908-f0c0-4cb9-89c1-8f836aeac371 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification allows cross-domain single sign-on, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. By using SAML 2.0, the system administrator is prevented from providing several authentication tokens and, the user does not have to deal with several credentials. \r
In addition, the use of the specifications helps to enhance and foster digital communication between administrations and users avoiding the non-digital data exchange. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94c5140e-daac-4f5a-a755-71d6ee5f337f .

camssa:5454d86a-2fcc-4b0c-af54-009919fa8762 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:5456d612-d558-429b-9544-1eb8f7d3a46e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CSS is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8846e3f-6a3d-4528-b7c3-be662ae0b6d5 .

camssa:54583d47-b7f9-453a-9710-8d270d18875b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CPOV defines a data model for describing public organisations in the European Union. The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary addresses specific needs of businesses, public administrations and citizens across the European Union.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea1a4b86-0ffd-405b-bf5d-794a753f96bf .

camssa:545a559e-313f-42f6-966d-7a05974bd675 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """8 Member States are recommending LDAP in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are Croatia, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, Netherlands, Spain and Sweden.\r
 \r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b2410f2-a619-430f-93eb-70c036148901 .

camssa:5460a7bc-b536-4d26-ade1-72d37cf25120 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV is useful for modeling of business processes in public administrations. It CPSV and CPOV addresses the need for public administrations to describe their services and events in a common way. Moreover, the CPOV provides the ability to link public services to public organizations, hence defining which organization has the authority over specific public services. 

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary/distribution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary-version-100-pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2517753f-d229-44f7-ba15-a254adf24006 .

camssa:546dc78d-af8e-4b7d-a075-82ece9c669a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD 1.1 is defining the schema and datatypes in order to define and constraint the structures and content included in XML files. Moreover, XSD 1.1 is describing an abstract data model which provides details on the schema definition. Therefore, XSD is defining a cross-sector reusable data model. \r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema11-1/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0b7494a-99c8-467c-9d49-f9627a53d4c7 .

camssa:5475c9fe-b6a3-4456-8633-54430cb3ee03 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Data on the Web Best Practices was produced in 2004 by W3C, and it has the full support from the W3C group which is an international community where Member organizations, a full-time staff, and the public work together to develop Web standards.\r
\r
W3C Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b9abe7e-6536-41a9-8138-43e503641b8d .

