        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:54b4259a-f815-4494-9b81-f25de0761d56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The classification scheme outlined in ISO/IEC 19944-1 can be adapted and tailored to suit the specific needs and circumstances of an organization. This means that organizations can choose to implement certain elements or categories of the classification scheme that align with their data management objectives and priorities.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7b17e716-cfd0-4c69-b4fc-67e1a180d49f .

camssa:54bcb2b7-2870-40e2-870c-af47f1d79024 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Core Vocabularies allow you to choose properties according to the needs of an organization. In this way, if an Organization only needs to capture data on the organizational structure, it is not necessary to include other properties which captures data far from our interests.

CPOV partial implementations:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary/distribution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary-version-100-pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94a75df7-1f66-4320-9872-02998164497d .

camssa:54bf63d5-1b06-462e-a509-3e329a891c59 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CSV has documentation regarding Use Cases and Requirements which analyses its effectiveness & efficiency.\r
\r
CSV on the Web Use Case Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/csvw-ucr/     \r
      \r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e8e5302-6e7c-4e96-a8e0-1571d227040a .

camssa:54c1ced6-31a0-4930-9b96-0dfa13793909 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT supports the evolution and implementation  of European Public Services by enhancing the searchability and discoverability of datasets across borders. DCAT is an interoperability enabler.\r
                                                                                            \r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/     '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75dd3077-4110-4e68-8d78-7ca97bf4eb2c .

camssa:54c2fb64-466d-4cdb-8047-1d782e449507 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CAdES is not related to the publication of public data as open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7a7bbdd-b311-418e-b750-06999cc8ebc6 .

camssa:54c42c4b-10e7-4ba0-ae76-5117d743ba16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a063d52-680f-4c73-8985-4ae63819d788 .

camssa:54c52cf8-0ded-4810-a658-f0e3f0ead0b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42a2bb56-8417-4f05-9aef-d37a8693da64 .

camssa:54ca3281-6ab4-4337-a596-6a7fd0ed93e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At least 7 Member States are recommending HTTPS in their ICT National Catalogues.                                                                                          \r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f712c4a3-5868-42bd-834f-fe6f684f3825 .

