camssa:5559e783-3c67-45ca-aa28-6add4403b73b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XHTML fosters e-accessibility helping people with disabilities to understand and navigate through web and mobile web applications with friendly tools and proper information formats. \r
Moreover, the Regional Government of Bizkaia developed his website to promote the integration of groups with disabilities into the Public Administration of Bizkaia. They used XHTML 1.0 recommendations and CSS2.\r
\r
XHTML 1.0 implemented in e-accessability project:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/einclusion/document/eaccesibility-public-administration-bizkaia-bizkaianet"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a302049b-fe0f-4434-ac27-3a8840c36dd9 .

camssa:555a5b1e-f5f3-4803-9888-e036a4954770 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State that includes EN\\xa0319\\xa0422 in their national catalogue with its National \r
Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories: 1. Conceptual model for integrated \r
public services provision, 2. interoperability layers, and 3. interoperability principles.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a5c1ae4-f9e7-4e38-8276-24afe744e10e .

camssa:555b2eb5-a4a7-4056-8741-9145d53edd3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PNG is an image extension which allows visualizing and storing images. However, as they cannot be protected with a password or something, everyone who has access to a PNG file can visualize it.\r
\r
PNG W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/PNG/\r
\r
PNG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/29581.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7dfd45b-d083-4c72-9fc4-280e67940f0b .

camssa:555f7a1d-18e4-4fbb-a4fd-010f7e4ef89f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OSI contributes to improve the delivery of public services since it is designed for being used by all the interconnected systems, therefore if Governments and public sector organisations implement it, they will enhance the delivery of services, improving interoperability and portability of data.

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34cee433-b177-4bcf-aca0-edd4db0ac97b .

camssa:556bb7c1-0bec-48a6-9630-ab91acc2daf9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of Core Location Vocabulary is not related to the secure processing of data. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to the specification.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d4c6ac9-86f9-429f-ab2b-67b382fb4754 .

camssa:558a7bd7-32f5-4aae-a178-e26a16aa0640 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:558df697-17b5-4625-9d18-94b2cfc421c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv6 can be found through EurLex in a regulation. The "Regulation (EU) 2019/881 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 17 April 2019 on ENISA (the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity) and on information and communications technology cybersecurity certification and repealing Regulation (EU) No 526/2013 (Cybersecurity Act)" mentions the IPv6 specification as a key protocol for the security of the public core of the open internet and the stability of its functioning.
Moreover, IPv6 can also be found in "Action Plan for the deployment of Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) in Europe". In this document it is explained that the European Commission will disseminate best practices and will work with vendors to provide full IPv6 functionality in terms of privacy.

EurLex "Regulation (EU) 2019/881 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 17 April 2019 on ENISA (the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity) and on information and communications technology cybersecurity certification and repealing Regulation (EU) No 526/2013 (Cybersecurity Act)" reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32019R0881&qid=1729248000483

EurLex "Action Plan for the deployment of Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) in Europe" reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52008DC0313&qid=1729248000483'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f75beb16-5058-48e9-b121-a62a17fad0b9 .

camssa:558e58ca-fa75-4764-8ada-f3de656a1fb1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is included within the European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) initiative, which is a cross border initiative that aims to simplify the steps when procuring public contracts. The initiative has been running since years ago, and although is not mandatory to use, Member States acting as contracting authorities are able to publish tenders. These tenders can be applied across borders. Therefore, it can be considered as an interoperability agreement between public administrations at supra-national level. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff93a1de-f3c5-46dc-be7f-ed42145fa4d1 .

camssa:5592ad54-95c3-45dc-a486-201cce395a28 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4017a1ae4d077fbb3847280a1c20b41bf00c32d65fc9beaa2bea8cce550ac463 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5595780f-5c92-497e-b912-7c2b6c45dbcb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5596ca6d-eb2f-4d54-a5f3-cb65a503ffbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification provides a common method for the interoperability of systems when referring to access rights and licensing. This is a key aspect when developing any solution, including innovative solutions. Besides, as a core vocabulary it can be extended to adapt the needs of users allowing to get the maximum benefit of the implementation. \r
\r
The working group in charge of ODRL development provides a set of implementers and the results of the implementations, which, as can be read in the table from the following resource, it is positive. Meaning that ODRL is a good asset and fosters the creation of solutions, including innovative ones.\r
\r
W3C working group implementators report: \r
https://w3c.github.io/poe/test/implementors"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c33ef0a6-8cdd-4f24-9d95-da45a8473bdc .

camssa:5599dc14-2053-49bc-ae98-e700149098b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-396b6535162f7bba7733ebcc30d2e467321ce07cd8e48b86ab8201acf27031f9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:55a095a6-8b3f-450a-9f51-3352b6af972f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence that the specification has been explicitly endorsed by any European Union member state.

OGC TrainingDML-AI:
https://www.ogc.org/standard/trainingdml-ai/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:169e8e6f-a706-4257-8900-2a3b9a0e4b35 .

