camssa:5675f5ab-f7f7-4480-bfa6-db61855c86e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF specifications are made available free of charge to the general public via the website. IETF drafts are published publicly discussions take place online in archived mailing lists. Moreover, the IETF Datatracker is the day-to-day front-end to the IETF database for people who work on IETF standards. It contains data about the documents, working groups, meetings, agendas, minutes, presentations, and more, of the IETF._x000D_\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision._x000D_\r
See:_x000D_\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/_x000D_\r
http://www.ietf.org/id-info/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e08bc419-de71-4a3e-b96b-1bf27b12558e .

camssa:56786214-b5b6-46a6-8e27-3dbdcdc5e57c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a18abe4842e04b608025fd70e54c3db5c2a10130c0dab0495479e7d5effb55d ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:56859721-319e-4411-a09a-24e357d65807 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox market acceptance lies in the European Public sector which has set it as the framework for the development, implementation and assessment of the impact derived from public policies and laws. Currently there some market acceptance as described on the European Parliamentary Research Service briefing regarding the Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox. The report does not describe a formal, public change management process for these documents -such as public consultations on modifications to the guidelines, public version control, or detailed release notes for external consumption. Instead, they are characterised as internal documents, with references to internal procedures that are not publicly available.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

European Parliamentary Research Service briefing
https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2022/699463/EPRS_BRI(2022)699463_EN.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8a4d832-662e-46b4-b852-755dc2878748 .

camssa:568b98bd-c4f5-49ed-8469-1c191efa4a80 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification explicitly addresses and enables data integrity with the implementation of digital signatures. A digital signature is data appended to, or a cryptographic transformation of a data unit that allows a recipient of the data unit to prove the source and integrity of the data unit and protect against forgery e.g. by the recipient. As a result, the value of a digital signature is the result of the cryptographic transformation of a data unit that allows a recipient of the data unit to prove the source and integrity of the data unit and protect against forgery.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4b50140a-66b9-4a0a-a762-aacf5915bd7f .

camssa:568da6e1-9ed5-4304-921d-cd2348840512 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5691c8d5-a956-4ceb-926f-d58d65a8c859 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of the specification is not directly related to the visibility of public administrations' procedures, rules, data or services. Publiccode.yml focuses on the reuse of software developed by public bodies, ensuring the efficiency and effectiveness of the budget dedicated to address specific needs. So, administrations can benefit from other administrations services with the implementation of the specification, however, it is not directly impacting visibility.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3923959-cce0-4552-9bd9-cb4d94d0100f .

camssa:56954ee0-99bf-479f-93fd-f446196ae811 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS has a long history of developments and improvements.  Starting in 2010 as the Swagger API, OAS quickly increased in popularity, and in 2015 acquired its actual name under the sponsorship of the Linux Foundation, and other funding members such as IBM, resulting in the most widely used tool for the creation and documentation of APIs.\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:769fd83f-f08a-4364-beb4-861b0de0a65c .

camssa:56977cb4-a872-4295-8a5a-f65e7fa533e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx has not been found to be included in any open repository or catalogue of standards at European level.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9e423e7-46bb-4fb0-b53f-52f4d2a449c1 .

camssa:569c3354-a208-46d7-8245-bd2a62c99c7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NFVI releases do not foresee public reviews. However, the Testing, Experimentation and Open Source (TST) Working Group provides feature requests to open source projects and results of implementation experience to open source communities (see NFV participation requirements reference). Moreover, there is a wiki that openly provides release notes and draftings.\r
\r
TST NFV reference:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/NFV/NFV-WGs-amp-EGs-ToR\r
\r
NFV participation requirements:\r
https://www.etsi.org/network-functions-virtualisation/get-involved-in-nfv\r
\r
ETSI NFVI wiki reference:\r
https://nfvwiki.etsi.org/index.php?title=Main_Page'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03366ffa-0bc1-4814-a721-f2e1a5048bbf .

camssa:56a18764-1856-4b39-a52e-26e7722f8928 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a64b01ca9e737c550b205ba3a8a46b3fcfc9447b648ba8ef15d62d3ada26141 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:56a496cd-294b-4a02-a021-106a912591e5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:56a62d87-68ed-4bd2-8789-35abd170a58a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The ESPD also aligns with the European Interoperability Framework (EIF), which sets out principles and\r
guidelines for promoting interoperability among European public administrations. The EIF includes a focus on ensuring the protection of personal data, as well as promoting transparency, accountability, and the respect for individuals' rights.\r
\r
ESPD data protection:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/espd-seminar-2020/privacy-statement\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32fdaf5a-2ac3-41b9-89c9-54b1e44e7e74 .

camssa:56af272d-0122-41ec-9395-00b354964c44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The MIME-Based Secure Peer-to-Peer Business Data Interchange Using HTTP, Applicability Statement 2, RFC 4130 (AS2) has been found eligible as one of the most popular methods for transporting structured business data securely and reliably over the Internet by the Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2017/1358.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
 MIME-Based Secure Peer-to-Peer Business Data Interchange Using HTTP, Applicability Statement 2, RFC 4130 (AS2):\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4130.html\r
\r
ICT Specifications for e-procurement:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32017D1358'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0c637dc-d008-46c9-a85a-3bf232bba838 .

camssa:56b11b36-42c1-422f-9280-66b1cdc90cf0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP Cookies enable web servers to store stateful information on the user's device or to track the user's browsing activity. They can also be used to save for subsequent use information that the user previously entered into form fields, such as names, addresses, passwords, and payment card numbers. Therefore, HTTP Cookies can facilitate data portability having a positive impact in interoperability.\r
\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-5\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07ca28b8-aab0-498f-8661-ff802e23afd0 .

camssa:56b8bb17-6eb1-45a5-a9ef-d3c5cdc41304 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is developed by the European Commission, specifically by the DIGIT B.2. The development process is open, there is a team working on the action, but there are spaces and communities where users can participate providing feedback for the update and creation of new features. The evolution of the EIRA follows the semantic versioning approach x.y.z. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41cc29ca-3673-4cb2-8ee9-964c11062596 .

camssa:56bb2116-d751-4319-9f7f-403cf3affd91 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b4f0d1b7f1d41c70797fa200c6fc73ac01f2f1659319e5cb1cebe8f5e79c1fcb ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:56bfaa98-fbf3-4676-a9be-fe93363a9b29 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification itself does not encourage the creation of communities, but as a part of IETF, its community does encourage people to join and contribute develop specification sharing the data on European platforms.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88719b2b-7efa-4c8a-b201-fce5d8df7f7f .

camssa:56c84aab-7b4d-4a4f-96e4-a6d0a8b529f0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:56cff6dd-cddc-49ed-bc1a-8873078933da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES (ISO 14533-1:2014) is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b2a29489-a16f-4760-bf15-936d03afafbd .

camssa:56d21355-175c-446c-9c2b-365cd924bced a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 maps its requirements according to relevant data protection regulations such as the Article 24.2 of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014, which state the requirements for qualified trust service providers, and outlines the specific security procedures such services need to apply.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market and repealing Directive 1999/93/EC\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:256eb2a8-5a97-4319-b8c7-ee8e4db5d185 .

camssa:56d61e2e-e4f2-4872-b53d-3be50a615860 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39e7870e79b2999a8b61c97f0c356312b88174320d6464fce5639e57ec0de011 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:56d7887a-af4c-46e0-9a80-c21f7b4b5af8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """EuroVoc is used for data processing acrosss Europe by the European Insitutions and also the National ones. Moreover, there is the possibility to search European Laws amongst other documents using its classification. It can be done through a EurLex, the European Gateway for regulation. \r
\r
Additionally, it is used in the EU Open Data Portal as a method for knowledge classification. In the EU Open Data Portal, datasets are related and linked to EuroVoc domains that improve the searchability and reuse of information.\r
\r
EU Open Data Portal example:\r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/es/data/dataset/building-stock-observatory \r
\r
Search by EuroVoc: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/browse/eurovoc.html?params=12,1216#arrow_1216\r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09ebca8e-f1dd-466f-8c49-882807107259 .

camssa:56dccc75-c462-419b-84a5-c9bd0678e128 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-aa6ea51e02f049efbd153499fb071e07c5f49ba6a0343203440380497057d70e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:56e10667-5c74-4760-9591-4c6524b49553 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:56e188a7-7d1d-46f1-b771-084c67487392 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TrainingDML-AI Standard primarily centers on crafting a UML model and encodings for geospatial machine learning training data. Its adoption can indirectly enhance the efficiency, effectiveness, and inclusivity of public service delivery. By offering a framework for the standardized utilization of geospatial training data, it supports the creation of AI/ML applications capable of revolutionizing the design and delivery of public services.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d8ce1f85-594b-470d-b8d9-c7efe34aec91 .

camssa:56e204e5-8ffc-4d06-9630-313574872f39 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of LegalRuleML is not related to long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecd4a0a3-84f7-4d8b-86ad-0f0e9d2c3581 .

camssa:56e3d852-2dc2-47d6-85f1-3777dd6cdc1e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:56e5afde-5f40-4ecb-87c1-ad0e8f5ed3f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Conforming to the UBL standard means that all business document types remain machine-readable and therefore enhances interoperability between systems, as the document transfer is done in a standardized way.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62c40d11-a759-41fb-802a-a9614b7da3a4 .

camssa:56e5f968-a365-491f-a25d-088b0d085847 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'We can state that OAS is related to the publication of open data given that it constitutes a tool that facilitates the development of RESTful conformant APIs.  Since RESTful APIS can generate plugins that allow for the retrieval of resources in any given format, we can state that OAS facilitates the publication of open data.\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee in the 5-Stars approach: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79decb75-ef0a-4aea-9bb3-8fd8916f2a73 .

camssa:56e6449f-0235-41f9-95bd-415037fbe355 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI) is the first pan-European, public-driven blockchain initiative of its kind and verifiable credentials and verifiable presentations play a major role within the EBSI ecosystem. EBSI VC/VP data models build upon the W3C Verifiable Credentials, which defines the standard way to present credentials/certificates on the internet in a common digital way.\r
\r
EBSI W3C Verifiable Credentials (VCs) and W3C Verifiable Presentations (VPs): \r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=555222155'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3697ddf-eac0-47cc-851b-32955c647f34 .

camssa:56e97dec-3578-4747-82bd-45bcbdf961ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPSV-AP is a reusable and extensible data model for harmonising the way public services are described in a machine-readable format. So it describes the public administrations and eases their visualisation and comprehensibility.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62e26e38-f5f8-4e27-a45d-002ca1ff2ae4 .

camssa:56ef2c88-fc32-4749-a677-68e3239bb352 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:56f42946-5f90-44e1-97fd-54ef09f35379 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c93e2e7-37b6-4248-9dc2-5b9a0ffb8314 .

camssa:56f85e49-49b7-4777-b703-a08f901acb39 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Such means as ensuring the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations can be provided as SOAP extensions using the SOAP extensibility mode. The SOAP Messaging Framework does not directly provide any mechanism for dealing with it directly.\r
\r
SOAP Reference, section 7 Security Considerations:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/#secconsiderations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5818e07-a56c-42a2-b69b-ae63b8d23e4f .

camssa:56fddf0b-5080-43d3-8615-fa8aebf7b22f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The main purpose of HTTP Cookies is to track and store user's data on the webpage.  Nonetheless, in some way, it contributes to the comprehensibility of administrative services by remembering client's information and therefore, providing a better operational website that can be adapted to the user's preferences. \r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#creating_cookies\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fafb172-5599-4c51-8ae3-87d1337972c0 .

camssa:56fea0fb-4e5c-47ea-9bad-2794d90bdc99 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:57023b36-871e-4602-b0d3-0f2a2facfa82 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation (Regulation 1025/2012 on European Standardisation) has been found. Therefore HTTP Cookies is not a European Standard. \r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16e6b454-0bc2-4446-b6f6-7cef3235582b .

camssa:570450c3-df4f-4844-a90f-23774281ec1b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISO 3166-1 is not related to secure process of data. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this\r
specification.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a97cab91-f438-4336-ac27-3dda2f5cd452 .

camssa:57073f14-0e0b-4aaa-9e80-6c31ec014e83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TLS 1.2 is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, TLS 1.2 can define the interoperability aspects of the "Network",  "Networking Service", "Private Network" and "Public Network" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31449643-b783-4709-9091-931391126d01 .

