camssa:577dd90f-8ab8-4850-8c19-5c257e7e08da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Ogg can help comprehend the multimedia data of public administration by adding text as subtitles. In this sense, the specification can play an active role on the representation of the information in an easier visual way. This fact can consider Ogg to foster the comprehensibility of administrative rules and data.\r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f53476a-9544-426d-807c-b0958ebc5f22 .

camssa:578303a1-233a-41b9-a5c0-16f93fa1c620 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:578ea8cb-ddd8-4bef-9d57-084605d476b8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:57932d58-9942-45fd-9c39-c7e8ff4841f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OpenTelemetry, while primarily designed for observability, can be comprehensively scoped to provide significant insights into administrative procedures. For instance, by instrumenting each step of an administrative procedure, OpenTelemetry captures detailed information about the execution flow, including the time taken at each step and any errors encountered. Furthermore, this helps in understanding how often rules are accessed, modified, and by whom.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d8bf9ce-d74c-4949-8db5-dd3a6401fbd8 .

camssa:5796ffc8-6c69-4f10-8721-a0b4d2f255de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of REST is not related to the development of business processes.  Therefore this criterion is not applicable.  \r
\r
REST reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e5debef-6a55-4b44-92f2-896e374e9004 .

camssa:579f6530-4010-4607-a990-c830b82d6f15 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 is specification-independent and can be implemented without dependencies on specific technologies or platforms. Moreover, the IETF, a vendor-neutral Standards Development Organisation, developed the technical specification independently of any vendor products.

TLS 1.3 2018 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc31883a-38f9-47fb-aad0-408683c3690d .

camssa:57a6be54-233b-4f0b-8d72-8253ecc1edea a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:57a90e48-2e12-4ce9-9a31-e2d7f1b39ce0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been successfully implemented in multiple ways and with different approaches by several early adopters from the research services community:\r
• The Helmholtz Centre Potsdam (GFZ) has prototyped it for use in GEOFON to manage large numbers of overlapping seismological datasets https://github.com/javiquinte/datacoll\r
• The Perseids Project at Tufts University has used it to improve data sharing and annotation management http://collections.perseids.org/; https://github.com/RDACollectionsWG/perseids-manifold\r
• The Max Planck Computing and Data Facility (MPCDF) has included it in a generic data repository software https://github.com/TomZastrow/reptor\r
• The German Climate Computing Center (DKRZ) has used the recommendation to deploy an operative service that enables data users to create custom research data collections ("data carts") as part of the global Earth System Grid Federation (ESGF): https://esgf-data.dkrz.de/projects/esgf-dkrz/datacart_pid\r
While these are service providers for specific scientific research communities, the early adoption prototypes demonstrate that, in principle, service provisioning based on the specification is feasible and not bound to particular usage domains.\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:692f272f-abe1-4073-948e-b21ab11e35a2 .

