camssa:57c73c48-b469-4171-9cc4-daa711848330 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In the DTD for Schemas Section there is a part for "Customisation entities" that can lead to think this specification allows customisation.\r
\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4c9164b-6ac2-4258-b4d2-388b8879cdcd .

camssa:57ca70c4-7e5a-4f8f-b0b8-3478e900d017 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification allows saving and exchanging content as images. However, the typology of PNG files are not the most used to exchange and reuse information across borders. At least not in the domain of eProcurement or the development of CEF Building Blocks in which the once-only principle is based.\r
\r
PNG W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/PNG/\r
\r
PNG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/29581.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b64f1dd6-9d92-4594-ba92-55272a4a9d49 .

camssa:57cd79cb-6ec5-403e-a0c9-283da82f474a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML5 can be used independently from other technical specifications, depite that it can be enhanced by mixing HTML5 along other specifications. For instance, CSS is a commonly used together with HTML5. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2014/REC-html5-20141028/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7625a65b-5f8f-4483-928d-840ffa7b2008 .

camssa:57ce6c6c-9f3f-4dd6-9f24-d239be8ef9f1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the different standard catalogues at the supra-national level, the Publications Office has listed it with all the specifications and resources produced and used for open data production, reuse and shareability. \r
\r
EUR-Lex:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/homepage.html\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
EU Vocabularies Business Collection:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/business-collections\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:566c668e-a608-4bcf-b4c8-5a3a15cece36 .

camssa:57ce9d94-e6b4-47e5-b591-7200a869f7e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TESTA network service – which stands for Trans European Services for Telematics between Administrations – provides a European backbone network for data exchange between a wide variety of public administrations. It is an ISA2 solution and which has been designed to support the needs for a whole range of application architectures relying on protocols such as HTTP or the secured version HTTPS. 

Trans European Services for Telematics between Administrations reference:
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7594c3e3-3e13-4973-a052-3efb33248ff8 .

camssa:57cfbf05-7c55-47fb-8e26-09b7dbbfd920 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XHTML has some features to prevent possible security vulnerabilities. Moreover, by allowing to exchange data via online websites, XHTML fosters the secure and trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders. \r
\r
XHTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d5d45a0-16f4-48f0-929b-a84304087098 .

