camssa:58788221-a26b-4ac7-80e7-11b1454d3d49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is development for the evolution of interoperability.\r
The development of XBRL GL comes with close relationships with European public services participants\r
through collaboration in the development of OECD’s SAF-T and UN/CEFACT’s accounting and audit\r
artefacts, as well as international collaboration through the ISO.\r
\r
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1a1HJJJfwsLUbLvJzQ9hQ-ZGtiz2peyGt/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=117964998322026798794&rtpof=true&sd=true'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b64ed81e-b208-485f-9d5e-9a9c06620c08 .

camssa:587e8d49-9b2b-4896-84ac-a3e6311c5f4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Several implementations and studies are assessing the usefulness and exploring how the usage of the specification can enhance the legal domain. This fact contributes to the market extension of the specification. A key point is also the incorporation to trans-European projects as LEOS or MIREL.  \r
\r
Moreover, it has been included within the EU Observatory for ICT Standardisation and their catalogue of standards.  \r
\r
EU Observatory for ICT Standardisation:\r
https://www.standict.eu/standards-repository/working-group/oasis-legalruleml-tc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0dbcb193-415a-4d50-93dd-c03cdf888bb0 .

camssa:58889eee-a299-48f3-965f-3914e962165f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Malta and the Netherlands. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States varies when aligned with the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Whereas the Netherlands perfoms higher, Malta has a middle-lower performance compared to the European average. Some of the Maltese weaknesses relate to the three EIF categories, the need to improve the EIF Principles and the Conceptual Model scoreboards. In addition, there is data missing on the Inclusion and Accessibility and Preservation of Information on the EIF Principles.\r
\r
National catalogue Malta: \r
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243\r
\r
National catalogue The Netherlands:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:475e3a1c-a3cf-4aec-ba71-3dc86b49578e .

camssa:588a4d83-32c1-4568-b58b-a794664311bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """\r
EuroVoc is publicly available for its use and implementation. Moreover, it is available for everyone to study with no cost.\r
\r
EuroVoc reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/browse/eurovoc.html?locale=en\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f787dd2-ae54-4f1c-8875-bf23a1e2e070 .

camssa:589033f4-3723-45bc-b74d-d25460bdc4b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 is the previous version of the Internet Protocol, but it is widely adopted and still prevailing. The newest has specific features and improves security aspects. Thus, it is not dependent of any specific platform and the adoption of IPv4 does not hamper the interoperability. 

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62a3c382-3842-4e90-bad9-75b8f34cf20b .

