camssa:58d50efc-fe7f-4b74-a3c5-fb914dd8dbbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The REST specification appears in the EIRA Library of Interoperable Specifications (ELIS) as a technical application associated to the machine to machine interface ABB,  therefore it can be mapped to the EIRA.\r
\r
ELIS referenece:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c00c984-ce10-45f2-8d9b-e223bbb538f7 .

camssa:58db7485-1966-4d42-8a68-4673de1c45aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification can be found in the e-CODEX system. In this system, the gateway is responsible for the basic exchange of communications. In this context, the ebXML and ebMS 3.0 specifications allow for the structuring of message headers, securing message exchange, and enabling global communication.

Eur-lex ebXML reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/ES/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32022D2519&qid=1743495780482

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2535ae8-aec6-4770-9c35-9f2dce82db7d .

camssa:58db7559-172b-46f3-bd8b-3698ad531278 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 can facilitate interoperability between organisations by providing a common framework for signature creation and verification. Standards such as XAdES (XML Advanced Electronic Signatures) and PAdES (PDF Advanced Electronic Signatures) define interoperable formats and procedures that enable signatures to be exchanged and verified across different systems and platforms. Furthermore, an open and accessible protocol encourages widespread adoption and interoperability by minimising barriers to entry for organizations wishing to implement digital signature capabilities.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da3c08fd-a610-4c31-8f0a-54aff41e0713 .

camssa:58dd6afb-4cf1-412a-8189-3f9d65539729 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:58deffc6-cda3-4dbb-91c2-dbe65d964573 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The European Interoperability Reference Architecture (EIRA) is an architecture content metamodel defining 
the most salient architectural building blocks (ABBs) needed to build interoperable e-Government systems. 
Currently the specification is not included in any catalogue of a member state.

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and\\x02specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3fbd1fc-4099-43f4-b668-35646deeccdd .

