camssa:5932e60e-931a-412e-b445-fb5fb0520d06 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL can support interoperability, achieving comprehensive data portability involves considerations beyond the technical aspects covered by WSDL. Additional factors, such as data standards, semantic interoperability, governance frameworks, and compliance with regulations, contribute to effective data portability in the context of European public services. Moreover, the adoption of standardized WSDL descriptions can contribute to data portability to some extent by promoting interoperability between systems and applications. \r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:989c8831-0659-4dea-af4a-c5abcb8290bc .

camssa:5937e475-34d9-45ee-b16f-d483baab73f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SOAP is defining a data model, which represents application-defined data structures and values as a directed edge-labelled graph of nodes. Therefore, as a sector agnostic specification, SOAP defines a cross-sector reusable data model. \r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2007/REC-soap12-part2-20070427/#datamodel"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20bcb720-cb0e-4406-88bf-830fa871412c .

camssa:593907a9-2732-4c44-a7cb-3e60210460f1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL specification is not included in a formal open repository or catalog of standards at the European level, such as those maintained by organizations like CEN (European Committee for Standardization) or ETSI(European Telecommunications Standards Institute). ODRL is typically managed by the ODRL Initiative, which is a community-driven effort that supports the development and promotion of the ODRL standard.\r
\r
ODRL Community Group Home page:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/odrl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:afeb1823-56d0-4eec-8bda-4e0464b6378e .

camssa:593e7eeb-0f39-476f-94d6-e738582c3124 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This specification is supported by ISO's Information technology commitee. In order to participate in creating standards, the user must be part of their national standards body (assuming their country is part of ISO).

ISO Technical committees:
https://www.iso.org/get-involved.html

ISO Information technology commitee:
https://www.iso.org/committee/45020.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac00e8c3-9e8c-4f54-b9fa-356a2d61b205 .

camssa:5942332f-7f59-44a3-bdf8-09aac2ec7c1d a cav:Score,
