camssa:59a29c81-ee07-47fd-9255-3ac0f037e4d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI EN 319 422, operates under \r
the ETSI Intellectual Property Rights (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a royalty-free \r
basis.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights Policy, ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:14b2bee7-eb4c-49de-b34a-6da0ace3e056 .

camssa:59a2fc0f-c118-430e-8f01-3e19c9e83278 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SHACL is not related to the long-term preservation of data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:900677b1-bb5f-4b6d-9c80-b87cd11ca7db .

camssa:59a5aca5-2557-4725-a306-d86a76fb4965 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Since ShEx is a language for describing RDF graph structures, consequently, and according to the main principles of open data, it is a good enabler for the publishing of linked data, given that ShEx schemas are intended for use in validating instance data, communicating interface parameters and data structures, generating user interfaces, and transforming RDF graphs into other data formats and structures, therefore, it makes sure data is well structured to be published as open data. \r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc2af042-9ad2-4e5e-bb4b-a29e5e1de977 .

camssa:59ab53f0-e9bf-4340-be50-38360df1c289 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 16234-1 e-CF does facilitate the modelling of business processes. The Digital Organisational Frameworks and IT Professionalism (DigiFrame) seeks to reach a mutual agreement on new coordinated procedures for reliable, effective and efficient measurement and forecasting of the demand and supply of high-tech skills at European and national level.\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, Reports & Publications section, Workshops on the Digiframe (2018) – Presentations subsection:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/app/uploads/2021/01/DIGIFRAME_workshop-4-morningafternoon_report_201811205_final.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed427794-15fd-46b7-b895-c760ab4647b0 .

camssa:59aca6b1-2ea0-4c29-afa7-a2c2aceb3164 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'8 Member States are recommending MIME in their ICT National Catalogues. The Member states are Croatia, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden. \r
 \r
CAMSS List of Standards:   \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f91505ad-3df7-45e2-beda-40097e90a69f .

camssa:59ad4420-eec7-4ae3-b2f5-7297ebbdad8a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Not enough pieces of evidence have been found to answer positively or negatively to this criterion. It seems that OpenPM2 goal is not related to enabling e-accessibility for European Public Services.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c5373c64-4107-409d-a686-15e6569825b5 .

camssa:59ae2477-7bf2-42f2-ae7f-6c4097a8bc34 a cav:Score,
