camssa:59fc1add-bd81-4a3e-8a21-e67b0154779e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML facilitates organisational interoperability agreements, as one of the specification's objectives is to boost interoperability within organisations. In this sense, it is noteworthy that it allows for the creation of a standardised framework to share XML documents. Moreover, it also enables the creation of a Collaboration Protocol Agreement (CPA).

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:efa5d7ec-4ffb-4794-94a9-aac91228e42f .

camssa:5a019f4b-f05b-496f-9c33-4bffbbfef435 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SEMIC, the Semantic Interoperability Community, who is in charge of developing DCAT-AP, has a specific Change and Release Management Policy for DCAT-AP where they encourage any stakeholder to contribute to the development of the specification.\r
\r
DCAT-AP change and release management policy:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/document/change-and-release-management-policy-dcat-ap \r
\r
DCAT-AP in Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about\r
\r
SEMIC DCAT-AP:\r
https://github.com/SEMICeu/DCAT-AP\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03f79f09-6017-4fed-84b8-9e1dc554ef0f .

camssa:5a048eed-3545-49f7-9ad6-fd8b46b96623 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5a04b54d-475d-43ea-9542-5a323ad09f31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the time of elaborating this assessment, OWL current version (OWL2) is not included in any EIRA ABB in the current EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). However, the previous version of the specification can define the interoperability aspects of the "Core Data Model" ABB of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9cb6add0-74ee-4be9-84ff-e655865bb582 .

camssa:5a07dfbc-e5b3-4053-b1ac-c8aa7243cd8d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69dbbbfc4ff4c79244a3bd99f7c3f883f2a7114ec515cb4d576f0d807c94b9fd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5a0b8ec3-0259-4ece-90e9-008525005ad0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) is not inherently designed to facilitate organisational interoperability agreements. While DoH may not directly address organisational interoperability agreements, it can play a role in ensuring secure and private DNS communication between systems or entities that want to make an organisational interoperability agreements. 

RFC 8484: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82ff1e89-ab73-4469-9a3a-4863975e8e93 .

