camssa:5a50831f-6ffd-4369-b238-cf0c2726e2ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS enables authenticity features through server authentication using digital certificates issued by trusted certificate authorities. This ensures that the client is communicating with the legitimate server and not an imposter, providing confidence in the authenticity of the connection.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d756198a-efad-4fae-a3c6-85d142e95b69 .

camssa:5a532243-38e5-4201-b202-c07664f3b8dd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5a55cc90-7ae3-4812-81b6-376f8437bd13 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of JSON is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:65bffa23-5db9-40b8-84af-b2b846856c0d .

camssa:5a56dddb-0001-40b4-8af3-749ef5da704c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DPV working group was created as an outcome of the W3C Workshop on Data Privacy Controls and Vocabularies in Vienna in 2017, and started on 25th May 2018 – the date of the enforcement of GDPR.
Since then, the DPVCG has worked to fulfil its aims and objectives, and produced the Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) as a deliverable.
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d38abf1f-5c04-459f-a77a-438aed0b9bd8 .

camssa:5a595d78-c17b-4c70-9bee-fd6e8d35bf63 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a0101cb11c30c1bbf94adb74479472f2a40c53ccc4b442180fece91506c20a9d ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:5a598301-998a-46d6-aca2-146e29928ac5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification addresses data integrity by providing identity and access management in International Data Spaces, ensuring that the right users (that are part of the ecosystem connected to or within an enterprise) have the appropriate access to technology resources.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7edfec8-4a13-43a5-975e-de5d2375abbb .

camssa:5a59a1a1-b211-482a-98e9-4fc58f3469b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:5a5ba660-f750-4d00-bb96-258cbd5238ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS is included in the national catalogue of Slovakia. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of this Member State is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
\r
Slovakia’s Catalogue:\r
http://www.informatizacia.sk/standardy-is-vs/596s\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab43d79b-61f6-46d2-82af-69a40655046a .

camssa:5a6144f7-e36c-4e2a-98ab-088dc98985df a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TS 119 614-1 is a testing conformance suite that can be applied in any domain and context where the \r
exchange of documents is required. Therefore, the specification is usable beyond any business-specific \r
domain and ensures its implementation across business domains.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0a1cccf0-99c5-4ab7-a8cd-88bcca52083e .

