camssa:5b467536-03d6-4e16-a979-6d0b718c09b7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"W3C Data Quality Vocabulary's first public working draft was published in 2015. Since then, three major releases have been published and several minor changes have been recommended. In addition, different 
documentation on its supporting processes has been published to ensure the correct change and release of 
its content. For instance, section B of the specification explains changes made since the last published version. Therefore, this specification has been evolved enough and mechanisms for its development have 
been put in place.

Change History DQV: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/#change-history

W3C Recommendation Track: 
https://www.w3.org/2021/Process-20211102/#rec-track

General Requirements for Technical Reports: 
https://www.w3.org/2021/Process-20211102/#recs-and-notes\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e717940-6124-4229-825f-db3645b21969 .

camssa:5b4e0d4d-ba00-4e9e-a2ea-b4936f85d942 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard does not allow the customisation of its core components when is implemented. 

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da21b855-a72c-44b4-996f-2e55ed8d160f .

