camssa:5b690e66-8400-4e42-afb0-99c679fb7179 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CSS is to give format to web documents, including layout, colours and fonts. A well-formatted web document helps the public administration to make the information more comprehensible. Without a CSS, the information could be confusing and it could take longer to see the meaning of the information.\r
An example of this is EUR-Lex, the cross border gateway to EU Law. It is using CSS to present the different documentation contained in EUR-Lex. \r
\r
Presentation style sheets EU Vocabulary:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/presentation-style-sheets\r
\r
EUR-Lex:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/homepage.html?locale=en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0849387-4274-47a5-8de3-298304bd8868 .

camssa:5b6fe41d-889b-4313-a9f3-862365ec2f7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is widely adopted amongst others like SMTP for the exchange of data over the internet. It allows sharing several file formats, which makes the specification highly reusable. The specification has been implemented and it is supported by numerous mail software as Mailchimp amongst others, demonstrating the market acceptance of MIME.\r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f69ad281-aa42-4ff6-b72a-d7f0aab7fb6b .

camssa:5b70a7f7-6247-4c49-887f-550c868ea3fb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISO 3166-1 is not related to the protection of personal data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:703f6487-fee0-4582-ac83-0a11259bcac6 .

camssa:5b75f9f4-520e-4aa1-9f63-2c4beeae1078 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of CSV is not related to security and privacy of the data exchange. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.           \r
                                  \r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:810ab01a-f430-45d1-affe-d6c880a886e7 .

camssa:5b76277c-c0f8-4474-8b06-33aec5fc72cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL is built around RDF and is highly dependent from it since its purpose is to  validate RDF graphs.\r
\r
However, note that RDF is a European standard since 2014 and the common data format for Semantic web."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c18949f4-dba3-438b-bf1e-4c78402d7840 .

camssa:5b78d73e-cb45-403c-afc3-946ba8a5e339 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Internet Protocol Security (IPsec), a protocol providing a network layer security (authentication and encryption), is an optional feature that allows the Internet Protocol to secure the data exchange. However, in the latest version of the protocol (IPv6), the feature has been included as mandatory enhancing security settings. \r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc791\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1349\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2474\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6864\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2460"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85e4e8af-e4bc-4bc2-8739-bf7da1d2c531 .

camssa:5b7b1d03-8056-4d70-9d3f-d8b52a7aa865 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 is widely adopted as a key protocol for making data, information, and resources available on the internet. However, it is worth noting that the newer version, IPv6, is being gradually adopted and incorporates several innovative solutions. Despite this, IPv4 is still in use and continues to be adopted in many countries, such as the Netherlands, where it plays a crucial role in terms of security and privacy.

National catalogue of Netherlands:
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst

IPv6 specification:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460

IPv4 to IPv6 transition:
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/transition-from-ipv4-to-ipv6-address/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00daeb79-7fb8-4faf-bf6f-a3d5ac4407bc .

camssa:5b7b30e0-7149-4b47-b784-b79d74747c28 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "20" .

