camssa:5c531121-70a9-4836-85ae-33b6acef7b87 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XACML is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Cyprus and Germany. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Cyprus and Germany is fully aligned with at least 
3 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards

National Interoperability Framework Observatory: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets

National Catalogue of Cyprus:
https://dits.dmrid.gov.cy/dmrid/dits/dits.nsf/all/B83AA8E4EB4EFD19C225855800288B10/$file/Cyprus%
20eGovernment%20Interoperability%20Framework_new%20EIF_v2.0-To%20Publish.pdf

National Catalogue of Germany:
https://www.cio.bund.de/Webs/CIO/DE/digitaler-wandel/architekturen-und-standards/architekturen-und\\x02standards-node.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d564c6de-7dcb-479f-b03d-0ab0d22299aa .

camssa:5c584422-79a4-4892-aed3-c1b0123de4d4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:5c64834e-9aab-46c8-92a4-e03518a825e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of this Core Vocabulary is to support the exchange of information between organisations that define criteria and organisations that respond to these criteria using evidences. So, it facilitates the visibility of administrative rules.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc7bae9f-75db-4ad1-95cc-dfb51c7537f2 .

camssa:5c64a617-7cb0-4568-b624-a9251b6fecef a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5c6b54a4-a9fe-4556-a329-37a3d41aef21 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5c6d4b9e-1592-4c1f-96e1-8e82877726eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification encourages the creation of communities by providing a common framework for the development of interoperable public services and the sharing of data and results across communities and platforms.   \r
                                                  \r
AKN4EU reference: \r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c2e04e7-c763-4343-b1c5-f5d791df50f7 .

camssa:5c71e53e-82aa-40ca-84e8-9b41c5031e85 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA specification itself does not explicitly address multilingual considerations. However, the accessibility principles promoted by WAI-ARIA can be applied in a multilingual context to enhance the user experience for individuals who use assistive technologies and may interact with content in different languages. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.


WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/

WAI-ARIA roles guide:
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Roles'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d4e7414-2dc8-41dc-b77f-60a55abf709b .

camssa:5c7a134e-c031-430c-b628-dd2728228931 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe8baf5c-dd4b-408e-9498-e96991d05e87 .

camssa:5c7d1fdf-cba4-4b83-a5a3-0a7e57ff7bbc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does dwell in data portability between systems/applications or supporting the implementation/evolution of European public services since it is designed to support the interchange of information among heterogeneous information systems. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae491f8c-5a22-4d97-99b7-ee582c4be57d .

camssa:5c7ddc5b-0e1e-4dc6-85c8-0446786cf4db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OpenTelemetry GitHub is where all major and minor releases foresee a public review during which collected feedback is publicly visible. The repository has two public sections dedicated to issues and pull requests, which means that any user can see the whole release lifecycle of the specification and participate in it.

OpenTelemetry GitHub: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:facb6d85-32d8-4284-ad12-6f9c91a1c97c .

camssa:5c7fdf7c-9c2e-4ed2-a2e8-8739477a7adc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No overlap has been detected with European standardisation organisations activities at EU level.\r
This conclusion is based on the work programme of CEN  and ETSI  as published on their respective websites, and on the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020 .\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c1b7950-7c55-4fdd-a427-8a83a9ec6165 .

camssa:5c8199fd-6fe0-4936-8e94-7e007bf43535 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5c8527aa-b9bf-4b20-bfd7-57931057a5be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is not included per se in any supra-national catalogue. Despite this, SOAP 1.2 is part of the Electronic Signatures and Infrastructures (ESI); Rationalized framework of Standards for Electronic Registered Delivery Services Applying Electronic Signatures, which is an ETSI Special Report. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_sr/019000_019099/019050/01.01.01_60/sr_019050v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a2502dc-c1bf-4408-86ff-c56570723381 .

camssa:5c87bd7a-4065-4c92-9caf-24979b5ffa10 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is recommended by The Netherlands and Malta. \r
\r
National Catalogue of The Netherlands:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden\r
\r
National Catalogue of Malta:\r
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac6ed749-92c2-4caf-a08f-b6be83826bd4 .

camssa:5c87c060-6e08-4b40-b922-960d5c051f2d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

