        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5c8da603-254d-4a41-a210-0b60c66b02e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to supporting the evolution of European public services, \r
therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de45ec6d-55b9-4332-a233-e4128162b408 .

camssa:5c96ddcc-5194-46a6-a323-dc0d26fb2413 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In the specification documentation, there is no reference to the possibility of customisation, so it is asumed that it is not possible.\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48937621-7ba2-480e-9a7d-16f2519b341f .

camssa:5c96f1ff-a675-44b5-9127-9fec91b78916 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:5c970bf3-5b1e-4475-8f54-4a0a15c88ba6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"RDF is compliant with one of the maximum levels of maturity provided by Tim Berners Lee’s 5 stars schema for open data. Moreover, RDF is highly aligned with the principles for Linked Data promoted by W3C and Tim Berners Lee. In fact, RDF is one of the proposed standards for the publication of Linked Open Data. \r
The specification is compliant with Tim Berners Lee's principles for the Linked Data and, as well, is highly aligned with the different levels of maturity of Tim Berners Lee's 5 stars schema for open data. In fact, RDF is one of the proposed standards for the publication of Linked Data. \r
\r
W3C Linked data design issues:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
\r
Tim berners-Lee 5 star linked open data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/ld-bp/\r
Best Practices for Publishing Linked Data\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c754e37-e3e5-41df-94d0-e97eb24f780b .

camssa:5c9845e9-3dec-43dc-9767-f184ab79aa28 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5ca90eab-e35c-4bcc-bb0b-a52e07dfc7c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. So it can be said that WS-BPEL is independent of any specific technology or platform. \r
\r
The specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:807c3c72-a62e-4e17-b25b-231e7ddc3387 .

camssa:5ca9df21-1168-4209-a1fa-ec4ba70dab50 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5cae67a1-3e3e-442b-8d01-3d26aed1a6a3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is not yet used in European institutions but BFO contributes to improve interoperability and portability of data.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9c51ed5-479e-4c6c-a568-4910bb5f6eaa .

camssa:5cb240ea-7e82-4b15-b8e9-0c8259629832 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:5cb53f24-ac98-4de4-bca1-b91a2d453752 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5cb87f43-7ef1-419d-bd93-f0cd2659b887 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData allows for including custom transformations (query options) that the user explicitly requests, which are not necessary defined in the OData specification. However, these extensions are restrictive or limited to a specific functionality.

OData reference on extensibility:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358848'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93e8b9c6-4910-4c4e-b5d3-874db0e2cd13 .

camssa:5cb9adb5-605a-43dc-8d77-18f925ac1845 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:5cbbcb3f-626c-420f-b7c3-11f87a797341 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can facilitate the modelling of business processes by helping standardize and agree to the form which the information is described. Standardising the evidence modelling may help in the cross-border participation by eliminating language barriers between European countries. \r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6180eb81-67be-4728-9a3b-dbcea70c0c74 .

camssa:5cbbec96-1b71-41fb-b32e-91417fcde089 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, FTP has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:858a8a21-eaef-4f58-b7f5-a5bf711893c1 .

camssa:5cbe3d4d-f333-4b83-87cd-001a098e602e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UDDI registries or nodes depend on WSDL to complete the data exchange transaction and provide the requester with information. Additionally, UDDI relies on SOAP to enable the service invoke by the requester. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c51a6d2-192c-4a3b-a53e-3292988a8e81 .

camssa:5cc32b0e-5e7a-42fa-ab19-dbc0e0291a72 a cav:Score,
