camssa:5e2168c6-05f7-47ba-b321-a530a7bc1e2f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As can be seen on the Oracle documentation about ebXML MCD implementation, the ebXML specification can work with some components that can be customised. For example, Message Control Documents (MCD), which serve as an interface between a back-end system and WebLogic Integration - Business Connect for processing business messages. In this sense, when using MCD, some elements are optional to implement. However, the core elements of the specification cannot be customised.

ebXML MCD implementation:
https://docs.oracle.com/cd/E13215_01/wlibc/docs81/admin/xml_protocols.html#1032357

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ecb6020-eb54-4675-bac0-c8056d64be05 .

camssa:5e233c6f-6a0e-41ad-b540-a0b6e40f088d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

