camssa:5ea083f1-35c2-4090-92e7-4637a7ba1349 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b59c7e3-8b96-491b-91b5-b3b0ebf0e38d .

camssa:5ea0b5e9-6319-4ae2-80aa-e5fc87f2381d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'6 Member States are recommending IPv4 in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are Croatia, France, Germany, Netherlands, Norway and Sweden. 

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36458b59-bf77-4f4e-aea6-a0f613dfa3b9 .

camssa:5ea62fd6-e1ee-4418-94c0-f037f6d0129d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 along with the whole Electronics Signature Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications, has been proven effective for the Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Documents (TR-ESOR), a document from the German Federal Office of Information Security that specifies security-related requirements for the long-term preservation of evidence of cryptographically signed electronic documents and data along with associated electronic administrative data (metadata).\r
\r
TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/EN/BSI/Publications/TechGuidelines/TR03125/TR-03125_B_v1_2_2.pdf?__blob=publicationFile&v=1\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d841c01-fbc7-4874-8284-5cf85bae41cc .

camssa:5ea6ab33-c4e5-43ee-b702-52641bd98064 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DPV is based on the legislative requirements of the European Union, such as the GDPR, which aims to harmonise data privacy laws across Europe. Therefore, the DPV promotes the comprehensibility of administrative procedures by providing a clear vocabulary that defines all levels at which personal data will be processed.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

GDPR reference:
https://gdpr.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21fb5cbc-91ec-46bb-87bc-6fc33adb54b7 .

camssa:5eab4319-f52a-4f6e-91af-fbd518658524 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This Core Vocabulary is included in the Center for transfer of technology (CTT), in the Spanish ICT National Catalogue. \r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
Spanish National Catalogue:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/ctt/CTTprincipalEs.htm?idioma=en&urlMagnolia=/pae_Home/en/pae_SolucionesCTT.html#.ZC1eDXvP02w'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a0b8c29-5bde-4cef-ab4b-c59ede1bbef2 .

camssa:5eb068ff-26d5-472d-8357-1642bb4d9f19 a cav:Score,
