        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CSS v2.1 is not related with data portability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable for this specification. \r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82416048-085b-45cd-9509-3f85b0fb5b90 .

camssa:5ecea5ef-8d58-4cc7-ba79-16c5fbe8484f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All solutions developed in ISA² Programme are under ISA Open Metadata Licence which is perpetual, royalty-free and non-exclusive license to Use and re-Use the Works.\r
\r
ISA open metadata license:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/licence/isa-open-metadata-licence-v11"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a7a13e2-3eef-42a0-a936-4a527318aa86 .

camssa:5ed0f070-9f86-407f-aeb0-1e0b19c41811 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TGF promotes the use of secure and resilient infrastructures to ensure that data processing is performed in a secure and reliable manner, as well as the implementation of appropiate security controls to ensure authentication and access-control methods.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a9dcdb8-aee4-40b7-814e-338a6ad140e5 .

camssa:5ed5ed50-616b-403b-a0f3-f83bbd1ca6d6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:5ed86cff-0963-4d7f-8d7a-2d14b9b2347b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI TS 119 512 specification outlines protocols for trust service providers that offer long-term data preservation services for digital signatures and other types of data. Using digital signatures and time-stamps tokens, is guaranteed that data has not been changed since it was signed. Moreover, it is possible to establish access control mechanisms to access data. Therefore, data is secure and protected against unwanted changes.

ETSI TS 119 512:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.01_60/ts_119512v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae0fc96c-b99e-42f9-811d-c9a9cea2ef0f .

camssa:5ed98926-3a31-42d7-a266-eb357ad20475 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of ISO 639-2 as a European standard.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue: \r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d12ef92e-04ec-4cbb-9a35-b01a60ae249f .

camssa:5edc11b8-b6c6-4b8c-8f6e-a236fcbf61db a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d7be9f0dd52944e6c25f5469c86355a42ae446838bd9759b4986d21f7db4814b ;
    cav:value "1" .

