camssa:5f667466-8bfb-4a1f-983b-ca2962fef3ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 provides the infrastructure for data transmission, media access control, and network performance optimization, supporting digital service delivery channels.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c7d77db-57f9-46ae-8949-cb5ffb788e7c .

camssa:5f67b46a-4329-4937-aa67-83c6b6510b61 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval process so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the Request for Comments (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications. _x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.  _x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
See:_x000D_\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/  _x000D_\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:272eadfd-9aaf-4259-be8c-b217b5fe65f9 .

camssa:5f681dd3-1473-4644-b346-d5e409222224 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 can enable the exposure of interfaces if combined with other specifications, notably those specifications inherent to the interface of a given public service. For example, the specification prompts the display of data associated to the country or territory where a user is submitting an ESPD (European Single Procurement Document) form.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html\r
\r
ESPD reference, Legal framework and context section:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_business_handbook.html#_i_1_1_legal_framework_and_context'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:769ac86e-d71e-4bce-92f5-294bf83aa876 .

camssa:5f6c40ff-b25a-496a-98a3-573f28ad15c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'For the ISO 639-2 maintenance, there is the Library of Congress Registration Authority (ISO 639-2/RA). This community supports the development of this specification and attends language code change requests.\r
\r
ISO 639-2/RA reference:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bdd852b-3512-486e-9d96-69b400f4c35c .

camssa:5f6edeb9-ef6d-4d89-9e43-9e811fc259b6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "0" .

