camssa:5fa232bb-0569-49a7-9392-4a49d4db131e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary facilitates information sharing between governments, businesses, and citizens. The CPOV allows managing a cross-border repository of public services and organisations. So, it fosters data portability between systems and applications supporting the implementation and evolution of European public services.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1cf8cbba-148d-426c-8160-d048f4647479 .

camssa:5fa639d4-35df-456b-a101-99438a8f7eb7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No evidence has been found of the specification being included in an interoperability agreement between organisations involved in the European public services provision. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e818db79-4457-4ecc-a5fc-2a0d59850b04 .

camssa:5fa6672b-b966-4a90-b076-2f98461682ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary has been used to develop some European projects, for example, ESPD-EDM (European Single Procurement Document - Exchange Data Model) which is the technical representation of the legal European Single Procurement Document. It is used to support interoperability between ESPD services provided all over Europe.\r
\r
ESPD documentation:\r
https://docs.peppol.eu/pracc/espd/edm/\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04d53de5-2b20-4d2b-a100-2cc645416a07 .

camssa:5faa85a1-47f9-48ad-a37e-739ebd714203 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a vocabulary to describe assets within a Repository, it provides concepts and properties identifying the content creators and other informative metadata such as dates involved in the release of the solutions described. These facts increase the reliability of the exchanged data. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00a05ca5-56dc-464a-b0d7-b12803cbb115 .

camssa:5fafd362-9a86-4cd5-80fb-d448423ba52b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:5fb7258e-c757-438f-b7f7-307ef91c7d2b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAREF is not related to guaranteeing the authenticity and authentication of roles agents involved in the data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. 

SAREF: 
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94895759-3080-4b88-80e6-7669d8f98a1c .

camssa:5fbcad69-a94c-4016-b8ff-deef56048d8c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b4f0d1b7f1d41c70797fa200c6fc73ac01f2f1659319e5cb1cebe8f5e79c1fcb ;
    cav:value "1" .

