camssa:6044b9b6-a3e2-4466-b010-515dcdb261ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Effective data management practices, as encouraged by ISO/IEC 19944-1, can contribute to an improved visibility of administrative procedures, rules, data, and services within cloud computing environments. By categorizing and organizing data according to the provided classification scheme, organisations can enhance the visibility and accessibility of their data assets, including administrative procedures and rules. Additionally, ISO/IEC 19944-1 promotes effective governance and management of cloud services, which can indirectly contribute to the visibility of services within cloud computing environments. By adopting the recommended practices outlined in the specification, organisations can establish clearer governance structures, define service management processes, and ensure the appropriate visibility of services.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9bc0b5f-940d-4900-b421-a2405a71ea59 .

camssa:6044c3d4-454b-4519-8944-d4feb744b8c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Data on the Web Best Practices gives some advice on how to publish data on the web. However, it does not make data available on the Web, or it does not make data available as structured data. So, this specification does not support any level of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data.\r
\r
Data on the Web Best Practices W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f2e440f-9ecf-49a9-a64a-f3542f9af679 .

