camssa:608ca282-4076-47bf-bb60-65aa711d6f90 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The DCAT vocabulary supports the attribution of data and metadata to various participants such as resource creators, publishers and other parties.\r
\r
 In addition, it also supports the association of rights and licenses with catalogued Resources and Distributions.\r
\r
Such metadata improves the reliability of data exchanged between citizens, businesses and public administrations. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21712276-6f6b-491f-90b2-783f55fa466f .

camssa:60910129-d3fd-443a-b457-b5f64c5fdb6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are various implementations where AMQP is utilised. For example, AMQP 1.0 is used with Azure Service Bus, which includes creating connections, sessions, and links, and transferring messages to and from Service Bus entities such as queues, topics, and subscriptions. Another application of AMQP is in Red Hat AMQ, which is based on open-source communities like Apache ActiveMQ and Apache Kafka. This flexible messaging platform reliably delivers information, enabling real-time integration and connecting the Internet of Things (IoT).

Red Hat Enterprise MRG:
https://docs.redhat.com/es/documentation/Red_Hat_Enterprise_MRG/3/html/messaging_programming_reference/index#idm140626033708592

Microsoft Azure Messaging services :
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-amqp-protocol-guide

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f46f849-b28e-4f97-b454-275e5015ab58 .

camssa:6092128a-6ef5-423a-91ab-711ff595122e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:60970d2c-774a-4337-8b6e-049b7fb0f0c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Open Data Protocol (OData) supports the creation of data services based on REST, which allow resources to be published and edited by web clients via HTTP messages. OData could allow a third-party information system to act on behalf of citizens who cannot, permanently or temporarily, make direct use of public services. In this sense, it can contribute to e-accessiblity.\r
\r
OData reference, 1 Introduction:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:29e2feef-66d6-4e7a-98d6-f653030bc189 .

