camssa:60eb443d-7cb4-49c3-adc8-c656be1c757c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating an Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all of the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:\r
- Technical excellence;\r
- prior implementation and testing;\r
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;\r
- openness and fairness; and \r
- timeliness.\r
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, through testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.\r
\r
IETF Reference: \r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9de08e63-eb2b-4412-86ba-7b3c29ce9ca5 .

camssa:60ecb838-4f6b-4b89-a967-947f98b4bf55 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a1eafd9c95081eeabe19f0511239b88139f02f95e2349049eeea058a89c80f49 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:60f3b62c-9114-452f-8fa3-bf5386ce14b1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is an internationally-standardized specification for a suite of common business documents (invoices, purchase orders, waybills, etc.) and a concrete XML syntax (using XSD or RNC) for expressing those documents in a machine-readable format. It is flexible enough to include its own business objects and XML syntax as extensions. It is structured in such a way that it can make business documents utilizing a common library of business objects.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
UBL guidelines for customization:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/guidelines/UBL2-Customization1.0cs01.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1de63b4-4c92-4ac9-ac95-6caeded259cd .

camssa:60f7a9fd-6699-419f-9e57-8075c8bdd72a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:60fc7652-2101-4c2f-9a01-0a17f9b57799 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Some European projects using UBL have been found to conduct effciency assessments.  Such is the case of PEPPOL BIS Billing or ESPD.  In addition, there has been found some academic papers and assess the efficiency of UBL conformity to specific data models.  \r
\r
\r
Peppol BIS Billing 3.0\r
https://docs.peppol.eu/poacc/billing/3.0/\r
\r
UBL data model architecture discussion paper:\r
https://www.academia.edu/3213815/UBL_v2_Data_Model_Architecture_Discussion_Paper'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ecb5881-beec-4a88-a59c-00bddbfceeb6 .

camssa:61009a23-6a3d-4074-bd49-e82c6979b839 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

