        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6103e366-9cc3-4f27-a33e-5114ba5b8157 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XACML is included in the DSSC catalogue, where XACML is classified as a Data Sovereignty and Trust 
standard.

DSSC catalogue:
https://dssc.eu/space/SE1/185794711
/Data+Sovereignty+and+Trust+standards+and+technologies+landscape'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:999be9d3-0318-4519-9be9-5720df6627a1 .

camssa:6105826f-bcc6-4eb2-9670-7b867923fa11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"When it comes to logging into website, HTTP Cookies can reuse the client information by means of granting him access to the website's services. The stateful nature of HTTP Cookies, therefore, makes it a tool to store and reuse information.  \r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-5\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5fa05802-0c4d-4c31-8479-8a51b5aa8596 .

camssa:61071c98-5a66-413c-a2cb-467a54cc64e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Extensible Forms Description Language specification is based on XML. In this sense, XFDL implementations can be assessed by checking if they follow the correct XML structure. To test this, there are many tools available to test and validate an XML document, such as xmlvalidation.

Xmlvalidation platform:
https://www.xmlvalidation.com/

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e07fb67e-f722-4393-aa9a-7d3e4c173e82 .

camssa:6107f237-b98d-4e8e-8f5e-20b124bddb8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of OWL2 is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ef5e0e0-b364-4081-9994-078ae8520140 .

camssa:610c6eb8-744b-47d3-9513-362e74b09add a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 can be applied in any domain and context where the use of the time-stamping protocol is realised. Therefore, the specification is usable beyond any business-specific domain and can be used in any kind of organisation (See section 6 in the following document).

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3336db9d-c6e2-4768-9a9c-55cbcb0ecf1b .

camssa:61103093-4f6e-436d-9033-9cda8633f956 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) is used in the VeraCrypt project as an encryption algorithm to protect data from unauthorised access.

VeraCrypt AES project:
https://veracrypt.eu/en/AES.html

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f79e8edc-f553-41b2-b162-8b5608d27aae .

