camssa:61d8fc13-7eed-4151-84ef-95b33e4267f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP contributes to data integrity through features like secure transport (TLS), caching and invalidation procedures, conditional requests, and message framing that help to ensure the complete and unaltered transmission of information.

HTTP/1.1, RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Caching, RFC 9111 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111#name-updating-stored-header-fiel

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-http-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d7f295b-80f1-42b0-b960-3e8048db2138 .

camssa:61da65db-960c-4cd2-bd0d-5b8fe1853752 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 can facilitate the modelling of business processes when it comes to defining the relationships among the preservation schemes,  preservation profiles and their related policies on a given business-specific trust service (see section 4.4).\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:77a4de8a-1138-4acc-ac16-ba25fa9f3cbd .

