camssa:624f6651-093a-4c64-82b6-896284f71789 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 is part of the Electronic Signatures Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications. The ESI\r
dates back to 2012, when the General Policy Requirements for Trust Service Providers supporting Electronic Signatures (ETSI EN 319 401) specification was first issued. Since its first publication, there have been many extensions one of which is ETSI TS 119 511, whose version 1.1.1 was released in 2020 when the eIDAS regulation identified the need to create protocols to develop preservation services for trust service providers, as mentioned in ETSI SR 019 510, giving birth to both TS 119 511 and TS 199 512 specifications.\r
\r
ESI specification history:\r
https://standards.globalspec.com/std/14387016/EN%20319%20401\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 401 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:daf43235-a330-43ba-98ee-94a03e2f1638 .

camssa:6252a251-60d8-4eac-a9d8-8321c7c229e5 a cav:Score,
