camssa:62658f2b-3ca7-456c-9429-ff1a417601a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 can be enhanced with IPsec, which ensures the authenticity and integrity of transmitted data. IPsec guarantees that the content remains unchanged from its original form when it is sent, and that data will reliably reach the receiver.

IPsec protocol:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/network-layer/what-is-ipsec/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:408103e4-e4ab-4dcf-a398-cb83461a2f0b .

camssa:6270915a-41d9-4f56-94fd-02502c28dec1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV provides mechanisms for extending concepts in order to align existing concepts or vocabularies with the DPV taxonomies, such as by declaring them as subclasses of a particular concept. This allows for the creation of domain or jurisdiction specific extensions, such as DPV-GDPR for expressing the legal bases provided by GDPR.

DPV Extending concepts for use cases:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#using-dpv-in-use-cases'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ef4e362-73a0-4562-906b-a5d3a267230c .

camssa:6271d758-3d1e-4d81-aa44-09e5df12fa2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAIS appears in the National Catalogue of France.  France gets a high performance on interoperability according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) Factsheets.\r
\r
National Catalogue of France:\r
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd6e4e9b-23cf-4639-9575-9f79739e7fcf .

camssa:62733107-ea3a-448c-b01c-c8ef236c9a98 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The centralised databases that GraphQL is able to generate actively promote visibility and the ruling of data insofar it facilitates the retrieval and publication of data in a system, thus having the potential to leverage administrative procedures.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37633063-fe2c-4269-aae4-43927e22452e .

camssa:627939c3-c1af-42cf-ba6e-09ca2c476ce1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:62798d72-12b4-455b-bd43-54fdfd14e0aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The first version of ODF was released in 2005, but it was not published as an ISO standard until 2006. It is implemented by LibreOffice, a worldwide Open document format that has the support of The Document Foundation, an open community focused on the improvement of LibreOffice.  \r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office\r
\r
The Document Foundation  \r
https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/ODF"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8935be6d-d149-495b-9a32-990fb8e8a096 .

camssa:627c767b-2af8-4fe8-bab9-837dd16c3ad1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification is an independent technology that takes a top-down approach to providing business process standardisation. In this context, the specification requirements also address interoperability, ubiquity, extensibility, security, transactions, and so on. Moreover, several initiatives in Europe have adopted the Universal Business Language (UBL), which is designed to be agnostic with respect to any EDI infrastructure and mapped to the ebXML core components.

Interoperable Europe Portal OASIS UBL reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/eprocurement/solution/oasis-universal-business-language-ubl

"ebXML and Web services" study:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/1200304

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:628409dc-2351-4216-a5ca-63cdc0cb5d8f .

camssa:627ed6d8-e1bb-4b56-812e-ca80d0be2959 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the forth star corresponds to represent data with URIs. According to the Odata home page, OData enables the publication of open data. This specification supports REST-based data services, allowing any resource, as well as open data, to be published and edited via simple HTTP messages.\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
Odata reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff1a931f-2de2-415c-b9e8-fd747a708ec2 .

camssa:627f7600-d4d8-45f3-b382-1fc947b7cd49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org grants data exchange permissions through the schema.org type DigitalDocumentPermission. Such metadata improves the reliability of data exchanged between citizens, businesses and public administrations.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
Schema.org reference, DigitalDocumentPermission type:\r
https://schema.org/DigitalDocumentPermission?msclkid=fe03a55bab5411eca9752ad0bc8beac1\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af01b519-4e19-4fd6-b119-145a758eae96 .

camssa:62802d53-aedc-4e1f-8619-b69f2d997747 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RegOrg is a business domain agnostic data model that can be reused in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
RegOrg about Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:19a4a587-95a1-4313-b5ce-651127690114 .

camssa:628409dc-2351-4216-a5ca-63cdc0cb5d8f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6287911c-5a3a-4b44-b8e8-7735a3abf547 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UDDI specification includes a flexible data structure that can be extended to accommodate additional types of data beyond the standard set. This extensibility is facilitated through the use of tModels (type models), which are abstract descriptions of concepts or business services within UDDI.

tModels UDDI reference:
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/uddi_v3.htm#_Toc85908315'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c265ac9-3530-4a3a-94c1-17013eeb2c46 .

camssa:6288db2b-bff0-4820-97ae-f9d22958e69c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI system does not inherently provide protection against unauthorized changes.Therefore, this criterion
is considered not applicable to this specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c75d96a4-138a-48a2-a939-06ab589a594a .

camssa:628a63bd-632e-4ccb-b2e4-f2378651ad74 a cav:Score,
