camssa:62a41b52-809b-4cf0-847a-91cbf796eb01 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI specification significantly enhances the facilitation of organizational interoperability agreements by
providing a standardized framework for the identification and referencing of legal documents across different
entities. Its design promotes consistency and compatibility, fostering a more seamless exchange of
information and collaboration among organizations.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3878f80-3a6e-404b-8383-0b0dc383e027 .

camssa:62a66610-fe18-4b5a-a693-55a7a01ea31e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:62a811b7-d60a-448e-8f1d-fec518a454f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"GraphQL does not provide any feature that contribute to covering authenticity aspects. Only the GraphQL JavaScript extension may process the user's authenticated viewer object via the rootValue argument when resolving a response.\r
\r
GraphQL specification, Authorization section:\r
https://graphql.org/learn/authorization/#gatsby-focus-wrapper\r
\r
GraphQL-JS extension:\r
https://graphql.org/graphql-js/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2dcca594-5dde-4158-b22f-d3da337457fb .

camssa:62ab1a8b-c1a8-4b79-bf5f-06cae0e45dd2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:62b89569-229c-499b-a692-567749d131c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA offers the possibility to manage and orchestrate resources for the provisioning of cloud applications and services. In this sense, when combined with other specifications, the specification can scope comprehensibility of data and services.\r
\r
TOSCA reference, section 1.2:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969412'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ea75fa8-6bd0-41eb-bbcf-e767e46fd658 .

camssa:62baa825-9653-4956-b5aa-ad46b8b84b16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 16234-1 e-CF framework is intended to serve as a device to represent the European e-Competence Framework, which focuses on skills and competences of the ICT professional workforce. There is no possibility to extend the specification, as EN 16234-1 e-CF has a single purpose.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b7b30e0-7149-4b47-b784-b79d74747c28 .

camssa:62bc2fb5-4ee5-4a57-89f9-9d14068b8815 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6ec33e201b803a1cc0150c0da8dc42b2a0f1029cf31e7a2c0fc81d1d8336ef36 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:62bf58a9-9d80-41a8-9fdf-1812a4bd80e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In accordance with ISO/IEC JTC 1 and the ISO and IEC Councils, ISO/IEC 19944-1 is classified as a Publicly Available Standard (PAS) and therefore is publicly available for Standardization purposes.\r
\r
ISO/IEC JTC 1:\r
https://jtc1info.org/\r
\r
Publicly available ISO/IEC standards:\r
https://standards.iso.org/ittf/PubliclyAvailableStandards/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff59cc8d-4d71-411c-bf19-3e255f1e504d .

camssa:62c40d11-a759-41fb-802a-a9614b7da3a4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:62c4d5dc-6efb-462a-89b9-f6eb6e1e0b56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de42e4f9-4569-47bd-b608-23a2f46aef07 .

camssa:62c67ed5-8656-40a5-be42-40a0fbcb24c8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:62ce15cb-fc12-4129-b511-5aa47c787f57 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog allows for customisation to a significant extent. The syslog protocol is designed to be flexible, and various elements within syslog messages can be customized based on specific needs and requirements. 
Some aspects of syslog that can be customised are: Message content, facility codes, severity levels, structured data, timestamp format, transport protocol, etc.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b735611-0d53-48c4-8c5f-9a928d434fcc .

camssa:62ce7aba-3faf-4b3b-ac04-6b5957419f66 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) allows for partial implementations. Implementing DoH can be done selectively for specific clients, applications, or DNS queries, rather than applying it universally across an entire network. This flexibility enables organizations to adopt DoH gradually or in a targeted manner. For instance, organisations can adopt DoH gradually by implementing it on a subset of devices or services. 

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f03e798-234c-462e-9f5b-de34241a173f .

camssa:62d3fe08-401e-4a36-8a23-8ed9bf706d69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML utilizes XML namespaces. This allows you to incorporate custom elements and attributes from other
XML vocabularies within your XHTML documents.As an example XHTML could be used in conjunction with
the MathML.

MathML Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/#ref-xhtml-mathml

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c87c060-6e08-4b40-b922-960d5c051f2d .

camssa:62d564c1-0809-41a5-8333-eb065bc78336 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OpenTelemetry significantly enhances the exposure and management of interfaces as it enables detailed tracking of API performance, improves reliability and user experience, offers deep tracing and diagnostic capabilities and helps ensure compliance and security. By leveraging OpenTelemetry, public administrations can ensure their services are robust, efficient, and user-friendly, leading to better service delivery.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66c06f63-9b31-4857-aa32-388e3c53bf96 .

camssa:62daa872-b272-4d5b-b981-f27a5aeb7532 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ef096f898c938883daab1b22e784cfaf985b5e5c855e170ecf6eab6f37b01b50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:62db3f41-792a-4f46-b5af-7bc956d3eff6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:62dbd7b7-c58e-4fb0-9dfe-6c3d34c5dc1b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of NFVI as a European standard. \r
\r
ICT technical specifications: https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue: https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09c33b6b-7939-4ccb-899c-ac18e6790e24 .

camssa:62e26e38-f5f8-4e27-a45d-002ca1ff2ae4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:62e3681e-7945-44fe-80f2-f7d725b43651 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33b5b305bcc0a995fd3c592dc8a6f52d0749a6e817aa85844f3e4f31c7dea344 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:62eac80e-2f16-489a-bdb5-16a7d3bedb1a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence of any assessment regarding the efficiency of this specification, nor any evaluation submitted by a European administration.\r
\r
Publications Office reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home\r
\r
Language codelist reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/language'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00ba8865-a299-4001-9dfb-c6efd8a6eeaa .

camssa:62f7e93e-5803-4df2-8053-e92042ee3d17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISO 639-2 code suite was developed to be used by libraries, information services and publishers to indicate language in the exchange of information, especially in computerised systems. Therefore, the specification prompts visibility of administrations by allowing, for instance, the publication of data or the display of web content in the language of the user. For example, the European Commission website (http://ec.europa.eu) can be switched into one of the official languages of the EU. \r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5\r
\r
Language codelist reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/language\r
\r
European Commission reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5161bd11-1542-4cf2-815e-a88afd5f045d .

camssa:62fb9d02-df21-46ab-bf9f-71eb2590effa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
