camssa:6301613f-e40c-47f0-a93e-5bb7111d0c54 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has published the major releases but no public documentation or supporting processes are available. 
The specification current version replaces the previous version from 1984 which was developed as an industry effort, attempting to get industry participants to agree on common network standards to provide multi-vendor interoperability. 
It was common for large networks to support multiple network protocol suites, with many devices unable to interoperate with other devices because of a lack of common protocols. When TCP/IP came into widespread use on multi-vendor networks for internetworking OSI was relegated. Nonetheless the OSI reference model is still in place in certain aspects like cloud computing


OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html

OSI and cloud computing
https://blogs.cisco.com/cloud/an-osi-model-for-cloud'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f374e99b-71c6-48a8-bb40-2e115f41c8df .

