camssa:659f4c86-b05c-4574-bcd3-c29ef7d612e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is technology-agnostic at the application layer, meaning it is not tied to a specific operating system, 
programming language, or underlying technology. Syslog operates at the network layer and focuses on the 
transport of log messages between devices and systems. This characteristic makes syslog a versatile and 
widely adopted logging protocol.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bf33a1e-6055-4dac-aedb-6f2329672ff0 .

camssa:65a37372-9844-4b01-bb3b-61dddbe64bf3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL encourages the creation of modular and reusable service descriptions. Developers can design services in a way that promotes consistency and reduces redundancy, leading to more maintainable and efficient systems. WSDL has adopted the "+xml" convention that is described in the IETF RFC 3023 defining XML data types and its security considerations. As an XML document, every implementation can have different security requirements.\r
\r
As an example of implementation is the SELIS project, which aims to make available a web services regarding the eInvoicing. This topic is included within the Once-only Principle and Digital Single Market frameworks. \r
\r
SELIS Documentation:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eprocurement/document/secure-electronic-invoicing-service-selis\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/\r
\r
WSDL IETF 3023:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/#RFC3023\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:61009a23-6a3d-4074-bd49-e82c6979b839 .

