    cav:value "2" .

camssa:678ed652-b6c2-4928-8d59-e00ff7056803 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) has established Working Groups. These Working Groups are open to the participation of everyone interested in semantic solution working for public administrations in the Member States or in EU institutions.\r
\r
SEMIC working groups:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:25396bae-c05d-47e4-8387-e28032f0db93 .

camssa:678f78db-db48-4ef4-be5b-2c980c991bfd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden.\r
\r
EuroVoc fosters interoperability between public administrations, cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment.\r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:270f693e-d770-4a86-94ab-f8e549424f46 .

camssa:67944bbc-dc44-4fa7-89d4-41ed9386530c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of SVG is to exchange and represent graphical information over the internet. Its compatibility with XML, CSS and other transformation elements like XSLT, allows the data portability of the information contained in SVG files. Also, it can represent graphical content from simple XML inputs.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/\r
\r
SVG and XSL: \r
https://www.w3.org/People/maxf/papers/2002-07-SVGOpen/svgopen.html#id2590005"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa4c1926-a9c3-432d-ad99-98066c3a79a8 .

camssa:679cee6e-a2f9-4cdc-b50b-f903b4f83574 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:679d01ea-9609-48f2-bd5e-5392eb81b673 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"No evidence has been found that ISAE 3402 is recommended by any European Member State's Catalogue.\r
\r
CAMSS list of standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specificationscamss\r
/camss-list-standards\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0317ff84-9533-4ea2-bb8a-78c5acb6c5d6 .

camssa:679e60c7-e19d-4fe9-af1d-4bb5febeec3d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:679fde0f-4a8c-4427-9f67-ed1080436dfb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The self-assessment model allows users to manage the development and deployment of software and adapt the actions to each specific purpose targeting depending on the organisation's needs. This fact helps public administrations to create and implement secure digital public services without wasting time and means. \r
\r
Moreover, the creation of secure digital public services fosters the eGovernment and the digitalisation reducing administrative burden.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec9740c4-7bcb-4d63-bad8-0d52a06c4390 .

camssa:67a7e806-3b9c-43ae-940f-0077be25667e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:67b6772a-9eaa-4309-9a2a-43f3a25cfe26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The first version of the specification was released back in 2009 and has been maintained and evolved on a community-driven basis until achieving version 2.0 released in 2020. The evolution of the specification involves a wide range of technical profiles and experience in the field of this specification. Through continuous improvement and discussion the specification has been released late in 2020 but with a cured development ensuring the maturity of the specification.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b93384f3-b7e7-4c3b-8e8b-470914ecf635 .

camssa:67c40216-2c3a-417e-87d2-a656faac9229 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP is a a protocol that determines the status of a digital certificate. Therefore, this criterion is not\r
applicable to the specification.\r
\r
OCSP reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be213b31-6070-43f4-ad80-c19350953869 .

camssa:67cad909-1320-4f65-8d36-1c1a6669961a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9cf3743-00a6-440b-898f-bd782faba11d .

camssa:67cbafc0-c5ec-4ad3-a2f3-c5c17cd1e7ee a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:67cbcfcb-222b-4c8e-946f-b09c828bb313 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SEMIC Support Center is responsible for the development of the specification. They are in charge of its maintenance, implementation pilots, knowledge sharing and, strategy and roadmap.

SEMIC in Joinup:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e0f5a30-ef76-46f5-8bc7-bfeda98fefa3 .

camssa:67d013f6-97ad-434d-b083-61129e64713b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) was defined in 2001 and is a cryptographic protocol for certifying timestamps using X.509 certificates and public key infrastructure. Moreover the IETF has published all documentation about TSP in the web. Therefore, it is demonstrated that TSP has enough maturity for its use in the development of products and services.

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0ef18c2-6fc0-4bcd-8806-c98e28c1eaf5 .

camssa:67d119d1-4121-4b58-8475-f05fadb0e9c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:67d51b4b-33c2-4616-8629-2cd94f97f573 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b8f7f5098ef900044e245ff5b30832215e00204b1e244545d80a28013685c811 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:67d80f5a-23c5-42d6-9092-a04b8da23afe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has an holistic perspective that goes from Legal to Technical aspects following the LOST approach from the European Interoperability Framework (EIF). This implies that EIRA can help Public Administrations to analyse and design digital public services that considers interoperability across views as requirements and also specifically the reuse of relevant information. The EIRA can help also with the use-centric approach from design, as it can help to establish the precise requirements that could later on extended by eGovERA and solutions focused on guaranteeing that users do not need to provide additional information. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca0eac23-7a91-47d6-86c6-9961570bcb2b .

camssa:67da9fc9-b121-4056-b5cc-88f921ae2f1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is not related to multilingualism. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb68453e-062a-451a-8940-191c2738e4be .

camssa:67de44fc-c880-40e4-b0a8-79a1a6a19fc5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:67df05db-a536-42be-abcb-552d51e2802f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP Cookies provides a way of addressing the secure and trustworthy processing of data by adding the "httpOnly" attribute to prevent access to Cookies via JavaScript, or by setting the "SameSite" attribute to "strict" when it is necessary to authenticate sensitive information from the user. In browsers that support SameSite, this ensures that the authentication cookie isn't sent with cross-site requests.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies security reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a13ba8c-c319-4602-a1b3-2dd6bab767de .

camssa:67e24faa-6963-48e8-9c0b-caeacf594626 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As defined on the TC standardisation, only TC members are involved in the development of ISO standards. A review is carried out to arrange the consensus firstly within the TC members and subsequently is reviewed by the different ISO member bodies. However, it cannot be considered a public review, because only TC members can participate.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e2133213-2c5c-4b96-8e61-3ae1679e4c35 .

camssa:67eb0234-d473-41cc-babb-1d3a33bab702 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DPV is not related to data integrity, therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d5c84bf-f48e-4549-a983-fd7cac99d960 .

camssa:67ecebba-1f25-4752-9cd6-dad6a1da0b42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Better regulation toolbox is an internal European Commission resource designed as a complement to the Commission's Better regulation guideline. It provides more specific and operational guidance to those involved with the various better regulation instruments. By allowing to make the data available to other persons or organisations, the Betterr Regulation Toolbox Contributes to the development of eGovernment reducing the administrative burden. \r
\r
Betterr Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1fb2ab60-ffc0-401a-82c1-f68b8c7c4845 .

camssa:67eebe84-1f1d-43fb-b74b-0750f6d766e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any European cross-border project using the TGF.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:06063acd-c2f7-46dd-b220-ce0367a48f09 .

camssa:67f14b63-8592-427e-a6dc-f272d5b0fa5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification defines a profile for the time-stamping protocol and the time-stamp token defined in IETF \r
RFC 3161. It defines what a time-stamping client supports and what a time-stamping server supports. \r
Time-stamp validation is out of scope and is defined in ETSI EN 319 102.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1bedf736-fc2e-44da-9c3a-5d34daf05ee4 .

camssa:67f232fd-8e7d-406d-bc37-e9c5e1df6d52 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification itself does not inherently provide any built-in mechanisms for ensuring the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. CSV is a simple, plain text format primarily designed for storing and exchanging tabular data.\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11e9516b-8017-4c38-8008-c6066e785f5d .

