camssa:683915b7-1b88-40c7-aac1-959896e4abd4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """When HTML 4 became a W3C recommendation it had a good acceptance, it was the best markup language in the market, but when XHTML and HTML5 appeared, its use decreased considerably. It can be seen in the following link, a comparison of usage of the different HTML languages and it is obvious that HTML 4 is near 0% of usage.\r
\r
XHTML trend:\r
https://try.powermapper.com/Stats/HtmlVersions"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71d7204b-c31a-4917-a801-411e40bdd028 .

