        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:68567b3b-f46c-4d24-ae87-27e8fc337ab6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The AKN4EU specification itself does not provide inherent mechanisms to protect information against unauthorized changes. However, several measures can be implemented to protect information integrity and guard against unauthorized modifications when utilizing the specification.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f2f17f0-890e-47f2-8e48-f52cdb43b717 .

camssa:6856932f-3832-4f97-988e-458412bd4e0d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:6856f4d2-5031-4744-ab2e-07bbeb96bafd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"While SCIM's primary focus is on the exchange of identity-related data, it can indirectly contribute to organisational interoperability agreements.For instance, SCIM provides a standardised protocol that helps ensure that different systems, even from different organizations, can understand and process identity data in a consistent manner. Furthermore, by adhering to SCIM, organizations can establish interoperable identity management practices and ensure consistency across systems.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41a6d892-eacc-4a21-b370-589cb8e73416 .

camssa:685b922c-be39-4ec8-bcd1-8a2b7d3637b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAML 2.0 can be used independently from any other technical specifications or operating system. The specification has been developed by OASIS Security Services Technical Committee independently from any specific platforms or technologies. Even though SAML 2.0 is XML based specifications, as XML is a well-known specification it does not cause technological dependency. \r
\r
See:\r
https://developers.onelogin.com/saml\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:70454e1f-72f9-4925-a66d-234ec5d454e5 .

