camssa:689cdd7c-2f68-4ef5-aae6-547e95eb1eb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 1.4 of the OAIS specification states that, although the archive has to support OAIS information model (section 2.2), the same does not define or require any particular method of implementation of the concepts. Moreover,  to be conformant with OAIS, all the responsibilities defined by the section 3.1 have to be fulfilled,  Nonetheless, there can be found some tools that help to assess archiving systems conformity to OAIS, but this is a ""proposed measurement"" not an official one.\r
\r
OAIS functional model conformance test: a proposed measurement:\r
https://www.emerald.com/insight/content/doi/10.1108/00330331211244850/full/html \r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f7ce9e7-6ef6-47d5-82b0-8c7dbca0c045 .

camssa:689e5436-c047-47a2-887c-e5ec4c28c005 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:68a0b5ab-9b99-4c0a-b61e-71142c9f0742 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"LDAP has various authentication methods to prevent from hostile agents. SASL is an example which supports a variety of authentication mechanisms. However, with the bing system that LDAP have, it insn't necessary to implement any implementation to guarantee the authentication. 

LDAP Authentication methods and security mechanisms:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4513.txt\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b63d1e0a-8ae2-4e99-8eb8-90a8ea82bded .

