    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:69145542-208f-4a48-a78f-52f154e2f9ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary can facilitate the modeling of business procesess by describing the characteristics and registration details of legal entities to ease data exchange between business registers.

Registered Organization Vocabulary specification reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:358e3230-f1cc-4d41-812b-0d91531cf430 .

camssa:69183e89-b3c4-4edb-a144-ae1998ba9cf4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:691b0c70-5483-4ca2-aa69-b0cba767f02f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WS-Security is an extension of SOAP specification to improve the security web services, so it is dependant on it."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20803488-cbe2-4aa0-a7ff-757679d2919e .

camssa:691dce4e-5378-4c31-8eaa-a9e386a6a8de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has been selected as one of the key elements for the data interchange between administrations and stakeholders. Europeana is using JSON within the Search API, the method created to diving into the european cross-border project data. These features allow retrieving information from EUROPEANA. Moreover, the Single Electronic Data Interchange Area (SEDIA) is using JSON as the basis to make data available for stakeholders. Examples SEDIA activity is the Call for Tenders, a key point on European eProcurement. Additionally, the EU Open Data Portal is another cross-border initiative that relies on JSON as a message format for API’s communication. \r
\r
EUROPEANA website:\r
https://pro.europeana.eu/resources/apis/search\r
\r
SEDIA website:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/support/apis\r
\r
EU Open data portal:\r
http://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/data/dataset/eu-open-data-portal-api"\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fde6460b-c396-4e1a-bc7b-ef87f0e5c98a .

camssa:691efada-d2ca-47bb-83e1-025fe6a2dbbf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:692065f6-f373-47c4-9954-8bd0cbe5fbdc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data,\r
the first star corresponds to the publication of data under an open license. OCSP generally uses open\r
source protocol syntax when determining the status of a digital certificate, such as HTTP and SMTP.\r
\r
OCSP reference, section 2:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d17b1d59-521b-471a-83ca-8e3428c974b0 .

camssa:692079ee-665a-4156-90e0-8653d8d5bd98 a cav:Score,
