camssa:694201e2-236a-4607-9a57-66d2e57f21fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As specification to structure data in order to allow the maximum interoperability between systems, RDF fosters the data portability between administrations at the same time that helps to enhance data discoverability and enabling the cross-data set queries using SPARQL. Specifically, RDF helps data portability and exchange between databases. The serialisation of RFD has several forms that ensure the availability of data, thus, supporting the implementation and evolution of European Public Services.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:527cb118-5662-4602-a82f-a986208be896 .

camssa:6942b9b5-76ed-45c7-b962-260a2506cd09 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:6946512b-3f19-4148-9b23-8e4bf3c2ff87 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6946f0db-e08d-4d4f-ab5d-c3ae40ed05a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Yes, the specification can enable digital service delivery channels. By providing a common, interoperable data format, it can help facilitate the exchange of information between different systems and applications supporting the implementation of European public services, including those delivered through digital channels in the legal domain.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae46df42-f4bb-4902-a01c-b756df2f7ffb .

camssa:694a87f3-e284-4ac8-b09a-997f4adec468 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There are no evidences of existing studies or documentation assessing the standard or specification in terms of effectiveness and efficiency to justify the criterion."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3f28541-5c8b-4299-9ad7-da7f0fd19497 .

camssa:694d0a50-6d68-48bd-b3dc-175c004d5148 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:694d3dc0-1f1f-4f08-846c-879e777b6a19 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Ogg has a good market acceptance. The online news portal Tagesschau was awarded for making all its video entries available in the open format Ogg. A few countries recommend Ogg as an open source multimedia container.\r
\r
Tagesschau awarded for Ogg:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/open-source-observatory-osor/news/former-german-justice-ministe\r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01efb001-7bc4-4b12-94fb-b5e7cab63688 .

camssa:694d75f5-0db7-4bd1-a3ef-0b1ae731cd9d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0514c5eb-96b7-48eb-a731-0ece7cde094b .

camssa:694dba74-3ee7-4d14-a868-cb1b7e2c1819 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6959cb97-baf9-498c-9c07-b38217a4b084 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Althought eh specification is not used a t EU level, the specification is used in the European Materials Modeling Ontology (EMMO) created by the European Materials Modelling Council (EMMC).

EMMO reference:
https://emmc.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ed347cc-61cf-409a-8a2c-22e509c7861b .

camssa:695eb001-d08b-4f75-a3c0-cafbb48584d3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-450e8a1f4cffbbf3de202e37bd642f098174559028df90ccc657473a6086bc0b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:69698221-12f2-4f6f-b791-736042edfe17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition. In this sense, ShEx addresses and facilitates interoperability between public administrations, and cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment. This is because of the fact that it has been designed to enhance the semantic and technical interoperability layers of ontologies expressed as RDF graphs, and RDF is a European Standard used by public administrations in projects for sharing Linked Data.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e5ca3ae-2b5c-4bdb-889b-e226928126fd .

camssa:6969a1ca-f4ac-47b6-adb6-4b95db55524f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fef5941bab92019b7692f8544de94715a42ed9ff76d89cbec4fb6f9821611925 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:696c7afb-3662-4aa6-83ec-65eeebe368fe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:696e8f70-863c-4a97-bf68-db1e4ed643f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OpenTelemetry’s design allows for flexible, partial implementations, making it highly adaptable to varying organizational needs and constraints. Its modular architecture, pluggable exporters, incremental instrumentation capabilities, configurable sampling strategies, and interoperability with existing systems all support the ability to adopt OpenTelemetry gradually.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f77bab5-96ad-4c36-98f0-f12f5d968917 .

camssa:69748d67-1c64-452c-b559-90267fff2ae4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family of documents allows for customization, enabling organizations or systems to tailor the PROV specifications to their specific requirements and domain-specific needs. For example, organizations can create domain-specific extensions to the PROV Data Model or define custom attributes to capture additional metadata or domain-specific information in their provenance representation.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a928af84-5fb2-461a-a44d-0faf9e70a3f1 .

camssa:69796edf-be69-404b-a40e-da80dade0eaa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

