camssa:6a03fb66-ebc9-44aa-8114-0758f70a0fb5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS is a hierarchical and decentralized naming system used to identify computers reachable through the Internet or other Internet Protocol (IP) networks.  For that matter it can be implemented in any domain.\r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1034  \r
\r
Domain Names - Implementation and Specification:                             \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035   '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eeca0b91-8b90-4041-839c-482bc65c6fc6 .

camssa:6a05be6d-d26c-4987-9291-639d831a8a7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ESPD is a modular document that consists of several sections, each of which covers a specific area of information related to the procurement process. Contracting authorities can choose which sections of the ESPD are relevant to their procurement process and request that suppliers provide the corresponding\r
information, therefore allowing for partial implementations.\r
\r
ESPD Business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7fa7a18-c53b-4438-adf5-b65c25a6ee75 .

camssa:6a09aaf3-4084-4eb3-ac53-b44efbef3127 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the Principle 3.5 of the E-ARK CSIP specification, the structure information packages must explicitly define the possibilities for adding additional components into the information package, therefore, allowing for extensions.\r
\r
 E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b6211f7-564e-4e17-a997-29080b7e8a59 .

