        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6a59a8ac-7b58-4716-bd14-3112ff080d7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the specification does not directly specify the sharing of results and data on European platforms, it is free and open for everyone to check their information and results, and join the community through GraphQL Foundation. There is also an open Discord platform community to join and a GraphQL Slack channel for historical discussions at European level.\r
\r
GraphQL Foundation Website: \r
https://graphql.org/foundation/         \r
\r
Discord - GraphQL Community Resources:\r
https://graphql.org/community/         \r
\r
GraphQL Europe Slack (historical discussions) channel at EU level:             \r
https://www.graphql-europe.org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:19cb9b92-3204-46aa-8270-1733a193fb94 .

camssa:6a5ba607-fbbd-4b4d-98e2-ae18140a9f6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The implementation of the specification fosters the data portability according to its purpose. CAdES Baseline profile has been developed to provide basic features necessary for electronic procedures including eSignature across borders. The implementation of CAdES Baseline Profile enhances the interoperability in the context of the European Single Digital Market. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d15f7822-b384-4893-b502-acf1889c873a .

camssa:6a5ea17b-ac70-4dab-84ed-a9e410b423bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6a65d91f-04f8-456b-a3b7-adadaa786ee3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST apis have 8 main security design principles that aim to provide a secure and trustwrthy exchange and processing of data.  \r
\r
REST API security essentials reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3cf971f9-3868-4bb6-93da-c5dd3c0f352e .

camssa:6a661845-300a-4645-aa41-7c1e86a1e412 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6a6918ee-9402-43bb-8285-0c0ec4c1567b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6a69f1e9-f2f0-4669-bb01-010a27000489 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of DCAT-AP is not related to the medullisation of business processes. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46062062-d7ba-4860-b5b4-d359070203e5 .

camssa:6a77aeab-a14d-4e96-b2c1-4fa65f8f9771 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:6a77af12-1191-4209-8488-ce1a87bc004b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSLT Baseline Profile is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, ASiC Baseline Profile can define the interoperability aspects.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/search?keys=xslt&page=0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0142ec37-9365-4e58-a4bb-f74977f30567 .

camssa:6a8df8a2-f455-4c26-adf4-f71e143aea87 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WSDL is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09dee33b-127f-4a43-997c-9dd8816fc1a6 .

camssa:6a91c223-07a9-49e9-abed-937a22d7fb43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the specification is using the SOAP Processing Model, it can adopt the HTTP binding to benefit from a consistent specification for an authentication credential, enabling authenticity in the process.\r
\r
SOAP Reference, Section 4.2 Binding Framework:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/#secconsiderations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7c2a54b-9921-4384-959b-741c83b3b50f .

camssa:6a91c8df-7027-4eba-b934-38c6e0a8e20b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, XML has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
See: \r
