        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined WS-Security-dev and the standard feedback from OASIS which is the process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. \r
 \r
See: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c07f1e40-0ea0-42a3-848e-bb0239da08a5 .

camssa:6bb3a06b-4184-4a32-8bf9-6c972eeb4deb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP can provide a common language and set of rules for web communication between different systems or users and services. This standardisation is important for the interoperability as it ensures that different implementations can exchange information effectively.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Semantics RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-routing-http-message

HTTP/1.1 Caching, RFC 9111 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7405e72e-cad8-4824-8c39-7b2eb3bff088 .

camssa:6bb87d97-7bbd-4761-b36b-7c4078b78cef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As one of the main markup languages for encode web resources, WS-BPEL is involved in the data exchange. WS-BPEL files are largely used to exchange information through the web.\r
\r
The specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68648dea-4d6e-4bce-be14-6cb0cef8badf .

camssa:6bbeb187-2bff-49c9-8090-923ee98dcdbb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is included in several national catalogues from Member States. A total of 14 countries listed the XML within their national catalogues (e.g. Belgium, France, Germany, etc.).\r
\r
See CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79207283-604a-456d-8308-a7a3e8e0a809 .

camssa:6bc1ebd5-3010-48ed-84c0-c9fe48eee4a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML is the standard markup language for web documents. It can be assisted by technologies such as Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) and scripting languages such as JavaScript.\r
It proportionates to the users an environment for cross-platform applications with access to device capabilities and accept all type of files to be published. So, it is proportionate to the needs of its users.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1efc82dd-0aee-4869-bb55-cd0409c16fc0 .

