camssa:6bc8a787-0c0b-49a1-99d0-8a4b2aedf5ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. Therefore, OCSP is\r
independent of any specific platform.\r
\r
OCSP reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2a50b24a-cb10-49e1-9827-7bef6e2a1bea .

camssa:6bd16375-aae5-4bd2-99c0-c5f96ca29d16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2b8f706d-0dab-4bae-9f0e-c49dae86be43 .

camssa:6bd576fc-4e8a-4464-9756-127c056b812d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification can be used independently from specific vendor products."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9cb6fe9e-9a83-4b06-82e8-954d45ef0b72 .

camssa:6bd7ada0-9a5b-4e7e-9353-eb319af3b3fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OWL2 has a positive impact on system interoperability. While developing ontologies with OWL2 a syntax is needed in order to store ontologies and to exchange them among tools and applications. RDF/XML syntax provides positive interoperability among OWL2 tools because it can be written and read by all conformant OWL2 software.\r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/\r
\r
RDF 1.1 XML Syntax\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8964ac25-38cc-49bc-9537-f497f9f6c56a .

camssa:6bd939f6-9da5-4627-b34f-e09ab6ef4c12 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6bdd3258-cc04-438f-91cb-c37b7e5ef981 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSD 1.1 is an open specification that can be used independently from other technologies or platforms. However, XSD 1.1 is defining datatypes which depend on definitions in XML and Namespaces in XML. This fact is not hampering the adoption of XSD as XML is worldwide adopted. \r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6bc80691-9368-48b3-8351-059fa09415f1 .

camssa:6bded7dd-7d82-44f1-b64e-52441ee1965f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification aims to be the basis for the development of public solutions that could be reusable across borders. It provides codebases that can be adapted to reach specific business requirements of certain implementations. Security is a key aspect when exchanging information and in this way, the specification states that when developing or implementing public source it should be enabled communication points to communicate regarding security aspects.\r
\r
Moreover, the flexibility that codebases grant allows administrations to integrate specific security capabilities to ensure a secure and trustworthy data exchange. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3cdb5c9a-4aa7-4494-ae6e-b01a191c892f .

camssa:6bdf415f-85fe-4f28-a34f-a872d7e4ec7b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33ea90f5c1bb01d4398c57d03a25934dc5722d5ddbc98a43911ea4fb302ec54c ;
