    cav:judgement "The specification can be used independently from specific vendor products."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82fa95e1-ffae-4c06-8899-3b33087516f2 .

camssa:6c0a2e9f-e70a-40d2-8a89-52a7ec4992ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of OData, operates under RF (royalty-free)
on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. Therefore, the specification is licensed on a Royalty-free and mostly aligned with F/RAND principles.

OASIS Intellectual Property guidelines, section 5.2:
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/#contributions'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e2218c9-d038-4552-b3fc-a837fb0c86cd .

camssa:6c0cdcad-2d04-41dc-acc8-fc26636d6285 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Vocabularies can be used as the foundation of common export formats for data in base registries like cadastral, business registers or public service portals. The Core Location Vocabulary is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of a location, represented as an address, a geographic name, or a geometry. \r
\r
By describing locations (addresses, geographical names, etc) in a common way using both human and machine-readable format, it allows the publication of information as linked open data for its consultation and reuse.\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary\r
\r
Use cases and benefits of ISA² specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/docs/publications/isa2_study_use_cases_and_benefits_of_isa2_specifications_january_2019.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ee55687-95f9-461e-b196-ff18e6dc2c79 .

camssa:6c201831-2926-4ac8-8c66-17761f05ad33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CPSV-AP is a reusable and extensible data model for harmonising the way public services are described in a machine-readable format. So it describes the public administrations and eases their visualization and comprehensibility.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f677b545-0fb5-48a0-91a1-7d5f8a667946 .

