    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c3ea5d5-144b-4fa3-a2c6-ed4fc747c7de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Taking the initial purpose of the specification, which is to enrich connector identities by issuing up-to-date information in form of signed claims, it can be considered that the specification is involved in fostering the comprehensibility of Public Administrations data as well as relevant data produced for the \r
decision-making process.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d614141f-64de-4a1b-b09e-e84fc74705f9 .

camssa:6c3ecde9-6981-4c94-8328-a86717ab4693 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of TOSCA is not related to the secure exchange of data. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
TOSCA reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3106034-7354-4d5e-9945-6fdf0c75c1d4 .

camssa:6c464b13-cb3d-42c6-9d3c-3889254f559e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c5244c7-c794-4f02-a4b7-d1fb9b64aa7d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cac1c963ee5c3624035d7a98a8577db18d04ad6528afc51785f1230f23566ff1 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:6c526902-4fc5-43af-a768-2a4788fb93a7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:6c54a322-05b4-43cf-b047-0b9139710fed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been developed under a voluntary agreement between the Member States aiming to enhance the legal framework and the cooperation between administrations for building an interoperability environment across borders. \r
\r
Council communications and conclusions "Council Conclusions published on 26 October 2012 (2012/C 325/02)", and the "Council conclusions of 6 November 2017 on the European Legislation Identifier" are the official legal document where ELI is defined. \r
\r
Council Conclusions published on 26 October 2012 (2012/C 325/02):\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52012XG1026(01)\r
\r
Council conclusions of 6 November 2017 on the European Legislation Identifier:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52017XG1222(02)\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3678444e-9409-4cf4-8950-e4065bc7f2e7 .

camssa:6c59a03b-bdc6-4bf5-a25a-45c2328e09da a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c5b86d5-0116-4adb-979d-b098d6f0c05f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although TOSCA is widely known in the field of cloud computing, the specification offers versatility, as it runs in a container (or software unit) and specifies orchestration process models that enable the management of services, as well as their use in various domains, independently of the application context. \r
\r
TOSCA reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e789410-87f3-45d3-a5cb-bdd7322ee8ec .

camssa:6c5fc144-a013-4daa-9297-574f5992589b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0229101dfe08cbe58da1e454363d30a8178a2e120466c8db23965488cae5c8b1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6c616f1c-0196-47f9-a629-2f67daf1d7d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By associating a name to an IP, DNS facilitates the identification of the content of domains and therefore, it 
can be said to reduce the administrative burden. Currently the EU is working on creating secure DNS services for the european organisations and citizens.

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499

Backbone networks for pan-European cloud federation (CEF-DIG-2021-CLOUD)
https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/cef-dig-2021-cloud-dns-works'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:449f416c-6b89-4ab8-a746-fb303c4857fe .

camssa:6c649213-b95e-4e2a-96d3-a6822db1aa78 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c693dbf-99e4-4913-85e8-5b56681b7824 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of HTTP has been shown through its evolution into HTTP/3. HTTP/3 improves speed and reliability by using modern transport protocols, addressing the limitations of earlier versions. These advancements show that HTTP continuously adapts to meet new technological and security demands, proving its lasting efficiency.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

Measuring HTTP/3: Adoption and Performance:
https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.12358'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f18d8ee2-2e5b-4566-81bc-0d761ffacf10 .

camssa:6c6e95a9-22af-4cfc-ac2e-7b2d1208f550 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c742f3d-aff0-479f-beb2-b180b842b38f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c7c5ebf-f0c9-4b1b-ae02-f1698e0d6bc3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """eDelivery SMP 1.10 is part of the eDelivery Building Block (BB), which is provided by CEF and aims to help public administrations to share electronic data across borders in a reliable way. The BB eases the integration between implementers fostering the creation of interoperable infrastructures used for the digital data exchange. \r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/How+does+eDelivery+work"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:909cc1b3-20d0-4005-8bc0-ea9f5aa60ef7 .

camssa:6c7d0ee4-0f85-4ea0-b963-ccf1c2c55c32 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Executive Committee has to review and coordinate the progress of the TCs and, from time to time, review the terms of reference given to Technical Committees. In addition, the Technical Committee shall review and approve the minutes of the preceding meeting. Although Ecma is the SDO that first developed the specification, it is currently being maintained by the IETF, thus, adhering to the development process defined by the organisation, which comprehends public reviews.\r
\r
ECMA Directives:\r
http://www.ecma-international.org/memento/policies.htm\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:676bbd2c-766b-4653-85f2-f41ddfeca425 .

camssa:6c80a8ba-6659-4b94-a860-7f2e4c1e79d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SAML 2.0 is not related to ensuring and enabling data processing accuracy. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:173a03ad-d928-47be-bc19-74ae11a011ec .

camssa:6c845b09-a0a4-4a83-89b6-11f3067bb463 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Insufficient information is available to conclusively determine whether this criterion is met. Furthermore, the
specification does not appear to be designed with the explicit goal of enhancing data exchange security and
privacy. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7a8642e-1a98-4c68-b733-e8e99f66c43c .

camssa:6c93e2e7-37b6-4248-9dc2-5b9a0ffb8314 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6c97f3cf-221e-48ed-8d4c-6ee97781941c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6c9b838b-f133-42db-bf0f-f76257a4ebef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XAdES is not related to the visibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7002996-3b35-4e19-8b9f-26a2abddab69 .

camssa:6c9c061d-50ab-48d1-a6f2-592ebc880ab1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XSLT's main function is transforming XML data, which is essential for interoperability between different systems. In European public services, which often involve diverse systems and data formats, XSLT can convert data between these formats, ensuring seamless information exchange. An example of usage is at the European Single Procurement Document (ESPD). XSLT is used to transform ESPD documents into different formats, such as PDF or HTML, making them accessible and readable across various platforms and devices.

European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) Github Reference:
https://github.com/OP-TED/ESPD-EDM

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11ae4ba8-edc4-4d9a-bfb2-31dd79f3c27b .

camssa:6ca04df0-609c-49a9-ba9b-fbd7f0d2f5e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification is included in the solutions catalogue of ICT Standards for Procurement created by the 
European Commision. The European Catalogue will contribute to these objectives by offering a one-stop shop for procurers on guidelines for procurement, including on vendor lock-in, on the use of standards, and a 
lifecycle costing scheme that accounts for the often neglected interoperability costs. It will streamline the 
numerous guidelines and provide for a platform of exchange and dissemination.

ICT Standards for Procurement: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f52fc2ce-b21b-4778-8e71-7e39307c135f .

camssa:6ca2953f-fd6d-4fd9-ac97-e5d6baba3911 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML is one of the main markup languages to develop web resources. XHTML files are used to exchange
information through the web. This fact proves that XHTML fosters data portability between systems and
applications.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8a0dc4b-a41d-413f-8484-80900f4287c6 .

camssa:6ca71657-6530-44d7-896f-d0779f66381d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Conformance requirements of DNS queries over HTTPS (DoH) are expressed with a combination of descriptive assertions. The key words “MUST”, “MUST NOT”, “REQUIRED”, “SHALL”, “SHALL NOT”, “SHOULD”, “SHOULD NOT”, “RECOMMENDED”, “MAY”, and “OPTIONAL” in the normative parts of this document are to be interpreted as described in BP14.

BCP 14: https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/bcp14'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21d2b427-aa33-4391-9718-7840f7010e40 .

camssa:6ca8bd2e-f0ee-40e0-9121-6e83bc24a905 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State recommending EN 16234-1 e-CF in its ICT National Catalogue.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e5ce812-b301-4db9-8393-22b2257d879b .

camssa:6cae9608-6aad-4dfb-a9c4-bc0667ece677 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6cafbb1e-1238-4627-a09a-206b1300d602 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpopse of Indexed Database API is not related to comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a46ca13-f5a8-475c-b1fb-bced775d33c2 .

camssa:6cb8dfb1-988e-4b5a-bf9e-34cd98f13e11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS is an attribute server that issues OAuth2 access tokens to International Data Spaces connectors. The connectors need these to access the services and data of other connectors. the decision about permitted access is not made by DAPS but always by the requested connector itself. Therefore, DAPS merely administers the International Data Spaces attributes of the registered connectors.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ced338e-066a-454d-a7d3-936a2dfeb52a .

camssa:6cbf52c6-508b-411d-8c68-2bcbcb5ae4a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is not directly used in any European Cross-border initiative, but IDTA it is including the GAIA-X services. In this sense AAS has been included in some GAIA-X initiatives that are cross-border such as the Digital Product Passport.

Digital Product Passport reference:
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2212827124003482

IDTA and GAIA-X:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/use-cases/demonstrator-collaborative-condition-monitoring-data-sharing-as-win-win

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c6e95a9-22af-4cfc-ac2e-7b2d1208f550 .

camssa:6cc126f2-1677-44d3-9825-d29d56b4efd6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPv4 has been selected within the cross-border project of The Compendium from the National Research and Education Networks in Europe (NREN). The Compendium structures its services in an IP-based network using mainly IPv4. The protocol acts as the backbone of the Pan-European network provided by GEANT.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.geant.org/Resources/Documents/Compendium2016.pdf\r
https://www.geant.org/Networks/Pan-European_network/Pages/Home.aspx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7405ba5c-de95-480c-9e91-df6b643a5561 .

camssa:6cc99687-b0ff-44b9-b8aa-07d42f59065b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the moment of performing the assessment, UDDI is one of the foundations of web services together with SOAP and WSDL. Even there is a new implementation mode as is REST, SOAP is still active and highly used in the creation of new solutions including innovative solutions. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de23fe18-9013-4a54-a6c6-03e0ca83a94a .

camssa:6cca244f-376d-4c24-9ec2-79a706a4f559 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6ccaba4c-3098-4a89-8105-a9b6cac60029 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS provides a standardised method for describing assets and their distributions. Therefore, while providing a common way and components for the metadata provision, it helps the comprehensibility of data and services of Public administrations across borders.\r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0eb3bc58-ea17-46d2-8ff4-326520d25168 .

camssa:6ccb5a46-439c-42da-9a6d-74819b3a1185 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog, as a protocol for message logging, is not specifically designed for the long-term preservation of data, 
information, or electronic records. Its primary function is to transmit and store log messages related to 
system events, errors, and activities.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b85a92a-7cd5-4f6b-b603-b9343afa270c .

camssa:6ccf6540-a411-4187-acca-5698fc41690d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0375e3f4-07e0-4273-953d-1a77df8c095c .

camssa:6cd29fdd-0ce4-4447-8067-cf3d42534281 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"WSDL itself doesn't enforce or dictate language-specific aspects, it provides a foundation for describing the technical aspects of web services. The broader considerations for multilingual support involve design choices, documentation practices, and the implementation of the web service itself.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c4cd5d5-6036-40a1-841e-0aec585344bc .

camssa:6cd2f9ad-8399-4b84-9881-077d2a4884ac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:6cd94cdb-d49c-4c89-90f6-906cb6874f92 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is not included in any Member State national catalogue for ICT. Despite this, eDelivery SMP 1.10 is a European profile recommended by the European public bodies in order to establish a common interoperability framework."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a06670f-ce56-496d-b847-f245785add53 .

camssa:6cd9af12-cb9a-453f-9e0b-afe9c9e42dcd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ebXML is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, ebXML can define the interoperability aspects of the "Registration" ABB of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/v610

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1733a9df-f784-4575-aa16-76689760d240 .

camssa:6cda24e1-0e93-4050-81c3-8dd21206fd35 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing studies assessing the effectiveness of DNS. Particularly, there seems to be a general 
interest on the effectiveness of DNS security extension mechanisms, and on the DNS Tunneling tools. 

Exploring Domain Name-Based Features on the Effectiveness of DNS Caching: 
https://ccronline.sigcomm.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/p36-hao.pdf 

A Comparative Performance Evaluation of DNS Tunneling Tools:
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Alessio_Merlo/publication/221271469_A_Comparative_Performance_Evaluation_of_DNS_Tunneling_Tools/links/00b4951c1e5065b0e6000000/A-Comparative-Performance-Evaluation-of-DNS-Tunneling-Tools.pdf 
Performance assessment and analysis ofDNS tunneling tools:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235996771_Performance_assessment_and_analysis_of_DNS_tunneling_tools

A survey of domain name system vulnerabilities and attacks:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/345017736_A_survey_of_domain_name_system_vulnerabilities_and_attacks '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a07cd84-6ab4-4038-b57c-55047113a368 .

