camssa:6d94c88f-a56e-4f53-9e24-49b2a536a54a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT specification is a language designed for transforming XML data. This functionality is applicable to any domain that uses XML as a data representation, generating different output formats for different use cases.

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a8fc4ba4-fc73-4c1d-abf9-aebf36a722d2 .

camssa:6d98c923-1ffb-4990-837b-0cd31436544e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the purpose of OWL2 is not related directly to long term preservation of electronic records, there are examples of ontologies developed for the preservation and maintenance of metadata in archives systems. An example of this is the Library of Congress initiative PREMIS OWL Ontology. \r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/\r
\r
PREMIS OWL Ontology\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/premis/ontology/index.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d65c464-9048-430e-b95f-bd4f4dcb9510 .

camssa:6d9b914b-2e97-4ce3-8ae4-f57cac82539e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of ebXML, operates under RF (royalty-free) on RAND (reasonable and non-discriminatory) Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. Therefore, the specification is licensed on a Royalty-free.\r
\r
OASIS Intellectual Property guidelines, section 5.2:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b2452279-09dc-4ab8-9f09-24e8a649f5fa .

