camssa:6e0cdf4d-4fe5-42ac-baf3-89f2c1318d3a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All XIPH standards are under BSD-style license which is a specific license for open source specifications. More specifically it is a free-software license with only minimal restrictions on how the software can be used, modified, and redistributed, usually including a warranty disclaimer.\r
\r
XIPH documentaiton:\r
https://wiki.xiph.org/index.php/Main_Page"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e7b9048-5909-4aef-a31d-6ab954af4815 .

camssa:6e12a185-be1b-456d-8f97-f18ef6beb286 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is technology-agnostic, meaning it does not depend on any software or platform.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2fb7011c-0d0a-42de-ba49-0cda5db5d82c .

camssa:6e1c2f08-0f60-475d-8bd6-0d57badda547 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol is a set of specifications designed to negotiate Agreements, among other functions. The Contract Negotiation Protocol and Contract Negotiation HTTPS Binding documents section of the specification definese how Contract Negotiations are conducted and requested via HTTPS endpoints. Furthermore, IDSA Rulebook aims is to describe clearly which rules are mandatory and which are optional guidelines. This governance framework includes functional, technical, operational, and legal dimensions.

Contract Negotiation Protocol: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/contract-negotiation/contract.negotiation.protocol

IDSA Rulebook: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/idsa-rulebook/idsa-rulebook/1_introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:19ffbf1d-0962-48ca-a2cb-5ecee66eb98e .

camssa:6e1cf3b3-d535-4be0-b97c-ae82bfbcc420 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The WAI-ARIA specification itself does not provide means for the restriction of access to information or data.Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e66c829c-2e09-4433-83dd-92e7cd6f32b8 .

camssa:6e1fff2b-8263-40af-bc22-3fc828a368c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XACML is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02b8eb73-0fc7-4107-9caf-ca8fb4077c32 .

camssa:6e214c79-1958-45a3-8911-6c52f93b89b9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6e217c09-321b-4f72-8356-adcae7a66ef0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Public Service Vocabulary Application Profile 2.2 is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, this Core Vocabulary can define the interoperability aspects of the "Core Data Model" and "Data" ABBs from the EIRA Semantic view.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:042e8259-e1d8-4dd4-b375-5d582ae95e12 .

camssa:6e26936e-7afe-4668-a47b-4d8e92eef486 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:6e26bb04-34e5-479e-9b32-81fc7983b8fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this specification is not related to reduce administrative burden. The main purpose of Ogg is to proportionate a multimedia open source format/container. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:966a9b6a-42a1-4aca-89da-a9dec12a5f86 .

camssa:6e2ee6ad-03e3-452d-9043-7d601ad146aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IDSA was formed in 2017 to develop the IDS (formerly known as Industrial Data Spaces) reference architecture model and certification procedures based on industry requirements thus, DAPS is related to facilitating organisational interoperability agreements.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7de88972-4992-4002-8752-6af1be16efcb .

camssa:6e2fa976-97f1-4ff4-b8ea-2e63f93bf091 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "83%AssessmentScoreAverage",
        "90%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:6e302778-8ddc-4200-b4e5-ed0b6b13b776 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the primary focus of OpenTelemetry is on observability and monitoring of digital systems, it indirectly supports the long-term preservation of electronic records by ensuring the integrity, reliability, accessibility, and security of the underlying infrastructure. OpenTelemetry can improve long-term preservation of electronics resources through the integration with storage backends.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c0fbafa-81a6-4940-9db7-6f284db8d44c .

camssa:6e31409e-4244-4614-a738-11477fe806d6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:6e319fcc-eafd-4064-ba16-df64c976fbb7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:6e369550-5515-479b-b78a-668b231ab461 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData queries and shares data across different systems via RESTful interfaces. RESTful APIs may be platform-agnostic, without any dependency on the environment or programming language being used, and in this case OData primarily exists to expose data in a platform agnostic manner so that .NET, Java, Php, Python, REST, etc clients can all access the data. So, the specification is platform-agnostic.

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2af4c072-7c67-47a9-bebd-de62b9ae3a6c .

camssa:6e449d6e-b8a1-4776-ba26-367d5207e9ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architecture style that defines how different systems should interact. REST APIs generate a way of accessing web services in a simple and flexible way without having any processing,Therefore allowing for a comprehensible display of administrative procedures, and services.\r
The french government website data.gouv.fr which hosts the french governments datasets is built under the REST architectural style.\r
\r
REST reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/\r
\r
Data.gouv.fr reference:\r
https://doc.data.gouv.fr/api/intro/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d0eabdb-8460-4960-8c63-2ae8a8c78943 .

camssa:6e44ce38-bac3-4552-bb65-91cccf505c67 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "83.59%AssessmentScoreAverage",
        "86.67%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:6e451cc0-fcdf-48ca-aaea-4e6dbfee13de a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6e45a6e4-62e6-4091-b297-2c9c3f6e02e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, HTTPS has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:238d2c98-acf0-4263-85f5-616c5eaa8d67 .

camssa:6e45b807-6c5a-4cd5-aa35-653480411ebe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:6e4be6de-4bf1-4f08-9443-e93a3218518a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6e5a9e0d-a895-44d9-a3ab-3c9c059eb0b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e9e0cf4a339c837607828404dd0e9b360d643528fcc1df488a95ca67166acea3 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:6e5be1c5-d2d0-438a-9fa0-be7fd0b7faf6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 7.9 of the specification focuses on the component for language selection. This component shall be used to request a preferred language of the response and shall be specified according to IETF RFC 5646. The service should provide language-specific responses using the requested language. In the case the requested language is not supported then no error shall be raised and the responses shall be produced in the SCS default language.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf

IETF RFC 5646: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc5646/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd416ba9-a147-47c7-97b4-e1cc8c082b5a .

camssa:6e608c20-7dc2-46e1-b9cc-dbf9c5f8938d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec allows the exchange of data between systems, supporting the evolution of European public services. An example of its implementation is the TESTA project, which provides a secure cross-border data communication network service for public administrations.\r
\r
IPSec reference, What IPSec Does:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-7\r
\r
Interoperable Delivery of European Egovernment Services to Public Administrations, Businesses and Citizens (IDABC) Reference Link:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/idabc/en/document/2097.html\r
\r
TESTA Service:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cfe7e13d-725f-4c05-9899-6c8de601f9fe .

camssa:6e64bcb4-c47d-4f66-bb71-15b1d6840722 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is completely open to newcomers. There is no formal membership, no membership fee, and nothing to sign. The IETF's standards development work is organized into 8 Areas Each Area has 1 or more Area Directors (ADs), which together comprise the Internet Engineering Steering Group (IESG). The IESG is responsible for technical management of IETF activities, the Internet standards process, and for the actions associated with entry into and movement along the Internet ''standards track'', including final approval of specifications as Internet Standards and publication as an RFC. Within each Area there are multiple Working Groups (WG). Each WG has one or more chairs who manage the work, and a written charter defining what the work is and when it is due. There are more than 100 WGs. The WGs produce Internet Drafts (I-Ds) which often lead to the publication of an Internet standard as an RFC.\r
\r
See: http://www.ietf.org/newcomers.html """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:faf51c62-5e8c-4443-964b-8e539561ab6b .

camssa:6e64f44b-0457-456f-83c9-78c0a9ce7a37 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GITB TDL is maintained and supported by the interoperability test bed team. Further developments have been carried out by the developer community regarding GITB TDL that can be viewed at its webpage.\r
\r
GITB TDL change history reference:\r
https://github.com/ISAITB/gitb/tree/master/gitb-validator-tdl/src/main/java/com/gitb/vs/tdl\r
\r
JOINUP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/detailed-information#releases'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85caf7d0-c022-4d0f-aae2-7fe4d0c5a1ab .

camssa:6e687d34-326a-4942-8cbb-54a50fa989ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This specification is currently included in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS).
Currently the specification is listed in the following ABB's:
DataManagementApplicationService, DataAnalyticsApplicationComponent, DataAnalyticsApplicationService, DataManagementApplicationComponent

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/version-610\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:943bc76c-1644-4990-bcf9-b9f58e94a6ad .

camssa:6e693bd7-a203-4686-8da3-a8289e7226f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of DCAT-AP is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fae01b12-1577-42da-9a97-9871e23ec7d3 .

camssa:6e70e1f3-44bd-4d59-a2cf-cd91b30d88d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed in 2012 and has been implemented at European level, and it has been evolved together with the application profile used in the European Platform for the reusability of interoperability Solutions, Joinup. \r
\r
ADMS in Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:296dcc0e-6e85-4914-85be-9b6692c6c2de .

