camssa:6e7a54ee-a940-41da-979a-bfcf65330e33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "As a specification that enhances the discoverability and access to different web services, it can help to ensure access by providing SOAP endpoints where the services and internal information are located. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:301da8cc-7269-4b97-8b91-898e082bb746 .

camssa:6e7aa267-fc76-4b01-8e32-6f753281fe3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Criteria used to define NUTS codes do exist, but there is not a reference document to this end: 'NUTS 1981- NUTS 1999' and 'REGULATION (EC) No 1059/2003'.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, History of NUTS section, 'NUTS 1981 - NUTS 1999' document, 'Structure of this document' section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/history\r
\r
EUR-LEX reference, REGULATION (EC) No 1059/2003' document:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/ALL/?uri=CELEX:02003R1059-20180118&qid=1519136753473\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a59a1a1-b211-482a-98e9-4fc58f3469b1 .

camssa:6e7cf95b-40bd-489b-ad51-3d1e8dae90d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 27001 includes requirements for the assessment and treatment of information security risks tailored to the needs of the organization. The requirements set out in this International Standard are generic and are intended to be applicable to all organizations, regardless of type, size or nature.  \r
\r
ISO 27001 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso-iec:27001:ed-2:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a174f64f-3dee-4c30-a0b0-4098bf79a343 .

camssa:6e8582b3-53b1-4974-ac52-63f8aff1001e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6e8bdc3d-bbcd-477e-a663-d449730bb54e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"DNS Queries over HTTPS (DoH) is included in the EU-funded SAPPAN project, which seeks to introduce a privacy-preserving sharing and automation platform to facilitate efficient response to and recovery from cyberattacks. DoH has been created to improve users' privacy on the internet and it will develop a cyberthreat intelligence system to assist security and IT personnel within and across organisations in timely responding to threats. 

SAPPAN Project: https://sappan-project.eu/

DoH Insight: https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3407023.3409192\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42e42861-f8be-4790-9a86-eebebad09a8e .

camssa:6e8f00f8-a183-405a-9a94-0d9a25575bfc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL foresees support for multilingual context as it provides clear rules for extension and a number of subsets and tool resources such as localization dictionaries in Chinese, Danish, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Spanish and Turkish. This enables communities to create explicit extensions that are locally profiled for their context of use.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
The Meaning of UBL: The Value of a Semantic Data Model:\r
http://ubl.xml.org/forum/the-meaning-of-ubl-the-value-of-a-semantic-data-model'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa7af8ba-10ae-41e2-bede-4543dc12310a .

camssa:6e8fc3f9-bde4-4fb3-9574-1976305ba333 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The majority of real-world ebXML messages have unique XML-based, message-level security requirements, including digital signatures, non-repudiation, data privacy, and content-borne threat protection. As described in the Oracle document about security features, these message-level mechanisms provide protection over and above transient application layer security such as SSL/TLS. Therefore, the specification can help to ensure a secure exchange of data between users.

ebXML security:
https://www.oracle.com/technical-resources/articles/enterprise-architecture/ebxml-security1.html

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cf07008-ca53-478f-a921-123c78a2af4e .

camssa:6e971b6b-8eb8-497c-a5ed-845b7b85b06a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6ea1282d-4bc7-49db-9e13-dfb06bddb716 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv6 incorporates some security and privacy-adressed extensions. In addition, there are extension headers, each identified with a different Next Header value, which allow additional features and better flexibility. In addition, an IPv6 packet may carry zero, one, or more extension headers.

IPv6 extension:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460#section-4'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb1df50e-e388-439e-8d29-84907d586219 .

camssa:6ea69e7f-da5e-49f6-94ef-38b7ab127103 a cav:Score,
