camssa:6f2f015b-7940-451e-8e0a-2d03961f1191 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, CSV has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
CSV being compliant with 1025/2012 regulation Reference: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32012R1025'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d64cdf6d-cd36-4880-8ddd-3bc1fcc43396 .

camssa:6f2fe135-e015-424e-9ddc-56089644f789 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The classification scheme outlined in ISO/IEC 19944-1 is intended to be flexible and adaptable, allowing it to be applied across different cloud platforms and architectures.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1abd80a3-3312-4acc-93f8-903b6cdda1e9 .

camssa:6f38856a-40d4-44f0-ad92-144ec2552be0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6f3a0198-4250-49a6-a5ce-da034cab0300 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'An OAIS should take into account the intellectual property rights concepts, such as copyrights, patents and any other applicable laws (e.g., data protection) prior to accepting restricted materials into the OAIS. It can establish guidelines for ingestion of information and rules for dissemination and duplication of the information when necessary.  Nonetheless it does not explicitly address GDPR compliance.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47528f23-889f-4985-8af6-f675d609a688 .

camssa:6f3ef7fc-bac2-475c-b611-3d40762a023f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:6f460788-30ce-420e-9bcf-99c7cd691510 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been selected within the scope of LEOS project to develop the LEOS software, which aims to ease the drafting and edition of legal documents. \r
\r
LEOS: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/justice-law-and-security/solution/leos-open-source-software-editing-legislation"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce3a6cd9-fe25-4ff9-adc5-142ba255068c .

camssa:6f489f59-c10f-4d25-98ff-26ffdcf7e7e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec is a business domain agnostic specification and therefore can be used in any domain.\r
\r
List of IPSec Implementations:\r
http://www.mit.edu/~tytso/ipsec/surv9607.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74030871-d3b7-48e6-abab-8a9e345c481d .

camssa:6f4c7e88-1a85-47cf-ab0a-ec631e146930 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be9b50cf-b189-4579-a251-fcc2fe3835d0 .

camssa:6f4eab65-8055-4b12-b11e-d77eea0c974c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-31bf959b6c4a983ec70eb87e0177f2739575ebce42c7c3b95b9012ef3bfe673e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6f4f0708-e430-4069-9325-072f72dbc350 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a solution developed by the  SEMIC action of the ISA2 Programme funded by the European Commission, DCAT-AP is part of their supra-national catalogue of reusable solutions.\r
\r
SEMIC repository of specifications - DCAT-AP:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/our-solutions\r
\r
ISA2 Solutions:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22a131af-d2a2-41c2-bff6-b852432c013e .

camssa:6f5004b0-5d46-4a62-a92f-55b20020eee0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTML5 is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39292da8-ce26-446a-887a-f90255559e84 .

camssa:6f507e8c-8607-4709-b1ba-989569c8cfa8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As it happens with all the e-Government Vocabularies, it has the SEMIC action from the ISA2 as responsible for the maintenance of the development.\r
\r
SEMIC in Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a8aa0db-bfae-4765-93da-994403fd6a54 .

camssa:6f563221-73f8-44a7-8247-4aba80877a17 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-838030847fa0adf54939e3feaac0ac2510924c54035e1cb671b223b54b02fd70 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:6f589f77-9970-4d93-98ee-89fa7ecd54fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Open & Agile Smart Cities & Communities (OASC) are an international network of cities and communities that partners with local administrations of all sizes and all over the world to assist them in their journey towards digital transformation. They facilitate seamless sharing and re-use of digital, data-driven solutions to avoid vendor lock-in, to reduce innovation costs and improve efficiency, thanks to open standards and APIs (application programming interfaces). One of the standards mentioned in their blog is CIM NGSI-LD API, particularly how it targets Smart City applications and government services, which is an indicative evidence of its positive market uptake.

ETSI Releases Full-Feature Specification to Support Smart Cities & Communities: https://oascities.org/etsi-release-full-feature-specification-to-support-smart-cities-communities/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1c824e4b-2afe-48f0-a165-5fe57ab29f00 .

camssa:6f5d282f-6a96-4995-99f5-f2774d42f73e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are not specific assessments nor any deployment use case evaluating the specification's effectivenes. \r
\r
TOSCA reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3dd32f1-eed9-48cd-9684-6f07ea354f77 .

camssa:6f60d388-cf11-44fc-b6a4-3d1597843ef8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No regulation has been found directly mentioning CAdES as a subject of the agreement. Despite this, eiDAS regulation is focused on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions. CAdES Baseline profile is specifying the profile of CMS signed-data on the context of the European Internal Market. Moreover, it is compliant with eiDAS regulation, a key enabler on the trustworthy data exchange across borders. \r
See:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv%3AOJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32006L0123"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:373833c7-7b7f-4355-9d5b-7d84584b1c9c .

camssa:6f6521da-6aa5-4034-b7b2-9ad69c24db42 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "40" .

