camssa:6fa3e7dd-393b-42b5-a13c-efb279127adb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData services return URLs to identify resources requested by clients. Where possible, interoperability increases by exploiting the information found in the route part of the URL. However, attention must be paid to those URLs including custom transformations (that is, query options) and clients must be aware of it in future requests to the identified resource.\r
\r
OData reference, 6 Extensibility:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752211'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60f7a9fd-6699-419f-9e57-8075c8bdd72a .

camssa:6fa5a09d-d033-4067-bbf3-ba343c445033 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6fa62c64-1fdd-43d3-ab9c-fa9da59938ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML is a markup languages to develop web documents and make them online to share and publish information. The specification supports the first level of maturity which corresponds to make data available on the Internet. So, the specification is aligned with the different levels of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee's 5-star schema for Open Data.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9fb3e9bc-7ddc-4f21-b553-ecf7184673b9 .

camssa:6fa722dc-aedb-484b-ba11-559498bfcd3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GITB TDL allows the review and provision of feedback but there is no pre-release public review process defined. There is no direct evidence that a public review is conducted according to the GITB TDL documentation.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#what-is-the-gitb-tdl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc37715d-654a-4fc8-a744-e1911dc32546 .

camssa:6fa90c37-da98-45ba-a2f1-9e806a1c1350 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TGF emphasizes the importance of clear and unambiguous definitions for data elements and process steps, which can help prevent errors and ensure consistent processing of data. In addition, the TGF supports the use of standards and protocols for data exchange and communication, which can help ensure the accuracy of data as it is transferred between systems and organiSations. \r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:827aafe3-67cd-4cf0-8a1b-ac3c1c5e3ea3 .

camssa:6faaea33-e949-4f0c-bb44-579d401fc197 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8954ddabf37f4899562b9ea4c8f0bbf204f3e48c9203043bc231f368092396a2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:6faebe0d-ed66-4995-bad2-623092dd51d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are multiple mentions to the extension of XSD throughout the specification's documentation.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d93954df-9858-4b82-b396-54a9b5b01bca .

camssa:6faf8ae4-6bfa-4847-8ea5-d5d418c0244c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is included in 1 Member State' catalogue of recommended specifications. This Member State is Spain.\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:9e2c2877-5103-4934-8440-c60ba2e10c48/Catalogue_of_Standards_NIF_Spain.pdf\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:850f28a8-fa08-4ff5-ae2a-87e966b8a494 .

camssa:6fb044f2-4918-4988-bf52-6bd2b406507f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in different catalogues and repositories, there is no evidence found of ETSI EN 319 532-3 \r
being included in the catalogue of any Member State or the List of Standards.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1ae5e8d-e2a4-4f15-8ab0-bc859a8e9e7f .

