camssa:6fe139c4-7e2c-4d79-b415-4a45b4c04a20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has been found included in two Member States National catalogue: Slovenia and Ireland. It is also added in Cyprus even though the NIFO factsheet of Cyprus is not fully compliant with the EIF. All three countries that the specification has been found in, comply with middle-upper performance than stated in the Digital Public Administration Factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards 2022\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1db57cb1-e997-4a4b-a3dd-b1f4b473e3c8 .

camssa:6fe24835-660d-4f1f-ab8e-bc3343561387 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By testing the requirements established in ETSI TS 119 612, which aims to enable trusted list for validating \r
the stutus of services, the specification helps to enhance and upgrade the delivery of digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dcaff257-8d18-41c9-a06b-e1f2892cf096 .

camssa:6fe840db-ff62-4028-b8fa-641ece5f2897 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related to the delivery of multilingual European public services. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:845090cf-7021-4162-ae60-226d7eb9e32e .

camssa:6fed0012-0329-4d4b-8735-fa2d2a0f8332 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XACML is the basis of the Polocy Management impelemented by the cross-border project SEMINARIS. This projects aims to provide e-services with the required underlying secure authentication and management approach\r
\r
Semiramis home page: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8096584-1a26-4847-949a-b4e6926e1d07 .

camssa:6fee925b-557a-4837-83f8-fd5a570e86da a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:6feee983-a3aa-4a3b-8014-c1d19ffd182b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As most of the vocabularies, DCAT reuses several existing ones (e.g. "adms", "foaf") and the Resource Description Framework (RDF). This results in a dependency that can hamper interoperability, especially in the case where new releases of the reused vocabularies are not backward compatible.\r
                                            \r
                                                                                                                    \r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:            \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/                                     \r
\r
ADMS reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/            \r
\r
FOAF reference:\r
http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43c2005f-ad35-4b79-985f-32256943389c .

camssa:6ff4cecf-dc64-440a-b8ee-e343fbefb393 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4017a1ae4d077fbb3847280a1c20b41bf00c32d65fc9beaa2bea8cce550ac463 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6ff77ba4-4c68-43e0-8fc6-b9612ef0cd1a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS, so it can be concluded that through it processes, data and services are fostered."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6c7db9c-f84a-41f3-b52d-79ca69b81a8b .

camssa:6ffad8cc-e2f2-481a-bb9f-6bf4ad4bae55 a cav:Score,
