    cav:value "1" .

camssa:6ffed551-9add-48dd-af90-338f6c39d9d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba9d7c6f-caca-46ec-86c7-fe02f42d8e8a .

camssa:6fffc5f3-3569-4de9-8afc-bf297ef24ba8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the availability interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fed0ade-6c3b-40ce-b63b-2b31fcb30f91 .

camssa:7004bb14-4f38-4433-b8ed-4d395bddba52 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Taking the initial purpose of the specification, it can be considered that the specification is involved in fostering the comprehensibility of Public Administrations data as well as relevant data produced for the decision-making process. \r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc6e9801-892d-4072-9bb1-b1e5dae17efc .

camssa:7006344e-6331-469f-97bb-3ca3fbcb070f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTP is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, FTP can define the interoperability aspects of the "Network",  "Network Service", "Private Network" and "Public Network" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d10163f4-85a0-499c-a62b-836e92ff667f .

camssa:70087995-ad23-4f93-874f-1891e5b624e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """' Assessments of the efficiency of W3C Verifiable Credentials primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. Real-world Implementations provide valuable insights into how Verifiable Credentials perform in diverse use cases and environments and the W3C Working Group has published a collection of those:\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials Use Cases: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-use-cases/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d87c41b-c81b-4747-8360-cc614a312620 .

camssa:700d51a0-019b-4c89-9df6-c3f8b39fd028 a cav:Score,
