camssa:709451f4-7704-4edd-aa0c-622fa953b883 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SFIA has been adopted by governments, companies and individuals since its inception in 2000. For example, at European level SFIA has been mapped to the e-Competence Framework (see SFIA reference, Standard skills profiles section, EU ICT Role Profiles subsection). In addition, SFIA has created a worldwide community of users for the collaborative development of the specification. SFIA has not only been kept relevant through open consultation, but also has been updated every few years to address the changing needs of industry and business. In addition, the maintenance of SFIA is carried out with the support of relevant stakeholders in governmental organisations world-wide (see SFIA reference, Standard skills profiles section, USA National Initiative for Cybersecurity Education (NICE) subsection).\r
\r
SFIA reference, Standard skills profiles section, EU ICT Role Profiles subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/tools-and-resources/standard-industry-skills-profiles/european-union/eu-ict-role-profiles \r
\r
SFIA reference, About SFIA section:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/about-sfia\r
\r
SFIA reference, Standard skills profiles section, USA National Initiative for Cybersecurity Education (NICE) subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/tools-and-resources/standard-industry-skills-profiles/usa-national-initiative-for-cybersecurity-education-nice-work-roles'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:297b0f57-6e2f-4869-9e0d-f8450ffc7c72 .

camssa:70963bc3-0257-49f1-9606-11d70b6c9b34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By providing style, the CSS is an asset that when used properly could help to enhance and ease the accessibility of disabled people. It could help to provide context and support the functionalities of the web design. Moreover, the Regional Government of Bizkaia developed his website to promote the integration of groups with disabilities into the Public Administration of Bizkaia. They used XHTML 1.0 recommendations and CSS2.\r
\r
CSS and JavaScript accessibility best practices:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/Accessibility/CSS_and_JavaScript\r
\r
CSS2 implemented in e-accessability project:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/einclusion/document/eaccesibility-public-administration-bizkaia-bizkaianet"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43c0c6c3-ac07-4e56-a52f-f57f374bfd8e .

