    cav:value "1" .

camssa:70cff14b-e688-4088-9c26-2d4553621638 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By easing the creation of secured web services, XACML contributes to the increment of digital public services between administrations and stakeholders and among administrations. This public services can include Secure Data Transfer amongst other services. \r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html\r
\r
SEMIRAMIS project: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df801db8-a4a0-452a-a59a-507523f6e362 .

camssa:70d99c08-56d7-44b5-8e5f-8a64704c9e32 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing tools for testing the implementation of XACML policies. The Security Pool Policy allow to check for enhancements in a XACML implementation. Also, a tool known as WS2 Identity Server is 
available under its own licence to allow the testing of XACML implementations. Furthermore, XACML defines 
conformance provisions in section 10. 

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html

WS2 Identity Server
https://docs.wso2.com/display/IS541/Using+the+XACML+TryIt+Tool '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58ec8341-2b62-47a0-bc1a-4a40056dc6d2 .

