camssa:7114577c-8a20-4afc-988b-b77e6c0a6dc0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSS v2.1 is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, CSS can define the interoperability aspects of the "Human Interface" ABB of the EIRA Technical Application View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f25f7e25-b04f-4078-a1cb-c840215661bb .

camssa:711a3d6c-72da-47dc-95fc-a73ea2c4412a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e46f1a4a060cc7e143e32e4833c94af9164c37bc0d4c844bd1fa974ffb2ac225 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:711b5b78-03ba-482d-a9a2-4c894f1eec6b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """' SCIM is designed to facilitate the exchange of identity information between identity providers and service providers, which can be valuable for data portability scenarios between systems and applications, including those supporting the implementation or evolution of European public services. While SCIM is primarily designed for managing identity information, its features can contribute to data portability in the context of user identities within the European public services framework.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:78d81cd7-d3a2-42af-9f7d-3914b7d85815 .

camssa:71236b02-3a41-483f-831c-7a7b08b42c03 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:71241ec7-a906-4760-9ae6-aec4a0718dca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By allowing communications over the internet, IPv6 contributes to the exchange of information between public administrations. Therefore, it reduces administrative burden.

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7dbe535-b9f4-4fbd-818d-5be05a4bdae7 .

camssa:7124b76c-aabe-443b-be94-e40e051c49ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WS-BPEL is maintained and developed by OASIS which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
Developer community OASIS: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/org/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb56b177-4ab3-4eee-9c0c-3d6397bfb8d1 .

