        "90.26%AssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:7164f2c9-acd9-4d80-bef9-d4a396b39b7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"All schema.org releases provide for public review. Changes to the schema.org specification are proposed, discussed, prepared and reviewed by the schema.org Community Group and ultimately reviewed and published by the Steering Group, which holds the final decision. Collected feedback is also available through the schema.org Github (see Schema.org-W3 Github reference, Issues section).\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github reference, Issues section:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/issues\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a8c0b4b5-46ff-45cf-bd68-933cdb8c08a1 .

camssa:716652e8-5e3d-497e-9da1-9442333a9e0f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:71673f1c-9ee0-4ba1-b10f-069358cf46c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML can enable digital service delivery channels. By using XML to structure and share data, organizations can make it easier for customers to access their services through digital channels like websites, mobile apps, and APIs.\r
\r
As a use-case example  a government agency could use XML to make their services available online. By structuring their service data using XML and providing APIs for accessing that data, they could enable citizens to access and interact with government services through digital channels.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f41a33c-0310-4034-a429-8803cc91d67e .

camssa:71684b15-e85c-447f-bee2-d0b9adfcaed8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification in itself does not  include security features, but the security considerations aim to put together the benefits of the WS-BPEL and the WS-Security specifications, that can be used to secure the Web services transactions. Therefore, it can be said that the orchestration of web services combining both specifications can ensure the trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders. \r
\r
The specification: \r
\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af94d773-c4cc-4d0d-bf1d-94eb20138836 .

camssa:716952f3-a5e5-4a7d-ab7e-b8c96184c1ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of En 303 645 specification is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
EN 303 645 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ed68c7b-9ab7-4c74-a308-7e311b30bedf .

camssa:717582a8-8b4f-4013-afff-61f797aa98f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The European Public Sector Information platform assessed the impact of the use of DCAT for the European Open Data Catalogues.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.europeandataportal.eu/sites/default/files/2013_impact_of_standards_in_european_data_catalogues.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d7bdd8c-f2e4-45bd-b87a-791222ff0f50 .

camssa:717b7843-deaf-4bd2-b125-8820fed5bd60 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8aee43521f6b3ab69785784831b651574a5496fd5996bb8c61a80e479f633fa0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:717f49af-fbf0-41ee-8343-a931ae76d34b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IDS have a method of certificating conformance to the IDS standards. IDS certification has two parts: First, the interested part needs to prove that the IDS component is built correctly. Second, they need to make sure their IDS component’s operational environment is supporting data sharing according to the requirements and rules. While the certification of operational environment focuses on security and trust, the component certification also ensures interoperability. \r
\r
IDS Certification: https://internationaldataspaces.org/offers/certification/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:45f9ec07-349c-40e7-bf19-4e06c447865e .

camssa:717fdb9f-7d04-49c1-b809-31849a7cd15b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family of documents use in systems or applications can indirectly support security efforts through traceability, accountability, integrity, non-repudiation, auditing, and forensic analysis. However, implementing comprehensive security measures is essential for ensuring the secure exchange of data.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7124fc2-9ba3-4da4-8b8a-b7d0d58c5147 .

camssa:717ffc05-cf3a-4a91-911d-083630028968 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification was developed in 1991 by the IETF group, and it has become a widely used format for the transaction of different types of files over the internet. It is focused on the transfer via email, and it is supported by numerous mail software. This fact demonstrates the maturity of MIME for its use for the development of services and products.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6538b59-2a91-4e9b-ae5c-4cdad18f0322 .

camssa:718526c3-118a-41a5-9887-e7b93ceff09a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1624157830122d60825aa5aa88ab70d0b140b2e7e510086699f9a9773efef6bd ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:718b192c-9c40-49b4-9fdb-f7bd8050027b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISO 639-2 code suite was developed for its use by libraries, information services and publishers to indicate language in the exchange of information, especially in computerised systems. Indicating language in the exchange of information is becoming more necessary in the European cross-border context.\r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e476ced-9b66-4a25-9136-b783e49cb871 .

camssa:718b5085-36a5-4dc8-a3ad-519dc9f54388 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData services are used by a large community of users. The OData protocol differs from other REST-based web services in that it provides a uniform way of describing both the data and the data model. OData should be implemented as a very basic and compliant service; in this sense, th specification is domain-agnostic, designed to be implemented in any domain. For example, there are the \r
Cambridge Weather-Pyslet demo service and the City of Medicine Hat Open Data Portal, in the field of academics and medicine, respectively.\r
\r
OData ecosystem, Live services reference:\r
https://www.odata.org/ecosystem/\r
\r
OData reference, 2 Overview:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752201'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c2080c9-e001-4720-95b5-d99b70635d65 .

camssa:719198f0-57d6-447e-888d-8bda67e32220 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:71953e30-114e-4fe8-9247-7a2e624787da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Open reviews are an essential part of the verification process for eArchiving Building Block\r
specification documentation. A review is a systematic examination of a document by experts and\r
other stakeholders to find and remove errors early on in the specification life cycle. For example, the github issues channel from the CSIP is a tool used by anyone who wants to contribute to the development of the specification.\r
\r
Open review guidelines for eArchiving Building Block specifications and documentation:\r
https://dilcis.eu/images/procedures/LC-001390244_CEF-TC_2019-3_M23c.pdf\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP Github isues:\r
https://github.com/DILCISBoard/E-ARK-CSIP/issues\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fad77f06-ae08-4f18-a61f-8711a463e5a2 .

