camssa:7250a35a-8ee2-4ca7-9322-6ffe16e3b986 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UTF-8 can play an important role in facilitating accurate representation and exchange of multilingual data and information, promoting inclusivity, and improving communication and interoperability in administrative contexts, thus, fostering comprehensibility of administrative procedures.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3629 \r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1232a3c-2bd9-42ad-abd7-0a6fd050ba34 .

camssa:7256445a-482f-414b-aab3-27cd37e0928d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0c9dd43038136296b52f50e05f9d6eef39f7b8018517224007990b15be2eb19e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7258fe70-32a2-40cc-9977-341f512469ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of PROV is not related to multilingualism. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specfication.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26f2f599-d3cf-4e0f-81e4-878082a2717f .

camssa:72666a82-43b6-46f1-9e08-63a8a68647d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification defines how different parties and transactions have to be done in order to allow proper discoverability and data exchanges. Therefore, it is defining organisational requirements for the data transaction between two or more parties.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37e25889-ed08-46a0-abee-df8acc0af54d .

camssa:72689dd1-cd5a-44dc-8648-31f6e62b8fba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:726d9bab-b6b5-46bb-a625-66125e567724 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is a markup language that was  designed to store and transport data, and defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a human-readable format and machine-readable format. XML is appropriate to areas of applications like IoT requiring lightweight payloads of data and is applicable  to any business domain.\r
\r
However, it is worth noting that  XML has some limitations with heavier amounts of data due to the time consuming process for parsing and validating of data expressed in XML."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0103510-6334-4a8a-8964-63fca60e059c .

camssa:727d26e4-618d-4457-88e1-424cf922fdb2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7281500b-ee98-48eb-8b1e-a008c698cf07 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-Security is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:78fe36c5-3c83-4593-8df3-0f7afeab2c38 .

camssa:72837409-8f94-4629-92dd-329383904f2d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no such assessment and evidences found addressing the effectiveness of the specification.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58ef4d47-934f-40cd-842f-96725ffd1d32 .

camssa:72847dad-38a7-495b-a137-958d76fbae44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS itself does not facilitate organizational interoperability agreements directly. However, its secure and standardized communication channel can support interoperability efforts by ensuring secure data transmission, standardization, authentication, and compliance with regulations. Interoperability agreements require additional efforts and coordination beyond HTTPS implementation.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2d465ee3-8cdb-47a7-877d-df1544a7bc63 .

camssa:72861892-b6a1-423e-82d3-4971c6a88834 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b349b0c8-12b2-46a6-90c0-b36d2d46825c .

camssa:728dd6d1-4ee5-4f13-b3b8-46621545cdaf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:728f3080-47ef-4752-a06d-70638ececa79 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3c0edf049cd95575b46d688ed31be0ccce7a5822c5bcc22adf05d491f01f2780 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7293f40c-5a8f-49e1-92be-3ae98531afd3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:729460c7-1de2-4251-808a-43e5530c1097 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XFDL specification does not directly handle the authentication of role agents involved in data transactions. However, it supports digital signatures, which ensure the authenticity of the data and verify the identity of the signer. By using a digital signature, public administrations can confirm that the form data has not been tampered with and that it was signed by an authorised agent. This aligns with the XML Signature Syntax and Processing specification, which provides a standardised method for generating and verifying digital signatures in XML documents, ensuring the integrity and authenticity of the data, as well as the identity of the signer within a secure, interoperable framework.

XML Signature Syntax and Processing reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core1/

XFDL security reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL#button'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a211ffcf-75bb-4560-8ec2-3fe703c8a531 .

camssa:72a34b54-3219-4016-8302-92758e3eae74 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are some assessment evaluating the specification's digital solution effectiveness and efficiency which involve SMP2.0.\r
\r
OOTS eDelivery Access Point Reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=647955048\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55b9095e-e363-43e2-80f3-1bffb9cdfd28 .

camssa:72ad5eed-782a-44e5-9d12-9e16dac8346b a cav:Score,
