camssa:72d1ca5b-8bdc-4295-b81e-2b45534384cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the second star corresponds to make data available as structured data, an area of application of XML. \r
\r
Additionally, RDF is a W3C specification that defines XML syntax for RDF, the de facto standard for publishing Linked Open Data. \r
\r
See:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c22f84cd-56bf-494b-848b-278876416000 .

