    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:734aaed9-9d0a-4973-b09d-e4a9a0f4c554 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 319 532 is a European standard, delivered by a European Standardisation organisation (ETSI), \r
according to the specification documentation.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35aac1a3-159b-427a-81e6-07922fb4f784 .

camssa:734ade94-8372-4b09-b3b6-e8b13649efaa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, UTF-8 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
Identified Standards for Procurement:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/identified-ict-specifications-procurement '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eded46f5-f1f6-4358-88e0-4f6886ec1694 .

camssa:734fa585-df5e-4fd4-9de7-26768d444914 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:734fb621-a3c2-4e8b-86f3-d460a30ce9cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of EuroVoc is related to the delivery of multilingual public services. By establishing language equivalences between identical concepts expressed in different languages, it allows documents to be indexed in the language of the documentalist and searches to be made in the user’s language;\r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:824ea708-94ba-4217-b9b8-ff1c639176ec .

camssa:73503829-8a10-40c9-8570-46323cd0355c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The SMP eases and fosters the discoverability of administrations data or services to others that can be administrations or other stakeholders. Easing this communication the specification allows different parties to discover others' capabilities and information to exchange documents amongst them. This fact increases the visibility of administrations' data and also improves and helps the decision-making processes.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b65d594-144c-4448-8e9f-b17aa4af54b5 .

camssa:7352b059-d255-4af5-8c5d-db105bd70b63 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:73674764-72ef-4016-968b-a84bbed4180f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WSDL was developed by IBM, Microsoft, and Ariba initially in 2000. The following version was at their charge as well, introducing minor changes. The last version became a W3C recommendation in 2007. Nowadays, the international organisation is maintaining and developing WSDL. Moreover, it continues having support from companies with a wide market share. Therefore, it is demonstrated that WSDL has enough market acceptance and maturity for its use in the development of products and services."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1f20b4d-42e3-47fb-ad1c-90f40445043e .

camssa:7369691a-62c1-4865-a37a-4297bc5fa14f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e46f1a4a060cc7e143e32e4833c94af9164c37bc0d4c844bd1fa974ffb2ac225 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:736d6ff3-297f-4bcb-8a5b-8ab9413dab99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of OCSP as a\r
European standard.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technicalspecifications_\r
en\r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:debe32a9-81cd-4afe-93c8-53939a4a74df .

camssa:736ed37e-6f9f-465f-bd66-8ac8c707894b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Participation in ISO technical committee work is possible, depending on the membership category of the participant. Public reviews are not foreseen, provided that the Public Administration was a subscriber member.\r
\r
ISO membership manual, 'ISO member rights, good practice and obligations' section:\r
https://www.iso.org/publication/PUB100399.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75120f21-3903-4bd6-a28b-25659afa6dd2 .

camssa:73755c28-4285-4853-b878-e27e9adb5136 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification was originally created by Facebook. In 2015 it became open and it is now supported by its own community in GraphQL Foundation.\r
\r
GraphQL FAQ Website: \r
https://graphql.org/faq/#who-founded-the-organization'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ebe8164-b553-4f9a-b33c-626f4fda2892 .

camssa:7378acfc-03f4-4b26-a50d-fd0c021cd438 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EN 16234-1 e-CF is not related to the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data and services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a5271ff-8036-4038-a6b7-70709ce04db7 .

camssa:7379fb9f-2f82-4b86-8623-1632b00a3890 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the time of elaborating this assessment, DCAT is extensively used to create innovative linked open data solutions. Especially by public administration looking forward to foster cross-border interoperability and transparency.\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2fa155b-9a31-4041-a3df-c337dc0752ba .

camssa:738707a4-ff34-4a31-b627-f6ce1d2f9bd0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAML 2.0 primarily facilitates authentication through Single Sign-On (SSO). However, its assertions can include user attributes and roles, which Service Providers can leverage for access control decisions. Thus, while SSO simplifies the login process, SAML 2.0 also indirectly aids in implementing access control mechanisms.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7635ec44-f143-4c72-83d5-b1efac7fe552 .

camssa:738cb119-b31f-4d25-930e-2ec597c498c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e370a4af17e89cbb70bb5079082a1e21cdee85435c8fc30b12a8987f18db367f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:738fef55-6369-47fb-a3dc-0bd6e5100bbd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The uniform interface constraint is fundamental to the design of any RESTful system. It simplifies and decouples the architecture, which enables each part to evolve indepently.  For that reason, REST architectural style ensures standarized transfer of information between softwares, thus enabling the exposure of interfaces.\r
\r
REST reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/#uniform-interface\r
\r
REST Chapter 5 from Roy Fielding's dissertation:\r
https://www.ics.uci.edu/~fielding/pubs/dissertation/rest_arch_style.htm\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e76c17d4-3bf7-44a7-8b8e-b225eb791404 .

camssa:739070d8-3a93-416b-b099-f9f0cf7c32e0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7390d149-9e30-4cd4-88db-30b30a6176c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:739439c3-407d-439d-ad15-b019eac5837b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:739badc6-49cb-47ed-ae51-4aa9806bbd13 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No Member States have been found recommending Syslog in their ICT National Catalogues.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a215ef18-2ed6-4a3f-b73a-a1735b8075da .

camssa:73a5a680-ca78-445d-b047-0322f23ead44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is included in 5 national catalogues. They belong to Member States which comply with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the EIF according to the NIFO factsheets. \r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c552bb90-bf00-4b32-a4ce-fb190bbf14a9 .

camssa:73b42dc9-8d6f-45f1-bb18-e3879cc11e6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 3 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. This Member States are France, the Netherlands and Spain.\r
\r
National catalogue France:\r
http://references.modernisation.gouv.fr/sites/default/files/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf\r
\r
National catalogue the Netherlands: \r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8aed6a27-a8e0-49d1-afed-e70e75cc2611 .

camssa:73b51553-bb7c-4ff6-a70d-88e06dfbdd19 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "PAdES is relying on PDF to verify and validate signed PDF format documents. Despite this fact, PDF is a widely adopted format for data exchange and this dependancy, thus it does not hamper its adoption."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39703896-c43d-4e2e-9b9c-327c1a38d742 .

