camssa:763e9c1b-48a5-4c74-b3ab-846d1a5c6c21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"OpenTelemetry is included in the Spanish National Institute of Cybersecurity (INCIBE). OpenTelemetry-Go Contrib is a collection of third-party packages for OpenTelemetry-Go. Prior to version 0.46.0, the grpc Unary Server Interceptor out of the box adds labels `net.peer.sock.addr` and `net.peer.sock.port` that have unbound cardinality. It leads to the server's potential memory exhaustion when many malicious requests are sent. An attacker can easily flood the peer address and port for requests. Version 0.46.0 contains a fix for this issue.

INCIBE-CERT Vulnerabilities: https://www.incibe.es/en/incibe-cert/early-warning/vulnerabilities/cve-2023-47108\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35d8c7e2-2962-4a7a-bcc9-5bc56ef80def .

camssa:76407ca8-1742-4f13-b4f1-52334c8cb22a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XACML specification provides significant mechanisms for protecting personal data managed by Public 
Administrations through fine-grained, attribute-based access control, policy enforcement, and audit capabilities. Moreover, XACML should be integrated with other security measures.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68e4fff0-ccfc-4fc9-ba1c-4bee08087062 .

