camssa:767484e9-f904-4fb6-97d0-2a9e5c46b2b4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ebXML is originally associated to the electronic business domain. However, the specification could be\r
indistinctly implemented in other domains as the automobile domain (see ebXML application reference).\r
\r
OASIS ebXML Registry TC reference, Announcements section:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep#announcements\r
\r
ebxml.xml.org reference:\r
http://ebxml.xml.org/milestones\r
 \r
ebXML application reference:\r
http://ebxml.xml.org/resources'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64b091cc-79c7-4920-aaf9-b647c979c944 .

camssa:767a06e6-9b18-4a0f-8f65-427211e06d25 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that use CPOV nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification. Despite this, there are countries that extend Core Vocabularies to use them with specific attributes they want.

Core Vocabularies reference:
https://www.w3.org/2013/share-psi/workshop/berlin/EuropeanInteroperabilityTheISACoreVocabularies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8cd99e4c-26f6-4ffd-a5e0-b93138a3f482 .

camssa:767c2d74-b90e-4619-94fe-612b14cdf6c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, MIME has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision. During the evaluation process, all the Member States are invited to share their doubts. The positive evaluation of MIME and its identification is considered an interoperability agreement.\r
\r
ICT Standards for Procurement:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e3fa8d5-10e8-4773-ad74-58bfc8110c76 .

