camssa:76ad65cf-cc11-4f0b-a318-4bb0ca3e9de1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Core Location Vocabulary facilitates the process for institutions to classify and to describe data about location aspects of public organisations, citizens, and businesses. By ensuring the reuse of information among administrations and systems, it fosters interoperability and impacts positively on the development of eGovernment.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1d3dc76-5938-404a-9b12-7fa53f226c33 .

camssa:76ae4c3a-b319-40cb-8af9-ac5992ac6543 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of CSV is not related to enabling the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's service. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.                                              \r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d1dd3ca-9fdf-40d2-a35e-df24851288c9 .

camssa:76aec04d-6f04-4145-ad1d-850cca93acec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification had reached a mature state, with version 1.0 of the specification having been released in October 2019. The specification was developed through a multi-year process involving stakeholders from across the European Union, and is designed to provide a common framework for the creation and exchange of legal documents in a machine-readable format.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58184aa5-0cf7-4f2c-b03d-e1868eb05e49 .

