camssa:76c718b2-68c0-4e47-a3d7-35d6edaa2755 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XACML can be used independently from any other technical specifications or operating system. However, it is worth noting that since it is based on XML, it can be dependent on conventions and rules for the correct XML usage. \r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0ab84e57-517f-4729-a75c-2d439b195fa7 .

camssa:76caa209-1e5f-43fd-a6e6-fe97a9537fb4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI has been selected several times for European administrations in order to make their web services available and discoverable for each other, and their stakeholders. 
An example of this kind UDDI use case is SELIS project, which aims to ease the eInvoicing processes. It is included within the Digital Single Market framework. 

SELIS reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eprocurement/document/secure-electronic-invoicing-service-selis'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34932ca9-88c2-455b-9dab-f34c784bad99 .

camssa:76cb82dd-091c-496a-be7d-a57b3b927377 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of HTTP Cookies is not related to the modelling of business processes.  Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#creating_cookie'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73ba9bda-22c6-4012-b1b5-30c6a06dc525 .

camssa:76db29a4-f404-45f2-845b-7b4098ebeed9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:76e0a65f-fbdc-4513-9940-0f3c4df27a27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Conformance to DPV implementation means it is correctly mapped and aligned with the vocabularies it defines. For that matter, the "Development Guide" section found in Github indicates how the conformity process has to be carried out.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

DPV in Github:
https://github.com/w3c/dpv'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:63c7fe59-41ff-4369-ab6d-1638d6d67220 .

camssa:76eb7d66-a42a-49f5-802c-7ea34032a2be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:97fc91de-8149-48ee-b1ed-7e729e1a42b2 .

camssa:76f5ba58-6a32-43ab-926e-3c3aefec9427 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7702ce9a-8a61-4b25-9f3c-0cae0f6ba79c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS has become the standard protocol for transmitting sensitive data over the internet, and it is widely supported by web browsers, web servers, and other software applications. The majority of websites that handle user data, especially those involving e-commerce, online banking, and user accounts, use HTTPS to ensure the security and privacy of their users. The maturity of HTTPS is evident in the widespread adoption of SSL/TLS certificates, which are essential for enabling HTTPS connections. Certificate authorities issue these certificates, and a robust ecosystem exists for their issuance, management, and verification.\r
\r
SSL Certificate explanation:\r
https://www.kaspersky.com/resource-center/definitions/what-is-a-ssl-certificate'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7152316c-252f-4ef1-b66a-94a7bbce638c .

camssa:770a773d-b306-4460-ad9f-57e11755c085 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI specification does enable digital service delivery channels. According to the ELI ‘Pillar IV’ protocol, an
ELI provider must provide two channels: the ELI Sitemap and the ELI Atom feed. These channels facilitate
the dissemination of ELI metadata in a structured format embedded in the web pages of Official Journal
websites.

This allows legislation publishers to share their data in an interoperable way, thereby enabling digital service
delivery channels. However, to be compatible with the ELI ‘Pillar IV’ protocol, it is necessary to have ELI
Pillar III implemented, which involves the inclusion of structured metadata in web pages.

ELI IV specification refrerence:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/ELI-Pillar-IV-protocol-specification-v1.0_en.pdf

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec86df50-8833-4799-86aa-23998f1f145d .

camssa:770d962a-6398-4e18-a2b9-56e4d56890a0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "0" .

