camssa:771736d2-b0e2-463c-9181-7cb80181bd99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is a widely used de-facto standard. Thus, it is sufficiently mature for the development of products and services. Since it's release 1995, IPSec overcame most of its initial problems and has been used by many products and services.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.ibm.com/it-infrastructure/z/zos\r
https://www.ibm.com/it-infrastructure/power/os/aix\r
https://www.oracle.com/solaris/solaris11/\r
http://www.mit.edu/~tytso/ipsec/surv9607.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d129b55-89e8-4430-9cca-cb8d695157d3 .

camssa:771ebee2-4149-4b7b-8ba2-6ce60ee0ae83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The information on (new) standardisation activities is widely announced via the IETF websites and working group activities. There also is a mailing list one can subscribe to for announcements. This so-called IETF Announce list receives announcements about IETF meetings, the activities and actions of the IESG, the RFC Editor, the NomCom, and other announcements of interest to the IETF community._x000D_\r
See:_x000D_\r
https://www.ietf.org/how/lists/announcement/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96e786de-2504-49e5-ae37-0b35a6bb9b64 .

camssa:7731ef47-0354-4157-96e4-43d1f70531b2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7732a96c-7317-4082-9290-e81f6e82305c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS is not related to the reuse of information, therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a5a8c02f-6d72-4b56-99b9-ce6578c30d6c .

camssa:77338ac5-6c9d-4922-b1c0-3ba38415648a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:773735a5-b28e-48ba-a98d-bac088488f50 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7737e027-cd49-401b-8468-43b42a25298b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Domibus, as a messaging platform, focuses on ensuring the secure transmission of messages and documents. While it supports digital signatures that contribute to data authenticity and integrity, it doesn't inherently guarantee data accuracy beyond the scope of secure message exchange.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10a40e75-64c0-4901-a718-62d42dddccea .

camssa:77398cdf-7e5b-4139-85fc-899fca1a741a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES and CAdES Baseline profile are included in the ETSI’s catalogue of standards. As ETSI is considered an official standardisation organisation, it can be considered that the specifications are included in a supra-national catalogue. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20103%20173&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&historical=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2020-01-08&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b994bb2b-eff4-42b8-8ebe-8d0f872187bf .

camssa:773f576a-e6f6-4c7d-8efc-66e5b85c5f1e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3fc24cbc-2f5a-4e06-bc9e-4cefd113274a .

camssa:7753cce1-1f0f-4676-b830-56bb87e58388 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After researching there has been no success finding any indication of conformance on the specification.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2dd89064-8c08-4018-b11e-44723fa32218 .

camssa:77558685-0359-4d8a-a3de-47f0bd3749de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of WS-BPEL, operates under RF on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free and (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
OASIS IPR:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/security/ipr.php\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3499f631-055f-4331-8115-2bbf5b08f190 .

camssa:7764cc55-1f62-464c-93d0-d6f65c54000f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:77752f63-4496-401e-9884-01cd1d468f30 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Data Spaces Business Alliance (DSBA) aims to converge the best skills, assets, and experience in Europe into a one-stop-shop for data spaces, from inception to deployment. The Data Spaces Business Alliance are Gaia-X European Association for Data and Cloud AISBL, the Big Data Value Association (BDVA), FIWARE Foundation, and the International Data Spaces Association (IDSA), who created and currently maintains DAPS. With this cross-industry expertise, resources and know-how, the Alliance drives awareness, evangelizes technology, shapes standards, and enables integration across industries.\r
\r
 Data Spaces Business Alliance (DSBA): https://data-spaces-business-alliance.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d92120b6-1c91-4dfe-836b-e5a23c623c68 .

camssa:777bc641-af80-4f9c-9c8a-aba02561b212 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc272cd8a2e3e9c5e4edaa5ac7d59735c377a9db89d6958335a2cf0538761ab3 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:777bd111-caaa-4533-9beb-2dce07d7c5ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By allowing the authentication for using services SAML 2.0 fosters visibility by simplifying access to administrations’ services. Moreover, it can be used internally by public officers which enhances the decision-making process.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f13cb912-ddf6-4f75-8516-276b0e4abce2 .

camssa:777d8cfc-2823-4fc4-b67c-fee14a771c4a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
