camssa:77c943fd-ffb5-4a0c-8c86-134cbfd8b30f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A few assessments have been carried on the specification effectiveness, in particular regarding the administrative burden and simplification.
Given the nature of the Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox only a few assesments can be carried out since the specification is rather stable. In this sense, all are conducted by think tanks that focus on administration simplification and integration. It is worth mentioning that the Cambridge one is the most recent one and focuses on what can be adapted from the Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox in the UK context post brexit.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

"Can We Better the European Union Better Regulation Agenda?" Cambidge's article:
https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/european-journal-of-risk-regulation/article/abs/can-we-better-the-european-union-better-regulation-agenda/46A0BA96D46266FF5C8320A2DA3B937F

"To the Commissioner responsible for better regulation" Bruegel's study:
https://www.bruegel.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/MEMO-Better-Regulation.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd2748a6-740a-404a-9f5d-19a373618f7c .

camssa:77cda83f-779d-46cb-a57b-eb13db4711e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification has a section dedicated compliance and consistence with the OSI reference model. Section 9.2 details the application of consistency and compliance requirements regarding ISO/IEC 7498:1.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:827f3859-9fac-4c47-b375-79ece510b3df .

camssa:77d072b6-0932-44be-9594-1b3fd5ad5617 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification contains a number of cloud interoperability and portability facet models that state the aim of the facet and its requirement. For instance, the syntactic facet of cloud interoperability aims to receive data in an understood format therefore, data exhange formarts should be standardized in JSON, XML, ASN.1 etc.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9bd15a40-9515-46f9-a6ee-f75641ad9492 .

camssa:77d5dfcf-bdde-43e1-8b16-b8c10d020491 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary facilitates the information exchange between business registers, improving the interoperability of systems used by European public services that rely on information about registered organisations. It also promotes the reuse of European vocabularies such as ADMS, enhancing metadata management, ensuring semantic consistency, and supporting the discoverability and interoperability of organisational data across different systems.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

Asset Description Metadata Schema (ADMS) reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:539f1d16-9c38-426f-92aa-81b6996f3e98 .

camssa:77e08395-c8c3-47d5-8822-0995c0d5b11a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The authentication verification relationship is used to specify how the DID subject is expected to be authenticated for purposes such as logging into a website or engaging in any sort of challenge-response protocol. A particular DID method could decide that authenticating as a DID controller is sufficient to, for example, update or delete the DID document. Another DID method could require different keys or a different verification method entirely to be presented, in order to update or delete the DID document than that used to authenticate.

DIDs authentication W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca9f1125-dccc-4717-a3f3-e3fe1d1c7f99 .

camssa:77ec93f5-db4e-4919-b2e3-5b7722030124 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF standards are free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. The specification is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
See:_x000D_\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9fbe1578-5661-45fc-a4e1-f1c6edf1d60e .

camssa:77ecec05-3b82-45f4-bd08-e201fa1d5964 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-838030847fa0adf54939e3feaac0ac2510924c54035e1cb671b223b54b02fd70 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:77ed9420-9f62-4102-b5c2-a4932f308855 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP specification facilitates the publication of data on the web. It provides the necessary mechanisms to create, access, manage, and efficiently distribute data in various formats, giving a diverse user base and ensuring data integrity and security.

HTTP/1.1 Semantics, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110

HTTP/1.1: Semantics and Content, RFC 7231 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7231'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8548e89a-13f7-43e6-b681-9dbff01854bd .

camssa:77f6eb77-496b-47cd-817b-d1978ba990dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The ISO 12639:2004 which refers to TIFF/IT is not available for free for everyone to study. Payment is needed to reach access to the standard.\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:222d1b58-fd11-4ee3-b857-796c1fe05d46 .

camssa:78007f0d-7d88-46c0-8ff7-96fe259ae0ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP specifies the data that needs to be exchanged between an application checking the status of one or\r
more certificates and the server providing the corresponding status. The purpose of OCSP is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services.\r
\r
OCSP reference, section 2:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d336f2e8-c17a-4cea-9446-66b0f15e5ef6 .

camssa:7828b0f2-f3df-44f1-8c48-79a6a88fd9e7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7828e870-65de-4173-a5a4-1c535f5ea14a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:78297e46-d678-48e7-99e8-e8292463e4b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification facilitates the restriction of access to information and data through security layers such as filters and hostname verification, for example SASL Init,which ensures that the client is properly authenticated before any further communication occurs. It is the implementer of the specification who determines the level of access to the information and data.

Oasis AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31515d36-8eac-4b36-a125-4b39a8b564ca .

camssa:782fcaf3-128a-48b9-a87b-ee3645834251 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OASIS has defined a clear Technical Committee (hereby TC) process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process.\r
\r
OASIS guideline:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/casestudies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86bee0b3-908c-4fd5-80a5-9c54fa564616 .

camssa:7832030c-9672-42f2-b165-7f4eaa1506e0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:78369f61-3b9c-44ad-90d7-b4b842fbefe2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DPV taxonomy and data model can be adapted to the business-specific needs, allowing for partial implementations depending on the requirements of any particular context where it is to be applied.\r
\r
DPV specification: \r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c3c04c0-9776-4b8c-86eb-a1b6b322dcf3 .

camssa:783a98fd-2db5-4214-b9e4-09605e8c183e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can enable digital service delivery channels to some extent. FTP is a protocol that facilitates the transfer of files between systems, which can be utilized within digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0dcf35e2-72d4-4a0a-ae8e-cd0117ad4a72 .

camssa:783bf059-4719-4123-8ec8-785adf29d1e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DIDs is not related to long term preservation of electronic records. Therefore this criterion is 
considered not applicable to this specification.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e631926c-429a-4c97-9bb7-80f91fbcb66c .

camssa:7841cc53-a70d-4ce2-be9a-7d94e63b46b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) is not designed to address the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge, including electronic records. DoH is a protocol that focuses on securing the DNS (Domain Name System) communication by encrypting DNS queries and responses.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93f906a2-ac7a-478c-85d5-fe27748422d0 .

camssa:784e8d35-ffca-491e-9f4a-2263ab2a962a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:78512a0f-5758-4613-baed-69c0c6b1c858 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:786286f8-3c2b-425f-a2aa-2009347d0ecd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs allow for extension. The data model supports two types of extensibility. For maximum interoperability, it is recommended that extensions use the W3C DID Specification Registries mechanism. Representations may define other extensibility mechanisms, including ones that do not require the use of the DID Specification Registries.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#extensibility'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6172140-9a00-486a-84d7-6e0dd2e8db69 .

camssa:786b882a-6ea7-4152-a3f4-b7e84b51ee9a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7872a9a5-5373-49dc-85c5-429f3eb54f57 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PDF/A has been assessed previously by the Netherlands using the Technical scenario which is fully aligned with the European Standardisation Regulation 1025/2012. As the result of the assessment is positive, PDF/A can be considered compliant with the European regulation. \r
\r
PDF/A in JoinUp: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/camss-assessment-pdf-a2-scenario-2"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1eafdee-7692-49ea-95ad-556c206f2698 .

camssa:7878eb88-55ba-4d3e-9ee6-147e2f3c77d4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-73a8058bec757a2fdb0f8513c2f11841e982cbef76c3be82af67707c294da8b8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:787b499c-a995-43db-a4d2-dc7350361d5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Information can be exchanged in a secure and trustworthy manner. With peer-to-peer basis and using verification methods, data  and information can be exchanged in a secure manner, which also guarantees the secure processing of data. 

DIDs security requirements:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#security-requirements'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc8f55ec-cdcf-40ea-9c2b-3fc8483f37ca .

camssa:787b9d71-51ce-4acf-a17c-5dcef816c5d0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7881303c-9970-4d7c-9b50-fce68171a54a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abc8ecb4-cc0d-4462-84b4-bc260ed73b1f .

camssa:7894794b-64f6-41c4-93fb-1c84ccbb360f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP Cookies is a business domain agnostic specification that can be implemented in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies: \r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e92a8e7b-8d4f-4d34-ba98-de35aa684f6d .

camssa:789b0212-966c-43ec-bc5d-8591954bc786 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:78a02f0f-be6b-47a5-8069-18f1ac9d9ae1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Open PM2 is an initiative supported by ISA2 to bring the PM2 Methodology and its benefits closer to its broader stakeholders and user community. The European Commission ISA2 Programme supports the development of solutions in the area of interoperability.\r
\r
ISA2 programme:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/home_en\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d93d1c7e-f3ed-45c7-8568-6fb85feb11c9 .

