camssa:78bd9cd4-1dae-4e64-9b9d-f958abb4e338 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 7.7 of ETSI TS 119 432 is dedicated to the component for the client application authentication. This component shall contain information to authenticate the client application to access to the SCASC or the SSASC. However, the way a client application authenticates to the SCASC or SSASC is out of scope of the protocol.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcada0f8-31aa-4a0d-8a84-35cffc424aab .

camssa:78c38ccd-d7dc-4460-9a1a-e12eeae18cf1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 is specification-independent and can be implemented without dependencies on platforms. Moreover, the IETF, a vendor-neutral Standards Development Organisation, developed the technical specification independently of any vendor products.

TLS 1.3 2018 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d6f78047-10ae-4d5f-b9a8-247f4ec51024 .

camssa:78c81d71-2f9c-4054-b91f-8b03ecf2524e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EN 16234-1 e-CF is not related to data portability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f5cf334-b2a6-4d64-872a-5e85580c3bdc .

camssa:78c90f02-6256-4bf1-8b87-10c0337d6f47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of this Core Vocabulary as a data model does not hamper the scalability of systems.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:18309b63-c985-4f82-8b0a-296b34df9476 .

camssa:78c94aa4-2060-4114-b9fe-8e475ef5ff0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Even though at the moment of elaborating the assessment the specification is used, the specification in itself does not give any innovative solution since it is a language used for the composition of web services.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7036be44-ea04-4a79-8587-aeaaef530718 .

camssa:78d074e4-6a6b-4d38-9b1b-9f87d2be19d8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There exist two independent communities, one providing public support and the other one in charge of the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification maintenance (see CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022). On one side, there is the IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE), which was created in 2018 and performs all activities related to counselling and advice under this specification; and on the other side, there is the CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences which is in charge of the maintenance of the specification, although it is also responsible to provide public support. The CEN/TC 428 comprises participants from national and CEN-recognised working groups (see CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 5 and CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences section, CEN/TC 428 Subcommittees and Working Groups). Interestingly, only ITPE provides an e-CF preview through the Access e-CF Explorer service. \r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/about-us/\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences section, CEN/TC 428 Subcommittees and Working Groups:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:29:0::::FSP_ORG_ID,FSP_LANG_ID:1218399,25&cs=1C0456547BD827F5A977AD2936836C8DA#1\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, Access e-CF Explorer:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/about-it-professionalism/competences/the-e-competence-framework/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:828845dc-5d6c-4bb0-a48d-950278216b76 .

camssa:78d5140c-efdc-4ce4-b410-8fb80a8ee7ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of CAdES as electronic signature for signing online documents does not hamper the scalability of systems.\r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:030161e8-5c6d-48c7-b579-8363b9e2a327 .

