        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT is hosted at W3C's website and it is available to everyone for free for its use, implementation or study.                  \r
\r
See:                                                                                                                                       https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84c219c1-481f-4038-8994-132f0840d019 .

camssa:79b55343-abc2-40ba-a5c7-f5e6f6d76fb8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS achieves information confidentiality through the use of SSL/TLS (Secure Sockets Layer/Transport Layer Security) protocols, which encrypt the data exchanged between the client and server. The encryption process scrambles the information in such a way that it can only be deciphered by the intended recipient, ensuring that it remains confidential even if intercepted during transit.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc4e1213-da40-428d-bf8f-1f45a9edf747 .

camssa:79b6af3d-13f7-45d5-ae4a-4410c67fd890 a cav:Score,
