camssa:79d6b77f-2a1e-4fb2-9077-644750c51d41 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDF N-Triples is a lined-based plain text format that performs encoding RDF graphs, this encoding is carried out by using UTF-8. As RDF is the main technology used to publish Linked Open Data (LOD), therefore, the specification could help to the publication of data as LOD. \r
However, N-Triples presents a tedious process if the purpose is encode big amounts of data. \r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/n-triples/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:945b8c53-f37f-40c9-a7fd-bb816e2b94ae .

