camssa:7b332670-09bd-437e-a5e2-54a64c0dbf31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is primarily focused on the transmission and reception of log messages and does not inherently guarantee data processing accuracy. However, following the standard format proposed by the protocol can 
guarantee data accuracy to an extent.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:45cdc7fb-0826-4476-a5b2-bc89d600fc06 .

camssa:7b402258-41a9-46a4-8422-e3da26b356cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are Directives regulating participation on the development of standards. Participation is limited to \r
membership approval and sometimes the payment of a fee.\r
ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has \r
adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop \r
standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation \r
through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The \r
decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical \r
feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
ETSI Portal reference: \r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/esi/esi-activities'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01be744c-e33a-4937-991a-6deb2f9f8ac3 .

camssa:7b44b3a3-6de9-4c92-b7cb-1bca0135dd7c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EuroVoc is to facilitate the processing of data of administations mainly European but also National. By allowing to make the data available to other persons or organisations, the EuroVoc Contributes \r
to the development of eGovernment reducing the administrative burden. \r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0805e5aa-5bec-401c-9215-b74688c2621c .

camssa:7b4cd8e6-6fc8-4a73-a965-385ace5bb1b4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification includes detailed guidelines for business process modeling, which helps in defining and automating administrative procedures. Additionally, the registry and repository components manage metadata about services, facilitating efficient discovery and access. Finally, the messaging services ensure reliable and secure delivery of business information, which is crucial for handling administrative data.

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cff747fb-0792-4af2-a8d2-848cf66d214c .

camssa:7b4ce13d-0bfc-4871-8fb8-3a10f3ce706d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS is independent of any specification and can be implemented without dependencies with technologies.

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499

Domain Names - Implementation and Specification: 
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10c2eb29-20da-4b49-bae1-bbe5a51e8957 .

camssa:7b4ed48e-d4de-4631-a9c8-f0b674a838bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS takes into account essential safety aspects when it comes to the design of APIs.  Security in OAS is tackled with the "Security Requirement Object" where security mechanisms are settled to authorise requests.\r
\r
OAS Security Requirements Object:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#security-requirement-object\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5921106-9c75-41f8-ac78-9547611a5bd8 .

camssa:7b4f5368-d73d-450c-a7fc-3231ce4fe6ed a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:7b524175-f97f-42a1-b0a1-ea9d90cda1ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF), a global, open standards organization not specific to any particular region or governmental body, developed HTTP. While not a European Standard, HTTP is used extensively across all Member States.

HTTP and IETF reference:
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Evolution_of_HTTP#http1.1_%E2%80%93_the_standardized_protocol
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb9646ab-ee4c-4c66-ad22-d4afb6f7b2f7 .

camssa:7b5565c3-d2a4-47b7-8f73-50e7b9612eb8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Neither PROV, nor any of its specifications have been found included in the National Catalogue of recommended specifications of any Member State.\r
\r
CAMSS List of standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f5a1fa7-f711-4ced-b70c-5116327ba216 .

camssa:7b57bf91-dcc5-4b30-b6ef-4f200a07e4a9 a cav:Score,
