camssa:7b5f7ea9-2951-4b4d-9c48-18191394005a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS can be extended with several transport protocols to provide a safer data exchange.   the Domain Name System Security Extensions (DNSSEC) modify DNS to add support for cryptographically signed responses, while other extensions such as Transaction Signature  (TSIG), add support for cryptographic authentication between trusted peers and are commonly used to authorize zone transfer or dynamic update operations.\r
\r
Resource Records for the DNS Security Extensions:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4034\r
\r
 Extension Mechanisms for DNS:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6891\r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc1034.txt\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41e16105-98f6-470f-a2a5-afd91ce56696 .

camssa:7b6051b3-81e0-4717-bfb5-f0a28a1b042b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to section 4.4 of the ETSI TS 119 512 specification document, the Profile element outlines the 
technical details of a preservation profile, allowing a client to use the preservation interface to communicate 
with the preservation service. Full implementation of specific provisions is achieved when combined with its 
companion documents, ETSI TS 119 511. This combination ensures a more comprehensive understanding 
of administrative procedures, rules, and services.

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.02.01_60/ts_119512v010201p.pdf

ETSI TS 119 511 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7228d590-14d1-4f76-9ad7-adec12ab224a .

camssa:7b6668f0-0e04-4b92-a44a-78cf775119c3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

