camssa:7c9626c2-c0cc-4e9b-ac78-2bb780e71b16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP has been selected for the description of datasets by three European Initiatives: The European Data Portal, The European Open Data Portal and the JRC Data Catalogue. \r
\r
DCAT-AP for data portals:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:669fe83d-e0c9-4d6b-a4a0-513f2863c596 .

camssa:7c9849c5-ed03-4dd8-906c-7c6546205c16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2022, IPSec has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:867f0f84-1252-480a-ae85-51cc430d4c3b .

camssa:7ca4433e-9051-417e-b2ce-4ab536e3b2d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of TSP is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable specification. \r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ad16e8f-107a-44dd-a424-0d1c256bd23f .

camssa:7ca4d06c-bd1e-43c9-83e4-f0e01c96d537 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalRuleML aims to close the gap between natural language text description and semantic norm modelling. Providing a common solution for treating legal resources the specification can then foster Semantic Web technologies such as: NLP, Information Retrieval (IR), graph representation, as well as Web ontologies and rules.\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6da98297-919a-4709-a815-50706d0700e7 .

camssa:7caaa2a0-a9dd-41ad-8e85-b142b9a1cbd5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is sufficiently mature, and there is documentation available on the following link:\r
\r
IPSec Working Group Documents:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/wg/ipsec'"""@en ;
