camssa:7cf8624b-2c23-40cb-9794-dc0d00361be4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"TLS 1.3 provides mechanisms for reusing relevant information, notably through Pre-Shared Keys and session tickets. With this method, systems save and reuse details from earlier secure exchanges, speeding up future connections. As an example, after a client authenticates, the server can give it a 'ticket' to remember that authentication, avoiding the need to re-authenticate next time.

TLS 1.3 Resumption and Pre-Shared Key Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-2.2

TLS 1.3 Session tickets Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-4.6.1\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:65a420d2-d11e-488e-aa89-32989b09673d .

