        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of genericode is not related to providing an access control mechanism. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9fd5f93-f63d-4024-abab-4da5dd0db3e3 .

camssa:7d1945fc-5a72-4892-8833-bba528f7494c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is part of the Electronic Signatures Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications. The ESI dates back to 2012, when the General Policy Requirements for Trust Service Providers supporting Electronic Signatures (ETSI EN 319 401) specification was first issued. Since its first publication, there have been many extensions one of which is ETSI TS 119 612, whose version 2.2.1 was released in 2016 when the eIDAS regulation identified the need to create protocols to develop preservation services for trust service providers, as mentioned in ETSI SR 019 510. Finally, in 2024 was published the latest version of the specification (version 2.3.1).

ESI specification history:
https://standards.globalspec.com/std/14387016/EN%20319%20401

ETSI TS 119 612 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf

ETSI EN 319 401 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf

ETSI SR 019 510 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_sr/019500_019599/019510/01.01.01_60/sr_019510v010101p.pdf

eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:246ed86a-ab41-4d5f-b4ca-0a38768776b9 .

