    cav:value "0" .

camssa:7d56998d-96b1-4739-8f54-33016b79f1c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As Internet Protocol Stack, IPv6 it is being selected gradually by different Member States. The specification is the most used for the data exchange over the internet therefore IPv6 fosters the visibility of data across borders. \r
\r
The European Union is willing to implement the IPV6 as state on the following report: "The adoption of IPv6 in Europe, in particular within European public administrations, is still low, but the availability of IPv6 communication is vital for the economic development and the digitisation of European public administrations. The goals of the Digital Agenda for Europe and the Digital Single Market Strategy are based on stable and reliable data networks."\r
See: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/ipv6_framework_for_european_governments_0.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e61844b-cf9f-464a-983b-a4695cdd7852 .

camssa:7d5a1114-cdb5-4f84-bb3b-b515ab82efb9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Slovenia is recommending ODRL2 in its ICT National Catalogue.\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c699ca57-9042-4213-b631-16f4f206c757 .

camssa:7d5a3e4f-5d32-4655-b410-ea64df72b7e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
ETSI standard making:\r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c5d387bb-c1f7-48d8-9dfd-6cf34453dae5 .

camssa:7d5c84bf-f48e-4549-a983-fd7cac99d960 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7d5d836f-c520-4408-abe3-4a01a2b89f95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a5f4b20-079b-4a28-982d-2ee03f4d4d45 .

