camssa:7dd94164-6922-433d-bd1b-cbe9cf945ea8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are many tools assessing the conformance of DNS's implementations.  For instance, the DNS Compliance Testing provides tools to allow Registries and Registrars (amongst others) to check the DNS protocol compliance of the servers they are delegating zones to.\r
\r
GITHUB DNS Compliance Testing:\r
https://gitlab.isc.org/isc-projects/DNS-Compliance-Testing\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9ab7c80-2554-4f84-9aac-77aa75b1fedf .

camssa:7dd94e3b-af01-48e7-b835-c969fe5c7bbc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD 1.1 is supporting the second level of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee's 5-stars schema for open data. It eases the availability of the data and structures XML files. Additionally, XSD 1.1 is implied within the RDF 1.1 XML Syntax, used for the serialisation of RDF documents as XML. Therefore, XSD fosters the publication of data as Open Data. \r
See: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ab59021-c0ec-472b-878b-9e721fdb0cfb .

camssa:7ddb0d4b-5482-419d-8662-8150a99af69d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'PROV primarily focuses on capturing and representing provenance information rather than providing specific mechanisms for secure data processing. However, the use of PROV in systems or applications can indirectly contribute to the secure processing of data by providing traceability, accountability, integrity, and auditing capabilities.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1c7e2cdd-3387-4b12-8b02-ee3ad325c2d5 .

camssa:7de01dcf-7f90-4edf-b33f-df40e130cfd7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7de4a646-b3e0-41b2-8cc7-638e14d33a0a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CPSV-AP is a reusable and extensible data model for harmonising the way public services are described in a machine-readable format. So it describes the public administrations and eases their visualization and comprehensibility.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4e200cf-3950-4d93-a265-11db1e034593 .

camssa:7de68f8f-a38c-42a2-b883-fc82df936177 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b4f0d1b7f1d41c70797fa200c6fc73ac01f2f1659319e5cb1cebe8f5e79c1fcb ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7de7f827-9a39-47b4-8339-8267b194145f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Better regulation toolbox is an internal European Commission resource designed as a complement to the Commission's Better regulation guideline. It provides specific and operational guidance to those involved with the various better regulation instruments. These instruments aim to give support for the implementation, monitoring, and impact assessment of public policies and laws on which new and innovative solutions should be based. Therefore, it can be considered that the Better Regulation Toolbox fosters the creation of innovative solutions and services across Europe.\r
\r
Better Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf ."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db728f48-b3e2-44f6-98f8-6be4265f15b8 .

