        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ASiC and ASiC Baseline Profile are open standards developed and maintained by ETSI, and it is available for free at ETSI’s webpage for everyone to study or implement. \r
See:  \r
https://www.etsi.org/standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a07d0487-cf4d-42e2-870d-09c2e2ef812b .

camssa:7e8d0659-d6d3-4e0b-b1cd-34d3108c67d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, CSV is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. CSV is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on the IPv6 specification (RFC 2818).\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfa00445-7260-4472-bd01-c49797c8fd6c .

