camssa:7e9d169f-48b3-4a95-a176-ced97ca96357 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After searching in the different official European websites, a cross-border project, called SML software, has been found that uses SMTP as his email server configuration. The specification is included as the implementation of the eDelivery BDXL, which as the CEF eDelivery, aims to help the European public administrations to exchange digital data across borders fostering a common digital environment. The reference to the usage of SMTP can be found in the Quick Start Guide v2.2.\r
\r
Main page project:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/SML\r
\r
CEF eDelivery BDXL:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/eDelivery+BDXL+1.6\r
\r
Quick Start Guide v2.2:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/download/attachments/82773331/BDMSL%20Quick%20Start%20Guide%20v2.2.pdf?version=1&modificationDate=1582037177388&api=v2"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eeb98198-51ed-43b2-a697-7f9aa826775f .

camssa:7e9d716b-6b90-4e22-9c30-584ae57e8507 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification describes a set of security features of ebXML RegRep and incorporates different specifications to enable the secure processing of data. According to the specification documentation, ebXML supports the management of authorized users of the ebXML service.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
ebXML RegRep Part 2:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rs-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__32703_422331532'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39c89adf-8441-4106-80d9-20cc34b32215 .

camssa:7ea1d840-8fbc-4518-8edc-546206f59988 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS Queries over HTTPS (DoH) is included in the second report of the observatory function on encryption by the Europol and Eurojust Public Information. Europol is the law enforcement agency of the European Union (EU) that aims to support its Member States in preventing and combating all forms of serious international and organised crime, cybercrime and terrorism. On the other hand, Eurojust is the European Union Agency for Criminal Justice Cooperation where national judicial authorities work closely together to fight serious organised cross-border crime. 

Second report of the observatory function on encryption: https://www.eurojust.europa.eu/sites/default/files/Publications/Reports/2020-01_Joint-EP-EJ-Report_Observatory-Function-on-Encryption_EN.pdf

Europol: https://www.europol.europa.eu/

Eurojust Public Register: https://www.eurojust.europa.eu/public-register'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f83241f9-fd41-4046-886f-5b119a00c09d .

camssa:7ea92a73-89a5-4dc8-9493-ae3b291883db a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:7eac8a01-9275-454d-a3c7-52a715fa020c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are no requirements on the extent of the implementation of the specification and the extent of the data\r
contents being used should vary between use cases. It's recommended to publish sets of requirements per\r
implementation.\r
\r
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5bbc7e77-4a8b-4923-878c-452a60151645 .

