camssa:7ebadf11-a8f2-45b7-b263-c30df6a09f45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Many implementations are using OWL2 in the market. In the following link, there is a summary with some important examples. Moreover, there are a lot of software supporting the implementation and usage of the specification.\r
_x000D_\r
OWL2 implementation:_x000D_\r
https://www.w3.org/2001/sw/wiki/OWL/Implementations"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b88a2008-be15-496e-83dd-288411ca6ba0 .

camssa:7eca71d9-e28f-493f-8596-84bac4b707a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SEMIC developed a service that checks the integrity and consistency against the DCAT-AP specification of one or more software description metadata files. It is available for free in Joinup, the European Commission collaborative platform for the reuse of IT Solutions.\r
\r
DCAT-AP validator: \r
http://dcat-ap.semic.eu/dcat-ap_validator.html \r
\r
DCAT-AP in data portals:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:043c049c-7c14-470e-91e6-886b1b1bcfa6 .

camssa:7ecd6704-d34a-43aa-a717-d4e8537c2d44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the specification comes from the IETF community, different initiatives surrounding CSV encourages the creation of communities that work on the specification and digital solutions.\r
\r
IETF Community about: \r
https://www.ietf.org/how/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:180132b3-316a-4897-bca0-cc33af311d1c .

camssa:7ecea193-c52f-4215-a12c-38e110c734ed a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ba46c76c10ad769a23ce4a9a34cb4d96a00407d5fc14ad1c791a870be7563c2b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7ed51ea7-ac2d-41f3-879b-076eb867548c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODRL is a specification that provides a core vocabulary that allows the description and representation of information in a standardised and machine-readable format fostering the data exchange and the interoperability of organisations and resources using it. \r
\r
An example of its potential use on the publication and exchange of open data is the inclusion within SPECIAL, an H2020 European Project that stands for "Scalable Policy-awarE Linked Data arChitecture for prIvacy, trAnsparency and compLiance". This project aims to provide solutions for data protection and its reuse using standards to allow maximum applicability and interoperability across borders. \r
\r
Moreover, the specification offers serialisation in common formats for open data publication and shareability such as RDF or JASON-LD. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core \r
\r
SPECIAL Deliverable: \r
https://www.specialprivacy.eu/images/documents/SPECIAL_D17_M17_V10.pdf\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6380a80e-196e-44d0-be41-2ce76dcc484f .

camssa:7edc26e6-b678-4d77-a618-5fb9f3104307 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7edc2a5d-3c5e-4f81-b5b9-d5945da59c0c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7edc3950-3db7-4f30-b7be-976ba8bdca36 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is designed to express and manage digital rights, permissions, and restrictions related to digital \r
content. It includes mechanisms for specifying access controls, limitations, and conditions on how digital \r
assets can be used.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d193084-523e-48e6-98da-baf9af4b8434 .

camssa:7ee49673-6e62-4308-b0ca-b15c1cd5c971 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ab118934e7af3d561b9036668a1de9f17c020207e8ebb0ed33d9405e12eeef4c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7ee4bf38-fa13-4518-9df3-5390fc983fad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are some projects that include XSLT "A Prototype Cross-Border GML Data Service" that has opened new opportunities for creating\r
integrated cross-border spatial data services with Geography Mark-up Language. In addition, the INSPIRE Directive and related regulations can also be considered a cross-border EU initiative, included in the ISA programme.\r
\r
See:\r
https://agile-online.org/conference_paper/cds/agile_2004/papers/4-2-3_lehto.pdf\r
https://ies-svn.jrc.ec.europa.eu/projects/registry-development/wiki/Re3gistry_1_0_documentation#_cp3"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dda34b62-372f-423f-85d1-604bd329a8c6 .

camssa:7eea1a22-ab3c-4889-b506-1e8eb80207da a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7eea407b-608b-4dc1-be99-dc955694a5fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL helps to ensure interoperability when it comes to define processes for setting standards-based infrastructure  for electronic Extensible Markup Language (XML) business documents exchange. This is why, among other reasons, it appears as one of the setting standards for the  "Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications eligible for referencing in public procurement"\r
\r
COMMISSION IMPLEMENTING DECISION of 31 October 2014 on the identification of Universal Business Language version 2.1 for referencing in public procurement:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/ES/TXT/?qid=1657095448506&uri=CELEX:32014D0771'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:693115d4-024e-46a3-95d4-2da28c818246 .

camssa:7eee255f-7eb4-4fd0-863d-19ccb801a782 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:7ef05ddb-f827-40ce-a93b-163f8cd71b6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Since the specification is directly related with the certification of existing data, it can help administrations with the implementation of the once-only principle. Allowing the reuse of existing data that has been certified, the specification can avoid administrations asking for same certified references in procurement, for instance.\r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39bfdee8-68ab-449b-a32e-658f78d39e0b .

camssa:7ef06584-1992-48e4-8678-8488411608ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the time of elaborating this assessment, FTP does not foster the creation of innovative solutions. Since its development in 1971, it has been used in combination with other specifications in order to enhance security (e.g. TLS & SSL). However, even these extensions of FTP are not considered innovative solutions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f0794eb-720b-486e-afe1-fa7f7f8e1a2b .

camssa:7f0166a8-cc77-4344-bcbc-5df70c1dbb21 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:7f046af4-af5e-40dd-b468-3aaf556f6547 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-164f43cef11b50b88c51c7115a7b37e506af696852ddaf46dfc1cb1c1521ec6d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:7f07ce56-b1ac-42d2-b0c1-ebea531fbcfe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GraphQL does not mandate a particular programming language or storage system for application services that implement it. Instead, application services take their capabilities and map them to a uniform language, type system, and philosophy that GraphQL encodes. Therefore, GraphQL can be said to be independent of any technologies.\r
\r
GraphQL specification overview:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f585471-5375-472b-8d5c-bcc3d6591a3e .

camssa:7f0974a3-f211-44b1-940e-cabd8d4fe8ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The degree to which the ELI specification accommodates partial implementations is contingent upon the
particular requirements and characteristics under consideration. Typically, specifications such as ELI are
crafted with a focus on modularity, thereby enabling those implementing it to select and rank specific
elements in accordance with their individual needs and available resources.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9cbdc36-a9f8-4125-bdbd-219b84c83aeb .

camssa:7f0c3c20-7104-494f-8bf9-95c8ab92ff88 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There exist different initiatives across Europe adopting the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification. It is the case of the Digital Competence Framework for Citizens (DigComp) initiative, which provides a common understanding of what digital competences, knowledge, skills and attitudes are, and helps citizens to engage with digital, new and emerging technologies.\r
\r
Digital Competence Framework for Citizens (DigComp) reference:\r
https://joint-research-centre.ec.europa.eu/digcomp_en?msclkid=27a7a8f2b64611eca3ebf019d32a2764'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1000eb1e-3152-4566-b223-37fd184c9f5c .

camssa:7f161684-230f-4560-a3ce-d15d3cf0f048 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No document or study has been found assessing the CPOV in terms of efficiency or effectiveness.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0993689-7f6c-418a-95c3-5c6a18f4c200 .

camssa:7f19c96c-b452-470b-89a6-04fae9015639 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There exist some assessments indirectly addressing the effectiveness of OData in industry (e.g., Microsoft Open Technologies), or documentation focusing on the improvement of the OData specification (e.g., the future release, OData.Neo).\r
\r
OData assessments reference:\r
https://www.odata.org/blog/\r
\r
Microsoft Open Technologies (China) reference:\r
https://www.odata.org/blog/microsoft-open-technologies-releases-odata-producer-for-sugarcrm-to-boost-the-efficiency-of-corporate-data-exchange/\r
\r
OData.Neo reference:\r
https://github.com/OData/OData.Neo'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6cd2f9ad-8399-4b84-9881-077d2a4884ac .

camssa:7f2040e9-057b-40fc-b1f8-e7f4884bbdc2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:7f23c706-5a06-45ab-bcbd-e5002f7f2d2b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
