camssa:7f23d3ba-29fe-4ff4-8a4a-b6a0c3f7058c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/\r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e683955b-a416-4eb7-a0d1-c988098c32f8 .

camssa:7f2c4233-4c91-4ff0-8f5e-2fc2dc5e4152 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a64b01ca9e737c550b205ba3a8a46b3fcfc9447b648ba8ef15d62d3ada26141 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:7f2fbe72-4f2d-42d6-9990-30f7e119b799 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP is involved in the European solution for data spaces and digital transformation, enabling data sharing, interoperability, and efficient data transport within the context of European initiatives.

Emerging approaches for data-driven innovation in Europe Reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/custom-page/attachment/2022-02/jrc-tr_ddi_2021_v9_online.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:936ca4d5-4000-4995-b39b-da7723b21c60 .

camssa:7f306361-fb48-491d-b1ed-ccc67716e5db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By easing the digital communication SMP is an asset for the simplification and the reduction of administrative burden. The specification fosters the digital exchange of information by enhancing the discoverability of Access points easing the digitalisation of data transactions between administrations and also with other stakeholders like business or citizens.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1de65596-4364-4826-9b5e-adc327d8b1af .

camssa:7f30bd3f-6d2c-4beb-8c31-938a4e28d0cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG is a specification that supports data portability, and therefore, supporting the development of European Public Services. \r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:646819fc-5232-4f46-83a9-2d0c57d8b95c .

camssa:7f30c835-2f9b-48b9-8979-f4a286ee8806 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XACML is used in Privacy Preserving Perimeter Protection Project. In this project, XACML is used to implement a privacy-aware access control module.

Privacy Preserving Perimeter Protection Project:
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/312784/reporting
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3df2b696-69b0-45b4-a785-f900b2063e24 .

camssa:7f3386eb-238c-4253-85b4-50f9a4f01cca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Transparency of the development process is evidenced by a defined and publicly available documentation on the development and maintenance of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98bc9186-bb12-41a5-b34a-5907d5d6bf56 .

camssa:7f34f083-41de-495c-b4b6-7d29bf15968f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6746b40-0cbb-4507-9a49-c208b527f37b .

