camssa:7f73c879-1c88-48cd-abad-20b97a74f16f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EuroVoc is used for the EU Open Data Portal, the site where EU Institutions publish their datasets for their \r
reuse. In there, it is also used the classification of EuroVoc in order to improve the shareability, researchability and interoperability when processing the data. It helps to link data under knowledge domains. \r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.htm'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58f2da8b-b046-4ca4-b639-2170d690f1c1 .

camssa:7f73f04b-c41c-4e54-a8b6-9d6fb3eb4625 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:7f75291f-644e-4233-b41f-6427e553e91e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is a powerful tool for providing visibility into administrative procedures, rules data, and services within 
a networked environment. For example, syslog can be configured to log various administrative actions and 
commands executed on network devices, servers, or other systems. Also, syslog is commonly used for 
logging security events and incidents and allows administrators to define rules for logging specific events or 
conditions.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e83b18b3-d748-4416-a633-0fc59dd11cb6 .

camssa:7f7eafeb-ecfa-47ff-997e-22c4b593c362 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:7f82c3f7-fa2b-493c-8b05-6a7547673459 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS is an extension of FTP which allows public administration to exchange information securely, so it avoids multiple requests of standard information to citizens or businesses. \r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04fc554e-5aa4-492d-b0db-0029f003875f .

camssa:7f898d49-b7b6-42dd-bbdb-4a432f4536c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
