camssa:7facc026-4943-464a-a6e9-eee939c4ac47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL specification is designed to support extension. The extensibility feature of ODRL allows users to \r
introduce custom elements, semantics, and vocabulary to meet specific requirements beyond the core \r
features defined in the standard. This extension mechanism is valuable for accommodating diverse use \r
cases and industry-specific needs.\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:111ea483-6ea8-4502-9f5e-e487fd57815e .

camssa:7facffa2-6b74-4eb8-8036-1873c1316b3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0114f677-6ace-4ac6-ab99-5e7e0db33e45 .

camssa:7fafb172-5599-4c51-8ae3-87d1337972c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:7fb6b4da-9178-41d8-a601-301b54c04234 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of ISO 19941 is often evaluated through various means, including practical implementations and pilot projects. For instance, a 2017-paper mentions this specification as a reference for an FBM model of ISO Cloud Computing Architecture, which demonstrates the effectiveness of ISO 19941 as it taken into account.\r
\r
An FBM Model of ISO Cloud Computing Architecture: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-73805-5_16\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ae83c4b-4edd-49c6-972f-6387018ca8c8 .

camssa:7fb81695-ed2f-42ef-ac99-c2478e2d0ca2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documents assessing and documenting YAML features and providing 
possible improvements of its performance among other aspects. There are two papers that can be useful to discover how YAML can be effective.
In "Comparision between JSON and YAML for data serialization" it is determined and discussed the primary differences between two different serialization formats, namely YAML and JSON. 
In "YAML: A tool for hardware design visualization and capture", is described an approach that helps to capture the structural aspects of a design at a high level of abstraction and enables the system designer to enter designs "schematically" using predefined structural and functional entities conforming to UML notation.
Therefore, the specification can achieve different objectives alone or together with other specifications.

"Comparision between JSON and YAML for data serialization" 
https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?repid=rep1&type=pdf&doi=636a2b04d98c0af8e9d6f59148352dd63af4f0c1

"YAML: A tool for hardware design visualization and capture":
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/874023'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2797f211-e5f1-4887-a904-8ef817fd34da .

camssa:7fb933ec-330f-40cf-bc04-3939868007c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the specification can be associated with solutions or projects aiming to ensure the availability of interfaces with internal information, the specification in itself does not foster its availability.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1c40da6-9090-4513-a4c9-6c7d72c68c7b .

