camssa:80ecc8ee-4982-463e-9ff5-c54f5fcfe148 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EuroVoc is not related to security and privacy of the data exchange. Therefore, this criterion \r
is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73c069bf-8f7f-442e-af19-c2aa589a41fa .

camssa:80ed5a48-87d7-48cc-9806-6482c3000d34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Genericode can be used effectively in a multilingual context due to its flexibility in representing code lists and controlled values. The "Language" tag support allows for the inclusion of metadata alongside code values, which can include language tags to specify the language of the metadata. This means that descriptions, labels, or other textual information associated with code values can be provided in multiple languages within the same genericode file.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:379bd9c9-6714-4731-9750-10a3763c636c .

camssa:80f1555d-2b37-40bc-b0ad-3259c79c3265 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being a standard protocol for mantaining and accessing directory services, LDAP can be used across \r
business domains as long as they require the storage and management of user information. \r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f0555c5-6a90-45a8-b872-1bb6942f66ca .

camssa:80f3d339-b865-4144-b8b9-c2a8ae23c437 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Every new version of the specification goes through a defined process with open and public consultations. Request for comments are not restricted to the RDA members but are open to all."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3233e014-fe5f-4575-a3c3-b41859044af6 .

