camssa:8115f1d2-1539-4984-bbcc-84aba97867d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Every new version of the specification goes through a defined process with open and public consultations. Request for comments are not restricted to the RDA members but are open to all."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:799f7fa8-c751-496d-8c8a-ab6bfb618629 .

camssa:81213573-1300-403f-af40-6697c423b904 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP allows applications to determine the revocation status of identified certificates. In this sense, the\r
specification addresses data protection but does not make any reference to relevant regulations at a European level.\r
\r
OCSP reference, section 2:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfb6c1a4-f0fb-4eea-92b9-c3cc7cadb400 .

camssa:812d2d43-3779-4673-9ed1-92b1efe48098 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TS 119 614-1 is a set of conformance testing practices for electronic signatures and preservation and is \r
intended to support the development and manufacture of different solutions at EU level. The specification is intentionally not linked to any software development technology and is also intentionally agnostic on implementation strategies. This is one of the reasons why the test assertions set includes tests on the correctness of the structure of all elements specified by the XML Schemas associated with ETSI TS 119 612.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88573eaa-6528-4622-979c-b18cedcf0b48 .

camssa:812e4ebc-1f94-46ea-abac-8c6a2cff8dbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a11c59c9-f62e-4572-bbaa-ec5ee51a7d0a .

camssa:812ebe71-b5ab-4ae8-a1d9-74855ef785ca a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:8130cba6-0715-4adb-bb8e-96e17b118ded a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Not enough information has been found to answer negatively or positively to this criterion. Moreover, it seems that the specification is not aimed to foster e-accessibility to legislation. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:225d4e5d-847d-4c59-b717-7feb3788328a .

camssa:813922dc-9e7f-4afa-ae6b-86e32a80ff4f a cav:Score,
