camssa:81776cf1-b22d-4faf-8772-b163c1160ade a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ETSI TS 119 612 does not allow any kind of customisation as it has to be implemented how it is described in the specification's document.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:49f66292-3b66-4b55-bea9-c7a23924c274 .

camssa:817f49fa-ed21-47fb-9347-5ae11511ea90 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EUROSTAT (European Commission) is in charge of maintaining and publishing each of the three NUTS levels. The specification is upgraded by national, regional and local administrations and representatives of the Member States in collaboration with the European Commission. However, contributions are not always available (see EUROSTAT-NUTS lattest amendments reference, History of NUTS section, NUTS 2021 XLS document).\r
\r
European Parliament reference:\r
https://www.europarl.europa.eu/factsheets/en/sheet/99/la-nomenclatura-comun-de-unidades-territoriales-estadisticas-nuts-\r
\r
EUROSTAT-NUTS lattest amendments reference, History of NUTS section, NUTS 2021 XLS document:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/history'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:313b3851-bfce-44c4-8b85-6a1994c60c29 .

camssa:818060e0-31b6-492c-9699-27e555e96033 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification promotes a common framework for security in communication between organisations. This can help facilitate agreements between organisations to define a unique method for securing communications. Thus, IPsec can help to protect data using a common framework.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e90778d-c31c-46cf-8a8b-5b6029526df9 .

camssa:8189ce2a-9079-4d6c-bc8b-aed43f12bf84 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"CPOV standardizes information on public organizations facilitates interoperability between systems, and allows government entities to share and reuse data efficiently by reducing duplicates and improving information accuracy. By facilitating access to consistent data, CPOV improves citizens and businesses' ability to interact with public services, and therefore, simplifies the delivery of them.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e6b6844-a83e-42f1-9752-477308edc6a4 .

camssa:818a9df6-2be9-4c45-a7dc-110b3b429b07 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:818baf3f-5556-4dea-a8c7-2636e50cc248 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All solutions developed in ISA² Programme are under ISA Open Metadata Licence which is perpetual, royalty-free and non-exclusive license to Use and re-Use the Works.\r
\r
ISA open metadata license:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/licence/isa-open-metadata-licence-v11"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1835340e-0806-432a-beaa-e79a6333e001 .

camssa:818c40a1-a806-47c8-9f03-8b10bf7ec766 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are many free online tools that uses OWLAPI code to validate whether an ontology is conformant with the different OWL profiles. One working example:_x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
OWL Validator:_x000D_\r
http://www.cosasbuenas.es/blog/owl-validator\r
\r
OWL 2 Validator: \r
http://visualdataweb.de/validator/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ccb0b769-5a17-4dfd-9f7a-668f13c61a58 .

camssa:818d7853-bc34-4c2a-9bae-47e69d3a33ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XACML specification provides robust capabilities for customization, allowing organisations to define, implement, and manage custom access control policies tailored to their specific requirements. Moreover, there are XACML customisations available on the market.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html

XACML OASIS Hierarchical Resource reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/standard/xacml3-0-hier/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0afce7c-18c4-4eae-b44e-c529f1cedb4e .

camssa:8193098a-893c-43a8-bad9-3e418e836b9c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33b5b305bcc0a995fd3c592dc8a6f52d0749a6e817aa85844f3e4f31c7dea344 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:819e2b9c-b87d-4f1c-8f29-f3d64aa8c94c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed by 2011 and has been broadly implemented and used for the representation of graphical information containing vectors and mixed vector/raster. Also, it is interesting to mention that it has been evolving along with other specifications to ensure the interoperability between some of them.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3320b6e6-0226-4491-9645-1eec51e03b0f .

camssa:81a2308c-5c43-41bf-ba9f-9d48b98b4b41 a cav:Score,
