    cav:value "1" .

camssa:82007bdd-129d-4cec-a33a-c9bdaf06317f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification can use XAuth (Extended Authentication) to guarantee user access. XAuth increases security by requiring remote dial-up clients to authenticate. In addition, XAuth utilises established authentication mechanisms, such as LDAP, to authenticate dial-up clients. Therefore, the specification can enhance access control mechanisms to improve security aspects.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

XAuth authentication mechanism:
https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortigate/7.4.0/administration-guide/277729/using-xauth-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:479334e5-130f-4dc6-95b8-1ebb1b277dfd .

camssa:82041b72-845f-45ba-a110-166432c5a5dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c09094de9d71f12686896827a205db683b6df58fa363bc5be2a7d99989e7dd0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:820cfccb-fa7d-4106-a426-71032f03c192 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP primarily focuses on enabling the discovery and access of datasets and data catalogs, rather than exposing interfaces to access public administration services directly. However, DCAT-AP can indirectly facilitates the exposure of interfaces by providing a standardized way to describe the datasets and data services that are available on a data portal. DCAT-AP includes metadata elements for describing data services, such as web services, APIs, and SPARQL endpoints, that can provide information on the technical characteristics of the service, and by using standard vocabularies and identifiers, it can provide additional information about the datasets and services that can help users to select and filter the most relevant services for their needs.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba078405-10d4-4a4a-84a7-5f8e039a8a1c .

camssa:821df186-ddab-4714-b825-488828c6f6f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:821e9393-b3e0-483e-8d4f-b5343ce7ada2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:821f5e89-d906-4f93-8443-bac1abaec3cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There is no assessment regarding the compliance of the specification with European Standardisation Regulation 1025/2012. Despite CEF is a European Commission action, there is no evidence to answer positively to this criterion. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f736dd9f-84e3-4fa2-b964-9666af7e9519 .

camssa:822444a4-f5f7-479f-94eb-72b145c2b27c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4a006ad6785e066d16c13daf48a60ee43ec33d1de1b06613c8e656ccf330a6d5 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8226b4f3-30da-42d9-973f-b7a780e57fd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification does not fully address all use cases of the IPsec architecture. The user may refer to other documentation that addresses additional details of the architecture in specific environments where ****\r
15comprehensibility considerations may be an asset.\r
\r
IPSec reference: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4301 '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2bc40b8a-8dee-4baa-b890-ace3887b1cf0 .

