camssa:826595d4-7afb-49d5-9249-aaec048c6be5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Taking the initial purpose of the specification, it can be considered that the specification is involved in fostering the comprehensibility of Public Administrations data as well as relevant data produced for the decision-making process. \r
\r
ELI provides a common schema for the definition of legislation metadata, easing the understanding and the shareability of legislation documents and their access. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a32021ce-7a34-4e49-a79f-ef0779d7bf88 .

camssa:8266a831-054d-4541-a193-4d72956d59df a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 16234-1 e-CF framework is not dependent on any other specification, operating system or web platform; therefore, the specification is platform-agnostic.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02b2eb83-c2d3-4eac-8a72-2af8760c1dac .

camssa:8267813b-e2be-4d9f-ae8b-ec238de9bcfe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS gives itself a criterion and guidelines and structure to develop APIs and also constitutes an environment for testing the conformity of the  application to the OAS parameters.  To this end, OAS conformance testing functionalities range from data and description validation (to check for the correct syntax and data flow) to mock servers (to provide example responses before writing code).  \r
\r
 Advatages of using OpenAPI:\r
https://oai.github.io/Documentation/start-here.html#advantages-of-using-openapi\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c38a6ecb-f85e-4093-a33e-6d6257b1a0d7 .

camssa:827226ec-6bc1-4dfd-b134-1f89e424f11d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8275da41-fc3b-4a51-b079-85d1ac72446d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As defined on the TC standardisation, only TC members are involved in the development of ISO standards. A review is carried out to arrange the consensus firstly within the TC members and subsequently is reviewed by the different ISO member bodies. However, it cannot be considered a public review, because only TC members can participate.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d5690e1-413b-4642-8237-03ff65e5d807 .

camssa:82771a0d-53d6-43d4-bcd8-c61eeaa80797 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software or platform. The Registered Organization Vocabulary can be used by any organisation.\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:33c1f41a-6df7-429f-9a07-2b557336f6d8 .

