camssa:828b1db8-e5d2-4e9a-9edd-b393a5cb3663 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, UTF-8 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision and included in the European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba71221c-2ba9-4d3a-bfd2-8c05536b348b .

camssa:828d36b7-6965-469f-ad38-7bb3fa160215 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Using Xforms 2.0 contributes to the increase in digital public services. By allowing public administrations to develop online forms, it reduces the administrative burden. \r
\r
Xforms 2.0 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/xformsusers/wiki/XForms_2.0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:380c3db4-2796-4716-aa21-f2ff11cbeda7 .

camssa:8290d9d9-bf18-4943-96f5-300b6e41480d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 is not related to enabling e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11468342-7d82-4f53-bfff-9a6718822d52 .

