    cav:value "100" .

camssa:82d61f80-f783-4f63-b21e-95e8615bcc97 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Standard for Public Code is a set of criteria that supports public organizations in developing and maintaining software and policy together. Therefore, the specification fosters the reduction of the administrative burden by enabling digital public services, reducing the extra cost of non-digital communications. Moreover, the specification aims to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of development processes for the creation of reusable solutions, which also contribute to the reduction of administrative burden. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fab967c-154d-4f9b-ac24-bf973c499f81 .

camssa:82da9e6f-1500-40fe-aa50-669f484f9a9e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6ec33e201b803a1cc0150c0da8dc42b2a0f1029cf31e7a2c0fc81d1d8336ef36 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:82dbe1ee-1f98-402d-ab76-1fe228849512 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification is an element with high relevance in the data and information exchange. UTF-8 as a specification to encoding data ensures that files, web applications and systems can be read by both parts implied in the communication ensuring the reliability of transferred data. Therefore, UTF-8 eases the trustworthy data exchange between administration and stakeholders. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:137e8f9d-6ba6-4693-a1f8-ac67f33919a0 .

camssa:82dd18d6-c95a-4535-873d-63017bd5f580 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:82e289a9-a4ff-4e73-8c24-353007e7161d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:82e59c52-8f4c-4d6a-95d3-38f6e7ad32e7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:82e67b7e-15db-4c76-89c0-f48690ff672d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Through the caching architectural principle, REST has the ability to store copies of frequently accessed data in several places along the requeest-response path.\r
The Cache Control Headers can indicate when a representation never expires, meaning that the data of the representation is well preserved.   \r
\r
REST Caching resference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/caching/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ce41769-860d-4260-878d-728b28500e02 .

camssa:82ef6644-4ab6-4cde-a566-9bf187b5c20b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "PDF/A is a business agnostic document format that can be reused in a cross-domain way."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:693fe460-0b20-44e3-8b94-efc010d3fc9d .

camssa:82f1aba8-5d14-4a17-a479-ac2112f110eb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33ea90f5c1bb01d4398c57d03a25934dc5722d5ddbc98a43911ea4fb302ec54c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:82f55b12-eb78-4a08-b878-2d8cda335d6d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData is tied up to RESTful APIs communication. Although the OData service declares its own data model in a machine-readable form, which allows customers to interact with the service on a generic basis, OData relies on RESTful APIs in order to be implemented.\r
\r
OData reference, 4 Service Model:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752204'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:122e9f7d-c682-4c6e-9595-cd869e6f02f6 .

