    cav:value "40" .

camssa:83cc5f73-c06c-4dc3-a695-2dc99f5b8195 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The SHACL has been assessed through the CAMSS Method which is in full compliance with Annex II criteria set out in the Regulation 1025/2012, hereafter 'the standardisation regulation'."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad0f0442-f42a-486a-b553-3cc02773fb57 .

camssa:83ccbd02-e339-4ec7-8246-758ed89b16e2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:83cd2747-d324-4423-9ab8-18bd1928908f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification provides a set of viewpoints that are related to different aspects such as security, privacy or governance. Also, it provides a few more that can be considered in a nutshell, the core components that digital public services need, and also the key building blocks to achieve interoperability. These views are High-level viewpoint and the Key Interoperability Enablers. 
These viewpoints and its components are elements considered when validating using the Interoperability Architecture Solutions Validator. If some of these basic elements are not including, the validator would report some errors and warnings. Nonetheless, this is what confirms the partial implementation of EIRA when defining solutions.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59d0abc1-d8b7-4392-be19-a4fff93259fb .

