camssa:83d926b1-281f-4d6b-b922-b0af37817977 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the main purpose of IPsec is not to simplify the delivery of public services, it can play a significant role. Public administrations often share sensitive data, and IPsec can protect this information. In this sense, IPsec can make communication between public administrations more efficient by establishing a unified security architecture. Thus, it is not necessary to establish a specific security layer for each individual communication.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0e71485-a43c-4fd7-b8e2-d60cdd92d92d .

