camssa:84064562-b6ca-4528-b128-a8aae2ea2a99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'First of all ISAE 3402 provides a guarantee in the context of the security and confidentiality of information for \r
users and companies. Therefore, when a public administration contracts a service from a private company, it \r
can request the ISAE 3402 to ensure that their data complies with adequate confidentiality and security.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc2d58a5-f4c3-43a3-ab27-cb0261215569 .

camssa:84191e60-350e-497f-8af8-aa36c95d726f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:841a3ebe-4bda-4e37-bcb1-9fd7d1ea3427 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'To support unauthorised access and modification of information, LDAP foresees a set of additional layers of \r
security that require authentication mechanisms such as SASL and TLS. It is vital that these security \r
functions be interoperable among all LDAP clients and servers on the Internet; therefore there has to be \r
minimum subset of security functions that is common to all implementations that claim LDAP conformance.\r
\r
LDAP Authentication methods and security mechanisms:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4513.txt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76687041-dafb-4ffe-bb1e-ce4873fb04c5 .

camssa:842271ab-f005-4678-87a2-950fc23ae53e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a18abe4842e04b608025fd70e54c3db5c2a10130c0dab0495479e7d5effb55d ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:842998f9-596f-4600-b0ce-0207bdfe040e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:842b7a7c-4822-4fd9-aa7f-099687ccc453 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are Directives regulating participation on the development of standards. Participation is limited to \r
membership approval and sometimes the payment of a fee.\r
ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has \r
adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop \r
standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation \r
through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The \r
decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical \r
feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
ETSI Portal reference: \r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/esi/esi-activities'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72689dd1-cd5a-44dc-8648-31f6e62b8fba .

camssa:842bde92-54f6-4298-b673-4887f119f3ed a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8434d0f7-a15c-4436-8d59-f53fe2ab9e25 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PAdES (ISO 14533-3:2017) is an ISO standard and as all ISO standards, they have to be paid to access its content. However, it can be checked out in ETSI website where the content is aligned with the ISO standard.  \r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09f87e93-0714-4aa2-a579-4eef4b607629 .

camssa:84386284-86cc-442b-9bb3-186596a869c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The objective of ETSI TS 119 612 is not to enable the long-term preservation of data/information, moreover it is described in the documentation that the hyperlinks described cannot be guaranteed to have long term validity.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6da3a326-7a90-447f-803e-617c36b7dde7 .

camssa:843cae46-0052-4398-abc5-2974519ed0de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After carrying out information retrieval, no document or study has been found assessing the CLV in terms of efficiency or effectiveness. However, there is an ISA2 documentation where there are defined use cases and benefits of using its solutions, including the different Core Vocabularies. \r
\r
Use cases and benefits of ISA² specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/docs/publications/isa2_study_use_cases_and_benefits_of_isa2_specifications_january_2019.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:070b7339-3039-43bd-9df2-67fc65b9fe45 .

