camssa:84e1e32a-db2b-48cf-9c73-3abd5616765e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification offers various ways to customise messages and connections. These mechanisms enable implementers and users to customise AMQP to suit their specific needs and environments, promoting flexibility and interoperability. For example, custom data types, filtering messages, and negotiation features are the most common customisable options. (Refer to sections 1.1.2 Described Types, 2.2 Version Negotiation and 3.5.1 Filtering Messages)

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e541cec-3bf5-4834-8367-45d80d6f778e .

camssa:84e67696-c429-4b2b-a493-c9fe4f803b73 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Better Regulation Toolbox in itself is a common method for planning, developing, assessing and monitoring the implementation of policies and laws. It is used by de different EU institutions involved in these tasks, moreover, it can be transposed to national level to ensure that national laws and policies are developed with the maximum accuracy. \r
\r
Better Regulation Toolbox on European Comission webpage:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/law/law-making-process/planning-and-proposing-law/better-regulation-why-and-how/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox/better-regulation-toolbox_en\r
\r
Law-making process: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/law/law-making-process_en\r
\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b9d110b-4662-413a-8a6f-ca6919b0acd3 .

