camssa:8524138f-40d7-4d05-887b-0dba77f8393f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is to support the exchange of information between organisations that define criteria and organisations that respond to these criteria by means of evidences.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02ed240f-6d7e-4f3f-b1e9-4a5afdf700aa .

camssa:852aca82-0eca-4ff3-8918-030c516ad5a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SMTP is widely used and implemented in the context of email services, therefore, this fact demonstrates the market acceptance of the specification. Moreover, there are several implementations of the specifications that support the market acceptance of SMTP.\r
\r
SMTP Transactional Email Solutions 2020:\r
https://formedbythemosthigh.com/2020/01/27/email-verification-25/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9374b335-336c-447a-946e-6801b7f72985 .

camssa:85311292-63d2-4ce8-9a41-1cad108c09e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:853d8c56-744d-4337-bfa5-972029804a62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the Core Location Vocabulary is to create a reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics related to people, locations and businesses. By providing a set of information to describe data in the sectors mentioned before, it helps public administrations to save and comprehend in an orderly and standardized way, information related to people, locations or business.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a3d4d34-5d8f-44fc-8ca4-50807bbc7c83 .

camssa:853e93fd-174a-4a22-a912-b29b079dde4a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any platform to test conformance to ETSI TS 119 512, nonetheless, the specification lists a set of requirements needed to comply with in order to be conformant can be checked manually wether or not applied. \r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:08452e4a-76ea-4863-8a17-0e1c35101c19 .

camssa:853e9a72-135a-435c-b55e-05ba198459d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, TLS 1.2 is  a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. TLS 1.2 is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:752c4b17-82a5-485e-82d3-0a9120d38a65 .

camssa:8541a775-8937-452b-82ca-7d0f6b9104af a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"OData follows REST principles and there exists some kind of data access. It is up to the stakeholders to define if the diferent API's are secure via the suggested tools (RFC 7617).

OData on authenticathion:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#sec_Authentication

RFC 7617 reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7617

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:45020c93-a41a-4186-8d27-ed0c3257dd30 .

camssa:85423993-a994-48a9-b825-3d48f1f23668 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAML 2.0 is a format that allows seamless cross-border interoperability between systems, regardless of its implementation.\r
\r
The specification allows cross-domain single sign-on, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. As well, providing authentication across sectors and platforms allows administrations and stakeholders to exchange and reuse data fostering the data portability across borders. \r
\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1ca1d34-8214-4f2b-a6ca-97bf3a569f8d .

camssa:85425d77-a8a6-4940-aaae-2314e3090a8e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Domibus facilitates the exchange of electronic messages and documents between different entities, such as government agencies, organizations, and partners. Its primary purpose is to ensure the secure, reliable, and standardized transmission of data while adhering to relevant standards like the AS4 profile of the ebMS standard.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:522a54a0-7275-4fbd-a740-b5bcaf94bff8 .

camssa:8548e89a-13f7-43e6-b681-9dbff01854bd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:854b8ed6-648f-4720-a48c-21c61182a076 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME itself is not directly related to the enabling of exposure of interfaces, nonetheless, it can indirectly contribute to such purposes by promoting content negotiation and define data exchange formats. \r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca4b1923-b68f-4e4a-8811-7489a34ecfb6 .

camssa:854c7894-bbee-4e31-8bc4-95f3d1e9f3c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"LDES has been recommended by the Spanish government through their open data initiative webpage. The government's blog explains how LDES can help overcoming data publishing challenges.

Overcoming Data Publishing Challenges with Linked Data Event Streams (LDES): https://datos.gob.es/en/blog/overcoming-data-publishing-challenges-linked-data-event-streams-ldes\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c637dc86-5b0f-4ac1-81a1-48650e3a3d2d .

camssa:854d3295-96b5-407f-9ba8-2318bf0c6bca a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/5e8e7c58-0271-49ed-89b6-6af814615c45"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:85517f40-6feb-4365-94fe-d72cb4d8a489 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records. Therefore, e-Delivery SMP 1.10 is not fostering the long-term preservation of electronic resources. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1535570-eaa5-487d-93be-fb5ce341ccac .

camssa:8558fa58-ae2f-41a5-a568-047f0be4410a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are already existing documents and studies assessing the JSON's features and performance. In some cases, the study has been carried out in a comprehensive comparison between XML and JSON. \r
See: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Hanif_Ullah/publication/321361853_Behavior_based_Comparative_analysis_of_XML_and_JSON_web_technologies/links/5a1eb56f0f7e9b9d5e000bfd/Behavior-based-Comparative-analysis-of-XML-and-JSON-web-technologies.pdf \r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Kamir_Yusof/publication/320045078_Efficiency_of_JSON_for_data_retrieval_in_big_data/links/5a3f14ea458515f6b0456f54/Efficiency-of-JSON-for-data-retrieval-in-big-data.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b72ff49-fbc2-40c8-912e-7523594739bc .

camssa:855a40c1-f0a9-4278-ac25-25c8e075416d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'All solutions developed in ISA² Programme are under ISA Open Metadata Licence which is perpetual, royalty-free and non-exclusive license to Use and re-Use the Works.\r
\r
ISA open metadata license:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/licence/isa-open-metadata-licence-v11'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79255f74-1255-46d7-b320-c9e59e1eeac2 .

camssa:856313e1-30d0-4bfa-b5e3-3cf28fe8b435 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:85633070-4160-4e10-91f3-35f32eeb5a44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence that the GITB TDL encourages the creation of communities along with the sharing of their data and results on national platforms.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6ea3bea-fe69-43fd-8ef2-5182e0b56790 .

camssa:85696d28-6787-4aef-b8c9-8a9976e48ddf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing assessments assessing the efficiency and effectiveness of the ISO/IEC 27001. An example of such assessment can be viewed on the following link.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 27001 assessment:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/286651142_Evaluating_the_Effectiveness_of_ISO_27001_2013_Based_on_Annex_A'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:993fb8e5-7813-4483-8133-1554b3297093 .

camssa:8569befa-0119-44ee-a04b-1622cd66e699 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the ETSI TS 119 612 specification does not provide information about if it can be partial implemented, it specifies some mechanisms which can be implemented incrementally or separately. There are some attributes that must be implemented, but other are optional. 

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f6521da-6aa5-4034-b7b2-9ad69c24db42 .

camssa:856a5bab-0e7e-4dc6-a1d1-0b2f03b93b66 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The use of SAML 2.0 has been agreed for the eiDAS technical subgroup to use the specification on the eiD Building Block to support eiDAS regulation. The regulation 910/2014 is a document that implies all the Member States and their responsibilities as public services providers. Therefore, the agreement for using SAML 2.0 as part of the eiD Building to support eiDAS regulation can be understood as an agreement involving public services providers. \r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/futurium/en/content/eidas-regulation-regulation-eu-ndeg9102014"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dca07201-45a2-4737-8f76-2ddd06c7fb9d .

