camssa:85cc8b4b-928e-4265-b119-3db1b0f47c7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Valid PROV documents have to satisfy certain definitions, inferences, and constraints, and are specified in PROV-CONSTRAINTS document. Moreover, there can be found automated ways of testing PROV conformance, such as the PROV validator, a tool that validates PROV representations or translate them into other representations. \r
\r
PROV-CONSTRAINTS:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-constraints-20130430/\r
\r
ProvValidator:\r
https://openprovenance.org/services/view/validator'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:070978ef-079b-4fd9-92a4-52f8aad1c73d .

camssa:85cfc343-58f6-41bb-96b4-dede9aadf1c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML can be used with kubernetes. Kubernetes objects are intention registries that can be found inside Kubernetes system. These objects are useful to represent the state of a cluster. More specifically, kubernetes objects can describe which applications work in containers, the resources available for these applications, and how these aplications behave, in relation to reboot and update policies.

Kubernetes reference:
https://kubernetes.io/es/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/kubernetes-objects/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:698b99b7-af7f-4ae4-861f-c82c26b27487 .

