camssa:8690b6d0-01b8-4182-8ab3-1f617f729b3b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is a versatile logging protocol that allows for the comprehensive capture of administrative procedures, 
rules data, and services within a networked environment if combined with other specifications. This specification scopes comprehensibility by allowing standard user authentication and authorization, configuration changes, firewall and security rules, Intrusion Detection/Prevention Systems (IDS/IPS), network services, etc. Although it does not directly manage administrative procedures, it does provide the necessary data for these tasks.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46e31766-eadd-45ec-98ec-9a062574aef2 .

