camssa:8707da94-ddcd-439a-8e0d-8892ee0bc8af a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SHACL is not related to enable the secure exchange of data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a46f18b6-ce41-4158-873a-97c90d4ca76f .

camssa:8708e325-7681-4f77-8b51-2247ed5c50ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Transparency of the development process is evidenced by a defined and publicly available documentation on the development and maintenance of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9c32aaa-c451-4420-a377-d60e601ea305 .

camssa:87098582-a3e4-469f-aec8-67d5816dcec7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, FTPS is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore, FTPS is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b192319-ce3d-4996-aaad-803c859560b6 .

camssa:870ce4cd-6970-4cc8-aa88-147ed83a8b42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Better Regulation Toolbox is a public asset developed by a European Institution and can be accessed and reused without any payment conditions. Therefore, it can be considered that the specifications is licensed under royalty-free basis and (F)RAND basis. \r
\r
Better Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0674588-70d4-4368-bb5e-318153853036 .

camssa:870fe4e9-3750-4631-ae0b-f03ec868d4c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CSV is included in 12 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to the Netherlands, Estonia, Sweden and Spain, among others. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 2 out of 3 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO)factsheets.\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards   '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:073997b4-e702-45c7-aff8-d4cfa5cc8155 .

camssa:87180812-d57a-4bd0-9451-ffbf5f1a199a a cav:Score,
