camssa:871adb91-c6cd-49c7-9ede-db27c0bdcf72 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of OWL2 is to allow accessing, importing, sharing, and reusing public ontologies. The data described by an ontology in the OWL family is interpreted as a set of "individuals" and a set of "property assertions" which relate these individuals to each other. So it helps administrations to infer knowledge over other administrations and stakeholders' data. It also happens in a bidirectional way, easing the visibility and the relationship between the data and datasets of the administrations. Moreover, it makes data reusable and visible, enhances, and fosters the decision-making process._x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
OWL2 W3C reference:_x000D_\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b3e1124-b864-4497-ace4-c9bd59adb713 .

camssa:8724019e-037f-4455-aa1e-bfa401c87f6c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:8725717c-c9fa-4068-aa5a-619a130ef582 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:872e3209-9234-435e-a889-7b5982890414 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Secure processing of data can be provided by DNS adding the DNS Security Extensions (DNSSEC), which is, in fact, almost a mandatory extension between major stakeholders.  Processing of data is secured by the encrytion under which the domain is protected provided by DNSSEC or other extensions addressing security issues. \r
\r
Resource Records for the DNS Security Extensions:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4034\r
\r
 Extension Mechanisms for DNS:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6891\r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc1034.txt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bf980ab-be9f-4713-af1b-ecfb02c777af .

camssa:873271b8-d23f-4c10-a827-1324d414a001 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT includes features that allow extension by implementers or users, designed to maintain interoperability (see Section 2.9).

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30/#extensibility'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ef4efac-dc26-4d58-bbd6-aebb7054bd61 .

camssa:873785d5-4f04-430e-aa26-b701944fae2b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:873849eb-842c-48bf-b0a3-ce96444a22be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no conformity test coming from the IETF, but there are existing free online documents that will help you validate LDAP specification when it is implemented. However, it is a manual process that does not provide 100% automatic validation.

IBM testing LDAP authentication settings:
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/SSZQFR_2.2.5/doc/iwd/ldap_test_settings.html

Test LDAP configurations:
https://docs.microfocus.com/itom/Operations_Orchestration:10.80/Develop/Working_with_API
/Testing_LDAP_Configurations

LDAP Tools:
https://ldap.com/ldap-tools/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3099cd34-7c86-493d-a0e0-5ca836da1805 .

