camssa:88abf999-7970-4da7-b13c-ae87d0e39c0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI specification allows for extensions. The ELI Task Force is responsible for proposing updates to the
ELI specifications. They also provide resources like the ELI annotation tool and the ELI validator to assist in
the implementation and validation of ELI metadata.

ELI governance reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/governance_rules.pdf

ELI annitation and validator tool:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/resources.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a24540b7-5ab1-4f03-9089-d5bea59d307b .

camssa:88afb0ea-0b1e-4595-b606-7861a7d29514 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is recommended by the Netherlands according to the CAMSS List of Standards, which means that this specification is included in their national catalogue of standards.

Netherlands Standardisation Forum: https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/aanbevolen
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7514bb9b-2440-4cd3-989e-99a6cadd282a .

camssa:88b08e28-e82c-4ac2-95a5-6dfe51371da8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The AKN4EU specification itself does not provide specific mechanisms for the secure processing of data. However, it can be used as part of an overall approach to enable secure data processing.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d09a41d-658b-4228-b445-819e00e7a5de .

camssa:88b38902-f934-4490-a67a-60fb8f168bef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 specification simplifies the delivery of European public services by enhancing both the security and speed of online connections. The 0-RTT feature, which allows for faster reconnections and minimises delays, directly contributes to a more efficient user experience. Moreover, TLS 1.3 emphasis on security ensures that sensitive public service data remains protected. 

TLS 1.3 Major Differences from TLS 1.2  Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-1.2'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4d7dcbe-1e2f-4a0e-a8a4-7704e992b3f8 .

camssa:88b42083-d04c-4ade-a026-d0c6dc3cdb40 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS is an RDF vocabulary for representing concepts of a repository, intended to facilitate the co-operation. By describing the assets, releases, and distributions of a repository, it fosters the publications of data and its discoverability. _x000D_In fact, ADMS is the basis for the ADMS-AP used in Joinup to describe the different reusable solutions and make them better discoverable and reusable across borders. _x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
ADMS in Joinup:_x000D_\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/adms"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e37dae31-4c81-4ca3-8aa8-69b925e2afe4 .

