camssa:89881c0b-0e4e-46ef-84bb-f794c14dc1ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The DCAT vocabulary has a strong support from the interest groups and is extensively used by public administrations’ for the exchange of data across borders and sectors.\r
\r
Additionally, the specification is widely used by public administrations profiling or extending it to fit domain-specific or national requirements\r
- DCAT-AP: Application Profile for Public Sector Datasets.\r
- DCAT-AP-BE: Extension of DCAT-AP for Belgium specific requirements.\r
- StatDCAT-AP: Extension of DCAT-AP for the publication of statistical data.\r
\r
See DCAT Implementations: \r
https://www.w3.org/2011/gld/wiki/DCAT_Implementations """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43283e6c-27e0-498d-8ffd-7b3065dc05ce .

camssa:89893832-dc00-4672-8580-19489d4dcece a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has been found some studies assessing the effectiveness of PROV. Between some of the studies, we can find one assessing the effectiveness of PROV when applied to signatures and validation methods. More assessment samples can be found below.\r
\r
Measuring PROV provenance on the web of data:\r
http://provenanceweek.org/2016/p3yl/papers/paper_89.pdf\r
\r
The rationale of PROV:\r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1570826815000177\r
\r
A Canonical Form for PROV Documents and Its Application to Equality, Signature, and Validation:\r
https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3032990'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:885a0c89-cf97-45f1-8639-37b2d09a2b3f .

