camssa:89b4930c-c5bd-490e-8c55-06accf664ba0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The main purpose of HTTP Cookies is to track and store user's data on the webpage, and to use this data to remember the user's preferences (such as language, name, etc) for a certain period of time, so that you don't have to re-enter them when browsing around the site during the same visit. For that matter, HTTP Cookies, to some degree, enables the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#creating_cookies\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a19645b-89d9-45d2-8e1d-f70f15c8d5a9 .

camssa:89b619a7-7086-4eca-a284-c18f9e133042 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'COMMISSION IMPLEMENTING DECISION (EU) 2016/120: "The XBRL 2.1 should therefore be identified as\r
ICT technical specification eligible for referencing in public procurement," and " The eXtensible Business\r
Reporting Language version 2.1 is eligible for referencing in public procurement." XBRL GL is a taxonomy\r
based on xbrl.\r
\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?toc=OJ%3AL%3A2016%3A023%3ATOC&uri=uriserv%3AOJ.L_.2016.023.01.0077.01.ENG\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:039cff7c-5d5f-4d66-8b01-53a9d50d18d9 .

camssa:89bfb771-76df-4e93-a354-453d6466bb5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XAdES is within the European eIDAS regulation which is legally binding for all EU members states."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:701fcbfa-24b3-45f4-b42c-2fc269c9b031 .

camssa:89bfecf3-ca34-4aaa-aa59-3ee08562a112 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODF is included in 4 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Denmark, Estonia, the Netherlands and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
 \r
CAMSS List of standards: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards \r
 \r
National Interoperability Framework Observatory:  \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff57578b-935f-4e9e-9131-931b7310af52 .

camssa:89c193c3-33ab-4d98-b413-83c89ed6b8ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TIFF/IT is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Estonia and Spain.\r
The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
\r
National catalogue Estonia: \r
https://www.mkm.ee/sites/default/files/interoperability-framework_2011.doc\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a7348ac-1172-47a6-a6ca-1ea587608906 .

