camssa:8a68fb85-7d16-4b26-bac6-b0369e513917 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTTPS is an internet protocol for the data exchange over an Internet network. It supports the first level of maturity defined in the Tim Berners-Lee´s  5 stars Open Data deployment scheme, "Make your data accessible on the web". \r
\r
See: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/     """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58b5081c-a705-4e76-a7b7-3d2700f5e205 .

camssa:8a6c1949-129c-4ede-bab2-1cd296393a79 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification demonstrates technology-agnostic characteristics as it is designed to function independently of specific technologies, ensuring reliable information exchange between parties across diverse systems.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51f8f3de-5801-478b-8cff-8368012dd133 .

camssa:8a6d538f-18bd-4469-be8f-08cf845baf6c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:8a6e6cac-932c-4b18-a39c-8c918f2e5e08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DQV provides a standardised vocabulary for describing data quality information, including dimensions, metrics, indicators, and constraints. By adopting DQV, organisations can ensure consistency and interoperability in how data quality is represented and communicated. This standardised approach enables the reuse of quality-related information across different datasets, systems, and applications.

Data Quality Vocabulary: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:430befda-902d-4c27-9038-e5fa924b8a8a .

camssa:8a725ea1-e5fe-4867-bc59-e6c6d48a0244 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 specification does allow for partial implementation to a certain extent. It defines a core set of features that must be supported by all conforming SOAP implementations. These core features include the SOAP envelope structure, the processing model, and the SOAP encoding rules. It also defines additional capabilities that a SOAP node may support, such as message transmission optimization, reliable messaging, or security features. SOAP modules, on the other hand, define sets of related features that can be grouped together.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/   '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1b83d03-beba-46dd-816f-4a4aa5cb2422 .

camssa:8a78edcb-4586-4025-bb87-5f40193b4904 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Core Location Vocabulary has a good market acceptance for its use in the development of products and services. For example, it has been used to create the OSLO Vocabulary which is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of information exchanged by public administration in Flanders.\r
\r
OSLO Vocabulary:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/oslo-open-standards-local-administrations-flanders/solution/oslo-open-standards-linked-administrations-flanders/about\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1c6a4f38-3309-4de7-9ae7-0531fb6c71af .

camssa:8a7c5fc8-e3d1-4b31-9920-f3e0cb1c8f4d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS does not define a cross-sector reusable data model, but defines a network protocol for exchange data.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6faaea33-e949-4f0c-bb44-579d401fc197 .

camssa:8a833d82-ae0d-4781-8408-979854c65fa6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The CPOV eases the description and publication of datasets including information of different public organisations, their services and responsibilities. These descriptions are done using human and redeable formats which ease the reusability and the information exchange across-borders. \r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fafceec8-1481-41ec-a390-f51c4cf89368 .

camssa:8a870263-3e46-4bc9-ac72-ee3ccb1dcec9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Core Public Organisation Vocabulary facilitates the information sharing. The trustworthy data depends on the publisher, but Public administrations can complement CPOV with other specifications added to ensure secure data exchange.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2ff4ed36-7ca0-4956-88cd-f1b2a8eb1243 .

camssa:8a882dcf-e0ae-4ddf-99ba-e70e2d3e623c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8a8aa0db-bfae-4765-93da-994403fd6a54 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8a8ac51d-cc96-4b43-bc9f-90caf2c57219 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As one of the official European Standardisation Organisation, ETSI develops standards that are compliant with the European Standardisation Regulation 1025/2012  . \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/about/etsi-in-europe """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c00ca630-2286-4407-a4f2-23bf9bae8e87 .

camssa:8a8bf4c3-6568-4d55-b93c-0a72c161b485 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SCIM itself is not designed for exposing interfaces to access public administration services, identity management plays a crucial role in various service-oriented systems, including those in public administration. SCIM can be a component of a broader identity and access management (IdAM) strategy within public administration, ensuring efficient and secure management of user identities across different systems.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5108358-002b-4401-8b97-e38ba03aa645 .

camssa:8a8db390-6825-41af-b3cb-94822ec3638a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SOAP 1.2 is a messaging protocol for exchanging information in a structured way, it provides endpoints that foster the availability of interfaces containing data from internal information systems of a public administration.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSAW57_8.5.5/com.ibm.websphere.nd.multiplatform.doc/ae/cwbs_soapverdiffs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6742c99f-5340-4d70-9d4f-9267a6c77d3e .

camssa:8a902fad-8721-42a3-b385-6700fdb76204 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of RDF is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0225de24-2ec3-482b-9b86-7d9a946615f1 .

camssa:8a92f401-39ea-49e3-bc9e-f97701a5b8f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be4a099e-ce80-43e8-9cfa-f48d28fb9ef9 .

camssa:8a93e870-bd3f-4fa5-8aa0-d7ef719a0eaf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML is not specifically designed for the long-term preservation of data, information, or electronic records. One of its functions is to transmit and store data in a human-readable and easy-to-write format. However, organizations can leverage YAML in conjunction with other practices to contribute to the long-term preservation of relevant information. For example, it is possible to store and transmit python objects using YAML format.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/

Pythonforbeginners reference:
https://www.pythonforbeginners.com/basics/convert-python-dictionary-to-yaml#htoc-what-is-the-yaml-format'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59117ba6-52ce-4295-88d2-c0d950d3f807 .

camssa:8a94ad5b-fe4c-40c6-9678-6e46dcb7b646 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There can be found many assessments that confirm the usefulness of the OAS.  In terms of effectiveness, there are articles analysing OAS for security design issues, or others that prove the effectiveness of the automatic generation of test cases for REST APIs using OAS.\r
\r
Analyzing OpenAPI Specifications for Security Design Issues:\r
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/9652639\r
\r
Automatic Generation of Test Cases for REST APIs: A Specification-Based Approach:\r
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8536162\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b7d8f8b-6f52-40c4-995c-d1709bdd752c .

camssa:8a9525bc-4efb-4dd2-99fc-52eb90e237e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fef5941bab92019b7692f8544de94715a42ed9ff76d89cbec4fb6f9821611925 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:8a959296-2a3d-4429-bce9-8feed3329f92 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary facilitates information sharing between governments, businesses, and citizens. The CPOV contributes to the managment of cross-border repositories of public services and organisations. So, it fosters data portability between systems and applications supporting the implementation and evolution of European public services.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b2e5e07-880b-47f3-9f65-6401ae48740e .

camssa:8a96b40d-096f-4f7b-b472-415784fe46e6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8a9f7abe-8dc6-4846-b055-1e034f258ab6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:8aa1128c-290a-4ad4-9906-b75eb21fcd22 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDA specification and recommendation processes are open from inception. Individual membership to RDA is free and open to all, as long as individuals subscribe to the RDA Guiding Principles (https://rd-alliance.org/about/get-involved.html):\r
• Openness – Membership is open to all interested individuals who subscribe to the RDA’s Guiding Principles. RDA community meetings and processes are open, and the deliverables of RDA Working Groups will be publicly disseminated.\r
• Consensus – The RDA moves forward by achieving consensus among its membership. RDA processes and procedures include appropriate mechanisms to resolve conflicts.\r
• Balance – The RDA seeks to promote balanced representation of its membership and stakeholder communities.\r
• Harmonization – The RDA works to achieve harmonization across data standards, policies, technologies, infrastructure, and communities.\r
• Community-driven – The RDA is a public, community-driven body constituted of volunteer members and organizations, supported by the RDA Secretariat.\r
• Non-profit - RDA does not promote, endorse, or sell commercial products, technologies, or services.\r
\r
Organisations may join RDA as members for an annual fee. Full details are provided at https://rd-alliance.org/organisation/rda-organisation-affiliate-members/rda-organisational-membership.html\r
\r
RDA Specifications, upon delivery, are assessed by the RDA Technical Advisory Board (TAB) and feedback / comments are given. All outputs go through an open and transparent Request for Comments process of 1 month on the RDA web platform. Details on the process are available at - https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/creating-and-managing-rda-groups/working-group-outputs.html\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de2ec5f9-3654-4e52-b940-297bcfa3fc1a .

camssa:8aa25901-9980-419d-9c37-631491aed039 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8ab35efc-359e-4908-97df-47595f7d6c62 a cav:Score,
