camssa:8b4af4cb-36cc-4d41-8fa5-c25c43b2b414 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is part of the Electronic Signatures Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications. The ESI dates back to 2012, when the  General Policy Requirements for Trust Service Providers supporting Electronic Signatures (ETSI EN 319 401) specification was first issued.  Since its first publication, there have been many extensions one of which is ETSI TS 119 612, whose version 2.2.1 was released in 2016 when the eIDAS regulation identified the need to create protocols to develop preservation services for trust service providers,  as mentioned in ETSI SR 019 510.\r
\r
ESI specification history:\r
https://standards.globalspec.com/std/14387016/EN%20319%20401\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 401 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI SR 019 510 specification reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_sr/019500_019599/019510/01.01.01_60/sr_019510v010101p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:115b4c27-af7c-4069-8d36-0651415252bc .

camssa:8b4c4839-f42a-4f67-8eb5-6c03ee0bc479 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:8b502290-a2e4-49b4-baf9-83428342b79d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6e48368-2b09-4bb8-afb9-0fdff68cf8ab .

camssa:8b5650be-c9f9-4525-9288-c8139214aa9d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 is widely accepted and used globally across various industries. It ensures interoperability among different vendors’ equipment, crucial for seamless technology integration. Ongoing reports and projects highlight its future-proof nature and continuous evolution.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reports and Projects:
https://mentor.ieee.org/802-ec/dcn/24/ec-24-0045-00-00EC-ieee-802-3-ethernet-working-group-march-2024-closing-report.pdf

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:135122d7-0dfe-4fa6-9b44-957902c3a309 .

camssa:8b581b0a-b867-4806-b901-8e9391b3b5da a owl:NamedIndividual,
