camssa:8b5d14d3-5c53-442b-b4a3-86bc0bd3f74e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although it is mostly suited for public administrations, ETSI TS 119 512 protocols can be used in any business domain. For example, the specification uses different preservation schemes that build the so called preservation profiles (see eIDAS reference).\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c341b34-cad4-4344-85aa-515d60e07ce6 .

camssa:8b604596-84a1-4791-a088-919e7a565c27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"NUTS was originally created to be used in a statistical environment and its field of application is not expected to change in the short term. However, NUTS could be used 'as-is' to other domains, in the sense that territorial divisions are also interesting in other statistical research areas like tourism (see NUTS tourism-application reference), and not only limited to the fields of policy and demography.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics\r
\r
NUTS tourism-application reference:\r
https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1177/0047287520979673\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71cf31da-216d-4bb6-91f3-c89c1d655d05 .

camssa:8b6211f7-564e-4e17-a997-29080b7e8a59 a cav:Score,
