        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8b856bb1-013a-4e66-b68e-b073a60100b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the SCIM (System for Cross-domain Identity Management) specification is typically assessed based on its adoption, implementation, and how well it meets the identity management needs of organizations. For instance, a 2023 paper by the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineering (IEEE) highlights how SCIM is a relevant industry standard for Identity and Access Management (IdAM) and how Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) can fix some some opening points encountered in SCIM implementations.

SCIM: Survey and Enhancement With RBAC: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/10214272'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1eeec212-aa42-44f6-b4f6-a5f2d405e7bd .

camssa:8b88d07c-1e0b-4716-9b88-6196c058240e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e46f1a4a060cc7e143e32e4833c94af9164c37bc0d4c844bd1fa974ffb2ac225 ;
    cav:value "100" .

