        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8b93664d-7843-46ec-bf98-9d3c26267c0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ebXML is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Germany and \r
Norway. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States varies when aligned with the \r
European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. While Norway performs well above the EU average, Germany shows an imbalanced level of implementation of the EIF Principles due the absence of data on this respect.\r
\r
Catalogue reference Germany:\r
https://www.cio.bund.de/Web/DE/Architekturen-und-Standards/SAGA/SAGA%205-aktuelle%20Version\r
/saga_5_aktuelle_version_node.html \r
\r
Catalogue reference Norway:\r
https://www.difi.no/fagomrader-og-tjenester/digitalisering-og-samordning/standarder\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-\r
administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01cbc553-5d58-4235-92f7-e5bc7205fe2b .

camssa:8b967577-7750-4cc5-af77-f40bf2cccf31 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b8f7f5098ef900044e245ff5b30832215e00204b1e244545d80a28013685c811 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:8b986719-455a-49b9-a068-fdeec6217f04 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8b9ac412-c4e0-407a-8924-f7f1c59ea7d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "As XML is used to encode all communications all over the internet, XSD fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of administrations by providing validation of exchanged data."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:405c3bcc-382d-461e-a94d-c5f72fbbf51e .

camssa:8ba78070-c141-4b10-a3e9-270991065923 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of XAdES as an electronic signature format helps citizens, business and administrations to secure documents. So it does not hamper the scalability of systems.\r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed72e84e-cd2f-410d-a6dc-ef653227ea5b .

camssa:8baf3b37-74dd-40fc-aa4b-7b0b4076c73d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP is maintained and developed by IETF which is an international community developing open \r
standards. In addition, the OpenLDAP Foundation is another community centered around the distribution \r
and maintenance of the open source version of the specification.\r
\r
Developer community IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/about/\r
\r
OpenLDAP website:\r
https://www.openldap.org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87bae9cd-4472-4d5e-b5e7-98b90349f6b6 .

camssa:8bb07323-4f02-405f-b556-13fec52a4a6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT, as a data vocabulary, can be used for large amounts of data and does not hamper the scalability of systems using it.  It is evidenced by the several implementations at the national or European level.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/2011/gld/wiki/DCAT_Implementations"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2b3fb00-ab39-426c-ad39-1ddf96c1aa24 .

camssa:8bb168e4-1a2b-437a-951a-856af88e83cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "ASiC Baseline profile is a specification that defines a set of features needed for the successful creation of containers containing data and information related to eSignatures. The specification performance is closely related to the different specifications involved in electronic signatures across borders. (E.g. CAdEs Baseline Profile, XAdES Baseline Profile). In the context of the European internal market, it can be considered as an asset for the creation of solutions enhancing the interoperability between administrations and businesses when eSignature is needed. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc133cb6-0796-4984-970b-c5ec3349f55d .

camssa:8bb17e89-779e-47c9-9da4-6ff93571a31f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8bb2e5e5-5b43-4610-868a-4e128b2d4483 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8bbe3839-5ee6-4e80-83dc-edd48c8afe8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is highly adaptable to the business-specific needs, allowing for partial implementations depending on the requirements of any particular context where it is to be applied.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6365265a-f169-473a-be9d-30a2d3b5af6c .

camssa:8bbf7601-e059-479b-b87d-ca815212bfe1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6ec33e201b803a1cc0150c0da8dc42b2a0f1029cf31e7a2c0fc81d1d8336ef36 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8bc395ee-3209-4395-a2e9-60f7d209713a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like other vocabularies, ADMS reuses components from other vocabularies. (e.g. foaf, dcat), and also the resource Description Framework (RDF). This causes a dependency that can hamper the interoperability in those cases where new releases of the reused vocabularies are not backward compatible. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:420892ea-d0b3-496c-820d-46cc9c492e8b .

camssa:8bc3ce9b-e15c-4187-b3f7-52abd2a8f4a8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:8bc9d6c9-9ded-4ab8-83b6-cc22a4167c94 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8bccf7df-1809-4bd9-a0f7-a613ef74b57c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DNS over HTTPS (DoH) protocol itself is language-agnostic, and its functionality is not dependent on the language used for communication. Additionally, the User-Agent and Accept-Language request header fields often convey specific information about the client version or locale but, these aspects are typically addressed at the application layer rather than in the DoH protocol itself.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fd95ff24-fc86-492f-a891-dc1958b1df42 .

camssa:8bcd74b9-adab-4da6-bafc-268d41adee0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL can contribute to managing digital rights in certain contexts, nonetheless, its impact on the \r
simplification of delivering European public services is indirect and dependent on how it is integrated into \r
specific systems and use cases. The broader landscape of standards, regulations, and user experience \r
considerations will also play significant roles in the overall delivery of public services.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a036bba-954b-41a6-9c05-53bc1307b7b1 .

camssa:8bcf700c-e335-48c4-b2c0-f452383747e3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8bd2138f-32de-46d2-95cd-629c34d4f7af a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OCSP is not related to the allowance of extensions.\r
\r
OCSP reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2560'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5251c0af-edde-4231-900a-44c1fc607191 .

camssa:8bd259df-14ce-40a7-afb4-dcbbc91cb52f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the ESPD does not directly ensure or enable data processing accuracy, it includes features that can\r
help to improve the accuracy of the data collected and processed in a public procurement process. The\r
responsibility for ensuring data processing accuracy ultimately rests with the supplier and the contracting\r
authority.  Moreover, the ESPD model provides descriptions and suggests which data is relevant to suppliers of data.\r
\r
Commission Decision (EU, Euratom) 2017/46 of 10 January 2017 on the security of communication and\r
information systems in the European Commission:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1548093747090&uri=CELEX:32017D0046\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c0833c7-5f82-4db7-a51a-0b8e118ea5ef .

camssa:8bd2841e-8406-48ee-ab30-1ce387d54f4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"TLS 1.3 requires the use of symmetric encryption algorithms. These algorithms produce an authentication tag alongside encrypted data, which the receiving peer uses to verify the data's integrity.

TLS 1.3 Record Payload Protection Reference: 
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-5.2\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3893bdab-ab24-421e-bf87-44019e76fb6d .

camssa:8bdf2679-e675-4411-8da1-8e28b02ed0f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ebXML RegRep is data preservation enabler. Specifically, the specification stores and indexes any type of electronic content and preserves it as defined in the ebXML Part 1 on the ebRIM (see ebXML Part 1 reference).\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
ebXML Part 1 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rim-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__39647_1821683062'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1bfbc354-0870-4a1f-a28f-dea7fbe22989 .

camssa:8be15b69-c3e9-4deb-98bb-b8a02632d74f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8bea647c-c14e-400f-b40a-6f615265c07c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a specification that aim to allow and stablish exchange of documents, MIME can be used for the exchange of documents solving administrative burden. Additionally, it can avoid the exchange of non-digital documents that are generally a source of administrative burden.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96ee4a5e-bc90-4088-947e-57591d10b662 .

camssa:8bf0a242-28c6-4651-ae9e-521c27cf6dff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XAdES is not related to the publication of public data as linked open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
\r
XAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/56025.html\r
\r
XAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101900_101999/101903/01.04.02_60/ts_101903v010402p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83cf5a10-3bee-4a93-ad80-ee95c5590c30 .

camssa:8bf3ff2e-13c9-4519-9391-70e517f1554f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ETSI TS 119 432 was part of ENISA's 2018 Trust Services Forum. The European Union Agency for Cybersecurity (ENISA) is the Union's agency dedicated to achieving a high common level of cybersecurity across Europe.ENISA contributes to EU cyber policy, enhances the trustworthiness of ICT products, services and processes with cybersecurity certification schemes, cooperates with Member States and EU bodies, and helps Europe prepare for the cyber challenges of tomorrow.

ENISA ETSI ESI and Signature Validation Services:
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/events/tsforum-caday-2018/presentations/C03_Rock.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b9219eb-9ba0-4c52-ac99-93ecdbc275ae .

camssa:8bf6ab5c-4219-400b-8547-22a3fab42787 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b8f7f5098ef900044e245ff5b30832215e00204b1e244545d80a28013685c811 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:8bfac99f-4a58-4e29-9379-db18c783601c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8bff8c17-09c4-4ab8-8da4-9658b7821223 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c001d6f-f8aa-4955-8ba5-1f5fa67f2621 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The provisions for the use of different languages in the ESPD are described in Article 61 of Directive 2014/24\r
/EU on public procurement. According to this article, contracting authorities must ensure that all procurement related documents, including the tender documents and the contract, are available in the official language(s)\r
of the member state where the procurement is taking place.\r
\r
Directive 2014/24/EU:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:32014L0024\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0766007-0b27-414c-baee-26ac8983b8da .

camssa:8c0027bd-7eb3-4fa1-b479-e5b36615e9f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "ASiC Baseline Profile is a business sector agnostic specification which is reusable beyond the domain for which it was developed. Specifically, it can be implemented whether electronic signatures are needed even it is focused on implementations within the European internal market. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:845de33f-3b9b-43c9-9589-bf1dba54d74e .

camssa:8c0337b3-87a8-48a0-a112-a2c54b94769e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NFVI specification, as a sum of hardware and software components that builds up a virtual environment, reduces the dependency on dedicated infrastructure, and therefore enables for customisation.\r
\r
ISG NFV Deliver, Terminology for main concepts:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/NFV/001_099/003/01.06.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc07a3f8-0297-46fe-a8d6-34a373ec1dd5 .

camssa:8c03ef54-7280-4993-91aa-312da2d266e3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "CSV is one of the most used formats. It can be concluded that accomplishes the user needs. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b28eaeda-74ef-4b18-b2c3-0578cc545464 .

camssa:8c04addb-9c01-4fe6-a7d9-961f9842f5d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is associated with EIRA ABB's in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). \r
More specifically, the specification uses the ABB's "Data Quality Component" and "Data Quality Service".\r
\r
ELIS link:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5357cf46-2bb5-4bb4-b04b-17f26dd4efb1 .

camssa:8c0cecec-7a66-461a-b933-688affa32965 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c0f9187-ceba-40a3-a809-69d971288687 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c10ffb3-6344-4a10-9b7a-aaa00e6c21be a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c11f434-2087-4e2e-92ea-f6c6c8ca5faf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 639-2 is included in 3 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Ireland, Norway and Spain. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States varies when aligned with the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.For both Norway and Spain, interoperability has a high performance in all the interoperability layers. In the case of Ireland, there is a need of improvement in Interopearability Governance, the Legal and Organisational layers. \r
\r
National catalogue Ireland:\r
https://data.gov.ie/pages/opendatatechnicalframework#recommended-standards-for-open-data\r
\r
National catalogue Norway:\r
https://www.digdir.no/samhandling/verktoy-og-ressurser-digitalisering/2150\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16b796bc-f770-4618-b0fc-6870d6e5e5af .

camssa:8c1beb4c-7dce-4152-9a2e-00a856e0bae0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c1de357-54cd-45ac-848e-d5187669cadb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8c2401af-bc7f-4afd-99cb-1991341aa45f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While ISO/IEC 7498:1 may not directly address data protection, the specification can be part of a broader IT infrastructure that, when implemented and managed in accordance with applicable standards and regulations, contributes to a secure and reliable network environment for the handling of personal data by public administrations. 

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e40bfadf-395b-43ff-a183-e04a15d43d24 .

camssa:8c267ce4-886f-4b1e-bcd8-328494a1c365 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'FTP has been widely used for the exchange of data in the past years and has been supported for long time by most of the web browsers. \r
\r
However, there are other FTP alternatives, such as SFTP and HTTPS, that are highly recommended as they are much easier to configure, as well as additional network protocols, such as AS2, that are also potencial replacements of the FTP specification. \r
\r
Five Alternatives to FTP - Secure File Transfers:\r
https://pro2col.com/blog/five-alternatives-to-ftp-secure-file-transfers\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3acde2f-cb89-4e74-a194-7c5609da0375 .

camssa:8c2e2449-ccd5-473e-8898-7a9859a64dd6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS does not directly help with the provision of application programming interfaces (APIs) or Web services. However, the specification allows to provide of a standardised description for assets in a repository. As well, it allows the discoverability of resources from a single access point. An example of this is the European platform, Joinup. \r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d186c392-838b-4efa-9774-fb8f7dd57e1d .

camssa:8c35b288-cc86-4d4e-bdc4-dae9f734294e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c391bac-b87a-4a7e-8ae4-52ca82a093ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTP is developed and maintained by IETF, a widely recognised open international community developing standards to enhance the internet. \r
\r
See: \r
https://www.ietf.org/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50f88c2e-60c9-4289-9631-b71bc4c1c0d0 .

camssa:8c3c04c0-9776-4b8c-86eb-a1b6b322dcf3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c3ebf15-6502-4329-b554-f62a8e4c0e3b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-396b6535162f7bba7733ebcc30d2e467321ce07cd8e48b86ab8201acf27031f9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8c3f01b4-4043-4b45-bd22-715a7d615012 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8c448670-0633-4db5-b9a4-fbad94b323ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can be used as an annex in interoperability agreements.\r
Through the use of XBRL GL Profiles, organisations that wish to interchange data can communicate and\r
agree upon the scope, amount, and restrictions on the data to be interchanged and, where feasible,\r
automate the evaluation of conformation and data quality being exchanged.'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bde5ed07-7e06-41c8-beb7-1b3bb892cd3b .

camssa:8c4f2484-feed-4a91-a956-3405f1717627 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:8c5199b5-647a-4e48-a7e3-4370f672a813 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
