camssa:8cdf0343-5c20-4887-9d5f-10fa70447465 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As defined on the OASIS ebXML Registry Technical Committee (TC), only TC members are involved in the \r
development of the ebXML specification. External contribution to this committee is possible through open \r
channels (see Mail Lists and Comments reference).\r
\r
OASIS ebXML Registry Technical Committee reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/comments/index.php?wg_abbrev=regrep\r
\r
Mail Lists and Comments reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep#feedback'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ec51650-c38b-4dae-aa83-7294cfe6b068 .

camssa:8ce063b6-8049-4aba-9664-38a405b222ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS ensures data portability as it improves identity and access management to IDS. Only the needed attributes can be included in the DAT. This limits information leakage, so only needed attributes are communicated. Furthermore, baseline certificates can be issued to enable connector deployment in uncomplicated manner.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:201d439b-878e-4dfb-a067-63a6f67d9ba2 .

