camssa:8cf84d6c-91b8-410f-87b4-6d22e9adca5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary helps to the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services by providing a structured vocabulary for describing organisations that have gained legal entity status through a formal registration process. Furthermore, the Registered Organization Vocabulary, despite not being maintained anymore, is still used by the Open Standards for Linking Organizations (OSLO), more concrete in the application profile of "Slimme Stadsdistributie". 

In the application profile previously mentioned an example, could be to access mobility permit data exposed by an administration and understand who is the "Registered Organisation" holding the permit is and what its "legal name" is simply by following the definitions provided by the profile and vocabularies thanks to the Registered Organization Vocabulary properties.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

OSLO Smart City Distribution - Application profile Reference:
https://data.vlaanderen.be/doc/applicatieprofiel/slimme-stadsdistributie/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef5b5e53-b7de-4aa6-a678-d2e93317feb9 .

camssa:8cfacba0-383f-4300-bdad-d74cdd4c2a34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There have been found some studies assessing UTF-8 in terms of effectiveness.  For example, ""A case study in SIMD text processing with parallel bit streams: UTF-8 to UTF-16 transcoding"" or a study on the influence of UTF coded data in HDB-3 operation efficiency.\r
\r
A case study in SIMD text processing with parallel bit streams: UTF-8 to UTF-16 transcoding:\r
https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/1345206.1345222\r
\r
Compatibility of UTF-8 Encoding System to HDB-3 Scrambling Method:\r
https://koreascience.kr/article/JAKO201322045164159.page\r
\r
USING UTF-8 TO EXTRACT MAIN CONTENT OF RIGHT TO LEFT\r
LANGUAGE WEB PAGES:\r
https://d1wqtxts1xzle7.cloudfront.net/48691891/Using_UTF-8_to_Extract_Main_Content_of_R20160908-2680-142ekn6-libre.pdf?1473403996=&response-content-disposition=inline%3B+filename%3DUsing_UTF_8_to_Extract_Main_Content_of_R.pdf&Expires=1681810571&Signature=L81oWxuCSbKBEjZutRFI60cE2AZQIrVRvVOOwZRL~RqRBiljibUAzXWYjJ7PhUPmI4FQmeotkmYICafh0fwP8pzSbXoaPjxgXFeiM9OaDqjcQS42K~acPonBHCWwQv~bx3HkpbnBjygdTUyxfLBTuXVsoKy997PH5gxPDklji-c1ML7uiPEkCyeKesaVDaRbxoGOVqoaBAEBhopXSRXx2hV0pREbuIjoUZ2HMB~QYCx8DG7iE1rm1V~nogGMPnZCVzBafoWs2ZbYvyVChU15f0eHI7mXuqwibzLmMAwNGAxRYPr~EQpOsYvEJKBWEN-XPG~PO7iz9njPWt8KqLa5PQ__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAJLOHF5GGSLRBV4ZA"\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4bf1381c-a4b3-4ba4-8728-4ea1bc2a1a71 .

camssa:8d000aaa-3eb5-4aa4-9c69-6b22e7e0dc75 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several conformance validators for ODF, for example, The Document Foundation validator.   \r
 \r
The Document Foundation ODF Validator: \r
https://odfvalidator.org/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d2ff3c2-108b-4540-9166-5bf3a3611467 .

camssa:8d00a23b-797e-4ea8-94bb-afcbcfc9a847 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TSP can be partially implemented depending on specific needs and constraints of a system. It is flexible enough to be used in scenarios where only certain aspects of transaction management require timestamp-based ordering, allowing for tailored applications that address specific concurrency or consistency issues without fully implementing the protocol across all system operations.

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161

Weisser Zwerg implementations reference:
https://weisser-zwerg.dev/posts/trusted_timestamping/#free-implementations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52e2081a-fded-4890-8f7a-cdf16f93c0ad .

camssa:8d074ff6-c64d-4a97-9a45-fa98fd0aa86b a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "None"^^xsd:anyURI .

