    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8d6a2b87-e68e-4730-b37f-ef5babde020f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 specification does not directly address the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge, including electronic records. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

TLS 1.3 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c33995d3-f6a6-4cc1-bd7d-9f5ca5214615 .

camssa:8d6faa13-e7db-4d2a-85d2-346975b20d0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Every new version of the specification goes through a defined process with open and public consultations. Request for comments are not restricted to the RDA members but are open to all."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:206989dc-d508-4ba4-a2ef-434039113a45 .

camssa:8d72a60a-5bdd-4f31-9b57-39a9dc32c43d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is designed to facilitate the secure exchange of identity-related data between identity providers and service providers within an organization. While SCIM itself does not provide encryption or security mechanisms at the protocol level, it leverages underlying security features of the HTTP protocol and can be implemented in a secure manner. 

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f16ae3ac-b58a-4b36-bdfa-d293e1be8187 .

camssa:8d768293-9062-4108-9976-21f621b94692 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI organizes and exposes web service metadata but does not validate its accuracy. Ensuring data correctness in UDDI registries is the responsibility of the service providers who enter the information. UDDI supports service discoverability, not data validation.

Security UDDI reference: 
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was/8.5.5?topic=curs-access-control-uddi-registry-interfaces'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:425f8cef-ac0e-47a1-aeb2-fe6616dff27b .

