camssa:8dbd291b-6b3a-4e20-8ce6-7b89b45efc7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is used to encode all communications between web services. Therefore, it fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of public administrations data and services. \r
\r
See:\r
https://esentool.ted.europa.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53514f2c-5542-43f1-9d58-2479e00bc489 .

camssa:8dc212b5-9ec2-4052-a621-a943188b02a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UTF-8 can facilitate organizational interoperability agreements by enabling the exchange and processing of data in different languages or scripts. It can also help to promote the adoption of international standards or frameworks for interoperability, which can improve the compatibility and interoperability of different systems or organizations.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6d10000-c14c-4455-9ad7-dc1930e2a96e .

