        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-105c699a138c27ab9a1af9174253cd7488b278f700acdbb1bdbcc3e0b9c5ec3d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:8e07d258-184a-4837-891d-6579da704236 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d4ec0fb-4121-421b-9c52-5dfbb962673f .

camssa:8e0f5a30-ef76-46f5-8bc7-bfeda98fefa3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8e113b04-065a-4db8-89e8-c62dc083ab48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of the Indexed Database API is the storage of information. In this context, the specification is ideal for storing information locally and retrieving it when needed. In addition, the specification allows data to be stored permanently and deleted when it is unnecessary or no longer needed.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:251620d2-f868-4849-98ad-c74566699bf9 .

camssa:8e121325-e131-448d-9fc9-1b48d7c2ab02 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RPKI statements are published by network services of the Dutch Ministry of Justice and the Central Government\r
\r
See:\r
\r
https://rpki-validator.ripe.net/announcement-preview?asn=AS29311&prefix=2a04:9a04::%2F32\r
https://rpki-validator.ripe.net/announcement-preview?asn=AS41887&prefix=178.22.80.0%2F21"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10f09ff8-05aa-4aab-822b-7032e552cbee .

camssa:8e13d61d-850f-45c8-bbdb-96ab09b22685 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of NUTS is not related to enabling digital service delivery channels. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5718e24-7849-4633-8e46-54fde2d9a243 .

camssa:8e170a85-c8e0-4fdb-b3dd-c7ea3217c4dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP provides communication between clients and AD, which means it is responsible for transporting highly sensitive information. For that matter LDAP can be developed to meet high performance security standards, including those related to data processing. An example for that could be the layer/transport layer security (SSL/TLS) encryption can add vital protection to information shared through LDAP and enhance the security of organizations’ communication channels. 

LDAP Authentication methods and security mechanisms:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4513.txt
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7160c542-1262-43a1-b639-3e1bb24f4650 .

camssa:8e215ada-0e23-4c52-bfcd-d5eadaf97939 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is involved in the creation of interoperable solutions for data exchange across borders, which aims to evolve public administrations to reduce administrative burdens meanwhile adapt to new ICT needs. CEF’s Building Blocks can be considered as innovative solutions in the field of eAdministrations and eGovernment, therefore, eDelivery SMP 1.10 fosters the creation of innovative solutions. \r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/Background"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3523dcc8-5dbf-4cb8-9965-ba05a20fdf5d .

camssa:8e22cc3d-d1d0-4435-8cf5-a5f044202c67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is part of the Electronic Signatures and Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications and is dependent on some of the protocols and semantics they convey, therefore, this specification is not technology agnostic.  See Annex B for an example.\r
\r
\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification, page 52 Annex B:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a20cf608-7a86-4d7b-a77d-42a0ecbb63fc .

camssa:8e24215d-be6d-471d-abf3-27324b9661e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT supports the evolution of European Public Services by enhancing the searchability and discoverability of datasets across borders. DCAT is an interoperability enabler.\r
 \r
See:                                                                                                                                       https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6bc26ff-cae4-4864-aba4-25df0b7429ef .

camssa:8e2579f0-7e1b-43b5-88e8-607e8d559736 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This Core Vocabulary is included in the Center for transfer of technology (CTT), in the Spanish ICT National Catalogue.          \r
              \r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f924c749-0256-464f-8c65-d8ca1316ee5b .

