camssa:8e330c67-f31a-4113-b0ce-45941f751e7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is designed to provide a standard way to represent legal documents in a machine-readable format. While the specification was initially developed for the legal domain, it is not limited to this domain and can be used in other domains as well.\r
\r
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aca4c293-4cf7-4657-93ab-2e6761d9b8a9 .

camssa:8e33e14c-b837-4024-a27a-f97d7752402b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:8e34c022-4f89-4a73-b758-d2b0bcd7dbe1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:8e486415-5697-453a-b363-1c8dc86e7684 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification does not define a cross-sector reusable data model. EuroVoc is a taxonomy created for helping the data processing across EU Administrations. Its use can be extended to external users and improves the searchability of information, but it is not a data model.\r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7bc66472-22e3-400a-9a2d-4daa73e26dea .

camssa:8e4987fa-7bb6-4a80-8a6d-64cbca69cdad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UTF-8 is included in the catalogue of recommended specifications of 10 Member States.\r
\r
See CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standard"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:baff4307-1417-49b6-9b8c-dab9f96f24ab .

camssa:8e4ee5ab-d5f4-4917-9fed-376cb2b2f118 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:8e4f302c-a9ce-4d2f-8a36-6f7248ac7387 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of UDDI is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

UDDI OASIS reference: 
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/uddi-spec/doc/spec/v3/uddi-v3.0.2-20041019.htm#_Toc85907967'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98583355-62ff-4f0c-ba2b-ee36cf592535 .

camssa:8e500d67-710f-4f34-b918-4f0ae64f93ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Each of the specification approval phases (TAB, Council, Public RfCs / Consultation) allow for objections and appeals.\r
See: \r
https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/creating-and-managing-rda-groups/working-group-outputs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3259e49-a145-4876-a440-816f5e33dc14 .

camssa:8e5835d9-9473-453b-b225-a108b989be05 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:8e59c072-d4e7-4917-90c7-d5e2c248fdbb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 primarily provides a classification scheme for organizing and categorizing data within cloud computing environments, and it does not impose specific technology requirements or prescribe the use of particular technologies.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3378a76e-0876-4891-9075-93327ac38b3f .

camssa:8e5d7ec3-bb2e-4de9-965c-23bd95615126 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:8e5f71ad-226c-4589-a7d1-9ceacb5aac8e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The implementation of SMP can ease the implementation of the Once-Only principle. Since the specification is related to ease the identification of services and the exchange of data, it can be useful for administrations to reuse and exchange information already available reducing the interactions that users need to do with them.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c1a77d1-a244-42c5-bbd1-e78686587a41 .

camssa:8e5fc8b2-cc74-4889-a49f-3152e9060200 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification counts with some major releases, making visible that it has some wide-spread use that indicates market acceptance as they are working towards newer releases of the specification.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:afd0d5b6-69a6-4f76-8d97-166fda0ec7ae .

camssa:8e61fa75-3e01-4236-ad9e-e15e193220a1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8e632778-0e29-488c-85b7-6fcc603dea75 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8e6a4baa-5d0c-4e71-9182-de35227a2db2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
CCCEV reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82634cdb-c359-401e-aa1d-f9baa97b4909 .

camssa:8e6ae39b-d6e4-4472-bd1b-871811481f93 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8e6f115f-a119-4f83-aa05-0571b83faa21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is not focused on enabling e-accessibility as it was designed to make identity management in cloud-based applications and services easier.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:535057b0-4aef-46e0-b63d-de9b005c219b .

camssa:8e6faa57-7cc0-47a4-b423-0c4eaea2d620 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, TSP is  a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. TSP is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50beb420-0b51-4e45-b0a2-32e8b40fb64e .

camssa:8e732f30-4ca7-4e23-bb12-eafa3881899c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of SAREF is often evaluated through various means, including practical implementations and pilot projects. For instance, a 2018-paper by the Ontology Engineering Group from Universidad Politécnica de Madrid asserts that the SAREF ontology represents a reference model for smart appliances, originally focused on the smart home domain and creates an extension for building devices as well as their location, which demonstrates the effectiveness of SAREF.

Extending the SAREF ontology for building devices and topology: 
https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2159/02paper.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37310eb6-6d7f-4710-bfb9-5df170749728 .

