camssa:8e812a67-a5ab-49aa-bba1-ad569896ccf9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OAIS reference model is designed to be a flexible and adaptable framework that can be used to support the long-term preservation and management of digital information in a wide range of contexts, including those that span multiple business domains and industries.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef27e1d9-8db0-4cce-ac15-d921a0ac52ca .

camssa:8e88298c-6633-4fcb-9105-05ca76610117 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"As it happens with all the e-Government Vocabularies, it has the SEMIC action from the ISA2 as responsible for the maintenance of the development. Additionally, there's a post on W3C in open government community group that talks about the specification.

CPOV page on Joinup: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary

CPOV post in W3C:
https://www.w3.org/community/opengov/2016/02/21/core-public-organisation-vocabulary/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1fbf9c2-a551-424a-8c4d-14058ce2ad60 .

