camssa:8ea15f65-4661-4b31-8689-6e5ce1411dc3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI has several authorization methods to protect data and information from unauthorised cahnges. UDDI security API ensure authorization trough authInfo element. Furthermore it is possible ensure authorization trough tModels representing authorization concepts.   

Authorization UDDI reference:
http://www.uddi.org/pubs/uddi_v3.htm#_Ref8981734:~:text=the%20authorization%20policy.-,9.4.9%20Modeling%20Authorization,-A%20policy%20that'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0a38a2be-53a6-4edb-8148-e874d3a5fe5e .

camssa:8ea175d2-86be-4acf-99f4-a93ffd441c82 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the SFIA licensing, public sector organisations can use SFIA on the same terms as the corporate user licence (SFIA reference, Choosing a licence). The SFIA Foundation ensures royalty-free basis under certain use cases, then the specification does not provide a royalty-free licence in most cases.\r
\r
SFIA reference, Choosing a licence:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/licensing-sfia/choosing-a-licence\r
\r
SFIA reference, Corporate user licence:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/licensing-sfia/corporate-user-licence'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6f79126-8e78-4f06-a44c-4ce939cb9062 .

camssa:8ea6a623-ddd2-4cc8-b5f7-22feae1b84a6 a cav:Score,
