camssa:8f35f237-c28c-4c66-adcf-79c6efac5195 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is maintained by the European Commission in an active manner, with teams working specifically on EIRA and related specifications such as eGovERA. This guarantees that the specification evolves as stakeholders and the interoperability environment detect new needs. 

The success stories of the Interoperability Architecture Solutions is a good example of how the Commission supports the evolution of the specification by providing assistance to stakeholders. From the collaborations between the EIRA and Member States, the specification evolves from real needs and expectations on Digital Public Service provision. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA 

Interoperability Architecture Solutions Success Stories: 
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira/success-stories'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c21402a5-fcf3-4bc7-b671-0cafd7ead80b .

camssa:8f372ccd-f1d5-45f2-aa42-995ca93ea704 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPSV-AP is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. So it can be said that the specification is independent of any specific technology or platform.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8308040-4a16-4a1f-85ef-1354694a7d17 .

camssa:8f39e76e-9097-4e04-86bc-bbcf92b8ff21 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:8f45f6eb-47e8-45c4-9943-80ae174b15c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documents that evaluate and document the characteristics of the UDDI and provide possible improvements in its performance, among other aspects.
In "Indexing traditional UDDI for efficient discovery of web services" it is proposed a framework which combine the traditional UDDI with search engines to get a more efficient web services discovery. And in "Binding Now or Binding Later" various "UDDI modes of operation are evaluated using performance tests of the UDDI's implementations", to obtain the most efficient use of UDDI in different cases.

"Indexing traditional UDDI for efficient discovery of web services" reference:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/303921682_INDEXING_TRADITIONAL_UDDI_FOR_EFFICIENT_DISCOVERY_OF_WEB_SERVICES

"Binding Now or Binding Later" reference:
https://www.academia.edu/14435163/Binding_now_or_binding_later_The_performance_of_UDDI_registries'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e324916-2bf0-4fa0-9dd2-94b75ac2bb26 .

