camssa:8fac5367-0870-4772-8c3e-029641b548fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not related to the modelling of organisational interoperability aspects. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b11511d-7012-486f-9ac6-09cc657ac450 .

camssa:8fad55db-922b-458d-9d6a-b5f580f1eccb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'For TLS 1.3 to function correctly, it is essential to include a core set of mandatory components to ensure proper operation and avoid interoperability issues. Specifically, a TLS 1.3 compliant application must implement the TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 cipher suite. While TLS 1.3 allows for extensibility with optional features, omitting these fundamental requirements, including the mandatory cipher suite, can result in a partial implementation likely to encounter client/server connection failures and communication issues with other compliant systems. 

TLS 1.3 Partial implementations Reference :
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-9.1
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:919a153d-4e69-472f-aef2-e5dc4cf82465 .

