camssa:906f9dcc-3ab1-49d2-b300-fd01e4baee30 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF is a business domain agnostic specification that can be used at any business domain requiring RDF features.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4aaffa87-6bc4-492d-ba64-b0708a22069f .

camssa:906fd197-2d11-4bbf-bfd6-d526048aa864 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of IPSec is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:018981fd-a969-4842-9764-c9f15757b282 .

camssa:90714862-7ede-4565-8768-18276082df62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several studies assessing SOAP 1.2 performance and features in terms of efficiency and efficacy. As REST and SOAP-based web services are living together nowadays, one of the topics is the performance comparison. Moreover, the comparison between different SOAP toolkits is an exploited topic. \r
\r
See: \r
https://aaltodoc.aalto.fi/bitstream/handle/123456789/29224/master_Makkonen_Joni_2017.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y \r
https://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=1033266"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:49a225e1-1179-4846-9fd3-2237d52b2bf6 .

camssa:9075c660-47d9-45af-bbee-e5927b2c67ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CCCEV does not enforce the information carried in an Evidence to be directly accessible i.e. contained within the payload of the response.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0b2751c-5062-4022-b0d5-1820e1a569ea .

camssa:907d07a0-b13d-4f80-b1dc-d80ab45a6bb6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of PROV is not related to access control mechanisms. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15c9f44e-e1be-4aa4-8517-dcd0328a3dc3 .

camssa:907f812b-9189-41c7-a6fe-0327189d11fd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6bedf555bffb837990b9eb353447fa116eb9d2384770b1dd3de46d3c5901d4f4 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9086f06d-0330-4608-b70d-be5324fde4aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI EN 319 401 specification, which is complementary to ETSI TS 119 512, defines a mechanism to guarantee the that only authorised persons can make entries and changes to the stored data. Using this mechanism, data changes are limited to those who have permission to do so, therefore, it guarantees data integrity.

ETSI TS 119 512:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.01_60/ts_119512v010101p.pdf

ETSI EN 319 401:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2f7e0dc-eb1b-493a-aa06-3bb8f840e555 .

camssa:908a044d-06a7-49c7-a0fd-4a3f3fe590d2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Extensible Forms Description Language (XFDL) specification plays a role in some niche software, used to create digital signatures or legally binding forms. Although it is used in niche software, it is domain-agnostic and can be implemented in any domain.

XFDL specification domain-agnostic reference:
https://amazingalgorithms.com/definitions/extensible-forms-description-language/

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ca81fb7-e356-42b9-b352-f1c464c7e8a8 .

camssa:908a4c0d-c32a-4627-b6a9-2c42ac45c812 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:908eca68-21bd-4387-af7c-561eabd5781d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:908f9301-4840-491b-af52-4dacfae3e9cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV is one of the most popular formats for publishing data on the web. An example of those developments is CSV Dialect which aims to deal with a reasonably large subset of the features which differ between dialect.\r
Add history, structured data, support from wide range of organisations (private and public)\r
See:\r
https://frictionlessdata.io/specs/csv-dialect/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9a156ea-9ccb-48a7-b323-f9b5a4776cbd .

