camssa:90c442f7-26dc-4925-8f0b-19daac9451a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the moment of performing the assessment, no initiative at national or European level has been found to use ADMS to cover privacy aspects.\r
\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83a12bf8-055d-469d-ade6-94617b2a1bab .

camssa:90c630b0-cf8b-4d76-8b17-9f84de8e04b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV is independent of any specification and can be implemented without any dependency on platforms.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec6424a1-dd68-4d8a-ae35-2d818d1625cf .

camssa:90c96410-e25b-434b-89e2-1a87d2faa3c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although it is mostly suited for public administrations, ETSI TS 119 512 protocols can be used in any business domains.  For example, the specification uses different preservation schemes that build the so-called preservation profiles (see eIDAS reference)\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b9ba3e0-6266-4148-b18c-c34504c07e90 .

camssa:90cf9543-f788-4289-809e-ee3b706ca8e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"DNS is a de-facto standard. It's extensive use as an enabler of the Internet can be summarised by the DNS4EU initiative. 

DNS Domain Names:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499

DNS - implementation and specification:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035

DNS4EU initiative
https://www.joindns4.eu/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc2feab1-4db9-4d03-975f-69fa9330251f .

camssa:90dfbdd2-afb3-4b0e-acf8-620f671ba290 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:90e3749a-4b1c-4733-a9e1-8eca0bef9979 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TrainingDML-AI Standard is primarily design for geospatial machine learning training data. While it facilitates the development and deployment of AI/ML applications within the geospatial realm, it alsoi mprovides valuable guidelines applicable across various industries. These guidelines can enhance data management and AI/ML model development practices beyond the geospatial domain.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ce98cae-9804-4f4a-806d-61767b07a907 .

camssa:90e4365e-5f1f-40e0-93ae-6163a973f235 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Verifiable Credentials is included in the Rolling Plan for ICT standardisation regarding electronic identification and trust services including e-signatures.\r
\r
Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation: https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/electronic-identification-and-trust-services-including-e-signatures'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d1d0b98-f888-45f4-a044-7a2d2e42d103 .

camssa:90e7a275-f9b2-4102-865f-5b963f3f10ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:709e2189-6c57-4d3e-90f1-1c7267d7b166 .

camssa:90eff4e0-9219-4e82-93df-76e1bbd170e3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:90f10f21-2103-4bb9-b8eb-d96ea740ef0b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is domain-agnostic, its main purpose has to do with document exchange and therefore can \r
be used in either public administrations or any other kind of organization.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcb0facf-3ae8-4a2e-acf0-5a6090aaa864 .

camssa:90f2d8a1-88c4-42d7-80fa-ab76729212a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NFV distribution has been included in several European projects. NFV offers virtualised network environments, dynamically configurable and fully automated, that automatically respond to the needs of the traffic and services running on it. This is the reason why the NFVI component has been included in last European projects such as T-NOVA, or in ongoing ones such as the 5G network deployment in the Digital Single Market.\r
\r
NFV reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/technologies/nfv/nfv\r
\r
T-NOVA reference:\r
http://www.t-nova.eu/\r
\r
5G roll plan reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/5g\r
\r
5G NFV whipe paper:\r
http://portal.etsi.org/NFV/NFV_White_Paper_5G.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0601dcea-227c-4caf-b4f5-1d882a9cc4a5 .

camssa:90f3eba0-28b3-40a9-8082-37e23042e825 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:90f4169d-8e43-4d40-9d6b-49b25d29e814 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No member state has been found including the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) in its national catalogue of recommended specifications.

CAMSS list of standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2696ba1-f287-4b18-a617-a540009ceffa .

