camssa:91043daa-fad7-47b6-9da7-76dfe247c925 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OGC TrainingDML-AI is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered
not applicable to this specification.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bf88865-a37d-4e5a-a3af-521557a36e9a .

camssa:910de04e-0176-4c41-832d-e8dccec1969f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSD provides schemas for the validation of XML and the proper data exchange by means of it. Therefore, by ensuring the well formation and validity of the documents being exchanged, XSD fosters the data portability between systems and administrations across borders. \r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:551d64c4-9694-4918-90aa-d31f6c0695c7 .

camssa:910e03d7-bc5a-4de0-a5d6-48e84710755f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:910fa20f-2b58-43ff-90b6-8f6e3778cc58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a document exchange format, SVG is a valuable tool for sharing information through the internet between administrations and stakeholders. Allowing sharing data and information the standard fosters the visibility of administration data and services. Fostering the collaboration between public administrations, the specification eases the decision-making process of institutions.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0ebe7e5-0649-487b-8957-b3a03fdf0cea .

camssa:9110372c-cc39-44cf-a2b3-1f4dad73834c a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "None"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:9111a555-5c09-4485-ac48-c16728099678 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"BFO's aim is to provide a foundation for further developments of ontologies or other external resources. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17f997a4-3ece-4358-aa49-ce2f31120b3a .

camssa:9114018b-e278-481e-9eda-29be7d380807 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing studies assessing the efficiency of DNS. Particularly, there seems to be a general 
interest on the efficiency of DNS security extension mechanisms, and on the DNS Tunneling tools. 

Exploring Domain Name-Based Features on the Effectiveness of DNS Caching: 
https://ccronline.sigcomm.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/p36-hao.pdf 

A Comparative Performance Evaluation of DNS Tunneling Tools:
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Alessio_Merlo/publication/221271469_A_Comparative_Performance_Evaluation_of_DNS_Tunneling_Tools/links/00b4951c1e5065b0e6000000/A-Comparative-Performance-Evaluation-of-DNS-Tunneling-Tools.pdf 

Performance assessment and analysis ofDNS tunneling tools:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235996771_Performance_assessment_and_analysis_of_DNS_tunneling_tools 

A survey of domain name system vulnerabilities and attacks:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/345017736_A_survey_of_domain_name_system_vulnerabilities_and_attacks'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5450ded7-cc15-4493-9f8d-f0350db9b0b4 .

camssa:91193a38-bc15-4820-b61d-a2f0c75aaeee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is part of the Electronic Signatures and Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications, and it is dependent on some of their protocols and semantics they convey; therefore, this specification is not technology agnostic. 

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4943ba5-5f85-4d33-bcf3-fbab204a948e .

camssa:91196b0e-b26b-4feb-ba3c-40bf66c45280 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:911beaa1-e992-4a82-b790-e3eef7b0646d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDF has been selected within several initiatives at European level in order to provide open data and linked data to be used for Member States, citizens, and businesses.\r
\r
An example of RDF use is the European cross-border project ESCO (European Skills, Competences, Qualifications, and Occupations). The project uses Turtle extension of RDF in order to make available the project's data. At ESCO's webpage can be found the link to data resources and as well as information resources needed for the proper use of provided data. \r
\r
Additionally, RDF has been selected as one of the core elements on the euCASES project, a platform for linking legal documentation and offer it as Linked Open Data. \r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/esco/portal/escopedia/RDF\r
http://eucases.eu/start.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea16da44-a814-4fd7-a841-39bde1a28ec0 .

camssa:911f9103-907e-46d3-bcd7-0a973310819a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:912737d2-9c8e-48e1-abca-2e66c4a8918e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is designed to be implemented in any domain, as it can describe any web resource and its not related to any specific domain.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ \r
\r
Dublin Core Application Profile:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/blog/2011/application_profile/\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:978c6f6d-a35c-4780-9295-37fc2e1ed877 .

camssa:912cec29-63d9-4bce-bd40-e105aeb70f2c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:912e13d5-998a-41c4-8b62-b3b18c2b0353 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:913221b2-8065-45c0-8d96-5072c436e4e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 is a component derived from the actions implemented based on the Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market. This regulation aims to enhance interoperability when it comes to the trust services of e-signatures in the European context. 

Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01216882-d3ed-4d69-a398-17c847da63cf .

camssa:9138d392-e21f-43aa-acb8-f9348185c3cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PAdEs and PAdES Baseline profile are included in the ETSI’s catalogue of standards. As ETSI is considered an official standardisation organisation, it can be considered that the specifications are included in a supra-national catalogue. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/103100_103199/103172/02.02.02_60/ts_103172v020202p.pdf\r
https://www.etsi.org/standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:057dfa4d-482d-4256-9cf9-4ab0bfbdb168 .

camssa:9139f0f9-20ff-43a4-ab67-6143caa1fe1b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:30354c43-34fc-4407-beff-c1e4f0245923 .

camssa:914137d8-9728-487b-b61d-6fcb8e73d35f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL International and the community around it provides support for the specification.\r
National XBRL organisations provide support to members.\r
\r
https://www.xbrl.org/guidance/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1dbbfc74-2556-4882-944f-c269b341508a .

camssa:9141b693-fae4-47f8-8d86-b84b7774ee91 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """' No evidence nor disclosures have been found in the specification regarding fostering or harming the long-term preservation of information.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51c1c14d-1f06-4ee5-99b7-92a7accee232 .

camssa:9151a128-eb75-4740-a3d4-1dde94b0770b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No Member State includes ODRL in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/nifo_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ffe9f3d-7af8-423f-b035-c2077e656941 .

camssa:91542bf2-e69a-40b6-90ff-c6c58c7a81bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of CAdES is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:986fda90-22fe-4393-8926-1651d65ff11c .

camssa:915baf10-3078-4bb3-887d-679286bb3262 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Implementation of OAIS can be carried out under any combination of operating system and underlying processor architecture. Therefore, the specification is platform-agnostic.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e6ae39b-d6e4-4472-bd1b-871811481f93 .

camssa:915d8da2-e46c-4dac-92f2-a7d336c075ad a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:91624e65-d42f-444e-b362-92aa79ee6f09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAREF is designed to support the reuse of relevant information when needed. The principle of reuse and alignment of concepts and relationships are embedded in SAREF, contributing to the ability to reuse information effectively across different contexts and applications within the domain of smart appliances and the Internet of Things (IoT).

SAREF: 
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ac193cd-8425-4427-9d71-127be3cbf247 .

camssa:916327f1-f968-486a-bbb0-813c44dd6004 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:9165d2a5-2abf-4813-be4f-b1fe8f95250c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No evidence has been found of the specification being included in an interoperability agreement between organisations involved in the European public services provision. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:388c9633-e8cc-4e94-8ebe-7398ade8cdf9 .

camssa:91664287-caf7-43cb-80cc-5868e285749a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of LegalRuleML is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:889df98f-e118-4f4a-866a-dcca74a1b482 .

camssa:91670493-6ce8-4df1-9f97-61fa9c632131 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The use of genericode, a standardised format for representing code lists and controlled values, can contribute to simplifying the delivery of European public services by  providing a common format for representing code lists, which improves standardisation so that public administrations can establish clear data governance policies and procedures.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2f43c6d-dc8f-42f0-884a-2e3b54c42e56 .

camssa:916a4979-d169-4a17-9a46-af3c0b97faab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org, as a cross-border and cross-sector vocabulary, increases government-to-government reuse of data and therefore can prevent citizens or businesses from providing information multiple times. According to the Publications Office (OP) of the EU, as a mark-up schema, the specification may boost governmental data reuse helping to achieve the once-only principle in future releases of DCAT-AP, once this schema is mapped to schema.org which will result in the Schema.org profile of DCAT-AP (DCAT-AP-SDO).\r
\r
OP reference, 'DCAT-AP standard can become a tool for internal information governance purposes' section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/dcat-ap-key-european-data-publishers-reach-data-consumers-and-create-european-open-data-ecosystem_en\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abeb6cb4-f8e2-4829-a088-9d467295bd50 .

camssa:916a4fe2-83ef-477b-92da-c0f1c260a303 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of LDES is often evaluated through various means, including practical implementations and pilot projects. A 2021-paper for the International Conference on Web Engineering (ICWE) introduces the concept of a Linked Data Event Stream (LDES) for publishing base registries like air quality sensors and observations or a registry of officially registered addresses, which demonstrates the effectiveness of LDES.

Publishing Base Registries as Linked Data Event Streams: 
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-74296-6_3'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c66fdfb-0106-4504-bc51-e02813f4aacc .

camssa:916a61b5-468e-441d-b6ba-e46a6f7f0376 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WSDL helps to make administrations and stakeholders' web services available, with information related to them and endpoints that ease the consumption. This fact supports the reuse of data and web services avoiding administration and stakeholders to carry out unnecessary steps or transactions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d6e8958-e70f-415c-bc23-46f7df23e6b8 .

camssa:916e2b02-1516-4736-9891-381fd1de14db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of RegOrg is to capture the typical details recorded by business registers and thereby facilitate information exchange between them. So it facilitates the visibility of the different legal entities' data, including public administrations.\r
\r
RegOrg about Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee94fbfe-02a9-43ab-adf7-62566af9286f .

camssa:916e70a9-d42a-4fd0-9fce-61ea5782d480 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:9172bbc9-85e6-4779-b4d1-87d185c08f7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WSDL is available for free at W3C's webpage and administrations and organisations are free to use or implement. \r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db1d76d9-8d24-4a41-90fc-77ceb6992709 .

camssa:917a8f02-46e8-4679-b318-3a3be4a6942a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI and any of its committees, in charge of the development of ETSI TS 119 511, operates under the ETSI Intellectual Property Rigths (IPRs) and IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
ETSI ownership of IPRs section:\r
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21e8db83-12cf-450c-a588-ad6172a2de4e .

camssa:917c187b-febb-4ba9-be6c-d1d4613bfc08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP Working Group is part of the OASIS consortium and is responsible for maintaining and evolving the AMQP specification. They provide resources and forums for developers and organizations to collaborate and share their experiences.

AMQP Working Group Reference:
https://www.amqp.org/product/different'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f8a6199-fa34-4851-b847-3559cebf3d0b .

camssa:917c533d-6d28-4d78-a4d1-b40f0b5a942a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is  related to being usable beyond business-specific domains as it can describe any web resource. The specification makes use of extension vocabularies that broaden the field of applicability of the Dublin Core Ontology, also known as DCAM.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ \r
\r
Dublin Core Application Profile:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/blog/2011/application_profile/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:207c4dbf-c433-4452-bb1f-3c04a3689de8 .

camssa:917ebf80-afa4-4518-ad11-449a92e51719 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9188c7d3-004e-44b6-9b6f-69eef666d9f0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:918944c4-aefd-4e2b-b0bc-b8aa2bd83469 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is designed to be flexible, and it does allow for partial implementations. SCIM defines a set of core features, including the ability to create, read, update, and delete user identities and their associated attributes. Additionally, it supports features like filtering, sorting, and pagination for querying user information. However, not all features need to be implemented for a system to claim SCIM compliance.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09691072-9596-47db-a678-53e792b7fcf0 .

camssa:918bbc60-06af-4e8b-bc21-4b578e742dc0 a cav:Score,
