camssa:919b54bb-2657-48f2-9f96-511fb33d202e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The implementation of the specification is still underway in Finland and Estonia.\r
The mandate for the use of XBRL GL by all companies with any significant sales in Turkey is an indication of\r
the impact on ERP developers for those enterprises to implement XBRL GL in their systems.\r
\r
Estonia: https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/CEFDIGITAL/2021/03/22/eInvoicing+helping+standardise+transactional+data+in+Estonia\r
\r
Turkey: https://www.ifrs.org/content/dam/ifrs/publications/jurisdictions/filing-profiles/turkey-18-november-2015.pdf\r
\r
https://www.edefter.gov.tr/edeftermevzuat.html\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ccbacb3f-1045-4169-8b52-62bff446b09e .

camssa:91a6ab79-01c3-4f94-836f-35fbd70b5653 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ELI (European Legislation Identifier) is designed to be platform-agnostic. This means that it is intended to
work independently of specific computing platforms or environments. ELI is formulated to be flexible and
adaptable across various technology platforms, ensuring compatibility and interoperability regardless of the
underlying infrastructure. This platform-agnostic approach enables ELI to be implemented and integrated
into different systems and applications without being constrained by the specifics of a particular platform.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a8e0291-b54e-45fd-815a-a329005ed3f9 .

camssa:91a841b7-0c0c-41c3-a8f1-90938ec67e21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software or platform. The Core Location Vocabulary can be used by any organisation.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7534d0bd-67b3-4294-9829-108c3040c6c5 .

camssa:91b2586c-f254-4b4d-ae47-5c81101574ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML specification itself does not directly provide built-in mechanisms for restricting access to information
or data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c5c6abd1-6522-4232-b903-1beabf0685c4 .

camssa:91b6c100-6c9c-48f6-89b7-4d93ea893204 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main goal of DPV is to develop a taxonomy of privacy terms, which include in particular terms from the new European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in order to ease proof of compliance with the GDPR and related privacy protection regulations.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/

DPV primer document:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0d0797f-a59b-4f7d-ac5f-6e1e4519f31f .

camssa:91b76617-4489-42ee-a21f-4d56ec67f76f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are existing documentation and studies assessing and analysing the performance and effectiveness of IPsec in different contexts and application areas. For instance ENISA provides documentation recommending the use of IPsec in order to improve security.\r
\r
Semantics Scholar, TCP/UDP network performance evaluation of various IPSEC algorithms:\r
https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/8971/9848f632259138d5d4b1052ad24ede803625.pdf \r
\r
ENISA reference, 'Algorithms, Key Sizes and Parameters Report' document:\r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/algorithms-key-sizes-and-parameters-report/at_download/fullReport\r
\r
ResearchGate, 'Interoperability Issues for VPN IPsec Solutions' document:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228437109_Interoperability_Issues_for_VPN_IPsec_Solutions\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc9acc27-0588-482b-af0f-e3643772c300 .

