camssa:92494592-e40a-4c4f-b687-beac505194a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS provides a standardised method for describing assets and their distributions. Therefore, while providing a common way and components for the metadata provision, it helps the comprehensibility of data and services of Public administrations across borders.\r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:793ad464-49f3-403b-b11e-eeb5231e2470 .

camssa:924b16fb-b83d-42b3-94e2-eb7a27d4dd12 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f6edeb9-ef6d-4d89-9e43-9e811fc259b6 .

camssa:924bb41a-f16d-4e70-a429-7b41f0ad640e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A test suite for XSLT, containing over 11,000 test cases, is available. The metadata for each test case describes any dependencies on optional or implementation-defined features of the specification, and provides expected results for each test. 

Test Suite Page:
https://dvcs.w3.org/hg/xslt30-test/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f015aca8-9e55-4515-9097-1c509ec67d19 .

camssa:924fd4de-6482-455f-bf69-f129445f08c3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:92518beb-e742-4bad-a981-419192d5c988 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAREF is designed to be compatible with a multilingual context to some extent. This specification allows the use of labels and annotations for concepts, properties, and individuals. These labels can be provided in multiple languages to support a multilingual environment. Implementers can use language tags or annotations to indicate the language of the labels.

SAREF: 
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02129f4f-91c5-431a-afae-5f22a02ac0ed .

camssa:925637d8-df74-4b0c-b170-27b8abd71145 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2's purpose is to enable Project Managers (PMs) to deliver solutions and benefits to their organisations by effectively managing the entire lifecycle of their project. Besides, since it helps to deliver different solutions, it helps foster to the visibility of administrative data and to support the decision-making process. Therefore, by being involved in the quality assurance of projects and data generated, it can help to enhance the visibility of public data and services, and also helping the decision-making process.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc7a5c46-c036-420c-8346-4924c7e24099 .

camssa:925aefd3-ed1c-4a1a-b316-69b405bfbe89 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData builds incrementally. Customers can easily build a very basic standards-compliant service. Only additional work will be needed to support extra or or add-on capabilities.

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ff96e63-bc09-42bf-91ef-fe0326e7f484 .

camssa:925feb3d-195d-44ed-8be7-e4c88b67289e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "''"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ba8ea55-acae-46b8-9aa1-512c7f775122 .

camssa:9264cba8-b2ca-4c1f-a42f-2ad0382f9301 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Web Services Description Language (WSDL) allows for extension through its extensibility mechanisms. The extensibility features of WSDL enable users to include additional information beyond the core elements defined by the standard. This extensibility is crucial for accommodating specific requirements, custom features, or domain-specific details that may not be covered by the standard WSDL elements.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/#extensions-and-modules'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:311f2b72-3f41-4635-98b1-efc960c88479 .

camssa:92654410-a2d4-4014-b73d-f129fb352714 a cav:Score,
