camssa:92b76547-f2cb-402e-8a0f-4176c5a22979 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of Extensible Forms Description Language is not related to enabling the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:225038d4-a534-49e8-a6ea-edddd151c196 .

camssa:92baff74-7200-4379-ab0f-62f844be951f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData offers a way to both break down data silos and increase the shared value of data. The specification contributes creating an ecosystem where data consumers and producers can interoperate more than ever, allowing more applications to make sense of a broader set of data and eases the delivery of European public services (see the Netherlands Advisory report stating the usability of OData as a solution to streamline the delivery of public services).

Interoperable Europe Portal OASIS Open Data Protocol reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/odp-oasis-open-data-protocol-odata-tc

Netherlands OData Advisory report reference:
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/odata
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:568da6e1-9ed5-4304-921d-cd2348840512 .

camssa:92c1f05d-5c90-4cfd-9a47-b41d1dd2fe76 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ef096f898c938883daab1b22e784cfaf985b5e5c855e170ecf6eab6f37b01b50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:92c48bcc-05a4-45b8-bf40-c9a175fe2a07 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UTF-8 supports many languages and can accommodate pages and forms in different cases including a mixture of these languages. The fact of allowing encoding with several languages allows the data consumption by the different linguistic groups that form the EU. Therefore,  UTF-8 fosters the delivery of European multilingual services.\r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/International/questions/qa-choosing-encodings.en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf5c4b78-0375-45d3-a858-5952eb18c308 .

camssa:92c8a80f-bdda-492f-9788-9fe2779c0a01 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:92caa39d-ef82-43fb-aaa7-8f5d2c3be86a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WS-BPEL is included in some national catalogues from Member States. A total of 3 countries listed the WS-BPEL within their national catalogues. They belong to Cyprus, France and Germany.\r
\r
See CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c08c660-0996-4f75-8954-fea96691284f .

camssa:92cc726d-2194-4e88-aed5-d409e43c93f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-25deb65536af2c7e82f921c56df2c7e21093b2c06fdddd63021b4bccea0b9cd7 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:92ceb7bd-f20b-4d1d-bf25-a4362fc92f15 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'FTP is a protocol exclusively designed for the transfer of files which does not secure the traffic.\r
\r
However,  there are existing extensions of FTP that secure the information delivery. For instance, FTP over TLS, known as FTPS, uses the Transport Layer Security (TLS) to secure FTP communications over a network.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\r
\r
Securing FTP with TLS Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b114beb3-5c47-4576-93c8-cd0402bb0250 .

camssa:92d08b27-e599-40ce-afa3-939f9b3fe379 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:92d221b3-d68e-41fc-968f-f7f1b79612f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e370a4af17e89cbb70bb5079082a1e21cdee85435c8fc30b12a8987f18db367f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:92de2cf8-f17d-4450-9c19-c62bde96dc56 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:92e216fe-266f-48b5-8aa2-bf6ec2285208 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TLS 1.2 is a protocol cryptographic protocol that provides end-to-end security of data sent between applications over the Internet.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.internetsociety.org/deploy360/tls/basics/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af5875b2-63eb-4e5e-9460-f9e7ac578628 .

camssa:92efd508-e1fd-4ac7-887e-2718e17ade0a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By establishing constraints on the creation and exchange of XML documents XSD fosters the trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders. However, XSD does not include security features in itself. Despite this, XML includes several recommendations in order to ensure the security of data and users.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/\r
 '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be841b39-ae7a-4ac1-a80a-95af57aca50b .

camssa:92f3f8e9-b738-41b7-9df5-10790a0d5ac1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ba46c76c10ad769a23ce4a9a34cb4d96a00407d5fc14ad1c791a870be7563c2b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:92f6445d-93bc-4951-bed5-2204d49810c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Such as IPv6, which is an advanced version of IPv4, the core specification is not customisable. Despite this, there are aspects such as implementations that can be tailored to meet specific needs.

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f2ee7a04-bb62-44e7-933d-b73be4abb3a5 .

camssa:92f664aa-cbb9-4172-835e-91b411aa455c a cav:Score,
