camssa:93d201b5-f01a-4fb4-9707-e6e5f4ddc8b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing documents and studies about the XACML performance in different environments. 
An example of this is the research article "A Performance Analysis of the XACML Decision Process and the 
Impact of Caching", which analyses the performance of XACML involved in the decision process of web services developed in the cloud and the impact of caching. Also, there is an article focused on the testing of 
XACML policies, which provides different approaches to improve effectivity.

A Performance Analysis of the XACML Decision Process and the Impact of Caching: 
https://www.researchgate.net/publication
/283307011_A_Performance_Analysis_of_the_XACML_Decision_Process_and_the_Impact_of_Caching'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0054ffee-d11e-4c91-ac72-420bea6d7f19 .

camssa:93d9977f-9074-45a0-a79a-1a7c02afd5a6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:93dc108f-c2b3-4001-a9f1-8128e5fa22a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTTPS is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, HTTPS can define the interoperability aspects of the "Network Service", "Network Component" "Private Network" and "Public Network" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c6b4b24-b4cb-4a03-9aed-4e05e79951b5 .

camssa:93ddba71-f3bc-4445-a7f2-ef31e8cf3a83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """8 Member States are recommending XSD in their ICT National Catalogues. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f9f1374-68f1-4c63-a1ef-19d52ac26c29 .

camssa:93e3c129-9239-4a4c-82a6-aad386f1d5cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:93e673a8-39e9-4b2e-815e-75fabeec8ce7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TLS 1.3 offers better performance compared to earlier versions due to TLS false start and Zero Round Trip Time (0-RTT). These performance improvements are especially evident in browser traffic and less with server-server connection (ebMS).\r
\r
The biggest improvements are in the area of security, because a number of security risks are limited. This is because unsafe options from TLS 1.2 are excluded, SHA-1, RC4, DES, 3DES, AES-CBC and MD5, which reduces the chance of the protocol being configured in an unsafe manner. Configuration is also simpler, which means there is less chance of incorrect configuration\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7b62697-69f2-4b5e-9e74-d9e93f929e3d .

camssa:93e6a7cf-f85d-4155-8cd3-83e917da1567 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can facilitate the modelling of business processes by helping standardize and agree to the form which the information is described. Standardising the evidence modelling may help in the cross-border participation by eliminating language barriers between European countries. \r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1e382d2-0a1f-4508-9c3e-72421104a0e0 .

camssa:93e6f77e-7069-450c-89fa-6e4426ed0d45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'E-ARK CSIP has not been found included in any initiative covering privacy aspects neither at national nor at European level.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3dacbebf-6e01-40d9-b4b2-200b128a73d2 .

camssa:93e8b9c6-4910-4c4e-b5d3-874db0e2cd13 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:93eb79dc-d15c-4f95-ba89-5f26b57bbe97 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The implementation of ISAE 3402 could, for example, allow administrations to properly track how the \r
different organisations providing digital public services are distributing funds. Or also to ensure that the \r
procedures and transactions with stakeholders are properly mapped. ISAE 3402 auditing tool, is designed to \r
be used in any domain.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4898a6c9-993b-4cbb-a075-012f97467869 .

camssa:93f13752-39be-4805-8cd2-a14434d8f1bf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of XACML is not related to data portability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6247bef9-d5e0-459b-8a15-9cf0bcc3e66f .

camssa:93f6be09-a82d-4e9c-af3b-11483bbe5812 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/323e06e5-331b-4076-a99f-f1c0b5ebf7fb"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:93f8db76-b8cb-44a1-a0d4-2516005938b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODRL has been used in several use cases developed in the context of development of data protection related solutions as SPECIAL (Scalable Policy-aware Linked Data Architecture For Privacy, Transparency and Compliance), an H2020 European project which involves ODRL for compliance check. \r
\r
Approaches for GDPR compliance utilising Semantic Web: \r
https://harshp.com/research/publications/035-representing-activities-processing-personal-data-consent-semweb-gdpr-compliance\r
\r
SPECIAL Deliverable: \r
https://www.specialprivacy.eu/images/documents/SPECIAL_D17_M17_V10.pdf\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0a182be-25bd-4614-8d2d-db1ceb32a19a .

