camssa:944a4944-d16a-41dc-a14d-ac46686d1d61 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST enables digital service delivery channels by providing a widely-used architectural style designed for client-server applications.  \r
\r
REST reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94a6e3ba-1b86-4e29-9cc2-b84d794ab170 .

camssa:944e5be0-8c23-4460-b2c0-1fae6e91c2a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPSV-AP is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Specifications (ELIS) and so is the 3.1. Specifically, this Core Vocabulary can define the interoperability aspects of the ""Core Data Model"" and ""Data"" ABBs from the EIRA Semantic view. The specification covers Digital Public service Catalogue from the Organisational View, Controlled Vocabulary, Data, Data Model, Data Syntax, Forms Structure, Hash Code and Metadata from the Semantic View and API Discovery and Catalogue Service from the Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v501'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d14df04-f603-4764-8d36-429741c41418 .

camssa:944f0705-6245-4477-ba0f-64d4a0c50b58 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:94551d32-bb68-4f92-ab6d-77d18313254d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b6ba3f2f556446c68c55833e72b217be87ad5f0dd07744e2c39c6070aff6c10f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:9457974c-2ac1-43d0-a2a7-5a53418379c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TSA can be used to protect data using Time-Stamp Tokens and making documentation accessible only to certain requesters, who could be public administrations in this case. Therefore, TSP can help to ensure the protection of personal data managed by Pubic Administrations.

TSP/TSA IETF reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9dcc8e9-22aa-4a2e-a472-0334566cd93a .

camssa:945b8c53-f37f-40c9-a7fd-bb816e2b94ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b6ba3f2f556446c68c55833e72b217be87ad5f0dd07744e2c39c6070aff6c10f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:945dfc63-331e-4a42-b147-7aacc7c62b0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP, as a data vocabulary, can be used for large amounts of data and does not hamper the scalability of systems using it. It is evidenced by the several implementations at the national or European level.\r
\r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/2011/gld/wiki/DCAT_Implementations"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bcfc2c9a-75cb-4ecb-af48-19dc6b4cfe77 .

camssa:946080cf-c1cc-4b91-8db0-4e3e5406c1bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:94627c8e-85b4-47e7-80de-cdfa805f2367 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of HTTP has been shown through its evolution into HTTP/3. HTTP/3 improves speed and reliability by using modern transport protocols, addressing the limitations of earlier versions. These advancements show that HTTP continuously adapts to meet new technological and security demands, proving its lasting effectiveness.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

Measuring HTTP/3: Adoption and Performance:
https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.12358'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64c5cf2d-abbc-4215-bf88-87ae2e0b1ff8 .

camssa:946756c7-152b-4e27-9aab-e56f5fc1e418 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LDAP can be found for free along within the European Collaborative Platform, Joinup.\r
\r
LDAP in Joinup platform:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/lightweight-directory-access-protocol/distribution/rfc4511-lightweight-directory-access-protocol-ldap-protocol"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:37c40096-d3b1-4231-a069-5694f6db8361 .

camssa:9469f5cc-fa20-4b70-aa8a-de32cb3601e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XAdES (ISO 14533-2:2012) is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, ISO 14533-2:2012 can define the interoperability aspects of the "e-Seal Preservation Service" and "e-Signature Preservation Service". Specifically, this Core Vocabulary can define the interoperability aspects of the Technical infrastructure view ABB from the EIRA Semantic view. \r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e91b959-6375-4c42-a7f1-11ab40417ea6 .

camssa:946cecda-4fd6-465a-a31b-f47aff07b952 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State recommending schema.org in its ICT National Catalogue.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3e08030-6a70-4775-be6c-38c24fb170ab .

camssa:947584cc-761b-4110-a0e8-ea555ea06344 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData services are used by a large community of users. These services use a common data model, which allows any client to interact with the service in a well-defined way (see OData reference). In this sense, the specification is domain-agnostic. For example, there are the Cambridge Weather-Pyslet demo service and the City of Medicine Hat Open Data Portal, in the field of academics and medicine, respectively.

OData ecosystem, Live services reference:
https://www.odata.org/ecosystem/

Cambridge Weather-Pyslet demo reference:
https://github.com/OData/odataorg.github.io/blob/master/_ecosys/liveservices/Cambridge-Weather-Pyslet-demo-service.md

Medicine Hat Open Data Portal:
https://www.medicinehat.ca/en/home-property-and-utilities/mymh-portal.aspx

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8aa25901-9980-419d-9c37-631491aed039 .

