camssa:94f117ce-51d3-490a-bf75-e7e8ed441c07 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"DNS Queries over HTTPS (DoH) security and privacy considerations are based on RFC 8446, IETF's Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol. The standard defines confidentiality and how the record layer of the protocol should provide it. AEAD encryption provides confidentiality and integrity for the data. 

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484

Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol RFC 8446: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cde0936-440c-4bba-ae2f-1ed071989f96 .

camssa:94f475d1-450d-4a1d-9f8c-a794c4151618 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of SVG is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a6d538f-18bd-4469-be8f-08cf845baf6c .

camssa:94f8de3a-af57-40de-b89c-25f257391b23 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No evidence of direct implementation of DPV in any particular business domain could be found, although use cases can be found in which the DPV vocabulary is intended to be applied, such as online shopping.

Data Protection Aspects of Online Shopping - A use case:
https://www.w3.org/community/dpvcg/2019/12/12/data-protection-aspects-of-online-shopping-a-use-case/

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86107457-2287-437e-9553-0a494e593f45 .

camssa:950a46c3-a9f3-4feb-83c1-44cfda6b68ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The GITB TDL is used in the GITB test bed software, nonetheless it is not tied to it. It can also be processed by any test bed implementation that conforms to the GITB specifications. \r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#where-is-it-used'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51706899-3742-4250-a3f7-1b53fad7e2af .

camssa:951cb141-bdee-4088-9e2b-076c8d1d41a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 enhances the visibility of administrative procedures, rules, data, and services by providing standardised protocols for clear communication. It offers extensive documentation for implementation and management and facilitates interoperability among equipment from multiple vendors.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e68e8405-860d-4ab5-b7a9-502fc15e7f1b .

camssa:951dbc14-9e34-4cc0-890d-83fccfcf4756 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"LDES is a conceptual framework where a list of immutable objects can be used to describe and publish real-time event data and it is not mandatory to use all objects.  It can be used for basic events' publication, or focus on adopting LDES alongside other existing data exchange mechanisms, creating a hybrid model that embraces the strengths of each approach.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:700d51a0-019b-4c89-9df6-c3f8b39fd028 .

camssa:951e37bf-4d26-4234-a762-d2c721c7f5e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAIS is not related to e-accessibility, therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9765d074-1ca1-439f-9809-bd7cc156f5e2 .

camssa:95284332-7c61-4879-bdc0-aeb933a3d675 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:95285084-583f-4b8f-aa11-101956c06d4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'​The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) that developed this specification, is in charge of developing solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks.

Specification development process by the ISA Programme:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications

Detailed document ISA Programme:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1d74a96-fa99-44f2-a822-7d01eb6338ca .

camssa:9528ba01-bbf4-4f8e-92c7-683fd65d2442 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 is a format that allows seamless cross-border interoperability between systems, independent of implementation. \r
\r
The specification allows cross-domain single sign-on, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. By using SAML 2.0, avoid the user to deal with several credentials nor provide information twice. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1af2acf-89a2-46a7-8275-24eae2da9da1 .

camssa:9538674f-9e29-44ac-ab8e-354b22de20eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 includes provisions that address data integrity by promoting the implementation of security controls, data governance practices, and compliance with relevant standards and regulations. By following these provisions and complementing them with additional best practices, organisations can ensure the integrity of data within cloud computing environments.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:888000f1-ce64-4a55-994b-06d381616d49 .

camssa:95447ae8-151d-4b92-8d8a-07a2f5196a7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification can help understand the data of public administration by adding high quality print-ready pages. In this case, the specification can play an active role on the representation of the information in the visual way. This fact can consider TIFF/IT to foster the comprehensibility of administrative rules and data.\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html\r
\r
TIFF/IT explanation:\r
https://www.prepressure.com/library/file-formats/tiffit"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:582b8221-fe3c-40a5-a15e-09f638e641fb .

