        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b09c1b86-7dc7-40b3-bb81-585241554217 .

camssa:972b8fb3-edab-4a91-b158-9c1f2af239fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Only nationally recognised members as well as national and CEN-recognised working groups are allowed to contribute to the development of the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification. There is no evidence of external and individual contributions, and there is no provision made for them in the CEN Internal Regulations (see CEN-CENELEC Internal Regulations reference, Part 2, section 3). Depending on the degree of involvement, financial contributions could be also applicable (CEN-CENELEC Internal Regulations reference, Part 1, CEN (1A) section, Annexes).\r
\r
CEN-CENELEC Internal Regulations reference, CEN Statuses, Members (IV) section:\r
https://boss.cen.eu/reference-material/refdocs/pages/\r
\r
CEN-CENELEC Internal Regulations reference, Part 2, section 3:\r
https://boss.cen.eu/reference-material/refdocs/pages/\r
\r
CEN-CENELEC Internal Regulations reference, Part 1, CEN (1A) section, Annexes:\r
https://boss.cen.eu/reference-material/refdocs/pages/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee4d71a1-7cd1-4f76-8b1a-b2522c01a40c .

camssa:972c8d95-da7a-4b78-8073-948a51d6610e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DQV is designed to be independent of any specific data format or storage technology. It focuses on providing a standardised vocabulary for describing data quality information in a machine-readable format. As a result, DQV can be implemented and utilized across different platforms and environments without being tied to any particular data format or technology stack.

Data Quality Vocabulary: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2e04ee2-f713-46a2-bc72-a801634c47fb .

camssa:97304f8f-d361-4db6-ac5c-f04277539653 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/8f57d945-41cd-4ae0-ba4f-8f4a03f12c23"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:973059f9-dc1d-4bb8-a660-8010a9af7dbd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of OData is not related to the organisational interoperability agreements. Moreover, one of the MS recommending this specificacion, the Netherlands, confirms its not applicability over organisational aspects. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
OData reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html\r
\r
Netherland's OData report:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/odata\""""@en ;
