camssa:97cba90a-d5b9-4ea2-bcdd-19132b248025 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Principle 2.4 from the E-ARK CSIP specification states any Information Package should have an identifier which is globally unique and persistent, fact that allows repositories to participate more easily in cross-institutional information exchange and reuse scenarios.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3c34439-0825-4c8c-9733-d1c9d57bdb30 .

camssa:97ce22c3-6639-408c-941a-cf86399721d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In some aspects, OAS can facilitate the modelling of business processes since it is a tool to document the design of an API in an automated manner as well as to develop RESTful APIs themselves in a simpler and more efficient way.  \r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eaa70da4-b033-4a0b-b3f6-5415ed4994a7 .

