camssa:98102514-4bfd-494c-af2c-7344c9240690 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISO 639-2 is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8cb3d782-cf28-4bc6-bd3c-9aae3167ae16 .

camssa:981565b5-7871-4a43-97b1-74e462b6ab4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the IPv4 is to enable communications over the internet, so much so it does not hamper the scalability of systems. By using IPv4, administrations, citizens or businesses can provide or consume data over the Internet without hampering the interoperability between systems.  \r
Despite the progressive adoption of the new version, IPv4 and IPv6 are meant to coexist for years. The mechanisms to enable the compatibility avoid interoperability hampering. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0961647d-a303-46d9-a735-35fca582b746 .

camssa:981a2007-e150-46ec-98b4-7dc9812dc2b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSD 1.1 is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. It also encourages people to join and contribute to making the community bigger.\r
\r
W3C Consortium Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9742a6b6-b6e7-4d4a-96d5-942ea5985dad .

