camssa:98f9dc70-2964-4b1c-9e01-7868ddeb58e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A DID document can express verification methods, such as cryptographic public keys, which can be used to authenticate or authorize interactions with the DID subject or associated parties. For example, a cryptographic public key can be used as a verification method with respect to a digital signature; in such usage, it verifies that the signer could use the associated cryptographic private key.

DIDs core properties W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#core-properties'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75be5058-6196-49c6-b851-b2adbc26a3bb .

camssa:98fa2bdb-eb53-4283-89e8-6a78eb286cf3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-138786a6e7517e10b94e83ec3b3e7ac79b4c49dcbeaef8d8e993c8df0d173529 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:98face1a-534f-4ece-a38c-1c898be48e19 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification supports and makes possible reporting for different needs from the same data.\r
The well-documented vision of XBRL GL driving its development was “A piece of business information, once\r
entered into any computer, anywhere, never needs to be retyped as it flows through the business reporting\r
supply chain.”\r
\r
http://raw.rutgers.edu/carlab/Cohen.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04a5f3b7-3210-4360-b433-aa25ef594977 .

camssa:98fd6812-8e7e-4a76-a2d8-d56c3d9ba323 a cav:Score,
