camssa:99334d21-8153-4322-ab9c-94290db75392 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "As most of the vocabularies, DCAT reuses several existing ones (e.g. \"adms\", \"foaf\") and the Resource Description Framework (RDF). This  results in a dependency that can hamper interoperability, especially in the case where new releases of the reused vocabularies are not backward compatible."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e4beac4-38c5-4903-996e-8c2de198d068 .

camssa:993a7a51-cdfa-4300-837d-83013b7608d8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS is recommended by eight Member States, including Cyprus, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, the Netherlands, Norway, and Spain.

France National Catalogue of Standards (Referentiel General Interoperabilite) Reference:
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf

Netherlands National Catalogue of Standards TLS Reference:
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/tls

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7ebfdb7-1e2d-4b2a-b81e-b32064997c95 .

camssa:993e3972-81d7-4ccf-8610-3dc17edc824c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a vocabulary, the implementation of CPSV-AP can be tested using methods like SHACL shapes and using semantic reasoners to ensure that the implementation is well-formed. These validation mechanisms can be used with open source tools or lite versions of tools like GrapghDB or Protégé.\r
\r
SHACL validation: \r
https://graphdb.ontotext.com/documentation/free/shacl-validation.html#what-is-shacl-validation\r
\r
Semantic Reasoners List: \r
http://owl.cs.manchester.ac.uk/tools/list-of-reasoners/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e54528e4-35d0-4fca-af55-7fd7cfd1e8d5 .

camssa:993fb8e5-7813-4483-8133-1554b3297093 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:99428b70-c0fe-494e-846a-c2cd39d6bdc0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98e1b4c9-1796-43c3-9b9a-f4adc1e5dd79 .

camssa:994a629c-91a4-4609-8a35-bb6fb9efef9f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Indexed Database API is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, Indexed Database API can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data Management" and "Cache Manager" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v610'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c725789c-83c2-456d-ac1f-dff77c2b942d .

camssa:994b5d24-2883-4429-8454-e54086c45b64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GraphQL is used in the SmartM2M project, which proposes guidelines for using semantic interoperability in the industry in ETSI TR 103 535, where IoT systems address trustworthiness, privacy, data protection and security by combining different ontologies and practices.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://graphql.org/learn/schema/\r
\r
ETSI TR 103 535 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103500_103599/103535/01.01.01_60/tr_103535v010101p.pdf\r
\r
SmartM2M - Study for oneM2M (ETSI):\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103700_103799/103715/01.01.01_60/tr_103715v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c5bc328-2c16-40b2-830f-8b528fe83e1f .

camssa:9955077e-15a1-47d7-8467-1bdc1b74e0c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is included in 10 Member States catalogues of recommended specifications. This Member States are Austria, Croatia, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, Netherlands, Spain, Sweden and Cyprus. Moreover, LDAP is used in the ULISSE project as a database to store user credentials, and controls user access to tools as well, with some exceptions.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards

ULISSE project reference:
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/218815/reporting'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:319b735a-5b16-45f9-8e6a-99051d687219 .

