camssa:99a83f5c-fc84-43a5-9b07-ab44d1011547 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of SOAP 1.2 is to store, transport and exchange data through interoperable systems. Moreover, SOAP 1.2 uses XML which defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a human-readable format and machine-readable format enhancing the reusability of data and stimulating the interoperability of systems and services.  \r
\r
Additionally, W3C develops its specification independently from any vendor. Thus, the adoption of SOAP 1.2 does not hamper the data portability of data expressed with it. In fact, the adoption of SOAP endorses the binding and invoking of web services allowing data exchange across borders.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e026f0d8-f383-438e-bb34-78e6c2e29f9b .

camssa:99ad1b00-1090-4031-8122-68203102fdc2 a cav:Score,
