camssa:99b73acd-c11f-4fa7-b861-922dc2dee7c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The objective of the specification is to allow the different partners to share manufacturing assets to facilitate their interoperability.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:405b6b70-f804-4a86-8352-ce44d2b35d75 .

camssa:99bd754b-a74d-4f2f-9aa9-07e42a525041 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The Wheat Data Interoperability Guidelines Specification covers a specific area of application, wheat-related data exchange; that is actually not covered by any other technical specification being under consideration to become a European standard. This conclusion has been drawn from the examination of all the programming mandates addressed to CEN, CENELEC and ETSI to the date, CEN’s webpage , CENELEC’s webpage , CEN-CENELEC’s webpage ICT section , the EC Information Providers Guide, Directive (EU) 2016/2102 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 October 2016 on the accessibility of the websites and mobile applications of public sector bodies , the standards and tools for exchange and processing of actionable information inventory of ENISA  and the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020 ."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:415fc220-83ec-405c-b082-41d994f9af1f .

camssa:99c9ad0a-0e57-42d9-9f13-e50699ba25f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TGF has only been found to be used in the British PAS 182:2014 standard on smart cities, which builds on the TGF specification.\r
\r
PAS 182:2014 standard:\r
https://knowledge.bsigroup.com/products/smart-city-concept-model-guide-to-establishing-a-model-for-data-interoperability/standard'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a32a353f-f744-422b-8584-dd2c14ff9528 .

camssa:99caf151-f4f2-4c8c-ac1f-c6ff6bde8297 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The infrastructure component DAPS in a given IDS ecosystem enables enrichment of identities of organisations and connectors with additional attributes thus, facilitating the publication of data on the Web. Furthermore, DAPS' license is OpenSource/Apache2 so, it incorporates open standards.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75342330-2f8d-4f84-9650-dddb10dbd981 .

camssa:99cc72a1-bc3c-4629-b6b0-a9489d6603e0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:99d5dfe7-39d5-4ce0-8b7a-e245b46c586b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that uses PAdES (ISO 14533-3:2017) nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification. However, the specification PAdES from ETSI, is involved in some cross-border projects as "Analysis of standards related to Trust Service Providers" developed by ENISA (European Union Agency for Network and Information Security) which is a centre of network and information security expertise for the EU, its member states, the private sector and Europe’s citizens. \r
\r
ENISA project:\r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/tsp_standards_2015/at_download/fullReport\r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html\r
\r
PAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8c87dcc-9122-4e3f-93a5-594981b76ce8 .

