camssa:9a95b400-f3d1-426d-9460-8df975ecfdef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, IPv6 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d410e20d-d9c5-470e-8fcf-9808dc464ca1 .

camssa:9a9be8da-c902-4aa2-96ce-fddb64c8c040 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification of SVG is available for free, it can be checked on the W3C official webpage.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e6d592c-f9ef-470b-aed3-f725f429b685 .

camssa:9aa16472-f3d8-4d66-bc82-ecab578f9a68 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0c9dd43038136296b52f50e05f9d6eef39f7b8018517224007990b15be2eb19e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9aa2243c-8270-4b4f-9a89-f4f0eec8b086 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification allows for partial implementations, meaning that certain behaviours or features might not be supported by every implementation. This flexibility enables adaptation to specific use cases and system requirements. One worthy implementation is RabbitMQ, which is supported by most major operating systems and platforms. It is open-source under the Mozilla Public License. RabbitMQ is designed for business messaging and provides messaging through adapters, SMTP, STOMP, HTTP, and lightweight web messaging.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf

RabbitMQ Implementation:
https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/protocols'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5da1cf05-f8e9-47b4-9649-faaf856dc6f7 .

camssa:9aaa427b-b35f-49b4-87c5-64254aad1fd5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02e4b50e-ac56-4662-b8c8-f48c0e022566 .

camssa:9aab1340-10b1-433b-979b-941a64984680 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5839144ecfb6c41a2c3cf5c1e86a6b3ad7a9e3ec9c4efa5650a6e7b9e3586335 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9aab2bd3-07f6-403e-9062-6c398fcefa84 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON itself does not foresee access control mechanisms. These are typically implemented at the application level or within the systems that handle JSON data. The responsibility for access control lies with the applications, APIs, or servers that process JSON data.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e09db627-d1e5-48da-9b70-fc4a230cefe5 .

camssa:9ab1534b-3e36-4e4e-872f-b5f653505c3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in different catalogues and repositories, there is no evidence found of ETSI TS 119 512 being included in the catalogue of any Member State.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c0c44d7-e97c-4d11-8fd5-6d1232e4ef23 .

camssa:9ab2efb3-c153-41c3-97c3-9bd59604e9e5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9ab3bd6c-0214-43d2-a401-943066f21f1b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9ab4ff12-74f4-4e7b-91f8-5d1f2c612210 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OWL is developed as a vocabulary extension of RDF and is derived from the DAML+OIL Web Ontology Language. So it can be said that OWL2 is dependent of RDF.\r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a64f72cb-5bac-4a18-b684-0735160346ec .

camssa:9abcb4f7-4f0d-4802-9fac-d874e1e03189 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF is a vendor neutral standard developing organisation and HTTPS is independent from any technology or platform.\r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68ae6058-dd78-494d-8d48-15d3be767c65 .

camssa:9abec3ab-9c82-4871-a611-63eb4911c5e3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF is a vendor neutral SDO. However, FTP relies on TCP to ensure that all data exchanged is sent correctly to the proper destination.\r
\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc959\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc793"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4510e012-3f50-40b4-abb1-28dc363bfa1c .

camssa:9ac139d6-a716-44c4-848f-ed1da59bd45f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8a34a40e5bc5436b3530d898d75a57cf0488591887b31a5169499fe78952d84c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9ac1db11-36f0-4d12-b2b2-df3671b5daf8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ba46c76c10ad769a23ce4a9a34cb4d96a00407d5fc14ad1c791a870be7563c2b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9ac3054d-8a7c-4f26-a549-308c5ee03415 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-21276471c1781fa2c7e78c8e03851e076b840beddbf5cf64f53b54b8855a01b8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9ac5641b-a6da-4e02-9a9e-e121ceb90dae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Interoperability Test Bed (ITestBed) is used to allow the conformance of any model developed from EIRA. It is called the Interoperability Architecture Solutions Validator, that not only can validate models from EIRA but also the different specialisations such eGovERA models. 

Interoperability Architecture Solutions Validators: 
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/eira/upload

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d054bf2f-6769-4502-81f7-494d77da5714 .

camssa:9ac71950-769d-4f79-944c-fd367a99092f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c967c90bfc7bc13426924eca012de349ae51d4e8f652fe64bfbec2cccc8c8146 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9acb0421-0624-43e0-90f3-8acd46e7124b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The adoption of TLS 1.2 does not affect the system scalability. However, the new 1.3 version has improved security. Despite having this situation the interoperability is not affected due to its fluid interconectness."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9604cd4-2141-4bda-bfe3-ddef8abd28bd .

camssa:9acde850-0b1a-49bc-98b3-e4d6e5ac5307 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9ad7a94a-3d71-4206-9092-aed05a9f03db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS ebXML Core (ebCore) Technical Committee promotes the sharing of data and results and helps accelerate the specification adoption throughout the international community, particularly within government agencies. In this sense, the specification encourages both the creation of communities and the sharing of their data and results on international platforms.\r
\r
OASIS ebXML Core (ebCore) Technical Committee reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ebcore'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57fdc73a-6b3a-4c2d-b680-5c22e8a9ce3e .

camssa:9ad80915-5553-40ed-b9a7-bf64fbb14dd9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As specification to structure data in order to allow the maximum interoperability between systems, RDF fosters the data portability between administrations at the same time that helps to enhance data discoverability and enabling the cross-data set queries using SPARQL. \r
Specifically, RDF helps data portability and exchange between databases. The serialisation of RFD has several forms that ensure the availability of data. \r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:13b9a4f0-f343-471d-a766-b99b0677c445 .

camssa:9adfacb5-fdde-476b-9e0b-261cc9fd8005 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9af71b47-6e61-4159-a1ee-f65912595c27 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-838030847fa0adf54939e3feaac0ac2510924c54035e1cb671b223b54b02fd70 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:9af7a1fb-7f5b-44a4-9699-a549f205ff72 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Nordic Institute for Interoperability Solutions mentions the Dataspace Protocol in the making of Road-X 8, an open source data exchange layer solution that enables organizations to exchange information over the Internet. Road-X 8 Proof of Concept (PoC) started to integrate the standard Dataspace Protocol into X-Road and concentrate on the trust framework later.

NIIS Making of X-Road 8 - PoC: https://www.niis.org/blog'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6fa5a09d-d033-4067-bbf3-ba343c445033 .

camssa:9af93f13-b0ef-490c-a6ef-2ec4056f2561 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DCMI specification is not included in any Member State catalogue of recommended specifications.\r
\r
List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dee8a221-cf38-4fd5-8f55-9d61bdea6f85 .

camssa:9af9b7cd-39f9-45a0-a147-791078275d33 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cf1de0bf03a8ee372af0deddf9ef5c4609f5a7bb9c7e001c89d887c6789eaf56 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9b0174d3-4459-489b-812f-c4305be57102 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs does not directly address data processing accuracy, but can be complemented with others specifications to guarantee a certain degree of data accuracy.  DIDs is often used in conjuntion with VCs, which allow users to share claims in a verifiable manner. DIDs enhance data processing accuracy by ensuring data originates from verified sources, maintaining immutable records, enabling detailed traceability, implementing role-based data entry, automating data verification, and allowing selective disclosure. Therefore, using DIDs, individuals can control and manage their version controls, ensuring the accuracy of the information shared.

DIDs data accuracy W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/

VCs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5035ae2b-53ff-4723-bd89-5956c61aad7a .

camssa:9b046cc0-0f81-4e5a-90c2-b90f3900a400 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9b06642f-2359-4064-8da2-4e478b7be0a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of Indexed Database API. In "Evaluating IndexedDB Performance on Web Browsers" study, is conducted a comparative analysis of IndexedDB performance on four renowned browsers. In this sense, IndexedDB operations are explored in each browser and a statistical analysis is conducted to compare the performance of these operations on each browser.

"Evaluationg IndexedDB Performance on Web Browsers" study:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8080047'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8cd4e2a6-0f42-4dc1-8ced-b343db281576 .

camssa:9b0a12d7-7563-45a9-a016-ad7368656077 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are several validators for ORDL that help to ensure that the implementation and description of datasets are conformant with the requirements set out in the specification.\r
\r
ODRL Implementation:\r
http://odrlapi.appspot.com/\r
\r
ODRL Implementation evaluator:\r
http://odrlapi.appspot.com/apidoc/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7c8fddcf-4c8f-4d16-a999-e642279b9be0 .

camssa:9b11b286-c115-4c77-8a9a-2206d3981775 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification performs efficiently in accordance with the TR-ESOR middleware techincal guidelines. The goal of the TR-ESOR Guideline is to assist in the process of choosing and using suitable security measures for the preservation of evidence of signed electronic documents over long periods of time. The document outlines security requirements that implementations must meet, ensuring the integrity, authenticity, and non-repudiation of digital signatures.

TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:
https://www.bsi.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/EN/BSI/Publications/TechGuidelines/TR03125/TR-03125_v1_2_2-main-doc.pdf?__blob=publicationFile&v=1

ETSI TS 119 512 specification:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6da95d6e-e7d3-48ed-82c3-7d1e67a16019 .

camssa:9b11f441-c6b5-47a4-8cad-0a7c1b030da8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV is a business domain agnostic data model that can be applied in any field requiring the management of transaction orders and ensuring data consistency.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7b6bf69a-de21-4e70-a88a-1c9ce08e71ed .

camssa:9b12cd42-7191-4106-ab83-b47e78e6ab9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c03559b3-a387-4223-91ec-68312381772c .

camssa:9b183701-c17b-4df2-9353-fb38beefb876 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:9b1dcf3c-3def-4c4c-88cf-bf91d1526825 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "'The specification promotes visibility to business data and harmonizes the data contents thus enabling better usability for the data.'"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6368edf-8c8d-48f6-b45b-234658400842 .

camssa:9b225f91-842b-4cd7-9eb2-4dffea6dc98e a cav:Score,
