camssa:9b9620ec-0466-4258-86ad-6672569c937b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD is widely used when exchanging information in XML is needed. There are two european initiatives that are using XSD to provide services. \r
\r
The first initiative is TED eSentool, a free web service of the Publications Office which is focused in allow eSenders to follow-up the process of their notices until publication. \r
\r
The ESPD, is another cross border initiative using XSD for the validation of the XML documents generated while generating eProcurement process and documentation.  \r
\r
See: \r
https://esentool.ted.europa.eu/\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/public-procurement/digital/espd"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0b13372-bdf2-480f-b7d1-e38836a998f9 .

camssa:9b968986-6e0e-4922-bc3a-33dd19aa6b37 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As EN 16234-1 e-CF was designed as a common standardised framework for Europe-wide application, resulting from a common effort between the public and private domains, the specification has sufficient market acceptance for its use in the development of digital solutions and services. Nowadays the IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) is in charge of carrying out all the consultive efforts regarding the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification (see CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.1).\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.1:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, e-Competence Framework:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/about-it-professionalism/competences/the-e-competence-framework/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f6a1152-b3db-48de-924d-af6091efe2ac .

