camssa:9b9e9958-aaa9-429a-a2b3-b2caadbde421 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Genericode is recommended by four different European Member States. For instance, it is included in the Dutch ICT National Catalogue as a useful standard for defining code lists. *No encuentro los otros catalogos con genericode aunque en la lista pone que están.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards

Netherlands Open Standards Catalogue: https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/aanbevolen'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9efa6ae-5eb1-414b-8f50-e2c0c29b37ae .

camssa:9b9fc7b7-ab39-4e70-9175-82aa63186740 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9ba74ea4-b175-4c15-a468-8fbb875303e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP is included in 9 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Croatia, Cyprus,\r
France, Germany, Greece, Malta, Netherlands, Spain, Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework \r
(NIF) of Spain is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework \r
(EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Nonetheless, \r
countries like Sweden or Malta do not get a high perfomance, being alligned with 3 out of 5 and 2 out of 5 \r
respectively.\r
\r
National catalogue Malta:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio\r
/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
National catalogue Sweden:\r
https://www.avropa.se/globalassets/dokument/open-it-standards.pdf?_t_id=1B2M2Y8AsgTpgAmY7PhCfg%\r
3d%3d&_t_q=standards&_t_tags=language%3asv%2csiteid%3a95d515a5-23ca-47bf-87a9-\r
07b10d8ac360&_t_ip=178.139.72.144&_t_hit.id=Avropa_Core_Models_Media_GenericMedia/_ff07d720-\r
f793-44b0-994d-27e79b28f6bd&_t_hit.pos=7\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a88c6b2-19ac-4590-a7c2-35676f58fa0d .

camssa:9ba83d99-250a-4c00-a2f9-e15f2fb882d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecac085a-7a10-41a5-be9b-013c2c6399df .

camssa:9bad5694-ec84-446a-80f0-2c9eada8d9be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary was previously developed and used by the ISA Programme. The ISA (Interoperability Solutions for European Public Administrations), is a European Union programme (implemented by the Commission) contributing to a European Union free from electronic barriers at national borders.

However, according to recent discussions on the CBV GitHub, W3C has discontinued the Registered Organization Vocabulary and the community along with the continuation for the development moved to the Core Business Vocabulary.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

ISA Programmae Reference:
https://publications.europa.eu/resource/cellar/c80c7ff1-14e7-43d6-a56f-99bf254c33f9.0001.02/DOC_1

Core Business Vocabulary Github reference:
https://github.com/SEMICeu/Core-Business-Vocabulary/tree/master

Core Business Vocabulary Github Issue 51 - RegOrg maintenance reference:
https://github.com/SEMICeu/Core-Business-Vocabulary/issues/51'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:18fbd401-0135-4a0d-9645-1cda520b3b64 .

camssa:9bb0e729-4b55-4164-a2a4-7ab5e41ffa41 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9bb97d03-57ce-4aff-9700-21514c0ab5b7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP does provide a basic framework and elements that can be built upon to enable access control features like offering an authentication framework (Like Proxy-Authorization), method-specific semantics (Such as: GET, HEAD, OPTIONS), and relevant status codes (Such as: 401 Unauthorized,403 Forbidden or 405 Method Not Allowed).

HTTP/1.1, RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-http-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f6fd1d4-6544-471b-9981-b691069ae88a .

camssa:9bb9d203-7bec-46d4-8388-7d239442e00e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP does focus on ensuring the accurate transmission of data between clients and servers. It incorporates mechanisms that contribute to maintaining accuracy during the transmission and storage of data in caches.

HTTP/1.1, RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Caching, RFC 9111 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-http-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5454d86a-2fcc-4b0c-af54-009919fa8762 .

camssa:9bbabb70-8aab-480a-8dfb-99eb083b1d7e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9bbbbec4-2a7e-472d-a9ba-81befa932457 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DCAT-AP is not related to the provision of access control mechanisms.  Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:271d28e1-fa58-4938-a1f3-806197a64b3b .

camssa:9bbd17a9-cfc1-4d3a-9cbb-2e49788892a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON is a text format that is completely language independent. The specification uses conventions that are familiars to C-family of languages, including C, C++, C#, Java, JavaScript, Perl, Python, and many others. For these reasons, JSON is an optimum data exchange and interchange language.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc8d4004-4e45-4d09-aa75-3f872e20e758 .

camssa:9bbdf3a5-b25f-42db-81de-d5a4853381f4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:9bc137a6-7e46-447a-9761-6a40911f8c51 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e8c3529a6146f0b0d269112be717ba4e9c5979ea4f43f57d217c0f998d26ce17 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9bc5e01c-e33f-4273-8742-69b6adccf426 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the specification does not include a public review of the release life-cycle although the specification and its releases are publicly available. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af099020-24d0-4411-acf5-f301d7d4aacf .

camssa:9bc67936-f6fe-4d4f-ba70-cff18fd4c8d2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9bc70545-9099-4fcd-a1b3-a80806ac421a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification provides a standard format for representing legal documents, which can facilitate data portability between systems and applications supporting the implementation of European public services.\r
\r
By using a standard format, different systems and applications can exchange legal documents in a common language, which can help to avoid compatibility issues and ensure interoperability.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2973f13c-ba9b-45e4-9b7a-192e3f7ec8c3 .

camssa:9bc8bdcd-9e70-4d98-be98-00a2885a04ab a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9bc8f43d-2ec9-48dc-b33c-ac91987ef01c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON in itself does not provide security features, which is a weakness per se. The storage of private data as JSON format is not recommended in order to avoid malicious activities against stored information. Despite this, there are several additional features with the aim of protecting data exchange.\r
\r
How do you secure and encrypt JSON and XML data in web communication:\r
https://www.linkedin.com/advice/0/how-do-you-secure-encrypt-json-xml-data-web-communication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e52e23e-b4d7-49a3-a1fd-d590355076e5 .

camssa:9bc9921e-89a1-49d7-8035-7b048e4b2c64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is considered platform-agnostic, as it is not tied to a specific operating system or hardware platform. 
The syslog protocol is designed to provide a standardized method for message logging and can be implemented on various operating systems, including Unix, Linux, Windows, and others. Additionally, syslog 
is used on a wide range of network devices, such as routers, switches, firewalls, and servers, making it 
platform-independent at the application layer.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad4637a8-e528-4cdd-b418-3cb2a4ccc829 .

camssa:9bcbb6f8-856b-4f73-8a23-ac36e3e526c4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9bccdd45-ccdf-4e18-a7b6-ebb6f7d6007d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS, campliant with the European Directive of electronic signature of the European Parliament and the Council.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/103100_103199/103171/02.01.01_60/ts_103171v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79f75319-9800-4d26-b6b2-7de96b807f53 .

camssa:9bd15a40-9515-46f9-a6ee-f75641ad9492 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:9bddbdb7-f29c-494e-83d4-24663ea3a703 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are assessments that analyse and demonstrate the efficiency of AMQP and other similar specifications. For a detailed explanation of AMQP's efficiency and a comparison with other messaging protocols, refer to the document "Choice of Effective Messaging Protocols for IoT Systems: MQTT, CoAP, AMQP and HTTP."

Numerous real-world scenarios and products utilise the AMQP specification, proving its efficiency. AMQP connects hundreds of systems in various sectors, including telecommunications, defence, manufacturing, internet, and cloud computing, as well as many other market segments. Notable examples include Deutsche Börse, VMware, and Mozilla, among others.

Choice of Effective Messaging Protocols for IoT Systems: MQTT, CoAP, AMQP and HTTP Reference:
https://pure.port.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/12197128/IoT_Messaging_Protocols_Naik.pdf

Products and Success Stories - AMPQ.org Reference:
https://www.amqp.org/about/examples

Deutsche Börse Reference:
https://www.deutsche-boerse.com/dbg-de/

VMware Reference
https://www.vmware.com/

Mozilla Reference
https://www.mozilla.org'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20292e7e-984b-49d8-9781-abad438d3e0a .

camssa:9be6b903-0cc2-4622-8bc8-2b4e0558a592 a cav:Score,
