        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"1 Member State is recommending OCSP in its ICT National Catalogue. This Member State is Spain and\r
CERES is the digital public service procured by OCSP.\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio\r
/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
CERES' OCSP reference:\r
https://www.cert.fnmt.es/en/catalogo-de-servicios/validacion-de-certificados/ocsp\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fea63892-d0c4-43b1-b5b2-cc9fafc6789c .

camssa:9cc99fae-cac3-406c-bac9-0bec7073eab2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is  maintained by the Platform Industrie 4.0 and has a dedicated working group in Github. In order to participate in the development of the specification, users must be members of the Industrie 4.0 consortium in the Digital Twin initiative (IDTA).

IDTA members:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/about-idta/become-a-member

Asset Administration Shell (AAS) Github documentation:
https://admin-shell-io.github.io/aas-specs-antora/index/home/index.html

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0efdd07-9906-453d-b1eb-cf56ff392a2e .

