camssa:9d2e74ce-8382-4d7b-9726-4f73db101f26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a vocabulary, the implementation of CPOV can be tested using methods like SHACL shapes and using semantic reasoners to ensure that the implementation is well-formed. These validation mechanisms can be used with open source tools or lite versions of tools like GrapghDB or Protégé.\r
\r
SHACL validation: \r
https://graphdb.ontotext.com/documentation/free/shacl-validation.html#what-is-shacl-validation\r
\r
Semantic Reasoners List: \r
http://owl.cs.manchester.ac.uk/tools/list-of-reasoners/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecc997b7-f36a-4ffb-8b35-3ced3dfb167a .

camssa:9d305fcf-c0fc-4d42-b0a4-83b08c320dab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The CCCEV is used in several cross-border projects that are regulated using Legal acts. Examples are ESPD-EDM, the TOOP, and the eCertis, all projects are focused in the field of eProcurement, and use the CCCEV as the basis for building up the requierements in procurement procedures.\r
\r
CCCEV Joinup page:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee3ea555-c461-422e-83e4-114156c9f6d7 .

camssa:9d32a810-6dd9-4c97-9f9d-ef02e5e56813 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Internet Protocol Security (IPsec), a protocol providing a network layer security (authentication and encryption), is included as a mandatory feature in the IPv6 specification. IPv6 is more secure than the alternative Internet protocol, IPv4, its previous version.\r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2460"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7734c2f-cd2e-491a-a914-7dc9014eb9b7 .

camssa:9d3a4ed1-d424-4e6c-840c-023652d1c41e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the specification, a compliant DAPS must offer Server Metadata according to RFC 8414 (OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server Metadata). This offers informative metadata such as dates involved in the release of the solutions described, which means that the reliability of the exchanged data is improved. \r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS\r
\r
RFC 8414 (OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server Metadata): https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8414'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11b306aa-483b-4e53-a9a5-9349951cb731 .

camssa:9d3c0f11-0da3-440b-ae33-2c5c5118a076 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing mechanisms to carry out SAML 2.0 conformity. For instance, SAMLtool.com provides a SAML Response XML validation on open source that can be found at their Github. \r
\r
SAML XML Validator Reference:\r
https://www.samltool.com/validate_response.php'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9659f0aa-e9e6-4bd7-8575-b8d34aae1728 .

camssa:9d43fd08-6db8-4d81-9699-fe3f713ae5e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As it happens with all the e-Government Vocabularies, it has the SEMIC action from the ISA2 as responsible for the maintenance of the development. Additionally, there's a post on W3C in open government community group that talks about the specification.\r
\r
CPOV page on Joinup: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary\r
\r
CPOV post in W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/opengov/2016/02/21/core-public-organisation-vocabulary/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:267e3a8f-cefd-482a-a285-2d1309c1ac54 .

camssa:9d4b1fc6-b253-44fc-afb2-ad60837fb137 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification eases the access to information via webpages. Therefore, it reduces administrative burden for citizens, businesses and public administrations."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b62a1548-0240-441b-985e-87709df78bcb .

camssa:9d4e7414-2dc8-41dc-b77f-60a55abf709b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:9d4ea5ec-79fb-49a6-b5a2-fedceabb01a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"IEEE Std 802.3-2022 has been found in the Standard reference list for European Smart City initiatives. These cities integrate traditional infrastructure with cutting-edge digital solutions to enhance efficiency and quality of life. While the standard itself isn't explicitly mentioned in other projects, its underlying network infrastructure and Ethernet extensions can provide a robust foundation for these projects.

Report of TWG Smart Cities: Landscape of Smart Cities Standards reference:
https://www.standict.eu/sites/default/files/2021-12/StandICT.eu2023_Smart%20Cities%20Landscape%20Report_Booklet_V1.0.pdf

Smart Cities Project:
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/smart-cities-and-communities
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3144c7b2-4684-47a7-83d9-622ed8aad5ee .

camssa:9d543f5b-b94d-41e0-bdfb-bc72daff6462 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although HTML can be used independently of other technical specifications, it can be enhanced along other specifications, for example, it can be used with CSS to give a visual format to the HTML code.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48ea3801-ebec-4199-8190-434c5eecc216 .

camssa:9d554da9-f363-4cdf-9c82-c945eef7ac3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "ASiC Baseline profile depends on the different electronic signature standards (CAdES, PAdES, XAdES), and its settings regarding the level of conformity to provide a convenient result. Even though all the specifications above mentioned are interrelated, each one takes into account the others avoiding interoperability issues by indicating the requirements of each use case. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02e940ff-b101-4f09-a5bf-1e636f21bb6e .

camssa:9d5b1fe5-bba2-41a7-a6bc-fb94f0add03b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. Moreover, there is a public review in the TC process.\r
 \r
OASIS guideline:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb97ffbc-eb13-41b0-bad3-5c43a6dba239 .

camssa:9d5c68af-aa99-4ff0-a555-667810b5e2a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are no disclosures of ISO IPR Database to identify the licensing under the specification. ISO 10918-1:1994 (JPEG) is not listed in ISO/IEC/ITU Common Patent policy, so it cannot be confirmed that the specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
ISO patents:\r
https://www.iso.org/iso-standards-and-patents.html \r
\r
ISO standards and patents IPR database:\r
http://isotc.iso.org/livelink/livelink/13622347/Patents_database.xls?func=doc.Fetch&nodeId=13622347 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:691efada-d2ca-47bb-83e1-025fe6a2dbbf .

