        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:9e43ce71-b868-47a8-be5a-b3929d8a6cea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification does not directly address e-accessibility, as it primarily focuses on metadata for cataloguing public sector software. However, by promoting software transparency, reuse, and sharing, publiccode.yml can indirectly support the development of digital public services that adhere to accessibility standards, such as WCAG. The specification could facilitate the discovery and adoption of accessible software components, encouraging developers to prioritise e-accessibility principles in the creation and reuse of public sector software.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62a66610-fe18-4b5a-a693-55a7a01ea31e .

camssa:9e4592df-a961-4331-8664-c77dfe82eaab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LDAP is still excellent with authenticating Linux-based applications including many open source solutions, for example: OpenVPN, Jenkins, Kubernetes. It is often used to complement Active Directory (AD) as a directory services protocol. Therefore, it is demonstrated that LDAP has enough market acceptance for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
LDAP used with OpenVPN:\r
https://openvpn.net/vpn-server-resources/openvpn-access-server-on-active-directory-via-ldap/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b345af58-4090-4d3b-9d8f-72e4079080ac .

camssa:9e45bcdc-958a-4394-8612-67a556ef29c7 a cav:Score,
