    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9f4cc7b7-a3e1-4ede-bb19-cd6e246c73cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """8 Member States are recommending SMTP in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are Croatia, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden. \r
 \r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a8a93d90-9986-4a28-bd5c-77754013e7eb .

camssa:9f533ca1-5a30-41a4-8a89-3ff5aad43860 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512  has been developed to provide services for the long-term preservation of data in general.  The specification fosters the implementation of the once-only principle by ensuring data is well preserved and stored, and that it can also be retrieved when needed. \r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42dc9cec-3f3f-48c0-8d87-75b9fd085029 .

camssa:9f53f52f-0185-42db-b396-dca0058c6c40 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main uses of HTTP Cookies is to authenticate when a user is logged in, and with which account they are logged in. Without the cookie, users would need to authenticate themselves by logging in on each page containing sensitive information that they wish to access. Cookies can also be used to save for subsequent use information that the user previously entered into form fields, such as names addresses and passwords. For that matter, this specification helps enabling digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd83bbd8-18f1-49dd-99f5-f1b716a9e867 .

camssa:9f56871b-4283-4776-9b41-b483ca3dfa96 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSS v2.1 is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain manner.\r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a37a94b-8ca6-427a-91ad-5671e5b21e96 .

camssa:9f5bae4f-7a7e-455b-99d5-d66d47fbeff4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In Taxes in Europe database, to access the Web service for accessing the VAT rates in the EU, which includes SOAP in combination with the WS-Security standard.\r
\r
Web service for accessing the VAT rates:\r
https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/online-services/online-services-and-databases-taxation/tedb-taxes-europe-database_en'"""@en ;
