camssa:9f77e3e9-a339-4045-ab86-4b1a81c05ee6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of RDF is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc49147d-d8c6-45e2-8dc6-794597b7621a .

camssa:9f7fb0f3-1df0-413b-946b-63e6c138602f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UTF-8 is a format involved in data exchange as a key point by encoding data. Facilitating the digital data exchange, the specification helps to avoid the non-digital documentation exchange reducing the administrative burden. UTF-8 eases the digital data exchange between administration and stakeholders, therefore, it is a mean for the reduction of administrative burden."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af2b18e8-8548-4117-918d-edb6a8e327b4 .

camssa:9f851451-0310-463c-88f9-f05320d12187 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OASIS have defined a clear Technical Committee (hereby TC) process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification being formulated. 

Review process OASIS:
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a571a596-839b-4044-bb07-6ba6567dd009 .

camssa:9f89e620-6a5f-4d5b-9f6c-d6048d6bde6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) was defined in 1982 as a method for e-mail transmission. Nowadays, it is still widely used between mail servers for e-mail messages exchange. Therefore, it is demonstrated that SMTP has enough maturity for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
SMTP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5321"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0882902d-bcd6-4b56-af89-8e53253ed245 .

camssa:9f8c0e76-c1d4-4a14-ab8a-f1c228434d68 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9f8d6f09-afb0-44ec-9215-7d2a28477486 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV has documentation regarding Use Cases and Requirements which analyses its efficiency.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/csvw-ucr/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39455a90-eb2d-4947-a261-43b6c554a124 .

camssa:9f90612b-38a6-41ab-a5ea-0dfc18085160 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of WAI-ARIA is increasing accessibility of web content and applications for a large range of
users, either with special needs or without disabilities. Therefore, this specification addresses and enables e-accessibility.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4148554-a465-4256-a1a0-122a265f53fa .

camssa:9f92b32f-82be-4308-b5f6-1e268fd08f33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SHACL specification ensures the authenticity and authentication of the roles and agents involved in data transactions by establishing comprehensive SHACL access control lists. These lists define the criteria for validating the identity and authorisation of each agent, thereby safeguarding the integrity of the data transactions. 

"SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43458-7_4

SHACL-ACL github:
https://github.com/SDM-TIB/SHACL-ACL

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ecbd3d6-742b-4155-8593-8949eb7cc522 .

camssa:9f938698-2c21-4bb2-a24c-868500200899 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:9f945b1b-a46c-43c5-8561-a86505303a9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Even though there have been several implementation at different levels of EIRA and its specialisations, there are no studies so far evaluating the effectiveness or efficiency of the specification. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3f3fe52-01a6-4924-9fff-d5c6f1260265 .

camssa:9f98f117-dc74-458e-bad7-24b91461b651 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a mark-up language that describes resources in the web, the specification may increase government-to-government reuse of data and therefore can prevent citizens or businesses from providing information multiple times; however, this is not consistently done.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df7bab0f-9403-44b6-aaf4-867bc507cf08 .

camssa:9f994dfc-0839-49d9-b9f5-f1191ebe401d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL can be used to validate the data of a public administration while published as RDF. Therefore it could foster its comprehensibility.\r
\r
An evidence of this is CELLAR, which is the semantic repository of the Publications Office. CELLAR recognises SHACL as its standard of preference for data validation in the Semantic Web.\r
\r
See:\r
https://publications.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/658088eb-c071-11e8-9893-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-86108820"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d101e5ee-cd22-4268-aa8b-28f283414376 .

camssa:9f9bc946-3385-4a1b-985c-b314b6e9730e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While JSON does not directly relate to e-accessibility, there can be found resource that allow for JSON to create Accessible Rich Internet Applications (ARIA) widgets.  Therefore, it can enable e-accessibility if combined with other specifications.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf\r
\r
JSON ARIA:\r
https://wiki.mozilla.org/Accessibility/JSON_ARIA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39050080-cea9-48bc-bc46-35089bb9515b .

camssa:9f9c706e-5964-44da-97db-0a59f7f2960c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is a widely used de-facto standard. Thus, it is sufficiently mature for the development of products and services. Since it's release 1995, IPsec overcame most of its initial problems and has been used by many products and services (see IBM products and services and Oracle Solaris reference).\r
\r
IBM z/OS operating system: \r
https://www.ibm.com/it-infrastructure/z/zos\r
\r
IBM AIX operating system:\r
https://www.ibm.com/it-infrastructure/power/os/aix\r
\r
Oracle Solaris 11:\r
https://www.oracle.com/solaris/solaris11/\r
\r
List of IPSec Implementations:\r
http://www.mit.edu/~tytso/ipsec/surv9607.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9986b6d-7d43-4ebc-9fad-a83381b07fd5 .

camssa:9fa808ee-fb99-468e-9806-b9c16a5c247c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ELI is publicly available for its use and implementation within the Publications Office's website . Moreover, it is available for everyone to study with no cost.\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
ELI Technical Information: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/technical_information.html """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd503265-ee5a-42d7-a5ac-ccf97fd59d90 .

