camssa:9fff5177-c860-45ac-b02b-63bb761c5574 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol is aligned with various European regulations regarding privacy aspects. Some of the regulations include the Data Governance Act (DGA), which aims to make more data available by regulating the reuse of publicly/held, protected data, and the Data Act Proposal (DA-E), which aims to ensure fairness in the digital environment, stimulate a competitive data market, open opportunities for data-driven innovation and make data more accessible. 

IDSA Rulebook Legal Dimension: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/idsa-rulebook/idsa-rulebook/6_legal_dimension

Data Governance Act (DGA): https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/ip_22_1113

Data Act Proposal (DA-E): https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32022R0868'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17c87903-ec7c-4c89-a4c6-5d2d1eca9ea9 .

camssa:a001f6e8-f81f-47e5-938f-5b8e90372768 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4017a1ae4d077fbb3847280a1c20b41bf00c32d65fc9beaa2bea8cce550ac463 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:a00754d5-cd3a-4b02-94b6-70c690ae7285 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, IPv4 is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. IPv4 is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
See:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47e0beea-940d-4b48-86cf-434d96537f7b .

camssa:a00e4ee1-3723-468c-b6ba-a9e940a7d443 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-58010a47630ff9ea23336bf3fc558deff59905e0292551fcabc95740082cb378 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:a00f84a3-7bec-4693-9c9b-24bb49e2b7fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The first version of OWL was released in 2004 which was designed as representation languages for authoring ontologies. Some years later, in 2009, a new W3C working group started to extend OWL with several new features. W3C announced the new version, OWL2, on 27 October 2009. \r
This new version soon found its way into semantic editors such as Protégé and semantic reasoners such as Pelle, so this specification is mature enough for its use.\r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a3d7c6b-090d-4265-aa10-b98c719d26f1 .

camssa:a01380c8-0da9-4e5c-a7c0-4065ee6fd802 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:a018f7fd-650d-48c9-a17c-26dd96212c66 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"OData services return URLs to identify resources requested by clients. Where possible, interoperability increases by exploiting the information found in the route part of the URL. However, attention must be paid to those URLs including custom transformations (query options) and clients must be aware of it in future requests to the identified resource.
In this sense any user that imports data needs to check the URL provided by the system since it might contain certain parameters that filter the values (ID's, dates,...) for more information consult the Microsoft guide to import OData values onto powerBI/Excel. 

Analyze sales data from Excel and an OData feed
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/connect-data/desktop-tutorial-analyzing-sales-data-from-excel-and-an-odata-feed 

OData reference on extensibility:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358848\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b38e47e-bf3b-44a5-bcb0-8db283636fdd .

camssa:a020634d-6271-4c77-8deb-d2b256935b80 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:a023378d-d3eb-459c-863f-b4fad5167d0a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
