camssa:a1773eed-d8f5-4a9b-afb6-6f10f2096351 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does enable  the exposure of interfaces. For example, government agencies can use the  specification to create machine-readable versions of administrative procedures and rules data, which can then be used to automate various processes, such as the processing of applications and requests, or the generation of reports and statistics. These machine-readable versions can be made available through APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) or other interfaces, which can be used to enable access to public administration services.\r
\r
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f333092-b94f-4e8b-9ea4-cde83ab5fef1 .

