        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:a2d8a21d-fdd3-43be-a0f2-a68981260049 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the key features of the ESPD is the digital signature functionality tool, which allows contracting authorities and suppliers to electronically sign and verify the authenticity of the document. The digital signature provides a mechanism to verify that the document has not been tampered with, and that the information contained within it is authentic and accurate.  It is important to note that the e-signature functionality is something that is built on top of the ESPD model, and each Member State is responisble of implementing it on their respective procurement digital services.\r
\r
Commission Decision (EU, Euratom) 2017/46 of 10 January 2017 on the security of communication and\r
information systems in the European Commission:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1548093747090&uri=CELEX:32017D0046\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d8634e8c-04f0-41e6-bc1b-fb046b50567a .

