    cav:value "100" .

camssa:a4b8192e-ea1e-4217-9327-fed99f6d692f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The main objective of the Portable Document Format (PDF) is to allow text format and images to be independent and work for any software, hardware or operating system while transferring. Additionally, PDF is widely used by administrations in order to share their information and data. Fostering the availability of data and information, PDF fosters the data portability by means of documents. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b1fb3b4f-6fd0-4873-b3d3-ee6ba13eac73 .

camssa:a4b9a157-90ff-4cbd-9616-13580484819d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:a4c04565-33c4-4d30-a66b-a530a0c26f76 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CPOV is publicly available for its use and implementation. Moreover, it is available for everyone to study with no cost on Joinup webpage.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82c80db2-d2a5-481a-9ee6-a9d61704192e .

camssa:a4c0eb2f-37fa-4987-9ef1-eed8ddaba52d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'No Member State includes the ShEx in their national catalogue with Their National\r
Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories 1. Conceptual model for integrated\r
public servicesprovision, 2. interoperability layers, and 3. interoperability principles.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d75e8d53-cb87-4086-aaf7-827dc8c09d5c .

camssa:a4c1bf7e-b903-4a83-8c9a-eccd72862fa9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to principle 3.2 from the E-ARK CSIP specification, information packages should ensure that data and metadata are physically separated from one another in order to allow digital preservation tools and systems to update respective data or metadata portions of an Information Package without endangering the integrity of the whole package, therefore, addressing the implementation of mechanisms to guarantee data integrity.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP principle 3.2:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#principle3.2:'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:086239db-5754-437d-94d8-3184561f7ffa .

camssa:a4c4710b-33d4-4a0f-a5af-7cca82dac28e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e62f07fe-0769-45d1-80ba-4eccf851833c .

camssa:a4c6b66a-aad5-4408-a0d0-a49af0d20d48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData is a protocol of querying and sharing, and as such is not supposed to offer long-term preservation of data. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d32a11c-3348-4f29-ace7-af37283c9eb7 .

