camssa:a57b631d-4c54-4024-9ae4-96dedf1f7324 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Authentication Header (AH) and Encapsulating Security Payload (ESP) protocols, which can be used with IPv4, ensure that transmitted data has not been modified by anyone. Additionally, mechanisms such as Access Control Lists (ACLs) ensure that only authorised individuals have access to and can modify the data.

AH and ESP protocols:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/zos/2.1.0?topic=ipsec-ah-esp-protocols

IPv4 ACL:
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst2960l/software/15-2_6_e/configuration_guide/b_1526e_consolidated_2960l_cg/m_sec_acls_cg_danube_2960l_cdb.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23882d07-9547-4742-81e6-6660ce6f8668 .

camssa:a57e99fc-bc5b-4ab1-9a5b-1ca21d7a8e48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:193710e1-94e0-4468-9607-16b49395ef53 .

