camssa:a5d0fd00-de56-4d1c-b2b9-18d19baa5ca1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the specification is not listed in catalogues of the European Standardisation (CEN, CENELEC, ETSI), the OpenPM2 is highly recommended and promoted within European organisations. It is published within the Publications Office website, and also it is included within ISA2 catalogue of solutions, which can be considered as a set of solutions (specs included) that are standardised at the European level.\r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home\r
\r
OpenPM2 reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-search\r
\r
ISA2 Solution Page:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/open-pm2_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66b5a6b2-ef33-47f3-a217-db9a7c32a096 .

camssa:a5d2db92-951c-4cea-8e6a-85bb23d40e7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"EU Member States' trusted lists were established in the EU and aimed primarily at supporting the validation of advanced electronic signatures supported by a qualified certificate and advanced electronic signature supported by both a qualified certificate and by a secure signature creation device, as far as they included as minimum trust service probided supervised/accredited for issuing qualified certificates. This method can explicitly address and enable the secure and trustworthy exchange of data as it is using an advanced electronic signature which is supported by a qualified certificate and a secure signature creation device.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b64017f8-737b-421b-a01d-224dedd28881 .

camssa:a5d313b2-2126-4255-8b77-a3809b39d7c3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a18abe4842e04b608025fd70e54c3db5c2a10130c0dab0495479e7d5effb55d ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:a5e2739b-4428-4302-b39a-45ec1245e2c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of RDF is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31d16256-fa0b-4d11-8f15-c48b9aa4ba5c .

camssa:a5e463b7-83e9-45b9-91a0-c8877ca8966b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of LDAP is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b00b3c61-3d78-44aa-8ead-f5e355d96cd4 .

camssa:a5e8a5a3-811d-4e66-913c-3c54fdfb28fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ETSI TS 119 612 is not related to enabling the visibility of administrative procedures, rules, data and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3776ea08-fcc9-404d-9288-18ee5c6db588 .

camssa:a5ee399e-cbb0-490f-9c84-ae13b839b366 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XSD 1.1 is an Open specification which is implied in the validation of XML documents. As XML is a de-facto standard implied in in the creation of solutions, including innovative ones, XSD is also fostering the creation of innovative solutions. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89af2e86-aa46-497f-a2ea-e5864b192a76 .

camssa:a5f2f9bc-f8b8-4ce3-b538-88792214cc08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData is tied up to RESTful APIs communication. Although the OData service declares its own data model in a machine-readable form, which allows customers to interact with the service on a generic basis, OData relies on RESTful APIs in order to be implemented.

OData reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html#_Toc31358832'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:514f0947-5c91-4d61-b59d-03b060e02252 .

camssa:a5f708a1-e6db-4531-9bbd-9401e06e7d59 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 is a messaging protocol for exchanging information in a structured way, it provides endpoints that foster the availability of interfaces containing data from internal information systems of a public administration.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  \r
\r
Differences in SOAP Versions:\r
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSAW57_8.5.5/com.ibm.websphere.nd.multiplatform.doc/ae/cwbs_soapverdiffs.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a76481f-3f20-442c-8f23-5a93e6be53f5 .

camssa:a6064620-5f98-4350-b149-43c1da3dd7f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GITB TDL does not deal with personal data protection given that its purpose is to provide a language for interoperability and conformance testing. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51fd1aa0-c315-4bb1-8815-8dc0ce737081 .

camssa:a60c807d-f6aa-40f4-8014-66945058e9a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The conformance of implementations of the AKN4EU specification can be assessed using a number of different tools and methods. One approach is to use validation tools that check the syntax and structure of documents to ensure that they conform to the specification. Another approach is to conduct interoperability tests to ensure that systems can properly exchange documents using the specification.  \r
\r
 \r
Regarding the conformance of the implementation: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/nifo_en.     \r
 \r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32ce0ac9-5d96-4f5c-8a94-65a1339aec83 .

camssa:a60cbecb-e92b-454b-a9fd-2be1c41bc12a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

