camssa:a83fb32d-657b-456a-a5fc-60bc970868db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this core Vocabulary is not related to ensuring the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c6f8224-5ed7-4b33-846c-489f9cfd8f2e .

camssa:a8437d21-9023-4e53-a981-13a0d8de6bde a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification provides SASL authentication mechanisms. By authenticating the client, the system can then determine what level of access to grant. 

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d70d19f-7c0c-46d0-9792-4957e57a7656 .

camssa:a8479350-5864-4dca-88d5-b3d77e08bfd1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition.\r
\r
The specification allows cross-domain single sign-on, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. By using SAML 2.0, avoid the user to deal with several credentials nor provide information twice.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7352b059-d255-4af5-8c5d-db105bd70b63 .

