camssa:a8d6c820-6caf-46fa-9c1e-07be3937bda6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is designed to be extensible, meaning that users can introduce custom elements, semantics, and \r
vocabulary to meet their specific requirements. This extensibility allows for the adaptation of ODRL to a wide \r
range of use cases and industries.\r
\r
A clear example of customizations is Core Vocabularies, which define a set of general requirements that \r
could fit in any context and allow for the customization to fit specific business requirements in the \r
implementation.\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93c128a4-a943-4459-bff9-cfe60d84a23e .

