camssa:aa870394-eaf1-4375-aba2-bc7dc8523d51 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although it is mostly suited for public administrations, ETSI TS 119 512 protocols can be implemented in any business domains.  For example, the specification uses different preservation schemes that build the so-called preservation profiles (see eIDAS reference)\r
\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:822db373-5487-4901-9e44-84a325416065 .

camssa:aa9386cc-c4cd-4b33-bab0-294a63cea43b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF specifications are made available free of charge to the general public via the website. IETF drafts are published publicly discussions take place online in archived mailing lists. Moreover, the IETF Datatracker is the day-to-day front-end to the IETF database for people who work on IETF standards. It contains data about the documents, working groups, meetings, agendas, minutes, presentations, and more, of the IETF.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/\r
\r
http://www.ietf.org/id-info/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02e89e99-9fa2-404c-883e-e971310e11e3 .

camssa:aa9b01eb-dafc-4c0e-80bf-e0395672adfe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aaa17b14-ba3d-44e0-8807-9000838dd0c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS as a profile of DCAT, is an RDF vocabulary for representing data catalogues that allows data owners to provide metadata about the datasets they publish. By describing catalogues, datasets and resources, a publisher makes them easily searchable and discoverable.\r
\r
Following the previous statement it can be said that ADMS can simplify the delivery of European public services.\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0a54658-3230-49db-86e4-41c97879176d .

