camssa:ab0105cf-f48d-43b0-9063-5e772d7111ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to this specification, IDS connectors request a digitally signed JSON web token (JWT) from a central International Data Space (IDS) component called Dynamic Attribute Provisioning Service (DAPS) in order to authenticate themselves. Without these DAPS tokens called Dynamic Attribute Token (DATs), no connector can participate in the IDS. For this reason, DAPS is only meant to be used as a whole.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:905f10be-9ae4-44cc-855f-019b1cb0d4c5 .

camssa:ab0d641c-81fb-4763-9090-3caa2466b25f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EIRA has been successfully used together with eGovERA in several initiatives at national level, and in some of them, included privacy aspects. These privacy aspects come from EIRA, and as the process of analysis and design evolve, the building blocks are specialised making use of the flexibility. This fact helps these initiatives to ensure their specific needs are covered. Some of these projects can be found in the Interoperability Architecture Solutions collection in the Interoperable Europe Portal. 

Interoperability Architecture Solutions Success Stories: 
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira/success-stories

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac1d53a8-c005-408a-8890-ba67396ec8bf .

camssa:ab12cae0-7610-4326-b0ef-1965aa908fbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 has been included within several European cross-border initiatives as can be read in the European Interoperability Architecture (EIA) called Common Vision for an EIA. \r
\r
e-SENSE, e-PSOS or SPOCS are initiatives that implemented SOAP 1.2 in order to carry out their purposes. All the projects are related to the enhancement of interoperability between European administrations across borders and across sectors. \r
\r
ETSI SR 019 050 Reference where SOAP is included:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_sr/019000_019099/019050/01.01.01_60/sr_019050v010101p.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bada31dd-feea-44ce-bb74-7539bace2bcd .

camssa:ab1b3c30-8556-47e3-9d32-f272d0b6311a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7828e870-65de-4173-a5a4-1c535f5ea14a .

