camssa:ab559176-2bf5-4e6d-9104-3a5cd7a10581 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISAE 3402 depends on NIA 402 and ISAE 3000. ISAE 3402 states that assurance engagements should be \r
performed in accordance with the ISAE 3000 standard.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 exposure draft:\r
 https://www.ifac.org/system/files/uploads/Trans/ISAE%203402%20(definitiva%202013).pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c72fdcb-fc9b-4a70-8cae-1858f388c841 .

camssa:ab58a97c-b704-4b6e-b4b2-9c69b4c5c072 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:ab58dd35-f03b-4eaa-81b8-1fee063b1a30 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 provides the essential physical and data link layers that enable devices to communicate effectively. However, while IEEE Std 802.3-2022 is crucial for data transmission, it does not directly facilitate the modelling and optimization of business processes; therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58a1e848-a739-4104-b23b-7c9681157d6a .

camssa:ab5a0975-7f79-4f4e-bdfa-9c00492664bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP Cookies allow for partial implementations depending on the needs and requirements of the webpage on which it is implemented. For example, a developer can manage the user's session and not make use of the web tracking functionality.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-5.2\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:afb9c2c5-29c3-42e0-92ed-6efc477aaae9 .

camssa:ab5c584f-96ef-4b25-a003-58ae7d442096 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol supports the publication of data on the web by providing a framework that balances the need for open data access and collaboration with the requirements for security, compliance, and data sovereignty. It enables organizations to share data in a controlled manner, fostering innovation within secure and trusted data ecosystems. Some of the most relevant standards reused in this protocol include: DCAT for dataset deployment, ODRL for usage control and HTTPS for secure transfering.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0519e2b-afd4-49df-9fe6-08f3b1727907 .

camssa:ab60a106-5bd9-419c-9f90-b9d1e1a17b71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0866298b-1adb-443d-afd4-f8b8c5662a98 .

camssa:ab60d075-4096-4f7c-9c49-a01cf48a36f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cd828c0ec9887027bdb6b981560bde593cda27c080298ab36323ba5441ba4c31 ;
    cav:value "100" .

