camssa:ab6a64c8-e085-48b5-ab71-16cae283f009 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPv4 is a protocol that allows the exchange of data through the internet, therefore, the specifications fosters the data portability. Moreover, the European Commission launched in 2012 a programme to ensure the coexistence and the proper transition to the new version of internet protocol.\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/MEMO_12_414"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac363fb0-9c25-4ed2-a925-66553172b2d1 .

camssa:ab6d64e9-42d2-4455-a067-d2d6979ab2b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. So it can be said that SVG is independent of any specific technology or platform.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7e4c446-5fe6-43d3-ae73-f5f433c794c3 .

camssa:ab6d7a16-b5fb-415c-bb00-b3e57fe3e52b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:ab703c0a-a18e-490f-b85f-08d7d7ae7ca0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA allows extension as long as each implementation fully supports all required functionality of the specification exactly as specified. Cloud services execution and their lifecycle management are dependent on the availability of all the TOSCA corresponding artefacts (deployment and implementation artefacts) in all cloud environment use cases.\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Artifact types section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969466\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Conformance section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969508'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d95a0710-7b15-4e51-9bf8-16719b260b4b .

camssa:ab7286c1-de53-4ae4-b5de-5a07aeb7c747 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification allows the exchange of authentication and authorization data between parties. It is mainly used to ensure single sign-on (SSO).  It extends SSO across security domains independently from any platform which prevents non-interoperable proprietary technologies. For instance, a relevant implementation of SAML 2.0 is SAML Web Browser SSO profile. This profile was specified to promote interoperability by allowing the authentication to service providers through external identity providers. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f074ca69-1a10-4f2b-bf0c-4386a0c21e9d .

camssa:ab7c471c-346b-486e-b594-342d4f701e9d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Every time the protocol is used, the whole information needed has to be rewritten and re-provided to maintain the protocol secure.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:efb95cfb-c4cf-4f77-aede-32ca37770225 .

camssa:ab7c529c-9e05-46d2-b267-15540c232a8a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

