        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-02333ef99fbcb4f101a106bcf97c9559888756b085b1729b7c2ac9626dc4bc63 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ab8c95a6-d5bd-4e97-8e58-16d28b1fb897 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is intended to identify a country, dependencies and special areas of geographical interest. This specification relates to metadata, and can be used in any system that ingests metadata. Therefore, it can be considered platform-agnostic.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9e05b9c-2141-44fd-a75f-06aa7dead25c .

camssa:ab8e3f6b-27f0-40d9-b4ae-1aa0f1be3df9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ab8ec984-ffd6-4886-bdf3-0607be4093ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of BFO is not related to data accuracy. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9552720-f223-4025-97d8-22869f742f1d .

camssa:ab95e1dd-8dc2-443e-9721-2a8cb6ece508 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA does not foresee any public review. As defined on the OASIS Topology and Orchestration Specification for Cloud Applications (TOSCA) Technical Committee (TC), only this TC is involved in the release lifecycle of the specification. External contribution to this committee is possible through the Comment List.\r
\r
OASIS TOSCA TC reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep\r
\r
Mail Lists and Comments reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=tosca#feedback'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b416da53-3dbc-489c-b4c7-0023be328dce .

camssa:ab99bba4-eb99-4841-b10c-758800c6a66b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are already existing studies and documentation assessing different RDF features. For example, there is a study assessing the effectiveness and efficiency of RDF queries. As well there are studies focused on specific topics as is the fact of using RDF in the Smart Cities Modelling. \r
See: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221466941_Effective_and_Efficient_Entity_Search_in_RDF_Data \r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1045926X1730246X"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfa86289-030d-48c5-9aac-7e0ee1c4b48e .

camssa:ab9a9219-9297-4bfc-853d-d939c2995fc8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalDocML is XML based, however, it is not dependent on any other technology or platform, so it can be implemented independently from specific technologies or platforms.\r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abdd6482-3379-4c21-bb88-9364a9cdf16f .

camssa:ab9fdabf-079e-43b0-9552-d403dcb67ad0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML is publicly available for implementation and study for free on W3C's webpage. \r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d79eaf2-2df7-48fe-a61f-be6743fef28e .

