camssa:abeac71c-b307-4c2a-b5d3-8c0996205b3a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TrainingDML-AI Standard does not explicitly address the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Its primary focus is on the development of a UML model and encodings for geospatial machine learning training data. However, the detailed metadata provided by the TrainingDML-AI Standard could potentially be used to inform such procedures and rules, particularly in the context of preparing and managing training data for AI/ML applications.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3b7bec6-a104-4cf6-9457-4c469cf5360d .

camssa:abeb6cb4-f8e2-4829-a088-9d467295bd50 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:abeb8c13-f0a7-4ebc-a6d3-5ef143f26465 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By using ADMS to describe assets/solutions, the administrations ensure and enhance the visibility of these solutions and assets that are involved in the development of EU administrations’ activity. \r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0ff23a6-abe6-4a98-9158-299466d67964 .

camssa:abed2782-33d3-4eed-9f13-f5bb18a3441b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is not directly designed to enable digital service delivery channels. Instead, syslog is primarily used for the collection and centralization of log messages from various devices and applications within an IT infrastructure. 

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20f57ae5-f10e-4af6-8bf5-a612d935e172 .

camssa:abf8e8cc-db66-4687-9f18-b87ba271892e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The term of CAdES was first introduced in 2005 as CMS Advanced Electronic Signatures (CAdES) on ETSI Technical specifications. In 2008 was introduced in IETF webpage as a copy of the ETSI specification. So, it is mature enough for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
ETSI TS 101 733 V1.6.3 (2005-09):\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/01.06.03_60/ts_101733v010603p.pdf\r
\r
IETF CAdES:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5126.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81f12b31-97e6-45c9-a246-2b63a1d0d4ca .

camssa:abf90fee-e954-4638-a05f-4fd54b796829 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a67ecbc29e70e62b18dba3ae4f8d1f91d5b3196777dbf8b58c6713cd517eb768 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:abfb4901-bdbe-44a5-81ec-866385817e5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP specification does not address or provide any insights into the modeling of business processes.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:427fe495-a4ad-44df-b617-6d487b48f11a .

camssa:abfd8444-8519-4ab0-a4e5-bd6e4fdf48aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) develops solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks.\r
\r
Specification development process by the ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications\r
\r
Detailed document ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e46fafd-cf62-4390-b104-7ff429d4c119 .

