camssa:ac320a7d-a220-4d3f-8808-4e6661ef3886 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 specification is distributed from the ETSI platform. ETSI supports European regulations and legislation through the creation of Harmonised European Standards. ETSI’s mission is to provide platforms where interested parties come together and collaborate on the development and promotion of standards  for Information and Communication Technology (ICT) systems and services.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:80e381ab-bb33-416e-ae1f-e35d73149646 .

camssa:ac335188-d4a1-46ce-9db2-fb578916ef6d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the version being assessed is not included in the ICT technical specification in itself, the version 1.0 of the specification was already identified and included within this list of specifications that are compliant with the standardisation regulation for being user in eProcurement. Moreover, the SMP has been the basis for the development of the CEF eDelivery Building Block which helps public administrations to exchange electronic data and documents with other public administrations, businesses and citizens, in an interoperable, secure, reliable and trusted way.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEF eDelivery Building Block:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/inea/sites/inea/files/building_block_dsi-introdocument_edelivery_v1_00.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:620f1388-6e9f-4856-9811-ffe6005401c7 .

camssa:ac363fb0-9c25-4ed2-a925-66553172b2d1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
