camssa:acb31384-9b26-4b7c-8d70-f75ee65846c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OGC TrainingDML-AI standard is a developing framework with the goal of offering a universal language
for describing AI models and their data. Although still in the process of widespread adoption, it has undergone multiple iterations and testing phases. Despite its current limited usage, there is potential for it to enhance the development of AI-driven digital solutions, especially as several OGC members are interested in developing similar standards. Moreover, the specification encompasses published documentation regarding supporting processes like change management and release management.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://www.opengeospatial.org/standards/trainingdml-ai

OGC Member List:
https://www.ogc.org/about-ogc/ogc-member-list/

OGC Technical Committee Policies and Procedures reference:
http://docs.opengeospatial.org/pol/05-020r29/05-020r29.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1cd63f5e-d5c1-46d0-9f5b-2301aaa79e2e .

camssa:acb49da2-40c1-4363-ae07-2e9979f61f65 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """In the context of eSignatures and Seals, the European Commission has stated an Implementing decision (2015/1506)  where urged the Member States and other Public services providers to recognise CAdES, PAdES, XAdES, and ASIC as formats for electronic signatures purposes. \r
  \r
See: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32015D1506 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3976d27-317c-4f02-bb86-9dc9f56d5e4a .

camssa:acb650f5-e465-459b-b2c2-b186b7c118fc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:acbd4eea-e2b6-4448-9513-d383ee17ae7e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML can be used independently from any other technical specifications or operating system.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e71ff7d7-df24-4c8d-b545-590c695d3335 .

camssa:acbd8a44-a3b1-424a-9e72-b8f6acf2ff40 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:acbee341-183f-4b75-ab56-c6114bef0a4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP involves storing copies of responses to reduce server load and improve response times by the catching method. While primarily intended for performance optimisation, caching can indirectly contribute to preservation by creating redundant copies of content, though not for long-term retention.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Caching, RFC 9111 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46a728c2-d5df-477d-9914-22874a526367 .

camssa:acc0ef6e-f16c-4eff-b0af-eeeca2a040bb a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "None"^^xsd:anyURI .

