camssa:ad12588c-a1b9-431c-be37-1d7287f8dfa1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WSDL helps to describe and make available administration’s web services, which contain public data and information to be reused. The data is structured as WSDL is an XML based language. Taking into account these facts, WSDL is supporting several maturity levels from Tim Berners Lee’s 5 stars schema for Open Data.  \r
\r
Additionally, there are existing W3C recommendation and notes regarding the semantics on WSDL.  Known as Semantic Annotations Web Services Description Language (SAWSDL). As well, a technical report from the Web Services Description Working Group that maps the representation of the WSDL model in RDF. \r
\r
See: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/ \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20-rdf/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/sawsdl/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d35179d-ab24-4b7f-b3c0-9f8bf9ace289 .

camssa:ad1332d3-98f9-414c-bc47-f341e20dc159 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:ad1452ac-4abd-4324-a438-abc9fbdcb7e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The European Parliament demonstrates its strong commitment to better law-making principles, as outlined in the new Interinstitutional Agreement on Better Law-Making (IIA-BLM), reinforcing the goal of enhancing transparency in public policy and law-making while increasing the visibility of public administration decision-making processes.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

IIA-BLM briefing:
https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2016/579076/EPRS_BRI(2016)579076_EN.pdf#:~:text=The%20new%20Interinstitutional%20Agreement%20on%20Better%20Law-Making%2C%20adopted,initially%20presented%20its%20proposal%20on%2019%20May%202015.

Objective of Better Regulation Toolbox:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation_en#what-is-better-regulation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7cb2638-cecd-4dfa-a2d2-2c247bf0e345 .

camssa:ad149fa4-bc19-4fca-9325-bc86bc8d1b56 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:ad1cf1b2-1aad-43aa-b26b-90b624070410 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:ad1e7c26-745e-4d02-a432-3205c2aea625 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of ELI is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. Moreover, not informacion has been found to support the positive or negative answer to this criterion. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:14907729-ba57-4884-93b3-1a25b5d66975 .

camssa:ad1f1119-a3cb-4ad6-8ddb-028a32a23e25 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP is designed to be platform agnostic. This design has been crucial for HTTP widespread adoption and ability to connect diverse systems across the internet.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP versions usage:
https://blog.cloudflare.com/http3-usage-one-year-on/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c612c136-d871-4bc6-9f54-584ca55bcdbc .

camssa:ad22d152-1969-4cb7-8f0d-e2b7c774f0e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Ogg is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96ea59bc-c7f0-455a-a8b4-b50c99018fc6 .

camssa:ad279fff-9e15-448d-9ddd-5b18eeb2fffc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of RDF helps to the reduction of the administrative burden by easing the publication and reuse of the administration's data. The publication of administrations' data allows the consumption by stakeholders avoiding extra steps while information is needed. In addition, the availability of public information fosters the development of efficient eGovernment and the reduction of administrative burden. \r
\r
Additionally, its availability for free is as well an interesting point on the reduction of administrative burden."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:38b0fda1-1bf6-45d2-9c20-5120d24a17cc .

camssa:ad2cdb4e-6d66-498d-adfc-c7c347c1b889 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ad302d63-016d-4623-940b-8f4d69323a71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently there are assessments regarding the specification effectiveness, The IDTA initiative provides the relevant information regarding the efficiency of the specification. This assessments where presented in the Smart Production Solutions in Nuremberg in the fall of 2024.

IDTA in Smart Production Solutions fair:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/news-dates/idta-shows-at-sps-in-nuremberg-how-consistent-data-flow-is-ensured-throughout-the-entire-lifecycle-6600

IDTA reference:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:261bea02-2e1e-4ccc-9c44-0ed2837301ef .

camssa:ad34ac25-19d0-4396-8d6a-cb84fc613cce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of UBL, operates under RF (royalty-free) \r
on RAND Mode of the UBL IPR Policy. Therefore, the specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
OASIS Intellectual Property Rights Policy, section 10.2.2:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/\r
\r
UBL Intellectual Property Rights policy: \r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html#S-IPR-POLICY'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9552eaf0-6604-4cfe-b0f2-e5ab308859fc .

camssa:ad37da3d-ff11-417c-bc74-0f84606f5bb2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ad3f5877-c311-44b3-b017-ae3b8015426a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ad4637a8-e528-4cdd-b418-3cb2a4ccc829 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ad52862b-9535-4e34-9992-7b86ffc5d8a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "JSON is a data-interchange format is used by APIs, which are involved in the delivery of information between platforms, and in consequence service delivery. This fact makes JSON an element that fosters de delivery of European Public services, including multilingual ones."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6def4127-2db9-49dc-83f9-e635d3ffb21a .

camssa:ad536b39-5e63-44f0-8896-d43be88fe4cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'An ebXML RegRep stores any type of electronic content, such as text documents, images, sound or video, and provides a set of protocols enabling data transfer among systems. For example, ebMS (part of the broader ebXML framework) contributes by providing the header structure necessary for message exchange over AS4.

OOTS AS4 reference:
https://code.europa.eu/oots/tdd/tdd_chapters/-/tree/86290aa801fb9a8e56486fc49019addcc1321a95/OOTS-EDM/xml/Request-Response%20Samples

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df39c041-0e78-467f-9efb-00680ad83c60 .

camssa:ad53be28-8688-42db-b254-a12879b79cf8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This document does not define a cross-sector reusable data model, but gives public organizations a model for building their own open source solutions to enable successful future reuse by similar public organizations in other places.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01a55022-a8e7-47d8-993c-c3bd538edcdc .

camssa:ad5c2516-cb0d-4139-bb26-26952630153b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification can be used independently from specific vendor products."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8193098a-893c-43a8-bad9-3e418e836b9c .

camssa:ad6290b4-f21c-4f21-bda0-4a442131d38b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Coherence of the technical specification is evidenced by the fact that there is no existing European standard or technical specifications being under consideration to become a European standard that has a similar area of application.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a303089e-49de-4880-997e-bdcc7c02382e .

camssa:ad66e52b-16ae-4994-9b4a-ce9ed3fd6cf5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification being assessed is a sector agnostic specification that is able to be reused when structured data needs to be exchanged. Additionally, CSV is designed to enable you to reuse the same schema when publishing multiple CSV files, even if those files are created by different organisations and therefore reside in different places."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07faed28-0ca0-487b-b777-b4e3658b64cc .

camssa:ad6f53e6-cf0b-4cfd-806e-4abd500aa5ea a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ad71ef4f-af0e-4f8c-91c5-e35cc250f858 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:ad724efb-5ef2-4672-b02c-1beeabefd1f3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6f7b3377cc1836eb056d44786260085e36fc1d6856a3aa3d37fe017e16cfc319 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ad79e39d-41de-4ee7-8b65-e9b15658db6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Access control, which involves determining who can access specific resources or perform certain operations, is typically addressed at the implementation and deployment levels rather than within the WSDL specification. Access control mechanisms are often implemented in the runtime environment or the infrastructure supporting the web service.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6d94ebe-4ddd-405b-8079-e494451b2850 .

camssa:ad7e7030-37ee-40c3-8e1c-9116cfbd2e88 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

