camssa:adbecff2-3771-4824-a4df-fd339fca37b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA v1.0 was released in 2013, including the XML schema that users are meant to use when deploying their IT infrastructure (see TOSCA wiki reference, Quick Links and Older Technical Work sections). Two minor releases, TOSCA v1.1 and TOSCA v1.2 were published in 2017 (see OASIS TOSCA TC reference, TOSCA in 2018 and beyond section). In 2020, TOSCA v1.3 prescribed TOSCA v1.2, and changed its name to TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML v1.3. The specification has a draft version of TOSCA v2.0 which aims at easing the portability of cloud applications and services. Additionally, the specification provides OASIS TOSCA TC-independent technical reports and documents/platforms proving its usefulness in the industry (see TOSCA wiki reference, Quick Links section), showing its maturity in the market. \r
\r
TOSCA wiki reference, Quick Links section:\r
https://wiki.oasis-open.org/tosca/FrontPage\r
\r
OASIS TOSCA TC reference, Older Technical Work section:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=tosca#technical\r
\r
TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML reference, section 1.2:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969412\r
\r
TOSCA Draft Version 2.0 reference, section 1.2:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA/v2.0/csd03/TOSCA-v2.0-csd03.html#_Toc56506175\r
\r
OASIS TOSCA TC reference, TOSCA in 2018 and beyond section:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=tosca#2018'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b69e7fcc-7f12-4e6d-98e3-a44059cf929d .

camssa:adc201d6-6fc9-40d1-ab86-754849aff211 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SHACL can be implemented across various platforms and systems that support RDF, making it versatile and adaptable to different technological environments. Its ability to validate RDF graphs ensures data integrity and consistency, which is valuable across multiple domains and platforms. Therefore, the specification is platform agnostic.

SHACL Platform and Technology agnostic:
https://medium.com/fluree/what-is-shacl-with-examples-2697f659d465

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d891ca2-e44c-4fef-97fe-9bc7796738b1 .

camssa:adc2fbe8-6fa1-460d-8cf2-e2375307906d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is included in 10 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. Some examples of Member States including SOAP on their catalogues are the Netherlands, Spain or France.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f2601519-3c08-4a07-ac4c-34e0ccc59aaf .

camssa:adc879e2-701d-4956-894c-0512bba61d9c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c967c90bfc7bc13426924eca012de349ae51d4e8f652fe64bfbec2cccc8c8146 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:adc9b1bd-c211-4889-9c73-795cf33846d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, UTF-8 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision. During the evaluation process, all the Member States are invited to share their doubts. The positive evaluation of UTF-8 and its identification is considered an interoperability agreement.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b35095b-d561-4bfa-ae70-aea0336acdd4 .

camssa:add0385f-bf20-4bc0-8715-2aa5a6d6d2f9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d7be9f0dd52944e6c25f5469c86355a42ae446838bd9759b4986d21f7db4814b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:add3b5ad-f707-4e5f-b3c2-8fdeafe3cafe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL was developed by IBM, Microsoft, and Ariba initially in 2000. The following version was at their charge as well, introducing minor changes. The last version became a W3C recommendation in 2007. Nowadays, the international organisation is maintaining and developing WSDL. \r
\r
Moreover, it continues having support from companies with a wide market share. Therefore, it is demonstrated that WSDL has enough market acceptance and maturity for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
WSDL report:\r
https://xml.coverpages.org/wsdl.html\r
\r
Implementation of WSDL in smart city Internet of Things:\r
https://europepmc.org/article/MED/37521954\r
\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6c67412-a923-423d-9635-966b24aa0340 .

camssa:ade33ffc-ca78-40fe-9376-314762b360c7 a cav:Score,
