camssa:ae2353a9-9bdd-4849-9f74-ae2a8d0f8ed8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a vocabulary, the implementation of CLV can be tested using methods like SHACL shapes and using semantic reasoners to ensure that the implementation is well-formed. These validation mechanisms can be used with open source tools or lite versions of tools like GrapghDB or Protégé.

SHACL validation:
https://graphdb.ontotext.com/documentation/free/shacl-validation.html#what-is-shacl-validation

Semantic Reasoners List:
http://owl.cs.manchester.ac.uk/tools/list-of-reasoners/

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d68a091d-7d44-4067-b831-f1c73d15d653 .

camssa:ae23bb5d-92ea-4d70-8a94-e9b360234b5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV has significant market acceptance in the European context for two main factors, institutional support and adoption by government entities and member states such as Spain, or the Netherlands.

CPOV Spain national catalogue: 
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/ctt/verPestanaActivosSemanticos.htm?idIniciativa=3351

EU Vocabularies:
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/corevocs

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3de25230-823a-4d15-8aa5-d1f2fd54a9e8 .

camssa:ae24bf1c-fee8-4355-8024-a6514a821bc7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"UTF-8 allows for partial implementations since it's a variable-length encoding scheme that can represent any Unicode character using one to four bytes. Systems that use UTF-8 encoding can choose to implement only a subset of the Unicode character set, but this may limit their ability to handle text data from different languages and scripts.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dbabc843-57a2-4149-bfc9-0b2e3f66eb88 .

camssa:ae24d8d8-b9c7-4651-9e4b-dbd283ac02e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PAdES has sufficient market acceptance for its use in the development of products. In the following link there is an example of integrating digital signatures like PAdES in a framework.\r
\r
Digital signature service:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:13392e49-41db-4338-96a4-a9dacfb6cdb1 .

camssa:ae2eb348-6a5b-46b4-9bd3-aa397e7fa80b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Transformational Government Framework (TGF) is supported by the TGF Technical Committee, which is responsible for overseeing the development, maintenance, and promotion of the framework.\r
\r
TGF Technical Committee:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=tgf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d41e9f1-a939-4908-b7c2-3117c7c1a68a .

camssa:ae2ec506-9618-467a-8036-7b4b45a1df48 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ae33ceba-00c9-49ea-855f-7f72f63eb2f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification provides features and guidelines that can help to support e-accessibility for legal documents. Specifically, the specification supports the use of structural markup and semantic tagging, which can help to facilitate the processing and presentation of legal documents in a variety of formats and contexts, including for users with disabilities.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d3f408a-1ba8-4911-b1a1-ac0d80af3741 .

camssa:ae39e973-151c-4f83-847f-abd2f3fe1e0d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are existing documentation and studies assessing and analysing the performance and efficiency of IPsec in different contexts and application areas. For instance ENISA provides documentation recommending the use of IPsec in order to improve security.\r
\r
Semantics Scholar, TCP/UDP network performance evaluation of various IPSEC algorithms:https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/8971/9848f632259138d5d4b1052ad24ede803625.pdf \r
\r
\r
ENISA reference, 'Algorithms, Key Sizes and Parameters Report' document:\r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/algorithms-key-sizes-and-parameters-report/at_download/fullReport\r
\r
ResearchGate, 'Interoperability Issues for VPN IPsec Solutions' document:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228437109_Interoperability_Issues_for_VPN_IPsec_Solutions\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4999d945-b9ab-4692-b696-a32396ed1141 .

camssa:ae3e5cbd-132d-4996-ab3f-da6e4ab7f771 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ae4037a4-af85-4c3f-9658-433448d7055d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are existing documentation and studies proposing the usage of ODRL as an efficient method for representing more fine-grained access policies for Linked Data. \r
\r
Also, there are studies that also checked the completion of the specification and its actual implementation and providing other formal semantics to improve the application of the specification and its purpose. \r
\r
Defining Expressive Access Policies for Linked Data using the ODRL Ontology 2.0:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Simon-Steyskal/publication/266652655_Defining_expressive_access_policies_for_linked_data_using_the_ODRL_ontology_20/links/565dc7a408aeafc2aac88d98/Defining-expressive-access-policies-for-linked-data-using-the-ODRL-ontology-20.pdf\r
\r
Formalising ODRL Semantics using Web Ontologies: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235902060_Formalising_ODRL_Semantics_using_Web_Ontologies"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72c42738-6d64-4db1-b256-d565694ce39c .

camssa:ae46df42-f4bb-4902-a01c-b756df2f7ffb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

