camssa:ae5368b8-3420-4636-a453-89c69fa7998a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is included in 8 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. Some examples of Member States including XSD on their catalogues are the Netherlands, Slovenia, Spain or Portugal.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
Spain National Catalogue:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:9e2c2877-5103-4934-8440-c60ba2e10c48\r
/Catalogue_of_Standards_NIF_Spain.pdf \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bec43efe-8b54-484c-aae2-a5cdf44e32e0 .

camssa:ae53868e-6b97-4188-83ec-798b6745afdb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GraphQL is a good enabler for the exposures of interfaces insofar it does not mandate a particular programming language or storage system for application services that implement it. Instead, application services take their capabilities and map them to a uniform language, type system, and philosophy that GraphQL encodes. This provides a unified interface friendly to product development and a powerful platform for tool-building.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:245a4058-6417-4383-bbca-4c6cfcd58cec .

camssa:ae53b7eb-d515-4628-a277-effd82760496 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All solutions developed in ISA² Programme are under ISA Open Metadata Licence which is perpetual, royalty-free and non-exclusive license to Use and re-Use the Works.\r
\r
ISA open metadata license:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/licence/isa-open-metadata-licence-v11"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7dbd094-be1a-4885-ace4-f84c51e3300f .

camssa:ae5426df-1468-4d10-801a-ed2a82c6e4ff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ae562ced-9a60-4c54-9ec9-900be0be08a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is associated with EIRA ABB's in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS).\r
It is associated with the ABB Binding Instrument and it's View is Legal. It is also associated with Legal Act Representation, Open Data and Representation of the Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v501\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b78f3c57-169d-4655-aea2-cbfd0007690c .

camssa:ae5642b7-fe45-47d5-8d26-ac4655cfaa1f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8954ddabf37f4899562b9ea4c8f0bbf204f3e48c9203043bc231f368092396a2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:ae567aa9-2598-4a86-a037-6eaced4fd8b8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4ac14cafe608f1dbe7e48f96edd7574c55f0aac2c2e99ede0418dae7225977af ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:ae5755d9-895c-4def-955b-003af3ae7a95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a protocol for data exchange, FTP allows the provision of data using an endpoint and therefore makes available interfaces of public administrations internal information systems.\r
\r
An example of implementation support this fact would be the Flemish initiative MAGDA. This initiative provides a platform that allows the different administrations to reuse the information contained within their registries. FTP has been selected by MAGDA to enable data exchange between the different registries. \r
\r
Magda Platform About: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/magda-platform/about\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5df50edc-1814-43e4-9fda-eab6145a83ce .

camssa:ae5a122e-3323-418a-92c8-1ae86535a6b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not specify if it ensures the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09727165-2422-41bc-ad9a-fed013ee5642 .

camssa:ae5d0223-dc97-4ba3-8fc5-93b12df2fe80 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ae646088-d007-4aae-b8dd-c374c60a23ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WSDL can be extended according to constraints defined in section 6 of the specification. This fact allows users to implement changes without hampering the interoperability and scalability of systems.  \r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl/#language-extensibility"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:210a5165-592f-4625-80c3-8d5be6687631 .

camssa:ae649643-08ee-4a4a-ad4a-bbdbe49e736f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ae675228-2a81-4273-a72d-3cd3091072d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"While genericode's first committee specification was published on the 28th of December of 2000, genericode is currently on its 1.0 version, last revised on the 31th of January of 2023. Furthermore, the submitting of Code List Representation (genericode) Version 1.0 OASIS Standard to ISO/IEC JTC1 was approved in 2023.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html

Approve submitting Code List Representation (genericode): 
https://groups.oasis-open.org/communities/community-home/digestviewer/viewthread?GroupId=1681&MessageKey=b519e373-2919-495d-a9b3-893ccc16e8b8&CommunityKey=7558fd85-f7ac-4dd7-b57b-018dc7d3f6f7\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:13191091-27cc-4f0c-b6cf-e5128ee7a614 .

camssa:ae679e0e-3308-4e10-be29-d8d07319354c a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/20abc7cc-a770-46d3-9d67-34a9b27934f4"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:ae6b1a1f-8790-491f-ad3c-2e387ba86b2f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:ae6c5fc6-a62b-4788-92f5-b3cc4833a41a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:ae725511-bb43-4224-8df8-4332d44047e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:29337072-27c9-458f-af71-0629d7fbb7f5 .

camssa:ae7a059a-a790-4417-b5f9-78e44ffacb6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SCIM may not be used for modeling broader business processes, it can be part of a larger ecosystem that includes business process modeling tools, identity and access management (IdAM) systems, and other components. In this context, SCIM serves a specific role in handling identity-related tasks within the broader framework of business operations. SCIM has several implementations that can facilitate the modelling of business processes.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b59a2aa6-d3c2-4b7c-9ce9-75c4d4dcdb69 .

camssa:ae7f822c-4290-49ed-ab0e-328a85742b4e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No formal interoperability agreement has been found involving European public services providers. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9fda2e4c-be26-4c1a-9d5f-32b60a5895b7 .

camssa:ae8708b6-7dc0-4373-8263-98cd26f811f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1f179c1d-653f-4f1f-87b4-2c71405d6833 .

camssa:ae8a282e-f19f-4b74-bc8c-7cf41847d6dc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS is a network protocol for transferring files over the Internet. It has the same specifications as FTP but it uses the Transport Layer Security (TLS) to secure the communications.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b91fa48-108b-464d-a326-9a4ac212b732 .

camssa:ae8b4e18-7cac-4e98-ab98-192238cff770 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ae93b8a1-5fdb-464f-92a8-b59a96de3184 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TSP is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose Member State NIF is fully aligned with at least 2 out of 3 sections of the EIF according to NIFO factsheets.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffe4cff6-30e3-4660-aaac-69cd8740b2ac .

camssa:ae9c02fe-6e69-401b-abdf-9002e199088e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The RDA website also collects expressions of interest from potential adopters via “Become an RDA Adopter” section  and encourages adopters to submit “Adoption Stories” . RDA has organised a series of webinars  focused on the adoption of the RDA Outputs & Recommendations encouraging dialogue and interaction and facilitating uptake."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0aefb9ad-e6fd-4fa1-b7bd-668dfe66cbbd .

camssa:ae9d7f39-5f45-4513-9922-68535e9f8f3d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all SEMIC services, SEMIC is the responsible for the maintenance and growth of the LDES development, as well as the community around it. In addition, SEMIC has launched a GitHub where contributions and discussions can be made freely.

SEMIC Joinup: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre

LDES GitHub: 
https://github.com/SEMICeu/LinkedDataEventStreams'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:623ad8d8-319a-4368-aae0-acdc166aa396 .

camssa:ae9ddd9f-eec6-422b-9084-88c36e4e5848 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EIRA includes mechanism to ensure that security and privacy is ensured when designing digital public services. It is done by providing architecture building blocks that address these specific topics, and also by considering all LOST views, ensuring traceability from legal requirements to technical. 

To go further in detail, there are specific enablers related to identify the requirements for identity and access management, which are the building blocks that will ensure that access to data is controlled. Additionally, elements such Trust enablers or blockchain can be consider assets and components that can help to ensure data integrity and data authenticity. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e1f4ba2-6886-48c1-9fc5-ec298532b0b8 .

camssa:ae9e538a-acaf-4938-a34f-b2a60e4e3356 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT specification does not address or facilitate organisational interoperability agreements.

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d88b39d-67bf-45d9-8cc2-b2fa24faf1d1 .

camssa:aea7d7e9-19a9-4b4c-8867-f152b4355109 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows for customization to a certain extent. It provides mechanisms that enable developers to define their own extensions, headers, and data types within the SOAP framework.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1781b34b-fe04-4c3e-84b0-09bf0da5684d .

camssa:aea9bdcb-a4cf-460c-8c66-f45b43967df6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aeac7646-8299-4204-944d-e65e5539d362 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification was carried out in 2001 and has been developed and maintained by OASIS. It has suffered 1 minor update (SAML 1.1) and a major one (SAML 2.0). This fact demonstrates the maturity of the specification that is being assessed. Moreover, it is also implemented by IT vendors and suppliers having a market dominance. For instance, SAML 2.0 is implemented by Microsoft for the Microsoft Azure Active Directory and by Amazon for Amazon Web Services. Therefore, it is demonstrated that SAML 2.0 has enough maturity and market acceptance for its use in the development of products and services."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f930afbe-1622-4409-a547-6c69a1803cb2 .

camssa:aeb0540c-c72b-4a2f-9f8e-eca0237ac657 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aeb2aa83-9887-4ae8-a06d-3f3e473002f3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aeb3333e-669f-4579-af17-edd40e0fc4f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While genericode itself primarily focuses on providing a standardised format for representing code lists and controlled values, it can indirectly contribute to the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services  by promoting clarity and consistency in how administrative procedures and rules are communicated and implemented, improving semantic richness, interoperability and integration of systems.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0e9996b-264c-45df-a7ce-a64e208be355 .

camssa:aebcfe95-eb67-4684-892a-803d552dcc03 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA specification does not deal with ensuring data processing accuracy or the integrity of data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e0024fb-fb31-4427-8246-2258ef58bbbd .

camssa:aec0dc4b-1eb9-4d15-9aae-f6e68aa7395f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of TOSCA as a European standard. \r
\r
ICT technical specifications: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue: \r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c758177c-e253-4a23-b856-dfb7a8adb9e5 .

camssa:aec26d49-06ee-4c49-b874-102203545f15 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aec4bcc4-9890-4318-8a9d-8eed8f39633b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After looking in the European Library of Interoperability Specifications, we can conclude UBL has not been mapped into the EIRA, although it is planned to be added in the Data Model ABB (semantic view).\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d18d73d7-c5b5-4e23-bf70-68574326a028 .

camssa:aed35436-4bf9-49f4-a482-3c1c981bcbfd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As most of the vocabularies, DCAT reuses several existing ones (e.g. "adms", "foaf") and the Resource Description Framework (RDF). This  results in a dependency that can hamper interoperability, especially in the case where new releases of the reused vocabularies are not backward compatible.                                                 \r
                                                                                                                    \r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/                \r
\r
ADMS reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/            \r
\r
FOAF reference:\r
http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb2eafdc-1b04-4dac-ba3b-641bb386c425 .

camssa:aed3e273-a51a-449d-b8ac-01dfd97989fd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:aed5a636-a4ef-4c98-a12e-75b317a08e20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including XSLT."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:97ad88c6-65f5-471f-86a3-43d94c787394 .

camssa:aed5becd-d059-447e-a2f4-ca86bf6c28b2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3c0edf049cd95575b46d688ed31be0ccce7a5822c5bcc22adf05d491f01f2780 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:aeda4538-11f1-4d45-ac64-b78abef4df2d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 conformance test is based on the Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement (PICS), is essential to ensure that a network device functions correctly and is interoperable with other devices on the network. This process, while not guaranteeing absolute interoperability, facilitates the identification of incompatibilities and ensures a level of confidence in adherence to the standard.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc0a5982-bb84-4c99-8fc3-84559bb4cd05 .

camssa:aedb44c0-4ecc-4b36-bc2c-f251d11b312f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "60" .

