camssa:af3281b8-f66b-47b1-9461-8c4b4f7e7b27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As it is stated in the "Implementation and Specification" document "The goal of domain names is to
provide a mechanism for naming resources in such a way that the names are usable in different hosts,
networks, protocol families, internets, and administrative organizations." Therefore, by allowing the
association of information with domain names, DNS facilitates their comprehension of data and services in a
network.

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499

Domain Names - Implementation and Specification: 
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035 '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5100e8be-95b1-4b64-8b8f-c4313583f9f0 .

camssa:af33ab34-51a8-4b0f-ba71-269689bd8f10 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:af3715b1-9e5d-4e4d-bca9-212bb108f875 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Verifiable Credentials can be used to represent different types of credentials, including those related to identity, qualifications, certifications, and more. The specification mentions that it is important to follow accessibility guidelines and standards, such as WCAG21, to ensure that all people, regardless of ability, can make use of this data. \r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/\r
\r
WCAG:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:991f0d2b-bf4f-4f27-80e9-fca1ff34505c .

camssa:af3f5cc7-bb6f-4fd1-99c8-09bed74afbf0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:671b1198-2a40-4386-b08b-20da3e54f651 .

camssa:af3fc2a2-6136-41ad-ac09-a697228ac5c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Tracking cookies, and especially third-party tracking cookies, are commonly used as ways to compile long-term records of individuals' browsing histories, a potential privacy concern that prompted European lawmakers to take action in 2011. For that concern legislation or regulations that cover the use of HTTP Cookies in the EU include The General Data Privacy Regulation (GDPR) and the ePrivacy Directive. With a global reach, these regulations apply to any site on the World Wide Web accessed by users under these jurisdictions.  \r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#creating_cookies\r
\r
GDPR reference:\r
https://gdpr-info.eu/\r
\r
ePrivacy Directive:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/LexUriServ/LexUriServ.do?uri=CONSLEG:2002L0058:20091219:EN:PDF\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7acca060-6681-4019-a6a4-af13ab85ddb4 .

camssa:af423873-aebd-4986-b8ff-27f8e1d65516 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:af45bb71-0b4d-418c-9420-f66e729c2600 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has been developed by the European Commission for its implementation across borders to improve the accountability and development of public policies and laws, in this sense the specification can be considered compliant with the different European Regulations.
Moreover, one of the main goals of the specification is to foster the consistency and proper development of the general public laws and policies.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6c7cfd0-21e8-4dec-9eaa-412bfaf6bdb2 .

camssa:af569025-2660-426d-9bfa-021bd891b759 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'[NOT FINAL ANSWER] The specification purpose is to help in the description of software, a metadata schema based on YAML. The publiccode.yaml file is the outcome of using the specification, and it is to be published in the repository where the solution is hosted. This allows the easy discoverability and automatic processing of solutions information, easing its reuse, evaluation or indexation in catalogues. 

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8fec777a-d13b-404a-8f52-81e72e52e3c7 .

camssa:af581f13-caf7-4a0c-b318-27e3a1015f53 a cav:Score,
