    cav:value "100" .

camssa:af73fc1f-4cd4-40a1-a644-3316dd254409 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML does not enable modern digital service delivery channels because it lacks the flexibility, multimedia
support, and responsiveness of newer web standards like HTML5. Therefore, XHTML is not suitable for
supporting the complex, interactive, and cross-platform digital services that public administrations need
today.

XHTML W3C reference
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:166502da-96f8-44fc-98ab-68ab030514b1 .

camssa:af7c170b-7b2b-48df-a0df-7409be292cf7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTPS is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:570facc8-a961-44e8-82fe-32089f6cf3b0 .

camssa:af8a110d-0d4a-42bb-8a17-8d1f7811db03 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TGF promotes the reuse of relevant information within and across government organisations. One of the core principles of the TGF is ""reuse before buy or build,"" which encourages organisations to leverage existing solutions, services, and data before developing new ones. It  provides guidance and best practices for identifying, assessing, and reusing existing information assets, such as data, documents, and processes, to improve efficiency and reduce costs. By promoting the reuse of relevant information, the TGF aims to improve collaboration and knowledge sharing within and across government organizations, and ultimately enhance the delivery of public services.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7929ce40-a011-415b-99ac-bb5500d35a44 .

camssa:af8b8a66-78f3-4941-b699-20c765194c29 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification's purpose is not related to privacy. Therefore, has not been found included in any initiative neither at European nor on national level covering privacy aspects.

GS CIM 009: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/CIM/001_099/009/01.07.01_60/gs_CIM009v010701p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d6a2a9ab-a4d3-400a-b893-089e37b833bf .

