camssa:aff4586c-88b7-4add-a018-42bea7ea6a62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has multiple methods to protect the information against unauthorised changes such as:\r
-Digital Signatures: SAML assertions and protocol messages can be digitally signed using XML Digital Signature.\r
-Message Encryption: SAML assertions can be encrypted for a specific recipient using XML Encryption. While encryption primarily ensures confidentiality, it also adds an additional layer of protection against tampering.\r
-Binding Profiles: Various SAML binding profiles, like the HTTP POST and Artifact bindings, have specific mechanisms to ensure the integrity and authenticity of the SAML messages transported using those bindings.\r
And more to be described.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ee50462-32d6-41c9-a5ca-97b5a762be69 .

