camssa:b075a807-9708-400a-bc57-3cd7aefd0b3b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are pieces of evidence that state OData is wide-spread and used (see OData ecosystem reference). Although there are some market alternatives to OData, such as GData (Google), it is worth to note that there is some evidence of OData as an innovative solutions creator. Moreover, the specification has a dedicated Github tailored by the Microsoft community.\r
\r
Stackshare-OData reference:\r
https://stackshare.io/odata/alternatives\r
\r
OData ecosystem reference:\r
https://www.odata.org/ecosystem/\r
\r
OData-Microsoft Github reference:\r
https://github.com/OData'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5bcb5127-adef-4e89-8317-13af42bbd4bb .

camssa:b0760e77-9f9f-415c-9640-4ffb01bab788 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP primary role is to provide a standardised framework for web communication by using a request response functions between servers and clients facilitating the access to websites. However, it does not specify how to structure administrative data or functions for interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26e360a4-9330-4e4e-8edf-635310ec9b11 .

camssa:b07c6e66-267c-4962-9a58-ffea31e87b63 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b07fac7c-5b40-4d17-bc9e-35a4df3cede4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of the  GITB TDL is to test the conformance and interoperability of specifications.  \r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/1.2.0/introduction/index.html#what-is-the-gitb-tdl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf256111-bace-4ebd-ae5d-b3b6b32466dd .

camssa:b0831b68-ad7a-493b-9743-4732fff0f7f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification does facilitate partial or incremental implementation by defining mandatory and optional components. It provides a foundational minimum level of implementation while allowing for additional fields to be included optionally for an extended configuration. This approach ensures flexibility, enabling adopters to start with core requirements and progressively integrate more detailed elements if desired. Thus, the specification does not require full implementation from the outset, supporting varied deployment contexts and needs.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db8451dd-938a-43eb-a921-1ca265e6c7e3 .

