    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b09d096e-3e48-4940-b31b-71e8991ae975 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification allows user to access and maintain distributed directories information over the Internet, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. LDAP, using SASL and TLS can manage users' access to directory services, as well as acting as an authentication method. Thus, it fosters the implementation of digital services, supporting the principle of digital-first.

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511

TLS cloudfare reference:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/ssl/transport-layer-security-tls/

SASL gnu reference: 
https://www.gnu.org/software/gsasl/manual/gsasl.html#SASL-Overview
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89d1eacd-388d-4b1d-84b3-256314eb7cdf .

camssa:b09d36a9-a912-4629-af11-56a1aaa8d633 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Even if iCalendar has been discreetly used at a EU context (EUROSTAT), the specification defines a set of conventions that could be integrated in the depiction of future organisational interoperability agreements.\r
\r
Euro-indicators (EUROSTAT) release calendar:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/news/internet-calendar\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46bf5b1b-4c29-4bcb-8ff5-f283bd00b56d .

camssa:b0a7dc3a-be09-466c-aa86-638f8ef9b22d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is developed and maintain within GitHub and in a public repository. Everyone can participate proposing new changes via issue or pull request. There is no limitation to participate in the development process. Users need just need a GitHub account. 

Publiccode.yaml contributing:
https://github.com/publiccodeyml/publiccode.yml/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af423873-aebd-4986-b8ff-27f8e1d65516 .

