camssa:b1483f81-ff08-4cab-873d-15740be77979 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP has a significant market acceptance. It has been successfully implemented by several European Union Institution:\r
• The European Commission DG CONNECT with the European Data Portal\r
• The Publications Office of the European Union with the European Union Open Data Portal\r
• The European Commission DG JRC with the JRC Data Catalogue\r
 and National Public administrations across Europe:\r
• The German GovData Business Office with the German Data Portal\r
• The Belgian Federal Public Service for ICT with the Belgian open data portal\r
• The Dutch Ministry of Interior and Kingdom Relations with the Dutch open data portal\r
• The Open Data Portal of Switzerland with the Geocat CKAN Harvester\r
• The Spanish Open Data Portal\r
• The Swedish innovation agency VINNOVA and the Swedish national data portal\r
• Swedish MetaSolutions and the EntryScape Catalogue\r
\r
See complete list of users/implementations:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af2f4cb8-be84-48dc-ac99-14f834de711a .

camssa:b1497764-90e0-4927-ae16-3f489e6c4ab9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b14d15c6-a0d8-4133-9058-b0362cbf337b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is a key component in the development of some national and cross-border projects and initiatives. However, ISO 3166-1 does not encourage the creation of communities nor promotes the sharing of data and results in any national platform.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e09a33b-8e6e-454f-b0a6-ff0b056e87a9 .

camssa:b1535570-eaa5-487d-93be-fb5ce341ccac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:b153b89e-cce7-4323-b2fe-0f7d27d1a1c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAREF is developed and maintained by the European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI). Its development involves contributions from industry experts and collaboration within ETSI working groups, particularly ETSI Technical Committee SmartM2M. This standardization body provides a foundational level of support for the ontology. ETSI takes into account the impact of users as they improve their standards and their relevancy. 

ETSI Technical Committee SmartM2M: 
https://www.etsi.org/committee/smartm2m'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0275c961-7cef-4cfd-a9ad-548e009389f0 .

camssa:b1556ebb-4cf1-4038-a8ff-45c92b990ba8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODRL is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
W3C Consortium home page: \r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core\r
\r
W3C Working Group Github space: \r
https://github.com/w3c/odrl"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3b5e824-e3cd-44c2-bf92-af4a4a817a42 .

camssa:b15a9eb9-b739-430a-98eb-a0843214eeaf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several reports assessing how DCAT-AP is effective and efficient for the publication of open data. \r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/dcat-ap """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2d8ccc90-cd86-433f-9e8b-f8f81c9a57ec .

camssa:b166d695-2386-462f-bad4-f7616b1c2738 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of OData, operates under RF (royalty-free) on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. Therefore, the specification is licensed on a (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
OData reference, section 1.0:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.01/odata-v4.01-part1-protocol.html\r
\r
OASIS Intellectual Property Rights Policy, section 10.2.2:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e2c965d4-c524-42c0-9d70-8b7d82253841 .

