camssa:b25fdec0-2ca4-47a1-bbc4-6cff24cdfa19 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently, the specification has been used in Italy to describe the software created in the country. This has permitted the creation of a national catalogue of software by crawling the content of the publiccode.yml available within the software repositories. The standard is also applied in opencode.de, Germany’s registry for open-source software in public administration.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Italian National Software Catalogue:
https://developers.italia.it/

Open CoDE:
https://opencode.de/en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f300b7ac-5b27-4b36-884c-1a30ca947949 .

camssa:b263268e-9232-4c72-9855-daf285c3081a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is not just included in a repository of standards, it is included within the Interoperability Architecture Solutions in the Interoperable Europe Portal, the site that the Interoperable Europe Act foresees as the place where interoperability solutions should be published, and where Member States and their different administrative levels can go to find reusable solutions. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21a95f3f-9a24-4e84-8836-7e970baf9f73 .

camssa:b264b8e8-27b2-473e-8329-91b41aa55214 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b2686eba-11ca-4acb-8cab-80920a7a890c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification is a family of XML-based standards that provides an open, XML-based infrastructure that enables the interoperable use of electronic business information. ebXML relies on XML, and therefore is not technology-agnostic.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5c5d604-5b7e-45f6-9f13-a3000c13f821 .

camssa:b27083b4-6c32-4f5a-9665-3055d114747f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b27113d3-1644-4e31-9054-1e5db9c8944b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EuroVoc Hanbook serves as a guide on how to input data and update existing entries. Consistency is key in \r
maintaining the specificaction, therefore, a long evaluation process takes place to ensure the correct implementation of changes in the thesaurus.\r
\r
EuroVoc Handbook:\r
https://publications.europa.eu/resource/cellar/a2723a83-574f-11eb-b59f-01aa75ed71a1.0001.01/DOC_1\r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b62709c-6ba9-46b5-af5e-8f69eb669387 .

camssa:b273fbaf-a7f8-4fa1-a006-f60c9b9bfa56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JSON is available for its use an implementation at ECMA International and EITF's webpages. \r
See:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/publications/standards/Ecma-404.htm\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8259#section-14.1"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ec4face-fc14-4722-983a-b4bc87cda483 .

camssa:b274e08b-b2ca-4cc0-977c-a97483bae799 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:b2756b5a-8c09-409e-8bd1-1729e60f2bdb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CSV is one of the most popular formats for publishing data on the web. An example of those developments is CSV Dialect which aims to deal with a reasonably large subset of the features which differ between dialect.\r
Add history, structured data, support from wide range of organisations (private and public)\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85eb1c67-100f-4b98-b0db-8b4276233041 .

camssa:b27a638f-4fab-4802-8771-c2a5cc308d8a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of MIME is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3119cb9-48cf-489e-8ecd-67d02328d32c .

camssa:b282cac0-46e4-4cb4-a0b7-4e650bd31ef6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification defines not only the codebase for the development of reusable solutions but also how the code has to be developed to ensure the maximum standardised method and its possible future reuse by other solutions or initiatives. In this sense, the specification provides a set of elements that stakeholders using and contributing must take into account to increase the successful and efficient collaboration between parties. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba77a81a-e772-4ba3-816b-4db1c996b162 .

camssa:b283328f-8e77-41f2-b005-1c102fb8a27b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:b2876809-4356-47ae-a3d1-1456b9d41eb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of UTF-8 is not related to the protection of personal data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b67b086c-f12c-4f9d-b9a4-b26479c5ddb9 .

camssa:b28d2e8f-da1a-4607-9f19-13af01269135 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The GITB TDL can be customised for a specific project’s testing, independent processing, messaging and validation extensions to address missing capabilities or domain-specific needs.\r
\r
JOINUP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/about\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#where-is-it-used'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b432dbf-492e-46f6-a1a2-3fe644127b2a .

camssa:b28eaeda-74ef-4b18-b2c3-0578cc545464 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1435ad894742693c2b99e329ef12399cd411ed6900f49b9658fd2231de3f201a ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b298ee0c-9fd0-47c0-8626-08d88efafefc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Given that OAIS purpose is to provide a reference model for the long-term preservation of archives, its implementation is subject to the changes of specific use cases.  Such changes  can be seen as customisations since they allow to add multiple functionalities not covered by the specification itself.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:92d08b27-e599-40ce-afa3-939f9b3fe379 .

camssa:b2a1f5a8-7b85-442e-a626-4901acfc2eb5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The implementation of ELI ensures that legislation is accessible to diverse stakeholders within government
frameworks. On one front, it facilitates interoperability among European Public Administrations, promoting
seamless data exchange and improving the visibility of administrative data. On the other hand, it contributes
to the availability of legislations, encouraging citizens and businesses to stay informed about the initiatives
and actions undertaken by public administrations.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3c2660d-5848-4933-809e-e512b5d28f77 .

camssa:b2a29489-a16f-4760-bf15-936d03afafbd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-838030847fa0adf54939e3feaac0ac2510924c54035e1cb671b223b54b02fd70 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:b2a3462c-57f1-4677-8281-45114ef7e9c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec is not related to interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
IPSec reference, What IPSec Does:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#page-7'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b27083b4-6c32-4f5a-9665-3055d114747f .

camssa:b2a8147e-6acb-498e-b7d6-11721de29c86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL is not included in a national catalogue from a Member State. The only interest group that is currently supporting SHACL are the Semantic Web users.\r
\r
However, note that SHACL is starting to be promoted by EU Member States as a relevant standard of their national standard catalogue. e.g. the Flemish (Belgium) project OSLO (Open Standard for Local Administrations).\r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/flemish-oslo-project-puts-add  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7460829-9c99-44fe-9e37-2fd3bfbc8504 .

camssa:b2b0aa5d-3c50-478b-95e1-dc33d4fc098d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is included in several national catalogues from EU Member States. A total of 14 countries listed the XML within their national catalogues (e.g. Belgium, France, Germany, etc.).\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.belgif.be/nl/specifications \r
http://references.modernisation.gouv.fr/sites/default/files/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf \r
http://www.cio.bund.de/SharedDocs/Publikationen/DE/Architekturen-und-Standards/SAGA/saga_modul_tech_spez_de_bund_5_0_download.pdf?__blob=publicationFile """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8dc4ea04-0591-41db-b6e5-cb2b21969642 .

camssa:b2b84f34-735d-4d74-936f-6c6dad1c257c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are two Member States recommending OData in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are The Netherlands and France.

Netherlands Catalogue reference:
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/aanbevolen

France catalogue reference:
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:473a137c-35a6-4fe4-a5e9-36a912c313cd .

