camssa:b2c8309f-ec60-4b8d-9fb2-f7dfa1d7525f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The iCalendar specification is technology agnostic. It is designed to be independent of any specific technology or platform, allowing it to be used across various software applications and systems for exchanging calendar data in a standardised format.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e214c79-1958-45a3-8911-6c52f93b89b9 .

camssa:b2ca8ae6-4e6c-4973-9f8b-f93a0a9d7aa4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Ogg is an open source container format which can multiplex a number of independent streams of audio, video, text (such as subtitles), and metadata. It does not support the first level of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data which is to make data available on the Web.\r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e6b2092a-c9ca-432b-bf7b-72d4abe625e4 .

camssa:b2cb1b80-92a4-4ef7-ab88-e0dbf941d95d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:b2cc5676-9dce-4e06-8dda-66b8a00c7003 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b2cf0458-757a-4754-a77e-e3c745b7866b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are many requirements in the documentation pdf but there's nothing related to conformance \r
requirements, all references relate to the REM Structure and REM Signature requirements.\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f93fde33-b01a-4051-ae38-dc97453bf63c .

camssa:b2d136dc-bd6c-4641-bf55-e93b654226d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "XSD 1.1 allows to define schemas according with specific needs, which allow citizens, businesses or administrations to create schemas. The creation of schemas eases the creation of XML complying with requirements for specific or general purposes. Thus, the implementation of XML schemas do not hamper the interoperability and scalability of systems. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5b2414f-219d-4c6a-b99e-3d1dc0dfe35c .

camssa:b2d23235-7708-4f1f-ad81-16a6e0df811d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:b2d929df-2513-45bc-92fe-860f86452b8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification in itself acts as a method to ensure that policies and laws are developed, implemented and monitored and enhanced following a standardised method that includes, guidelines, recommendations and requirements to reach the objective of exhaustive and comprehensible laws and policies.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20bad23b-10f2-406a-93dc-6f888774c287 .

camssa:b2db50dd-0bd9-4ed4-b6ef-ac31ff4e565f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are already existing documents and studies assessing the JSON's features and performance. In some cases, the study has been carried out in a comprehensive comparison between XML and JSON. \r
\r
Behavior based Comparative analysis of XML and JSON web technologies:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Hanif_Ullah/publication/321361853_Behavior_based_Comparative_analysis_of_XML_and_JSON_web_technologies/links/5a1eb56f0f7e9b9d5e000bfd/Behavior-based-Comparative-analysis-of-XML-and-JSON-web-technologies.pdf \r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d81b85c-be0c-4e74-8aaa-edd02f503d3a .

camssa:b2e12dca-cc47-45fe-9a0b-7040759debce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The ELI TF is the body in charge of the maintenance and development of the specification. In the ELI Governance document, it is defined how and by who the specification is evolved. \r
\r
Member States are open to participate in the evolution of the specification only with soft requirements like having implemented the specification at a national level and having the knowledge to contribute to the evolution of ELI.\r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
Governance Rules: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/governance_rules.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87023457-2b1d-48bb-91d7-c51812af4820 .

