    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b32c4878-5ef9-4e08-99f3-11b47e74ca2d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Following the completion of research into conformity tests and certifications, a tool has been identified that enables the testing of implementations. The "SHACL Test Suite" can be used to test SHACL implementations. Additionally, the format of the tests and the process to evaluate SHACL implementations are defined on a GitHub page by W3C. Moreover, the Test Bed also allows to validate RDF content by means of SHACL shapes.

SHACL Test Suite:
https://w3c.github.io/data-shapes/data-shapes-test-suite/

SHACL Test Bed:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/news/shacl-validator-updates

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1437ff68-645f-4e99-b690-ad2b19209904 .

camssa:b32eaf79-0aaa-428d-832e-60ced9b1445a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b331108c-a676-4d80-88ad-3ed90c23458d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of IPv6 is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:368f20d5-b4aa-46fc-a3ff-0a243876bf90 .

camssa:b338821e-b025-4e05-bf53-b1f235511768 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are documents that compare different secured versions of FTP (FTPS and SFTP), and the main differences between them. From there, it can be assessed the efficiency and effectiveness of the usage of FTPS in comparison with other type of FTP.\r
\r
FTPS vs SFTP:\r
https://www.goanywhere.com/blog/2016/11/23/sftp-vs-ftps-the-key-differences"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a6f67fc-0156-41b9-a356-39cd5616c0f1 .

camssa:b33a1829-5832-484d-92b3-2b4ea3894bcb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b3443231-ca64-4e89-9c0f-985052c4b24c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although TIFF/IT’s purpose is not the long-term preservation of data, it can be used to store data as print-ready pages. Moreover, TIFF is one of the safest image file types available with exclusive standout safety features. Moreover, OpenAire which is an European initiative founded by the European Commission, is recommending TIFF as one of the formats for the preservation of images.\r
\r
OpenAire Initiative:\r
https://www.openaire.eu/about\r
\r
OpenAire Preservation guide:\r
https://www.openaire.eu/data-formats-preservation-guide\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ace138d-c63f-4105-b5d4-767523d7838d .

camssa:b3445ea2-f258-4836-a413-02739ec0d2ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that use CPOV nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4491bead-bd8d-45d7-8ea8-d853fba45d2a .

camssa:b345af58-4090-4d3b-9d8f-72e4079080ac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b349b0c8-12b2-46a6-90c0-b36d2d46825c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b349f39a-ac7d-4fd9-a8ea-2e0492553261 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EuroVoc is used for data processing acrosss Europe by the European Insitutions and also the National ones. \r
Moreover, there is the possibility to search European Laws amongst other documents using its classification. \r
It can be done through a EurLex, the European Gateway for regulation. \r
\r
Additionally, it is used in the EU Open Data Portal as a method for knowledge classification. In the EU Open \r
Data Portal, datasets are related and linked to EuroVoc domains that improve the searchability and reuse of \r
information.\r
\r
EU Open Data Portal example:\r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/es/data/dataset/building-stock-observatory \r
\r
Search by EuroVoc: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/browse/eurovoc.html?params=12,1216#arrow_1216\r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0eef6e4-7544-4e78-a458-a59cf277c144 .

camssa:b34ca8ac-8250-4afc-afa8-6bd6bdb240da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not related to the protection of personal data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79b1c389-d030-4dac-ad30-2eda36f88670 .

camssa:b35034bf-19f6-4ff0-819e-fde6d4b96b27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP has been in use by the World-Wide Web global information since 1990. That fact evidences that the standard has the sufficient maturity.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1: Semantics and Content, RFC 7231 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7231'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fad6214c-a4a5-4a1c-a176-8821746fac48 .

camssa:b351caca-f063-4c80-8f77-e5dd6373e749 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification is designed to be implemented and used across various business domains, facilitating the reliable exchange of messages between parties. Its versatility comes from characteristics like its symmetric protocol, interoperable data representation, and flexible messaging layer.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9cf3f23f-6084-41d3-bcf3-5e12631e272e .

camssa:b359d8f2-a33a-4ff4-a0c5-4c201d0a722a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SCIM primarily focuses on identity management, its features promote the efficient and consistent reuse of relevant identity information across systems. Organizations can tailor their SCIM implementations to meet their specific needs and ensure that relevant information is exchanged and reused effectively in their identity management processes.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9f8cfeb-90b0-4d62-b3b4-f5f51017594d .

camssa:b35b2fde-b5c2-4272-ba74-ae13315802d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT is included in the catalogues of the Netherlands and Spain.\r
 \r
See: \r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst \r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:9e2c2877-5103-4934-8440-c60ba2e10c48/Catalogue_of_Standards_NIF_Spain.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f17cc768-2ef3-4481-b8c0-d92add8a0b96 .

camssa:b36215f2-bde5-4510-a152-909ac55c57f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV defines a data model for describing public organisations in the European Union. The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary addresses specific needs of businesses, public administrations and citizens across the European Union.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e150aff8-aecf-4d1b-a049-78b1db723d5a .

camssa:b3630bf5-cc2f-448b-b4b7-acee8e99dc32 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b3659b6b-ae63-401b-b9f8-77492f9c0665 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Estonia and Spain. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
\r
National catalogue Estonia:\r
https://www.mkm.ee/sites/default/files/interoperability-framework_2011.doc\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3461b2ce-5e29-44ba-80dd-ad2cae59f8f7 .

