    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b377dddb-e527-450b-b469-370c37daa4c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not included in any initiative at European or National level covering privacy aspects. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c5291865-072d-4f4b-b221-37e9c8eaa49b .

camssa:b377fa10-54d9-410a-ac11-14d456346ce4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Assessments of the efficiency of SAREF primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. A 2020-paper for the Applied Ontology Journal explains the need for interoperability of IoT healthcare applications and the role of standardised ontologies to achieve semantic interoperability. Furthermore, there is a first attempt to extend SAREF for specific e-Health use cases related to ECG data, which highlights the specification's efficiency across different sectors.

SAREF4health - Towards IoT standard-based ontology-driven cardiac e-health systems: https://content.iospress.com/articles/applied-ontology/ao200232\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1bd0f921-eddc-41ee-8292-83419ef1a96e .

camssa:b3785464-b0e6-4bfe-96a1-31d068884d6b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b3878f80-3a6e-404b-8383-0b0dc383e027 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b38efc9f-52cd-43af-94ef-864693a7cc2b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The European Union (EU) Member States are currently implementing the INSPIRE Directive and related regulations, included in the ISA programme. This projects includes the usage of XSLT for each member state of the Union.

Infrastructure for Spatial Information in Europe:
https://ies-svn.jrc.ec.europa.eu/projects/registry-development/wiki/Re3gistry_1_0_documentation#_cp3
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9bee6637-e450-422d-b92a-7b647733d9a0 .

camssa:b392b768-f58f-4a48-82fb-3bdc8d252e39 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"JSON strongly supports Tim Berners Lee's 5-star schema for open data. The adoption of JSON fosters the publication of data as open data by means of providing structured data and the usage of non-proprietary formats. Moreover, it helps to link data by means of embedding metadata. \r
Moreover, there is an existing extension of JSON which aims to help and support the Linked Open Data environments. The extension has been developed by the W3C working group specifically in charge of JSON-LD development. Additionally, the W3C has developed a syntax for RDF serialisation using JSON, and JSON-LD is recommended. \r
\r
JSON LD Community:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/json-ld/\r
\r
JSONLD.org:\r
https://json-ld.org\r
\r
Open Data Goldbook:\r
https://www.europeandataportal.eu/sites/default/files/european_data_portal_-_open_data_goldbook.pdf\r
\r
Tim-Berners-Lee 5 star Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f12ce09e-103e-44b6-8c49-41da63286527 .

camssa:b39d3ffa-7aee-4b19-856f-2b95a7c46451 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The implementation of the specification does not hamper the scalability and interoperability of systems. As part of the stack of the eDelivery Building Block, eDelivery SMP 1.10 allows enabling users to grow according to administrations or businesses' needs. \r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/Benefits+of+eDelivery"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1c3b1ab-96d7-4e4e-8992-4b41305114d4 .

