    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b3d264a6-9be0-4398-811e-e9fb6a709c89 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although TIFF/IT supports the first level of maturity from the Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for the Open data, it does not support the main principles for the publication of data as Linked Open Data.\r
\r
5-star linked open data:\r
https://www.w3.org/DesignIssues/LinkedData.html\r
https://www.w3.org/wiki/LinkedData\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:878af7b5-50a0-4bdf-ae66-da84a4bbbd83 .

camssa:b3d64f56-971d-4707-9352-cf4b3ca57011 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS supports the creation of APIs that follow the REST architectural style. RESTful APIs are encoded in JSON format which is a way to encode data structures like lists and dictionaries to strings that ensure that they are easily readable by machines.  \r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee in the 5-Stars approach: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e7b6f55-e439-499c-afc6-736ec5f19167 .

camssa:b3d7acd4-f77e-41bb-b1ab-0b2ac2a21af9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b3dcf320-c29d-40bd-be7e-325c206708d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UTF-8 is independent of any specification and can be implemented without dependencies with technologies or platforms. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bdcb5f0-a190-4caa-9852-0003c48f17de .

camssa:b3dfbd89-f4d9-405c-837b-919c8ea7ab75 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is designed to be extensible to accommodate specific requirements and features that may not be covered by the core specification. This extensibility is facilitated through the use of custom elements and attributes in the WSDL document.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43f68320-b602-46c4-bbd2-b88b32db72ff .

camssa:b3e0dae3-e18f-42c9-b252-3521c394bd7e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TGF is designed to be flexible and modular, which means it can be implemented in a partial or phased manner. The TGF approach allows government and agencies to adopt the parts that are most relevant and beneficial to them.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50fe468f-e240-4ea5-9696-9d1e3ff85acd .

camssa:b3e0df38-262f-4a3d-b9ef-2c2d66492f71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 protocols are designed in a way that can be implemented separately depending on the\r
functional goals (see section 4.2) or the preservation service the organisation needs to implement (see section 4.3). Partial implementations, therefore, are allowed in this specification.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3af8776-52c1-4217-93cb-e377a70b3756 .

camssa:b3e6a075-f8b3-4183-ad7b-eed736e64e68 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT does no directly help for the provision of application programming interfaces (APIs) or Web services.\r
\r
However, DCAT aims to ensure consistency by providing a standard description of the catalogues and datasets published by data portals across Europe. This description makes datasets more searchable and accessible for data reuse and encourages the data providers to use open data portals for dissemination of reusable data."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc8c63fb-c82e-49e7-a9cb-1e262cda8277 .

camssa:b3e7bbcd-13ae-446a-b035-f9ada7ebeb82 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:b3e8140d-447e-486e-bae2-079b36116915 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6bedf555bffb837990b9eb353447fa116eb9d2384770b1dd3de46d3c5901d4f4 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b3e9f9ab-1986-4a19-9cac-88f304b0022d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary specification simplifies the delivery of European public services by providing a standardised framework for describing location data. In this sense, public administrations can offer more efficient and reliable digital services, minimising the need for manual data handling and non-digital document exchange.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:503ef2f2-e57f-4979-8bf7-6880cfbfe021 .

camssa:b3eafe52-e29f-4799-9b2d-68700ae76537 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of HTTPS is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:006ecfed-217f-42dd-9d0b-1eeabdd43711 .

