    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:b3f7ae38-5d8e-44fd-84e9-d701f04d2ca9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The available information does not specifically mention the authenticity and authentication of the roles
agents involved in the data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this
specification.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f5715a3-a351-43f5-b501-9fcde816ff6d .

camssa:b3f9aad9-264c-4083-930a-6a4e612a60f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of PAdES is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
PAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/67937.html\r
\r
PAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e5b3a49-69a5-4f5e-8a74-0e37d9434cbe .

camssa:b400f216-5a52-4856-bc20-8c7bc9ef46f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL specification is mainly focused on the definition of a common vocabulary for the description and the \r
exchange of access rights and digital materials consumption. In the context of digital content management, it \r
can indirecly help to ensure the trustworthy exchange of data and to contribute the protection of personal by \r
determining access rights and conditions to digital content within which possibly may be there personal data \r
information. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0712aba-bc61-405f-8ba9-6a626d8b3523 .

camssa:b40e0c8f-5b77-40a9-8f82-7919373bf90d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the specification is an extension of XML, XML can be used to represent the data related to business processes, such as the steps involved, the roles and responsibilities of stakeholders, and the inputs and outputs of each step.\r
\r
XSD Reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff275f94-a7ff-4adf-a56f-089ab55c371a .

camssa:b4148554-a465-4256-a1a0-122a265f53fa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b416da53-3dbc-489c-b4c7-0023be328dce a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:b419dcf2-19fc-469f-ad7b-4593e50bc126 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Dataspace Protocol is a crucial part of the IDS, as it ensures a minimum viable interoperability between these different frameworks, products, or services. Thanks to this, trust and data sovereignity is possible in International Data Spaces, making data exchanges and interactions inside IDS secure and thus, enabling the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol Specification: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:100aed64-f98c-4279-b38a-da9acab9b9a1 .

camssa:b41aeae8-1790-47d8-a349-2fcecceab22b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several studies where implementation of OWL2 has been carried out to prove its scalability.\r
The first paper presents an implementation of OWL2, called Scalable OWL 2 Reasoning for Linked Data which purpose is to introduce scalable reasoning and querying techniques to Semantic Web researchers to make use of Linked Data and large-scale ontologies. The second paper presents a study that evaluates and optimizes an OWL2 implementation based on an Event-based eHealth Context with scalability issues.\r
Moreover, as a general language for representing ontologies and therefore the reality of specific knowledge domains, it can be implemented and extended according to the specific needs without hampering the interoperability. \r
\r
Scalable OWL 2 Reasoning for Linked Data:\r
http://aidanhogan.com/docs/rw_2011.pdf\r
\r
Evaluation and Optimized Usage of OWL 2 Reasoners in an Event-based eHealth Context:\r
http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1387/paper_6.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36fe68b9-f6ba-4fc0-9b03-02525321dc9b .

camssa:b41b3cba-23c5-4302-8e2b-09cc9fa7e3c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Given the nature of all the core vocabularies developed by the UE domain, platform agnosticism is a key feature, ensuring that the specification remains adaptable and applicable across various technological platforms and environments. Therefore, the specification is platform agnostic. 

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b62d49ce-fef5-49ef-ad78-48e0f5de548e .

camssa:b41d05e8-3e6d-4caf-b59f-415c0b10415c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The iCalendar specification (RFC 5545 and its updates) is sufficiently mature and widely adopted for use in the development of digital solutions and services related to calendaring, scheduling, and event management. iCalendar has been in use for many years and has become a de facto standard for representing and exchanging calendar data in the digital world.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c0c3421-e0d1-4d43-bff5-a14590cd0165 .

camssa:b41fd37b-e21b-4b51-b7ba-0c0c9a46df44 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b4224c4a-85f3-486b-8ba7-dd826d102291 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b422dcad-3bf9-4ed9-b3c8-971fde344d69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XHTML is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Estonia and Spain.\r
The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. \r
\r
National catalogue Estonia: \r
https://www.mkm.ee/sites/default/files/interoperability-framework_2011.doc\r
\r
National catalogue Spain:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3d37fbb-3875-4539-b57c-77897a39d5be .

