camssa:b444aba0-f1d5-4a1c-8319-29d16bca9b7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is used on  the European Materials Modeling Ontology (EMMO) created by the European Materials Modelling Council (EMMC) in order to organise the top level ontology that leads to a better integration of business processes related to material processing. 

EMMO reference:
https://emmo-repo.github.io/

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a64aa4ba-b2b7-4e6b-8bee-a418eb5292d4 .

camssa:b44684de-d491-4d71-8c58-7ae09b2c4cdf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is associated with the EIRA ABB's in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). DCAT can define the interoperability aspects of the Base Registry, Controlled Vocabulary, Data, Data Model, Data Policies, Data Set, Data Set Catalogue, Data Syntax, Forms Structure, Hash Code, Metadata\r
Reference Data ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View; and the Data Publication Component, Data Publication Service, Metadata Management Component, Metadata Management Service ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
            \r
ELIS reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v501\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:12a7d932-8a5b-4caf-9324-59647e0928bc .

