camssa:b45f5bba-e8dd-463a-ba07-6aab023d6b16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There have been found some assessments directly addressing CPSV-AP efficiency.  Below two examples: the first one of CPSV-AP being evaluated for comprehensiveness and compliance with EU policies, and the second one, a study on the use of CPSV-AP to publish public service descriptions as linked open data.\r
\r
Public Service Models: A Systematic Literature Review and Synthesis:\r
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8823991\r
\r
On using CPSV-AP to publish public service descriptions as linked open data: https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11761-022-00344-6'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb9552d2-b93c-4727-8787-41d79bb42824 .

camssa:b4614ebc-a1c6-469d-b124-0bd3965d594f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:b4745480-6a0c-4d03-8391-67f160c46243 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox is a public asset developed by the European Commission and can be accessed and reused without any payment conditions. Therefore, it can be considered that the specifications is licensed under royalty-free basis and (F)RAND basis.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b264b8e8-27b2-473e-8329-91b41aa55214 .

camssa:b479df2b-e7b0-4cfb-8928-afd6572db9cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, HTTPS can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data Exchange Component" "Data Exchange Services"  ABBs of the EIRA Technical Application View.\r
\r
ELIS reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/v501\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d18731f-6d06-46cb-8867-4ece93f462aa .

camssa:b4850840-a0f2-44ac-bd0a-e5eb78e22e42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 can be applied in any domain and context where the use of time-stamping protocol is realized. Therefore, the specification is usable beyond any business-specific domain and can be used in any kind of organisation. It can be consulted in section 6.Operations in the following document.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca1cb672-689e-43f4-91d5-4b4be6486f02 .

camssa:b48bf767-0b5e-4c74-9710-79644c580bba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5140e8f3-df61-4f4a-a5c4-64a6d65c33e2 .

camssa:b48c60f7-a231-46f3-9379-0905f9b1f41b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'iCalendar allows EU institutions to place their publications in the form of a calendar on the Internet. This is the case of EUROSTAT, which delivers the Euro-indicator release calendar in ics format for easy integration into the most popular calendar applications, such as Outlook or Google calendar.\r
\r
Euro-indicators release calendar:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/news/internet-calendar\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e9dcb998-ce7b-4ce8-94ea-e205896ae07d .

camssa:b49ad88e-abf2-467f-bcf4-a3f9d720cec1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV can be implemented in any platform and it is independent of any technology.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cce5b651-e867-4c4b-9382-f95ac133e36b .

camssa:b49bf37f-da76-4e57-a2dc-a33e785938b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a vocabulary, the implementation of RegOrg can be tested using methods like SHACL shapes and using semantic reasoners to ensure that the implementation is well-formed. These validation mechanisms can be used with open source tools or lite versions of tools like GrapghDB or Protégé.\r
\r
SHACL validation: \r
https://graphdb.ontotext.com/documentation/free/shacl-validation.html#what-is-shacl-validation\r
\r
Semantic Reasoners List: \r
http://owl.cs.manchester.ac.uk/tools/list-of-reasoners/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e2f2001-b252-4b3a-b987-950897639918 .

