camssa:b52717ee-0814-4079-93ec-179033b3ca4f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML allows extensibility or the addition of plugins in the specification's ebRIM and ebRS components. Although such extensibility is limited to some of the ebRIM and ebRS features, ebXML RegRep 4.0 - Part 1 and Part 2 specify how extensibility may be achieved, that is, either by extending ebRIM or modifying the ebRS service interface. It is the case of the ebXML RegRep SWG specification, which is an Open Geospatial Consortium's authoring of the ebXML specification and which deals with the use of geo-data in a variety of contexts.

ebXML RegRep Part 1, Extending ebRIM section:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/csprd01/regrep-core-rim-v4.0-csprd01.
html#__RefHeading__39225_1821683062

ebXML RegRep Part 2, Cataloguer Plugin section:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rs-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__32575_422331532

ebXML RegRep SWG reference:
https://www.ogc.org/projects/groups/ebxmlregrepswg

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a5bfb19-092f-4444-be53-04f7996e9eb7 .

camssa:b52b38c4-9d0e-454f-bf7a-fad4e7886542 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 can be applied in any domain and context where the use of the time-stamping protocol is realized. Therefore, the specification is usable beyond any business-specific domain and can be used in any kind of organisation.. It can be consulted in section 6.Operations in the following document.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb98d42e-c942-4e87-b7f3-b743328def2f .

