camssa:b5bcd1fa-bf08-4981-8877-c877797b8c08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification is relevant to data portability because it standardises essential information about public sector software, making it easier to share, adapt, and integrate such software across different platforms and jurisdictions. By creating a consistent, structured format for documenting code, it facilitates smoother data exchange and interoperability between systems, reducing dependency on proprietary formats. This approach aligns with data portability principles by enabling public administrations to reuse, transfer, or adapt software solutions with minimal effort, promoting openness and flexibility across technological solutions.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e80394ac-591e-4302-84c9-9934172ead33 .

camssa:b5c12c41-c295-4992-a8fe-90d24df61682 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b5c5d604-5b7e-45f6-9f13-a3000c13f821 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:b5c7a221-9238-4691-8420-738a8a940800 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAIS appears to be discussed in Joinup as one of the standards eligible for the preservation of digital cinema.  The EIF Toolbox, also found in Joinup, recommends OAIS as one of the solutions for the technical interoperability layer.\r
\r
OAIS EIF Toolbox:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/solution/eif-toolbox/solution-earchiving\r
\r
Preservation of digital cinema:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/rolling-plan-ict-standardisation/preservation-digital-cinema-1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:978a97c4-ee2c-47e9-8976-b147798dc06c .

camssa:b5caf2aa-0933-4b98-9c2f-e0fb637e9232 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e9e0cf4a339c837607828404dd0e9b360d643528fcc1df488a95ca67166acea3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b5cbe368-a166-4fe9-b1b8-c96ed8920a00 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 specifies generally applicable policy and security requirements for Trust Service Providers (TSPs) implementing a service component operating a remote signature creation device. While it does not explicitly address partial implementations, the document defines two different implementations for remote digital signature creation: A JSON-based Implementation based on the Cloud Signature Consortium specification and an XML-based Implementation that follows the OASIS DSS-X standard2. Overall, the specification allows partial implementations but there are essential componenets that ensure alignment with security requirements.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf

Architectures and protocols for remote signature applications:
https://cloudsignatureconsortium.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/CSC_API_V1_1.0.4.0.pdf

Digital Signature Service Core Protocols, Elements, and Bindings Version 2.0: 
https://docs.oasis-open.org/dss-x/dss-core/v2.0/dss-core-v2.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9f06ad35-dc3a-4a27-ab94-dd49a4480152 .

camssa:b5cf286e-5bf0-4e96-be31-8c586ae1d1e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2cedd44f05183dae5548108bdeace2c092b84c7c5d89c475b0741ddae7fc7b2 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:b5d18b33-6ef6-4cd1-99a3-0997c8d0d956 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any software, hardware, or operating system. So it can be said that ODF is independent of any specific technology or platform.\r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e6233415-c488-4c99-a36d-72baba151774 .

camssa:b5d217c0-421b-4e90-a82f-5f1fd3f53bac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XAdES Baseline Profile is referenced in the ETSI collection at the European Platform Joinup. Moreover, it can be found for free at ETSI’s webpage\r
See:\r
