camssa:b613cd88-838a-4e6e-9cc3-9ba7dded6741 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE 802.3 is included in several repositories and catalogues of standards at the European level. It is listed on platforms like StandICT.eu and Joinup.

Joinup list:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/ieee-8023-2015-8023-2015-ieee-standard-ethernet/distribution/ieee-8023-2015-8023-2015-ieee-standard-ethernet

StandICT list: 
https://standict.eu/standards-repository/ieee-8023-2018-ieee-standard-ethernet'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d05df6c-95d5-4d14-9c4f-1724098f9176 .

camssa:b615ed6d-d55b-4829-9ee0-a4669b812682 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "'The publiccode.yml specification does not inherently provide mechanisms for restricting access to information or data. Its purpose is to define metadata for documenting public sector software to facilitate reuse, transparency, and interoperability. While it aids in standardising descriptions and promoting accessibility, it does not include features for controlling access to the documented information or for implementing data access restrictions.'"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85c3ad4f-799d-4b49-a277-77261cdcba3b .

camssa:b617d0ea-469f-4932-b7b2-c2d5ee1af108 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification uses message-level security mechanisms to enhance data security. As described in the Oracle document about security features, these mechanisms provide sender authentication for long-running transactions. Thus, by authenticating the data sender, it helps to identify whether a user is verified or not.

ebXML security:
https://www.oracle.com/technical-resources/articles/enterprise-architecture/ebxml-security1.html

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0a6e8a10-f298-408a-8935-8c49cd8a66bd .

camssa:b61a7f5c-76e9-42da-bdeb-ad3bfe54b928 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:b61ce55a-17fa-4303-859e-d9f3465e3405 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There can be found serialisation extensions to RDF, such as TriG or N-Quads, which are used to encode multiple graphs.  Turtle (TTL) is an extension of N-Triples, it introduces a number of syntactic shortcuts which are aimed to ease the parsing, writing and readability.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05a739e0-d86a-450c-bf99-a60d322d6798 .

