    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b668d8e5-da49-4128-ba55-9f319ee4b4d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SHACL allows for extensions, by including an extension mechanism that enables the expression of more complex conditions using languages such as SPARQL, for example. This flexibility allows users to define custom functions, targets, and rules, enhancing SHACL's capability to handle a wide range of data validation scenarios. In addition, it can also be mentioned the SHACL-ACL extension, which include access control mechanisms and is based on SPARQL.

"SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43458-7_4

SHACL-ACL github:
https://github.com/SDM-TIB/SHACL-ACL

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f0f030e-613e-4de3-b9f7-c81c37172923 .

camssa:b66e78c9-7b62-4317-b24d-a02e09a87470 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After searching for a conformity test to validate JPEG format, no tool has been found with this purpose. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcb4df88-c242-42b0-81bb-aecd016450ec .

