camssa:b6ddded1-59c3-4c93-ac26-e53b3ede8494 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A DID is associated with a DID document. DID documents are expressed using the data model and can be serialized into a representation. There are three types of properties: DID document properties, verification method properties and service properties. In this categories there are required properties, but also optional properties which can be implemented depending users needs.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#core-properties'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b321a57-812c-4c81-b997-3ce572e8292b .

camssa:b6dfe086-3c9b-49f3-b537-1c4d73827f39 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'3 Member States are recommending SHACL in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are Belgium, Malta and the Netherlands.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3238ecb-c6ee-4c63-bf32-b9ed6be6ac43 .

