camssa:b701b0f4-79e9-443e-9c66-920c23a77cc1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPsec specification can be used in conjunction with XAuth (Extended Authentication) to guarantee access only to authorised users. With this extension, it is possible to ensure that data has not been modified by third parties and has reliably reached the receiver.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

XAuth authentication mechanism:
https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortigate/7.4.0/administration-guide/277729/using-xauth-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:827226ec-6bc1-4dfd-b134-1f89e424f11d .

camssa:b701f44d-f8a2-47c4-8851-7c6264e3cb58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM supports publication of data on the web with an open license and in a structured, machine-readable format. The current version of the specification is an open API thus, it can be considered an open standard.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72086895-a816-4f6b-98dc-08713d886416 .

camssa:b70a64aa-5d96-4dd8-a030-6cefc618023f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a1eafd9c95081eeabe19f0511239b88139f02f95e2349049eeea058a89c80f49 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b713df94-5b45-4db4-a881-e55c134228cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP is an EU cross-border project consisting in an application profile of DCAT for European data portals.\r
\r
DCAT Application Profile Data: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:237e6439-e9bc-486b-b2c0-6b78ffb946e1 .

camssa:b717b845-b268-42b5-adc2-5067c8b5fdaa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0229101dfe08cbe58da1e454363d30a8178a2e120466c8db23965488cae5c8b1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b71b9fdd-a6a0-4573-9d60-50be857454e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Web Services Description Language (WSDL) itself is not designed or intended to address the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge. \r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f7c948b-4981-42b1-9d97-2277e251f5c2 .

camssa:b71cd9d8-ecb9-4d6e-9dff-066dd298324c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The GITB TDL can be used in the conformance and interoperability testing of various domains. For this matter, a large set of elements are defined to match its foreseen testing constructs.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#what-is-the-gitb-tdl\r
\r
JOINUP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/detailed-information#domainagnostic'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f581b6db-4a0c-450d-ad43-13bebef78467 .

camssa:b72496a1-4d1f-4f8e-82cd-6fd734238ef3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A key component of ELI is the implementation of URI template patterns, which guarantee persistent access
to resources over time. This feature promotes the long-term preservation of electronic documents, ensuring
their continued availability.

Furthermore, by providing access to legal documents in a machine-readable format, ELI encourages their
reuse and adaptation to other formats, thereby facilitating the evolution of European Public Services.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e516ff18-b5d4-458b-8753-b7dd069dfe7e .

camssa:b72b85bd-0a68-495d-8e15-88102aa35eab a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b72d3dfc-3b59-47bd-9176-9e10a0ee6464 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As an open framework, the TGF specification is published and made freely available for use and adaptation by governments and other stakeholders. When new versions of the TGF are released or updated, they are typically made available for public review and feedback before being finalized. The public review process provides an opportunity for stakeholders to review and comment on the proposed changes, provides feedback on the usefulness and relevance of the framework, and suggests improvements or additions to the specification.\r
\r
OASIS document process:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b778334-02e0-400f-96ac-562e0d53df22 .

camssa:b730c576-3571-4e1d-acba-b8869ff61395 a cav:Score,
