camssa:b809941f-b4bf-4a9f-9e11-ec03f0b4fae5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TSP can be implemented in any platform and it is independent of any technology.\r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81027886-2ce0-469e-9bb3-ddbde987775d .

camssa:b816ceda-a78c-4778-a48b-c838ed95c0e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c23e0529-f631-4ce3-81da-d3d5c348ae11 .

camssa:b81aea92-0a10-45df-9612-380c57780650 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 allows customisation through cipher suite configuration, enabling the prioritisation of specific encryption algorithms, and the adjustment of connection negotiation parameters, such as key exchange, session resumption, and post-handshake authentication, amongst others. 

TLS 1.3 Extensions reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-4.2'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f2315cf-948d-467f-a1d2-9857e1851cf7 .

camssa:b81ed932-d62e-4573-a8e2-946acf64a38d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 639-2 has been extensively used in the library industry and can also be used for any domain that requires the expression of language in codes. This specification has been implemented in other domains where a linguistic solution was needed, for example in e-procurement (eForms).\r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5\r
\r
eForms Language reference:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/eforms/0.5.0/codelists/index.html#_tailored_codelists'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69abcf93-9ace-4873-9571-09a6feff3088 .

camssa:b8231fce-8c6f-4135-a3e3-a6cf473fcccc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EuroVoc has the support of the Publication Office of the European Union as a developer community. \r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b81ff2e-c0de-4ff9-ae52-e138ea0849df .

camssa:b82453b5-64a3-4f62-b2f5-f5e2cadc9eb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 is designed to be technology-agnostic. The OSI model is a conceptual framework that outlines the functions of a communication system and organises these functions into seven abstraction layers. It does not prescribe specific technologies, protocols, or implementations.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5921fd20-494c-41d8-8bd1-f4feaf37f8df .

camssa:b826065b-b79f-40f7-b9d0-834938f1e818 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification is associated with EIRA ABB's in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). It is associated with Data Syntax, Forms Structure, Controlled Vocabulary, Data, Data Mapping, Data Model, Hash Code, Metadata from the Semantic View.\r
\r
ELIS link:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/v501\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3c28217-5246-4a0f-86ba-9c4a19dfbfec .

camssa:b8272faf-23be-4c98-91bf-52e53d1c61a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are many testimonial from W3C consistorium that are a reliable example to know that HTML5 is a cross-sector reusable data model: ACCESS, Accessibility Foundation, Adobe, Ayuntamiento de Zaragoza, Ebay / PayPal, Facebook,  Intel, Microsoft, NTT Communications, Rakuten, among others\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:217f134d-cfeb-4b9e-a78f-93bd5dcb3da2 .

