camssa:b864e37d-ce6a-4087-ac7b-8b3eb741aaa8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:760f025a-2e35-43d4-8f1c-75c8c5892667 .

camssa:b86d23c3-b779-4707-9d1a-91c18fffbaac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a0101cb11c30c1bbf94adb74479472f2a40c53ccc4b442180fece91506c20a9d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b86e4b45-91e0-44f7-94f1-520a51c2b348 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the main purpose of the specifications is not the preservation of information it can be used in the context of eArchiving. An example of this aim is DCAT and DCAT-AP, data catalogues vocabularies built around RDF and which are used with the purpose of describing datasets included in data catalogues. The enrichment by means of metadata according to RDF schema could help to the long term preservation of digital documents.\r
\r
DCAT specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:692c41d5-5fd0-4499-9fc9-4ea9c511b11a .

camssa:b873810d-1754-4605-acdc-5ae4b06b6339 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b877f36b-48c0-4966-a78c-a5058ffc65fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD 1.1 is publically available at the European Platform for the reuse of ICT solutions, Joinup. \r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/w3c-xml-schema-definition-language-xsd-11-part-2-datatypes"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce0d0bcc-c8b5-43e3-9a30-c09450ec08cd .

camssa:b879aeb7-30b8-485a-ac5c-931ff679b8a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of PDF/A is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
PDF/A reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/38920.html\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/50655.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81c8afc3-ae27-4f07-ad2b-3abde08da94f .

camssa:b87aa1c4-2056-4565-a219-0e9d76b07b0d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b87e2047-ad55-47fd-8960-047d007c86fc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:b8812706-f5b5-4a35-8ae8-899a8033f4ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 is designed to allow for partial implementations. The layering concept of the OSI model facilitates the development and deployment of network communication protocols in a modular and flexible manner. Each layer in the OSI model is responsible for specific functions, and the interfaces between layers are well-defined. This modular design enables developers to implement only the layers that are relevant to their specific needs. 

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:900000e4-6c1c-48f8-9e87-8a6872733af8 .

camssa:b88207d9-d1d7-4909-a1ba-0e698ae92476 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The first version of ISO/IEC 19944-1 was first published in 2020. Since then, there has not been made a public review, and there can't either be found market uptake indicators. Nonetheless, it updates the previous standard ISO/IEC 19941 and builds upon ISO/IEC 17788:2014 and ISO/IEC 17789:2014 which are widely used standards for the development of cloud-computing environments.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 17789:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 Joint Technical Committee:\r
https://www.iso.org/committee/601355.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88bc4814-380f-4bab-ae25-449cbfba9177 .

camssa:b8843722-8cb0-49c5-abd2-812f01c426c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The classification scheme outlined in ISO/IEC 19944-1 can be applied to various types of data within cloud computing, regardless of the specific domain or industry. It provides a framework for categorizing data based on sensitivity, regulatory requirements, and business needs. It is important to note that ISO/IEC 19944-1 serves as a foundational standard for data classification within cloud computing, and organizations may need to consider additional domain-specific standards, regulations, or guidelines to address the specific requirements of their respective industries or sectors.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd6ab444-6e5d-4e5b-b892-4a00b8552dbc .

camssa:b8846e3f-6a3d-4528-b7c3-be662ae0b6d5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:b888f21e-d09f-4257-9595-70fa8b554028 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XSLT specification improves the visibility of administrative procedures, rules, data, and services. Its data transformation capabilities, support for multiple output formats, and JSON handling make it a valuable tool for presenting information accessibly (see Section 3.2 for output formats and Section B for JSON transformation).

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74deeb6f-2c5f-462b-9d05-92ecb70edc14 .

camssa:b8898277-2307-43f0-b7eb-72e661575c8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This standard is licensed CC-0, which essentially means that the project, along with the contributions is in the public domain in whatever jurisdiction possible, and everyone can do whatever they want with it.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9484682-b865-4bde-adcb-6107e1f27b43 .

camssa:b889f92e-fb4b-495b-9d42-979f2c48aaa8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv6 is maintained and developed by IETF which is an international community developing open standards.
Moreover, the deployment of IPv6 is rapidly expanding in the Internet. Support for IPv6 by private corporations has been lagging behind but these companies, such as Apple, are taking steps to rectify this situation and raise awareness to the problem.

IETF organisation:
https://www.ietf.org/about/ 

IPv6 development:
https://community.cisco.com/t5/jive-developer-archive-documents/ipv6-for-application-developers-whitepaper/ta-p/3647032'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32c91090-6dcb-4e70-9bd7-28e86473119d .

camssa:b88a2008-be15-496e-83dd-288411ca6ba0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d129862d6c9639e131c7d5eef095af16ef94d57ec0d52f955bf909ba8ec688e8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b88ba990-c02f-426d-b6a8-cf327778c277 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:56e3d852-2dc2-47d6-85f1-3777dd6cdc1e .

camssa:b88d17a7-ef17-412c-a935-df0d0149ee44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "No evidences have been found of the specification being included in a formal interoperability agreement between organisations involved in the European public services provision."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73eb2e1a-01c7-437b-9db6-16b6f225f006 .

camssa:b88feb56-cb17-4bd4-93cc-da4c82a5bbfe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"DAPS is a crucial part of Identity Providers in the IDS, as it provides short-lived tokens with up-to-date information about connectors. Thanks to this, data privacy and secure data exchange is possible in IDS, which enables the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04c1bdf4-080d-4fd1-940e-035c463d576c .

camssa:b8908501-815a-41dd-9b15-85c3d4f30ca5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON is being features at the The ENISA 5G Security controls matrix, which is a comprehensive and dynamic matrix of security controls and best practices for 5G networks, to support the national authorities in the EU Member States with implementing the technical measures of the EU’s 5G Cybersecurity Toolbox. \r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf\r
\r
ENISA: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/5g-security-controls-matrix'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ae6260b-fb33-472e-90d2-ce34d301b829 .

camssa:b89350c6-deef-4804-8fd2-9f9fa5485d43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence that the specification can be partially implemented, so it is considered that it is only meant to be used as a whole. \r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7b1a76b-eddb-4ba0-8ada-0b92a7777118 .

camssa:b89505d3-2f24-4ade-9ab9-8fbbd9586925 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification does support multilingualism by allowing metadata entries in multiple languages. This ensures that software documentation can be accessible and understandable to a diverse audience, aligning with the principle of making public services more inclusive across language barriers. By enabling multilingual entries, it caters to the needs of various user groups and supports interoperability at an international level, which is consistent with the EIF’s recommendation on multilingualism.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89d1ad57-6b12-4c35-bded-78c0041c655c .

camssa:b89c97a4-a72b-4f2a-8b99-53ce661ddfab a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:b89fabc6-0819-4627-b2ac-cadde1891956 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON provides a flexible and widely supported data interchange format that can be leveraged to establish common ground for data exchange between organizations. By agreeing to use JSON as a common language for data representation, organizations can enhance their interoperability, and streamline communication and collaboration across different systems and entities.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4aa5fc9f-fac1-4e05-87ad-4e3ffe5c3038 .

camssa:b8a8fa82-ee0e-425f-b924-2cdabacb5623 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is included in 5 national catalogues. They belong to Member States which comply with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the EIF according to the NIFO factsheets. \r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5edc11b8-b6c6-4b8c-8f6e-a236fcbf61db .

