camssa:b8bfe659-5c66-4a13-b056-bf0345ef46fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State that includes ETSI TS 102 640-2 in their national catalogue with its National \r
Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories: 1. Conceptual model for integrated \r
public services provision, 2. interoperability layers, and 3. interoperability principles.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public\\x02administration-factsheets-2021'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cd1493c-4566-4612-a65b-552754735f87 .

camssa:b8c8bb2f-364c-4bbf-8f76-f5b2ba939842 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Given the number of organisations that contribute to the funding of OAS (Google, IBM, Microsoft, etc) there can be stated that the specification has widespread market acceptance.  It is also being implemented in the RISIS project, which aims to develop an e-infrastructure that supports full virtual transnational access to research datasets.  \r
\r
Automatic Query-centric API for Routine Access to Linked Data:\r
https://iswc2017.semanticweb.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/MainProceedings/430.pdf\r
\r
RISIS webpage:\r
https://www.risis2.eu/about/\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79136471-ee83-433e-bdd9-798b9045694b .

camssa:b8ccdf30-2fe8-4330-a3a3-a0b6d4f3e675 a cav:Score,
