    cav:value "1" .

camssa:b920582a-8dfd-4f99-855c-c497e4ad6fc2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of NUTS is not related to the secure exchange of data. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:370b2da5-51eb-4cf8-9412-9f11fcfd3347 .

camssa:b9209c30-814b-4b2e-800c-b30b03fb8b7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF specifications are made available free of charge to the general public via the website. IETF drafts are published publicly discussions take place online in archived mailing lists. Moreover, the IETF Datatracker is the day-to-day front-end to the IETF database for people who work on IETF standards. It contains data about the documents, working groups, meetings, agendas, minutes, presentations, and more, of the IETF._x000D_\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision._x000D_\r
See:_x000D_\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/_x000D_\r
http://www.ietf.org/id-info/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8ecabcf-b7e2-440b-a875-73e2ee90c792 .

camssa:b92cd7ff-130e-4746-aab6-92e94db5426c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

