camssa:ba2f7504-c0c2-40a8-b48e-5f8d9a5dbbab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval process so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the Request for Comments (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications. \r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.  \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/  \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8329607b-278a-41c5-83b4-e9697485b27c .

camssa:ba31cdfb-9e0b-473d-be6f-e2376bd56876 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Reviews from CCSDS specification documents are not open to the general public.  Instead, only members and associated agencies can take part in the review process by submitting their comment to the review coordinator.\r
\r
CCSDS review documents:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/review/default.aspx'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:916327f1-f968-486a-bbb0-813c44dd6004 .

camssa:ba3b5e68-02e2-4262-8bb4-5239103d7223 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CSV specification itself does not provide any built-in means for protecting against unauthorised changes. Although the CSV specification does not provide these features directly, they can be implemented in conjunction with the systems or applications that handle CSV files to ensure proper access control and data protection.\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0fd1beb-40f6-454b-b881-92e67b378880 .

camssa:ba41f8a6-86fd-42f1-851d-019865b93e0f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ba4557e0-0d0c-4075-8568-7d0fb5884bd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d228d69-43a6-44d3-916f-0417a572c550 .

camssa:ba478eab-f9a4-4b38-b2ca-ca3f4ead5f9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification supports diverse technological environments given that it ensures broad applicability and adaptability.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6db28fa-6e56-4836-ab30-757f3c3511fb .

camssa:ba4acb86-8d59-4562-8df0-6a4c85f77ba0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The SCIM (System for Cross-domain Identity Management) standard is maintained by the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF). The development and maintenance of SCIM are carried out within the IETF's SCIM working group.

IETF Working Groups: https://www.ietf.org/how/wgs/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f9ea611-b024-4501-8a67-ebfef384c729 .

camssa:ba4cdfd5-b9b6-4e60-8d9c-e0786d8aa041 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of TIFF/IT is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e93914c-2f7c-440e-96a2-7fa2f1301f4e .

camssa:ba4dd339-696d-4c91-a783-0dcc325caf8b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:ba528970-91e1-4c62-9adf-474363ba1823 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4017a1ae4d077fbb3847280a1c20b41bf00c32d65fc9beaa2bea8cce550ac463 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ba565507-68c1-4c3d-a710-b7fd18499e8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML provides a set of components enabling users (data users) to store and work with any type of electronic content. The specification's ebRIM and ebRS components provides an ebXML infrastructure model, as well as a service interface contributing to this end. Therefore, ebXML facilitates the modelling of business processes.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f85ab39c-9e2e-4b94-a0eb-8d023a398d63 .

camssa:ba596163-ab5a-4980-a65c-f6ccf15780aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification makes use of optional classes that allow it to be more flexible towards the purpose it is working for. An example can be the Participation class that allows to define roles within a certain context.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22'"""@en ;
