camssa:bad91e01-c4c8-460d-9876-f9ccd496deba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There is documentation and examples of the use of services of Regional Internet Services, and examples of tooling and rooter implementations: \r
https://www.ripe.net/manage-ips-and-asns/resource-management/certification\r
https://www.arin.net/resources/rpki/\r
https://www.apnic.net/get-ip/faqs/rpki/\r
https://afrinic.net/resource-certification\r
https://www.lacnic.net/640/2/lacnic/general-information-resource-certification-system-rpki\r
https://rpki.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\r
https://www.juniper.net/documentation/en_US/junos/topics/topic-map/bgp-origin-as-validation.html\r
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/ios-xml/ios/iproute_bgp/configuration/15-s/irg-15-s-book/irg-origin-as.html\r
https://infocenter.alcatel-lucent.com/public/7750SR160R4A/index.jsp?topic=%2Fcom.sr.unicast%2Fhtml%2Fbgp.html&cp=22_4_7_2&anchor=d2e5366\r
\r
\r
And there are various websites where compliance can be tested and is even present in various software packages that support the standard:\r
https://ct.cloudflare.com/logs/cirrus\r
https://nusenu.github.io/RPKI-Observatory/\r
https://rpki-validator.ripe.net/bgp-preview\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e306596-ad75-472e-bd7b-3adb1bf03ea6 .

