    cav:value "20" .

camssa:bb3dbfa2-43a4-4680-b14d-3ab54ae881fb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EIRA as the reference architecture for developing digital public services in the European context, it covers horizontally from legal to technical aspects, going through organisational and semantic aspects. This way, the specification allows to approach data portability from different perspectives: 1) any possible legal conditions or requirements; 2) organisational limitations and agreements that help overcome transitions between systems; 3) data related requirements and limitations; and last but not least 4) technical requirements that ensure the reuse of best practices and components, as well as international standards that reduce risks. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a948114-88eb-48d1-a242-586c53136c70 .

camssa:bb415978-5a45-40f5-bd21-206935a276b3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-58010a47630ff9ea23336bf3fc558deff59905e0292551fcabc95740082cb378 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb41dc56-eb3e-4470-8a55-bbf36384d33f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification does not guarantee authenticity and authentication of the roles/agents involved in data transactions, but provides mechanisms to facilitate it such as Hostname Verification, the hostname can be specified in the sasl-init frame and the open frame, allowing AMQP proxies to determine the correct back-end service and validate client credentials.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10b27a79-04c2-41d7-90df-684db621282a .

camssa:bb42c2a0-79b2-4c6c-906f-6b96e9a4b4dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb43cf67-7c4b-444b-aa00-0d32bab9e2c0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb4ab81e-196f-4077-a993-882303aecb86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Indexed Database API specification is developed by a non-European organisation. Therefore, the specification cannot be considered a European standard.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ee5e82f-0493-4152-a01e-30b09d70d8bb .

camssa:bb4db66b-705c-429a-a01a-021ec6e4fccc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of LegalRuleML aims also to support the semantic perspective of data by providing a core specification for modelling legal documents based on requirements of the business domain. It can be part of the Linked Open Data environment not only supporting the data structuring for raw data but also of rules in conjunction with their functionality and usage. Without rules or axioms, legal concepts constitute just a taxonomy. \r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html\r
\r
Linked Data W3C: \r
https://www.w3.org/wiki/LinkedData"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1150135b-bd92-4e50-845d-0d9caa4656c9 .

camssa:bb4f6f91-af98-42b9-a725-88b99014f5c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is aimed to represent information in order to be readable in both formats, machine-readable, and human-readable format. Despite this, RDF does not help the availability of interfaces with internal information.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d4f636c-785e-497a-af74-77877b7f1684 .

camssa:bb58b369-36e7-4f89-8733-8c0704177ff3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The TOSCA cloud-orchestration service provides both the structure of a cloud-based service and orchestration models describing the way the service is managed throughout its lifetime. Although TOSCA offers an end-to-end approach, the specification may facilitate the exposure of interfaces within public administration's services. It is the case of the past CELAR project, which was meant to provide automatic, multi-grained resource allocation for cloud applications and boost administrative performance (see CELAR project reference, Cloud Information System report).\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Glossary section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969419\r
\r
CELAR project reference, Cloud Information System report:\r
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/317790/reporting\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84fe8864-c7e5-4b25-b571-30b171131475 .

camssa:bb59a3de-e5c7-44cb-ace7-76d3f410e78b a cav:Score,
