camssa:bb633ea4-74a3-4335-9447-254b26f768b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DAPS is not related to enabling the long-term preservation of data/information/knowledge (electronic records included). Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27775014-9ee9-4fb5-9ccd-ada38ff84e5b .

camssa:bb636049-6099-4561-bc22-ef019081c7e4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17bea234285e6e633e4e21105358610ad5f5f0eaaf82f4bd50cb64ec11538984 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb63fad1-55bc-406c-ba79-175832e7ecd3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bb6675eb-55ab-4056-9a5d-d7b24b9e7166 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'With the privacy architecture suggested by this specification, personal data can be exchanged on a private, peer-to-peer basis using communication channels identified and secured by verification methods in DID documents. Moreover, verifiable credentials, when associated with DIDs, enable users to assert their identity and qualifications in a privacy-preserving and tamper-evident manner.

DIDs restriction of access W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#keep-personal-data-private

Nasdaq Verifiable Credentials:
https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/what-are-decentralized-identifiers-did-and-how-will-they-boost-web3'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9be6b903-0cc2-4622-8bc8-2b4e0558a592 .

camssa:bb6ef3f1-7324-4958-ba72-09013b4f2b3a a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/9e4b0040-ebb4-4535-b3bf-d9d7a1910e49"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:bb75b97d-deec-4007-bda2-72b89f064b95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the key principles of the OAIS model is that digital objects and metadata must be preserved over long periods of time, and that their authenticity and integrity must be ensured throughout the preservation lifecycle. To support this principle, the OAIS model includes a range of features and functions that help to ensure the authenticity and integrity of digital objects and metadata such as the data provenance, data integrity and digital signatures.\r
\r
OAIS specification:\r
https://public.ccsds.org/Pubs/650x0m2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04e4d015-78bc-4009-8140-88edb4163414 .

camssa:bb78bd6f-f9bf-4092-acc0-715d4ee979f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The European Union (EU) Member States are currently implementing the INSPIRE Directive and related regulations, included in the ISA programme. This projects includes the usage of XSLT included in a catalogue of standards at EU level too.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ies-svn.jrc.ec.europa.eu/projects/registry-development/wiki/Re3gistry_1_0_documentation#_cp3"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dde71ca8-0cc7-4200-b5bd-d4e467046e05 .

camssa:bb862b5e-1430-4427-bb1e-cda2073d1411 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb87e47a-1870-4e25-83f5-7c4f6d84d7d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family is a recommendation of the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C), an international community that develops web standards. The W3C is a global organization and not specific to any particular region or country. Therefore, the specification itself is not a European standard.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea47e2b6-02cc-4cda-90dc-839e7e06fce5 .

camssa:bb89bc83-1a7c-40e2-91f9-64feaede8db1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Data processing accuracy is a broader concern that encompasses various aspects of information handling, including data input, processing algorithms, storage, and output. The accuracy of data processing is typically addressed at higher layers of the system architecture and involves considerations beyond the OSI model.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02106588-88ae-4c91-94dc-3f8a67e20df5 .

camssa:bb8de818-fddb-4325-8ecd-4aa9c91bb367 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe137c42-67b9-4cdc-a365-de21f7a12354 .

camssa:bb929532-4282-4ca3-bfcf-b7b9d1d757d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OASIS has established a comprehensive Technical Committee (TC) process that invites participation from all relevant stakeholders during the specification development journey. For every major and minor release, a public review phase is incorporated, and during this period, feedback from the community is collected and made transparently available for everyone to view and consult. All details pertaining to TC activities are hosted and are readily accessible for reference.\r
\r
OASIS Policies Guidelines: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:efca695d-730b-491d-88aa-57317a67696f .

camssa:bb9646ab-ee4c-4c66-ad22-d4afb6f7b2f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:bb9891eb-4af9-4fb7-9de9-2312872b9516 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39ffef052c31580b50b418f3991e9de7db4dc182fcf96f5a447d7f8e09560612 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bb999eb7-ec58-4159-9436-e69ebf1f0dc7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SMP is aimed to ease the identification of parties in data exchange. This data exchange can be part of a public service delivered by European Institutions. By easing the discoverability and the connection between parties, the specifications can help and foster the delivery of European Public Services including multilingual ones.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0357075e-acba-4b1d-aa28-24b2c3b9459c .

camssa:bb99af0a-9470-4ff0-a6ac-d1bf8b84112c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Following the purpose of the TC in charge of its development, LegalDocML can ease the accessibility of legal and administrative information commonly used and developed by public organisations and government bodies. The implementation within LEOS project demonstrates the usefulness of the specification in the visibility and the decision-making process of public administrations. Therefore, it can be concluded that the specification fosters the visibility of administrative rules, data, services and decision-making of a public administration.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php\r
\r
LEOS: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/justice-law-and-security/solution/leos-open-source-software-editing-legislation"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c1de357-54cd-45ac-848e-d5187669cadb .

camssa:bb9cc08b-21d3-4283-9c55-d71827971765 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:bba3ea98-f84a-4b8f-87e2-506caeca032d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "82%AssessmentScoreAverage",
