camssa:bc521d9b-218a-4335-8257-a15eaad90aa2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OAS is an open-source, royalty-free specification.  It is also available with any restrictions related to Fair, Reasonable, and Non Discriminatory ((F)RAND) rights, and it can be accessed from its website and in the Github repository.\r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation\r
\r
OAS governace rules:\r
https://www.openapis.org/participate/how-to-contribute/governance'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a79ea276-8ec2-47e8-b614-2cb916c223d6 .

camssa:bc556840-6c3e-48ed-a05f-517b586e9e69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Connecting Europe Facility (CEF) is meant to focus its activity on the improvement of European Cooperation processes and solutions, for both, private and public sectors. The development of the specifications included in the eDelivery building block performance are raised up by CEF eDelivery Team, which does not need to open their decisions by means of public consultations. However, CEF provides several communities focused on gather information related to best practices regarding the implementation of eDelivery. Moreover, the community eDelivery Governance aims to focus efforts to open the operational matters related to CEF building Blocks to all stakeholders for contribution. This fact helps to ensure that all parts take part in the development process, private sector, user organisations and standardisations \r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/eDelivery\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4aca260d-843f-4541-9391-0cd9062c56ae .

