camssa:bc6c5f3e-2953-4b7f-a0ad-ac920fa55760 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF specification does not give any provision for the protection of personal data, nonetheless, there can be found some communities addressing the way RDF-based restrictions for data protection can be applied.  The academic paper below gives a framework for the compliance of RDF data processing against the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).\r
\r
RDF-based Restrictions for Data-protection:\r
https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2548/paper-07.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a70e3ff5-d0f5-41ee-a760-ab9a9b7472e5 .

camssa:bc6e9801-892d-4072-9bb1-b1e5dae17efc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bc73cc47-29e4-4646-99ac-a1607df3aeb3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-25deb65536af2c7e82f921c56df2c7e21093b2c06fdddd63021b4bccea0b9cd7 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bc757fb4-cd4f-48d3-bf11-857edbd9dee3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI and ENISA are recommending its use for the development of software. It is a key aspect to consider that the specification is being considered and recognised for the development of public services.\r
\r
ETSI SmartM2M; Security; Standards Landscape and best practices:  \r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103500_103599/103533/01.01.01_60/tr_103533v010101p.pdf \r
\r
ENISA Advancing Software Security in the EU: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/advancing-software-security-through-the-eu-certification-framework\r
\r
ENISA Good Practices for Security of IoT - Secure Software Development Lifecycle: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/good-practices-for-security-of-iot-1"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:13b0b326-a1be-4da7-a2b2-9b15e73444fa .

camssa:bc75958e-6391-4e86-827d-ba6e5c352d6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """WSDL has adopted the "+xml" convention that is described in the IETF RFC 3023 defining XML data types and its security considerations. As an XML document, every implementation can have different security requirements. Even though, taking into account the considerations WSDL allows the secure and trustworthy data exchange between the stakeholders involved. \r
\r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/\r
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3023.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c458263-90ac-4caf-8ccb-3d16134cea22 .

camssa:bc7f51af-6eb4-4ce8-b264-bbd21718b354 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e370a4af17e89cbb70bb5079082a1e21cdee85435c8fc30b12a8987f18db367f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bc7fefa2-8d39-4521-9a8f-94679db35db4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'E-ARK was initially funded by the European Commission under the E-ARK project. Like all European-funded project, it is distributed under a royalty-free license, and can be publicly accessed for anyone to study.\r
\r
E-ARK supporting guidelines:\r
https://dilcis.eu/guidelines/supporting-guidelines'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd3ceed4-93c1-43cd-823e-12a7b9dfce3a .

camssa:bc84ca44-a968-494a-a061-3ef9739baf78 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP is an RDF vocabulary for representing data catalogues that allows data owners to provide metadata about the datasets they publish. By describing catalogues, datasets and resources, a publisher makes them easily searchable and discoverable. In fact, DCAT-AP is used for the publication of datasets in linked open data portals at a National and European scale (European Data Portal)\r
\r
DCAT-AP for data portals in Europe:                                                                                                                                      https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/releases\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ca0c2f0-3668-4fbd-b8ff-b5bb696a4750 .

camssa:bc892d02-4940-448d-9b87-cacb0d9edeab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 has a specific section called "Session Layer" whose purpose is to provide the means necessary for cooperating presentation-entities to organise and to synchronise their dialogue and to manage their data exchange. One of the services provided is token management, which allows the presentation-entities to control explicitly whose turn it is to exercise certain control functions.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17596893-901d-47b4-8f88-ed5622d63831 .

camssa:bc8c63fb-c82e-49e7-a9cb-1e262cda8277 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f41cca0d171e6f64dbc2bdeae9fbc87f2ea51ac00185b22114d59ab8a06e78d0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bc8f561f-46b0-44a6-8cc0-716c874279c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By providing information and access to web services across borders, WSDL eases the reuse of data and resources between administrations and stakeholders. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9803c4dc-1273-4349-8e18-86996cd163e3 .

camssa:bc9615b0-5f71-40b2-af24-4d3dc6d01150 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In the specification's reference document, there is a list of referenced documents necessary for the \r
application of the present document, among those referenced documents is included the "Secure Hash \r
Standard (SHS)" that enables secure processing of data.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference, page 7:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:722d0c70-acf4-4b0d-b07a-5131a6599c3f .

camssa:bc97b999-193f-4c9a-9ffa-1cf8801dd510 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Participation in ISO technical committee work is possible, depending on the membership category of the participant. Public reviews are not foreseen, provided that the Public Administration was a subscriber member.\r
\r
ISO membership manual, 'ISO member rights, good practice and obligations' section:\r
https://www.iso.org/publication/PUB100399.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e86af909-69b7-4e5f-ad7f-dd77f0eebe3f .

camssa:bc9c451e-e55e-4b7a-b013-ba3cc0b4606d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OSI is independent of any technological specification and can be implemented without dependencies since its a reference model to facilitate the interconnection between open systems and being cross compatible. 

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b089b692-8933-4e4c-9774-628024aed9fc .

camssa:bc9d2897-4e77-47b6-8795-23ca1e5ebfa4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD 1.1 is publicly available for implementation and study for free on W3C's webpage. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema11-1/ https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema11-2/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:512d497c-2658-42c5-89e5-b85c30d01d31 .

camssa:bcaca656-ca09-44ce-bace-8c04979eb8a6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:bcad8876-025c-496c-a9ce-9fd1e7a48050 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, SMTP is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. SMTP is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on the SMTP specification (RFC 5321)\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c96f1ff-a675-44b5-9127-9fec91b78916 .

camssa:bcb00b2a-125f-41bc-93be-89d002d83f17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to e-accessibility, therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aabd6d91-6ee8-4250-a93b-c9ab9a2a4d50 .

camssa:bcb264a1-9541-40a6-837d-fcae554e9d99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS is independent of any specification and can be implemented without relying on other technologies.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e03c3e0-a709-4bba-908a-669dbd4c0899 .

camssa:bcbf383f-7883-4fa1-9369-e1e0f3b8f51d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d90c4c0-2076-47df-aa8e-c34115bfb483 .

camssa:bcbff0b7-61d5-4b6f-8a71-55aa635e3f1f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of JSON is not related to the protection of personal data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e328859b-1579-4a3b-89ce-4c8076dc5882 .

camssa:bcc1cfbc-b920-4a06-b412-c49552801dfe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While HTTPS can contribute to the security and privacy of the data being transmitted, it does not comprehensively address the overall management, visibility, or control of administrative procedures, rules, data, and services.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab58a97c-b704-4b6e-b4b2-9c69b4c5c072 .

camssa:bcc6eea9-3e8b-42fe-87f8-6df0b33e8db0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) primarily focuses on securing the transport of DNS queries and responses, adding an additional layer of security to the DNS resolution process. DoH significantly improves online security and privacy by securing DNS queries and minimizing exposure of sensitive information during resolution processes, which is crucial in secure processing of data.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2c44487-6015-4744-a3ef-c01af007f357 .

camssa:bcc71355-f2a3-4118-9fad-82b7a5720c42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is a standardized protocol, and its specifications are designed to work across different technology stacks and platforms. SCIM is not tied to any specific programming language, operating system, or identity management system. 

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8785907-d45f-4461-b2db-334093ff048d .

camssa:bcc96969-f0e0-4417-b263-e80f10d0eca5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:bccca61f-4419-4ffa-9fc2-5096bf16f95c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In terms of administrative procedures, rules data, and services, the OGC TrainingDML-AI standard does not
explicitly mention these aspects. However, the detailed metadata it provides could potentially be used to
inform such procedures and rules, particularly in the context of preparing and managing training data for AI/ML applications.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e100bbd8-1207-44de-9663-78fccafb596b .

camssa:bcce7755-cede-456d-a2ce-109dc5e31db7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The main purpose of ODF is to exchange information through the internet, and its purpose is not related to the availability of interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:534c6453-4e7f-4fe0-a31c-cf5173dc9c6f .

camssa:bcd42a16-1344-4d2d-b76f-c2175b73b10c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is not enough information to determine that the ISAE 3402 has been included within an agreement \r
between organisations or countries involved in the provision of public services.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9a9111b-3a07-4c10-8b10-20a4b60b10de .

camssa:bce2add5-c396-446c-8337-ead76ae775a2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:bce42947-a8d7-4740-83f8-9567bca03570 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e18cc4da-f9a3-4ec2-9fe3-18caa19d5334 .

camssa:bcec3d2f-f86b-44ce-925e-94c68579c4d3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RegOrg is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, RegOrg can define the interoperability aspects of the "Core Data Model" and "Data" ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95f22d6c-7c5c-4114-b7b0-d5b894a7df1e .

camssa:bced8230-b39b-4946-9c17-94ca442fc21b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c09094de9d71f12686896827a205db683b6df58fa363bc5be2a7d99989e7dd0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bcefe0fa-7f7b-4fc5-8bc0-ea1650c902ea a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bcf293d5-a944-4591-a9c4-6e740a2301ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) develops solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks.\r
\r
Specification development process by the ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications\r
\r
Detailed document ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60421d31-90db-4893-83a9-e7f448651b84 .

camssa:bcf3664e-7b18-4e68-bb08-8b512d2904b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching the different national catalogues, no European Member State has been found to recommend 
the Extensible Forms Description Language specification.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:683563f7-b86f-42c0-9970-5888e7947aed .

camssa:bcf40db9-6a03-4894-8fd0-235414094377 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bcf9f16b-6352-431c-8b35-13857ef79ade a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary facilitates the process for institutions to describe data about the location aspects of public organisations, citizens, and businesses. In this context, although the specification is not designed for data reuse, it can help to reuse information among administrations and systems, improving the delivery of public services.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7371e3b-be5d-4ce1-b5bc-1410c2a58cae .

camssa:bcfc2c9a-75cb-4ecb-af48-19dc6b4cfe77 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1435ad894742693c2b99e329ef12399cd411ed6900f49b9658fd2231de3f201a ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:bcfe9d12-4ac2-47cb-898e-6aad05726403 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 5.1.3.2 of the specification is about cloud data portability, which is the ability to transfer data from one cloud service to another cloud service or between a cloud service customer’s system and a cloud service. This section talks about different considerations related to this topic, specially the retrieval of cloud service customer data, which is closely related to long-term preservation of eletrconic resources. \r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff6024ec-f2f8-44d4-a4fb-0109111243d5 .

camssa:bd022d14-a25a-4fce-a1d2-1954d3f3700f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ab64f97c21ac8b84c75d6f52a89765b1c8fd1856d2d2060926d05e94f306a88d ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:bd09b5c7-adc6-45e3-93e9-5e4b7730e7aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NUTS classification has been developed by a lage community within the European Commission (EC) and all the EC patents are available with any restrictions related to (F)RAND.\r
\r
European Commission reference, Regulation (EC) No 1059/2003 document:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1405939838475&uri=CELEX:32003R1059\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74addffc-46dd-4a8f-bc1f-5c70748dd76b .

camssa:bd0dae47-9b34-4f04-8637-7456fd558439 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """eDelivery SMP 1.10 is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, eDelivery SMP 1.10 can define the interoperability aspects of “Metadata Management Component”, “Metadata Management Service”, and “Interoperable European Solution Component” ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:802a332c-a7e3-4e0a-abac-ce6cc4596107 .

camssa:bd120036-9ec1-4782-b919-79929e794828 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

