camssa:bd850d0a-adc3-45b0-aed6-be82e11a1315 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP Cookies is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain way.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies: \r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1f58c08d-6137-4fee-9217-c005d6e36653 .

camssa:bd884878-dd13-445c-8219-6034f153c8e3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of IPsec. In "Testing topologies for the evaluation of IPsec implementations", the IPsec effectiveness is assessed. In this study, IPsec is tested in order to achieve confidence in its effectiveness and correctness. The study also concludes that IPsec architecture supplies a superior standard of protection when it is used with a proper configuration and over a correct implementation.

"Testing topologies for the evaluation of IPsec implementations" study:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221435103_Testing_Topologies_for_the_Evaluation_of_IPSEC_Implementations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:49221df5-dbaa-4d41-871f-f91b0f155241 .

camssa:bd8ab949-9776-4719-b344-270ad2ba0e62 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c8a79448e829e27f47318879de4899c3a6404aa66d7d8954e7a680cf6e5d1ca2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bd8b9646-d652-4b7b-84ad-d35634976291 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Technical Committee (TC) CYBER (Cybersecurity) provides feature requests to open source projects and results of implementation experience to open source communities; however, not in national platforms.\r
\r
TC CYBER reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/cyber-security/tc-cyber-roadmap'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:718526c3-118a-41a5-9887-e7b93ceff09a .

camssa:bd90e3ff-a58b-47a5-a8ab-b413a0da82ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There is no Member State that includes CLV in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1e5762c-0779-4e70-a54b-01e8fd02f034 .

camssa:bd971e68-e1a1-4745-ac91-dc48a1e91f86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. Moreover, there is a public review in the TC process.\r
 \r
OASIS guideline:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26\r
The Akoma Ntoso review process: \r
http://www.akomantoso.org/?p=141"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:719198f0-57d6-447e-888d-8bda67e32220 .

camssa:bd98d8fa-c897-4b33-b24e-88576552c2c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) develops solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. \r
\r
Specification development process by the ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/about#8\r
\r
Detailed document ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7037f54-0c08-4e57-ae28-c56516982dc0 .

camssa:bda4e2d8-a03c-4047-be16-c83b330b658d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:bdb2fdd6-af3a-4326-a880-3dc63f062e56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence of the inclusion of WAI-ARIA in an open repository/catalogue of standards at European level.\r
\r
EUOS repository of standards:\r
https://www.standict.eu/standards-repository\r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5e80849-48d5-482c-84a6-e3ebb9bc58c1 .

camssa:bdb80342-2886-4a60-85ac-951d7d579aff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CPOV enabels digital service delivery channels in many ways among which we could highlight the browse of public organizations by its function, managing a cross-border repository of public services and organizations, and sharing information G2G (government to government), G2B (government to business) and G2C (government to citizen).

CPOV joinup:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary/distribution/core-public-organisation-vocabulary-version-100-pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ceae8616-2679-4808-8d0b-a120fc275eb8 .

camssa:bdbb616a-e6a8-4562-8eff-f94412243bd9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bdbbdc0b-073a-4d41-a7b2-d772f970d36f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no study analysing the effectiveness of OCSP. However, there are several papers claiming that the\r
CRL (certificate revocation list) has been bypassed in favour of the OCSP specification (e.g. from the IEEE),\r
as well as forums (e.g. stackexchange) stating that OCSP offers a faster service.\r
\r
IEEExplore reference:\r
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/1045949\r
\r
Stackexchange reference:\r
https://security.stackexchange.com/questions/134100/difference-between-ocsp-crl-and-cdp'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f0166a8-cc77-4344-bcbc-5df70c1dbb21 .

camssa:bdc4d6fc-929a-4274-bd86-dd83d09d8d5c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bdcce9ee-0b90-463f-8c66-a08c30bbf6af a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DQV is useful for describing the quality of the different categories of a dataset. It can help identify where a dataset has more or less quality. Therefore, the specification facilitates the modeling of business processes.

DQV reference: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26f7ee82-55e1-4e15-9d31-9a16cca8f047 .

camssa:bdd20c0b-5e7c-478e-b446-eb74087006ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec is developed by IETF which is based in the USA, thus the specification cannot be regarded as a 
European Standard.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b55394f5-7032-474d-a23a-344837a0ccdb .

camssa:bdd3231b-e167-476a-a2cd-d01ed3322ffe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SAML 2.0 is not included in any catalogue of standards at supra-national level."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4d19071-fbb1-4f69-a887-18f9fd9ac436 .

camssa:bdd7564a-be34-431c-9ec4-84d2f76eb1cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 is a messaging protocol for exchanging information in a structured way, it uses XML for its message format. As the protocol is a messaging system for exchanging information in a structured way, it helps to promote the visibility and comprehensibility of the administrative rules. In addition, it is a key enabler for web services reuse across borders along with UDDI and WSDL. \r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  \r
\r
Differences in SOAP Versions:\r
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSAW57_8.5.5/com.ibm.websphere.nd.multiplatform.doc/ae/cwbs_soapverdiffs.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:51bba846-c267-4a59-98c9-4df8afc9f61c .

camssa:bddbc4d3-865c-43c9-8521-c0374a5d0885 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bddc86ab-296d-4dba-ab22-ee5a8cc2fe5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While CIM NGSI-LD API does not mention any specific action to support the reuse of relevant information when needed, the principle of reuse and alignment of concepts and relationships are embedded in CIM NGSI-LD API,  Linked Data principles can be applied to create a web of interconnected and reusable data, which aligns with the goal of the Once-Only Principle to avoid redundant data collection.

GS CIM 009: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/CIM/001_099/009/01.07.01_60/gs_CIM009v010701p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b4c4839-f42a-4f67-8eb5-6c03ee0bc479 .

camssa:bddcdf8b-171d-4d78-a802-1b9fcf849ee8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bde1ad1c-286f-49ec-bcf3-58d68205e5e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL fosters digital exchange of business documents and invoices by establising a commonly agreed vocabulary of business information transfer. An example of a project implementing UBL for such purpose is ESPD, whose main objective is to create a single procurement document for all European Member States.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
ESPD Handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0dea4c54-cf27-4bd9-b331-cfea9b0d2710 .

camssa:bde5ed07-7e06-41c8-beb7-1b3bb892cd3b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:bdec4ac6-0a61-4c99-ac7d-909bf6c7a6e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP is maintained and developed by IETF which is an international community developing open\r
standards.\r
\r
IETF developer community:\r
https://www.ietf.org/about/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee0d0e15-710d-4c58-bfc2-b72a9afbe632 .

camssa:bdf4414c-96b3-4441-8ad0-87f2d65dbe48 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:bdf8fccb-e3a6-48a0-b6d8-3412a0aedb8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA is meant to augment semantics in languages such as HTML5 and SVG2, or to serve as an accessibility enhancement technology in other languages that do not specifically include support for ARIA. In this sense, customisation may evolve faster than other web host standards, enabling additional digital service delivery channels.

WAI-ARIA reference, section 1.4:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#co-evolution'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27721e11-5010-41e0-9520-4133269515c0 .

camssa:bdfe4eef-5e36-4533-9a10-496edb094d97 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:be1b37ba-d5e4-4fd6-b960-24a638fa924e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SAML 2.0 specification allows for customization to a certain extent, and this flexibility is one of the reasons for its widespread adoption. However, there are boundaries to ensure interoperability and security. \r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74527411-3339-42fa-a8b0-6cf1f3e51e62 .

camssa:be1d4f31-57ab-4a3a-bbd1-fc2e77ee1ec4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After searching for a certification or conformity test to validate this document, no tool has been found that assesses the conformity of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c19cfeea-4299-4eb2-9fd2-4868d9e3de32 .

camssa:be1ebcc4-6a03-4a96-8277-a09fd3d1c448 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e46f1a4a060cc7e143e32e4833c94af9164c37bc0d4c844bd1fa974ffb2ac225 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:be213b31-6070-43f4-ad80-c19350953869 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc272cd8a2e3e9c5e4edaa5ac7d59735c377a9db89d6958335a2cf0538761ab3 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:be2c3dc4-cd19-4614-8251-490d90f3028a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 offers addresses spaces allowing public services to have unique, globally routable IP addresses for every device. This can simplify direct access to various administrative services without the need for complex NAT (Network Address Translation) configurations. 

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c78ae67-ae18-4723-ad62-12d82a44191a .

camssa:be301f8a-d443-4353-ad66-ea59eb749028 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol defines the schemas and protocols required for entities to publish data, negotiate usage agreements, and access data as part of a federation of technical systems termed a dataspace. Therefore, its use improves the interoperability, data sovereignity and standardization of the IDS ecosystem, which is important for the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol Specification: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1cbd5a59-0642-4bc3-a720-bfa288dd1ba8 .

camssa:be34eb47-c140-45b8-aa83-f3da4db9a06b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:be35da6f-7576-42a4-bc36-5f93d621f379 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XSD 1.1 is supporting the second level of maturity of Tim Berners-Lee's 5-stars schema for open data. It eases the availability of the data and structures XML files. Additionally, XSD 1.1 is implied within the RDF 1.1 XML Syntax, used for the serialisation of RDF documents as XML. Therefore, XSD fosters the publication of data as Linked Open Data. \r
\r
Moreover, although XSD is not related directly with Open Vocabularies, it can be found included within the Linked Open Vocabularies. It is possible because datatypes defined by XSD are commonly used as rdfs:range by properties. \r
\r
See: \r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/\r
https://lov.linkeddata.es/dataset/lov/vocabs/xsd"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1475c37b-bff5-484e-a1a3-e79318a7c354 .

camssa:be4a099e-ce80-43e8-9cfa-f48d28fb9ef9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:be4ccea4-de6f-4210-b7a9-6cdd6804c017 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the supporting documents of this CIM NGSI-LD API is ETSI GR CIM 007, which identifies the security and privacy aspects that are relevant when building systems based on the NGSI-LD API and the NGSI-LD information model. In this case, the specification is aligned with the General Data Protection Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2016/679, abbreviated GDPR) is a European Union regulation on information privacy in the European Union (EU) and the European Economic Area (EEA).

GR CIM 007: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/CIM/001_099/007/01.01.02_60/gr_cim007v010102p.pdf

GDPR: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32016R0679'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a30c6fa9-40db-46c0-b4bd-b1e4305ff7af .

camssa:be4d05b4-1386-4b9b-bdbb-0e5a80bebe8f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """It is worth to note that the specifications is freely available at the SDO's website. Moreover, SMP previous version can be found for free at the European Platform Joinup for its consultation and use.\r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505000"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89e128f4-45c2-4174-a000-4a1e29536b5a .

camssa:be4d0798-bfb8-4905-94cf-a0ec940af0e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Testing, Experimentation and Open Source (TST) Working Group provides feature requests to open source projects and results of implementation experience to open source communities. ETSI, as an acknowledged European standardisation, offers different channels for the creation of communities and the sharing of data and results in European platforms.\r
\r
TST NFV reference:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/NFV/NFV-WGs-amp-EGs-ToR'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:512c8d1f-c5cc-4a36-b068-540a35290777 .

camssa:be5b5ca6-f5bc-4fb9-b24a-d07c6f8775b4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not related to provide means for restriction of access to information / data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f7001d1-b7cc-48b2-b55c-b2f2189f958e .

