camssa:bffe0210-e5ca-4df1-b8c3-f257b2e73696 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After exhaustive research, several cross-border projects or initiatives that use OWL have been found. \r
\r
CELLAR is the repository of the Publications Office of the European Union. His main purpose is to disseminate the content and metadata created by the Publication Office. It drives the Publications Office’s major portals and its resources are semantically described by the CDM (Common Data Model), which is an OWL ontology. \r
\r
Another implementation at European Level is the Application Profile of DCAT developed for the description of the data included in the European Data Portal contributing to the openness of European data._x000D_\r
\r
CELLAR publication:_x000D_\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/50ecce27-857e-11e8-ac6a-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-73059305_x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
CELLAR description:_x000D_\r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/data/dataset/sparql-cellar-of-the-publications-office_x000D_\r
_x000D_\r
DCAT-AP Specification: _x000D_\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/distribution/dcat-ap-121-pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83461463-cfa0-445e-8683-5d13fdde6741 .

camssa:c0058016-a0b7-4469-85b8-e21f4b96d7fb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SHACL is not related in any way to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2323b15-5e88-4c9a-89d4-7f9d168d2b94 .

camssa:c007f2e0-1a61-4edb-a290-0ea61a7e803c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification is not a European Standard. However, it is an International Standard designated as ISO/IEC 19464:2014.

ISO.org Standard Catalog Reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/64955.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d5d32da-9bc4-4230-a977-292b8a8c2b1b .

camssa:c00ca630-2286-4407-a4f2-23bf9bae8e87 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e9e0cf4a339c837607828404dd0e9b360d643528fcc1df488a95ca67166acea3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c00ce0f0-c34c-4687-8de3-024a2a9fa715 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ESI/REM is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative procedures, rules data and \r
services, therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:91b8c670-89d0-4d9f-9fcc-69f1a5557f0b .

camssa:c00d7997-1d4a-4802-9208-b9c145c5fda2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed in 1991 by the IETF group, and it has become a widely used format for the transaction of different types of files over the internet. It is focused on the transfer via email, and it is supported by numerous mail software. This fact demonstrates the maturity of MIME for its use for the development of services and products.\r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6020bfd8-a1a9-4fcf-adcb-f7950603be69 .

camssa:c013d117-2cd9-40f5-a16f-90c437b20b17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 5 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. Examples of Member States including PAdES in their catalogues are France or Spain.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e035334-1b1a-4fc5-bc5b-f737451aaa89 .

camssa:c0188f1d-420b-4800-8e33-4068e709c8f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 provides a common time-stamping protocol and token profiles for a Trusted List Scheme Operator (TLSO) to provide information on the status and history of Trusted Service Provider (TSP) services. Since it has had three major versions it would be acceptable to consider it has a sufficient market acceptance for its use.

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d9be69c-135b-4949-ba45-8ca8f93e7859 .

camssa:c01a0409-9a05-4971-85e9-b327a39786f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of UDDI is not related to long term preservation of electronic records. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac3763bc-9ce1-48ba-a3d1-d1495126e7fe .

camssa:c01cc38b-85fe-451c-bfdf-816acea060ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e307649f-0033-446e-b54d-58e6f57f0a97 .

camssa:c024e5dc-86e1-4ba7-b244-e0dc33717d20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL provides a standardized way to describe web service interfaces, enabling interoperability between different software systems. This interoperability is crucial when building digital service delivery channels that involve communication between diverse applications and platforms.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b52dd5cd-b2e5-47d6-9aec-61cf62886a2e .

camssa:c027a8a5-00ba-43b0-aa52-573612425859 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The standardised terms and concepts within CIM NGSI-LD API can facilitate clearer communication and understanding between systems, which is beneficial for secure data exchange protocols. When different entities use the same standardised terms and classifications, it can reduce ambiguity and errors during data transmission, contributing to more secure and accurate exchanges.


ETSI Context Information Management (CIM); Security and Privacy:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/CIM/001_099/007/01.01.02_60/gr_cim007v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d99fe22-97fb-4cf1-b6b7-dff4ab9cbb2e .

