camssa:c044c493-0027-4b30-bd02-8cd789ca14c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of BFO is related to the provision of a hierarchy of categories to be used in multiple fields to classify and organise data. This core element of BFO is what gives it the possibility to be developed into an ontology dedicated to long term preservation of data, for example by referencing linked data via the use of IRIs.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e79e769-38f9-4e7a-aebc-d219e446eb38 .

camssa:c052c9f8-61a4-41ec-a31e-27f802b017d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After searching in the different official European websites, agencies such as ENISA or ETSI are recommending SAMSS as one of the reference frameworks for the development of secure software solutions. \r
\r
ETSI SmartM2M; Security; Standards Landscape and best practices:  \r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103500_103599/103533/01.01.01_60/tr_103533v010101p.pdf \r
\r
ENISA Advancing Software Security in the EU: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/advancing-software-security-through-the-eu-certification-framework\r
\r
ENISA Good Practices for Security of IoT - Secure Software Development Lifecycle: \r
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/good-practices-for-security-of-iot-1"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ddce5a22-66c1-47e2-ad67-4a2b0941daad .

