    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c09c540b-fe68-463f-98e2-d5746d193b4e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OSI is not related to authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions as such, but the specification addresses some authentication requirements on the transfer of data between systems. 

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3894f5c3-5c7a-4935-9cbf-fcda6faa4131 .

camssa:c0a18807-ecc5-4566-8aee-a41138f47cdb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the moment of performing the assessment, HTML is barely used to develop web pages. With the appearance of XHTML and HTML5, no evidences have been found to consider HTML as an asset to build innovative solutions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e089841-3ad5-4241-906c-0a9a5fa95518 .

camssa:c0a3e1bf-cf6a-448e-a269-e34105b0a9b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c0a68420-7c61-4d2f-8d44-a8627fc2846e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI TS 119 512 specification is designed to specifies protocols for trust service providers providing long-term data preservation services of digital signatures and of general data. Using digital signatures or other mechanisms such as time-stamp tokens, data can be protected against unwanted changes. Therefore, when digitally signed data is exchanged by two or more entities, it is certain that they are accurate and have not been modified.

ETSI TS 119 512:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.01_60/ts_119512v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7584145b-c4b2-4c04-aea1-ad6e06307aad .

camssa:c0a915c6-b53b-4046-b356-4b83ea8f06e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DQV focuses on describing data quality information in a standardised vocabulary rather than specifying a particular data format. This allows it to be applied to data stored in various formats, including structured formats like CSV, JSON, XML, as well as semi-structured and unstructured formats. DQV does not prescribe a specific data representation or serialisation format, making it technology agnostic in this aspect.

Data Quality Vocabulary: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf6e5329-60d5-4cca-acca-d5159c110afa .

camssa:c0a966b0-033e-4679-a4eb-d5efecb9b641 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of DNS is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f207be01-ca00-42bf-8bd7-196fac936b62 .

