    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c12fa646-17b0-4da3-9e2d-df6f2165d65c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is not related to public administration services but given that the specification creates the means to conceptualise assets among a group of organisations, they could be adapted in combination with other specification to provide better interfaces for public services.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b7dcc29-e023-4a39-b0c1-b63e332238a6 .

camssa:c1343f68-d8e9-4197-a6e4-60c429f66fa8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c1348852-4f74-4959-86fa-80299e2e607c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-093c1e09f5a65e4cba0247dcab5a8f4854f3e512db336b1855b9a4c48d3659e0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c13cfac6-6bee-423d-a9fd-738f0a3401c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'A few assessments have been carried on the specification efficiency.
Given the nature of the Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox only a few assessments can be carried out since the specification is rather stable.
In this sense, the CEPS report on the Better Regulation and Toolbox defines the specification as clear stepforward in terms of clarity for the administrations to follow although more attention is needed to consider impacts on innovation, especially when it comes to the legislative design and the quantification of impacts. 

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

"To the Commissioner responsible for better regulation" Bruegel's study:
https://www.bruegel.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/MEMO-Better-Regulation.pdf

Final report on the "Study supporting the interim evaluation of the innovation principle", CEPS Study:
https://www.ceps.eu/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/KI0219819ENN.en_.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b805e696-55fa-4bad-b3c5-75dd5f2757f9 .

camssa:c1421ace-ec3b-4423-8fd3-af88f14412e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3c0edf049cd95575b46d688ed31be0ccce7a5822c5bcc22adf05d491f01f2780 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c1432b1d-0611-4a08-a756-e7680c69c744 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """EuroVoc is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9af71b47-6e61-4159-a1ee-f65912595c27 .

camssa:c145ec81-6ef5-46ba-b452-b7ee94b229da a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:c1478608-99bc-4b48-b3b6-b05c17423be2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV defines a broad notion of semantics for providing a conceptual model of concepts and relationships between them. DPV can facilitate the modelling of personal data categories, and also provides a data model of concepts that act as a vocabulary for the interoperable representation and exchange of information about personal data and its processing. From this point of view, DPV is a good enabler for the modelling of business concepts.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:285f5a5b-66fc-4fd8-8c23-b2dc2987e96f .

camssa:c148cdb7-6ed8-435d-96d2-503d0f66392f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """MIME can be found for free along within the European Collaborative Platform, Joinup.\r
\r
MIME in Joinup platform:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/multipurpose-internet-mail-extensions-mime-rfc-2048-multipurpose-internet-mail-extensions-mime"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:997020bd-8bd1-4358-a386-209cbf605c4a .

camssa:c14ad13c-6a4e-4301-957a-97817d9825a3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c14cdc80-faa1-4912-b7c8-2aeb7c184612 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OCSP helps easing the formalisation of Interoperability agreements. E.g., the Digital Signature Service.\r
\r
Digital Signature Service framework reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0639af1d-4214-4750-af7e-23ca2ebb11dd .

camssa:c15b6343-5b47-4482-af91-6003d078eabe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being a widely used standard covering privacy aspects, HTTPS has a wide accpetance amongst cross-border projects, including European ones. An interesting example is the TESTA network service – which stands for Trans European Services for Telematics between Administrations – provides a European backbone network for data exchange between a wide variety of public administrations. It is an ISA2 solution which has been designed to support the needs for a whole range of application architectures relying on protocols such as HTTPS. \r
\r
TESTA project:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:277208f6-8a7a-4b49-a072-74861e144933 .

camssa:c160d886-f8bd-4145-8db6-5dbcac1c2f4c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c160de0d-e630-45dc-a147-1465d918b1c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By establishing constraints on the creation and exchange of XML documents XSD fosters the trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders. However, XSD does not include security features in itself. Despite this, XML includes several recommendations in order to ensure the information is protected against unauthorised changes.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1d245d4-b702-48ba-bc61-ff8e678d0d3a .

camssa:c16339b3-a117-4b30-989c-e3f3ff2c6afe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ELI is a European Specification developed for its common reuse and to foster the shareability of legal document across borders. It is used within the EU Open Data Portal for the provision of data sets described using the main requirements established by ELI. Doing so, European institutions, businesses and citizens can access and reuse it in a machine-readable format. \r
\r
Moreover, since ELI was developed taking Common Data Model (CMD) from the OP and the implementations require to be compliant with it, it ensures that the content is available from CELLAR, which is an access point to all the open data generated by the Publications office. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html\r
\r
ELI technical Information: \r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/technical_information.html\r
\r
EU Open Data Portal Data sets: \r
https://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/data/group/eli?groups=eli\r
\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66993f00-d390-4741-a31c-05f1b48de200 .

camssa:c1690795-7237-40b4-941c-8e54dce4e8b6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1624157830122d60825aa5aa88ab70d0b140b2e7e510086699f9a9773efef6bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c16befa9-764d-4016-864a-04fd4db42bbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 is currently recommended by one Member State: Malta.

CAMSS list of standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specificationscamss
/camss-list-standards

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cf88e93-f628-4dc1-8084-46df96b5cf16 .

camssa:c16ca5a3-a6d7-42da-b0be-55ec11cb128a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There exist several projects developing NFVI solutions. There exist some reports assessing the efficiency of NFVI and other specifications, such as OpenStack. OpenStack is an open source project that provides an open source cloud management system, that has jointly published a gap analysis with the ETSI Testing, Experimentation and Open Source (TST) Working Group. \r
\r
ETSI-OpenStack wiki reference, 'ETSI NFV meets OpenStack workshop materials' section:\r
https://nfvwiki.etsi.org/index.php?title=OpenStack_vs_IFA005006_Gaps\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95aeaeeb-7442-4da9-a7ad-a2b91c4f8cc2 .

camssa:c16d2fdd-12fa-495d-98e7-605047f2ce04 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "80" .

