        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "''"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c8ca725-b7fd-4a3c-aef9-a5f6528100ae .

camssa:c1fe5773-5683-4713-9dd7-a1d3ebf6cd01 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is focused on providing guidelines, recommendations and mechanisms for the proper development of public policies and laws. Within the recommendations and mechanisms, there are some implications for long-term preservation or archiving, mainly on tool 55 but it is only comprehensive if combined with another specification, the Management and long-term preservation of the European Commission’s Archives, registered under reference number DPR-EC-00837.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf

Management and long-term preservation of the European Commission’s Archives
https://ec.europa.eu/dpo-register/detail/DPR-EC-00837'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:743358c7-7968-4775-958d-bd2777726bb8 .

camssa:c210fdd7-7149-44ab-9170-ae9ae53e3866 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:c21402a5-fcf3-4bc7-b671-0cafd7ead80b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c21a5d84-c2f9-4285-889a-fbdfd4b8909c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By ensuring the availability of eSignatures elements and metadata, the specification avoids the users to provide information more than one time. Therefore, CAdES fosters the implementation of the Once-only Principle.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4db769c-d60a-4f94-8d1f-65723712a175 .

camssa:c21c7d16-79e6-492e-a391-7c9414d470ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """eDelivery SMP has diverse implications in terms of Intellectual Property Rights. On one hand, the SMP 1.0 specification which is under non-assertion IPR policy, from OASIS IPR Policy. On the other hand, the ministry of Justice and the European Commission are in charge of part of the specification content. Therefore, the specification is licensed under (F) RAND basis and Royalty-free basis. \r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/eDelivery+SMP+-+1.10#eDeliverySMP-1.10-Ownership\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5ce47fc-cba7-4b64-9b2f-da8748720d39 .

camssa:c21db297-4f76-409e-b8e8-69d5bd95b8bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "'The XML specification itself does not provide inherent mechanisms to ensure or enable data processing accuracy.Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification.'"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c5912c8-3f8d-4683-bbed-0fa1fd73218c .

camssa:c21f8d9f-20c4-4c9a-a42e-e5834e73fb70 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData offers access to information from relational databases, file systems, content management systems, traditional websites, and others. Therefore, it enables and reinforces the delivery of European public services. 

Interoperable Europe Portal OASIS Open Data Protocol reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/odp-oasis-open-data-protocol-odata-tc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:27e47108-ccbc-4f53-b1db-b29853c5076a .

camssa:c2213c7c-13b3-47e0-8605-34806cf22a20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The protocol for remote digital signature creation itself may not directly address data portability, as its primary focus is on defining the technical procedures for creating digital signatures remotely. However, data portability can still be facilitated as part of the broader digital signature workflow that involves the use of such a protocol. Implementations of the protocol aims for interoperability, allowing digital signatures created using one system to be verified by another. This interoperability helps ensure that signed documents remain portable across different platforms and environments.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce6f2572-7950-44f3-9bbd-e39811be713b .

camssa:c22673d8-8cb4-4303-9af3-a208fb8e3eec a cav:Score,
