camssa:c3060eb5-81c0-49d1-b706-c7181c79ff7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XHTML is not related to facilitate organisational interoperability agreements. Therefore, this
criterion does not apply to the specification.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c4b05e8-6d3b-4a17-9543-f9bb7bde6c50 .

camssa:c3081640-8a71-4362-9e0a-0141fbdefb33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ECMA International has clearly defined the procedures that have to be carried out in order to publish standards or technical reports. The procedures are defined in a set of documents that can be found at ECMA's webpage. \r
\r
ECMA International’s decision procedure is basically a two-step process: The first decision step takes place on the level of the Technical Committee (TC) level where consensus is the primary target.  The second step is approval at the ECMA International General Assembly.\r
\r
See:\r
http://www.ecma-international.org/memento/policies.htm"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f9c09b6-de21-49fb-8743-7555e68b9bd3 .

camssa:c30d6b2e-57d2-48a1-93f8-6781b643882d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7688b251-e1f7-4a68-a8d0-f175f173a48f .

camssa:c30ef0e0-816b-4da5-a285-bb1b913ba619 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification outlines conformance as requirements that are manually measurable. An abstract test suite
has been developed to manually verify the conformity of classes, with its feasibility confirmed through testing
across multiple distinct implementations.

OGC TrainingDML-AI, Abstract Test Suite section:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html#_5097f072-1f22-4e93-be63-429921ab323a

OGC TrainingDML-AI Implementations:
https://github.com/opengeospatial/TrainingDML-AI_SWG/tree/main/Implementations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e702846-e05e-4329-b89e-4308b54cec86 .

camssa:c3119cb9-48cf-489e-8ecd-67d02328d32c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:c314243e-435c-4388-a895-b1870eca3026 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the second star corresponds to make data available as structured data, an area of application of XML. \r
\r
Additionally, RDF is a W3C specification that defines XML syntax for RDF, the de facto standard for publishing Linked Open Data. \r
\r
See:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0302d01-4564-40a5-a47d-939b223c734a .

camssa:c319f5fa-64b3-43b8-a555-4d5ef04ca1d1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:c31c2c2c-7c31-4396-861d-9866de2d62a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Indexed Database API aligns with GDPR Regulation Article 32, which governs security aspects of personal data processing. In this context, within the Health360 project, the specification is used for data caching, ensuring data integrity and availability. While the Health360 project is not a European cross-border initiative, the specification is designed to ensure compliance with GDPR.

Health360 GDPR project: 
https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/12/17/8441'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f985889-60f2-46f2-b271-dd9c81f764e1 .

camssa:c320daa4-06e9-4169-ad03-13922080ce3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The once-only principle is an e-government concept that aims to ensure that citizens, institutions, and companies only have to provide certain standard information to the authorities and administrations once.
LDAP fosters the OOP in terms of accessibility by allowing administrations stakeholders to keep the contact and access to different distributed services without providing personal data for authentication more than strictly needed. 

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11926352-4b7d-457d-b962-7f035775555b .

camssa:c32a3cf8-020a-4c1b-8d90-b4ece19a81c4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ef096f898c938883daab1b22e784cfaf985b5e5c855e170ecf6eab6f37b01b50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c33995d3-f6a6-4cc1-bd7d-9f5ca5214615 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c339adc7-e585-49ea-9d3a-7a92c5244c21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is in the Interoperable Europe Portal, where solutions related to interoperability and the creation of digital public services are published. Apart from being publicly available there, EIRA can play a crucial role approaching semantic interoperability from the analysis phase, where requirements are set at all levels of the solutions, from legal requirements to technical. 

By addressing semantic interoperability by design, EIRA can contribute to work towards finding common solutions and can also leverage from other solutions at European or national level related to data management or exchange. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a96b40d-096f-4f7b-b472-415784fe46e6 .

camssa:c33ef0a6-8cdd-4f24-9d95-da45a8473bdc a cav:Score,
