camssa:c38cc8e5-9f00-4955-a4f6-4b03481c4d54 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. To achieve this, interoperability between public administrations is a sine qua non condition. WS-Security makes safer the SOAP messages which facilitates the exchanging of information within cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abb4ba73-8ed5-41aa-a026-b31097b8fde7 .

camssa:c38d8611-3959-4651-aca5-d867863c7547 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OWASP is an open community dedicated to enabling organizations to conceive, develop, acquire, operate, and maintain applications that can be trusted. All of the OWASP tools, documents, forums, and chapters are free and open to anyone interested in improving application security. \r
\r
Moreover, the community has established different ways to contribute to the development of tools and documents.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf \r
\r
Contribute page: \r
https://owaspsamm.org/contributing/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d37dc90-2fc6-4fe1-9ba5-11d9ceda335f .

camssa:c391bb51-8f8e-4013-af4b-84210f5a3ae2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c391fcc1-99d9-4144-90e0-4468f1c8da2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The data and information encoding is a key point in data exchange and use. In addition, the adoption of the specification as an encoding format fosters the data portability and reuse of information between administrations thus, supporting the implementation and evolution of European public services.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecbee570-1b90-435d-82cc-a89657db245c .

camssa:c3923959-cce0-4552-9bd9-cb4d94d0100f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:c392e3cd-1300-459f-9cb1-b7710875047e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SHACL can be implemented across various technology stacks and environments that support RDF. Therefore, the specification is technology agnostic.

SHACL Platform and Technology agnostic:
https://medium.com/fluree/what-is-shacl-with-examples-2697f659d465

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fdeb8b36-0db6-4933-9cc4-0ef7fcc33041 .

camssa:c397864a-a2ac-4c5a-b4a9-ec4a4db49e08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence found of the creation of any community along with the sharing of their data and results on European platforms.  Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc2dabf7-b18e-48d1-b7f7-7dd9a4671b5b .

camssa:c39ff298-2e90-44fd-80aa-b5649b7f5153 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"iCalendar defines an access classification as the only component of the general security system within a calendar application. However, the access classification serves as a method for capturing the calendar owner's intention for accessing the calendar component.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:08c00fb2-2df5-4d54-82f9-d529b543ad7f .

camssa:c3a710c5-05b6-4c02-a9db-157534659d84 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C DIDs first public working draft was published in 2019. Since then, changes have been made and are available in the W3C web. In addition, different documentation on its supporting processes has been published to ensure the correct change and release of its content. For instance, section C of the specification explains changes made since the last published version.

Revision History DIDs:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#revision-history'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e034369-570b-4bd9-90ec-730b914c3c06 .

camssa:c3af8776-52c1-4217-93cb-e377a70b3756 a cav:Score,
