    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c3eb3984-b948-42c5-8b08-c9fb15ffc2f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By allowing the publication of administrative data in the web, as the main language used in the web processing, HTML5 helps and foster the visibility of administration data, and services. Moreover, it also is easing the decision-making process by ensuring the data exchange and reuse. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/2012/12/html5-cr.html.en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68a4656d-901c-4951-87a2-2376a85357ca .

camssa:c3ee2d59-a9de-4ee4-94c9-b1ef6f5a0085 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c3f0975b-a0a2-4c79-a7cc-c083d2c7e06c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are Directives regulating participation on the development of standards. Participation is limited to \r
membership approval and sometimes the payment of a fee.\r
ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has \r
adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop \r
standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation \r
through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The \r
decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical \r
feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
ETSI Portal reference: \r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/esi/esi-activities'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:acccefe0-7ade-42ba-99a6-931b062890b6 .

camssa:c3fbd1fc-4099-43f4-b668-35646deeccdd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c4007615-ed5c-45b6-86ed-631eade0f474 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML can facilitate organisational interoperability agreements. The specification is easily readable by humans and data can be exchanged between organizations. This fact can help to improve organisational interoperability.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#11-goals'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98367533-b82f-434b-97ba-6f77207f01a0 .

