        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c40ac265-b804-4417-a141-beeaa963e681 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are two Member States recommending OData in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are The Netherlands and France.\r
\r
Netherlands Catalogue reference:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/aanbevolen\r
\r
France catalogue reference:\r
http://references.modernisation.gouv.fr/sites/default/files/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd964106-b770-49bb-bf3d-de79007b04ff .

camssa:c410261e-4276-4cce-b002-3721cffc1a65 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although there is no platform for testing Indexed Database API implementations, there are some resources that offer guides on how to test an Indexed Database API code. In this context, the "Testing your IndexedDB code with Jest" offers a guide on how to test two asynchronous IndexedDB functions with Jest.js.

"Testing your IndexedDB code with Jest" guide:
https://dev.to/andyhaskell/testing-your-indexeddb-code-with-jest-2o17'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3239ae25-45b5-4e94-9cfb-ef019f305918 .

camssa:c4128284-513a-430c-8479-82bc07e634e4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c41683e6-82a8-46ba-8c00-f5065ed7035d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c417003a-6f6d-41f8-b8f3-a5ca062c3465 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ef096f898c938883daab1b22e784cfaf985b5e5c855e170ecf6eab6f37b01b50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c41d5b6e-0d2d-4647-bb92-f4f8f3c9af7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML provides a set of components enabling users to store and work with any type of electronic content, fostering the visibility of administrations. As well as providing an electronic data interchange model (the ebRIM and the ebRS core components), the specification contributes and promotes to some degree to the visibility of public services' implementations.

ebRIM component reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rim-v4.0-os.html

ebRS component reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rs-v4.0-os.html

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:902fdfa1-0008-43ce-837b-d8df2ab7f935 .

camssa:c41f16c2-3054-4b1f-b104-9c03e4010127 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc272cd8a2e3e9c5e4edaa5ac7d59735c377a9db89d6958335a2cf0538761ab3 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c41f1a98-20f4-4f64-8b45-752d43a6529c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f6669d041c301e6aadc132bb9de2d1d2f620f9fcb8b5d147c7b08c0393b53d0c ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c420db9d-c9b1-46a2-8875-9b34fedaae27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Even though ISAE 3402 is more focused on auditing and ensuring the management of the information \r
provided in transactions from the private sector, this specification could also help to ensure that the public \r
services requiring information from both parties (Public administrations and the service consumers) are \r
properly managed and monitored allowing the information to be secured and exchanged between public \r
administrations fostering the once-only principle.\r
\r
ISAE 3402 handbook reference:\r
https://www.ifac.org/system/files/downloads/b014-2010-iaasb-handbook-isae-3402.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:646aab5f-7989-459b-acbe-9988a7e34045 .

camssa:c4245d99-12ac-4f12-a3f6-cfd5802c8fa8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification can be extended by using capabilities negotiation. This is where systems use "offered-capabilities" (e.g., high-priority messaging) to indicate the features they can provide, and "desired-capabilities" to indicate that it wants to receive messages that have been marked with a priority level. Additionally, the AMQP type system lets you add extra details to values, called annotations. These annotations provide more context and meaning to the values, making them easier to understand and work with.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:08b19da3-d341-4d79-bc8c-886590c6d491 .

camssa:c431cc9b-a890-4020-a622-c5741e7ce51e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c4361634-ed0d-4153-b0c6-07281b5ab237 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PNG was first published as W3C recommendation in October 1996. Later in March 1997 was published in IETF's website as informational RFC 2083. In 2004, it became an ISO/IEC standard (15948:2004 PNG). Nowadays, there are millions of images with PNG extension over the Internet. So it is demonstrated that PNG has enough maturity for its use.\r
\r
RFC 2083 IETF - PNG informational:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2083\r
\r
PNG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/29581.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:688a64df-04ab-41ba-805c-7d116947c537 .

camssa:c43d8091-673e-4fe0-a59e-0f6e73c7f981 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8a34a40e5bc5436b3530d898d75a57cf0488591887b31a5169499fe78952d84c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:c44dd404-9ba5-4e9b-bc4b-97bd161690fc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c44e6af5-1e18-426e-92ed-a01434154f02 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DNS is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable specification.\r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc1034.txt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d823c8f-986c-4397-ae8c-259b58832954 .

camssa:c452a9e1-d79c-49f2-b6bb-75eb6fb60b34 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c454df04-6093-45a4-9361-a27fe37ba7bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData offers access to information from relational databases, file systems, content management systems, traditional websites, and others. Therefore, it enables and renforce the delivery of European public services.\r
\r
Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/odp-oasis-open-data-protocol-odata-tc/about'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef3f32c0-bbae-4d31-be2a-d73f3dbac9c7 .

camssa:c45a0896-a57f-4e50-9b7b-40f7b4f76e44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Consensus is a foundation upon which the Alliance is built and all processes and procedures, particularly in connection to the focus, work plans, deliverables, milestones and tangible specifications / recommendations are consensus based."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59f8dbb9-7f59-4bf9-9e14-5bf9f8a0d587 .

