        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of BFO is not related to the provision of means for restriction of access to information/data since the specification does not provide any means of restriction. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93329537-c797-47e2-96e6-b17db4493b69 .

camssa:c4923f52-25ef-41da-a43a-907f822ea4f1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XAdES (ISO 14522-2:2012) has the ISO community that supports the development of: International standards, Technical Specifications, Technical Report and Publicly Available Specification.\r
\r
ISO Webpage:\r
http://www.isotc292online.org/projects/iso-process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6945043-59df-45a1-b7a3-383349358adf .

camssa:c49449da-00da-45ad-bf2d-885b4a23befa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At least 4 Member States are recommending IPsec in their ICT National Catalogues. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:071dc4eb-eb52-4f40-ab61-f6df5db8b686 .

camssa:c49a1830-b4ee-49a3-b0ef-5cfd601903c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XACML specification is valuable for enforcing access control within business processes. Its ability to 
define complex, fine-grained access control policies and dynamically enforce them makes it a critical 
component for securing business processes and ensuring they operate within the defined access control 
policies.

XACML OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-core-spec-os-en.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d4c0c36f-8916-4e05-b1bf-727abe5891d3 .

camssa:c49ac2d6-5c1e-46bb-81c2-57b6271decbb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a mail format specification, MIME is a valuable tool for sharing information through the internet between administrations and stakeholders. It allows sharing data and information in a specific format, it fosters the visibility of administration data and services. MIME fosters the collaboration between public administrations and it eases the decision-making process of institutions.\r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:636f83c6-c80a-4379-9e09-bb46a66346e5 .

camssa:c49b60e6-4777-4c16-ab7e-c5ee71acedcd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By listing and describing administrations' web services and improving the discoverability of them, UDDI fosters the visibility of public administration web services. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e068b0e-4eb8-41d8-a1a7-a8a5b16aef42 .

camssa:c4b16d2f-8525-455a-ac36-c40ebef97db6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"At the moment of performing the assessment, SAML 2.0 is widely used to secure and authenticate access to the internal and external platforms as eases the single sign-on (SSO) processes. These types of SSO's are included in the development of platforms and services, including innovative solutions. \r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c743a823-f556-456d-9749-fe703dfd8ed3 .

camssa:c4be0e59-51df-49a1-af79-d5e2d9931f5c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c4c29a7b-da33-4d1a-9751-1d0e14343af9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JSON is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, JSON can define the interoperability aspects of the "Machine to machine interface" ABB of the EIRA Technical View. In addition, JSON can define also the "representation" ABB of the EIRA semantic view. \r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b072aa9-88bc-4aa2-ac97-3e69625806c5 .

camssa:c4c40194-2d6d-4ea6-811f-0bf4156b9437 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Better Regulation Toolbox includes accessibility within the requirements that ICT systems and solutions should cover for the proper implementation of a specific public policy (Tool 27). Therefore, it can be considered that the specification can positively impact the e-accessibility of public services and solutions.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1f79d7f0-8fa1-4067-9f4a-c8194028c343 .

camssa:c4c4bdf3-87bf-431c-a67f-0d6c1525748e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any platform to test conformance to ETSI TS 119 612, nevertheless, the specification lists a set of requirements needed to comply with to be conformant and can be checked manually whether or not applied (see Annex A). 

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3d0ec19-5bc7-4af4-b841-0e878dbc3684 .

