    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c51e1212-cc85-4d13-a3c1-af20f7d39dce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specifications is not directly related with the data exchange, but it could be used to provide user-friendly appearance and detail to those public services accessible via HTML. CSS could support the implementation of digital services avoiding the non-digital ones. \r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9d9a8008-928e-4f7e-bdd4-992c627dd0ca .

camssa:c520ca6a-88ff-4a64-8c11-1d4d6fa433d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db6d0d7c-65bf-460e-8366-68d80db77f88 .

camssa:c52103cc-3989-47cc-ae76-12d7e6e250b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Anyone developing software or policy for a public purpose can use this standard to work towards higher-quality public services that are more cost-effective, with less risk and more control. It means that the specification can be applied and implemented for different organisations in different business domains at no cost.\r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4906f0a8-30ee-4cbe-985f-96ffcce25944 .

camssa:c5232baf-d1ce-4f91-896b-8af68b10d19a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:c5244bbe-b0e9-457b-8b62-be6c1960b956 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES does not define a cross-sector reusable data model, but defines an electronic signature format. \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d231442-5294-4f45-b174-f82e0630c425 .

camssa:c526bc07-2000-4b36-811f-d1d685636534 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebRIM and ebRS core specifications constitute the implementation requirements of ebXML (see ebXML, \r
Conformance reference). Each feature of the core components of the ebXML specification has a conformance requirement set for its implementation. By no means, their implementation is explicitly foreseen according to the ebXML documentation; moreover, there is no specific provision in order to do it separately.\r
\r
ebXML reference, Conformance section:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__53396_365468741'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b6743fd-329d-4472-aa41-68c89baecb03 .

