        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary is publicly available for its use and implementation. Moreover, it is available for everyone to study with no cost in Joinup webpage.\r
\r
CCCEV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:80bfc244-3e36-4d30-a91f-56d5577e4f4f .

camssa:c6b99d44-575b-4f14-896b-60bbcabb08c0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL is used in many industries and business sectors. The following are examples of this:\r
\r
Wimmics \r
 \r
The web-instrumented man-machine interactions, communities and semantics is a research team that lists many projects that are implementing the Semantic web and therefore, RDF. In the context of Wimmics, a SHACL validator has been developed. It was developed using STTL, SPARDQL Template Transformation Language and LDScript.\r
\r
Netage\r
 \r
Netage is a system that uses smart data to prevent fire fighters getting injured. For this purpose, Netage implements SHACL for data validation.\r
\r
See:\r
http://wimmics.inria.fr/\r
http://netage.nl/en/home/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c28cdfd-2aa3-449a-9d45-8960e5a5b647 .

camssa:c6b9b54e-0b77-4191-aed5-c2e21dabda05 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c6bf203f-4d49-4fcd-b8a1-4a32c2186e5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPv6 has been selected within the TESTA, which provides a secure cross-border data communication network service for public administrations. \r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/idabc/en/document/2097.html \r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93584f63-bb58-4dcb-bc7f-bdbca4640c0a .

camssa:c6cd16de-5255-4d41-bdc3-6a4493146448 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 16234-1 e-CF framework represents the European e-Competence Framework, which focuses on skills and competences of the ICT professional workforce. Although the specification might evolve in accordance with different frameworks such as the European Qualifications Framework (EQF), European Skills, Competences, Qualifications and Occupations (ESCO), or the global skills and competency framework for the digital world (SFIA), the EN 16234-1 e-CF specification is not dependent on any other specification, and can be considered technology-agnostic (further information on CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 3).\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 3:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf\r
\r
EQF reference:\r
https://europa.eu/europass/en/european-qualifications-framework-eqf?msclkid=4e01b391b58811ec86a2e49c305e4614\r
\r
ESCO reference:\r
https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/about-esco/what-esco\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/about-sfia'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7553495-eb89-444d-b073-6de3be9ada0f .

camssa:c6d5372e-866e-472d-bb68-3716138e4056 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is a business agnostic specification that can be implemented in any domain requiring web services description and access, depeloved to be usable beyond business-specific domains and is designed to facilitate interoperability across a wide range of applications and industries.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b71ad36-ef1c-4569-b0ae-ccc394a4b489 .

camssa:c6d61c5c-b90a-4d61-a126-a20d8b1df079 a cav:Score,
