camssa:c6d9e203-d3cf-4bd2-9a48-7105c4107818 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME is a standardized format and set of rules for encoding and exchanging multimedia and non-ASCII data within messages and data on the internet. It is designed to work across different platforms, operating systems, and email clients.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
Gmail using MIME:\r
https://developers.google.com/gmail/api/guides/sending?hl=es-419'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dbd4f431-6d5c-436c-aa72-0022dc94edad .

camssa:c6ddb434-b6c8-4586-a90b-1ac292531456 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME is a business domain agnostic specification that can be reused in a cross-domain way. It can be used for the exchange of files addressing any domain.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55a2ad6f-59d0-406e-8a3c-b3ff5c295044 .

camssa:c6dec965-288d-456f-b88a-f01b54f96566 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Assessments of the efficiency of LDES primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. For instance, a 2023-doctoral dissertation for Ghent University presents LDES as an open data interface for live data consumption in integrated services,  which highlights the specification's efficiency.

Linked Data Event Streams as an Open Data Interface for Live Data Consumption in Integrated Services:
https://imec-publications.be/bitstream/handle/20.500.12860/41413/phdfinal-brechtvandevyvere.pdf?sequence=1\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f87144a-ca8a-41d1-8b18-1ce779a52446 .

camssa:c6e21d58-cf50-4a6a-a5ff-4e7e4c5400f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the Core Location Vocabulary is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:337ebad8-bf4f-48ac-9b12-250fccec2e81 .

camssa:c6e3ff8f-cb70-4d7a-abad-9fe1ac0639e2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c6e8d466-7113-43da-a7a2-44aff97758ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While is true that Core Business Vocabulary (CBV) gained more popularity on European aspects, the Registered Organization Vocabulary achieved W3C Recommendation status in 2013 indicates that it underwent a rigorous review process by the semantic web community and was deemed a sound and effective specification at that time. 

Moreover, the fact that CBV built upon the foundations of Registered Organization Vocabulary implies that the core concepts and design principles of Registered Organization Vocabulary were considered valuable and effective enough to be carried forward.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

Publication of the Core Business Vocabulary as RegOrg on the W3C standards track Reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/registered-organization-vocabulary/news/publication-core-busin

Core Business Vocabulary Reference:
https://semiceu.github.io/Core-Business-Vocabulary/releases/2.1.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:daaf3999-bb84-41b0-aacc-c3fd29a79f78 .

camssa:c6f157de-c957-440d-b380-8fb3df0fdb70 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several studies assessing the strengths, weaknesses, effectiveness, and efficiency of TLS which include several references to the version that is being assessed. Moreover, the studies compare the performance form the different versions laying emphasis on strengths and weaknesses. \r
See: \r
http://www-brs.ub.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/netahtml/HSS/Diss/MeyerChristopher/diss.pdf\r
https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.02531.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5edd2e44-94d8-4dcd-8091-d3ad1055c63d .

camssa:c6f5944f-06a7-4e66-8f31-5c5ee9158ef9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the moment of performing the assessment, TIFF/IT format is used in some cases because it is great for printing images. However, no evidences have been found to consider TIFF/IT as an asset to build innovative solutions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2187789c-33eb-49d9-ae9d-1ceddf2e8d51 .

camssa:c6f714ca-7b45-4181-9902-dea0448f7887 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is indirectly mentioned in the Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market. In this Regulation, one of the aspects that is mentioned is that the selected specification have to facilitate the implementation of the principle of privacy by design and ensure that personal data is processed in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC.

"Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market" reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:483f71c2-b44f-49aa-a8fa-34007451ede1 .

