camssa:c7b97853-9e45-4ef0-8e4e-167d24682fb0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPv4 specification can be extended with Access Control Lists (ACLs), which ensure that only authorised individuals can access the network. ACLs can help control which hosts can access different parts of the network or determine which types of traffic are forwarded or blocked at router interfaces.

IPv4 ACL:
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst2960l/software/15-2_6_e/configuration_guide/b_1526e_consolidated_2960l_cg/m_sec_acls_cg_danube_2960l_cdb.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:589abe70-0021-4981-b9e9-7f18b5429ed2 .

