camssa:c7e2c5a9-ee0e-4e1c-88aa-669231fe6653 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification uses the TestBed service to validate GraphQL queries against GraphQL schemas and it can help simplify the delivery of European public services. Test Bed offers support for projects using GraphQL by launching a new GraphQL validator to validate queries against their target schemas. The validator is based on the GraphQL reference implementation and expects as input the query to validate as well as the target schema.\r
\r
TestBed & GraphQL reference: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/news/new-graphql-validation-service'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df9c7f7a-1206-465d-b782-eab3e5792827 .

camssa:c7f1b97a-8d88-4084-8e51-a2a3a054b29d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The fact that the specification describes the model for being serialised and represented in a machine-readable format fosters the exchange and reuse of information and its translation to other languages different from the original in which was developed the initial resource. Therefore, ODRL can be useful to ensure the availability of access datasets licensing and the related services in different languages, easing the multilingualism of digital public services. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:844739bf-90b0-4e5c-aa2d-091eea6c3ff6 .

camssa:c80219b5-e9fa-44b7-9e48-228e14555486 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The extensibility of DCAT-AP makes the specification a versatile standard that can be adapted and customised to meet the specific needs of different organisations and use cases, while still maintaining compatibility with the core standard.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01d0dac1-2600-4759-b32e-9eb05f9a7919 .

camssa:c8038fbf-9043-4f90-a969-3a203354e353 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33b5b305bcc0a995fd3c592dc8a6f52d0749a6e817aa85844f3e4f31c7dea344 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c806d2f4-6af0-4395-be20-ceddb1825c5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of XSLT is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e6b0bf5-5692-4775-8ad3-64ca380465fb .

camssa:c8073bd4-9643-4e08-af14-888d347fc15f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF 3161 Time Stamp Protocol (TSP) is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, IETF 3161 Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) can define the interoperability aspects of the " e-Timestamp Creation Service", and “e-Timestamp Verification and Validation Service”  ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e28e6c5c-b453-44de-9dc7-1e22a1c0d8a4 .

camssa:c80942f4-93ab-4089-963f-d17d58d723e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification purpose is to enable communications over the Internet. IPv6 is the new version of IPv4 which is a widely used protocol thus it is not dependent of any specific platform. Consequently, the adoption of IPv6 does not hamper the interoperability. 

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:25682182-528d-416c-ae97-04574ee1fcfc .

camssa:c81290f1-1a51-475c-8fd1-68a7892fee7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"FTP is used as the main protocol for file exchange by many public organisations. By allowing public administration to share information with others, it fosters the visibility of data (e.g. Administrative rules, processes etc.) and facilitates public administrations decision-making. \r
\r
An example of implementation supporting this fact would be CIRCABC, a project with the purpose of enhancing the collaboration, communication and document exchange between different European Union's stakeholders. \r
\r
CIRCABC Reference: \r
https://circabc.europa.eu/ui/welcome\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81c68652-e173-4064-9c32-b9ffd0ea447c .

camssa:c812fbcb-776f-472b-a807-b39d07adab2f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-33ea90f5c1bb01d4398c57d03a25934dc5722d5ddbc98a43911ea4fb302ec54c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:c81bf685-b564-4440-8529-a1c4dee4cfc9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAML 2.0 is a format that allows seamless cross-border interoperability between systems, independent of implementation. \r
\r
The specification allows cross-domain single sign-on, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. As well, providing authentication across sectors and platforms allows administrations and stakeholders to exchange and reuse data fostering the data portability across borders. """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e49cd55c-bc0c-434d-8584-d69135c20a2f .

camssa:c81ef52e-3a41-4b99-a818-cb1664f2551c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'E-ARK CSIP can indirectly support the visibility of administrative procedures and services by promoting the use of descriptive metadata. Descriptive metadata can provide information about the administrative context of records, such as their origin, creator, date of creation, and other relevant administrative details. This metadata helps users understand the administrative procedures and services associated with the records.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:734fa585-df5e-4fd4-9de7-26768d444914 .

camssa:c81f02a5-f407-44b2-8f3f-3fbdb24a7f49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed in 2014 by Catalogue of Services actions, and it has been evolved taking into account the inputs of the different stakeholders involved according to the development process stated by SEMIC. It is supporting several initiatives at European level, this fact demonstrates the maturity for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69c684e6-90db-4262-83b4-455fa617c4b1 .

camssa:c81f67fb-6e69-481d-a915-0dbdd7040039 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-Security is not related to the publication of data as Open Data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96c2f87d-2776-4b55-9f79-96f594ef45c8 .

camssa:c823d36a-448f-4527-861d-d51423316635 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1435ad894742693c2b99e329ef12399cd411ed6900f49b9658fd2231de3f201a ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c82b5ec8-7e9c-4f18-a813-a4b48ac8abc6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "DNS facilitates the implementation and use of any solution using domains, including innovative solutions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3e86bf2-f329-4ee6-b9a6-83ceeb6f10bf .

camssa:c82e5eb8-e790-4343-afc2-0c6912f3a0b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is a European Standard. It is a set of technical specifications developed by the European Commission to facilitate the implementation of digital public services across Europe.\r
\r
EU Vocabularies reference:             \r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/schemas'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9bea63b0-d1c6-43c6-84e3-fbe577e4d476 .

camssa:c831dcbc-dab0-466f-b454-05996180d6f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c8344309-75ed-4108-b192-c4c9ad79ab88 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c835a444-fdde-406e-86d3-bfd492e28b9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dfa178cf-ba1f-4e66-ae02-360d51076c6c .

camssa:c839bafd-2058-4b79-8d21-592cc71b95fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This Technical Specification (TS) has been produced by ETSI Technical Committee Smart Machine-to-Machine
communications (SmartM2M). The participation in the technical group is reserved to ETSI members, who require registration, fees, and membership approval. Membership requires an annual contribution, determined
by the size and nature of the member company or organization and, in the case of large companies, by their financial performance.

 ETSI Technical Committee SmartM2M: 
https://www.etsi.org/committee/smartm2m

Member benefits: 
https://www.etsi.org/images/files/membership/Membership-leaflet.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:058b0498-c359-4722-8180-c8902252b239 .

camssa:c83c183c-06aa-44ef-8854-b6a5ae252058 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WS-Security is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d628109e-7698-4d1f-94a7-5b3d14594bc0 .

camssa:c83d1c25-d81b-4eaf-8d80-fad806097aa4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTTP is included within at least 11 Member States' ICT Catalogues (e.g. Spain, France, Sweden)\r
\r
See CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards   """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:38512a2b-97a3-45af-bb79-8bfddbc6db03 .

camssa:c846501f-3878-404b-a51f-5ad03acc2027 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CSV specification itself does not provide any built-in means for guaranteeing the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions. Although the CSV specification does not provide these features directly, they can be implemented in conjunction with the systems or applications that handle CSV files to ensure proper access control and data protection.\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b283328f-8e77-41f2-b005-1c102fb8a27b .

camssa:c84695b0-e3a3-4d75-8414-4b8d88b5c8f3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c84aad6e-bcc8-410e-bde7-5b9b704a2f64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Extensible Forms Description Language specification is developed by a non-European organisation. Therefore, the specification cannot be considered a European standard.

Extensible Forms Description Language reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d9be542-8ff2-49e2-a2e4-fee26efe4399 .

camssa:c84e14a5-f626-445c-87ca-7ee5066b1359 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-164f43cef11b50b88c51c7115a7b37e506af696852ddaf46dfc1cb1c1521ec6d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c85145af-0c74-4193-9894-67f975cea3a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:095c6a87-3469-402c-86ac-27eff63b6020 .

camssa:c854bbf3-c618-40ba-addb-761cf1337ae7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c85d4d27-69d4-48c2-bb07-16d4f0e375f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TGF specification provides guidance on the use of digital identities to support the authentication of roles and agents involved in data transactions. It recommends the use of existing standards for identity and access management, such as OAuth, OpenID Connect, and SAML, to ensure that the authentication of users and agents is secure and reliable.  However, the specification itself does not provide guarantees of authenticity and authentication, as these depend on the specific implementation of the guidance and the technologies used.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:67506861-733e-413b-a8ed-79417f25edc6 .

camssa:c85ddbc0-1d19-4cee-91ef-68243d15cd7e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c8608948-a448-43e3-b5f0-f7aa607a9ae9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of the specification Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is to enable the portability of data among partners in the context of the manufacturing industry interoperability. This purpose is in part of the digital twins European initiative (IDTA) which is a German initiative that seeks to create a shared set of tools so manufacturing companies can seamlessly share their assets. 

IDTA reference:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41f4f642-66c4-4745-8ab0-343701624df2 .

camssa:c8624e44-cabf-4289-84ed-6929cd535e75 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By allowing the data exchange between applications and systems talking different languages JSON fosters the data portability of European public services. \r
\r
JSON specification:\r
https://www.ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/ECMA-404_2nd_edition_december_2017.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1684eb9-80dd-4a4e-895f-7aa975c26300 .

camssa:c867624b-7b96-4c88-ae5a-5fe7bfb9baff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of schema.org as a European standard.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb1d7930-d33d-4915-82bb-b0770f1e3b74 .

camssa:c86c4760-4356-401d-9eca-6ab628d3488a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c86f99a8-f87c-4ae9-ae75-e8ead48240b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ADMS is not related to guaranteeing authenticity nor authentication. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2ccb30d8-260d-4f0a-aeaa-a2ef85c6157c .

camssa:c86fa6b9-3e6b-4cd6-b2ad-be981aa0f15f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This specification's protocol allows the connectors to authenticate themselves on DAPS with their X509v3 certificate and to receive an access token in exchange which they can use to access other connectors. Thus, DAPS has the potential to enhance privacy by providing more granular control over the sharing and management of user attributes.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c72b61f7-4354-42ca-b23b-cca3d02d7251 .

camssa:c878d048-b11d-42e0-8414-85a2c36e30b3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c87ff712-6039-43f6-93c0-f8a8ae940e56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC) is an international Standards Development Organization headquartered in the United States.While it is based in the U.S., the OGC collaborates with organizations and experts from around the world to develop its standards and specifications.

OGC Home:
https://www.ogc.org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abea9bf8-2cf2-4222-a902-ec67947d050c .

camssa:c88d1e01-e066-4786-85a5-57137e46e6ba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-105c699a138c27ab9a1af9174253cd7488b278f700acdbb1bdbcc3e0b9c5ec3d ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c892d048-06ba-4138-a782-11aaf4e50829 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:c894280b-104c-4020-b088-5ce5e238c3b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the ESPD is not related to confidentiality, Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:606d433f-5a74-4ffb-bbd0-f39f49a78048 .

camssa:c8960926-fef3-41e6-a285-69f5f0240f7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although ESPD is not directly designed to facilitate organisational Interoperability agreements, it may\r
indirectly support their development by streamlining the procurement process and reducing administrative\r
burdens for businesses and public authorities.\r
\r
ESPD business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
European single procurement document and eCertis:\r
https://single-market-economy.ec.europa.eu/single-market/public-procurement/digitalprocurement/europeansingle-procurement-document-and-ecertis_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2da5e3fd-40c4-488c-84c1-470ddd62856e .

camssa:c8992ab4-695b-4f41-96a8-d1746857eeb5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:c89b29e1-68bb-444a-bdfc-57450440148c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL provides a flexible and extensible framework for expressing digital rights and permissions related to \r
digital content, without being tied to a specific domain or industry, meaning that it is intended to be applicable \r
across various industries and use cases.\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core\r
\r
W3C ODRL Community:\r
https://github.com/w3c/odrl'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00f3bf90-4600-418f-a556-b46e6efb945d .

camssa:c89bb1ba-f425-4395-a41e-95d493b8a32e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec can be customised in the sense that the user might opt for one configuration or the other depending on the host implementation requirements needed to deploy the specification.\r
\r
IPSec reference, Where IPSec can be implemented:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#section-3.3'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c3c83b7-74bc-42a0-adec-e48a1b547b9e .

camssa:c89f4988-1db8-495e-b738-a2e42e0b028e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of LDAP is not related to the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data or services. \r
Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f75a73c8-aa8d-4460-b186-552f5195efd6 .

camssa:c8a0f9f1-cab1-450e-972a-d362e59dc138 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """No overlap has been detected with European standardisation organisations activities at EU level.\r
This conclusion is based on the work programme of CEN  and ETSI  as published on their respective websites, and on the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020 .\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6d6e4a80-ea80-4a45-a6f2-fb86cc95026f .

