    cav:value "0" .

camssa:c8ceecc1-e2d5-4606-ac3c-4526d196688f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Having checked the documentation included in point 2.2.1, the conclusion has been reached of “Research Data Repository Interoperability Recommendations” not being foreseen to be transposed into a European standard within a reasonable time period."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a384b0ff-7703-466b-bd51-2d26661d23e0 .

camssa:c8df396c-cbde-43e3-ad9c-954cbb978986 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family of documents can potentially simplify the delivery of public services by promoting transparency, supporting decision-making, optimizing processes, facilitating interoperability, and enabling knowledge sharing.\r
\r
PROV Primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-primer/\r
\r
PROV Ontology:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/\r
\r
PROV Data Model:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b07151f-faa6-4dc8-a246-c1a48bf954f9 .

camssa:c8e639e1-911a-4901-b31b-41bc9a4340fb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not related to enabling the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data and services, therefore it neither promotes nor hinders visibility.\r
Although, it can enable visibility of administrations if it is combined with other specifications, the ECLI report is a good example of that case, where ECLI is based on the Dublin Core terms and eases interoperability in search practices within case law.\r
\r
ECLI Report:\r
https://e-justice.europa.eu/175/EN/european_case_law_identifier_ecli\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:918eb5ba-ac0f-4524-9e71-39c169d3d498 .

camssa:c8eb7a63-6d21-49e9-8fc1-86a54c43e94f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The definition of the specification justifies this criterion. The Core Public Organisation Vocabulary (CPOV) provides a common data model for describing public organisations in the European Union.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3fe7ad2c-2cd0-4b42-8657-1f67221b4f57 .

