camssa:c8f76c75-a3d3-4d36-a128-5a7044bd05a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """JPEG is not available for free. It needs to be paid to get access to the specification's text.\r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:90fd3e96-bd2c-4cd3-979a-48181279e972 .

camssa:c8fb5cc9-dccd-4a2f-a529-71876a31fe4f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Since the CLV vocabulary reuses other vocabularies such as DCTerms, their classes and properties can be customised depending on the use cases.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:376f7b90-54a1-4a05-893a-8662157a3c40 .

camssa:c8ffccf1-dad8-4c2a-93db-1fc1add83b33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 enables data portability by providing a robust, standardised, and secure transport mechanism that is independent of the application protocol. Furthermore, the extensibility of TLS 1.3 also offers potential for enhancements that could address specific data portability requirements if needed.

TLS 1.3 Reference :
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9f8c0e76-c1d4-4a14-ab8a-f1c228434d68 .

camssa:c9066ea9-eb0b-42eb-80c6-eec5851c97b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ADMS is being used as the basis of the European Platform for sharing and reuse Interoperability Solutions Joinup. It is done by an application profile developed to address the specific requirements of the platforms and stakeholder. The ADMS-AP is the schema used for the description of the assets included in Joinup, aiming to increase the cooperation between participants. \r
\r
ADMS on Joinup:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/asset-description-metadata-schema-adms/about\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:08bc6283-6c31-4d11-b2be-b5952ea3401f .

camssa:c9089ac5-b687-49bf-8c41-5384653bcbf8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 27001 was developed by the ISO/IEC joint technical committee JTC 1.  The access to JTC 1 working area is restricted, and individuals or companies are not eligible as members of ISO.  ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process: \r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html\r
\r
ISO/IEC 27001 reference website:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/54534.html\r
\r
ISO membership reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/get-involved.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b2cb1b80-92a4-4ef7-ab88-e0dbf941d95d .

camssa:c90afbbb-2e24-49a1-8f85-3650404cfd79 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of EN 319 422 is not related to enabling the exposure of interfaces of public administration's \r
services. Therefore,this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff9a9041-75d7-4474-b1e9-c82cae476370 .

camssa:c92074dd-ec0f-4ac5-9280-02b6dd517731 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Germany is recommending XACML in their ICT National Catalogues.\r
\r
Germany catalogue of standards:\r
https://www.din.de/en/about-standards/din-standards\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:   \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b19cd5f-b7ac-40e9-9e4f-b8d9754d5ceb .

camssa:c921225e-9da2-4dc8-8bcc-1c4ddfac43b8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

