camssa:c958c70a-00e7-4624-bc5a-573cfbd71c62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c4f0ae5-8b5e-477f-bab2-93ed9119c9ef .

camssa:c959965b-14c7-4f14-8a9e-9c617fc2f317 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Core Location Vocabulary is publicly available for its use and implementation. Moreover, it is available for everyone to study with no cost on Joinup webpage.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4c1e23b-e2ee-47fc-9d66-c30b677b24a1 .

camssa:c95b4161-d6aa-4595-951a-722519b63b7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 is technology agnostic, supporting various physical media like copper, fibre optics, and wireless connections. Its layered architecture ensures interoperability across different hardware, making it a versatile and widely adopted standard in networking environments.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2cd922c-70a3-4fed-ae73-935aae34b665 .

camssa:c9611c5f-97d5-4535-9c1b-910e96c6be52 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:c9673b33-e2cf-4984-b518-136450a7c0cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSV is included in 3 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to the Netherlands, Estonia, and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of these Member States is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO)factsheets.\r
\r
See:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d13bd8b7-3469-4f36-b2bd-4048eec3c0bb .

