        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:c96cd313-943f-41ee-baa5-d7710f78b879 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By ensuring that data conforms to predefined shapes and constraints, SHACL simplifies the understanding and accessibility of administrative information. This enhanced visibility enables public administrations to transparently share their processes and services with the public, thereby fostering greater trust and engagement.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:17a131fe-db29-4a50-b7a4-58b1d203dc2a .

camssa:c96e34bb-e577-46f7-b74c-76d3283b8a81 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/a2e4b319-14da-48a1-bf9e-68e22fdc90e5"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:c970061d-cbea-4cbb-8014-8c43b587b4bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-450e8a1f4cffbbf3de202e37bd642f098174559028df90ccc657473a6086bc0b ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:c976dd69-ef9b-4349-9434-8b48e3e0e6b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022, despite its American origin, has become a widely adopted and referenced standard within European frameworks. Its inclusion in the standICT catalog underscores its key role in the European technology landscape. This established standard ensures compatibility and interoperability, making it an essential component of European network infrastructure.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436

StandICT list: 
https://standict.eu/standards-repository/ieee-8023-2018-ieee-standard-ethernet'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:376fab8c-6275-4c90-a3ef-0a672598e04c .

camssa:c9779dcf-a7c9-4804-86d0-cc169640c421 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 303 645 specification is not included in any national catalogue. However, the specification has been recommended by some European national agencies like the Federal Office for Information Security (BSI) in Germany, or has been integrated in a public service like the Cybersecurity label in Finland to certify safe smart devices and assist consumers in buying safer products.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
Finnish Transport and Communications Agency Traficom reference:\r
https://www.kyberturvallisuuskeskus.fi/en/news/finland-becomes-first-european-country-certify-safe-smart-devices-new-cybersecurity-label\r
\r
German BSI reference:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/DE/Service-Navi/Presse/Pressemitteilungen/Presse2020/SmartHome_130720.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:633d879b-df72-4ec5-9bb3-8122e4dd0c3e .

camssa:c978d09c-864c-494b-8a00-c0ba3ce85edc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6896fe79-368f-4315-8cd3-2ce395e9d842 .

camssa:c979a7e1-b220-4076-a858-0af44da234f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

