camssa:c9c271f8-6d36-4d3d-a646-86c600ff2195 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States' public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. This Core Vocabulary fosters interoperability between public administrations, cross border services and impacts positively the development of eGovernment.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  \r
\r
Joinup news page "CCCEV - a key enabler of the Once-Only Principle":\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/news/cccev-and-once-only-principle'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4d056132-6928-474e-9c21-7d55fcad6d10 .

camssa:c9c2a998-dcbe-4951-a682-629dcb30569e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c9c56d3d-90e8-4eed-8a56-ee16d75fc828 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the OSI model itself is not a direct enabler of data portability, it can be part of the broader ecosystem of standards and frameworks that contribute to interoperability. Achieving effective data portability typically requires a combination of standardised data formats, well-defined APIs (Application Programming Interfaces), and adherence to relevant regulations and guidelines.

ISO/IEC 7498: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fd4b787-729a-4f24-93e2-43773d9243af .

camssa:c9caeb30-b8b0-440f-8fef-00f59dbc306e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c9cf0e4c-de08-4919-891f-8a6ca1f0ceea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Standard for Public Code is a business domain agnostic document that can be reused in a cross-domain. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d79da5e3-f31d-4e41-bd1e-b58f3dd864bc .

camssa:c9d22b6e-c953-448b-9c2c-f65fe2692423 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though the specification is related to the use and publication of metadata, it is not directly related to the publication of open data. The relation with metadata and its publication is focused on the availability and discoverability of access points and different parties for the exchange of data. \r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/en/\r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf26ee0a-2c28-4446-8427-0d44d5ca32c7 .

camssa:c9d42091-5595-4e2f-907b-b7b7e53a3ba3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'With the IPsec protocol it is possible to guarantee the authentication of the roles agents involved in transactions, and to allow or deny their access to data. Data is therefore secured against unwanted persons. In addition, it is also possible to set passwords to enter in an IPv6 address.

Redhat IPsec reference:
https://www.redhat.com/en/blog/ipv6-packets-and-ipsec'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b6ff8ef-85dc-401a-88e8-260432b54a37 .

camssa:c9df1369-104f-46e2-9030-c6559385a142 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c9e4f38f-2c79-4e69-af93-1be5b42106b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f3a51914-ee21-438f-bfba-891f469e3cd7 .

camssa:c9e64de5-7178-4ae6-b407-b36a0299c226 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) publishes some analysis on the EN 16234-1 e-CF component in different sectors of the European economy. The e-Competence Framework was positively evaluated by the Estonian Association of Information Technology and Telecommunications (ITL) which demonstrated that its application is efficient in policy decision-making.\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, Reports & Publications section, 'e-CF for EU & national policy makers' document:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/app/uploads/2019/08/for-EU-national-policy-makers.pdf\r
\r
Estonian Association of Information Technology and Telecommunications (ITL) reference:\r
https://itl.ee/en/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:acbd8a44-a3b1-424a-9e72-b8f6acf2ff40 .

camssa:c9ece8fe-0954-49fc-b71b-e50501b32795 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:c9f0f3ba-26d8-47c3-ae17-34c4e09c6153 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although the usage of Registered Organisation Vocabulary has been replaced by the Core Business Vocacabulary in the e-Government Core Vocabularies solution, it has the same content and it is sufficiently mature for the development of products and services. Specifically, there are implementations at European Level combining the Core Business Vocabulary and the Organisation Ontology as it can be seen in the following links.\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary\r
\r
Core Business Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-business-vocabulary\r
\r
EU Core Vocabularies in action:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/news/attachment/eu_core_vocabularies_in_action_using_core_business_vocabulary_in_the_eu_.pdf\r
\r
Describe organisations in RDF with Core Business Vocabulary and ORG Ontology: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/registered-organization-vocabulary/document/describe-organizations-rdf-core-business-vocabulary-and-org-ontology"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60307f81-67de-4745-b7d9-9afb7ae64ea4 .

camssa:c9f56999-f430-47ff-9bbe-d36dd494f1fe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:c9fb5b0c-7f95-45b7-abe2-c6f6dcadd060 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of CSV is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5c00470-cafd-4537-a8c0-4ac2fbe442a9 .

camssa:c9fc5db5-1fc2-48a3-b0b8-b739c525a581 a cav:Score,
