camssa:c9fe7aa6-acce-4539-8a2c-79d3de6da033 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP is a cross-sector and cross-border reusable vocabulary.\r
\r
In contexts where there are sector-specific or national requirements, the specification is extended (e.g. DCAT-AP-BE, DCAT-AP, StatDCAT-AP) """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd38ecf5-0cc2-4b2e-b528-7b1db8da12e6 .

camssa:ca00c814-6d96-436f-836c-90a8df8c3709 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification is supported by ISO. In order to participate in creating standards, the user must be part of 
their national standards body (assuming their country is part of ISO). On the other hand, another group that 
also supports OSI standardisation include Ecma International, an industry association dedicated to the standardization of information and communication systems.

Ecma International: 
https://ecma-international.org/

ISO Technical committees: 
https://www.iso.org/get-involved.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9d9d831-a303-4b79-a3d5-7fe932d38e82 .

camssa:ca08f100-6670-41ad-b4f8-dae4d8249247 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process:\r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f93fc6df-c2f3-489f-a422-cdce1ec71c15 .

camssa:ca0a1d39-14b7-41db-b06a-e82aa1961d95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The once-only principle is an e-government concept that aims to ensure that citizens, institutions, and companies only have to provide certain standard information to the authorities and administrations once.\r
\r
HTTPS is a protocol developed to exchange information over the internet environment. Thus, HTTPS eases the implementation of once-only principle by means of allowing administration's stakeholders reduce interaction.    \r
                                                                     \r
See: http://www.toop.eu/sites/default/files/D21_Federated_OOP_Architecture.pdf    """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc5b22ad-e298-4359-ab44-3135fc2f8f82 .

camssa:ca0eac23-7a91-47d6-86c6-9961570bcb2b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ca11c7c0-f5b9-4ccb-8289-61904c6363c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"EN 303 645 is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe135c6b-b413-42b8-b974-0452bd7c5048 .

camssa:ca147333-1fd9-4c99-8422-d1852510cae9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After carrying out information retrieval, no document or study has been found assessing the ODF in terms of efficiency or effectiveness."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:23246f93-3ff6-439c-8ec9-60c8273ad20a .

camssa:ca192d0f-5993-4ce4-8e44-5f1dc9c9ddce a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ca197b5a-fe31-4d63-bba5-b08204d9de6f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no evidence of the inclusion of WAI-ARIA in an open repository/catalogue of standards at European level.

EUOS repository of standards:
https://www.standict.eu/standards-repository

CENELEC and CEN search tool catalogue:
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CEN:105::RESET::::'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be969621-f667-4838-ba03-fff34f76daa6 .

camssa:ca1cb672-689e-43f4-91d5-4b4be6486f02 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-25deb65536af2c7e82f921c56df2c7e21093b2c06fdddd63021b4bccea0b9cd7 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ca1eb714-5a13-468e-8a6f-4be8d5024c5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS is developed by W3C, a standard development organisation based in the US.  Moreover, ADMS specification does not appear in any of the main European  standard development bodies, therefore, the specification is not a European standard.\r
\r
CEN-CENELEC homepage: \r
https://www.cencenelec.eu/\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:808e0483-50ee-4d57-a46a-8f86fb4bb056 .

camssa:ca27bc99-57dd-45ed-81ed-b629149bdc60 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documentation assessing different RDF features. For example, there is a study assessing the effectiveness and efficiency of RDF queries. As well there are studies focused on specific topics as is the fact of using RDF in the Smart Cities Modelling. \r
\r
Effective and Efficient Entity Search in RDF Data:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221466941_Effective_and_Efficient_Entity_Search_in_RDF_Data \r
\r
Performance assessment of RDF graph databases for smart city services:\r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1045926X1730246X'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1752597f-6473-4840-b5a0-842bacda2012 .

camssa:ca2a6697-92e8-46b9-b817-755a3c0d921e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary is designed to support the exchange of information between organisations or persons (more generally Agents) defining Requirements and organisations or persons responding to these Requirements by means of structured or unstructured Evidences. The specification also uses codelists which are a valuable feature to provide accuracy.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:14353e53-144c-4b19-aef9-8d17f3174cf1 .

camssa:ca2af1fe-55de-4983-b479-b6784217d6ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documents assessing and documenting UDDI features and providing possible improvements of its performance among other aspects. 
In "Indexing traditional UDDI for efficient discovery of web services" it is proposed a framework which combine the traditional UDDI with search engines to get a more efficient web services discovery. And in "Binding Now or Binding Later" various "UDDI modes of operation are evaluated using performance tests of the UDDI's implementations", to obtain the most efficient use of UDDI in different cases.

"Indexing traditional UDDI for efficient discovery of web services" reference:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/303921682_INDEXING_TRADITIONAL_UDDI_FOR_EFFICIENT_DISCOVERY_OF_WEB_SERVICES

"Binding Now or Binding Later" reference:
https://www.academia.edu/14435163/Binding_now_or_binding_later_The_performance_of_UDDI_registries'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ab7a871-5e24-4892-a539-64144b6da11f .

camssa:ca30012f-c181-4019-83d5-4af76bacaa68 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26c3fa9eb08207b2dfbd8d7c3852f0c9db3fdc50491d24db5b2f2eb1acf68732 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:ca323e97-1d8b-4e5d-8889-ed1bc8ea635a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of ISO/IEC 7498:1 is often evaluated through various means, including practical 
implementations and pilot projects. For instance, a 2016-paper uses the OSI Layer model, which has defined the theoretical architecture for network communications, as the starting point for innovating additional Layer 2 security requirements for a protected stack, which demonstrates the effectiveness of the specification as it is taken into account.

Innovating additional Layer 2 security requirements for a protected stack:
https://ro.ecu.edu.au/ism/184/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3005264-bbcd-4675-bac3-4165d79b9be5 .

