    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cb09cf68-4329-4019-a3ba-45efa03aad7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData follows REST principles and there exists some kind of data protection. However, the purpose of OData is not related to the security and privacy of the data exchange.\r
\r
OData reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752201'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d63bcaec-8346-478b-8ea2-93ed18df0a51 .

camssa:cb176914-b90e-4c82-95f8-61dd3307622c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a standard protocol, DNS helps to ensure interoperability when it comes to define processes for setting 
internet domain names, thus easing interoperability between devices, applications, data repositories, 
services and networks, this is why, among other reasons, it appears as one of the setting standards for the 
"Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications 
eligible for referencing in public procurement"

Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications 
eligible for referencing in public procurement :
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32014D0188'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84db2e34-7eaf-4377-8184-b9b1e4c64fa1 .

camssa:cb1ee981-0603-4f27-b986-013b53bce17e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although the Core Public Organisation Vocabulary does not have a good market acceptance, it proportionates innovative benefits such as facilitate information sharing, facilitate the development of common information systems, and cross-border information exchange.\r
\r
CPOV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:070bcdf4-2451-4177-8390-e713f52c1635 .

