camssa:cb59070a-14e8-48a2-9686-22260729f8e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 is maintained by ETSI, one of the European Agencies for Standardisation.  Moreover, the ESI family of specifications is developed and maintained by a technical committee, and it is supported by some organisations such as BMWi or Cryptolog International.\r
\r
About ETSI:\r
https://www.etsi.org/about\r
\r
ESI Technical Committee:\r
https://www.etsi.org/committee/1399-es\r
\r
ESI work programme:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/webapp/WorkProgram/Report_WorkItem.asp?WKI_ID=53589&curItemNr=1&totalNrItems=1&optDisplay=10&qSORT=HIGHVERSION&qETSI_ALL=&SearchPage=TRUE&qETSI_NUMBER=119+511&qINCLUDE_SUB_TB=True&qINCLUDE_MOVED_ON=&qSTOP_FLG=&qKEYWORD_BOOLEAN=&qCLUSTER_BOOLEAN=&qFREQUENCIES_BOOLEAN=&qSTOPPING_OUTDATED=&butSimple=Search&includeNonActiveTB=FALSE&includeSubProjectCode=&qREPORT_TYPE=SUMMARY'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:452092c9-186f-4c4f-98fd-5c449a2ca4be .

camssa:cb5e0aea-acb8-4857-83c2-b68650700593 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-21276471c1781fa2c7e78c8e03851e076b840beddbf5cf64f53b54b8855a01b8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:cb6c3880-fcaf-4f38-81b4-5396c76d101d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification explicitly addresses and enables data portability syntantic, semantic and policy wise. The goal of data portability in this ISO is to enable cloud service customers (CSCs) to move their data or applications between non-cloud and one or more cloud services and between cloud services. The critical considerations for portability discussions are the porting cost, the risks associated with the porting and how to control the costs and risks compared to the expected benefits.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1696b327-5cb0-4548-9abc-13998ed38dec .

camssa:cb753141-26e9-46ea-8884-9f69ddfa426f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a document format, ODF helps to make data available on the internet. This fact demonstrates that the standard is supporting the first level of maturity from Tim Berners-Lee's 5-star schema for Open data.  \r
 \r
ODF ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/66363.html\r
\r
ODF OASIS reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=office\r
 \r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:\r
https://5stardata.info/es/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:391b5f5e-01f9-4718-81b7-7a9b515e0afd .

camssa:cb75914c-13cb-4b3f-8a34-dfa6ea821b9c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cb7e9efa-f43c-41ef-8e34-5d3e915538aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 can enable digital service delivery channels by leveraging cloud computing technologies. It provides guidelines for scalable and available services, promotes integration and interoperability, supports rapid deployment, and enhances the accessibility of digital services. \r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b3ddd54-0328-4efc-836d-c7e5055dba66 .

camssa:cb7fa872-3d16-4d40-a657-d45b327a0525 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7369691a-62c1-4865-a37a-4297bc5fa14f .

camssa:cb82735d-7994-47f9-8877-72553e71e7a8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cf1de0bf03a8ee372af0deddf9ef5c4609f5a7bb9c7e001c89d887c6789eaf56 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:cb8799ae-3abc-4b4f-9580-9497bde2c6a2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cb87d8a1-da1b-4651-9170-9f3ea8127a3c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6ec33e201b803a1cc0150c0da8dc42b2a0f1029cf31e7a2c0fc81d1d8336ef36 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:cb8d39e8-a838-467d-a610-803c8cd8b910 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While publiccode.yml is not yet embedded in a specific European cross-border initiative, it holds clear potential to advance the goals of the Interoperable Europe Act. As a structured metadata specification for cataloguing public sector software, it would significantly aid in the discoverability and reuse of digital solutions, supporting cooperation, co-creation, and cross-border collaboration. By promoting transparency and interoperability, publiccode.yml could serve as a foundational tool in fostering a shared European digital ecosystem.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Interoperable Europe Act: 
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/en/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32024R0903'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ac10786-f509-4d6d-b6c1-970640d12d95 .

camssa:cb92adfc-b664-4bfb-95a8-d8d5f20a8d08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Registered Organization Vocabulary specification enables data portability for European public services by providing a standardised vocabulary based on established ontologies and supporting the use of European standard classifications. It shares foundational principles with the SEMIC Core Business Vocabulary (CBV), which captures key attributes of legal entities registered through formal processes. 

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

Core Business Vocabulary Github reference:
https://github.com/SEMICeu/Core-Business-Vocabulary/tree/master'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:70a653c1-eee3-4444-bd92-0b9e2d705faf .

camssa:cb9552d2-b93c-4727-8787-41d79bb42824 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cb962945-1b3f-4c44-9ba4-6c599389a454 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF was carried out initially in 1997 by the W3C working group that included representation from several companies with an important market share (e.g. IBM, Microsoft, Netscape, Nokia). RDF has been widely adopted and developed by means of W3C working groups that have worked on the continuous improvement and consolidation of the specification.  RDF has strong support as a tool for publishing data as Linked Open Data. This support comes from public administrations but also for companies with relevant market share. This fact demonstrates the maturity and market acceptance for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a986ea9-602e-49c0-88ba-ed78bd4cc73c .

camssa:cb98d42e-c942-4e87-b7f3-b743328def2f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cb9c0b14-810f-47f6-b6fc-a97207f44db7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:cb9e78d8-455d-4c1f-9bf0-d1c377cdc53d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cba02f91-5900-45b7-b58e-43ff429dfb26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification includes a whole set of enablers related to security at different levels. Moreover, EIRA helps users when working on analysing the requirements for digital public services, and makes it by providing specific perspectives and viewpoints related to security and privacy. 

Going deeper in details, there are specific enablers related to identify the requirements for identity and access management, which are the building blocks that will ensure that access to data is controlled, e-signature, e-seal amongst others. Additionally, elements such Trust enablers or blockchain can be consider assets and components that can help to ensure data integrity and data authenticity. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:823530e6-b3ec-4ce8-a297-072f2a330323 .

camssa:cbac8576-bab0-41c1-8db5-453699150e81 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:cbbf38ff-6d76-4c96-a80a-b2e39d58b0e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML has no mechanism to guarantees the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in
the data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e1c6f72-4e5c-4e01-8de5-3e03b0884bea .

camssa:cbc1c490-9d1c-4402-b778-3e4b63b68075 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """8 Member States are recommending JPEG in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are Estonia, France, Germany, Greece, Norway, Poland, Slovenia and Spain.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c47fa69b-b9c5-464c-9a96-c215bf85458e .

camssa:cbc4d283-95b4-45f4-ba35-d7984477041f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PDF 1.7 has the ISO community that supports the development of: International standards, Technical Specifications, Technical Report and Publicly Available Specification.\r
\r
See:\r
http://www.isotc292online.org/projects/iso-process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d69832a1-c013-4cb8-b583-05e29e9e17be .

camssa:cbda1a18-1ee5-471f-ae57-276e1ad47c08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The NUTS classification counts for funding projects within the EU, that is the European Regional Development Fund, the European Social Fund Plus and the Cohesion Fund. Besides, the specification RDF model has been revised in 2018, so that it could be mapped to a European Legislation Identifier (ELI), and as a consequence the NUTS classification can be linked to other EU Vocabularies and used in other European cross-border initiatives.\r
\r
EUR-LEX reference, COMMISSION IMPLEMENTING DECISION (EU) 2021/1130:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32021D1130\r
\r
ISA Programme-Joinup reference, 'Revise the NUTS RDF model' document:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/supporting-implementation-persistent-uri-policy-eu-institutions\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0485ca9d-c559-42dd-80e9-cd5fc6b2a687 .

