camssa:cc07aca7-6418-4f1b-81b5-bd05adef7284 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By allowing the exchange of datasets metadata, DCAT increases the searchability, visibility, discoverability and reuse of existing data, including information on processes and administrative rules. It is worth mentioning the DCAT-AP specification for European Data Portals as an example of the previous explanation.    \r
                                                 \r
DCAT-AP & European Data Portals reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe\r
\r
DEU data provider manual:\r
https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/\r
                                                                                                         \r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:915d8da2-e46c-4dac-92f2-a7d336c075ad .

