        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the time of elaborating this assessment, this specification is included in the "Linked Data Event Stream" ABB in the current EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS), specifically the "Semantic View" layer. It is also included in the "Immutable Database Manager" ABB, which is in the "Technical-Infrastructure View" layer.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26d94720-4a30-484a-8a1c-d1a1e12a0c2c .

camssa:cc3884bc-520b-4de7-a014-ffebdd2286ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"AMQP specification allows systems to send and receive messages securely and efficiently. Once a message is successfully delivered and acknowledged, AMQP can delete it from the queue. This means that the data doesn't linger indefinitely, which helps in managing resources efficiently.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04426c97-a737-4694-9ad5-b42a498f9e11 .

