camssa:cd16efbb-d946-4337-a2ff-3e961a5b3ae3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed by 2004, by OASIS, and has been evolved through different versions. The current version is the 2.0, which is available since the 2007, which demonstrates that it has overcome the possible issues hampering its use and now it is established and used. \r
\r
WS-BPEL OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/wsbpel/2.0/OS/wsbpel-v2.0-OS.html\r
\r
OASIS webpage:  \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e269564-d9b9-43ce-a94e-1b8f2ec05627 .

camssa:cd19c4d2-65d9-4f6a-8d42-d1ceebf426ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8f5ad37-671a-4795-ab05-e33afafc2a0d .

camssa:cd1a6ee7-0a1d-4d3f-b71a-73fafa9e70a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS is an extension of the File Transfer Protocol (FTP) that adds support for the Transport Layer Security (TLS) to secure the data exchange. So it is dependant of FTP and TLS versions.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d3c47d1-6f6d-4a38-bbb6-65d37c0e48be .

camssa:cd1fb785-eedd-461d-b1ba-8ca0709fd37a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is not included in any european catalogue.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca6a0ce0-1e62-4459-8f45-24a138146f58 .

camssa:cd25ad72-dc84-49c0-91e5-ce506bd1481f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Standard is not included in European or National platforms, however, openness and the benefits for the creation of public and reusable solutions is the philosophy of the specification. Besides, it is fully accessible for its consultation, study, implementation or contribution to its development. Therefore, this criterion can be considered positively since the access and purpose is based on transparency and ethical principles. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a7c6a59-28ac-483e-a814-7d86859e1dc0 .

camssa:cd2ea1ed-c403-4cda-aab1-d58ede9b5702 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not related to the publication of public data as open data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc9f1743-7c0c-45c4-a68c-6cbf43d83424 .

camssa:cd30c3df-ace4-4185-9b86-2b99ccba3bd1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DCAT specification explicitly mentions a section in its documentation about rights and obligations that can provide an access control mechanism. It can use the properties dcat:rights, dcat:accessRights and dcat:license to provide this access.\r
\r
\r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference (section 8):             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15f03333-0701-4680-9d3c-bcc94dad00be .

camssa:cd336cdc-c97d-4665-a992-9249542f14cb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cd37f923-e97a-42e9-b98b-35d84d12f165 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification can be used independently from specific operating systems and hardware platforms."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b32a9ac-56b8-4402-9ed9-7a876143ab80 .

camssa:cd3e40ff-acee-445f-ba34-4d194bdedd40 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the Dataspace Protocol is developed by a European standardisation organisation called IDSA and is widely used, it is not a European Standard in the sense of being developed and published by CEN or CENELEC specifically for the European region.

International Data Spaces Association (IDSA): https://internationaldataspaces.org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6cae9608-6aad-4dfb-a9c4-bc0667ece677 .

camssa:cd3ed10f-acd1-411e-8d21-9be2504c1169 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, XML has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eda7a35e-191e-4b2e-b3e2-41d71550b149 .

camssa:cd416ba9-a147-47c7-97b4-e1cc8c082b5a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cd42c8c5-2f9b-4af2-9272-37e92ec9c689 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:cd5c64d2-5d40-4d72-bc10-4fbd179278ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While OpenTelemetry itself is not a framework for creating organisational interoperability agreements, it significantly facilitates interoperability by standardising how telemetry data is collected, processed, and shared across different systems and organizations. By adopting OpenTelemetry, organisations can ensure consistent observability practices, seamless integration of monitoring tools, and enhanced collaboration across diverse IT environments.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cc5e6f65-5cdf-45be-92c9-d81d196389b0 .

camssa:cd69a371-956f-4f0e-a01a-6c7e56ddb015 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XML is publicly available for implementation and study for free on W3C's webpage. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:715c3212-7481-4200-9b2a-162790f989e9 .

camssa:cd6ab444-6e5d-4e5b-b892-4a00b8552dbc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cd6e301d-3798-4319-8c48-a9a42607f874 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cd6efdbd-fe8d-419d-af87-df09aab5b19a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:cd717a3c-2e5b-4d69-8766-4c2456ca69ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is technologically agnostic, is a specification based on YAML focused on the description of solutions, specifically, software.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec60df88-d263-4e3e-a619-eb2b3d914118 .

camssa:cd73d8dd-97b7-49fd-8a78-66042d886b16 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is included in 7 Member States catalogues of recommended specifications. This Member 
States are Austria, Croatia, France, Germany, Netherlands, Norway and Sweden.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c24b8828-f0b0-4c21-8037-459b0165278a .

camssa:cd792107-e429-42e6-a5e0-1477d9d2f624 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Domibus enables the reuse of relevant information through features like message templates, standardized formats, metadata, integration with backend systems, customization, and real-time communication within its messaging scope.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:38c05e61-73a3-47a2-b5cb-3f1da318e724 .

camssa:cd7ef2d2-2f5b-4ba7-9bae-7ebc292d23fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is excellent for accessing and maintaining distributed directory information services over internet. The main function of LDAP is to help users connect to their IT resources safely, as well as data protection. In this way, LDAP helps ensure data exchange using TLS and SSL mechanisms. It also allows authentication methods and access control lists using SASL and simple bind. Because of this, LDAP is often used in public administrations and has become an staple of the identity management industry.

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511

SSL cloudfare reference: 
https://www.cloudflare.com/es-es/learning/ssl/what-is-ssl/

TLS cloudfare reference:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/ssl/transport-layer-security-tls/

SASL gnu reference: 
https://www.gnu.org/software/gsasl/manual/gsasl.html#SASL-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76992408-27e4-411a-a0b4-e25490166e16 .

camssa:cd7f07e8-cfd7-4f1f-99f6-c49c06d464bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
