camssa:cdf1119a-8f80-4dc1-bf86-0ee4c101c262 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Assessments of the efficiency of OpenTelemetry primarily involves evaluating the performance, scalability, 
and practicality of implementations. A 2024-paper about the development of an OpenTelemetry extension for call graphs. Acall graph is an important feature in the application performance monitoring (APM) domain that helps users diagnose issues within their production applications. The techniques described in the study provide for extending OpenTelemetry agents to automatically collect data required for call graph creation, which highlights the efficiency of the specification.

OpenTelemetry Extension for Supporting Call Graphs: https://www.tdcommons.org/dpubs_series/6992/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:558a7bd7-32f5-4aae-a178-e26a16aa0640 .

camssa:cdf5dbd1-c683-44ce-9163-9297297683cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1bd4754f-b2cd-4e65-aed7-56871e4deef2 .

camssa:cdfb94f7-31ad-4eb8-80e6-0fd0ac8d0b62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SOAP 1.2 is a messaging protocol for exchanging information in a structured way, it uses XML for its message format. As the protocol is a messaging system for exchanging information in a structured way, it helps to promote the visibility and comprehensibility of the administrative rules. In addition, it is a key enabler for web services reuse across borders along with UDDI and WSDL. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSAW57_8.5.5/com.ibm.websphere.nd.multiplatform.doc/ae/cwbs_soapverdiffs.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6686fc2-ebf5-4b5e-807d-139103b4efb0 .

camssa:ce0b834d-0f58-4f56-8ee2-7f0fcaae1f7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the E-ARK CSIP does not specifically address personal data protection, it promotes the use of metadata, including administrative metadata, which can include information about access controls, security measures, and data sensitivity. This metadata can assist in documenting and managing the security and privacy aspects of information packages, including personal data, throughout their lifecycle.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e26002d1-ad73-4910-a0e5-8b3131538146 .

