        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML does not have built-in mechanisms to directly prevent unauthorized changes. Therefore, this
criterion is not applicable to the specification.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff985fc9-1507-45e9-aeab-619fe9b7bb16 .

camssa:ce157d70-b8fc-4cd0-9695-302f5ce6f336 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CELLAR is the semantic repository of the Publications Office, and it recognises SHACL as its standard of preference for data validation in the Semantic Web.\r
\r
See:\r
https://publications.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/658088eb-c071-11e8-9893-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-86108820"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e9ce5cb-377f-4fe5-ab42-81012a0f8f99 .

camssa:ce15aba5-b37c-4d53-b389-54e32af691c4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b4f0d1b7f1d41c70797fa200c6fc73ac01f2f1659319e5cb1cebe8f5e79c1fcb ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ce18f808-6c18-4e24-8600-428a1256447a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification can allow public administrations to define XML schemas with semantic bindings for the reuse of information across borders including reference to contracts or other legal documents without requiring the submission or provision more than once. \r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f6376b1-7f52-486d-ab1c-8ebc46e8422e .

camssa:ce19324f-6c7a-4855-9c77-fe21461618d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:899a6a0b-3f77-4f52-af02-2b5d18359932 .

camssa:ce1ad9c3-e3ce-45f4-916f-bf1d83a44933 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF is a non-profit making organisation. It is large open community of network designers, operators, vendors, and researchers. It is open to any interested individual with the evolution of the Internet architecture and the smooth operation of the Internet._x000D_\r
See: https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3935.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68c34087-da08-4772-8ac7-0a3fb15a7979 .

