camssa:ce2466b7-78a3-4777-b6ee-45c73b806462 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are different documentation and information that takes into account EuroVoc as part of the narrative and includes it as valuable. An article shows the usefulness of EuroVoc since it is included as the core of an application for the categorisation of documents (see link below). Also, an example of a use case for the Italian Chamber of Deputies. In here, the use case was presented in a EuroVoc conference to show the result and the effectiveness of using EuroVoc as the basis for the semi-automatic classification of documents.\r
\r
JRC EuroVoc Indexer JEX - A freely available multi-label categorisation tool\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/256846257_JRC_EuroVoc_Indexer_JEX_-_A_freely_available_multi-label_categorisation_tool\r
\r
Eurovoc and parliamentary documents: A semi-automatic classification experience at the Italian Chamber of Deputies:\r
https://expertsystem.com/expert-systems-cogito-semantic-platform-to-be-featured-at-eurovoc-conference/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66366f10-b2e9-4425-9be2-fd1a2d38e72c .

camssa:ce359a9b-baab-4faf-8930-f9b54593019e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including XSLT."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62daa872-b272-4d5b-b981-f27a5aeb7532 .

camssa:ce363592-3e1a-419d-8a6e-3cbd7c8879e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"EN 303 645 is a set of security best practices for Internet-connected consumer devices and is intended to support all parties involved in the development and manufacture of consumer IoT devices. The specification's recommendations (provisions) are intended to depend on any product from the IoT domain, and therefore the specification cannot be considered technology-agnostic.\r
\r
EN 303 645 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:615be803-cc62-478b-82a0-909e5527feb2 .

camssa:ce3a4ee2-b99c-43cd-836b-c67b6f8d8759 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org is a (structured data) mark-up schema that helps search engines understand the information on web pages and potentially provides richer search results. Therefore, the specification addresses data portability. In future scenarios, DCAT-AP-SDO (Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe) will potentially replace the common European DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe (DCAT-AP), which aims to enable data portability between information systems in the EU.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\r
\r
DCAT-AP reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dcat-ap\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8de3befb-211f-40b8-a665-92f9ec6226ff .

