camssa:ce8a32e8-1986-438e-a7f7-9824b0604b11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP is Licensed on a royalty-free basis under the European Union Public License (EUPL).\r
\r
See:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/ctt/dcatap/abstract#.XbFndZozY2w\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/custom-page/attachment/eupl_v1.2_en.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81fffb84-20b8-473f-b43b-c60be877f852 .

camssa:ce93369e-e350-4fc2-ae8f-39360c4b46df a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS is widely used for EU cross-border projects. For instance, it is used by TESTA, the data communication 
network service operated by the European Commission.

TESTA Overview & Service Catalogue
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/default/files/testa_-_20_years_isa_2_web_page_-_01_2021.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fcdd221-9494-47e3-957b-36c1de61a768 .

camssa:ce99e5ee-e9b5-4eb1-9a10-3b39694986cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:cea4fd52-d3ee-46ab-9df0-0a44897fb2cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are many extensions that can be implemented within the DNS standard protocol. Many of this 
extensions address security issues, while others are centered on its conformance testing or its integration in a broader framework.

Extension Mechanisms for DNS:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6891'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f53106b8-edb5-474d-a665-7336028b229f .

camssa:ceae8616-2679-4808-8d0b-a120fc275eb8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ceb09e55-4c9c-4b7f-bdf9-0a181b1d7fe8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Yes, the specification is mapped to Ontology ABB semantic layer.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/\r
\r
ELIS:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v500'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8dcf5290-d084-49b2-9693-faac132eedfd .

camssa:ceb6ae5c-28aa-464c-a709-37a81ce32081 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is a component derived from the actions implemented on the basis of the Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market. The aim of this regulation is to enhance interoperability when it comes to trust services of e-signatures in the European context.

Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 July 2014 on electronic 
identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b212ffa9-a4cf-4801-a15c-be1992bcfe6a .

camssa:cebf7449-db05-495b-bad4-3fc6c5ef38b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There are assessments that indirectly address the specification's effectiveness. For instance, this paper provides an overview of existing literature and reviews current open-source dataspace connector implementations that are compliant with the International Data Spaces (IDS) standard. By using this IDS standard, they are indirectly demonstrating its relevancy and effectiveness.\r
\r
A Survey of Dataspace Connector Implementations: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.11282.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e4ee5ab-d5f4-4917-9fed-376cb2b2f118 .

camssa:cebfd485-dd63-4ad7-9b21-ab6ebca4cd42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The LegalDocumentXML Specs provides a common legal document standard for the specification of parliamentary, legislative and judicial documents, for their interchange between institutions anywhere in the world and for the creation of a common data and metadata model that allows experience, expertise, and tools to be shared and extended by all participating peers, courts, Parliaments, Assemblies, Congresses and administrative branches of governments. \r
\r
The specification is publicly available at OASIS webpage. \r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72c43318-920d-4b0d-8e5f-829663ef037a .

camssa:cebfee29-2c20-4297-80d9-6165fbdd744a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification describes a set of security features of ebXML RegRep and incorporates different specifications to enable the secure exchange of data. For example, ebXML incorporates the WS-Security Core Specification (v1.1), which supports confidentiality of all ebXML RegRep protocols defined by this specification when those protocols are bound to SOAP.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
ebXML RegRep Part 2:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rs-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__32703_422331532'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a90a0e9-d12a-4e8d-aeeb-ab3f991a53e8 .

camssa:cec2eae0-a803-4e69-8c3a-a02c81cc6caf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS has some core functionalities that can not be be implemented separately.  Nonetheless, the specification has beed developed to support some requirements that are not mandatory but recommended.  \r
\r
DNS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1034  \r
\r
Domain Names - Implementation and Specification:                             \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035   '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:92181f20-d2c4-407f-a445-5a17bdbbe9f1 .

camssa:cec4909f-9c1c-4a70-8429-7b878c47e480 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The objective of ELI does not pertain to the modeling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not
applicable to the specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a647294c-e5bd-46bb-980c-145460703386 .

camssa:ceca83d0-ccd9-43d0-b8cd-85c37deb9ce1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The FTP is published as a reusable solution in Joinup, the collaborative platform for Reusable IT Solutions funded by the European Commission. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/file-transfer-protocol/distribution/file-transfer-protocol"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f5eeb973-94fd-40ee-879f-e6ad6bc17500 .

camssa:cecabb4a-0292-4ac0-9dcb-0c2a4b3d20f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The fact that there are mechanisms to ensure that only certain users can upload or modify a data record guarantees the secure processing of the data. In addition, it is possible to digitally sign and UDDI entities can use it to give more confidence in the data.

IBM security reference:
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/was/9.0.5?topic=services-overview-version-3-uddi-registry'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:30670af3-5a44-479b-81a5-f227ee163488 .

camssa:cecb3555-9ad8-426d-8ecb-5b0159cb4c58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI has provided a conformance testing tool for electronic signatures according to the European Commission Mandate 460. The conformity testing tool involves different standards applied in the development of eSignatures, including CAdES baseline profile. \r
\r
See:\r
https://signatures-conformance-checker.etsi.org/pub/CAdESConformanceTestChecker_v1.0.pdf https://signatures-conformance-checker.etsi.org/pub/index.shtml"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59d2ab58-7605-4d49-9779-78e5f80637a9 .

camssa:cecd2548-d705-4939-b516-40696569bfdd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification was formally defined between 2015 and 2017 with the experience and the expertise of the Member States that were closely working together to consolidate the guidelines. In this sense, the Regulatory Scrutiny Board has published in their annual reports the evolution of the Better regulation framework implementation in terms of the quality derived from other pieces of legislation. This fact demonstrates that both guidelines and toolbox have been agreed as relevant instruments, therefore being mature enough for its use elsewhere.

Regulatory board reports:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/regulatory-scrutiny-board_en#annual-reports 

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Guidelines reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/d0bbd77f-bee5-4ee5-b5c4-6110c7605476_en?filename=swd2021_305_en.pdf

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:24b01821-2b83-44bf-9984-5f5466e37811 .

camssa:cecdb0cf-9c0d-4fcf-809a-f82f8c078889 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cecf35b5-ec9f-4ba3-bdf1-c69c90a2544c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Organizations like the Cloud Standards Customer Council (CSCC) and the Object Management Group (OMG) are involved in the development and promotion of cloud standards, including ISO/IEC 19941. These groups work with various stakeholders to influence standards development and advance the adoption of cloud computing.\r
\r
OMG: https://www.omg.org/cloud/deliverables/CSCC-Interoperability-and-Portability-for-Cloud-Computing-A-Guide.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6a188ff-aed9-4a3d-b7c7-4f140c56dd3b .

camssa:ced8cc78-cc18-4c5f-b7dc-9ad8a77998d3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'8 Member States are recommending UDDI in their ICT National Catalogues. This Member States are 
Bulgaria, Cyprus, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, Netherlands and Spain.

Joinup catalogue:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c4103a2-5879-4d55-bbfb-d64625c740d9 .

camssa:cedc0e27-bfd0-42d6-9471-ffe8701b342d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cedc408a-e4c0-46c8-9eac-bb9d9d7f0bf7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 16234-1 e-CF provides a reference framework for the ICT workforce and contributes inter alia to the adoption of the Shaping Europe's digital future approach (see CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.4). Digital transformation sets out actions to the development of digital public services.\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference, section 1.4:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf\r
\r
Shaping Europe's digital future reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/strategy/priorities-2019-2024/europe-fit-digital-age/shaping-europe-digital-future_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b75f9716-99c1-430b-973e-ad3a674b378e .

camssa:cedd4125-ea8c-45bd-bc5d-426fb725472d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'When XHTML became a W3C recommendation, it was well accepted, but with the introduction of HTML5, its
usage has significantly declined. The following link provides a comparison of the usage of various HTML
languages, showing that XHTML 1.0 is increasingly in decline, while HTML5 continues to rise.

HTML vs XHTML version statistics:
https://www.powermapper.com/blog/html-vs-xhtml-version-statistics/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f6588d9-f68a-47e7-87aa-5593e1cddec3 .

camssa:cee0c302-7319-4865-84a3-8db70f2b0ed5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are several reports assessing how DCAT-AP is effective and efficient for the publication of open data. For example, the study of DCAT-AP representation of Czech National Open Data Catalog and its impact, or an assessment of the application of DCAT-AP in the European Data Portal.\r
\r
DCAT-AP Specification:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/release/200\r
\r
DCAT-AP representation of Czech National Open Data Catalog and its impact:\r
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1570826818300532\r
\r
Linked Data in the European Data Portal: A Comprehensive Platform for Applying DCAT-AP:\r
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-27325-5_15'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d158cc0-8777-4aae-8acb-4b9b60c2b169 .

camssa:cee54cf8-a2ab-4b9c-9dfa-e9969fcd73b3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """One of the tools provided by the specification is focused on evaluating if the needs of a new proposal require any ICT aspect that can be foreseen and adapted to the most efficient manner, ensuring that the new proposal fits its needs and at the same time the process is efficient. Having said this, it is worth noting that the purpose of the specification is not related to the business process definition, and therefore, this criterion does not apply to the specification.\r
\r
Betterr Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4abb2543-579e-4c8e-81aa-2226a7c47a86 .

