camssa:cf6ac351-4dda-4266-81d5-791d102e5334 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This Technical Specification (TS) has been produced by ETSI Technical Committee Electronic Signatures and Trust Infrastructures (ESI). There are two paths to get involved in ETSI's Industry Specification Groups (ISG): as an ETSI member, or as a direct participant. The participation in the technical group is reserved to ETSI members, who require registration, fees, and membership approval. Organisations who are not members of ETSI may still participate in the ISG, attend meetings, subscribe to the e-mail lists and help build the specifications by making technical contributions. They do not have voting rights and must pay a participation fee per person per meeting day to attend ISG meetings.

ETSI Technical Committee ESI: 
https://www.etsi.org/committee/esi\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c4f2484-feed-4a91-a956-3405f1717627 .

camssa:cf6b9183-aa81-4c4b-9eae-9bb95e0cba1d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b8f7f5098ef900044e245ff5b30832215e00204b1e244545d80a28013685c811 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cf6d2ca5-dd2d-40f3-8a1b-a1c3e0f4b2aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EIRA covers all LOST views, which means from legal requirements to how technically are there implemented. In relation to the availability of interfaces, the specification can be key, as it the first step to identify what should solutions include in terms of data and functional requirements. They have to be aligned from legal to technical aspects. In this sense, EIRA can help to provide different mechanisms to access and use these digital public services from these different perspectives as they are the end-user or the public organisations internally. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36503c10-8f88-4421-b664-1c8d8fc1c34d .

camssa:cf722e57-d7bc-4a01-9a22-28b65a8e7530 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox acknowledges the relevance of Open Data in the development of public policies. However, it does not provide extensive recommendations regarding the means of publishing data on the web (Tool #4 and #28 provide recommendations on integrating systems using open data), nor does it exclude the use of proprietary software, in line with DIRECTIVE (EU) 2019/1024 on open data and the re-use of public sector information.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf

DIRECTIVE (EU) 2019/1024 on open data and the re-use of public sector information:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2019/1024/oj/eng'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d82aba22-1584-4f33-8b84-6224b0f8b945 .

camssa:cf793b44-e4f1-4e19-929b-426aa447c431 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS UDDI Specification Technical Committee in charge of the development of UDDI, operates under RF on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free and (F)RAND basis.

Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) Policy:
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr

Oracle OASIS UDDI Intellectual Property Disclosure:
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/uddi-spec/ipr.php'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89c3014e-beae-45fd-85e2-ecce634cc95d .

camssa:cf7cf1ea-6192-485e-b49e-8580f163c0dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

