    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cf899373-0492-4cc9-9e82-96c4b7194859 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The GraphQL specification does not give any provisions for the management and protection of personal data, but there are some best practices that can be adopted to tackle this issue, that may come from the server side.\r
\r
GraphQL specifciation:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:77be9f81-7ed9-4087-9638-b3f2704e972b .

camssa:cf8d53b8-85f6-4acd-ac5a-c4e89ea26fcc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the core specification is not customisable, there are aspects of its implementation and configuration that can be tailored to meet specific needs.

IPv6 customisation:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460#section-4'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0ab287b-c423-4862-a1fb-9d54a001a0bb .

camssa:cf8e3ff4-f609-4634-98a1-2027331e5443 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64bacef6-7959-4ade-835c-af8538ba0f7e .

camssa:cf967f8a-bd59-4434-a61e-53a74e493244 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cf993a01-3e5a-44e3-986b-d25b8ce9256d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dublin Core element set defines a set of metadata elements for cataloging library items and other electronic resources. Such items are known as "resources", and there exist certain relationships (Dublin Core calls these relationships "elements") between resources and other resources or data.\r
\r
DCMI Webpage:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d4401ad6-756e-4dbd-a435-880e9129a12a .

camssa:cf9abc9d-7330-4bf5-8176-4be38e6d8f59 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:cfadcc75-09a0-4ee0-8a2e-963601881c7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of MIME is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:905b3b9b-f308-4a7b-a76b-3ecdf3e46e39 .

camssa:cfaf0368-8101-4748-82b5-2a65a7f8c631 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the efficiency of SHACL. In "A Review of SHACL: From Data Validation to Schema Reasoning for RDF Graphs", the SHACL efficiency is assessed. In this study, different formal frameworks used to study this language and the various proposed semantics are reviewed. Moreover, practical aspects of SHACL are covered, discussing its implementations and state of adoption.

"A Review of SHACL: From Data Validation to Schema Reasoning for RDF Graphs" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-95481-9_6

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3883e8f-fa7a-42df-9c50-bf1da5c1c730 .

camssa:cfb58d1d-f164-4eda-9b31-7fef49f6e292 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related to  e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fde6402-7942-4122-9bec-0f1b11bb1d8c .

camssa:cfba59ec-34ba-4a77-b034-013bf59ea565 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TGF is already mapped to the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (EIRA). More specifically, TGF covers the Shared Governance Framework, Digital Governance, Digital Public Service Delivery, and Interoperability Framework from the Organisational view.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c35b288-cc86-4d4e-bdc4-dae9f734294e .

camssa:cfbd5440-8ff9-4de6-9b85-bb0a2e754803 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The fact that the specification has been adopted by different organisations and initiatives demonstrates that the specification has sufficient completeness and consistency for the use and development of products and services. \r
Additionally, the specification is easy to use, flexible and not bound to a particular business domain. \r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4bc9649-0713-48de-b1cb-f22dfc1ee0ac .

camssa:cfbef4ad-3b2f-40db-a37e-1c0c1d6a14db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Dataspace Protocol is part of both private and public innovative solutions. As for private, it is included in the "Building data spaces for sustainability use cases" section of Amazon Web Services Prescriptive Guidance, which provides time-tested strategies, guides, and patterns to help accelerate cloud migration, modernization, and optimization projects. 

Regarding public initiatives, the Dataspace Protocol is mentioned in the making of Road-X, a robust and secure solution to exchange data and establish a collaborative ecosystem developed by the Nordic Institute for Interoperability Solutions (NIIS). It streamlines data exchange processes, enhances security, and facilitates interoperability, enabling organisations to derive greater value from their data assets.

AWS Prescriptive Guidance: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/strategy-building-data-spaces/dataspace-protocol.html

NIIS Making of X-Road 8 - PoC: https://www.niis.org/blog'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b78fd5f2-2a83-47f2-a797-379a00ec7ced .

camssa:cfc1b579-56f9-44bd-a5d9-fbcb058609ee a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2cedd44f05183dae5548108bdeace2c092b84c7c5d89c475b0741ddae7fc7b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:cfc5794d-3543-4633-8652-5941560b59fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Taking the initial purpose of the specification, which is to reduce the cost and complexity of user management operations by providing a common user schema, an extension model, and a service protocol, it can be considered that the specification is indirectly involved in fostering the comprehensibility of Public Administrations data as well as relevant data produced for the decision-making process.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69b823cc-bfd3-489c-878f-4a93fe018505 .

camssa:cfc68589-9ee0-4584-ad97-acb9de55fdb0 a cav:Score,
