    cav:value "1" .

camssa:d04200ba-5736-483e-8132-d2fa45e2a3f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI system does not inherently ensure or enable data processing accuracy. Therefore, this criterion is
considered not applicable to this specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3e51e6c-f4a5-4566-bf99-60f1b2fd5e30 .

camssa:d04938f0-cf99-4336-8e47-44898a2ee230 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS can typically be extended to meet specific organizational needs and requirements. The extensibility of such services allows organizations to adapt the provisioning system to their unique workflows, attribute types, and integration points. For instance, it is possible to extend custom attribute types beyond standard ones. \r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6b9b54e-0b77-4191-aed5-c2e21dabda05 .

camssa:d049b33f-d2ed-484e-ba18-d5c22ed6c042 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has been found some studies assessing the efficiency of PROV. Among some of the studies, we can find  one assessing the data provenance on the web of data, or another testing the PROV encoding with social science data.\r
\r
Measuring PROV provenance on the web of data:\r
http://provenanceweek.org/2016/p3yl/papers/paper_89.pdf\r
\r
Encoding Provenance of Social Science Data: Integrating PROV with DDI:\r
https://ddialliance.org/encoding-provenance-of-social-science-data-integrating-prov-with-ddi-0\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89a291a8-6335-402c-b8c1-c4176bc73d8d .

camssa:d04ea8a9-98db-4e81-8bb3-f5849776a6bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "JSON allows the data exchange and consumption from different administrations stakeholders. Ensuring data exchange through applications avoids the interaction by means of reducing the non-digital data exchange. Therefore, the adoption of JSON eases the reduction of administrative burden."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc41b04e-7038-450f-9a83-7d28c3f65cf5 .

camssa:d04f60f0-0d9b-48f3-a637-04b2ed9e21b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is not included in any initiative at European or National level covering privacy aspects. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0eb9abb1-89e3-4d35-8031-6e8d41c802e5 .

camssa:d0505693-7b3f-4810-b3a0-5646ab61706b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Understanding data exchange as the publication by the administration of data for its later consumption by citizens, the specification facilitates the trustworthy data exchange in RDF format by providing the means to validate RDF data graphs.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4832ce19-0b8d-40b4-97ef-ca26cab4d8c5 .

