camssa:d0bbee4b-429a-4b41-bd05-f5aeb3f56ec9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The ISO specifications are published to be able to respond to a market need which represent a consensus of an expert group. It was launched initially by Adobe in 1993 as a proprietary solution but free of charge. In July 1st, 2008 PDF became an Open Standard published by ISO. In addition, PDF is highly adopted as a document format for exchange information, which is technological independent. These facts demonstrate the maturity and market acceptance for its use in the development of products and services. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:363e871c-ca11-4e98-8717-684fc897d17e .

camssa:d0bc3669-ee1d-4da0-ad94-84431eec1493 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not included per se in any supra-national catalogue. Despite this, SOAP 1.2 is part of the Electronic Signatures and Infrastructures (ESI); Rationalized framework of Standards for Electronic Registered Delivery Services Applying Electronic Signatures, which is an ETSI Special Report. \r
\r
ETSI SR 019 050 Reference where SOAP is included:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_sr/019000_019099/019050/01.01.01_60/sr_019050v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:377cab18-739b-4f6c-822a-4616a2f0f577 .

camssa:d0c0c8a3-aebe-4c47-87df-0466d8aee7c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been creation to exchange information through the internet, it has not security layer. \r
\r
The extension of HTTP; HTTPS, uses other protocols for securing communications."""@en ;
