    cav:value "40" .

camssa:d148e835-a246-4bcf-8a69-90b36f712f1a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Time Stamp Authority guarantee that the data has not been subjected to any form of unauthorized modification, thereby ensuring the integrity of the information in question. While TSP is a tool that can enhance data integrity and provide audit trails, it primarily helps in detecting unauthorized changes rather than preventing them. For comprehensive protection, it should be integrated into a broader security framework that includes preventive, detective, and corrective controls.

Emudhra TSP reference: 
https://emudhra.com/blog/what-is-timestamping

TSP/TSA IETF reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8de06cd1-b8b9-44d8-8959-ddec1f0bc81d .

camssa:d14a3b5c-c37a-4d35-9019-1459f3b6a010 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the second star corresponds to the availability of data as structured data. ebXML is a standard that proposes an XML-based infrastructure enabling the user to store data in a structured manner. In addition, this specification has been established as an open standard.

Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data: 
https://5stardata.info/en/

ebXML open standard:
https://www.oasis-open.org/2023/02/23/oasis-ebxml-repreg-v4-0-approved-as-international-standard/

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9827a20e-55d4-4788-82f6-e30d42fb64d3 .

camssa:d14b4751-f45f-4608-bff5-0667da872542 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CPOV, with its links between organizations, their departments and their responsibilities, structures the different relations and thereby spot similarities, duplications of effort or gaps in the system. Comparisons can also be made across borders so that potential efficiencies can be more easily identified. Therefore, with this function it is possible to have data sets with accuracy data. However, monitoring by public administrations is necessary to ensure that the published data is completely accurate.

CPOV Joinup reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-organisation-vocabulary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e35d2b2-42db-4a30-88a9-8f62e223dd52 .

