camssa:d196a7dc-2394-470e-b027-ab5811cbfcbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL has been selected for a European H2020 project called SPECIAL which aims to use ODRL to validate GDPR compliance of Legislation being produced.\r
\r
Its use has also been implemented within SERAMIS a project which extended ODRL for the validation of GDPR aspects.\r
\r
SERAMIS:\r
https://cordis.europa.eu/docs/projects/cnect/2/612052/080/deliverables/001-D55v4GDPR.pdf\r
\r
SPECIAL Deliverable:\r
https://www.specialprivacy.eu/images/documents/SPECIAL_D17_M17_V10.pdf\r
\r
Representing Activities associated with Processing of Personal Data and Consent using Semantic Web for\r
GDPR Compliance:\r
https://harshp.com/research/publications/035-representing'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:28ce25c1-e574-433a-9d0b-6a39b5d2a273 .

camssa:d19ea6b5-da42-494f-8d9e-44e8747ae021 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc5bd9a7d0b2acc7f246522414fd5f5d579b977180bb04fa60a545cb35dae90f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:d1a09e9c-a995-46be-814d-a5a6705e26de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DoH is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose Member State NIF has a high performance on interoperability according to the NIFO factsheets.

CAMSS List of Standards:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/camss-list-standards

2023 NIFO factsheets: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2023'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bd34b94-e286-49a2-80ed-64b1305f6eb1 .

camssa:d1a94dc2-1484-4bb5-8908-4f67162d3242 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) is the foundation for many different innovative solutions. For instance, BIND 9 by the Internet Systems Consortium (ISC). BIND (9.17.10) comes with initial support for DNS-over-HTTPS (DoH). Deployment of DoH is also a significant stepping stone for wider adoption of the Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) and Encrypted Server Name Indication (ESNI) features of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol. These features further improve users’ privacy by preventing third parties from snooping, and by making it harder to block websites by analysing and intercepting TLS handshake requests.

ISC DoH in BIND 9: https://www.isc.org/blogs/bind-implements-doh-2021/

Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol RFC 8446: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4aac3994-5254-41b5-812c-7f635f5af54e .

camssa:d1abfb59-d5bb-4e99-b968-2ce50d3365a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62fb9d02-df21-46ab-bf9f-71eb2590effa .

camssa:d1ac8bb6-74ae-4460-864f-e597cb56af50 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UTF-8 encoding can enable digital service delivery channels by supporting multiple languages and scripts, simplifying data processing and exchange, and improving accessibility for users who speak different languages.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36aafdae-09c4-411b-9765-e5a7c754aa86 .

camssa:d1b058ce-5913-4b46-98b3-71bdc2e980b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XSD specification contributed to enabling digital service delivery channels by contributing to the XML Europass 3.0 channels which is the final release for describing the domain of infromation for a learner.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/\r
\r
Europass XML Schema 3.0 Reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/employment-and-working-conditions/solution/europass-xml-schema-v30/about'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a522ae7d-ca21-4056-9865-58e2c626d6f8 .

camssa:d1b8844c-a880-45dd-bd2f-438817a03a18 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of LDAP is not related to the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's \r
services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:61ad14d3-469b-482f-bc54-c79de0aba6c8 .

camssa:d1c01d18-b80e-4ae4-8667-3917abc2090e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Public services can offer authentication APIs that accept DIDs and verifiable credentials (VCs) to verify user identity. Moreover, Decentralized Identifiers allow one to discover the location of an authoritative public master data record of an entity. This mechanism can be used for organizations like public administrations. 

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/

DIDs use cases:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-use-cases/#crossPlatform'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:adafccfc-22a7-492f-bf3c-830642ae4576 .

camssa:d1c7f98e-b15c-4b93-8368-535a4d9cd337 a cav:Score,
