        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d2cd922c-70a3-4fed-ae73-935aae34b665 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d2cff650-ae48-4e81-8c86-d24acd27e45a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/\r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:515ea9cf-b2a9-41f2-8cc0-dbb5d519a7c5 .

camssa:d2d0f9ab-07e8-48af-9f81-150f11bbf843 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"This specification refers to the System for Cross-domain Identity Management whose purpose is to securely automate the exchange of user identity data between a company's cloud applications and any service providers. It is inherently abstract and can be implemented and/or used in any domain as long as it fulfills the requirements. Therefore, its use goes beyond a specific business domain.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:209dd171-ded7-4cff-8cb9-37ca67b8640b .

camssa:d2d178e3-b294-4af5-b694-3882460878a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SMP has been used as the basis for the development of the eDelivery SMP specification, which in turn is the basis for the implementation of the CEF eDelivery Building Block. The CEF eDelivery Building Block helps public administrations to exchange information with stakeholders (e.g. other administrations, businesses or citizens).\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009\r
\r
eDelivery SMP specification: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/eDelivery+SMP\r
\r
CEF eDelivery Building Block: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/inea/sites/inea/files/building_block_dsi-introdocument_edelivery_v1_00.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59b62785-f652-4a20-9bb6-7e953461800d .

camssa:d2d3798f-836b-4275-9194-20cab8bfda55 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT is included in 6 national catalogues,  this Member States are: Cyprus, France, Germany, Greece, Poland, Portugal and Sweden. They belong to Member States which are aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.

