camssa:d33d1e07-7424-4482-b743-d70a99eaaca6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 along with the whole Electronics Signature Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications, has been proven efficient for the Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Documents (TR-ESOR), a document from the German Federal Office of Information Security that specifies security-related requirements for the long-term preservation of evidence of cryptographically signed electronic documents and data along with associated electronic administrative data (metadata).\r
\r
TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/EN/BSI/Publications/TechGuidelines/TR03125/TR-03125_B_v1_2_2.pdf?__blob=publicationFile&v=1\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9f194609-0f21-4dcf-aac3-cff06a334398 .

