camssa:d416c615-6a6b-4381-a982-0dc266bafa08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML is a data serialization model that can be used in any domain. It is designed to be human-friendly, and works well with modern programming languages for common everyday tasks.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#chapter-1-introduction-to-yaml'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f1c7f550-ccb7-402a-a183-51a8faefc780 .

camssa:d417df3b-b823-4bf0-98f8-49dd82abbd67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"NUTS was originally created to be used in a statistical environment and its field of application is not expected to change in the short term. However, NUTS could be implemented 'as-is' to other domains, in the sense that territorial divisions are also interesting in other statistical research areas, and not only limited to the fields of policy and demography. At the time being, there is no reference to any implementation use case of the NUTS specification.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:301ac275-c303-474c-9332-6528b4d540c1 .

camssa:d41919c2-243a-4a76-aa1e-b5ded475fbec a cav:Score,
