    cav:assignedTo sc:c-093c1e09f5a65e4cba0247dcab5a8f4854f3e512db336b1855b9a4c48d3659e0 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:d492a25f-44a4-400b-abd8-3e486026cc67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 primarily defines the physical and data link layers for wired Ethernet networks. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a783a29-7571-4ff2-9704-6332d5f28a84 .

camssa:d495bf05-dbbe-4de0-aa9c-6aaed09e8040 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SVG is a specification that supports the graphical data exchange, which can be combined with XSL. It helps to the combination and exchange and integrations within other formats as XML, which is widely used for the data transmission across borders and between administrations.\r
\r
SVG and XSL: \r
https://www.w3.org/People/maxf/papers/2002-07-SVGOpen/svgopen.html#id2590005"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:217248ad-180a-423d-889c-b3c040fadd10 .

camssa:d4a0245c-ae4d-41fe-ac82-7e65ae8ca59c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The development of the ESPD is managed by the European Commission, which consults with stakeholders\r
during the development process. This can include representatives from public authorities, business\r
organizations, industry associations, and other interested parties. In addition, the Github platform hosts the larger community that contribute to the development of the specification.\r
\r
ESPD Business handbook:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/xml_business_handbook.html\r
\r
ESPD Issues in Github:\r
https://github.com/OP-TED/ESPD-EDM/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc11618c-8c06-44a8-8fbc-7157da151b9e .

camssa:d4a0e9fb-4db6-428a-b25d-95fc9c6ebe3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ShEx is not related to multilingualism; therefore, this criterion does not apply to the specification.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60c86411-bc5d-4d91-bbed-064e70037d3c .

camssa:d4a3a84e-7e40-4cfe-b22e-2d8f7e4a8a94 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 has been developed to establish, locate, access and authenticate a trusted like which makes available trust service status information, following the mentioned intention of the specification, it can be said it enables or helps to enable digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7346218a-34d5-47df-b5bf-9f156e4f9230 .

