camssa:d4dae1b8-2bc3-491a-ae93-0f590a234702 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData offers a way to both break down data silos and increase the shared value of data. The specification contributes creating an ecosystem where data consumers and producers can interoperate more than ever, allowing more applications to make sense of a broader set of data and eases the delivery of European public services (see the Netherlands Advisory report stating the usability of OData as a solution to streamline the delivery of public services).\r
\r
Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/odp-oasis-open-data-protocol-odata-tc/about\r
\r
Netherlands OData Advisory report reference: \r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/odata'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:181bebe6-e9de-48c5-a30d-4fe4a274bc86 .

camssa:d4e22c58-181e-4ff0-9e26-ae2dcf11eb85 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8eb17470327d32b3bb523447fe72ee5c60ddb03e81dae318b485fbe05f48a844 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:d4e8759f-4350-4af2-b5e7-7e164054d0e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The GraphQL specification, sub-specifications, and official reference implementations are developed using the working group model. The working groups meet monthly or as-needed in order to review ideas and plan their work.  The GraphQL Working Group is the main group that plans and implements changes to the GraphQL specification. They meet actively and is the default place for discussion for topics which do not have a separate breakout working group.\r
\r
GraphQL Working groups:\r
https://graphql.org/community/developers/#working-groups\r
\r
GraphQL participation agreement:\r
https://github.com/graphql/graphql-wg/tree/HEAD/membership"'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7b78803d-a60e-438d-8828-5405c4a8b4c2 .

camssa:d4e9c6ab-c386-45d6-82e2-fff7ac003ac1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All Outputs packages have been published under the Creative Commons Attribution (CC-BY) licence. RDA’s IPR policy:\r
See: \r
 http://dx.doi.org/10.15497/DA8C2CC2-A7AF-4E3A-A4D6-C100E5C27492"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5256dcc-5c05-4591-9922-f5a8ccec48c6 .

