        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "nan"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0db8a4d1-fc2a-4617-b0ef-1abeea1f0cf1 .

camssa:d518b9e1-3bfc-45b9-bc91-57ecf9ad915c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM has published documentation regarding change management and release management following the IETF internet standards process. The process of creating a standard under IETF is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience. Furthermore, The IETF welcomes the critical evaluation of protocols and has provided guidance for it. 

Standard process IETF: https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Protocol Vulnerabilities IETF: https://www.ietf.org/standards/rfcs/vulnerabilities/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68a60992-296f-4636-87c9-5980de2f791f .

camssa:d51c113b-45d0-49af-985f-b9c4c9cb636c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:d520e921-03fd-4a11-9d2d-36b8476122dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 most important role in ensuring the network interoperability by providing a solid foundation for organizational interoperability agreements by establishing a common language, framework and physical layer specifications, ensuring backward compatibility, and promoting global adoption.

IEEE 802.3-2022 Referenced in Smart Cities:
https://climate-change.ieee.org/news/ieee-802/

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d28f9fc-ebbc-4738-bc0b-eac15c3785b2 .

