camssa:d5311e84-20c2-4fa4-83b8-40cdef885fb5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI system does not inherently provide mechanisms for guaranteeing the authenticity and
authentication of roles.Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9af0d0c-99a6-4b2b-874b-a2bc6efd3ba3 .

camssa:d5395071-4788-45f1-b5d2-e73829a82f0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By using SHACL, organisations can create formal profiles and constraints that ensure data consistency and compatibility, which can be crucial for interoperability agreements.

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86c2eb1f-8e80-4762-8f21-c4e48845acad .

camssa:d53b567e-a3e8-4286-88d0-69c57954e2e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "By allowing the exchange of digital documents, PDF avoids to share non-digital documents and then helps to the reduction of administrative burden. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5642af5-7692-47b5-9669-ef4f0f883142 .

