camssa:d553045b-63f8-4cdd-aa8e-010ba7374e67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TSA is a TTP that creates time-stamp tokens in order to indicate that a datum existed at a particular point in time. In this way, TSP can contribute to improving secure loggins, as well as integrating with security protocols to improve confidenciality. Some of these mechanisms that can help guarantee the confidentiality of data are TLS or SASL.

TSP/TSA IETF reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161

TLS cloudfare reference:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/ssl/transport-layer-security-tls/

SASL gnu reference: 
https://www.gnu.org/software/gsasl/manual/gsasl.html#SASL-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c4aad72-9be0-4b28-b319-6818a4bc3629 .

camssa:d5547964-15db-4c59-8e4a-65b420c36f6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the availability interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f2e35dd-d52a-4c0a-88f3-d7712657e31d .

camssa:d557b117-9902-4dc3-9136-5f7fc9bc3e83 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/d69e4c94-af1e-4049-b83e-38336a8823dd"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:d558e9a7-8727-42ef-a40c-d3334f2180cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Advanced Message Queuing Protocol is only included in the Catalogue of the Member State of France. The Référentiel général d'interopérabilité (RGI) currently has AMQP "under observation", meaning that if the experiments prove conclusive, it will be included in a subsequent version of the General Interoperability Framework Status Explanation as "recommended".

Référentiel général d'interopérabilité (RGI) Reference:
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf

NIFO Factsheets:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcab9a20-0b87-4d2b-9ecc-412c0852b935 .

camssa:d55b2e81-8a47-4e1a-a04f-3406a257f258 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main purpose of the IPsec specification is to ensure data protection and offer security mechanisms. One of the features that can be enabled is the confidentiality of data. In this context, IPsec can enable mechanisms to guarantee restrictions who can access to information. In this sense, it allows functionalities such as encrypting IP packets and preventing eavesdropping on network traffic. Eavesdropping is a type of cyberattack that can result in financial loss, identity theft, or privacy breaches.

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html

IPsec security reference:  
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/ip-security-ipsec/

IPsec eavesdropping attack reference:
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/what-is-an-eavesdropping-attack/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64fcf454-2707-4289-a7d5-8679843dbebc .

camssa:d55bab94-152a-4d00-8651-c949c1e19ee5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is not a European Standard nor have been adopted as such within the EU. 

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a3fb294-a405-4e48-b504-d590a07bde7a .

