camssa:d573a881-3e00-46fb-9c3b-f172df0b383f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c9845e9-3dec-43dc-9767-f184ab79aa28 .

camssa:d57810d0-930b-4bcd-acaf-c7607c7f4d2e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"RDF has been selected within several initiatives at European level in order to provide open data and linked data to be used for Member States, citizens, and businesses.\r
\r
An example of RDF use is the European cross-border project ESCO (European Skills, Competences, Qualifications, and Occupations). The project uses Turtle extension of RDF in order to make available the project's data. At ESCO's webpage can be found the link to data resources and as well as information resources needed for the proper use of provided data. \r
\r
Additionally, RDF has been selected as one of the core elements on the euCASES project, a platform for linking legal documentation and offer it as Linked Open Data. \r
\r
euCASES website:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/esco/portal/escopedia/RDF\r
http://eucases.eu/start.html\r
\r
ESCO ontology:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/esco/lod/static/model.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d846bce-a7be-43f8-a5dd-64c0286ed353 .

camssa:d57980d3-06a4-4f05-aa69-d8fd3b80aa52 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:d57aa6eb-1c0c-47ff-a927-80b2a6d4ce09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is included in 3 national catalogues of recommended specifications.  They belong to Greece Malta and The Netherlands.  The National Interoperability Framework of the Netherlands is fully aligned with 3 out of the 3 sections according to the European Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO)  factsheets, while Greece is placed on the European average (2 out of 3) and Malta scores below average (1 out of 3).\r
\r
NIFO factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2021\r
\r
National Catalogue of the Netherlands:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/aanbevolen\r
\r
National Catalogue of Malta:\r
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243\r
\r
National Catalogue of Greece\r
http://www.e-gif.gov.gr/portal/pls/portal/docs/1/211041.PDF'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:364d1c4f-db08-4c5b-a524-fa794da98f96 .

camssa:d580e889-d30a-4809-bbc5-1283ce4b1d38 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d5859a4b-13e6-4b36-bd37-7950f6275310 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WS-BPEL is not included in any catalogue of standards at supra-national level. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da0fe3d5-a0fa-4ab3-999a-42ffdbba32c9 .

camssa:d585c367-6c98-4238-8ed1-6abd9b3641a2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:d58a9756-1ab8-4e02-af72-860c047ea477 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TIFF/IT was released in 1996 as a standard for the exchange of digital adverts. It became an ISO standard in 1998 as ISO 12639:1998, the specification had some modifications and the current version was published in 2004. The last review of TIFF/IT was in 2017 and it was confirmed to be the latest version. So it is clear that the specification is mature enough for develop of products and services.\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f80c649f-7b63-426b-92b7-0023f8a5e433 .

camssa:d58e05f4-6bc3-407c-b3f3-ad1a69df3893 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of Advanced Encryption Standard is not related to guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

Geeksforgeeks AES reference:
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/advanced-encryption-standard-aes/

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:decb957b-ede4-46e4-80e1-d184872e7a96 .

camssa:d59210d6-afd6-4bb2-9f8d-538b2384ae2d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f378f9c-ab9f-4e80-a539-f6a74d147d07 .

camssa:d592559a-6a9f-4dc3-ad3b-a29212bd4f89 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the CSIP does not explicitly focus on the secure exchange of data, its adherence to open standards, inclusion of administrative metadata, and alignment with best practices can indirectly support the secure exchange of data. Organizations implementing the CSIP should complement it with appropriate security measures, encryption, access controls, and compliance with data protection regulations to ensure secure data exchange.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d277cfad-b131-47d6-98d0-6fae04ac7af8 .

camssa:d594b206-9e3e-4ff5-8ea0-542e08ee2abb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d59b4343-6089-4a82-a4d8-1d00ac606364 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of ELI is to be a system to make legislation available online in a standardised format so that it can be accessed, exchanged and reused across borders. By allowing to make the data available amongst organisations, ELI Contributes to the development of eGovernment reducing the administrative burden. \r
\r
ELI reference:\r
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59b99fda-999a-472a-a500-a205c3c3a5d7 .

camssa:d59f0d23-8183-4b44-bb2f-1b6730a035da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WS-Security main function is to enforce security for messages as an extension of SOAP. So it can be considered that helps to process data."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ebd94b4c-2b1d-4113-82c4-96522ac8ff0b .

camssa:d5a0060b-aca8-498f-b89f-c56cca5b2b0c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d5a52c63-f30b-438d-818c-da349bc2e25d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After carrying out information retrieval, no document or study has been found assessing directly the HTML 4 in terms of efficiency or effectiveness. However, there is information that compares different versions of HTML (HTML4 and HTML5), and the main differences between them. From there, it can be inferred the effectivity and effectiveness of the usage of HTML4. \r
\r
HMTL5 vs HTML4: \r
https://www.educba.com/html5-vs-html4/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:79ec5fea-6234-4d6d-8826-9f6471f8a940 .

camssa:d5a53440-9ef6-408a-ac17-fafb5586ecb7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02557e2b-a774-45bf-8daf-78774e5c0c1e .

