camssa:d5d07b3c-95c9-425d-ac6e-6ae6a45be067 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTP is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57afc582-9b9c-49ac-a6a0-ab3d4dbc6e00 .

camssa:d5d4cdfa-fedf-4727-b804-1bb3e6ab71a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification guarantees the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions (issuer and holder) with a verifier, a role where an entity performs by receiving one or more verifiable credentials, optionally inside a verifiable presentation for processing. This specification describes mechanisms for ensuring the authenticity of Verifiable Credentials and similar types of constrained digital documents using cryptography, especially through the use of digital signatures and related mathematical proofs.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials Data Integrity:\r
 https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-integrity/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8318c24e-9efd-4de6-9c12-198e9e5e684b .

camssa:d5d7dff3-feb3-49d3-9fd8-59a16739f53e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specifications is to define technical interoperability aspects. Therefore, eDelivery is used for business modelling processes. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:197db3e7-f235-463e-95a3-09f9150baa96 .

camssa:d5dde6e3-3c4b-41a8-a7c5-6d057b15e32d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d5de361c-6571-4a3e-85be-c090c6dca876 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'YAML can facilitate the modeling of business processes by providing a readable and structured format for defining workflows, configurations, and data exchanges. Its flexibility and compatibility with tools like BPMN (Business Process Model and Notation) and workflow automation platforms (e.g., Ansible, Kubernetes) make it useful for documenting and automating business processes efficiently.

YAML specification:
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/

BPML generator for YAML:
https://www.giancarlomangiagli.it/en/BPMNator_BPMN_generator_from_YAML.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c452a9e1-d79c-49f2-b6bb-75eb6fb60b34 .

camssa:d5e2fbfe-aef7-4761-9919-bcd34fd8f322 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv6 is included in 7 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Austria, Croatia, France, Germany, Netherlands, Norway, and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Germany and Austria are fully aligned with at least 3 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Nonetheless, countries like Sweden do not get a high performance, being aligned with 3 out of 5.

National catalogue of Austria:
https://neu.ref.wien.gv.at/at.gv.wien.ref-live/ag-ii-austrian-intero.-framework

National catalogue of Germany: 
https://www.cio.bund.de/Web/DE/Architekturen-und-Standards/SAGA/SAGA%205-aktuelle%20Version/saga_5_aktuelle_version_node.html 

National catalogue of sweden:
https://www.avropa.se/globalassets/dokument/open-it-standards.pdf?_t_id=1B2M2Y8AsgTpgAmY7PhCfg%3d%3d&_t_q=standards&_t_tags=language%3asv%2csiteid%3a95d515a5-23ca-47bf-87a9-

NIFO factsheets:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d913decd-1aae-4aee-a5b6-b33426bc2af7 .

camssa:d5e4cc1e-3ede-4fb8-a025-048a07707103 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "Nowadays, JSON is not included in any supra-national catalogue of standards. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d27e036-7aed-4563-86ac-35ed061b71c0 .

