        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d63a420c-15b3-4b62-bd5f-6a65fee54bb3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is implemented in a wide variety of business domains and fields.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.htmll
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4125df51-923a-4569-8408-a50dd552447f .

camssa:d63ac51f-9123-4ded-ae60-ed21701b8c6f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI specification promotes data portability in European public services by encouraging technological
neutrality and providing clear recommendations. It supports the transferability of data among different
systems to avoid lock-in and facilitate the free movement of data. Legal initiatives like the European Directive
on patients’ rights and the NIS Directive, and frameworks like ISA², further enhance these capabilities.

ELI Technological Neutrality and Data portability reference:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/solution/eif-toolbox
/underlying-principle-5-technological-neutrality-and-data-portability

ISA2 Framework reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=COM%3A2017%3A134%3AFIN

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:214d6e5f-9f29-4d05-94e8-2a693477473a .

camssa:d63bcaec-8346-478b-8ea2-93ed18df0a51 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d64016ae-e315-4b50-bd5d-50657e54b78f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:d642ff02-f169-430d-a0bc-142aa5f2c187 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Following the completion of the research into conformity tests and certifications, a tool has been identified 
that enables the testing of implementations. The "Maxwell Pro's TCP/IP Test Suite" automatically identifies bugs in IPv4 and IPv6 implementations so developers can fix issues prior to release preventing product failures.
Moreover, there are existing free online documents that will help you validate IPv6 specification when it is implemented.

Maxwell Pro's TCP/IP Test Suite:
https://www.iwl.com/protocol-testing/ip

Document "The next generation Internet protocol and its test" for testing IPv6:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/936305

Document "IPv6 Conformance Testing: Theory and Practice" for testing IPv6:
https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/1116164.1116526'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31d5c9a4-bd7c-49aa-851f-09ba03df2bb5 .

camssa:d64cdf6d-cd36-4880-8ddd-3bc1fcc43396 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d64ee48a-3a77-4c60-96a9-7d6e8e7746fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, the second star corresponds to the availability of data as structured data. WAI-ARIA is a document-level markup language, therefore it structures data as any other mark-up languages (e.g. HTTP or XML). \r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/	'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c97f3cf-221e-48ed-8d4c-6ee97781941c .

camssa:d655b319-9846-4c9c-acc8-394b1e0c054e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has a namespace which focus is to know information about who access the resource or an indication of its security status, the namespace may include information regarding access or restrictions based on privacy, security or other policies. The specification ensures and enables the secure processing of data.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ \r
\r
DCMI Access Rights:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/terms/accessRights/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71b23362-2087-4a30-840d-f9dfaa2159b7 .

camssa:d6593708-23c7-4bfb-b870-47cfb9c0e76d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to the publication of public data as Open Data. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification. 

DIDs specification:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7db8abe-ae54-4ec5-87fa-b3a49a061e7a .

camssa:d6597f91-606f-495c-ad95-eb69a0cf5a36 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There are no evidences of existing studies or documentation assessing the standard or specification in terms of effectiveness and efficiency to justify the criterion. Note that SHACL is th first W3C standard mechanism for defining data constraints. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76173edc-e7b4-4f82-8a84-7f68a587e215 .

camssa:d65e23a4-f873-42ab-9f3c-efb39c77693d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e370a4af17e89cbb70bb5079082a1e21cdee85435c8fc30b12a8987f18db367f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:d666805c-15b2-40bd-95fc-a8b40f4cb5c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ODF is already associated to an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, ODF can define the interoperability aspects of the "Representation" ABB from the EIRA Semantic view. \r
 \r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/release/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96d3ab11-08c6-4d23-8eb3-6492874ea4ca .

camssa:d666d7da-5028-499d-9f9b-5820a4ea10f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA allows customisation but authoring processes might be difficult to execute; hence the creation of related specifications based on other host languages (see TOSCA reference, TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML Objective section). Moreover, there is an attempt within the TOSCA TC to create a core TOSCA specification compatible with a variety of deployment use cases that would minimise the specification dependence on hosting technologies (see TOSCA Draft Version 2.0 reference, section 1.2).\r
\r
TOSCA reference, Cloud Service Archive (CSAR) reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969474\r
\r
TOSCA reference, TOSCA Simple Profile in YAML Objective section:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html#_Toc26969412\r
\r
TOSCA Draft Version 2.0 reference, section 1.2:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA/v2.0/csd03/TOSCA-v2.0-csd03.html#_Toc56506175'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0051abd4-d060-449b-85a4-f48d992d371a .

camssa:d668d7f7-c4e8-43c3-931d-a222640f0f47 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
