camssa:d671899a-2a49-44e9-9535-cb11c90b8e51 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPsec allows the exchange of data between systems and is compatible with both versions of the Internet Protocol, IPv4 and IPv6. Therefore it prevents the  storage of data in silos that are incompatible with one another. \r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4301 """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c64dde32-75ec-415c-baec-8e2bccd32082 .

camssa:d67bfb54-5381-4121-9878-6c716e16fccd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:d67f4a7f-81f4-4144-aa49-375de2199c33 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox is a European resource created by the Commission where privacy is defined through the implementation of privacy policies such as the GDPR. In this sense, the Tool 28 covers this element extensively.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52003280-283e-462c-81cd-ca82f3c502e4 .

camssa:d68267c1-9f95-4d33-b7e3-01aa162e55a4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d686e195-a047-4f0f-8ff5-29cecf982f5b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification was developed in 2012 by an Action of ISA2. In 2013, it was standardised by W3C. This fact demonstrates that the specification has overcome the initial problems. On 23 May 2012, the Coordination Group of the Interoperability Solutions for European Public Administrations (ISA) Programme renamed the specification to Core Business Vocabulary and it has been added to e-Government Core Vocabularies. So the specifications can be considered mature for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
RegOrg W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/\r
\r
RegOrg Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/registered-organization-vocabulary/about\r
\r
Core Business Vocabulary reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-business-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6380ed29-5377-42e8-b938-a16213c6d8f1 .

camssa:d68817e3-fd6e-4c33-a2f8-76830d79454a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being a Core Vocabulary for data privacy, an important aspect of DPV design is its support for customisation to meet the needs of individual organizations while maintaining complete interoperability within the standard framework. The aim of DPV is therefore to provide an upper-level abstract taxonomy of categories of legal bases that can be customised and applied as needed.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b9344db-70f4-4e4b-97ba-d4376ad7da10 .

camssa:d688e518-b89e-4a9c-a796-24d50cc28cc0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org relies on more than one development community, mainly the Community Group and the Steering Group (see Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section). All information relating to this specification can be found in the schema.org homepage (see Schema.org reference, Releases section), as well as in relevant platforms supported by W3C (e.g., Mailing list and Github). See also the Github Wiki section to engage with other schema.org external communities (e.g., Stackoverflow).\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Releases section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/releases.html\r
\r
W3 community reference, Mailing List:\r
https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-vocabs/\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github reference:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github, Wiki section:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/wiki\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d2248ac-6281-4723-8091-ecf6f8ff34b7 .

camssa:d68a091d-7d44-4067-b831-f1c73d15d653 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:d68ae034-2786-4b5c-b6df-ac32dcd859ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA is already associated with an EIRA ABB in the EIRA Library Of Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, the specificaiton can define the interoperability aspects of the Orchestration Component and Orchestration Service ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffa3f59d-6d9f-4c23-bf65-39f0f44186f3 .

camssa:d690499b-ee0f-4781-8e56-263539207f52 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox can be used and applied independently from other standards, or software requirements. Therefore, Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox establishes guidelines and principles, ensuring applicability across all platforms.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2fdf1943-ba0c-4e73-bf9f-e513154722e8 .

