camssa:d6993508-355d-4209-b25b-92daef38a6ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA specification itself does not provide an access control mechanism. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ffad8cc-e2f2-481a-bb9f-6bf4ad4bae55 .

camssa:d69a2358-7995-4b36-9f52-4c2281282265 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:d69def20-c794-4c78-af07-9f4c463d0f56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification does not address data integrity protections or provide mechanisms to prevent unauthorised data alterations. Its scope is solely to document metadata regarding public code projects, and it does not include features or protocols to support data integrity. Consequently, it does not align with the data integrity requirements referenced in EIF Recommendation 15.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ee1742f-43af-4e68-b4a6-a15892113a18 .

camssa:d6a1587a-37ce-4335-87c1-340ff1350b6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of SMTP is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable specification. \r
\r
SMTP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5321"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa5e25db-e2ad-4493-8496-531b7720d2d0 .

camssa:d6a17182-3fd3-4565-b8c7-f5b6c720ea5b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 was developed by the ISO/IEC joint technical committee JTC 1. The access to JTC 1\r
working area is restricted, and individuals or companies are not eligible as members of ISO. ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is\r
interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards\r
body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard.\r
ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a\r
standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is\r
returned to TC/SC to be further studied.\r
\r
The ISO standardization process:\r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html\r
\r
ISO membership reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/get-involved.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca729ef7-aba5-4693-9004-f7b15b3d23b4 .

camssa:d6a2a9ab-a4d3-400a-b893-089e37b833bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
