camssa:d7774ac4-7829-443b-b28e-4403c5d2f9a4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The application of the once-only principle in all EU Member States public administrations aims at reducing the administrative burden. \r
\r
XACML addresses and facilitates interoperability between public administrations, cross-border services, and impacts positively the development of eGovernment. This is because it has been designed to evaluate and control access by ensuring the compliance of security policies. \r
\r
Also, the project SEMIRAMIS, uses this specification to ensure secure channels for the exchange and reuse of information.\r
\r
XACML OASIS reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/errata01/xacml-3.0-core-spec-errata01.html\r
\r
SEMIRAMIS project: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:193ee0d3-03bc-46cf-9f37-3eba809f647a .

camssa:d77a4b9d-0d3b-4c6c-9a3d-f3b7ec8e33dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAML 2.0 primarily focuses on the authentication and authorization aspects of user data exchange, rather than data protection per se. There are several features and best practices within the SAML specification can be leveraged to enhance the protection of personal data, especially when used by Public Administrations or other entities. \r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e46fe951-8d0e-4b7c-a3c0-bbefd30daae3 .

