camssa:d787ac42-9851-4548-9368-66f3f883d4e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The XFDL specification helps protect information against unauthorised changes through its digital signature feature. When a form is signed, the digital signature ensures the authenticity and integrity of the data. In addition, the use of encryption in the signature's mimedata option further secures the data, ensuring that the original information remains intact. This approach is in line with the XML Signature Syntax and Processing specification, which defines how digital signatures are applied to XML documents, guaranteeing the data’s integrity and verifying the signer’s identity.

XML Signature Syntax and Processing reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core1/

XFDL security reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-XFDL#button\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7828b0f2-f3df-44f1-8c48-79a6a88fd9e7 .

camssa:d78c6c91-77f9-40d8-947c-af00e6b6165b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1cd71a7b6d54631ba58cc8b0655a443d696f49ec74a0f4cccc871de7789d6a60 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:d7942e56-db36-4207-96a9-c2f25d26cf94 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is a widely used de-facto standard. It was launched for the first time in 1998 by engineers from Microsoft. Other companies with a wide market share are contributed to the development of the specification. Additionally, SOAP is developed and maintained by W3C and its working group. Thus, it is sufficiently mature for the development of products and services.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d906ccfe-ed86-41bd-aee9-b51c5023132e .

camssa:d795ec3a-f5eb-4554-85f0-61d643c91175 a cav:Score,
