camssa:d7eec938-5d83-43a2-8a45-3c6eeb90d4e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"There exist some studies assessing digital solutions' efficiency that are based on iCalendar; however, most of them are restricted to learning environments. One of these assessments evaluates how Google calendar contributes to an efficient reservation of a learning room.\r
\r
Google calendar in learning environments - Design and Implementation of a Study Room Reservation System: Lessons from a pilot program using Google Calendar:\r
https://research.library.fordham.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1002&context=lib_staffpubs\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3259575a-64f9-4064-9f75-df76d4969e29 .

camssa:d7f1a76a-ede0-4ef5-828b-d0cc42455631 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has four defined interoperability levels that serve as guidelines for determining the level of interoperability, having a defined level means that the previous levels to the one mentioned are included, so it is a level 3 conforming specification it automatically conforms level 1 and 2.\r
The intention is to provide a "ladder of interoperability", specifying the choices, costs, and benefits involved in designing applications for increased levels interoperability. \r
\r
DCMI Interoperability Levels:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/interoperability-levels/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:631735e2-4e67-4e84-a238-c8bb30211dc5 .

