camssa:d874d994-165f-432c-addb-424c7f743525 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification was launched in 1999 jointly by OASIS and the United Nations Centre for Trade Facilitation and Electronic Business (United Nations/ECE agency CEFACT), and was known as the Global XML Framework for Electronic Business. ebXML v1.0 was published in 2001, ebXML v2.0 in 2002 under the ebXML RegRep TC, and approved as ISO 15000-2 and ISO 15000-3 in 2004. A major release (ebXML v3.0) appeared in 2005, including the documents ebXML Registry Information Model (RIM) v3.0 and ebXML Registry Services and Protocols (RS) v3.0 (respectively, Part 1 and Part 2). Finally, the latest version (ebXML v4.0) was published in 2012. \r
\r
OASIS ebXML Registry TC reference, Announcements section:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep#announcements\r
\r
ebxml.xml.org reference:\r
http://ebxml.xml.org/milestones'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4aa6123-e0ea-4000-a37f-7c3cccb1163c .

camssa:d876162b-db85-4ae7-a192-775bbc471aaf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SFIA is not related to facilitating the publication of open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a292c0c-2263-4c94-9a6f-89a526d97e85 .

