camssa:d8832fd0-0ef9-48e0-aed5-731f6c20d7d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, HTTP has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a582dea0-2d07-42a8-829f-c838a0a4955a .

camssa:d8937b88-7aac-4ecc-bba8-7fc2f9caed1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Registered Organization Vocabulary's usability extends beyond business domains to include any organisation that gains legal entity status through a formal registration process. As a profile of the W3C Organization Ontology, the Registered Organization Vocabulary inherits the ontology’s agnostic nature, enabling flexible and interoperable representation of registered organisations while maintaining alignment with broader organisational modelling frameworks.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

W3C Organization Ontology reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15c2997c-7e64-4663-b628-031f3db457a2 .

camssa:d89b9c71-cbd1-47e0-9e17-c049d5ee9d80 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d89c5200-f711-436d-8529-e9f5298d2331 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Being a standard protocol for mantaining and accessing directory services, LDAP can be used across business domains as long as they require the storage and management of user information.

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df9f1fc2-a52e-49dc-b186-cfb34ab03513 .

camssa:d8a395d9-8675-4b0b-8be7-06aeff19af21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Yes, the specification does encourage the creation of communities along with the sharing of their data on European platforms.          \r
                                                                                                                                                                                       Use case Integration Platform for Digital Transformation in Web Methods: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/joinup/discussion/integration-platform-digital-transformation-web-methods'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0cd83435-2feb-45dc-b73f-1fcc28572d9d .

camssa:d8ae5e96-8fa5-40e7-9a30-d5f8610a921a a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "None"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:d8bd4c1a-7e3a-4e01-befb-85bf011fba45 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Given the nature of all the core vocabularies developed by the UE domain, technology agnosticism is a key feature, ensuring that the specification remains adaptable and applicable across various technological platforms and environments. Therefore, the specification is technology agnostic.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f591aed-80c3-46a1-aecc-cb0485100bbc .

camssa:d8bf59f4-12f2-47c0-8e4a-05ef7b18e436 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main purpose of the DPV is to model the legal aspects of data portability, in order to link them with more technical aspects of electronic data echange.  DPV suggests mechanisms for the data to be protected, and data transfers in contexts where cross-border exchange is needed.\r
\r
DPV specification: \r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:716652e8-5e3d-497e-9da1-9442333a9e0f .

camssa:d8c10844-c824-4932-b317-dc518690bdc8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """All the IETF specifications are made available free of charge to the general public via the website. IETF drafts are published publicly discussions take place online in archived mailing lists. Moreover, the IETF Datatracker is the day-to-day front-end to the IETF database for people who work on IETF standards. It contains data about the documents, working groups, meetings, agendas, minutes, presentations, and more, of the IETF.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's Internet-Drafts directory. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/\r
\r
http://www.ietf.org/id-info/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:029c03ba-e004-4662-8921-a05982ec384b .

camssa:d8c8cca7-64bb-49f3-baec-8ae85144bd24 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While DQV may not comprehensively cover administrative procedures, rules data, and services on its own, it can be integrated with service descriptions or metadata schemas to provide additional context about the quality of services. It can complement existing service description frameworks by incorporating data quality aspects. This integration enhances the overall understanding of services and their reliance on quality data.

Data Quality Vocabulary: 
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dqv/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f77ee43-99c1-4910-91e1-ca6a8d3becdc .

camssa:d8c9f2d4-4cce-4a67-943e-1b3f763ca181 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any assessment addressing the efficiency of the TGF specification.\r
\r
TGF specification:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/tgf/TGF/v2.0/cs01/TGF-v2.0-cs01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0649a8a-a78c-4ed0-b31d-7a4a6c5c5179 .

camssa:d8ce1f85-594b-470d-b8d9-c7efe34aec91 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d8d2b29c-d94c-42b8-9fd3-3fda99404de1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consists in a 6-steps process where everyone who is interested can participate. However, if you want to participate, you have to contact your national standards body and you have to be approved for joining the Technical committee (TC) who will develop the standard. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said. For the approval of a standard the two-thirds majority of P-members of TC is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC to be further studied. \r
\r
The ISO standardization process:\r
https://www.iso.org/stages-and-resources-for-standards-development.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0fa9309-4067-446a-bdcd-2adb3f5e8c4c .

camssa:d8d56071-8202-40bb-8b35-769d23b1468d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 639-2 was published in 1998. And this specification is reviewed every 5 years, last review was in 2021. \r
\r
ISO 639-2 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/4767.html\r
\r
The Library of Congress Network Development & MARC 21 reference, change and release management:\r
https://www.loc.gov/marc/languages/languagechg.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:379cac8d-5173-4215-9631-20deec7fd126 .

camssa:d8d5d19b-7c67-42a2-a7fb-a62a7a264bbd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS XACML Specification Technical Committee in charge of the development of XACML, operates under RF on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free and (F)RAND basis.

OASIS Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) Policy:
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b190c31-b968-4112-8a48-38e34e5235f0 .

camssa:d8d8a5f6-c326-46a1-96df-7af4863120ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS allows public administration to share and exchange information with others, so it helps with the visibility of data. However, FTPS is a protocol only intended to exchange the data, it doesn't help to comprehend it.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0cf45f8d-3f43-4551-a80e-c6b4db8556ad .

camssa:d8d8ea61-7628-40e7-82d4-5e6b8bd58d89 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "20" .

