    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d914d5d3-224a-428b-91c8-df083bb50ed9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) itself does not directly simplify the delivery of European public services. However, it can impact positively on the delivery of European public services as it improves security and privacy measures and facilitates interoperability between systems, which can be useful when establishing a reliable infrastructure.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f9d5145-859d-422e-8d29-54440c1d941f .

camssa:d914fca1-7a86-41b8-a82d-4a24ef906821 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows user to access and maintain distributed directories information over the Internet, which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. By ensuring the access to different directory services, while managing user identities, and implementing access control mechanisms, it fosters the implementation of digital services, supporting the principle of digital-first. 

LDAP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:578303a1-233a-41b9-a5c0-16f93fa1c620 .

camssa:d91705fb-0403-4950-a5fa-b5a380a91185 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification enables a secure exchange of data through security layers like TLS and SASL are employed to ensure authenticated and encrypted transport, which can be combined for enhanced security.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:46d6a22d-59e1-4523-899a-e0d2030ace49 .

camssa:d9171574-facc-4229-a602-37ae15382339 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The specification can be used independently from specific operating systems and hardware platforms."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:037d9711-0d77-4b1d-aac4-5c01bf4e6fd5 .

camssa:d9176962-4a34-4444-b51a-adac4436e26d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:d91cb968-0baf-4e7e-b606-cd5e3fc10abf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI IPR Policy which is part of the ETSI directives seeks to reduce the risk that our standards-making efforts might be wasted if SEPs are unavailable under Fair, Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory (FRAND) terms and conditions.
The main objective of the ETSI IPR Policy is to balance the rights and interests of IPR holders to be fairly and adequately rewarded for the use of their SEPs in the implementation of ETSI standards and the need for implementers to get access to the technology defined in ETSI standards under FRAND terms and conditions.

ETSI’s intellectual property rights policy:
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:010aabf8-7993-4541-801e-dfe36bca30a7 .

camssa:d91e04a7-82b7-42c4-943c-abd2b0f38a01 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "DCAT is not included in any supra-national catalogue of specifications or standards. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4a927e0-463c-40f5-a2f1-1b36a94b664b .

camssa:d92120b6-1c91-4dfe-836b-e5a23c623c68 a cav:Score,
