    cav:value "60" .

camssa:d9699443-a1c5-413f-8c9a-85d2bedf537d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox provides specific and operational guidance to all the stakeholders implicated in developing legal framework instruments that will be used to create EU services delivery channels.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

Better Regulation Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/document/download/9c8d2189-8abd-4f29-84e9-abc843cc68e0_en?filename=BR%20toolbox%20-%20Jul%202023%20-%20FINAL.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef3132c3-ff6e-47c4-b182-1a13c292f737 .

camssa:d96b5911-6e5d-4b26-851a-1feb3fda7835 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IndexedDB specification is used in the Health360 national project, a framework designed as an integrated tool for managing and analysing data related to neuromuscular disorders. In this context, IndexedDB is utilised for data caching, making it easier to access. Additionally, this functionality can be combined with other specifications to secure cached data.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6212a030-b67a-4256-b6d7-acc924f3c70d .

camssa:d96bf6a4-6509-41f5-b65d-213c8bb8d489 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:d96fdb21-ee87-4b28-8a1b-f60ed30fb092 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary specification introduces some aspects that can contribute to data portability. In this context, for conformance with the Core Location Vocabulary, it is not mandatory that this happens in a RDF serialisation, but the exchanged format should be unambiguously transformable into RDF.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:06e42b6c-5933-426a-929f-510852a94273 .

camssa:d97bfff2-09f6-4601-8950-150642b8dd23 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF is included in 13 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Croatia, Cyprus, Denmark, France, Germany, Greece, Ireland, Malta, The Netherlands, Slovenia, Slovakia, Spain, and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Spain and The Netherlands is fully aligned with at least  2 out of  3 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c588446a-e979-4492-bcbc-d05b757a8e16 .

camssa:d9833c08-78a0-42ce-b60d-490122c00577 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The European Union Agency For Network And Information Security includes within a set of guidelines for implementing qualified electronic time stamps. That means that the specification, as part of this set of guidelines, is recommended when handling Timestamps.

ENISA Security guidelines on the appropriate use of qualified electronic time stamps: 
https://security.stackexchange.com/questions/173652/how-to-timestamp-a-document-without-electronic-signature-under-eidas '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62a3a23e-067c-4d3c-b13c-1c6d4ca0ef19 .

camssa:d983649b-48fd-4af6-80f1-baa810eec29c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of RDF does not hamper the interoperability of systems as it was developed to improve the interrelationship between systems easing the information retrieval and data reuse. The common framework that establishes RDF allows using common parsers and exchange information between different applications avoiding interoperability hampering. The different RDF serialisation specifications help on this purpose.\r
Additionally, the flexibility of RDF allows the creation of new vocabularies when users need/want to add new concepts without hampering interoperability.  """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a9f13b3d-aed6-4d70-a798-abd8bca28ed1 .

camssa:d986e881-627c-44c4-ba92-83623a37956c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "80" .

