camssa:da79c335-4b30-4429-9767-a896ca122541 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPv4 specification is mentioned in the "Alternative Bearers for Rail" project. The Shift2Rail initiative has developed a new Adaptable Communication System (ACS) to overcome shortcomings in current European rail control applications. In the project, IPv4 is analised, and some strategies for allowing the IPv4 and IPv6 interworking are proposed.

"Alternative Bearers for Rail" project: 
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101014517'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bff8c17-09c4-4ab8-8da4-9658b7821223 .

camssa:da834eb7-7d6a-4f86-9937-e22152726111 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There is no national or European platform with the specification CAdES (ISO 14533-1:2014) available for free. However, there are some free documents in Joinup that covers CAdES digital signatures - Testing Conformance and Interoperability.\r
\r
CAdES Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/etsi-tr-119-124-series-electronic-signatures-and-infrastructures-esi-cades-digital-signatures"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:584da591-faf1-40dd-b902-026c3bfca148 .

