camssa:dad696ee-17de-453e-8f29-d9fe053f3c9b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are already studies and documentation assessing the specification in terms of effectiveness and efficiency. The topics are different, for instance, there is a study assessing the capabilities of XML Schema for the defense against Signature Wrapped Attacks. \r
Another field of documentation is the XML Schema clustering, and its effectiveness for the improvement of user results.\r
See: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/252053794_On_the_effectiveness_of_XML_Schema_validation_for_countering_XML_Signature_Wrapping_attacks\r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/254858700_XML_schema_matching_balancing_efficiency_and_effectiveness_by_means_of_clustering"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a228914f-434e-40c7-8c17-ddca6db1df89 .

camssa:dad82785-fe57-414f-8431-895a25469cd9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The Working Group in charge of developing the specification initially provides a light-weight maintenance plan . However, it does not consist in a process for a long-term maintenance of the specification. For instance, no development or review process are described, and no versioning policy is specified."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98edb416-be83-4804-a87f-ab1695969cdf .

camssa:dadae3dd-4954-4129-8d95-f149af6002a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Library of Congress is de facto national library of the United States, and altogether with the ISO ensures the maintenance of this specification. However, ISO 639-2 does not encourage the creation of communities nor promotes the sharing of data and results in any national platform.\r
\r
The Library of Congress reference: \r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d6954078-1cd6-4b5e-bc61-cfeb6d6cf3f7 .

camssa:dadb19ae-3b70-486e-b8f7-e5f0c574cbd2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:dadb4939-9651-4ee2-8308-88271b4aeda7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ISO 3166-1 consists of a collection of codes for the names of countries, dependent territories and special areas of geographical interest. Although this collection can be mapped against this same collection to test the specification's implementation conformance, the specification does not publicly provide conformance testing requirements (see ISO 3166-1 reference, official preview documentation); the user may opt for their own techniques or for third-party software conformance services.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference, official preview documentation:\r
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:3166:-1:ed-4:v1:en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e6bfb78f-9a80-4e95-8e48-ab4222ff21c3 .

camssa:dadec47d-be6f-48f9-8392-02a2ae1c126e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:dae0ccde-2492-4527-8919-dc171093fd7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating an Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all of the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:\r
\r
- technical excellence\r
\r
- prior implementation and testing;\r
\r
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;\r
\r
- openness and fairness; and \r
\r
- timeliness\r
\r
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.\r
\r
See:https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95aa91a7-2654-4a20-b7ca-87c0569ea07f .

camssa:dae2e67d-3077-42b8-9861-7fe27046e6c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EN 303 645 specification facilitates business modeling, as the specification can be deployed into any architecture for consumer IoT in a home environment. The evidence for this is that consumer IoT devices are collections of hardware and software components, with physical or network interfaces, typically connected to online or local services.\r
\r
EN 303 645 reference, Annex A Basic concepts and models:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4b2c533-826e-4808-ac67-46d768dd70dc .

camssa:dae90ef7-36c3-4b43-bfd1-0323b91a2848 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:daf43235-a330-43ba-98ee-94a03e2f1638 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:daf885ec-b733-4247-814c-0bce26d6f4e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the time of elaborating this assessment, TLS 1.2 does not foster the creation of innovative solutions. In 2018 the creation of TLS 1.3 updated and improved the older version. So the focus of creating innovative solution is focused on the  latter."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7adcdb61-736f-490f-8a9c-c5a0fd9edaca .

camssa:dafc9209-881f-452b-a6ab-7cddd161de7c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME (Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions) itself does not enable the implementation of features to guarantee data accuracy. Data accuracy may be addressed at the application or system level through, validation, and quality assurance practices.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
S/MIME specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7832030c-9672-42f2-b165-7f4eaa1506e0 .

camssa:dafef90f-ecce-437e-afe2-d98a982c789b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f154e298-b9b3-4f9b-aaa9-7846fd0fadf3 .

camssa:db0536bc-b8d2-45cf-9e21-38ee0514e046 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards.\r
\r
\r
ETSI standard making:\r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31caea36-bc74-4ff8-9881-d2fb51d4b7ea .

camssa:db144ade-fd69-48d6-8119-a988c0d2ed0b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-02333ef99fbcb4f101a106bcf97c9559888756b085b1729b7c2ac9626dc4bc63 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:db18f414-629d-4088-bab8-e4449a2c2721 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalRuleML extends RuleML and provides a framework that can help to reduce the gap between semantics, natural language and text description. In this sense, the specification can help to create and model constitutive rules, technical rules, and prescriptive rules enhancing the data exchange of legal resources such as documents defining property aspects, contracts and others. Providing a common framework for this purpose fosters the trustworthy data exchange between administration and stakeholders.\r
\r
LegalRuleML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/legalruleml-core-spec/v1.0/legalruleml-core-spec-v1.0.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bd7e0445-a79e-4ce0-9518-999d5caf949c .

camssa:db1a8310-709a-4627-abd3-f7d2ccb840be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SFIA is intended to serve as a device to represent skills and competences of any ICT professional workforce. There is no possibility of partial implementation of the specification, as SFIA has a single purpose.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8f520b9-60d6-4e25-8df6-40c74a385737 .

camssa:db1afa4d-c19e-4a34-93cb-2fa19f63879a a cav:Score,
