camssa:dcabeea7-83b7-4109-8c61-f0d75953540d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Applications implemented based on OpenAPI interface files can automatically generate documentation of methods, parameters and models. This helps keep the documentation, client libraries, and source code in sync, thus, enabling data portability between systems.  \r
\r
OAS specification:\r
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification\r
\r
OAS in Github:\r
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1421ace-ec3b-4423-8fd3-af88f14412e9 .

camssa:dcac019b-8ac4-445a-adf4-089149f40ecb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While OpenTelemetry is not directly related to providing an access control mechanism, there are some provisions regarding access control mechanisms.  The Collector supports running as a custom user and should not be run as a root/admin user. In fact, for the majority of use-cases, the Collector should not require privileged access to function. If for some reason access requirements are needed, component developers must document the requirements and why they are placed.

OTel Security Best Practices: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/blob/main/docs/security-best-practices.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c054e474-73be-41ab-aad0-9adfaeb053d5 .

camssa:dcac3013-c2ff-4b46-bc34-198fb3fbdc63 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is a specification developed by the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C), which is an international standards organization responsible for many web-related standards. While WSDL itself is not a European Standard, its usage may be referenced or recommended in European initiatives and frameworks, such as the European Interoperability Framework (EIF), which provides guidelines for achieving interoperability among European public services.\r
\r
European Interoperability Framework:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/european-interoperability-framework-detail'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a60cbecb-e92b-454b-a9fd-2be1c41bc12a .

camssa:dcaff257-8d18-41c9-a06b-e1f2892cf096 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:dcb38bc0-c447-4376-b5fc-84ec8000311d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS has been found to be used in the Research  Infrastructure for Science and Innovation Policy Studies (named as RISIS) Where OpenAPI takes part in a project aiming to automatize query-centric APIs for accessing to Linked Data.  \r
\r
Automatic Query-centric API for Routine Access to Linked Data:\r
https://iswc2017.semanticweb.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/MainProceedings/430.pdf\r
\r
RISIS webpage:\r
https://www.risis2.eu/about/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a43a14de-8623-48df-b818-ba0787ecc35f .

camssa:dcb8684a-0441-4cda-bd80-2497e252105c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"In accordance with Common Patent Policy for ITU-T/ITU-R/ISO/IEC the ISO 3166-1 is licensed under royalty-free basis. Although there are terms included that allow patent holder to apply specific costs. It is defined in IPR disclosures that can be found at ISO's webpage. \r
\r
ISO patents:\r
https://www.iso.org/iso-standards-and-patents.html \r
\r
ISO standards and patents IPR database:\r
http://isotc.iso.org/livelink/livelink/13622347/Patents_database.xls?func=doc.Fetch&nodeId=13622347 \""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad049027-02e9-4dc1-8746-265c35466756 .

camssa:dcba9afb-ce99-4f0c-88f8-405f44d03da1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This Core Vocabulary was developed in 2014 and has good acceptance in the European Union. The CPSV-AP is already being used by public administrations in Belgium, Italy, Finland and Estonia to create a cross-border federated catalogue of public services. Moreover, it is the basis of the European Catalogue of Services \r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile\r
\r
CPSV-AP used in EU:\r
https://www.ceps.eu/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/NO0119341ENN.en_.pdf\r
\r
Catalogue of Services:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/catalogue-services-helping-eu-countries-catalogue-and-describe-public-services_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:20aa6153-505b-402b-a30c-2f25344d941a .

camssa:dcc19933-b2a6-4991-81c5-b8af6bf98d76 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT has been developed to facilitate the publication of linked open data by the W3C Government Linked Data Working Group.The specification is an RDF vocabulary for representing data catalogues that allows data owners to provide metadata about the datasets they publish. By describing catalogues, datasets and resources, a publisher makes them easily searchable and discoverable.\r
\r
In fact, DCAT is used for the publication of datasets in linked open data portals at European scale (European Data Portal).\r
\r
DCAT reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/         \r
\r
DCAT-AP & European Data Portals reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9338353-4e82-40ca-b00b-f63397f15248 .

camssa:dcc47d22-5c37-470c-893a-e608816f6997 a cav:Score,
