camssa:dcf74816-fce8-43ee-921d-0277d26209e3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 612 specifies a format and mechanisms for establishing, locating, accessing and authenticating a \r
trusted list which makes available trust service status information so that interested parties may determine the status of a listed trust service at a given time as well as enabling data portability between systems/applications. It defines the format and semantics of a TL as well as the mechanisms for accessing TLs. It also provides guides for locating and authenticating TLs.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 612 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a12441e-2a79-4aa6-8260-359e60248b58 .

camssa:dcf8b3d9-4d9e-48ce-afd1-72f2a0bb7bd4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:dd01c098-18bb-47ac-a790-2f20c61934a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The RDA website also collects expressions of interest from potential adopters via “Become an RDA Adopter” section  and encourages adopters to submit “Adoption Stories” . RDA has organised a series of webinars  focused on the adoption of the RDA Outputs & Recommendations encouraging dialogue and interaction and facilitating uptake."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac89a9aa-3e8c-4249-99fc-6af0b079208d .

camssa:dd08eb95-bc67-49e9-8f4d-121b71120206 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The Data Collections API specification covers a specific area of application, guidelines for the data collections exchange through APIs; that is actually not covered by any other technical specification being under consideration to become a European standard. This conclusion has been drawn from the examination of all the programming mandates addressed to CEN, CENELEC and ETSI to the date, CEN’s webpage , CENELEC’s webpage , CEN-CENELEC’s webpage ICT section , the EC Information Providers Guide, Directive (EU) 2016/2102 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 October 2016 on the accessibility of the websites and mobile applications of public sector bodies , the standards and tools for exchange and processing of actionable information inventory of ENISA  and the ENISA Programming Document 2018-2020 "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4860107-53ce-486d-9c85-90bd6ea00284 .

camssa:dd0c27fe-1157-4db5-be7c-9d8175c561dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The W3C organisation has been developing the Indexed Database API since 2015 and has released three versions. Since then, the organisation has published all the information about the specification, which can be found on its website. In addition, the point of the specification is to preserve persistent data on users' devices, and this is available in almost all web browsers.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/

IndexedDB RXdB:
https://rxdb.info/articles/localstorage-indexeddb-cookies-opfs-sqlite-wasm.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7562b4e-ea26-4af3-9a48-a9d488efcb4a .

camssa:dd0fe71f-8420-4cd2-9af9-86592dfa8f74 a cav:Score,
