camssa:dd7091d5-d0cd-4334-922c-7100e76efe0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Industry Specification Groups (ISG), a working group in ETSI, are encharged of the development and maintenance of the NFVI specification. ISG members and ISG participants cooperate in developing and maintaining this specification, and contribute to the report writing. Participation is open prior a registration process and a financial contribution (see ETSI Directives' Rules of Procedure).\r
\r
ETSI Directives, Rules of Procedure:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/Resources/ETSI-Directives\r
\r
ISG NFVI reference, NFV Member Agreement and NFV Participant Agreement:\r
https://portal.etsi.org/TB-SiteMap/NFV/NFV-List-members\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f63ad5fb-3e94-4a3e-8a7f-04f8b3dd1f4a .

camssa:dd732aee-d461-4aaa-ab5d-53bfa52d7cf1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There are several studies and documentation analysing the use of the IETF Time Stamp Protocol with different purposes and putting emphasis on its usage as an efficient way to implement Time-stamp services. \r
\r
Design and Implementation of a RFC3161-Enhanced Time-Stamping Service:\r
https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.101.7115&rep=rep1&type=pdf\r
\r
Study about the impementation of Secure Time Stamp Device:\r
https://www.sans.org/reading-room/whitepapers/vpns/analysis-secure-time-stamp-device-746"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ff8c20f1-35c5-4112-8f59-549c80e95439 .

camssa:dd796147-4480-4989-8ee5-5e1757687627 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification includes requirements for the alignment with relevant regulations at European level such as eIDAS, GDPR, Cybersecurity Act, etc. Ensuring that the development of policies and laws is aligned with the main legal acts, including the interoperability ones, the Better Regulation Toolbox supports the establishment of public services and tools fostering data portability.\r
\r
Better Regulation Toolbox reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/sites/info/files/better-regulation-toolbox_2.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c287df2-6690-4ab0-8d4f-62f3bbf7b740 .

camssa:dd7e8b08-fa9f-4bba-bfc6-865b7c256c58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "eDelivery SMP 1.10 is an open specification based on the OASIS’s standard SMP 1.0. As SMP is an agnostic standard, eDelivery SMP 1.10 inherits this property. Thus, it can be reused in any business domain requiring metadata management and exchange.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:576d71f1-b254-4b39-adef-0aabeefbd15d .

camssa:dd7fe458-18f3-4d71-a1b6-84718ec199ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "IPSec is a set of open standards and protocols for securing the exchange of data packets over a computer network. Therefore, it ensures the trustworthy data exchange between different stakeholders."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6508ab5b-fc76-4970-81c1-721022bf41e7 .

camssa:dd845bf3-eeac-423a-b87f-41eee463d5f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification does not include security features to foster secure and trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders.\r
\r
SVG W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73f737cd-f885-45ff-b802-10bd8ca92cd4 .

camssa:dd8f0757-0017-49e7-beac-4a9d67565ebb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:dd8f8cfc-d3f1-4684-97a7-192e4d5f3e1e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c160d886-f8bd-4145-8db6-5dbcac1c2f4c .

camssa:dd93bf0d-882e-4004-95f3-35d36ab2f78d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT-AP is an RDF vocabulary for representing data catalogues that allows data owners to provide metadata about the datasets they publish. By describing catalogues, datasets and resources, a publisher makes them easily searchable and discoverable.\r
\r
In fact, DCAT-AP is used for the publication of datasets in linked open data portals at a National (e.g. ) and European scale ( European Data Portal)\r
\r
See:                                                                                                                                       https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/releases"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:471c0370-839d-44b9-9030-95e9e2014376 .

