camssa:dda7fa88-c4c4-4432-a80b-95d910e5bac0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b62656b1-bba0-44d4-8b98-28fbe2e5d245 .

camssa:ddb4b37d-f1b6-4fc6-a333-e827b92ee9e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary has a good market acceptance. Some parts of this vocabulary have been used to develop European solutions, for example, ESPD-EDM (European Single Procurement Document - Exchange Data Model) which is the technical representation of the legal European Single Procurement Document. It is used to support interoperability between ESPD services provided all over Europe. Additionally, other projects/initiatives like The Once-Only Principle (TOOP), and the eCertis are based on the CCCEV.\r
\r
ESPD documentation:\r
https://docs.peppol.eu/pracc/espd/edm/\r
\r
Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary reference (v1.0.0):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary-v100  \r
\r
TOOP:\r
http://wiki.ds.unipi.gr/display/TOOP/Core+Vocabularies+and+Application+Profiles\r
\r
eCertis:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/tools/ecertis/#/about '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f29716ec-acb2-41a8-90c5-7953a13dfcb8 .

