camssa:ddf3e11c-2831-4e6f-bf48-a947b76bb49e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData services return URLs to identify resources that may be later requested by clients. Where possible, data reusability increases by exploiting the information found in the route part of the URL, or by easing datasets management. However, data reusability might be limited. There is no evidence of any European solution confirming this aspect.\r
\r
OData reference, 6.1 Query Option Extensibility:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/odata/odata/v4.0/errata03/os/complete/part1-protocol/odata-v4.0-errata03-os-part1-protocol-complete.html#_Toc453752211'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3b50ee4-9d6a-47b3-82cf-c15492e0c729 .

camssa:ddfa160a-f449-4bfb-b66f-56f4e5da6421 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA is meant to augment semantics in languages such as HTML5 and SVG2, or to serve as an accessibility enhancement technology in other languages that do not specifically include support for ARIA. In this sense, customisation may evolve faster than other web host standards, enabling additional digital service delivery channels.\r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference, section 1.4:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1be819f8-c427-47f4-bd8e-0e74cc8f30e7 .

camssa:ddfd0690-a0b9-446d-97f8-762bf6063c97 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ACL functionality in IPv6 helps to establish an access control. Access lists determine what traffic is blocked and what traffic is forwarded at device interfaces and allow filtering based on source and destination addresses, inbound and outbound to a specific interface. Each access list has an implicit deny statement at the end. IPv6 ACLs are defined and their deny and permit conditions are set using the ipv6 access-list command with the deny and permit keywords in global configuration mode.

Access Control Lists for IPv6 reference:
https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst2960xr/software/15-2_5_e/configuration_guide/b_1525e_consolidated_2960xr_cg/configuring_ipv6_acls.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f2338adc-b89e-435a-bfc2-888a4af85225 .

camssa:ddfd76b0-620c-4631-a216-76a83d4bd89f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:ddfe6d10-4c7a-4acc-a8df-128a76e58953 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of YAML is not related to the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.  

YAML specification: 
https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfb7c856-902b-4b75-a183-a09ebf4fc3f2 .

