camssa:de25f2db-bd22-4d9a-8d1d-a2062fd763e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is a protocol focused on the transaction of data, specifically on the certification of certain data, information or documents which either exist or not. Despite its relation to the data exchange, the specification is not related to data portability itself, but the trustworthy data exchange amongst Systems and European Public Services.

TSP IETF reference:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eec7fe59-71ab-41a8-89ba-ca097daae80e .

camssa:de2ebead-5cd5-4223-94b3-f096ad8f9fc4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SAML 2.0 specification is designed with extensibility in mind. Extensibility in SAML allows for the addition of new elements and attributes within the confines of the existing XML schema to accommodate specific use cases, environments, or new functionalities without altering the core specification.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb682fe1-6e3c-4c4f-b445-d3d83b4a7b25 .

camssa:de2ec5f9-3654-4e52-b940-297bcfa3fc1a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-4386f49ebcfb474f011867d54ec0e7a7c561f91c288f5809299a05d781432bf0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:de3137df-8182-4ffa-98c0-51f6e0316002 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LDAP can be used independently of any other technical specifications or operating system. However, it is often used to complement Active Directory (AD) as a directory services protocol.\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511\r
\r
LDAP with Active Directory: \r
https://www.solarwindsmsp.com/blog/difference-between-ldap-ad"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7a5100e-d147-4a56-a19d-de2ec96bc2b3 .

camssa:de37f477-9c32-47fa-aa0a-a1514d5507b5 a cav:Score,
