camssa:de9680a8-b517-4902-b774-f096165a9819 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc53a28c-69e1-414a-91eb-dc3c837318e7 .

camssa:de97f3af-525b-4994-b835-ba3489fc2070 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8598a79-e280-4da1-8ac2-56f4485356a0 .

camssa:dea33121-7638-4b88-9951-075bed38a340 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:dea35597-81c4-40d4-9a9a-7e08a107f931 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:dea5e079-0540-4494-95d1-e721c0dec1d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"GraphQL is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, GraphQL will define the interoperability aspects of the Virtual DataSet ABB of the EIRA Semantic View, as well as the Data Exchange Service, Data Exchange Component, Data Management Service, Data Management Component, 'Data Extraction, Transformation, and Loading Service', 'Data Extraction, Transformation, and Loading Component', Knowledge Discovery Component Service, Knowledge Discovery Component of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v501\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41a19968-2bf8-4d95-8bc0-77a8bdfc23f1 .

camssa:deaa5ecc-ccd2-4db3-bfb3-31211423c32f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification performs effectively in accordance with the TR-ESOR middleware techincal guidelines.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/EN/Service-Navi/Publications/TechnicalGuidelines/TR03125/TechnicalGuidelines_03125_node.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88c0a94b-debb-471b-96a8-874afffc7d80 .

camssa:deb23cc1-7407-4cd8-ac6c-46ae09772b5c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As it is specified in the section 2 of the specification, it has defined conformance as a requirements to be followed.\r
\r
ADMS Reference, Conformance section reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/#conformance'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:205aeb86-fd5e-442b-bfc3-cbd9644ef41f .

camssa:deb375f6-c394-470d-87a3-9e97f0df27ed a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fef5941bab92019b7692f8544de94715a42ed9ff76d89cbec4fb6f9821611925 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:deb7cee4-34bb-4fd8-a986-ad5ea4336b00 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:debb6ba3-6d53-474d-b90a-c6f7eadc88b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is  the standardised digital representation of an asset. The AAS may be the logical representation of a simple component, a machine or a plant at any level of the equipment hierarchy. In this sense the specification can contribute to the comprehensibility of the manufacturing processes and the generated data to the administrators. 

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ade33ffc-ca78-40fe-9376-314762b360c7 .

camssa:debe32a9-81cd-4afe-93c8-53939a4a74df a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:dec2a7f9-6da8-4da0-802a-5fe75fd10716 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"IEEE Std 802.3-2022 doesn't directly address data reuse, but its design indirectly supports it by enabling communication between different systems. However, to fully implement the Once-Only Principle, additional measures related to data semantics and access control are needed.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dadec47d-be6f-48f9-8392-02a2ae1c126e .

camssa:dec4ca49-1909-4aa5-a951-d55199a24939 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39ffef052c31580b50b418f3991e9de7db4dc182fcf96f5a447d7f8e09560612 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:dec5d79d-22ca-4fb2-af60-1b383d46a21c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAREF itself does not define mechanisms for protecting information against unauthorized changes. The responsibility for ensuring the protection of information against unauthorized changes lies with the implementers and the systems using SAREF.

SAREF:
https://saref.etsi.org/core/v3.1.1/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4baefe55-4ea3-4253-bc6f-bd5d265c8d37 .

camssa:decb957b-ede4-46e4-80e1-d184872e7a96 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ded04de9-13c6-456c-90d8-91dd2bdce8ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of CSV is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.                                 \r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0243b413-5c7e-4a9f-a358-c770b5fc6404 .

camssa:ded06ae7-e6a3-42e7-be62-c1dfca30419f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

