camssa:df4355d1-be68-4c89-9a8b-b31567dbb959 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is independent of any technology or software. Although most image software can open TIFF/IT images, there are some that may not.\r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac174bc1-9934-43a1-ac07-dea58fa60fea .

camssa:df454e88-1ac3-431d-93fb-0d2592302ab8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org relies on more than one development community, mainly the Community Group and the Steering Group (see Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section). In order to contribute to the development of shema.org specification, stakeholder's participation is only possible through the Community Group or the dedicated mailing list. While the Community Group requires stakeholders to register to the W3 community (see W3 community reference, Mailing List), the mailing list does not require any type of registration process (see Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section). Additionally, anyone interested can contribute to the mailing list using the dedicated contact point (by contacting public-vocabs@w3.org), or participate via the schema.org Github (e.g. in the Issues or Discussions section) prior to a registration process.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
W3 community reference, Mailing List:\r
https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-vocabs/\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github reference, Issues section:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/issues\r
\r
Schema.org-W3 Github reference, Discussions section:\r
https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/discussions\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:deec5047-5964-4166-b542-fda44e665c56 .

