camssa:dfb80bdd-4607-4640-b5de-7d6141c6af2a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After research nothing has found about the specification being technology agnostic. The specification relies on some ISO standards.\r
For example, the Syntax Encoding Schemes, rely among others, on ISO3166, ISO639-2 and ISO639-3.\r
\r
\r
DCMI Terms:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1dd646b6-b422-44c0-a0a8-84cf69761392 .

camssa:dfbadfd5-1c90-43a8-8d52-d0dec9e2358b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:dfbb542c-bc8f-49af-9e2c-d42a745bce55 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML 4 comes from the evolution of different versions of HTML that they were already recommendations in W3C. HTML 4 became a W3C recommendation on December 1997. It had a good acceptance because it was the best markup language. This fact proves that the specification is mature enough for its use in the development of products and services.\r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5a80374-bb8b-4f82-a2be-4e12297297a4 .

camssa:dfc50937-f0a6-4027-acb7-bbc21c84a93b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The outputs / recommendations are aiming to achieve seamless interoperability, trust, and ultimately to provide growth and employment opportunities by facilitating data exchange across organisations, disciplines and geographical borders."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c16c781-292b-4538-bd23-f48fd6bf54a5 .

camssa:dfc661b4-9d25-4ce3-aab0-cf6ca121ce84 a cav:Score,
