camssa:e06cd93c-8ab9-469b-9027-43faa68f8860 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Customisations in E-ARK CSIP can be made and they typically involve adapting or extending certain aspects of the specification to align with a given organisation's needs. These adaptations may range from metadata customisation to the integration of the specification within existing systems.\r
\r
E-ARK CSIP specification:\r
https://earkcsip.dilcis.eu/#introduction\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f5f6b9b-8343-4652-93c2-1c1ff9427ca1 .

camssa:e06d07fa-e054-42a5-8f96-2160ea156aa3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification has been selected as one of the key elements for the data interchange between administrations and stakeholders. \r
\r
Europeana is using JSON within the Search API, the method created to diving into the european cross-border project data. These features allow retrieving information from EUROPEANA. \r
\r
Moreover, the Single Electronic Data Interchange Area (SEDIA) is using JSON as the basis to make data available for stakeholders. Examples SEDIA activity is the Call for Tenders, a key point on European eProcurement. Additionally, the EU Open Data Portal is another cross-border initiative that relies on JSON as a message format for API’s communication. \r
\r
See: \r
https://pro.europeana.eu/resources/apis/search\r
https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/support/apis\r
http://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/data/dataset/eu-open-data-portal-api"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1fa7eeec-6ddf-4179-89b9-da3b5c1a7fff .

camssa:e06d5a2f-aba9-4b51-96df-288758fc9c44 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DAPS is not related to facilitating organisational interoperability agreements. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:739070d8-3a93-416b-b099-f9f0cf7c32e0 .

camssa:e0734b96-c656-4352-a485-67c65efb2084 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SAML 2.0 specification is a business domain agnostic specification, designed to be implemented and/or used in any domain.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f0ab717-6a4e-4d09-a2dd-552e88643ed0 .

camssa:e07c2907-41dc-46f0-b103-3d11b56f4bc8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPv4 specification allows for extensions in the areas of security and privacy. One example of an available extension is IPsec, which works with both IPv4 and IPv6 and can improve data integrity and authenticity through the AH and ESP protocols.

IPsec extension:
https://www.ionos.es/digitalguide/servidores/know-how/ipsec-arquitectura-de-seguridad-para-ipv4-e-ipv6/

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71e90186-3c22-4f6b-bae7-d069f3c96781 .

camssa:e07fb67e-f722-4393-aa9a-7d3e4c173e82 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e08bc419-de71-4a3e-b96b-1bf27b12558e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d310596912dbc916997008f4aed16a81cf5e708cd907e3c53a2e4207468b468b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e0909f5f-89e3-4d15-bfb1-2d32ad81a5c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Spanish "Accessibility Observatory" offers a methodology to ensure the monitoring and evolution of e-accessibility services, and includes WAI-ARIA as one of the elements reporting the current status of e-Accessibility in digital public services. The WAI-ARIA specification is implemented in this methodology and scopes comprehensibility of website contents when combined mainly with HTML.\r
\r
PAe reference, Survey Methodology PDF:\r
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/en/pae_Estrategias/pae_Accesibilidad/pae_Observatorio_de_Accesibilidad.html?idioma=en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83db39cb-489b-4f2e-aa2b-dc908a4a15b5 .

camssa:e09404aa-ae07-45e2-8ade-adf48b0f65b7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Joinup offers several services that aim to help e-Government professionals share their experience with each other. Joinup supports them to find, choose, re-use, develop and implement interoperability solutions. LDAP appears in many Joinup entries as a discussion topic, and the specification is distributed and can also be found in the platform.

LDAP distribution in Joinup:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/dutch-standardisation-forum-comply-or-explain-standards/solution
/lightweight-directory-access-protocol'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43386cba-a95b-4c4b-ad89-382efa193aa8 .

camssa:e095f598-84a9-4b84-90af-62e3c328e910 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Zaragoza's city council is using HTML5 to developments services in an independent way from the platform used by the citzens. Another example is the Accessibilitly Foundation, HTML5 offers great possibilities for improving accessibility of web and mobile web applications, digital signs, ebooks and devices not yet known for people with disabilities.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2014/REC-html5-20141028/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84719908-400e-4a66-a835-a1558641f38d .

camssa:e09934db-0140-42dd-a88e-b9c86ed6d41d a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/68f2b027-3b29-4cdb-80a0-e889b3935f22"^^xsd:anyURI .

