camssa:e24da61e-f0a0-4e3d-818e-0fe6234d4934 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TSP tracks the creation and modification time of digital documents. Therefore, it fosters the creation and digitalisation of services at the same time that guarantees the data trustworthy exchange. By providing these capabilities to administrations, allows the reduction of administrative burden avoiding non-digital exchanges and the procedures for ensuring data reliability. \r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3eb839f9-21fb-4ea6-b367-a581dfeffcff .

camssa:e251d5b6-711f-483c-95d6-c0756a474055 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a1eafd9c95081eeabe19f0511239b88139f02f95e2349049eeea058a89c80f49 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e257be83-3de1-4362-8cdf-1069bdb9f927 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As described on the Oracle documentation about securtity features, the ebXML specification includes mechanisms that help guarantee data accuracy, such as data encryption and user authentication. By authenticating users, it helps ensure that data comes from a reliable and trustworthy source. Additionally, other mechanisms, such as encryption, can help ensure that data has not been altered by an unauthorised user since it was sent.

ebXML security:
https://www.oracle.com/technical-resources/articles/enterprise-architecture/ebxml-security1.html

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03fbd0dc-3116-4408-8a79-f770493f0316 .

camssa:e25959a2-c8c8-4e3e-b7c0-003119f6c299 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of IPv4 is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:321cb71b-8a0f-4f1c-b862-6dd62f13fc0a .

