camssa:e29ed6cf-b95c-4f4c-835e-c036487db568 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is included in 5 Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications. Some examples of Member States including JSON on their catalogues are the Netherlands, Spain or Belgium.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16854dae-b11c-4b2d-92a6-d00e01a03880 .

camssa:e29f5a34-cb7d-439f-a008-b82db7fd7cb1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UTF-8 does not hamper the scalability of systems, but the implementation of the specification is proportionate to users' needs. The specification is a variable-width encoding character set which allows avoiding the overhead of byte growth. Moreover, due to the wide sample of alphabetic scripts that can be encoded by means of UTF-8 and its high adoption avoids the interoperability hampering. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:41603afd-1f07-4899-aac4-c39a553616d9 .

camssa:e2a06ce2-6eb4-40f9-b2a9-44e2d604a62c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

