        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e2aa6dd1-b202-427f-a38d-4835039bd98f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'[To be checked] The publiccode.yml specification does not incorporate access control mechanisms. Its primary focus is on documenting metadata for public code projects, and it lacks provisions for establishing user roles or managing access to resources. Consequently, it does not align with the access control requirements outlined in EIF Recommendation 15.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bd9c714-7cac-4ace-9a9e-8e14057a1bde .

camssa:e2ac5780-055e-4cb8-94f2-0e841c713b43 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e2b02197-0fcc-4197-8ab0-de5a308b6dae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this Core Vocabulary is to harmonise public services (information) stored in different local, regional and national information sources, allowing the information to be searched and shared easily within and across public administrations all over Europe.\r
\r
CPSV-AP reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02017115-c2f3-4e7d-8717-3c766e91e23c .

camssa:e2b4853e-3acc-4888-b998-6327480aa588 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e2b662ed-c2fc-4d1e-90b2-baa82fa3f050 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While XHTML is a reformulation of HTML 4 using XML, it is not entirely independent of these standards or
other technologies. XHTML relies on XML parsing capabilities and enforces specific XML-based rules.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f588262-6300-4bd4-afcf-36fb1ff368e0 .

camssa:e2b9a172-58be-4c69-99e9-b9fe1cb5138d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has enough market acceptance as its first year of release it was inactive, in March 2016 it had enough market acceptance to become active. EN 319 422 defines a profile for time-stamping associated to a signature.\r
\r
Standards Globalspec reference:\r
https://standards.globalspec.com/std/9998069/EN%20319%20422\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:214a15b2-b7bd-40d6-8233-369afb0c2a8f .

camssa:e2c01b5f-98ee-4fad-b793-d335d8e2119d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org allows the exchange of metadata across borders which, in some cases can reduce the administrative burden. For example, by linking the DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe (DCAT-AP) and schema.org data discoverability on the web (Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe, or DCAT-AP-SDO) will increase, considerably easing access to European public services.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
DCAT reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ef7e2bd-754d-49d1-b967-c85959fb3bd4 .

camssa:e2c21fe5-8ab5-499a-ac45-860f1a669046 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e2c965d4-c524-42c0-9d70-8b7d82253841 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-52e41801b0db7274d934a229fee15e657273655d70d448d16706fcbe0e4f9746 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e2c99548-9d0c-4fb2-9960-e6f8a81cb8ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SAML 2.0 is not defining a cross-sector reusable data model. The specification defines a schema for the assertions that are involved in SAML performance but it cannot be considered as a data model. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:099d44aa-3197-49d7-84a3-796d7f2fd08c .

camssa:e2cb4523-9c27-4db0-914e-c59558a257e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to the publication of data as linked open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable for this criterion."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e4b9660c-fa15-4be9-a68b-314de8009bb0 .

camssa:e2d37dbc-9aea-4dcc-8649-9f684c26a7dd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:e2d5067e-0266-4e49-8045-91233ed48074 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specifications is not related to the publication of Open Data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94551d32-bb68-4f92-ab6d-77d18313254d .

camssa:e2d901a2-8045-4cfb-9678-c8a8f0c9bcbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UDDI uses WSDL to describe interfaces to web services and it is a platform-independent framework. In addition, it is an open framework. 

UDDI techtarget reference:
https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/definition/UDDI-Universal-Description-Discovery-and-Integratio'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3eef0bcd-f583-4d96-a5e8-07b1911ed745 .

camssa:e2dc27c8-79f3-4680-9328-3e9ae9398f6e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-450e8a1f4cffbbf3de202e37bd642f098174559028df90ccc657473a6086bc0b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e2e32742-760e-473e-b802-31d9c35ed4b1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI IPR Policy which is part of the ETSI directives seeks to reduce the risk that our standards-making efforts might be wasted if SEPs are unavailable under Fair, Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory (FRAND) terms and conditions.
The main objective of the ETSI IPR Policy is to balance the rights and interests of IPR holders to be fairly and adequately rewarded for the use of their SEPs in the implementation of ETSI standards and the need for implementers to get access to the technology defined in ETSI standards under FRAND terms and conditions.

ETSI’s intellectual property rights policy:
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85a17f2d-f2bd-43e3-b568-5967df6d6d3d .

