camssa:e3f698ee-d23c-418e-98b1-3c06aa455640 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of OWL2 is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
OWL2 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-overview/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69d6d083-9667-4de4-ae51-2f18285176e9 .

camssa:e3f8bfc5-9a63-44c0-8dca-5194643802ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main benefits of the e-Government Core Vocabularies (CLV) is that they provide a concrete starting point for promoting semantic interoperability among European public administrations. In this sense, the Core Location Vocabulary specification allows organisations to avoid some manual processes and to digitalise some services, improving the quality of public services. 
In addition, the CLV vocabulary is related to the INSPIRE project. In this context, the development of the Core Location Vocabulary was chaired by JRC/H6 Digital Earth and Reference Data involved in the implementation of the INSPIRE Directive. Therefore, it fosters the creation of innovative solutions.

INSPIRE project:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/EU01%281%29_0.pdf

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7336ea55-918f-4b00-bfd5-75f530b3910e .

camssa:e3fca94a-e77c-40e6-80af-6bf6868c7825 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org was originally conceived for the semantic web. Nonetheless, the specification project has successfully extended schema.org to other domains because of the variety of attributes and types it presents (see Schema.org reference, Data model section). Besides, schema.org also offers additional domain-related schema extensions that may differ from each other (see Schema.org homepage reference, 'Organization of Schemas' section), increasing the specification usability beyond a unique business-specific domain.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'About Schema.org' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/about.html\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Data model section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/datamodel.html\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'Organization of Schemas' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/schemas.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47ce834d-d7f9-4beb-b72f-1cdfe8d2dd7c .

camssa:e3fee4d9-8e94-4fda-b1fa-e2ec82d9c39e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is not related to multilingualism.  Therefore this criterion is not related to this specification.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d1f7eba2-d364-4f82-96f3-24eb8142b74f .

