        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e435ff1b-6d39-4fc1-a691-a145c1167ed8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of DNS is not related to the publication of open data.  Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
DNS IETF referece:\r
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc1034.txt'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e93e66b-03ef-496b-a689-e99bf7c2926a .

camssa:e43b8049-d9af-45c8-8902-01ae82781f20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Digital service delivery channels involve the use of digital technologies to provide services to users or customers. These channels can include websites, mobile applications, APIs (Application Programming Interfaces), and other digital platforms. The OSI model, as a conceptual framework, contributes to the development and interoperability of protocols that may be used in creating these digital service delivery channels. 

ISO/IEC 7498:1:
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b04d8d77-a574-498d-a0eb-d8faec958cd3 .

camssa:e4410a09-afa2-4f5e-afb6-14e47c75a132 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-6d48464387e608d3022bd07338cd3859acfb0f84139186a979ef3b96baa51086 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:e441d578-40be-4115-a2b2-6ca03b977bfb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although XHTML is a reformulation of HTML 4 using XML, it is not dependant of any version of the two standards. So, XHTML is independent of any technology or software.\r
\r
XHTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e47a4130-e630-4551-a5c1-464b7f28ae13 .

camssa:e4448852-e673-46d8-ae44-cab23031b6e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the moment of performing the assessment, the specification is associated with several ABB from the latest version published of the ELIS. More specifically, Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox can define the interoperability aspects of the Binding Instrument, Non-Binding Instrument, Public Policy, Legal Act, European Legal Act, National Legal Act, Granularity Of Legal Requirements, Public Policy Context Constraint, and Digital-ready Policy making ABBs of the EIRA Legal View.

Better Regulation Guidelines and Toolbox reference:
https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/better-regulation/better-regulation-guidelines-and-toolbox_en

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/solution/camss-assessment-eif-scenario/release/610'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ac85763-70ef-43bd-b90f-a0ed7ad3a618 .

camssa:e448dd03-704c-4bb3-b28f-0b2b9ee85e6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 offers some provisions on the portability of documents containing digital signatures.  This can be provided by preservation and validation services, whose main functions are to authenticate and preserve the chain of evidence of official documents. Nonetheless, ETSI TS 119 511 only specifies the requirements of these functionalities, while its companion document ETSI TS 119 512 provides the protocols to implement these services.  Therefore, ETSI TS 119 511 supports the implementation of European public services.\r
\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3acc8366-2633-4ee6-a4ac-96df345d7e1b .

camssa:e44bf426-b368-431e-8c16-be3a6a20ae66 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS is a secure internet protocol for the exchange of data over an Internet network. It makes data accessible on the web which is the first level of maturity defined in the Tim Berners-Lee's 5-star for Open Data.\r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa9863bd-0264-4eb6-a903-483285e9c8f8 .

camssa:e461202a-bed6-4704-a14d-e4184c6c47cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF itself does not provide bulit-in mechanisms to ensure data integrity.  Nonetheless, there are various techniques and mechanisms that can be used to ensure the integrity, confidentiality and availability of RDF data.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3dd1c8e7-f693-46c5-b43e-ca0f22601220 .

camssa:e46fe951-8d0e-4b7c-a3c0-bbefd30daae3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:e47a4130-e630-4551-a5c1-464b7f28ae13 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e4819d2d-415d-4e67-bced-35274a5dae3b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:e488b65e-c3db-4e23-89b4-96434e3cee0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While HTTPS can facilitate secure data transfer, it does not provide specific mechanisms or standards for data portability. The ability to exchange data between systems and applications typically relies on other protocols, or data interchange formats such as JSON, XML, or CSV.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32a42e22-6ea9-4423-b231-6742bc743286 .

camssa:e48d66b9-d890-4a3a-8232-11eaf6a8a4c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is maintained and developed by OASIS, which is an international community developing open \r
standards; specifically, by the Technical Committee (TC). The specification maintenance is transparent, and \r
even if its development and the approval process is restricted to the specification TC, anyone can contribute \r
by submitting feedback to the mailing list. All the contributions are publicly available.\r
\r
Developer community OASIS: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dabbc8a8-ee87-46f0-8a14-9b6227ea6faf .

