camssa:e63ad8e4-dc5a-4c25-aa0a-66c1479f5740 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of this document is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
W3C Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8e33e14c-b837-4024-a27a-f97d7752402b .

camssa:e63d15f3-c0eb-4cc1-a378-9a328c90e09a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The hub format of the UBL is well suited to the public sector. A single adapter interfaces all suppliers to a common consumer and vice versa. It also interfaces all businesses to tax authorities, custom agents, transporters and accountants.  Therefore, UBL can be considered a strong enabler of external interfaces for European Public Services. For instance, in the ESPD project, UBL XML behaves as an interface document between tenders and public administrations.\\xa0\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
ESPD reference, Legal framework and context section:\r
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/3.0.1/xml_business_handbook.html#_i_1_1_legal_framework_and_context'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef80a3f2-29a3-4b57-931b-f8dbfe6ce975 .

camssa:e63f7d67-5299-48c8-9d55-90dc7b3db54e a cav:Score,
