        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e65aa11e-31f3-4bec-8283-9d2e6838e63c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed73069a-239b-4a32-8959-532d5b5a881b .

camssa:e660533c-19ac-4b63-be65-9445947c2b13 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA is maintained and developed by OASIS, which is an international community developing open standards; specifically, by the OASIS TOSCA Technical Committee (OASIS TOSCA TC). The specification maintenance is transparent, and even if its development and the approval process is restricted to the specification TC, anyone can contribute by submitting feedback to the mailing list. All the contributions are publicly available.\r
\r
Developer community OASIS: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/org/\r
\r
OASIS TOSCA TC reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16de89ad-5375-49e1-abed-70d033877992 .

camssa:e6640bae-b4f6-4ed7-820c-be491e993665 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST architectural style streamlines administrative processes by easing the communication and digital exchange of information between clients and servers. For that matter, the implementation of REST architectural constraints helps to simplify the delivery of European Public Services.\r
\r
REST reference:\r
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6cf89119-dcb9-4c2b-a588-590ac939560e .

camssa:e66c829c-2e09-4433-83dd-92e7cd6f32b8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e6774c9c-cfb8-466a-a705-666f8a608f41 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Germany is recommending FTPS in their ICT National Catalogues.\r
\r
National catalogue Germany: \r
http://www.cio.bund.de/SharedDocs/Publikationen/DE/Architekturen-und-Standards/SAGA/saga_modul_tech_spez_de_bund_5_0_download.pdf?__blob=publicationFile"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:67fc69c4-bc1c-4daa-8a6c-ca3a6bccd43a .

camssa:e679e400-5ee1-40c0-8956-39d6c29abd20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any Member State recommending the DPV specification.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bab9ff9-1c4c-4275-94b8-012dfeab5553 .

