        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS is included in the “Data Spaces Support Centre” (DSSC), an initiative funded by the European Commission to facilitate data sharing and link the expertise of data sharing practitioners and researchers. The collected standards for Data Sovereignty and Trust include DAPS.\r
\r
DSSC Data Sovereignty and Trust standards and technologies landscape: https://dssc.eu/space/SE1/185794711/Data+Sovereignty+and+Trust+standards+and+technologies+landscape'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cff9eaf-bc92-4bec-ad79-c8fb08b225da .

camssa:e7917857-2083-419a-8abd-026624e77c4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of UTF-8 is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is not applicable specification. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4806ec98-0255-46e0-8ba1-fef76224c092 .

camssa:e792ea7b-3751-4ccf-9a1a-d87ba0850e06 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As a system requirement enabler for the availability of spatial data among EU public administrations, ISO 3166-1 facilitates digital service delivery channels for the exchange, sharing, access and use of interoperable spatial data and spatial data services at different levels of public authority and in different sectors (see INSPIRE Data Specification on Administrative Units reference and INSPIRE reference, Directive 2007/2/EC document, Article 1).\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html\r
\r
INSPIRE Data Specification on Administrative Units reference:\r
https://inspire.ec.europa.eu/id/document/tg/au\r
\r
INSPIRE reference, Directive 2007/2/EC document, Article 1:\r
https://inspire.ec.europa.eu/inspire-legislation/26'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c799d048-919e-43aa-956a-dbb1e83210a9 .

camssa:e795fbc2-0d6f-47c5-aef4-d757666e0c59 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-31bf959b6c4a983ec70eb87e0177f2739575ebce42c7c3b95b9012ef3bfe673e ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:e796ac48-9c74-4ff9-909c-ead32ed635b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS is the hierarchical and decentralised naming system used to identify computers reachable through the 
Internet or other Internet Protocol (IP) networks. For that matter it can be used in any domain.

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499

Domain Names - Implementation and Specification: 
https://tools.ietf.org/html/1035'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe2b08f0-8cdd-4a24-9d39-4ac6a1146167 .

camssa:e796e2a4-c3a6-40d1-a7cb-4b38717c6dc6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, HTTPS has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision. During the evaluation process, all the Member States are invited to share their doubts. The positive evaluation of HTTPS and its identification is considered an interoperability agreement.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc84c3de-d188-493c-9154-f296bb02ed41 .

