camssa:029c6aab-0060-4ea3-997b-c9a823ceb054 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c70b91fe-0b8f-4ee7-99ba-77c8240bcf3e .

camssa:078fd864-ed84-45e0-b0ce-beb4c2db5800 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification does encourage the creation of communities along with the sharing of their data on European platforms, such as the case of European legislation Identifier ELI XML serialisation._x000D_
Furthermore, XML also has created a wide variety of discussions regarding it's implementation and its features in places like Stack-overflow._x000D_
_x000D_
Stack-overflow dicussion on XML versions:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6260975/should-i-learn-xml-1-0-or-xml-1-1_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack-overflow dicussion on XML implementation:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6883084/what-xml-version-to-use_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack-overflow question regarding browsers:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/4508283/xml-version-1-1-not-accepted-by-browsers_x000D_
_x000D_
ELI XML serialisation:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/eli-european-legislation-identifier/solution/eli-xml-serialisation_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e5aaf0a-d9cc-4116-bea0-49199bda6d14 .

camssa:09dba403-16ca-45ce-aa9c-e64143b11f3d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1141e66a-debd-4f05-b320-6264e82c1fed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce3fcdde-c067-407f-beaf-150a4ad2f14f .

camssa:1305cfdd-6dba-4a5c-a89f-bf14cc711df9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XML is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information per se but it can be adapted for storing descriptive and administrative metadata, as show by the DiVA project._x000D_
In this sense it is also worth mentioning the XAdES specification that provides with long term signature preservation._x000D_
_x000D_
DiVA project reference:_x000D_
https://edoc.hu-berlin.de/server/api/core/bitstreams/d5f02188-85d2-444b-9cb9-0845df86af7f/content_x000D_
_x000D_
XML Advanced Electronic Signatures (XAdES) reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.03.01_60/en_31913201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ab8be84-268b-41ca-b742-1f79d19856d4 .

camssa:14c39837-8fc4-4481-ad24-a1305d0ab713 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the XML specification has been assessed by the Eindhoven University of Technology (The Netherlands). The "XML interoperability standards for seamless communication: An analysis of industry-neutral and domain-specific initiatives" study, addresses XML in a central and comprehensive manner as a key foundation for achieving interoperability in the e-business environment. In addition, it is noted that the XML format is gaining importance in industry-specific e-business frameworks and dominates in cross-sectoral e-business process frameworks._x000D_
_x000D_
"XML interoperability standards for seamless communication: An analysis of industry-neutral and domain-specific initiatives" study:_x000D_
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0166361516302160_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:acb4e0d0-5d75-4ab3-8240-8a9d15a0e3b9 .

camssa:18ea5e57-ae7a-4256-b366-a411e5b38d2f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1c6aa03e-718d-460b-a816-746b25b65dd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML can be used independently from any other technical specifications or operating system. It works in all browsers and applications that support it._x000D_
_x000D_
XML and browser:_x000D_
https://kinsta.com/blog/xml-vs-html/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1f00c741-13d1-4b76-a1d6-70bdfdfb1eda .

camssa:1d6912b5-6103-443a-b3b7-1289478dd142 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML can be used independently from any other technical specifications or operating system. Furthermore, It can be used by any technology (i.e. JAVA) for data storage and data transfer purposes. _x000D_
Formats like RDF or HTML can be encoded within XML without affecting interoperability. This flexibility allows diverse data types and structures to be integrated and exchanged seamlessly across different systems as in the European legislation Identifier ELI XML serialisation._x000D_
The ELI/XML schema is provided with a set of XML transformations to generate ELI in RDF/XML, RDFa header or HTML+RDFa. It is meant to facilitate the integration of ELI in XML-based document workflows._x000D_
_x000D_
ELI XML serialisation:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/eli-european-legislation-identifier/solution/eli-xml-serialisation_x000D_
_x000D_
RDF reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
RDFa reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdfa-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
RDFa HTML reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/html-rdfa/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML in JAVA: _x000D_
https://www.tutorialspoint.com/java_xml/java_xml_quick_guide.htm_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac0ed21c-4f92-42d4-a298-3a867f45e816 .

camssa:1dc38a7a-2b72-4a98-bf21-96cb8f1dfc8f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is machine readable format that is specifically created to allow the publication of data on the web. In this sense, this corresponds with one of the five elements that constitute open data according to Tim Berners-Lee deployment scheme._x000D_
Additionally, RDF is a W3C specification that defines XML syntax for RDF, the de facto standard for publishing Linked Open Data._x000D_
_x000D_
Tim Berners-Lee 5 star open data:_x000D_
https://5stardata.info/en/_x000D_
_x000D_
RDF syntax:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fae7c28c-9e5a-4397-9700-e4d085e17593 .

camssa:1e029430-0104-4e1a-ade5-57d1671d4b90 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML specification has published extensive documentation regarding its supporting processes on the XML Core working group page._x000D_
_x000D_
XML is widely used and is the default standard for many products and services across the globe since its original recommendation by W3C in 1996. In this sense the specification has been in constant development for a long time and a lot of minor issues have been corrected over the different versions._x000D_
_x000D_
Finally, a new XML version, rather than a set of errata to XML 1.0, is being created because the changes affect the definition of of the characters permitted on the names (Name characters). Since Unicode is ever expanding it is reasonable that XML is prepared to allow any character to avoid future limitations._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Core working group:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/XML/Core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML reference with difference highlight from previous version:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/2008/REC-xml-20081126/REC-xml-20081126-review.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1, section "Rationale and list of changes for XML 1.1":_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml11-20060816/#sec-xml11_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d5f669eb-b3f3-4a39-8e60-4c88f415ec9c .

camssa:1f00c741-13d1-4b76-a1d6-70bdfdfb1eda a cav:Score,
