    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:28294a50-0f33-490d-9072-1c07dc2291f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XML promotes interoperability between public administrations and cross-border services, supporting the development of eGovernment. It provides rules for encoding documents in both human- and machine-readable formats, enhancing data reusability and system interoperability. XML also allows the creation of custom tags and attributes, which can be defined once and reused across multiple applications for consistent and flexible information representation. Additionally, XSD defines the elements, attributes, and data types in an XML document, enabling schema and information reuse across different contexts._x000D_
_x000D_
For example, the European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) is a standardised, electronic self declaration used in public procurement across the EU that is based on XML 1.0. It simplifies the electronic procurement for SME's since at it's core it reduces the administrative burden. _x000D_
_x000D_
XSD reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3schools.com/xml/schema_intro.asp_x000D_
_x000D_
ESPD reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/european-single-procurement-document-espd_en/ _x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a416522-3a9e-4ae1-abdf-68c4128e9ce7 .

camssa:2a04a635-32bd-4483-9fe5-33854c85478a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is a markup language designed for the structuring and representation of data. By itself it does not provide means to restrict the access to the data but in order to ensure certain degree of data protection the specification has some methods to provide some degree of protection to the information exchanged on the system._x000D_
In light of this, by using the XML Encryption Syntax and Processing, permits the encryption of an entire XML file or certain portions of it. Thus, by encrypting data, restriction access is applied to guarantee that only authorised users can access data._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Encryption Syntax and Processing reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fd41fddd-da45-4fba-ae97-13be7e8286d3 .

camssa:2ecf7cca-f979-4003-ac37-c2e15c96d5d0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2ed7e074-f795-4047-8124-8981359fc04c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:30719481-bb2a-4137-9051-4af19ac8c45b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is used to encode all communications between web services. Therefore, it fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of public administrations data and services. This is achieved with XML because it enables a standarised description of data via a machine readable format that can be later on transformed to other more user friendly formats like PDF, CSV and others._x000D_
An example of such application is the eForms service for Public procurement standards on the European Union._x000D_
_x000D_
eForms reference:_x000D_
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/eforms/latest/schema/introduction.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7efe3ff3-c903-42ff-be8c-67ad6c73ddf0 .

camssa:31d0b8e3-16e0-4931-bc6a-39f34e2b7c9d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. Specifically by the XML Core Working group._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Core working group:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/XML/Core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a2c6cf5-ad21-41be-9807-dd4693d9456c .

camssa:320f82d8-b522-495e-ad0b-99faecc6c445 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:32b2df98-283b-4c80-8601-b4cadc3ffeb3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3349000e-71a8-4630-9bd9-0a84b1e879f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XML is to store, transport and exchange data through interoperable systems. In this sense, XML defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a human-readable format and machine-readable format alike, enhancing the re-usability of data and therefore allowing the data portability among systems and services._x000D_
_x000D_
Additionally, W3C develops its specification independently from any vendor. So, the adoption of XML does not hamper the data portability of data expressed with it. In fact, the adoption of XML fosters data portability, especially between REST APIs._x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ddf9ea6c-1152-40b0-83d1-bea03838b8bb .

camssa:35213950-3782-4041-998a-c58366d787ad a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3d3ec1de-62d0-455a-a95e-a606539d016d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML provides the foundation for creating structured data, and developers and organisations then use that foundation to build specific languages for their particular domains. In this sense the specification is domain agnostic._x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aff47574-bfd3-49f6-90fb-3d0a5004b884 .

camssa:3ec21e95-c58b-42d4-8fec-10f6c1a0c923 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML specification itself does not provide an access control mechanism. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
However, it is worth mentioning that if authentication methods are applied to the exchange it can be verified the number of users accessing the data. In this sense, if the signature and encryption extensions are applied, certain degree of access control can be achieved._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Signature Syntax and Processing:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3cf7f23-99a8-4afe-aff7-994404225609 .

camssa:40733392-891e-4edd-a57a-ea05cb785f5b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is a cornerstone of Web Services, which provide a standardised way for applications to communicate over the internet. Many e-government initiatives use Web Services to provide public services, with XML messages forming the core of these communications, enabling automated interactions between government systems and external applications. _x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b66bf2fe-33c1-48d9-a1c6-edf38df94e6c .

camssa:4229e97d-acab-4cc0-b633-8c50c490ccaf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML can be found a part from XAdES in the context of eDelivery SMP 2.0. In this sense, SMP documents are defined in XML format. By using these XML documents, organisations’ systems can publish and consume service metadata in a standardised and machine-readable format, thereby supporting organisational interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
eDelivery SMP 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/display/DIGITAL/eDelivery+SMP+-+2.0_x000D_
_x000D_
XML Advanced Electronic Signatures (XAdES) reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.03.01_60/en_31913201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C  reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32b2df98-283b-4c80-8601-b4cadc3ffeb3 .

camssa:4530267b-1c2e-46cd-943a-24ece6071209 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification provides a syntax for exchanging information that can be validated against a schema designed to protect data processing. In this sense, XML can be extended with other security specifications, such as the XML Signature Syntax and Processing. This specification can help to encrypt XML data, ensuring its trustworthiness by protecting it from unauthorised users. Thus, data remains in the same form as it was initially sent._x000D_
_x000D_
For further information in the Fog and Edge Computing from ENISA report, the XML specification addresses data security and trustworthy data processing._x000D_
_x000D_
Fog and Edge Computing in 5G report:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/fog-and-edge-computing-in-5g_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C  reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2ed7e074-f795-4047-8124-8981359fc04c .

camssa:45657087-9e47-414a-a2dc-86d549d58434 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4bf0dd78-b17c-46e1-b335-8ad237555838 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML specification is included in 17 Member States catalogues of recommended specifications. These Member States are Bulgaria and Croatia, among others._x000D_
_x000D_
Bulgaria reference:_x000D_
https://www.mtitc.government.bg/upload/docs/2016-01/BNIF_EN.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Croatia reference:_x000D_
https://ssi.gov.hr/en/catalogue_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fb294531-7562-4555-8294-c192b688535c .

camssa:5c2cb83b-dd89-4e66-948a-29892e31140a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML specification itself does not provide inherent mechanisms to ensure or enable data processing accuracy per se. However, there are complementary specifications, such as the XML Encryption Syntax and Processing specification, that can work together to enhance the trustworthiness of data, ensuring that the data received is the same as that sent and that it has not been modified._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C  reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:18ea5e57-ae7a-4256-b366-a411e5b38d2f .

camssa:5c6c1608-2482-4fc9-8fcf-97d6742aaa1b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is a de-facto standard markup language that is used in a wide variety of solutions, including innovative solutions across multiple domains. In this regard it is worth mentioning that version 1.1 is not as widely implemented as version 1.0.  In this sense, one of the most relevant European services, the European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) is developed in XML 1.0._x000D_
_x000D_
A part, the lastest release of XML 1.1 revolves around Unicode ever expanding, therefore XML is prepared to allow any character to avoid future limitations by expanding the definition of of the characters permitted on the names (Name characters)._x000D_
_x000D_
ESPD reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/european-single-procurement-document-espd_en/ _x000D_
_x000D_
XML reference with difference highlight from previous version:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/2008/REC-xml-20081126/REC-xml-20081126-review.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f43b60e-9968-4ff3-891b-46f7cd94452b .

camssa:5d3bc77b-66cd-45f9-a6d4-361ad302cd23 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5e5aaf0a-d9cc-4116-bea0-49199bda6d14 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5f43b60e-9968-4ff3-891b-46f7cd94452b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:61c4f7e3-3e7d-4ccd-8ccb-9cee295f1ca3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML documents are based on Unicode, which supports all writing systems. Therefore, any language can be used in an XML document. Additionally, XML can be encoded using formats like UTF-8, ensuring that all languages can be properly included and represented in XML documents. _x000D_
In addition, it is worth mentioning that in the XML 1.0 specification is mentioned that all XML processors must accept the UTF-8 and UTF-16 encodings of Unicode. However, certain Unicode encodings, like UTF-16, can result in larger file sizes compared to single-byte encodings, potentially impacting storage and transmission efficiency._x000D_
_x000D_
UTF-8 reference: _x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3629 _x000D_
_x000D_
UTF-16 reference: _x000D_
https://www.iso.org/standard/76835.html _x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fea6acc2-78d1-4c34-92d7-fec2124ddb53 .

camssa:6a2c6cf5-ad21-41be-9807-dd4693d9456c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6ab8be84-268b-41ca-b742-1f79d19856d4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6c2875c7-9741-4c59-8197-899fb9083929 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is used to represent data steaming from business processes, in this sense the specification is the backbone to exchange data and therefore analise and model any process coming from it. Furthermore ebXML is a prime example of this._x000D_
_x000D_
ebXML reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ebxml-msg/ebms/v3.0/core/ebms_core-3.0-spec.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f737d189-4fec-4432-bac2-3b1c367b6b87 .

camssa:6ef3c32e-28c8-45fb-ab03-7d8671e3619c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML 1.1 specification is developed by a non-European organisation. In this sense, the specification cannot be considered a European standard, but it lies at the core of many European services and developments and is widely implemented by European institutions. Therefore this criterion is not applicable._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b018e668-2ff4-4ae1-8dd5-6a5837fd060f .

camssa:7ba74da1-be7d-42d5-89ed-c0e393126e20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the specification is included on the ICT Standards for Procurement list on the Interoperable Europe Portal._x000D_
_x000D_
European list of ICT Standards for e-procurement:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/identified-ict-specifications-procurement_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:018de197-3cf9-4417-995a-ace02c2d69c6 .

camssa:7c5c662f-5aa7-46bc-a8fd-7e03c0225751 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML is meant to be used fully, a document can either fully adhere to the specification syntax or not._x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:028657f3-9d30-4c25-bc1d-8df03c10f4d7 .

camssa:7cf536b0-c445-4516-bb5d-e11070de2a50 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'17 Member States are recommending XML in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are Bulgaria and Croatia, among others._x000D_
_x000D_
Bulgaria reference:_x000D_
https://www.mtitc.government.bg/upload/docs/2016-01/BNIF_EN.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Croatia reference:_x000D_
https://ssi.gov.hr/en/catalogue_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:320f82d8-b522-495e-ad0b-99faecc6c445 .

camssa:7d75809d-ae20-497e-8b22-60730092c0e2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7efe3ff3-c903-42ff-be8c-67ad6c73ddf0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:846aa02b-301c-49bd-8fa0-dadc0055ecd4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML specification provides a syntax for exchanging information that can be validated against a schema designed to protect the data exchange. In this sense, XML can use other specifications, such as the XML Encryption Syntax and Processing, which allows data to be encrypted and better protected against eavesdropping or unauthorised users. Thus, by using this complementary specification, data can be exchanged in a secure and trustworthy manner._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C  reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d75809d-ae20-497e-8b22-60730092c0e2 .

camssa:8c2b6e82-f777-419c-b8b9-469f5f6db3cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XML does not directly define or expose technical interfaces for accessing public administration services. However, the specification provides a standardised, machine-readable structure for data, which facilitates the exposure of such interfaces. Additionally, XML data can be converted into formats like HTML using converter software, further supporting the presentation and accessibility of these interfaces such as in the eForms application._x000D_
_x000D_
eForms reference:_x000D_
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/eforms/latest/schema/introduction.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35213950-3782-4041-998a-c58366d787ad .

camssa:9a416522-3a9e-4ae1-abdf-68c4128e9ce7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9ad223ce-59fb-4660-a7b0-112a988d48b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XML format, particularly through XAdES (XML Advanced Electronic Signatures), is recognised by the eIDAS Regulation as a compliant format for advanced electronic signatures._x000D_
_x000D_
Overview of Standards for eIDAS document:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/assessment-of-standards-related-to-eidas-i_x000D_
_x000D_
XML Advanced Electronic Signatures (XAdES) reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.03.01_60/en_31913201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:45657087-9e47-414a-a2dc-86d549d58434 .

