        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-01e6c1ce016de128117697d51a8fdaebb57c1f50343c081dfd72e2fbc56733a8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e922f97d-cd74-4f41-9cd8-443f73c5ce50 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of IPv4. The "A systematic review of transition from IPv4 to IPv6" study, examines and exposes how IPv4 has demonstrated reliability, compatibility with a wide range of protocols, applications and ease of implementation. In addition, it is made a comparision between IPv4 and IPv6, and how IPv6 can improve its predecessor.

"A systematic review of transition from IPv4 to IPv6" study:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/343820813_A_Systematic_Review_of_Transition_from_IPV4_To_IPV6'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0935530c-6acf-4c79-9760-c48146700177 .

camssa:e9271d26-f887-4d4e-a883-aee36c1ff857 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although DCAT-AP itself does not provide means for the enabling of data integrity, the SEMIC Support Centre has developed the DCAT-AP validator, a software tool to check metadata description of datsets for integrity and consistency.\r
\r
DCAT-AP validator:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/dcat-ap-validator'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f24dd727-a822-44af-a541-135cb2eb1508 .

camssa:e92a8e7b-8d4f-4d34-ba98-de35aa684f6d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-25deb65536af2c7e82f921c56df2c7e21093b2c06fdddd63021b4bccea0b9cd7 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e92d68e0-f878-4506-9fe0-caa0e815eac3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e92ed695-ce16-43e8-9874-e0ce2813b51c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP is designed to be technology agnostic, being able to adapt to new technologies and advancements in network infrastructure, ensuring its relevance and longevity. Examples are the creation of new extensions or versions like HTTP/2 and HTTP/3.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP versions usage:
https://blog.cloudflare.com/http3-usage-one-year-on/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d06ec456-facc-4544-9759-20701e2eb305 .

