    cav:refersTo camssa:3a5f5a95-cc9c-4691-aeb4-3ad68fbb4f88 .

camssa:e951df69-6d2a-46a2-8d52-c6bafee55b66 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e951ec54-6c46-42f3-ae1d-3603f60dffa1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ISO has defined a clear procedure to develop its standards. It consist in a 6-steps process where only the full members can participate and influence the development of ISO standards. Individual or organisations cannot be part of the ISO Member bodies, however, ISO has a wide network around the globe in order to capture information from the maximum stakeholders possible. \r
\r
Technical committees are in charge of the development of the standards. ISO has defined the roadmap of standards, it is composed of 6 steps as before said.\r
\r
For the approval of an standard the two thirds majority of P-members of TS is needed. If the result is negative, the document is returned to TC/SC for further studied.  \r
\r
See: \r
http://www.isotc292online.org/projects/iso-process/ """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e221f4f-cc19-406a-895e-15f5db51d7a8 .

camssa:e9541e41-66cb-4f2f-ae6d-f28ad9032599 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The first formal standard version of IP was version 4 (IPv4), created in 1980 and defined in RFC 760. Since then, many assessments and improvements have been made in terms of security and privacy, for example. In addition, despite countries transitioning to IPv6 addresses, IPv4 is still more widely used than IPv6. For example, the USA and Canada alone account for almost half of the world's IPv4 allocation.

IPv4 RFC 760: 
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc760

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791

IPv4 history:
https://ipv4marketgroup.com/a-brief-history-of-ipv4/

IPv4 adoption:
https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Allocation-of-IPv4-and-IPv6-Addresses-IPv6stylecom-2004-Palet-2003_fig1_228757766\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0227e09a-b2dc-4893-b5e1-1788f66f4679 .

camssa:e95a9caf-6168-4fe7-81b1-ca5639149514 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:e95ccbf4-0de4-4e0d-87dd-0adbc239c95b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a81c4b8658f57e819297eb0b7977407f8d814c6fe749c74a8ac497277ca7d9d8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e95ded77-4b68-4adc-9128-a84c05dba010 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA is enhanced by a conformance testing platform that facilitates the assessment of implementations. Additionally, the W3C Accessibility Initiative puts forth tools and methods designed to evaluate these implementations, ensuring that web technologies align with the accessibility standards.

WAI-ARIA W3C validation tool list:
https://www.w3.org/WAI/ER/tools/

WAI-ARIA Test & Evaluate:
https://validator.w3.org/#validate_by_uri

WAI-ARIA reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81c280c0-81f5-4d99-af91-be3d40e055a5 .

camssa:e95e2806-6fbf-40d9-b2e5-747b230d0bd2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """5 Member States are recommending WS-Security in their ICT National Catalogues. \r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7de68f8f-a38c-42a2-b883-fc82df936177 .

camssa:e9643cbc-3105-404a-b334-3339d7d138fa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-cc272cd8a2e3e9c5e4edaa5ac7d59735c377a9db89d6958335a2cf0538761ab3 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:e966768d-a98c-4434-98ae-c19700ad3c46 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17bea234285e6e633e4e21105358610ad5f5f0eaaf82f4bd50cb64ec11538984 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:e9693453-12dd-4548-9510-a3e3b12f9a93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification itself does not provide mechanisms for protecting information against unauthorized changes. While WSDL may include references to security policies and mechanisms (such as WS-Security), the actual implementation and enforcement of security measures are typically handled outside the scope of WSDL at the application and infrastructure levels.\r
\r
OASIS Web Services Security:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=wss\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58bfa823-d487-405c-b05c-f5409e605f17 .

camssa:e969d316-fbff-4308-a084-62e6e159f5b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of the EN 303 645 specification is not related to enabling the exposure of interfaces of public administration's services. \r
\r
EN 303 645 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31c5c6af-7991-46aa-9a08-07b2d831420a .

camssa:e96a13fa-20c8-4b29-a70f-97b3e286dd7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is not specifically designed to be multilingual but since the presentation layer deals with standardising data types and their representations, a single international character code standard such as Unicode is necessary for software internationalisation and multilingual communication of OSI based platforms. This has resulted in multiple attempts to translate the lower layers of communication values onto more universal codification for the upper layers.

OSI and multilingualism
https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0920548997000044

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7f2040e9-057b-40fc-b1f8-e7f4884bbdc2 .

camssa:e96b02f9-f42f-4291-b4c1-08beb9a69384 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Considering the original intent of the specification, it can be affirmed that its role enchances the clarity of
data within Public Administrations and pertinent information generated for the decision-making process. ELI
offers a unified schema for defining metadata related to legislation, simplifying the comprehension and
shareability of legislative documents and facilitating their accessibility.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c464b13-cb3d-42c6-9d3c-3889254f559e .

camssa:e9710d8e-a429-4e9f-bf22-c880fde41b8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification allows for customization to a certain extent. While the core functionality and commands of FTP are standardized, the specification allows for additional customization through the use of optional features and extensions.\r
\r
FTP implementations can include customizations based on specific requirements, use cases, or system configurations. These customizations can include features such as specific authentication mechanisms, custom command extensions, or additional functionality beyond the basic FTP operations.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6eed1950-b3b1-4165-a310-4dd9e47f06ec .

camssa:e971ff57-b112-4cc3-ab4e-dc32b7b0fe18 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:e9741fce-e605-4e3c-895d-83dcbe9c9b5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS’s purpose is the description of Assets within a Catalogue (repository), making them easy to discover and reuse. However, it is not related to foster the one-only principle between administrations and stakeholders.\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d8cccd9-1844-4bd6-a1e9-e6235b48ceb8 .

camssa:e9778896-d47f-42ca-b216-37c29e82d4a3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db4f7263-cec4-4945-878c-5cb9bc08c18f .

camssa:e97c4526-14ef-4e9f-b8b1-8b7cf6e75a5b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c265ca0c56e0f29a34039d496ba707b5486ccf6d445f9f058c19b4ece977861f ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:e97d7217-8889-4ab0-8044-4aa3f3b89f93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP appears in the Commission Implementing Decision "on the identification of ICT technical specifications eligible for referencing inpublic procurement". In this document, LDAP is said to be a stable technology that has the potential to increase interoperability and constitutes a de-facto standard for authentication, For that matter, the LDAP standard can facilitate organisational interoperability agreements.

Commission Implementing Decision of 3 April 2014 on the identification of ICT technical specifications 
eligible for referencing in public procurement:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32014D0188'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e233c6f-6a0e-41ad-b540-a0b6e40f088d .

camssa:e9802e3e-0de7-4ede-9221-1b786c77e3f8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:e989a89d-ab9b-4639-9118-70a9f640c3bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "UTF-8 is not defining a cross-sector reusable data model. The purpose of the specification is to define a schema for encoding data."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e6c1264-3d07-4680-8904-fb19105fe03e .

camssa:e989fa4b-cee8-4536-b28e-25a691a8d4f6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e98a5c72-0eb0-49ea-a17e-fd7910971a0a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has been used by several organisations at European and national level across Europe. There are implementations related to taxes in Flanders and Finland, and also implementations related to Smart Cities through Data Spaces. 

In relation with Data Spaces, EIRA includes an approach that is aligned with major initiatives such as the Data Space Support Centre (DSSC), the International Data Space Association (IDSA). This is a trend at European Level that leads to innovation, where EIRA and its specialisations can support public administrations to innovate. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA 

IDSA: 
https://internationaldataspaces.org/

DSSC: 
https://dssc.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54931fd4-6ad9-4202-af3f-dc6fb2590717 .

camssa:e98cbc1a-e3f1-4b09-835d-c75271c66f9a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DAPS has a repository which is open source and can be accessed at GitHub. It contains all major releases available and documentation on its supporting processes so, it can be considered that DAPS is mature enough for ts use in the development of digital solutions/services. Further documentation about the IDS Identity Provider/DAPS can be seen at GitHub too.\r
\r
DAPS: https://github.com/International-Data-Spaces-Association/IDS-G/tree/main/Components/IdentityProvider/DAPS'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4539f34d-c257-4aa4-aa6d-10c9bf8a8281 .

camssa:e9903580-7b8c-487e-b48e-1e02cbe1e9ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of HTML is not related to long term preservation of electronic records. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
HTML W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81dcc907-d639-4eb5-b531-46415ebf0295 .

camssa:e99388e6-366b-4807-a7a9-8d68fa36666e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e99fad5e-63b1-43dd-a736-0ead63191650 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The adoption of PDF as a document format for exchanging information does not hamper the scalability of systems. It is an widely adopted and used for this purpose and, moreover, it is independent from any platform or software. Therefore, PDF is proportionated to the users' needs and at the same time, it does not hamper the interoperability and scalability of systems.  "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8265fc1-da14-4efc-9c8d-d4cde05f5e68 .

camssa:e9a156ea-9ccb-48a7-b323-f9b5a4776cbd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a67ecbc29e70e62b18dba3ae4f8d1f91d5b3196777dbf8b58c6713cd517eb768 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e9a2f894-706c-47d2-b39e-027460bedef5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ec5bef7-8b0f-4ae8-883b-a69e422cddab .

camssa:e9a38732-d140-45d8-97c0-a192ba0a25e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of TLS 1.2 is not related to the publication of public data as open data to European public services. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bf4de47b-a0a9-4a01-9eac-ec9fa455f86d .

camssa:e9ad78ff-cfe8-4f5e-bd26-a9a2292c031a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is available for its use and implementation at the IETF's webpage.\r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9c53e6e-5190-4e6e-98ea-e4cb22870403 .

camssa:e9ae2f6d-7cc3-4635-a777-e26cc7dbaba4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The purpose of OSI is not directly related to data processing and therefore the specification does not provide with specifications for data security. However, one key characteristics of the open systems is the data exchange and the specification provides with the basic elements for it.

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html

OSI's Security architecture
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/es/#iso:std:iso:7498:-2:ed-1:v1:en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7a33c6d-04b2-41a5-a48c-18fc29458d54 .

camssa:e9b32112-91ab-43c4-bc8c-611e9e1b1b5b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State that includes NFVI in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories:\r
	1- Conceptual model for integrated public services provision\r
	2- Interoperability layers\r
	3- Interoperability principles\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f689ca5-d4fd-49f0-b9e9-8961a0d34c00 .

camssa:e9b7c366-10b8-4c14-8427-b2394ccb86bb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The DCAT vocabulary supports the attribution of data and metadata to various participants such as resource creators, publishers and other parties.\r
In addition, it also supports the association of rights and licenses with catalogued Resources and Distributions.\r
Such metadata improves the reliability of data processing between citizens, businesses and public administrations.                                                                                                                                                                                              \r
\r
DCAT (v2.0.0) reference:             \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-2/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58eaa9df-a128-4c2d-960e-c383f6a77c86 .

camssa:e9bc6650-84d9-4bbf-b9d9-285de43a7392 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Any interested party may propose and request modifications to SFIA definitions and skills/competence coverage after a registration process (SFIA reference, Future SFIA section, Change requests subsection). In addition, the SFIA Foundation facilitates a collaborative platform to promote visibility of the specification across different sectors (see SFIA reference, SFIA Views).\r
\r
SFIA reference, Future SFIA section, Change requests subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-9/change-requests\r
\r
SFIA reference, SFIA Views:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8/sfia-views'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9de52fb3-b3f9-43fa-8807-035710c8efb2 .

camssa:e9bcef6d-5bfa-4a7b-9799-95d8359c87ba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:e9bf3154-c6f8-407f-ac2e-c083e3ceb39c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) has at its core the idea of platform Industrie 4.0 that is the delivery of assets among partners and this simplifies the deliver of digital services. At the same time this is done in the context of the Industrial Digital Twin Initiative (IDTA). The AAS provides the partners with the adequate formats and resources to share a digitalised industrial asset (whether it is a tool or a product) among themselves, thus making possible the design and implementation of new assets in a collaborative manner. 

Industrie 4.0 initiative:
https://www.plattform-i40.de/IP/Navigation/EN/Home/home.html

IDTA reference:
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58b322f5-eef2-412d-a9cd-d4cd58a5cbb4 .

camssa:e9c3c783-0f21-4313-9433-ca5b48d6760b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """RDF defines a data model that can be reused in a cross-sector way. There is an extension of RDF vocabulary which extends the definition. This specific section (RDF Schema) belongs to the RDF stack focusing especially on main elements for the data modelling. \r
As RDF is an agnostic specification is defining a reusable cross-sector data model.  \r
See: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-schema/\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/#section-data-model"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:92a0f28e-34df-4381-9986-0b75b5c74c7c .

camssa:e9c51ed5-479e-4c6c-a568-4910bb5f6eaa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9d3df51-78c0-4ce8-9463-eb7c274d9d6e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e9d54bdb-cc23-40a9-b67f-d849fb1527ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9d5d82a-0cc0-42e3-81de-ff47d567bdf4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9dcb998-ce7b-4ce8-94ea-e205896ae07d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9e05b9c-2141-44fd-a75f-06aa7dead25c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9eb3db8-3b8e-4c2c-9845-513084d9cd6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By using SAML 2.0, the system administrator is prevented from providing several authentication tokens and, the user does not have to deal with several credentials. This fact helps to adapt the specification to user’s needs without hampering the scalability of systems. \r
\r
In addition, SAML 2.0 allows the exchange of authentication and authorization data between parties. It is mainly used to ensure single sign-on (SSO).  It extends SSO across security domains independently from any platform which prevents non-interoperable proprietary technologies."""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2bff4ab8-0367-4c18-92b3-f53dd54df8e9 .

camssa:e9efa6ae-5eb1-414b-8f50-e2c0c29b37ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9f0c995-f72a-49bc-8d1d-bf3d937b6583 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9f0ede0-a7cc-42ba-aa4b-38627e1413cf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of WSDL is not related to the delivery of multilingual services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:382903fd-f6c0-47ef-9668-b18dc317d15e .

camssa:e9f4231a-0989-45f3-bc0d-207bb8c9a7b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary does not guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions. The main purpose of the specification is to define a standardised way of describing organisations that have gained legal entity status through a formal registration process. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca64a914-7192-4f16-af41-112d630597b8 .

camssa:e9f74798-21a0-4520-a066-82ed1faa2778 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:e9f99cc0-24c6-4e41-8450-cc01430f1b5e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3aec34db3622bf18675b8216d0fc1d68fc7eeb501b4f3326402038a3ceb95c21 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:e9fc5d37-ce84-4bd2-96a4-92bed8bf3f16 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
