camssa:ea08ba0c-6e37-450b-b7aa-17fa1ef69a23 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CAdES (ISO 14533-1:2014) is an ISO standard and as all ISO standards, they have to be paid to access its content. However, it can be checked out in ETSI website where the content is aligned with the ISO standard.  \r
\r
CAdES ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/64756.html\r
\r
CAdES ETSI reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/101700_101799/101733/02.01.01_60/ts_101733v020101p.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:24df819f-9419-4e04-8da1-34999808176c .

camssa:ea0be9fc-0bdd-4bb9-b0e8-17008f362296 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The maturity of the specification can be seen on the use cases provided on the Digital twins initiative, the specification is present in already implemented initiatives such as Collaborative Engineering. This IDTA's AAS use case proposes a collaborative environment to design and implement modifications on a specific manufacturing tool.

The specification is released on the Github and IDTA. Furthermore, the documentation is readily available on the aforementioned pages.

Asset Administration Shell (AAS) Github documentation
https://admin-shell-io.github.io/aas-specs-antora/index/home/index.html

IDTA use case
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/10/2024-10_IDTA_UseCases_Collaborative_Engineering_Factsheet_en.pdf

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4a598131-fb79-4962-bf98-162e4aede136 .

