camssa:ea329d00-7f95-49bf-9635-55d7f3b3e2c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org enables the exposure of interfaces to access European public administration's services when combined with other specifications. The specification is currently used in combination with DCAT, in order to propose a common data schema (DCAT-AP-SDO, Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe) enabling administrations and citizens to find and reuse datasets located in EU data portals. Despite the fact that there is no evidence of any public administration's service making use of this common data schema (DCAT-AP-SDO, Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe), the specification may favour the promotion of semantic interoperability between different information systems and promote the adoption of a common mechanism to enhance the exposure of such services.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'Documentation' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/documents.html\r
\r
DCAT reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:24aeac14-56c9-4c7b-b371-58da00f1fc01 .

camssa:ea3a6cf1-4d70-4576-96a6-b6236958970f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 512 is part of the Electronic Signatures Infrastructure (ESI) family of specifications.  the ESI dates back to 2012, when the  General Policy Requirements for Trust Service Providers supporting Electronic Signatures (ETSI EN 319 401) specification was first issued.  Since its first publication, there have been many extensions one of which is ETSI TS 119 512, whose version 2.3 was released in 2020 when the eIDAS regulation identified the need to create protocols to develop preservation services for trust service providers,  as mentioned in ETSI SR 019 510, giving birth to both TS 119 511 and TS 199 512 specifications.\r
\r
\r
ESI specification history:\r
https://standards.globalspec.com/std/14387016/EN%20319%20401\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 512 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.02_60/ts_119512v010102p.pdf\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 401 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf\r
\r
eIDAS blog, New APIs for the eIDAS-Ecosystem:\r
https://blog.eid.as/tag/etsi-ts-119-512-en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5da11512-717f-4951-95b5-4629035b6992 .

camssa:ea3dc52e-1aea-4271-b605-7f028da27349 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification and its community ensures to give conferences based on metadata aswell as mantaining and developing metadata terms namespaces, contributting to scope comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data and services may be a side effect of all mentioned actions.\r
A good example is that ECLI implements DCMI which can be meaningful in scoping comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data and services.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/ '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4285b283-67d1-40c7-bdc3-6b92146207ef .

