camssa:ea6be05d-6fac-42e0-aa9e-b63281a5bfb2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP is included in 10 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Austria, Croatia, Cyprus, France, Germany, Greece, Malta, Netherlands, Spain, and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Spain and Austria are fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Nonetheless, countries like Sweden or Malta do not get a high perfomance, being alligned with 3 out of 5 and 2 out of 5 respectively.

National catalogue of Austria: 
The e-Government Bund-Länder-Städte-Gemeinden platform: http://reference.e\\x02government.gv.at/

National catalogue Malta:
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden

National catalogue Spain:
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/pae_Estrategias/pae_Interoperabilidad_Inicio
/pae_Normas_tecnicas_de_interoperabilidad.html#CATALOGOESTANDARES

National catalogue Sweden:
https://www.avropa.se/globalassets/dokument/open-it-standards.pdf?_t_id=1B2M2Y8AsgTpgAmY7PhCfg%
3d%3d&_t_q=standards&_t_tags=language%3asv%2csiteid%3a95d515a5-23ca-47bf-87a9-
07b10d8ac360&_t_ip=178.139.72.144&_t_hit.id=Avropa_Core_Models_Media_GenericMedia/_ff07d720-
f793-44b0-994d-27e79b28f6bd&_t_hit.pos=7

NIFO factsheets:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/national-interoperability-framework-observatory-nifo/nifo-factsheets
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3cfcb32-cf37-43a7-af9b-05901bd4f1da .

camssa:ea717c55-efbb-453e-a32e-10c263f98023 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-58010a47630ff9ea23336bf3fc558deff59905e0292551fcabc95740082cb378 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:ea755d32-802b-489a-9f4f-187e206d6580 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1, which defines the OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model, does not comprehensively address administrative procedures, rules data, and services in a detailed manner. Even so, given that the OSI model provides a common basis for the coordination of standards development for the purpose of systems interconnection, it can be understood that comprehensibility is taken into consideration.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73ec1aef-9604-4478-a802-cc41497d867d .

camssa:ea76b0c6-a16e-4358-9e5f-1b5e474f40d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Verifiable Credentials is being directly used to create innovative solutions in different areas. In the emerging Web3 landscape, the need for secure and trustworthy identity solutions has become more important than ever. Thanks to Verifiable Credentials, issuing organizations can generate fraud-proof digital credentials and verifying organizations can instantly check the authenticity of those credentials. One use case would be European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI), an European initiave that has developed several frameworks to address business problems using the 3WC Verifiable Credentials data model.\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0b1d1c0-074f-46fc-9580-a0f836e742b9 .

camssa:ea837cbc-d746-4f84-8aa2-69e06f8bba26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that uses W3C Best Practices nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7c34f25a-ef7c-42a5-827c-b2d4dacea78e .

camssa:ea83cd28-d9d9-4dd7-8e86-8994278ae25a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """HTML5 Geolocation can make an impact to the emergency service and\r
its citizens. It explains the capabilities of the existing web technology for accurate handset derived location\r
using HTML5 Geolocation.\r
\r
See:\r
https://eena.org/document/html5-geolocation/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:60ecb838-4f6b-4b89-a967-947f98b4bf55 .

camssa:ea896b0b-6086-4661-b20e-ba5cf63562c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the roles agents involved in the data transactions.Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81fb40a8-9045-4ccb-ae29-051e9d425dbb .

camssa:ea8a537d-e1f1-4f46-8d4f-5734576a3d0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) has established Working Groups. These Working Groups are open to the participation of everyone interested in semantic solutions working for public administrations in the Member States or in EU institutions. Moreover, the Core Location Vocabulary has been presented in some webinars to get feedback of the community. 

SEMIC working groups:
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/about

Core Location Vocabulary webinars:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/200

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:129495de-cc53-4e9e-a6b5-d4f75ffbae07 .

camssa:ea8cdfec-1dc6-4ec0-b2b3-1aa5904b5662 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The underlying XBRL specification was designed to permit not only the capture and expression of business\r
reporting facts in all of the languages supported by ISO 639, but also the internal capture and expression of\r
regulation and guidance related to the reporting content. The specification has support already for 8\r
languages and the process for adding new ones is defined.\r
\r
http://www.xbrl.org/specification/xbrl-2.1/rec-2003-12-31/xbrl-2.1-rec-2003-12-31+corrected-errata-2013-02-20.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3365a49-ed82-439b-99e9-2a1e6d75778e .

camssa:ea8fb0ee-aa6c-4d91-b5f0-5d61420372af a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
