camssa:eaa9be4d-1d6f-4309-861a-1975a4812dde a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ba2cbd6-70b6-46a5-9b57-ef88fb5a6c49 .

camssa:eaab9a5f-bf65-4460-984a-da44b6aba2fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification itself has created a community that share and develop as well as a dedicated platform in Github for sharing results and best practices. Therefore, the specification encourages the creation of open information about the specification and encourages relevant communities from the EU (as well as non-EU communities) to share their results.\r
\r
DCMI About:\r
https://www.dublincore.org/about/\r
\r
DCMI Github:\r
https://github.com/dcmi'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fa9d6959-270c-43b4-b912-d375f990f40f .

camssa:eab3f4f5-73de-44bf-bbd7-6b45624be45d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f851f50-20b2-485a-b454-3d8534301595 .

camssa:eab491bd-0f31-4b4e-91c8-5778c0b64c9f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is primarily focused on describing the interfaces and operations of web services, providing a standardized way to define the contract between service providers and consumers. The specification focuses on the technical aspects of how services can be invoked and what data structures are involved.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e87a9ab-3ec0-439f-a1f0-fefffc736f88 .

camssa:eab8ec53-147d-44d2-b360-79cd809bbff6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """PDF 1.7 has been assessed previously by CAMSS Team using the CAMSS method in the Scenario 2 in the CAMSS Tool v1.0.0. The CAMSS method is fully aligned with the European Standardisation Regulation 1025/2012. As the result of the assessment is positive, PDF can be considered compliant with the European regulation. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/release/camss-assessment-pdf-17/v100"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:897c0582-fa8d-4212-934a-f9872fa37883 .

camssa:eac3f8b7-5c6f-48e4-958a-9467a94c6dd9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs in not included in an open repository/catalogue of standards at national level. However, DIDs is used in eIDAS project, which is a Cross-border project.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:422da380-e80c-4d5e-99cd-96646bda3db7 .

camssa:eac4585c-de38-44aa-8167-1cf8c2ccd3de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68f8e44a-9d66-49f6-acdc-4b0416b4a47f .

camssa:eac6ba18-ef38-47ba-ae3c-f3e387c79c9d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 7498:1 is intended to be a generic and conceptual framework for network communication. Its design and abstraction make it applicable and usable across various business domains. The OSI model provides a structured approach to understanding and developing network protocols, allowing for interoperability between different systems and vendors.

ISO/IEC 7498:1: 
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9dbb490f-1795-413b-8f09-0e8c38fb75f9 .

camssa:eacad4f1-731f-4f9c-b4e6-883d58623040 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """This document provides Best Practices related to the publication and usage of data on the Web designed to help support a self-sustaining ecosystem. Following these Best Practices will facilitate interaction between publishers and consumers. Therefore, this specification does not foster the creation of innovative solutions.\r
\r
W3C Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4009658f-7d4c-456c-8abe-0b4b225a44e6 .

camssa:eacc97b0-ae82-4c6c-867b-37974a82e3dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs can be useful for modeling business processes in public administrations. DIDs addresses the need of  enable individuals and organizations to generate their own identifiers using systems they trust. Moreover, organizations and individuals do not depend of centralized authority.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7da97706-e949-48cf-8be9-a3314915ab22 .

camssa:ead4d5f9-816b-4b4a-92b1-fe70c908e7bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8eb17470327d32b3bb523447fe72ee5c60ddb03e81dae318b485fbe05f48a844 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ead617cf-1631-4b4a-bb37-a0bb9dc94600 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the Core Location Vocabulary is to create a reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics related to people, locations and businesses. By providing a set of information to describe data in the sectors mentioned before, it helps public administrations with the visualization of people, locations or business.\r
\r
CLV Joinup reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-location-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ea69e7f-da5e-49f6-94ef-38b7ab127103 .

camssa:ead88da0-a976-4c8d-8d40-6b4b5d744383 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Syslog protocol is included in the European Commission's Information System Security Policy as part of the standard on logging and monitoring. This standard provides mandatory instructions for the procedures to be used for logging and monitoring on all types of computer systems that are capable of generating information security-related log events, including servers, network equipment, workstations and mobile devices.  Its aim is to ensure that a sound minimum of logging and monitoring is performed consistently across the Commission, without incurring unreasonable costs or administrative burdens.

European Commission Information System Security Policy, STANDARD ON LOGGING AND MONITORING: 
https://extranet.eba.europa.eu/sites/default/documents/files/documents/10180/1449046/4e9f17de-4589-424c-a670-c0cdc1b5f67b/Annex%205%20Standard%20on%20Logging%20and%20Monitoring.pdf?retry=1\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7d96c78-bac6-4cc7-9e92-ed4d3290ae95 .

camssa:eade5ad1-f06a-4dcf-92fb-a0e70998eb13 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:eae250b6-76b8-42a6-b654-73ab842701b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The publiccode.yml specification facilitates the delivery of digital services by providing a structured framework for documenting public sector software. This standardisation enhances interoperability and enables better integration of APIs, thereby improving the efficiency of digital public services. By streamlining access to information and services, it allows public administrations to respond effectively and promptly to user requests, aligning with the EIF’s recommendation to utilise digital channels in service delivery.

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a79a4e87-883f-450d-9550-673d85d3ed53 .

camssa:eae3d126-0e07-4bf4-a3c2-2f1de9ffa92c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ELI´s Task Force team encourages ELI specifications to be available in multiple languages. Therefore,
the specification can be used to a significant extent in a multilingual context. However, the extent to which it
can be used in a specific language would depend on the availability of the specification in that language.

ELI reference:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli-register/about.html

Study on how users of legislation access transposition information:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/eli-register/ELI_usability_study_results-final.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3811cef4-34ca-41be-93e8-94f019111aa6 .

camssa:eae60657-7707-4c97-a41f-b994abfe4af1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SCIM itself does not have explicit language-related features, its extensibility and flexibility allow organizations to adapt the implementation to meet multilingual requirements. The specifics of handling multilingual data may depend on the design and configuration of the identity management system using SCIM and the choices made by the implementing organization.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f86b436-9b7f-41d7-bcc8-8ffead2265f7 .

camssa:eae95935-bc0c-4b19-bc9e-a128fceb219c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including DCAT.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:805e9770-153e-44f9-b2c0-2e32d2f92d66 .

camssa:eaed1422-a5a5-4f10-880f-9bd24ecd00ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TLS 1.3 is a business domain-agnostic protocol, securing communication independently of the application or industry in use. Its handshake protocol establishes encrypted tunnels, guaranteeing confidentiality and integrity for all transmitted data. For instance, HTTPS utilises the secure tunnel established by the TLS handshake to transmit web data.

TLS 1.3 2018 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html

HTTPS Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aeeadb9f-fcdb-40b6-a07b-547f0654f21d .

camssa:eaf1bad4-33e0-4518-af4e-ca1510bbf1da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EN 16234-1 e-CF is not related to data portability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f243d0bf-8f2e-4b2c-b57d-b21383696690 .

camssa:eaf70d78-828e-4036-b369-aee10ea59977 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:eafed13e-ad8f-4d3b-a8d3-02ec5477164b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bb9cc08b-21d3-4283-9c55-d71827971765 .

camssa:eb01df3a-85e1-4c72-9984-d02801b0d192 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS over HTTPS (DoH) primarily focuses on securing the communication between clients and DNS resolvers by encrypting DNS queries and responses. While DoH itself does not define access control mechanisms in the traditional sense, it relies on the existing security mechanisms of the HTTPS protocol, including server authentication through digital certificates.

DoH specification: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bf6ab5c-4219-400b-8547-22a3fab42787 .

camssa:eb03ce89-6b5e-4cd2-8fb3-1be7a840a524 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although ADMS was developed taking into account the perspective of the eGovernment System Development, it is a vocabulary that could be reused beyond this domain. It aims to ease the standardisation of assets description in assets repositories, to enhance the discoverability and reuse of assets and solutions. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e86829f6-bc37-49ab-8913-f7e7b96efc90 .

camssa:eb043fd7-df1a-4a82-a227-e10fc9559698 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By allowing communications over the internet, IPv6 contributes to the exchange of information between public administrations therefore, it reduces administrative burden\r
\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2460"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f863ca8d-979a-4dc1-b901-2b835c40ff34 .

camssa:eb05feab-0d69-4764-8d46-3ea65913662c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISG NFV community is a large community that continues to work intensively on developing the specification and incorporating the latest technologies. This community is open to ETSI members and non-members alike, with different conditions depending on ETSI membership status. The ISG NFV provides continuous support for the correct referencing of NFV specifications (NFVI included) by service providers and open source communities.\r
\r
NFV reference, Our Role & Activities:\r
https://www.etsi.org/technologies/nfv'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66dc2a91-7ef6-402f-b5f4-520389f3ddd3 .

camssa:eb065dbb-6df0-465d-b994-0fd064d72c42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"LDAP has some core functionalities that can't be implemented separately. Nonetheless, the specification \r
has beed developed to support some requirements that are not mandatory but recommended. For example, \r
some security layers such as the SASL can be implemented, but is not required to run the specification. \r
\r
LDAP SASL reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2444\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ebf83ad-05c1-4884-b2b2-1c307c6ca9bd .

camssa:eb098056-b13c-4fca-be7c-edf6a0531376 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b21a3eb972a2119979bc57368474efa809e8dd16cede48bc492e8b64da1abee9 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:eb0aff96-a8bc-4e7a-8af4-0c1b5c5888fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The rules on European standardisation allow the European Commission to identify information and communication technology (ICT) technical specifications - that are not national, European or international standards - to be eligible for referencing in public procurement. This allows public authorities to make use of the full range of specifications when buying IT hardware, software and services, allowing for more competition in the field and reducing the risk of lock-in to proprietary systems.\r
\r
After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, RDF 1.1 has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5caf2aa-0933-4b98-9c2f-e0fb637e9232 .

camssa:eb138bec-79c8-428d-85f6-8273b80301b6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:eb14e8c3-b78b-4d23-93e2-ee23ab436d37 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:eb1505c2-2649-4923-adc2-ea9aef52040e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT specification is designed to transform data from XML into other formats for building such interfaces.

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09ac062f-06a1-4389-ae53-3d5eabf8585a .

camssa:eb161f84-491a-4ea3-a4e8-002486ab22b1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"SFIA was first published in 2000 and was a framework for the ICT community. Between 2001 and 2005, SFIA has gone through a second and third release, in which the specification evolved into a framework that defines the skills and competencies required by business and technology professionals (Slideshare-SFIA reference, SFIA version 4). Since the release of SFIA 4 in 2008, successive versions have been incrementally modified to meet the changing needs of the world-wide ICT sector; a major consultation was held in 2011 through SFIA's online consultation forum (see SFIA reference, Transition to SFIA 5 document). All supporting specification processes for versions five (2011), six (2015), seven (2018) and eight (2021) are publicly available on the 'Moving to SFIA' subsections (see SFIA reference, SFIA 8 section, 'Moving to SFIA 8' subsection, and SFIA reference, Older versions-SFIA 7 section, 'Moving to SFIA 7'-'Summary of changes in SFIA 7' subsection). The specification is therefore sufficiently mature for its use in the development of digital solutions and/or services.\r
\r
Slideshare-SFIA reference, SFIA version 4:\r
https://www.slideshare.net/sfiauser/sfia-version-4\r
\r
SFIA reference, SFIA 8 section, 'Moving to SFIA 8' subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8/moving-to-sfia-8/summary-of-changes-in-sfia-8\r
\r
SFIA reference, Older versions-SFIA 7 section, 'Moving to SFIA 7'-'Summary of changes in SFIA 7' subsection:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/legacy-sfia/sfia-7/moving-to-sfia-7/summary-of-changes-in-sfia-7\r
\r
SFIA reference, Transition to SFIA 5 document:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/legacy-sfia/sfia-5/transition_sfia_5-en.pdf/@@download/file/transition_SFIA_5.en.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e451cc0-fcdf-48ca-aaea-4e6dbfee13de .

camssa:eb17e26e-db28-4d38-bd1f-47e7528a6e72 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no Member State that includes the ETSI TS 119  612 in their national catalogue with Their National Interoperability Framework (NIF) in alignment with the three categories 1. Conceptual model for integrated public servicesprovision, 2. interoperability layers, and 3. interoperability principles.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d1f82da9-ce18-4e6c-94aa-a4d148039042 .

camssa:eb1bc0b6-241c-4d81-85f5-fc57d96adbe2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3fff55dc-63e9-4c79-902f-9b1992ae2578 .

camssa:eb1c2a09-eb52-4c61-8eab-f73c9f0ddc6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The three-letter codes of ISO 639-2 and ISO 639-3 are complementary and compatible. Even if the two codes are designed for different purposes, ISO 639-2 can be considered as an extension of ISO 639-3.\r
\r
ISO 639-3 reference:\r
https://iso639-3.sil.org/about/relationships'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e95cddf-e2c4-4afd-98fc-dd3ba92742a1 .

camssa:eb1df50e-e388-439e-8d29-84907d586219 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:eb2633cc-b623-44d6-bef4-b356420a9230 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPv4 is included in 6 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Croatia, France, Germany, Netherlands, Norway, and Sweden. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Sweden and Netherlands are aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Nonetheless, countries like Germany do not get a high performance.

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards

National catalogue of Netherlands: 
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst

National catalogue of Germany: 
https://www.cio.bund.de/Web/DE/Architekturen-und-Standards/SAGA/SAGA%205-aktuelle%20Version
/saga_5_aktuelle_version_node.html 

National catalogue of sweden:
https://www.avropa.se/globalassets/dokument/open-it-standards.pdf?_t_id=1B2M2Y8AsgTpgAmY7PhCfg%
3d%3d&_t_q=standards&_t_tags=language%3asv%2csiteid%3a95d515a5-23ca-47bf-87a9-

NIFO factsheets:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ffea3958-53b8-4a91-9f7a-96911f6a2cf7 .

camssa:eb28a9a3-eb2b-441a-b6b3-ddb13e6e5722 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-53abe85b1365f86aa58a25566e54e082ea2d70ee8d9fbaf09ccab20af30f3332 ;
