camssa:eb321756-f26e-4271-bdf1-d1830ae7d833 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As described on the Oracle documentation about security settings, the ebXML specification provides authentication and authorisation mechanisms, helping to prevent unauthorised users from making changes to original data or accessing restricted information.

ebXML security:
https://www.oracle.com/technical-resources/articles/enterprise-architecture/ebxml-security1.html

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:280ec7cb-f6ff-40e6-ad80-8b4f0532a672 .

camssa:eb381167-2572-4664-b06e-5a9495d5f18e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IndexedDB can contribute to the client application state storage and can significantly impact the way interfaces are exposed or behave, especially in terms of offline functionality, data persistence, and performance optimisation.

Indexed Database API:
https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1b0840a2-4e02-4789-9c9e-dbe84c6728d8 .

camssa:eb4285bc-5733-4e2b-8d5b-4c9cad43cdf0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Vocabularies are context-neutral\r
semantic building blocks that can be\r
extended into context-specific data models.\r
\r
Handbook for using Core Vocabularies:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/ISA%20Handbook%20for%20using%20Core%20Vocabularies.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b10a5df4-79b7-46bb-afa8-73b524dc805c .

camssa:eb479186-50fa-487d-a91d-486971203582 a cav:Score,
