camssa:ebba70b6-66d3-4a92-a1ce-65ac9a54bb26 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are already existing studies and documents assessing and documenting DQV features and providing 
possible improvements of its performance among other aspects. 
In "DQAF: Towards DQV-Based Dataset Quality Annotation Using the Web Annotation Data Model" it is proposed to use the DQV specification for a Dataset Quality Annotation Framework (DQAF).
Furthermore, there are ducumentation such as "Introducing the Data Quality Vocabulary (DQV)", which makes and assessment of DQV and explains its components as well as how it works. 

"DQAF: Towards DQV-Based Dataset Quality Annotation Using the Web Annotation Data Model" reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/7799649

"Introducing the Data Quality Vocabulary (DQV)" reference:
https://www.semantic-web-journal.net/system/files/swj2079.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55544796-470b-40bd-9054-acf5251b8eaf .

camssa:ebbd9cfd-5e59-45e3-b430-57471722232e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As specification fostering the interoperability between public administrations, RDF helps to enhance the data exchange and reuse in a cross-border way and impacts positively on the development of eGovernment. This fact includes the support to Once-only principle implementation.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50daa8ec-3d9c-4a93-ae9c-5d2b35f0fa0a .

camssa:ebc221b4-8a0b-4c21-a1f9-e419098ce092 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTP provides a framework for access control and authentication, enabling servers to challenge client requests and clients to provide authentication information.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616

HTTP/1.1 Authentication, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#name-http-authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a19f1220-31aa-468e-9bcf-3edde23e7d67 .

