    cav:value "1" .

camssa:eca6eef8-ae6e-4f3e-ba59-f5a2ccbd7d60 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are pilot assessments made in Finland, Nordic countries and Estonia. However these are not official\r
assessments endorsed by XBRL International Inc.\r
\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/wiki/display/CEFDIGITAL/2021/03/22/eInvoicing+helping+standardise+transactional+data+in+Estonia\r
\r
https://www.oecd.org/tax/forum-on-tax-administration/publications-and-products/45045602.pdf : " In their implementation strategy for SAF-T, revenue bodies should consider data formats that\r
permit audit automation today while minimising potential costs to all stakeholders when moving to new\r
global open standards for business and financial data such as XBRL, and XBRL- GL in particular. " page 10\r
\r
https://www2.deloitte.com/content/dam/Deloitte/in/Documents/risk/in-risk-xbrl-the-new-world-of-reporting-noexp.pdf\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2a32edb2-569b-4b35-953d-7931c965b1b4 .

camssa:ecac085a-7a10-41a5-be9b-013c2c6399df a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7aa038b5496afb8cb229c692be9a2adc175deb2d5d47e35ad67e027c9eac28ba ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:ecb206fa-0f9e-4442-87e3-e4e29fa65cf4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The main objective of the Portable Document Format/A (PDF/A) is to allow text format and images to be independent and work for any software, hardware, or operating system while transferring. Additionally, PDF/A is widely used by administrations to share their information and data. Fostering the availability of data and information, it fosters the data portability using documents. Moreover, the PDF/A includes features that impact positively the preservation of the information contained in this format. It is an extended method to ensure the availability of digital information over time."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c5765b8-6b08-4b4f-8a0a-67a78293b5cd .

camssa:ecb2e6e6-7caf-4248-bde1-833fe1e4d11b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of FTPS is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e4debaf-3366-47e4-a05f-325a2a142c9c .

camssa:ecb32480-f8c5-458d-816e-5cc14f860279 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ecb39f04-45ae-4152-b769-d62794db30dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SCIM itself does not provide specific mechanisms for protecting information against unauthorized changes, identity management technologies inherently include access control that allows organisations to define who has permissions to perform specific operations on user identities, which is indirectly enabling data integrity.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfd3330e-3651-44eb-86bb-65b8a186428c .

camssa:ecb8b798-33db-4dfc-a92b-60642ec57cdf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'LDAP is an application protocol for accessing and maintaining distributed directory information services over \r
the net, it is independent of implementation.\r
The specification allows many applications and services to connect to the LDAP server to validate users, \r
which reduces the administrative burden of the system administrators and the users. As it is widely \r
supported the implementation of the LDAP would not hamper the interoperability between systems and \r
services.\r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:25258dde-29f4-40f0-bc99-6df5468c0d8a .

camssa:ecbee570-1b90-435d-82cc-a89657db245c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

