    cav:value "20" .

camssa:ece1c933-b071-4172-a72a-61c86481a60c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in the different official European websites, there is a piece of evidence of a cross-border\r
project that use OCSP involving the usage of the specification.\r
\r
Digital Signature Service framework reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0da2454f-b95e-4d85-9cc5-b2903ea9eea8 .

camssa:ece1ee47-d034-48b5-8478-fb51074c9c9b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ece22959-4f52-4ad6-9928-985fdcc3ee2d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently the specification does not include a public review of the release life-cycle although the specification and its releases are publicly available. This is dependent on the members off the committee involved on the review. 
Any IS/IEC Publicly Available  Standard (PAS) is systematically reviewed every 3 years, the committee members re-asses the standard and propose updates (if necessary). 

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html

ISO public review guide:
https://www.iso.org/files/live/sites/isoorg/files/store/en/PUB100413.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2908e038-165b-41ef-874c-81ee0dc027c4 .

camssa:ece244ae-f2c0-4dc3-ba34-d97ee335df3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification can help guarantee data integrity by providing mechanisms such as digital signatures. In this context, XML digital signatures are used in ebXML to ensure data integrity on messages, existing authentication and authorisation schemes, as well as non-repudiation between entities. As described in the "Secure ebXML Business Transaction Models Applying Web Service Security Standards" article, SAML is recommended to provide identification, authentication, and authorisation, and is often used with XACML to allow or deny access to an XML resource.

Secure ebXML Business Transaction Models Applying Web Service Security Standards:
http://article.nadiapub.com/IJSIA/vol6_no2/46.pdf

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:027af6bc-f2b2-4c8d-8de2-32da74cbe7d6 .

camssa:eced0c98-d774-4325-90a2-b051c1109083 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:ed00b6fb-80d9-4f89-82fc-6fc6cbbb7bc8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 emphasizes the importance of security controls within cloud computing environments. Public Administrations can use the specification as a basis for implementing security controls to protect personal data. This may include measures such as encryption, access controls, data anonymization, and data breach response procedures.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64c2b939-f7e7-447e-aa27-974a7b76d679 .

camssa:ed014f00-b632-44d3-8d1a-900038ffca3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'In accordance with ISO/IEC JTC 1 and the ISO and IEC Councils, these International Standards are publicly available for Standardization purposes.

Publicly Available Standards:
https://standards.iso.org/ittf/PubliclyAvailableStandards/index.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d32285f3-a070-4efc-9f0b-c9399c4b1fc7 .

camssa:ed038d5b-4259-4892-a024-a8e451cc269f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a0101cb11c30c1bbf94adb74479472f2a40c53ccc4b442180fece91506c20a9d ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:ed0c3c9a-19b8-4570-8e8a-0be924ceaed3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SFIA is not related to enabling the long-term preservation of data, information nor knowledge. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed64e358-0a8f-479a-a856-85bc0b1696af .

camssa:ed0f1f48-9ebf-442c-b3fe-5682482a09f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no public consultation foreseen in the development process of the EuroVoc. However, the maintenance team at the Publications Office collects and examines the proposals made by EuroVoc users.\r
\r
EuroVoc Handbook:\r
https://publications.europa.eu/resource/cellar/a2723a83-574f-11eb-b59f-01aa75ed71a1.0001.01/DOC_1\r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54999be6-8f58-4092-ab69-2d3b91cbdf8b .

camssa:ed12c75c-0ee7-4ba7-9a94-09aca212c5d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 511 specifies policy and security requirements for trust service providers providing long-term\r
preservation of digital signatures and general data using digital signature techniques. The specification\r
performance is closely related to the different specifications involved in electronic signatures across borders.\r
In the context of the European internal market (see article below), it can be considered an asset for the\r
creation of solutions enhancing the interoperability between administrations and businesses when\r
eSignature, and long-term preservation of electronic records are needed.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
Article: Towards a standardised preservation service for qualified electronic signatures and qualified\r
electronic seals:\r
https://dl.gi.de/bitstream/handle/20.500.12116/20980/proceedings-01.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6a7b609-99d5-4374-b29c-f77a7ff9bea0 .

camssa:ed13b1ec-3405-48d1-9b4c-0ec8ffd187f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Like all the IETF standards, LDAP is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. LDAP is therefore licensed on a royalty-free basis.\r
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on the LDAP specification (RFC 4511).\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9f6ada4-1f89-45b2-b9d0-94196874f0e9 .

