camssa:ed1fa64c-a0da-4efb-a288-450404606ef5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Even though EuroVoc is mainly focused on eGovernment since it was developed to support the data processing and classification within European Institutions, it covers different domains and subdomains that go beyond eGovernment such as energy or transports. Therefore, it can be considered as reusable amongst other business domains.\r
\r
EuroVoc webpage:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/eurovoc"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e189275c-f56a-4b9d-8f35-d584807351f3 .

camssa:ed215535-5af1-478b-93b0-d9eeffc7fdb7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:ed2778e7-1fda-4da0-a63c-a7fd6605a611 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """UDDI is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, UDDI can define the interoperability aspects of the "Service Discovery Component", "Service Discovery Service", "Service Registration Service "and "Service Registry Component" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/elis/distribution/eliscataloguev100betaxlsx"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d0317767-63ac-449a-bc9d-f564a3581394 .

camssa:ed27851e-477d-45fc-adc2-3af3039b2346 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """CSS v2.1 has had market acceptance for unified web design for years used with HTML which is widely accepted, but with the release of the CSS3 version that uses CSS v2.1 specification as its core, its use has been reduced. CSS3 has implemented some modules and functionalities of the CSS v2.1 specification. Moreover, some modules of CSS3 have been accepted as standard by W3C, for example: CSS Colour Module Level 3 (W3C Recommendation 06 November 2018). \r
\r
CSS v2.1 W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/ \r
\r
CSS Color Module Level 3 W3C reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2018/REC-css-color-3-20180619/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72c2ac29-3d4f-41bf-b5d4-411f5fc850b6 .

camssa:ed27e1f4-5d7b-4d6a-ace5-efd5aef49d33 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:ed2a8747-d538-4a49-aef6-d039efcb3b2a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of this specification is not related to ensuring the protection of personal data managed by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6b12b8d3-9f3a-4ecd-a73e-0b98fc547afb .

camssa:ed2d18cc-c325-4631-a1b5-47755b0910ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """There is no Member State that includes FTPS in their national catalogue with The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:631a6d1c-7d03-4fae-92b9-51950c6ae249 .

camssa:ed34fc1c-ac8e-413d-853e-8b0e3337568b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP does not enable the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1e51b38-0861-4d44-9194-3f0b5dcf645c .

camssa:ed3e91cf-6380-4305-b803-3cf2227c249d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is already associated to the EIRA ABB Ontology in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS).

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/v610'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:baf5438e-79f6-41c1-82d9-6d6b4bef8fdb .

camssa:ed427794-15fd-46b7-b895-c760ab4647b0 a cav:Score,
