        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:eda469bd-a502-49cb-a4ec-faa4bb7bfee7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """FTPS as an extension of FTP, is used for file exchange by some public organisations. By allowing public administration to share information with others, it fosters the visibility of data (e.g. administrative rules, processes etc.) and facilitates public administrations the decision-making. \r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11bf9113-6b3a-4398-b6a1-02391ee0d500 .

camssa:eda7a35e-191e-4b2e-b3e2-41d71550b149 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e9e0cf4a339c837607828404dd0e9b360d643528fcc1df488a95ca67166acea3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:edaa287d-260b-41c4-b5eb-f582f52e12fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently, ELI is associated with EIRA ABBs in the European Library Of Specifications. Specifically, ELI can define the interoperability aspects of the "Legislation Catalogue" ABBs of the EIRA
Legal View, and "Ontology" ABB from the Semantic View.

EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss
/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f2b3b20-1896-4945-af68-e8bb7296f6eb .

camssa:edb07174-df78-4d3d-abc6-31bfa25a9bce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"ebXML allows extensibility or the addition of plugins in the specification's ebRIM and ebRS components. Although such extensibility is limited to some of the ebRIM and ebRS features, ebXML RegRep 4.0 - Part 1 and Part 2 specify how extensibility may be achieved, that is, either by extending ebRIM or modifying the ebRS service interface. It is the case of the ebXML RegRep SWG specification (see ebXML RegRep SWG reference), which is an Open Geospatial Consortium's authoring of the ebXML specification and which deals with the use of geo-data in a variety of contexts.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
ebXML RegRep Part 1, Extending ebRIM section:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/csprd01/regrep-core-rim-v4.0-csprd01.html#__RefHeading__39225_1821683062\r
\r
ebXML RegRep Part 2, Cataloguer Plugin section:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-rs-v4.0-os.html#__RefHeading__32575_422331532\r
\r
ebXML RegRep SWG reference:\r
https://www.ogc.org/projects/groups/ebxmlregrepswg\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32a022f1-967c-4ea0-84f2-bfd2bb660349 .

camssa:edb199d7-43fe-4f51-a608-2cc3fe3cea2f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The adoption of Ogg as a media container format for exchanging data does not hamper the scalability of systems. It is widely adopted for this purpose because it is independent of any platform. \r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b22ae660-5cbe-4946-a1e3-60de44752fd3 .

camssa:edb998b5-41ac-477b-a4c7-a188f3293434 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The main goal of DPV is to develop a taxonomy of privacy terms, which include in particular terms from the new European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in order to ease proof of compliance with the GDPR and related privacy protection regulations.\r
\r
DPV specification: \r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4fbfa08b-69e1-4bae-b17d-f029f9f298ab .

