camssa:ede5b568-792b-4a42-9745-69c44da0dff4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OASIS specifications operate under OASIS IPR Policy, which is aligned with F/RAND principles. Genericode is freely available for anyone to use, implement, and distribute without the need for royalties or licensing fees. In fact, it is often promoted by the standards organisations and industry bodies because of its openess and accessibility.

OASIS Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) Policy: https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:694d0a50-6d68-48bd-b3dc-175c004d5148 .

camssa:eded46f5-f1f6-4358-88e0-4f6886ec1694 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:edede04a-672e-40d5-9f55-20ad2fb793b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PROV family is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, the PROV family can define the interoperability aspects of the "Controlled Vocabulary" "Data", "Data Model", "Data Syntax", "Forms Structure", "Hash Code", "Metadata" and "Ontology ABB of the EIRA Semantic view.\r
\r
ELIS reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/v501'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:da1b080d-5406-443f-b5af-b3e72c0ebedb .

camssa:edef0a79-6881-4be0-862a-9f5d48de618e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:edf46ccf-e7ef-4042-b674-bf2f2e1a9e51 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The message returned by a Service Metadata Publisher service is signed using one or more [XML-DSIG1] XML-Signatures. Moreover, the purpose of the specification is to ease and ensure the discoverability of different parties to exchange the desired information. The specification defines a set of requirements regarding the authentication of parties that ensures secure and trustworthy data exchange.\r
\r
The specification:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505000"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d7a66dd-20be-4133-a921-2f903ff6d9ca .

camssa:edf560c5-b90a-4ee4-81dd-05026c2bccf1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:edf67222-3567-40d4-b527-64f275767a7d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification conformance could be tested against a manual checking or even implementing a schematron validator based on the specification data model to check it's implementation.\r
 \r
CCCEV:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary/about\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:33166213-14ee-4785-8e82-58eb7fbad40c .

