        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of SOAP 1.2 is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0340383e-e9e8-462a-a8bf-28a9f2622da7 .

camssa:ee6f4485-eafe-43a4-9f17-e48d5287aed6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
\r
Internet Best Current Practices IETF:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d77c1d68-e52a-4fdf-b9b7-c020561fc37c .

camssa:ee6f4f6a-debd-4b5c-be34-3d9c06b5562b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'GITB TDL provides a framework for testing the efficient and secure processing  of information/data. See an example of this characteristics in the reference provided:\r
\r
GITB TDL example reference: ASiC container validation for eTendering processes\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/examples/index.html#example-7-asic-container-validation-for-etendering-processes'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ebef83b5-e9bd-479e-85e0-8674c6031292 .

camssa:ee720baa-ac6d-4750-8b75-a869a75f0732 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'EN 16234-1 e-CF does not foresee public reviews. There is no direct evidence that a public review is conducted according to the CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" and IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) documentation.\r
\r
CEN/TC 428 "ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences" Business Plan 2022 reference:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/BPCEN/1218399.pdf\r
\r
IT Professionalism Europe (ITPE) reference, Archive section:\r
https://itprofessionalism.org/resource-library/reports-publications/archive/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34c6913f-300a-469f-ae3c-3319f3922e9f .

