camssa:eed192f4-f83f-4bbb-8a27-492d8c7f8f96 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Schema.org allows for partial implementation as long as the schema implementation is conformant with the specification requirements, namely those requirements concerning the schema data structure. The schema.org project highly recommends the use of authoring schema validators.\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Data model section, Conformance section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/datamodel.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca192d0f-5993-4ce4-8e44-5f1dc9c9ddce .

camssa:eed2a23a-2d6a-4a8c-9d95-b91065931ede a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:eed51c64-d911-4be5-b79e-e0e0ea6925c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Extensibiltiy is one of the key factors that make LDAP a popular standard protocol. LDAP functionalities can be extended depending on the developer needs. Common extensions are the SASL Authentication mechanism or the Dynamic Password Verifiers. 

LDAP IETF Extension:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/ldapext/about/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7eb1785b-0048-4d7a-9189-88c5125890a8 .

camssa:eedc446b-1acf-4d90-b9a8-d7f39f3cd364 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is the standardised digital representation of an asset. The AAS may be the logical representation of a simple component, a machine or a plant at any level of the equipment hierarchy. The specification can contribute to the visibility of manufacturing processes and the generated data to the administrators. In this sense the specification helps the different partners modulate their manufacturing processes to the same specifications and make any given part interchangeable. 

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7fcf90e-68b3-44c2-9b60-019b98aaedfd .

camssa:eeebc107-3a57-4954-8778-67e01f3bb029 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:eeed1a10-d0b0-421e-b287-8b4678b53767 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"In the specification's documentation there is no mention to customisation.\r
\r
SMP OASIS reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/bdxr/bdx-smp/v2.0/cs02/bdx-smp-v2.0-cs02.html#_Toc30505009\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:002086cc-0d51-4169-a10d-e675fa187cec .

camssa:eef0a3dc-4026-4abd-8e5b-82e90fd57b8d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 addresses and enables the implementation of features to guarantee data accuracy. For instance, it guarantees data accuracy by providing a interface capable of warning if it cannot accurately present all parts of the SD according to the data content type when the SCASC presents the document to the signer. 

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0ef4dedc-9de3-4f19-ac61-db58f8b1e310 .

camssa:eef28bdc-62c1-4e29-8046-c27e65609264 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f41cca0d171e6f64dbc2bdeae9fbc87f2ea51ac00185b22114d59ab8a06e78d0 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:eef79c09-a5d5-4943-aabe-a0ddf823b352 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SCIM is based on web standards, particularly RESTful principles and JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) for data representation. This design choice makes it easy to integrate SCIM with different platforms that support HTTP-based communication and JSON data format. As a result, SCIM can be implemented in a wide range of environments.

SCIM: https://scim.cloud/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea9ecd95-af52-4aa0-8332-fda9da0f1b2d .

camssa:eefcd568-4276-4812-b83d-853c739ec3b9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-52e41801b0db7274d934a229fee15e657273655d70d448d16706fcbe0e4f9746 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:eefdc714-d92f-4e91-9283-8b8c2344a47d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OpenTelemetry specification is primarily designed for observability, focusing on the collection and analysis of telemetry data such as traces, metrics, and logs from software systems.  Modelling business processes typically involves higher-level concepts and frameworks that go beyond the scope of network protocols like OTel.

OpenTelemetry: https://opentelemetry.netlify.app/docs/specs/otel/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae2ec506-9618-467a-8036-7b4b45a1df48 .

camssa:ef002939-e3a7-431b-8dd0-210734f17b31 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100" .

