https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:208760b8-af90-485a-97c6-97b4dad35aa9 .

camssa:eff47e90-9e4b-488c-97d1-65ac0f76c30e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP Cookies is the most widely used standard protocol serving essential functions on the web such as storing stateful information on the user's device or tracking the user's browsing activity. The first version of HTTP Cookies was released on 1997, oundergoing several improvements until the last version from 2011. Therefore, we can say that HTTP Cookies is sufficiently mature for the development of products and services.\r
\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265\r
\r
HTTP Cookies first release:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2109\r
\r
Google Analytics reference:\r
https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/analyticsjs/cookie-usage?hl=es#analyticsjs\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:247cbaab-ff5a-403d-b7a8-a44ba6b08810 .

camssa:eff717da-5f52-4924-91cf-6139ea87a18d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Like all the IETF standards subject to the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents, OCSP\r
is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web\r
Foundation. Therefore, OCSP is licensed under (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
Intellectual Property Rights in IETF, section 8:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3668\r
\r
IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents: \r
http://trustee.ietf.org/license-info\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a34e15a1-2aee-40d3-8782-3485422f771c .

camssa:f001df7a-1b52-4dec-b587-443094a11658 a cav:Score,
