camssa:f002c7c2-adc4-4e2a-b916-75ba86991048 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL is a standard language that makes digital content rules clear, uniform and easy to automate across \r
systems ensuring transparent and controlled access to content or services. Furthermore, the specification is \r
designed to address administrative procedures, rules data, and services related to the management of digital \r
rights. By providing interoperable vocabulary, model and encoding mechanisms, the specification contributes \r
to the standardisation of the statements and conditions of use for public services and improves the \r
comprehensibility of administrative services.\r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef8c5689-cadf-4685-8473-30b91ff9b40c .

