camssa:f0d6f067-1bcd-4f7d-9aa6-ebc25c5d1db5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP is only recommended by the  Member State of France. The Référentiel général d'interopérabilité (RGI) currently has AMQP "under observation", meaning that if the experiments prove conclusive, it will be included in a subsequent version of the General Interoperability Framework Status Explanation as "recommended". Otherwise, it will be "withdrawn" from the repository.

Référentiel général d'interopérabilité (RGI) Reference:
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf

NIFO Factsheets:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a0fb5a84-a5f7-44ab-96d9-9d6f82865a24 .

camssa:f0d9a57e-3512-465c-9816-b284f83c2af4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f0dd7bef-30a6-4e61-82db-e9c3ff45381d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NFVI fosters and simplifies the digital exchange in network specific domains. Wireless network, e.g. 5G, deployment is a domain case where the NFVI specification is being considered at a European level. The counterside is that this specification has to be deployed collectively by all Public Administrations.\r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview section 7.3:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/ \r
\r
5G NFV whipe paper:\r
http://portal.etsi.org/NFV/NFV_White_Paper_5G.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef63be60-0583-4a19-afa5-27fd3fdc0586 .

camssa:f0e1a06d-d273-4498-9fee-b8b18149364b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Even though EIRA is not a business process modelling tool, withing the organisational view, Public Administrations are able to identify which is the delivery model, the agents, the capability, services and information involved. By establishing the traceability with other views, users can establish the relationship between elements at different levels such as semantic or technical, helping to provide a comprehensive approach of how are services going to be provided and the different components involved. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8fc739b7-15bb-492c-a90c-adf9750199b6 .

