camssa:f10fecd6-6620-4b2e-9c74-c3a232dc3ff9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """​The Semantic Interoperability Community (SEMIC) that developed this specification, is in charge of developing solutions to help European public administrations perform seamless and meaningful cross-border and cross-domain data exchanges. They develop semantic specifications and interoperability solutions under the ISA² Programme. When a new solution release is finished, it is submitted for a public review with a minimum period of four weeks.\r
\r
Specification development process by the ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/document/description-change-management-release-and-publication-process-structural-metadata-specifications\r
\r
Detailed document ISA Programme:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2016-10/description_of_a_change_management_release_and_publication_process_for_structural_metadata_specifications_developed_by_the_isa_progr.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a95cb43e-b93d-43aa-9bac-86b5b1255002 .

