    cav:refersTo camssa:be6345b3-2ca6-4e43-90c4-7000ed092fd0 .

camssa:f15cc2cc-ab6c-4164-a0dd-516f3787fb12 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There have been found some academic papers assessing the use of DPV in terms of efficiency. These documents describe the use of DPV personal data handling policies and information about consent (see Personal Data Handling in Multi-Agent Systems Interaction) or assess the efficiency when it comes to discover the relevant information in privacy policies by means of integrating the knowledge represented in the DPV with the information modelled in BabelNet.\r
\r
Personal Data Handling in Multi-Agent Systems Interaction:\r
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-49778-1_5\r
\r
The role of Vocabulary Mediation to Discover and Represent Relevant Information in Privacy Policies:\r
http://ebooks.iospress.nl/doi/10.3233/FAIA200851,'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:44934ce6-841e-47f6-a77c-d3980ebe557b .

camssa:f15e870b-c455-4916-889a-40f117612e6c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f1635eab-58a4-401c-aab3-06cba06fa668 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/b40340d4-9199-4972-b490-883a30c6573b"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:f163c076-2650-48df-ac90-45e66617ef6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to the 5 star Open Data model suggested by Tim Berners-Lee about how to publish linked data, schema.org is a structured data mark-up schema enabling search engines and other information systems to query data in a structured manner. As well as supporting the publication of data as open data, the specification facilitates the publication of public data as open data since it fulfils all the requirements to generate Linked Data.\r
\r
Schema.org reference, Getting started section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/gs.html\r
\r
Tim Berners-Lee 5-star schema for Open Data:   \r
https://5stardata.info/en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:354e0078-b0f6-44f5-933a-6ce420ecc909 .

camssa:f1684eb9-80dd-4a4e-895f-7aa975c26300 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f16ae3ac-b58a-4b36-bdfa-d293e1be8187 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f172bdda-75d9-4266-a4e9-ea153eb73022 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5879b43fc249f0098f3ed687235f432f71bf0c11bd3aa95e063dfdacd64606c8 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f173a64a-58eb-4188-9a91-037a86b93330 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec enables implementation of different profiles, which involve a set of specific requirements depending on the context of implementation: integration into the native IP stack, or "underneath" an existing implementation of an IP protocol stack.\r
\r
IPSec reference, Where IPSec can be implemented:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#section-3.3'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6290873a-ed36-42d2-975f-5d23feaa05ad .

camssa:f1762c65-64a7-4930-aa8f-08731e4e7191 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI TS 119 432 does not mention any specific action to support the reuse of relevant information when needed. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

ETSI TS 119 432: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119400_119499/119432/01.02.01_60/ts_119432v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0cb8f07-3749-4586-a87e-7ca06cdfb5b8 .

camssa:f17b3526-84f4-40b9-b6a4-110c60f04986 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification can contribute to the implementation of the once-only principle by setting the principles to manage and reduce the risk related to the information being exchanged between parties. In this sense, by securing and establishing the methods to control and reduce risks when treating sensitive information the specification can contribute, enhance and enable the implementation of the once-only principle.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 27001 reference website:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/54534.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:91c08f6c-6c6d-4f3d-b4a8-e5b104aefc04 .

camssa:f17cc768-2ef3-4481-b8c0-d92add8a0b96 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3671439b412291ce208a0ade6313c64aeb2942059c7543ca39322c56458bcf96 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f17e9dc5-3255-4ae2-afc7-8fa58e1569c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of the specification is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, e-Delivery SMP 1.10 is not easing the e-accessibility. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c0d2c94-e1fd-4ea2-8119-60e3d755cdc0 .

camssa:f18d8ee2-2e5b-4566-81bc-0d761ffacf10 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f18f5b70-95dc-47cc-95ef-10f7492423b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f19591cd-1d3f-4bc6-afec-6c8124bfa1ca a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-39e7870e79b2999a8b61c97f0c356312b88174320d6464fce5639e57ec0de011 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f1986aca-0dab-4b55-8354-6f0e91d6601b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to scope comprehensibly the administrative procedures, rules data and services, therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:26f91eac-523b-4b23-92fa-fea995836eb7 .

camssa:f199199e-cea6-4993-a412-ab9d61272b6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Although TIFF/IT’s purpose is not to foster the visibility of administrative data or services, it can help with the visualization and visibility of public administrations by providing high quality images and print-ready pages that can be easily edited later. \r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html\r
\r
TIFF/IT explanation:\r
https://www.prepressure.com/library/file-formats/tiffit"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:06eb40ee-0112-4d21-a638-2e266877b4f2 .

camssa:f19a1b44-6418-4b9f-9880-6e2862ffeae6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """LegalDocML is aimed to define a common data and metadata model towards the maximisation of information reuse. It is focused on administration purposes mainly for public administrations, but it also can be extended to more specific sectors requiring legal document management and processing.\r
\r
LegalDocML reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/legaldocml/charter.php"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:441c55eb-bb6c-4192-9323-149f3f3d2c54 .

camssa:f19bcbcb-bf40-4c62-8838-220c34fc2c62 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """When XHTML became W3C recommendation it had a good acceptance, but when HTML5 appeared, its use has been decreased considerably. In the following link there is a comparison of usage of the different HTML languages and it can be seen that XHTML 1.0 is declining more and more while HTML5 is increasing.\r
\r
XHTML trend:\r
https://try.powermapper.com/Stats/HtmlVersions"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bbeb5e5d-f7ca-4efc-8430-2342d1bc4009 .

