camssa:f1e5de4e-664b-4473-be82-ecfc2f072dc7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the purpose of Dataspace Protocol is not related to enabling digital service delivery channels directly, providing a common framework for the creation of IDS can improve data exchange between systems that implement digital services, improving effectiveness and efficiency.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/overview/readme'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0574b223-cbc5-4ee5-92b4-c87db769492b .

camssa:f1ea8438-4aa0-48cf-a404-e3d7bbb221b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currenlty OSI is used at European level and promoted through the Interoperable europe portal. Given that it can be implemented via different layers it gives the flexibility necessary to have a wide presence in multiple services via partial implementations.

OSI on the Interoperable Europe Portal
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/isoiec-7498-11994-information-technology-open-systems-interconnection-basic-reference-model-basic

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d3afc8c-1da1-48cd-accc-d18fa9d5e266 .

camssa:f1eabc8d-d37e-4c5d-b4e9-c303b47110a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI, the SDO/SSO that created and currently maintains the SAREF ontology, explains that most ETSI test specifications are developed according to the well-proven methodology defined in ISO/IEC 9646. This standard, which covers the entire test development process, provides an excellent basis for the production of high-quality test frameworks and specifications.

ETSI Conformance Testing: 
https://portal.etsi.org/Services/Centre-for-Testing-Interoperability/ETSI-Approach/Conformance'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05865ba7-b2e6-4083-b4e2-4e3ea115e156 .

camssa:f1ecd4ce-849e-41c3-ba01-1298da6add34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"TLS 1.3 specification permits extensions to provide further customisation and add features to the core protocol. For example, The ClientHello message includes several customisable extensions, enabling the client to communicate its specific preferences and capabilities. Additionally, TLS can facilitate the integration of extensions such as Server Name Indication (SNI), which allows a client to specify the hostname of the server to which it is connecting. This is important for servers that host multiple virtual domains on a single IP address. Without SNI, the server wouldn't know which certificate to present, leading to potential security errors. 

TLS 1.3 Extensions reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html#section-4.2\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:108185c8-51bf-40a9-a12e-01c25c9e52a4 .

camssa:f1ece261-3a9b-4651-bf12-d704e3bf757c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'BFO is independent of any specification and can be implemented without dependencies with technologies.

BFO reference:
https://www.iso.org/standard/74572.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6c3d09dd-6e0b-4d13-84b0-e093c2e260f6 .

camssa:f1f0aef1-7da5-4b02-9289-21f58956fd7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The OASIS Technical Committee, in charge of the development of XACML, operates under RF on RAND Mode of the OASIS IPR Policy. The specification is licensed on a Royalty-free and (F)RAND basis.\r
\r
OASIS IPR:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/security/ipr.php\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/ipr"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c09732fa-b01e-494a-acec-fb791e4a1c42 .

