camssa:f1f87b4f-a348-4894-841c-e64809c8ef3f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is designed to facilitate the creation and exchange of legal documents in a machine-readable format, which includes administrative procedures, rules data, and services. By providing a common framework for the representation of legal documents, it enables greater visibility and accessibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services.                           Specifically, the specification  enables the creation of structured legal documents that include information about the administrative procedures, rules data, and services contained within them.\r
\r
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    AKN4EU reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:739439c3-407d-439d-ad15-b019eac5837b .

camssa:f1f92926-829d-4951-94a6-49cb926c6ec9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"EU Member States' trusted lists were established in the EU and are primarily aimed at supporting the validation of advanced electronic signatures that are backed by a qualified certificate, as well as advanced electronic signatures supported by both a qualified certificate and a secure signature creation device. These trusted lists include, at a minimum, trust services that are supervised or accredited to issue qualified certificates. This approach explicitly facilitates the secure and trustworthy exchange of data, as it relies on advanced electronic signatures supported by a qualified certificate and a secure signature creation device.

ETSI TS 119 612:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/119612/02.02.01_60/ts_119612v020201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:278ca09c-8da3-46c9-bb94-86264d4eaa7f .

camssa:f206075c-bad3-47e5-a646-7d344a7c3a32 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of SAMM is not related to the visibility of administrative information, data or services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org/\r
\r
SAMM documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:020122c1-14bc-48e5-b320-8368b922cb3d .

camssa:f206eb27-6555-4cbe-adb8-d440661185d3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f207be01-ca00-42bf-8bd7-196fac936b62 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-73a8058bec757a2fdb0f8513c2f11841e982cbef76c3be82af67707c294da8b8 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f209f823-b5b4-4133-a725-bbd34fe5bd95 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of NUTS is not related to facilitating the publication of open data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. \r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e05ab56-8b86-4194-bad3-2a68aece4f3a .

camssa:f20dfead-04a3-4fa5-a937-6829b482d9b7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17edaee27de1ada5f8ee772a0aff160ecdce7a05ce9db18b9a2025f463d0e3a7 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:f212c612-be81-40d0-a564-bbb8a386de6f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Schema.org can scope the comprehesibility of administrative procedures, rules data and services on European websites. The specification favours the promotion of semantic interoperability between different applications, basing its logic on the reuse of existing controlled vocabularies and potential mappings to existing metadata vocabularies. The specification will be used along with another specification, DCAT, in order to propose a common DCAT schema (DCAT-AP-SDO, Schema.org profile of DCAT Application Profile for Data Portals in Europe) enabling administrations and citizens to find and understand datasets located in the European Union and all Member States' data portals.\r
\r
Schema.org homepage reference, 'Documentation' section:\r
https://schema.org/docs/documents.html\r
\r
DCAT reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/\r
\r
DCAT-AP-SDO reference:\r
https://ec-jrc.github.io/dcat-ap-to-schema-org/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c16d2fdd-12fa-495d-98e7-605047f2ce04 .

camssa:f2167050-1ef7-44b0-905e-23ad4c98d18d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As its name states, it is a Reference Architecture. It is the basis for the analysis and design of Digital Public Services in different areas. The specification provides wide range of flexibility, allowing users create solution architecture templates based on EIRA but with Architecture Building Block specific to users needs, or extensions/specialisations of these ABBs. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cfe7be2b-6aff-4a3a-bc1a-ae8b2580a950 .

camssa:f217164b-1f04-42d5-9b74-77c20594f7e3 a cav:Score,
