camssa:f24b5bb6-d5cc-44a1-8808-e5d4c48b1801 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The modularity of ODRL allows the implementation to the specific needs of a particular application or use \r
case. Users can focus on the aspects of the standard that are most relevant to their digital rights management requirements. This flexibility is beneficial because different industries and applications may \r
have diverse needs when it comes to expressing and managing digital rights.\r
\r
An example of this extension is the work done within the scope of SERAMIS project, which is a GDPR \r
validation tool that uses an ODRL extended model as basis for the validation. \r
\r
SERAMIS: \r
https://cordis.europa.eu/docs/projects/cnect/2/612052/080/deliverables/001-D55v4GDPR.pdf\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df2d0ac2-353a-4d21-97cf-b1d45bbb4513 .

camssa:f24dd727-a822-44af-a541-135cb2eb1508 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:f2520794-1f38-4b30-860d-bbc3c558f85f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2573254-afa6-4d36-a4f0-bbd6d78c9446 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ESI/REM is not related to the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data and services, \r
therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:435b57fd-d1c5-4797-8e35-e64fac2ab25f .

camssa:f25e4ab5-39f5-4bdc-b91a-2be9839172f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'According to section 4.4 of the documentation, ETSI TS 119 511 provides an interface between users and\r
preservation services, however, specific provisions are fully achieved if it is combined with its companion\r
documents ETS TS 119 512 therefore, enabling the visibility of administrative procedures, rules and services\r
if combined with other specifications.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 511 specification:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119511/01.01.01_60/ts_119511v010101p.pdf\r
\r
TR-ESOR Preservation of Evidence of Cryptographically Signed Document:\r
https://www.bsi.bund.de/SharedDocs/Downloads/DE/BSI/Publikationen/TechnischeRichtlinien/TR03125/BSI_TR_03125_Anlage_PEPT_V1_2_1_higher.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1d772e46-0e74-4c39-8f4f-6ca32e2d0a42 .

camssa:f25f0097-6e28-41a5-beba-34360e40061c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 27001 defines security aspects for information in IT systems, it is a key element when designing business processes and the requirements that the system and the organisation will need to meet.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 27001 reference website:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/54534.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1dfcac5c-2192-482e-b978-2e62988fe6c0 .

camssa:f25f7e25-b04f-4078-a1cb-c840215661bb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

