camssa:f2687fe8-042a-409e-987b-5e899cdf92e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The simplification of the delivery of public services is not on how they are deliver, it starts with the analysis and design phase of these services. There is where EIRA is meant to focus and support the simplification of European public services. 

The holistic approach of the specification ensures that there is a translation between legal requirements into the technical implementations. By providing different perspectives to different aspects such how services interact between them, how information is transferred, how user can send/receive information, EIRA can help public administrations to develop services that are completely aligned with their needs and expectations, including delivery channels that are more appropriate given the conditions of each Public Administration. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9eb9348c-5fe3-4d9e-9806-bf466d25ad95 .

camssa:f27f1710-d2da-463c-94e2-3266c0fb2364 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion does not apply.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9315a96a-b5a4-403c-a930-d44706cf82d7 .

camssa:f281672a-bb2f-4f7b-8f3d-f5298f5cbfd4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69dbbbfc4ff4c79244a3bd99f7c3f883f2a7114ec515cb4d576f0d807c94b9fd ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2816c62-f4f5-4b30-b0cf-0adaad98642a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There have been found some academic papers assessing the use of DPV in terms of effectiveness. These documents describe the use of DPV personal data handling policies and information about consent (see Personal Data Handling in Multi-Agent Systems Interaction) or assess the effectiveness when it comes to discover the relevant information in privacy policies by means of integrating the knowledge represented in the DPV with the information modelled in BabelNet.

Personal Data Handling in Multi-Agent Systems Interaction:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-49778-1_5

The role of Vocabulary Mediation to Discover and Represent Relevant Information in Privacy Policies:
http://ebooks.iospress.nl/doi/10.3233/FAIA200851,'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bbbd84a0-fad1-4d3b-9ee3-780bfe8d3a88 .

camssa:f281a47c-3f46-40b1-8ce0-5ea504252a0f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-02333ef99fbcb4f101a106bcf97c9559888756b085b1729b7c2ac9626dc4bc63 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f284f92c-99ab-493b-8883-924c99d1e2cc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2856f31-5437-4e82-b9c5-e2d247cab4fc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XHTML has been used by the EU comission in the context of the publication of regulations (EURLEX), in this
sense the proposal for a regulation on reduction of legal and administrative obstacles in a cross border
context is a prime example of it's use.

XHTML implementation by Eur-lex:
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:52018PC0373&from=EN\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e725e7b2-7913-4a55-ab05-5e0954e5e2eb .

camssa:f286c9d9-0aa3-412e-925f-49c8fef48f36 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx is built around RDF and is highly dependent from it since its purpose is to  validate RDF graphs. Nonetheless, it has many known implementations that range through a variety of business domains allowing for RDF graphs validation across business domains.\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc73cc47-29e4-4646-99ac-a1607df3aeb3 .

camssa:f28748cc-76d4-44c5-818e-433228a55c4d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The NFVI ensures the deployment and execution of Virtualised Network Functions (VNFs). The specification spans across multiple locations where data centres are operating. Connectivity between these locations is considered part of the specification.\r
\r
NFVI Deliver, Infrastructure Overview:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gs/NFV-INF/001_099/001/01.01.01_60/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07fe1eb4-1ecf-4bd0-83d0-bbb1a10904bc .

camssa:f28790e9-51fa-4577-9d5e-aa5282ac9698 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/1f8dff5a-5661-4657-a894-c4c44fc32f5b"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:f28c8963-b4ce-4e5f-8d12-597af9d00c58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary facilitates organisational interoperability agreements primarily by providing a common vocabulary and a consistent semantic framework for describing legally registered organisations. This enables different systems and organisations, particularly business registers, to understand and exchange information about these entities in a more standardised way.

Registered Organization Vocabulary specification reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:684c833c-fd27-458f-9316-49fc06c5fbab .

camssa:f293e675-21da-49a1-9dd4-6bc1b5d6b77e a cav:Score,
