    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f29b897f-50b8-46a2-8cab-6fe16ac3b619 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies proposing the usage of ODRL as an efficient method for representing more fine-grained access policies for Linked Data. \r
\r
Moreover, there are studies that also checked the completion of the specification and its actual implementation and providing other formal semantics to improve the application of the specification and its purpose.\r
\r
Defining Expressive Access Policies for Linked Data using the ODRL Ontology 2.0:\r
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Simon-Steyskal/publication/266652655_Defining_expressive_access_policies_for_linked_data_using_the_ODRL_ontology_20/links/565dc7a408aeafc2aac88d98/Defining-expressive-access-policies-for-linked-data-using-the-ODRL-ontology20.pdf\r
\r
Formalising ODRL Semantics using Web Ontologies: \r
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235902060_Formalising_ODRL_Semantics_using_Web_Ontologies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96a76f7a-86b1-4860-8cf3-35fad3e30c63 .

camssa:f2a8656c-7b8e-468b-aefe-7972b5c7aa14 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Data on the Web Best Practices gives some advice on how to publish data on the web. It encourages and enables the continued expansion of the Web as a medium for the exchange of data. It does not directly foster the visibility of data, but the usage of this best practice can help to implement solutions to foster the visibility of data and services of public administration.\r
\r
Data on the Web Best Practices W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:df28dd50-c76a-45b2-9bd5-ead1c5b6ff3a .

camssa:f2aa5203-e70d-45bb-a83c-d26ff4465673 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2b3279e-8958-42bb-b951-6aeb541042a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is aimed to participate in the evaluation of access policies, participating in authentication processes that can ease the secure and trustworthy exchange of data. An example of this fact is the European project SEMIRAMIS, a pilot infrastructure to provide e-services with the required underlying secure authentication\r
\r
SEMIRAMIS project: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/semiramis/about"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fb7a42cc-b413-4c98-acc5-2bf725b9485b .

camssa:f2bcd4a8-9080-4814-bffd-1d65d1766a71 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f2bd9a77-3758-489e-a31d-21fac9111252 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As defined on the OASIS Technical Committee (TC), only TC members are involved in the development of \r
the UBL specification. External contribution to this committee is possible through open channels.\r
\r
UBL OASIS Technical Committee reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ubl\r
\r
UBL v2.3:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d668d7f7-c4e8-43c3-931d-a222640f0f47 .

camssa:f2be1936-87e4-4743-b59b-fdf85a513265 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-093c1e09f5a65e4cba0247dcab5a8f4854f3e512db336b1855b9a4c48d3659e0 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f2be6510-a976-4ee8-9769-ac5e884fd8f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISO 639-2 code suite was developed to be used by libraries, information services and publishers to indicate language in the exchange of information, especially in computerised systems. It can foster data portability in the context of a an interoperability solution (e.g., the ADMS from the ISA Programme).\r
\r
ISO 369-2 FAQs:\r
https://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/faq.html#5\r
\r
ADMS ISA Programme reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/document/2013-06/Case%20Study%20-%20%20How%20to%20describe%20semantic%20interoperability%20assets%20in%20an%20ADMS%20compliant%20way%20-%20v1.06.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aa8583a5-4306-41e1-8168-e9ec1fa9b92f .

camssa:f2c7d7bc-a1dd-4ba9-837a-f8c98a12e01b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2cc2488-5932-482c-9c12-1df7ba0ea70a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f2ce62a0-3877-4507-82d8-62076a707a53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specifications first version was released in 2012, since then, it has undergone one major release, being now the version 2.0.0 In the TGF OASIS technical committee, there can be found information about the change management and release management processes.\r
\r
TGF Technical Committee:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=tgf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:893b218c-b4d5-4643-8d25-d148ad9bf46b .

camssa:f2d073bb-1d02-4e65-a7de-615ce4ff06eb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f2d15b9f-459a-4a95-9b84-c991f571e409 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of iCalendar is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
iCalendar specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83e191b0-602a-46aa-a71f-667a0160c38e .

camssa:f2d255f0-4dba-4e9f-bc48-769809f04686 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP specification can be used in a multilingual context. AMQP uses IETF language tags. These tags are used to specify the language of informational text, including connection, session, and link error descriptions but  implementations should understand at least the en-US language tag. (Refer to section 2.8.12 IETF Language Tag)

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cac496be-ebfb-4e57-8b30-bf469ff7d049 .

camssa:f2d6e880-34d6-4ad5-81a8-1a17399aef99 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """As a protocol for data exchange, FTP allows the provision of data using an endpoint and therefore makes available interfaces of public administrations internal information systems.\r
\r
An example of implementation support this fact would be the Flemish initiative MAGDA. This initiative provides a platform that allows the different administrations to reuse the information contained within their registries. FTP has been selected by MAGDA to enable data exchange between the different administrations. \r
\r
See: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/magda-platform/about\r
https://cordis.europa.eu/project/rcn/198414/factsheet/en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a35ec293-cf18-49fa-9a93-34a772f58bb3 .

camssa:f2d88702-b15c-45c5-a72a-3e61bfb62d7b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f2d8ab5b-137c-40fd-94e2-38126edb7a46 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/9d34f9f5-0558-4973-bc7c-657dde93d240"^^xsd:anyURI .

