camssa:f306a51d-53fa-439a-9aeb-40de3a75c5c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specifiation is the foundation for many different innovative solutions. For instance, syslog-ng, developed 
byBalabit IT Security Ltd, is a log management solution that improves the performance Security Information 
and Event Management (SIEM) solution by reducing the amount and improving the quality of data feeding 
the SIEM for Unix and Unix-like systems. It is widely adopted by many applications and devices, facilitating 
interoperability.

Syslog-ng: https://www.syslog-ng.com/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e105d664-ced6-47e7-8152-3bc44ac3c5a6 .

camssa:f306e486-f257-476a-ac25-691a745ca878 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f30787d1-ab5f-409a-a507-d176bfb9fa21 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Registered Organization Vocabulary is not included in any Member States' catalogues of recommended specifications.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/

CAMSS list of standards:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/camss-list-standards

NIFO factsheets:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:baf49da0-9bfa-4cb3-b527-8577a2440e8f .

camssa:f30adf3f-b4f5-416e-be9f-96a26cf442fa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the moment of performing this assessment, Linked Open Data portals are innovative solutions adopted by public administrations all around Europe. DCAT-AP fosters the implementation of Five-Star Linked Open Data by allowing users to discover interlinked information from other portals. \r
\r
European Data Portal:\r
http://data.europa.eu/euodp/en/home\r
\r
Joint research center data catolgue:\r
http://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/\r
\r
DCAT-AP - a key for European data publishers to reach the data consumers and create a European open data ecosystem:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/dcat-ap-key-european-data-publishers-reach-data-consumers-and-create-european-open-data-ecosystem_en/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88729dfb-1033-4e6d-8f88-aae3f7acd06c .

camssa:f30c2f66-5054-41fb-8546-92f0afa11a69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As it happens with all the e-Government Vocabularies, SEMIC is the responsible for the maintenance of the development.

SEMIC in Interoperable Europe Portal:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:905da7f2-75e9-4892-91a3-ed05811cf7cb .

camssa:f310cb2c-7441-4265-9193-5d26e6736202 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Since 1990, HTTP has been developed based on practical experience and extensive feedback from developers and organisations, demonstrating significant market acceptance. Major version releases, including HTTP/2 and HTTP/3, have been developed, each offering specific benefits and limitations depending on the context of use. All three major versions relies on the semantics defined by the original specification, and implementations are expected to choose the most appropriate transport and messaging syntax for their particular needs.

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1: Semantics, RFC 9110 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2ab3d88e-e7c5-42b1-822d-275e463b7128 .

camssa:f3123ce9-9c6d-4fd8-a03b-29133a093a8b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f314ff9f-600f-4f8f-ad00-e1819615cdcf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON is included in 9 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Cyprus, Denmark, Finland, France, Iceland, Malta, The Netherlands, Slovakia and Slovenia. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of France and The Netherlands is fully alignes with at least 2 out of 3 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of standards:\r
 https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022\r
\r
National Catalogue of France:\r
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0230c6dd-82f7-429f-a095-117b494554ae .

camssa:f318f099-4822-4da9-8c20-51432905849e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f31ac990-7cd5-476b-a636-af5dda9dea2f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the purpose of this specification is not directly related to restricting access to information/data, the Catalog Protocol part of the Dataspace Protocol defines how a Catalog is requested from a Catalog Service by a Consumer using an abstract message exchange format. Details for including authorisation tokens can be found in the protocol binding, e.g., Catalog HTTPS Binding.

IDSA Dataspace Protocol Catalog HTTPS Binding: https://docs.internationaldataspaces.org/ids-knowledgebase/v/dataspace-protocol/catalog/catalog.binding.https'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95736eef-2dab-499b-8086-27eea1babb5f .

camssa:f31ba8d2-3ce1-40e8-9f59-91c8ee2e2866 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion of XAdES (ISO 14533-2:2012) within any European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en \r
\r
CEN search tool catalogue:\r
https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=CENWEB:105::RESET::::\r
\r
CENELEC search tool catalogue:\r
https://www.cenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=104:107:0::::FSP_LANG_ID:25"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:38824809-285c-4197-a215-1ad7c6a67366 .

camssa:f31d687e-3888-4b35-92d6-eaa3a67d3aa2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although designed for use in business supply chains it can be (and has been) adapted for other contexts of use. This is because all the business document constructs in a UBL are drawn from a single library of reusable components. Therefore, UBL can be used across business domains.\r
\r
UBL v2.3 reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.3/UBL-2.3.html\r
\r
Developer community OASIS. UBL functionalities:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ubl#functionality'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9bff38c-7690-4014-99b1-7224bfb31a24 .

camssa:f32007ee-bae0-412c-b678-f10ad67dd0b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7a18abe4842e04b608025fd70e54c3db5c2a10130c0dab0495479e7d5effb55d ;
