        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:f374fb83-06f7-4487-ab90-7fd3d7406ec4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Secure processing of data can be provided by DNS adding the DNS Security Extensions (DNSSEC), which 
is, in fact, almost a mandatory extension between major stakeholders. Processing of data is secured by the 
encrytion under which the domain is protected provided by DNSSEC or other extensions addressing security 
issues. 

Resource Records for the DNS Security Extensions:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4034

Extension Mechanisms for DNS:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6891

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7c42dd9e-9e32-40cb-b8ed-e2a7dff0e2ac .

camssa:f3758709-04fc-4c1d-9e63-ea4728fd33cb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19c639047dab46befb5839503733c8f1e7ed8278f788a089d11d2caee84a8f7c ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f37698ac-3757-4ebf-81d2-b5f128f4e96e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ADMS is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8f1f3eb-b56b-4724-a89a-7de3ce39ab7f .

camssa:f37e671b-c1f5-4fcd-87da-7e29d87f57b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:f37ec54f-edec-4421-96c1-af4c60b21c42 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Both cloud data interoperability and portability contain a semantic section in the implementation's release. Therefore, it can be considered that the specification is involved in fostering the comprehensibility of Public Administrations data as well as relevant data produced for the decision-making process.\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea42de4e-dee2-47b6-bf3f-eda6baa1c83e .

camssa:f380847a-d9e0-491d-9a50-45340ed8807a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'iCalendar could allow third-party standards to protect data by applying access restrictions. The protocol for exchanging calendaring and scheduling data should prevent possible unwanted access to information.\r
\r
iCalendar Security Considerations:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545#section-7'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:331b388e-8523-4b85-a86a-f1fca0c62619 .

camssa:f3858044-e64e-43a9-b474-c7ac12237b02 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived. \r
\r
See:               \r
W3C Process document\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies   """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee7d1e44-441b-47ac-9b55-6de23b19971a .

camssa:f38d29b7-adb8-4828-8009-8fc15caefec1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). Specifically, WSDL can define the interoperability aspects of the "Machine to machine interface" ABB of the EIRA "Technical View".\r
\r
EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:851930b5-311d-4317-aabc-0c4952a54c3e .

