camssa:f4924ef6-1708-4b3a-9ab1-96e2b89263e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """DCAT is a domain-agnostic specification that can be reused for the description of any dataset independently from the business domain addressed.\r
\r
For DCAT users having business-specific requirements, the specification is generally extended (e.g. StatDCAT-AP for statistical data)"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:946080cf-c1cc-4b91-8db0-4e3e5406c1bf .

camssa:f4943ba5-5f85-4d33-bcf3-fbab204a948e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f49a071c-c689-49a2-9662-72cafd2e5576 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"After carrying out information retrieval, the Spanish CERES (Certification Authority Portal) is using OCSP\r
proving its efficiency. All the certificate validation services from the Spanish Certification Authorities are\r
using OCSP.\r
\r
CERES' OCSP reference:\r
https://www.cert.fnmt.es/en/catalogo-de-servicios/validacion-de-certificados/ocsp\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5b7cd62d-5765-494c-801f-e46bd75ab888 .

camssa:f4aa6123-e0ea-4000-a37f-7c3cccb1163c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f4aac888-5d88-4d76-8acf-d09414bc8bb4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f4ab3947-6d16-4dc5-99ba-8646677ebfe6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData offers a way to both break down data silos and increase the shared value of data. The specification contributes to creating an ecosystem where data consumers and producers can interoperate more than ever, allowing more applications to make sense of a broader set of data. In this sense, the specification promotes comprehensibility, for example through the OData data model. However, no evidence was found in terms of promoting and supporting the comprehensibility of European public services.

Interoperable Europe Portal OASIS Open Data Protocol reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/ict-standards-procurement/solution/odp-oasis-open-data-protocol-odata-tc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e82379f3-995a-443a-a732-b3333c24d290 .

camssa:f4b2296f-4c8c-4caa-9af9-1aebb4c2227d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-21276471c1781fa2c7e78c8e03851e076b840beddbf5cf64f53b54b8855a01b8 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:f4be2d8a-1af6-43f5-9de2-dd11ba26de88 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of SHACL. In "SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL", the SHACL effectiveness is assessed. In this study, is shown how SHACL can be utilised in a policy-based access control approach.

"SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43458-7_4

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:42d16506-dd4f-4157-96b3-bbc5000f7b77 .

camssa:f4c34419-f2d6-4e1a-ad3e-5fc4bf0766ba a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f4c457a7-5237-494c-8294-9dc669d2e1d1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Syslog is designed to be flexible, and partial implementations are possible based on the specific needs and 
requirements of a system or application. Implementer Guidelines in the protocol (Appendix A) show the extent to which syslog allows partial implementations depends on the features and components being implemented or omitted. It's important to note that while partial implementations are possible, interoperability may be impacted if the syslog implementation diverges significantly from the standard.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c546ba07-268b-4aa8-ac9a-2adcc1921074 .

camssa:f4c6ff12-3f6a-4bdc-b550-94f2c0f748be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAML 2.0 is a modular and extensive specification that accommodates a variety of use cases across diverse domains. The specification consists of various components and flows, meaning that implementers can choose to support certain parts of the standard based on their needs.\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:aedb44c0-4ecc-4b36-bc2c-f251d11b312f .

camssa:f4c9164b-6ac2-4258-b4d2-388b8879cdcd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

