camssa:f508bcd2-7562-497d-b361-fb90911aec1c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the moment of performing the assessment, the specification is not widespread known and used. However, it is a national initiative from Italy, that can have a great impact in the current European interoperability environment. Currently, the specification has been used in Italy to describe the software created in the
country. This has permitted the creation of a national catalogue of software by crawling the content of the publiccode.yaml available within the software repositories. The standard is also applied in opencode.de, Germany’s registry for open-source software in public administration. 

Publiccode.yaml documentation:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/developers-italia/publiccodeyml-en/en/master/index.html

Italian National Software Catalogue:
https://developers.italia.it/

Open CoDE:
https://opencode.de/en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68a94e03-13ff-49b6-b18a-8243845d0f0d .

camssa:f5125131-825f-4371-bc1a-50ed6dc098ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NFVI is already associated with EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, NFVI can define the interoperability aspects of the Hosting Facility, Hosting Service, Private Hosting Facility and Public Hosting Facility ABBs of the EIRA Technical View.\r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v110'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:622210f3-c5af-4141-af73-cbb53f8f6c4e .

camssa:f5167ce8-dab2-4cc4-97cf-1edfd81d0383 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'At the time of elaborating this assessment, this specification is included in the Controlled Vocabulary ABB in \r
the current EIRA Library Of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). \r
\r
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/solution/elis/release/600'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:75e099ea-b251-4435-9618-c8dd7f9342fc .

camssa:f5210d9f-7eb7-4ec6-bc36-6201879fed40 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the EN 303 645 specification is not related to data portability. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
EN 303 645 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:151f7dad-6a37-4751-979b-2eee433719d0 .

camssa:f5212f09-6375-4d95-b390-fd1b471bda50 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards. The decision-making process includes a public review, where stakeholders involved can provide technical feedback in order to enhance and maximize the quality and accuracy of the standards. \r
\r
See: \r
https://www.etsi.org/standards/standards-making """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d3c966d-f638-45d8-b6d4-f023a2888a71 .

camssa:f5216925-3634-4543-ad7f-2bf28784ae11 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'HTTPS is domain-agnostic, meaning it can be used with any domain or website. It is not specific to any particular domain or type of website. HTTPS can be implemented on various types of domains, including government websites, e-commerce platforms, social media platforms, news websites, and more.\r
\r
HTTPS specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:550846ce-12c7-4feb-9eba-e61f41bc8d3e .

camssa:f52988a9-133d-407a-94a2-dc3f834daa06 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the principles which is considered by the W3C working group is that DQV should be easy to map to as well as to re-use and extend. Therefore, DQV could facilitate organisational interoperability agreements. 

Interoperability reference:
https://www.semantic-web-journal.net/system/files/swj2079.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf5655f3-0f23-4392-997a-cbabc3dddb19 .

camssa:f52f9a4a-1fa2-421e-84c6-ad0ac1054047 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the syslog protocol is often assessed based on several factors that relate to its performance, scalability, and practical implementation. For instance, a 2020-paper for the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineering (IEEE) talks about efficient and robust syslog parsing for network devices in datacenter networks. Syslog usefulnes in this matter can be used as a testimony of its efficiency.

Efficient and Robust Syslog Parsing for Network Devices in Datacenter Networks: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org
/abstract/document/8988255'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3b6cb477-59cc-4a6e-bbf2-9ba3b2ddc4a7 .

camssa:f52fc2ce-b21b-4778-8e71-7e39307c135f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f53106b8-edb5-474d-a665-7336028b229f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5322897-338e-47be-a96d-1486b27d9410 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After checking the different standard catalogues at supra-national level, there is no evidence of the inclusion of IPv4 within any European catalogue of standards."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b232d0f6-0c5d-4b90-8102-1d8d81ba8d0e .

