        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f540e2a9-51c8-4d2e-a4d8-49d92cd8a7e6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification can enhance cloud computing services that support the development and deployment of e-government services, making it easier for citizens to access and interact with government services online. This can lead to streamlined processes, reduced paperwork, and improved citizen satisfaction. Also, it facilitates the migration of services and data across various cloud environments, making it an efficient and flexible solution for digital services.\r
\r
\r
ISO 19941: https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:19941:ed-1:v1:en'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe52ed69-e8c6-4bca-b9ac-b5ea3bef28d0 .

camssa:f543f22c-bacb-4044-95cf-5f81d7dac2a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, the specification is not mapped with any EIRA ABBs and therefore it is not included in the ELIS v1.0.1. \r
\r
However, it has been associated with Legal ABBs from EIRA Legal View and is being included in the on-going version of the ELIS that will be released in May 2021.  The ABBs included are: Legal Act, Binding Instrument, Legislation On Data Information and Knowledge Exchange and Non-Binding Instrument.\r
\r
ELIS Solution: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis \r
\r
ELIS v1.0.1: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v101-0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a720df2f-4c66-4659-871c-27e424fc2772 .

camssa:f544ae83-4ff5-4812-ba4f-dcc358165ddb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of SOAP 1.2 is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records and other kinds of information. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8344309-75ed-4108-b192-c4c9ad79ab88 .

camssa:f54d57e3-a7fd-4f6a-8adf-e9b19ba54ed5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The AES specification is designed to be adaptable and extended in the future. This means that future versions of the official AES standard could introduce changes or additions to the allowed values for some of its key parameters. For example, they might permit modify technical settings. However, at this moment the specification cannot be extended, and if it is modified, it can cause a loose of security capabilities.

Computer Security Objects Register (CSOR) reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/computer-security-objects-register

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a4af352-cd96-4f9e-b6c5-dee26e7638a7 .

camssa:f54fcc72-cf28-4972-8f81-fe7731350e3f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that use PDF/A nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6aa4e0d-5013-472c-ae8d-3acedb7ba809 .

