camssa:f5959762-c3eb-4303-b0c5-916f06ed3f01 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5a48e7e-ab61-453f-99f0-f7f5a110d44f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "JSON is a specification used for data exchange between different platforms, this fact facilitates the visibility and comprehensibility of administration's data. Moreover, it eases the communication between administrations enhancing the decision-making process. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfa64aac-e87c-430d-acee-64006db8aa39 .

camssa:f5af748a-62c3-4bde-862d-25a8186eb8c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification does not support the implementation of data accuracy mechanisms as SOAP does not focus on the content of the message.\r
\r
SOAP Reference, section 7 Security Considerations:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/#secconsiderations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a7811067-0203-470b-a15a-07efe2aaa099 .

camssa:f5b13d21-9b77-4909-9abe-8a5b4b3a1b15 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Participation and contribution in the development of the OASIS AMQP Technical Committee is open to all interested stakeholders. Stakeholders can actively contribute by joining the AMQP TC, providing input and offering feedback during public reviews of released specifications. TC members engage in committee work via the AMQP mailing list, which requires TC membership to post. The OASIS AMQP Technical Committee operates under OASIS Open, an organisation that promotes collaboration among individuals, organisations, and governments to address technical challenges through open standards and is open to all interested stakeholders.

AMQP OASIS Technical Committee reference:
https://groups.oasis-open.org/communities/tc-community-home2?CommunityKey=969c2da1-55c4-4bba-92d2-018dc7d3efe9

AMQP OASIS TC,  Charter reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/amqp/charter.php

OASIS Open Reference:
https://www.oasis-open.org/

AMQP working groups:
https://www.amqp.org/

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:326846c8-232b-4c5d-ad8d-f9ad4528cc82 .

camssa:f5b4180e-d813-4e29-8890-b76a2f418823 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently Microsoft has provided some insights regarding the specification effectiveness, but while it is implemented with other specifications, in this case via Microsoft network drivers.

OSI and Microsoft
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/network/windows-network-architecture-and-the-osi-model

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a44b02d6-6aca-43ae-a8a1-2d982f27a7d1 .

camssa:f5b5b0a1-d97b-44c7-98f1-c47264b6a49d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5be5c1f-8e84-4927-8b66-befd06337e9f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Stakeholders have several opportunities to contribute to the development of these frameworks and specifications. The ISA² program regularly organizes public consultations and workshops to gather feedback and suggestions from stakeholders across Europe. No public consultation or review have been identified, but the OP opens up different channels to participate in the development and adoption of its specifications.\r
\r
AKN4EU reference: \r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/akn4eu'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cc9cc6b-81a0-404e-b6fb-8b955ecbf05d .

camssa:f5c0e4b0-24cf-4a2e-bfb2-c5c04f844089 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "'Data portability is one of the key attributes of the specification.'"@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87ce1f95-d44f-4a34-b519-f87c37142042 .

camssa:f5c1cd51-a288-4efc-9079-8b36047badb5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SHACL does not defines a cross-sector reusable data model. SHACL is a web standard whose only purpose is RDF data graph validation."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b0b44823-cf96-45b4-ae16-aba0b96f9097 .

camssa:f5c35aab-d005-4089-91c0-0ee282014958 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are two Member States recommending ISO 3166-1 in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member\r
States are Malta and the Netherlands.\r
\r
National catalogue Malta: \r
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243\r
\r
National catalogue The Netherlands:\r
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a07dfbc-e5b3-4053-b1ac-c8aa7243cd8d .

camssa:f5c59653-5011-4f24-99eb-79d9329fa2ac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-1d35b341bcafc21377ae6ac358b9dc087e8ad32870012c2743e49e4566440f41 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f5c661e4-358b-4cca-a2b7-4e01a3785a83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """ECMA International's purpose is to make available the developed standards and specifications in a non-discriminatory and free of charges. Therefore, JSON is licensed under (F)RAND and Royalty-free basis. Terms and conditions for IPR disclosures can be found in ECMA's webpage. \r
See:\r
http://www.ecma-international.org/memento/Ecma%20IPR%20policies.htm"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16c97a62-97e8-47c9-bcb2-51ea13e01f38 .

camssa:f5ce47fc-cba7-4b64-9b2f-da8748720d39 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ef096f898c938883daab1b22e784cfaf985b5e5c855e170ecf6eab6f37b01b50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f5d012f2-c35b-44a1-aa49-51946250771e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are many communities that share their data and results of their implementations of HTTP Cookies. Some examples of such communities can be found in the following links.\r
\r
Stack overflow forum:\r
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12373738/how-do-i-set-a-cookie-on-httpclients-httprequestmessage\r
\r
Microsoft community:\r
https://powerusers.microsoft.com/t5/General-Power-Automate/Passing-Cookies-Between-HTTP-Actions/td-p/69761'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:15898e5b-1da8-4303-8398-d4e8be94af92 .

camssa:f5daee81-09d1-4f53-8330-9aef1014c6ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard is developed by a non-European organisation. Therefore, the specification cannot be considered a European standard.

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:241dd43f-8793-4ef7-b531-f63361ecb7ba .

camssa:f5dc0701-0561-4596-a06d-a0db4a415afc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The version being assessed is not included in the ICT technical specification in itself, however the version 1.0 of the specification was already identified and included within this list of specifications that are compliant with the standardisation regulation for being used in eProcurement.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22e125a7-3028-4174-a825-604fab7b2cb4 .

camssa:f5dd29cb-48ba-4c1b-a574-d9bd6572acce a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f5dd3a8a-a3a3-4657-ab78-5a2e7c0045de a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OSI is not related to data processing accuracy. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification.

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:33833ac3-166b-4863-bdd9-97094fbcca85 .

camssa:f5de45fc-52c1-41a6-bcb7-18a0015a7ad4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog protocol is developed by IETF, a standard development organisation based in the US. Moreover, the 
syslog protocol specification does not appear in any of the main European standard development bodies, 
therefore, the specification is not a European standard.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e2e99ce-6667-4091-9a38-dd61f667e3b7 .

camssa:f5e00d50-ed36-49b8-baa8-4c2873acace9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Core Location Vocabulary specification can be found in the Interoperable Europe Portal. In this Portal, people can discuss about the specification, and the maintainers can publish all of the releases available. In addition, the namespace of the vocabulary is given by the W3C, promoting the sharing of data and results regarding the specification. 
Finally, the specification can also be found in the Publications Office of the European Union (PO).

Core Location Vocabulary PO:
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/corevocs#:~:text=The%20Core%20Location%20Vocabulary%20%28latest%20version%29%20is%20a,Vocabulary%20is%20aligned%20with%20the%20INSPIRE%20data%20specifications.

Core Location Vocabulary Interoperable Europe Portal:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8eed927f-95eb-4c49-8960-fb20dbd7cf0b .

camssa:f5e0cf7e-7e28-44d5-9668-0ede6e138e3f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Advanced Encryption Standard can be implemented in any software, firmware, hardware or any combination of them. Therefore, the standard is platform agnostic.

AES Standard Reference:
https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/197/final'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a45e6ecd-505d-4d02-ac96-54321058614b .

camssa:f5e2d64f-b03c-41b5-9ed4-52046d8ff165 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f5e4106f-02cf-4827-8c14-f8499d7de7c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP Cookies enable web servers to store stateful information on the user's device or to track the user's browsing activity. They can also be used to save for subsequent use information that the user previously entered into form fields, such as names, addresses, passwords, and payment card numbers. Therefore, HTTP Cookies can facilitate data portability having a positive impact in interoperability.\r
\r
\r
HTTP Cookies reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-5.2\r
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9be1843-dbee-4017-8329-61e49707a2a5 .

camssa:f5e80849-48d5-482c-84a6-e3ebb9bc58c1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f5e95ce9-aab7-452e-aad4-799dae8a4dec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "PAdES Baseline profile provides the main requirements to ensure the correct use and exchange of signed data in the context of the European Internal Market. Furthermore, the conformance levels included in this profile of PAdES have the objective of ensuring the trustworthy data exchange between public administrations and stakeholders. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f094532c-fca4-4ffe-aa48-4622279425a8 .

camssa:f5ecf886-c76f-461f-acc8-0ed3e4611c22 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5eeb973-94fd-40ee-879f-e6ad6bc17500 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b45c8f7e446b1343c6b6961290d2106768aa43c1f123f5e436d0255c003abb50 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f5f391ea-3317-4b2c-a9e3-4f71c5bacf2a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of IPSec is not related to long term preservation of electronic records. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
See: \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4301 \r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f8ae5d82-1080-4fe1-9f6b-ea1e3276614b .

camssa:f5f3dd7a-0d83-49fc-8735-56b5eb8eb1a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "CSV makes sure content is available on the web, structures data and makes it usable in a non-proprietary open format. So it can be said that CSV facilitates the reduction of administrative burdens when making it usable and open."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7865dc4-7a5d-41c2-a6b1-c3a4fb0d3aa1 .

camssa:f5f6312a-4c48-46e5-b82e-71176d2169cf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5f7f42f-d410-4cc0-8fd4-7911fe4fd895 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5fa30da-7622-4ebf-87af-c2ec565f371c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5fb3b26-82ea-42dc-9f8e-669b00ef37a0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f5fbde93-6f46-4b9a-b961-0865d91ef996 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness of IPv6. The "IPv6 performance - and how to test it" study, makes an assessment for measure the efectiveness of IPv6 using scores for city (Frankfurt in this case), region (Europe) and Global. Moreover, the assessment almost includes other themes such as connectivity. 

"IPv6 performance - and how to test it" reference:
https://www.swissipv6council.ch/sites/default/files/images/sonar_article_02-2013-final.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a63f078f-2023-4624-b21a-c0eaec1c0d25 .

camssa:f5fcb505-e5b1-458a-b6b7-ebb1e66251cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV is based on European Union legislative requirements such as the GDPR, which aims to harmonize data privacy laws across Europe.  Therefore, public administrations benefit from the definition of a data model based on this regulation given that it promotes the transparency of the procedures and personal data handled by public administrations.  \r
\r
DPV specification: \r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction\r
\r
GDPR reference:\r
https://gdpr.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a29da52a-3ccf-4453-ac6c-dafe67525c0e .

camssa:f5fe6e2a-e047-4159-8b39-00c8e2dbf7f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'AMQP does not scope comprehensibly administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore this criterion is not applicable.

OASIS AMQP Reference:
http://docs.oasis-open.org/amqp/core/v1.0/amqp-core-complete-v1.0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e7149e2-2253-43ea-a1b8-07b6dae269a7 .

camssa:f60504a6-9b28-4d4c-8fa4-e1d4d42d0edd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f6069760-4b43-4d7d-a75b-40f57667a886 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Assessments of the efficiency of this asssessment primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, 
and practicality of implementations. A 2019-paper about Integrated Security Management Systems mentions ISO/IEC 7498:1 as one of the key standards analysed to suggest an approach to the development of integrated security and safety management system struc-ture considering threats of intrusion into physical, information and signal spaces, demonstrating how efficient the specification can be.

Integrated Security Management System for Enterprises in Industry 4.0: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/336027597_Integrated_Security_Management_System_for_Enterprises_in_Industry_40'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8917d307-3b7f-47d0-a3bf-b69f5c69d008 .

camssa:f60fdbc0-dc9c-43ae-92d7-a595b556ff32 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5df7a9f6081c945a22f500aa0ba2c452b8b9cd9497bd643ac76c39d34a18c319 ;
    cav:value "0" .

camssa:f611d60a-b491-4129-bd9f-f73f4e08d237 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "There are no competitors for RPKI since no standards with overlapping functional scope have been found. No interoperability issues with the implementation of existing European or international standards exist."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09ee08ad-afbe-4c4b-bb7e-2e99d3e5e8b4 .

camssa:f61d2150-adbb-4173-a9c6-fc48fb648e22 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f61f103d-10d6-4f0f-bc10-547e8f5c9060 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the specification is not related to supporting the implementation of European public services, \r
therefore it does not promote or hinder it.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:03065c78-5d1f-423f-a968-5d7e1dcf1b4b .

camssa:f62099de-b007-4055-adf9-cde26cebe18a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-41c6fd2dadb03cc64aad82cfa14f545c084f1a955a3ab7a61aab416a138c5dce ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f624b185-9d36-4bca-bd48-b22b4e9d9902 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XHTML is available for implementation and use for free on the W3C's webpage to cover any user needs.
However, since XHTML is superseded in favour of HTML5, the coverage of business domains is larger when
using HTML5.

XHTML W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/

HTML5 W3C Reference:
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:183ee005-9857-4fa8-a6f4-7e2bb6a3c797 .

camssa:f625f90d-07a6-4662-b30d-037bd96c94c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPSec is not related to interfaces. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
See: \r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d8bf13d-5d1c-4a9f-82ef-9228cf4ce4f7 .

camssa:f62f4f7c-502a-4375-bb7d-4784c2ba88ea a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPv6 specification supports digital service delivery channels by providing a much larger address space than IPv4, which facilitates the connection of a vast number of devices to the internet. This expanded address space is crucial for the Internet of Things (IoT) and other services that require unique IP addresses for each device.

IPv6 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2460'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a8202e2-614a-4fe4-818e-ed54e92a4ad6 .

camssa:f6316b21-0073-42cd-9f4f-63a51f6e132d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IPv6 as a protocol with objective of enhancing communications over a computer network, allows the scalability of systems. \r
Moreover, the European Union promotes the usage of IPv6 and the public administration are able to reuse it.  "MS as for instance Germany could bring strong support to the deployment of IPv6 within the European public administrations." \r
Source: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/ipv6_framework_for_european_governments_0.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d4389f12-738a-4353-beea-21b3d9854254 .

camssa:f635d778-9aa4-42d1-88d2-d052d9345605 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the specification is not related to the long-term preservation of electronic records. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:477339d7-77eb-4d4d-b874-ed4caf1b0dca .

camssa:f6363fcd-4151-4e21-aeae-505c619a51b4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog itself does not provide a built-in access control mechanism. However, access control mechanisms can be implemented at various levels to restrict access to syslog-related resources.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:24e05c91-41bb-4559-bb0d-7b8c05c08149 .

camssa:f638f55a-9871-485d-962b-6e537f3da42c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f63ad5fb-3e94-4a3e-8a7f-04f8b3dd1f4a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:f63f01b4-e63d-4dd2-91af-0478f70797f1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-624bc49501d58649e27cae4fb89fb5a56844685e54c5ce1625633894f8f752e1 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f6428cd7-82e3-4da1-8b2e-6b262ea29e6d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ebXML specification is assessed and discussed in various forums and across the Internet. For example, the ebXML Forum News discusses the specification. Additionally, there are many papers that explore ebXML and its implementation, such as the "EbXML simplified: a guide to the new standard for global e-commerce" document.

ebXML Forum News:
https://ebxmlforum.blogspot.com/

"EbXML simplified: a guide to the new standard for global e-commerce" document:
https://books.google.es/books?hl=es&lr=&id=y5mwRBUXgAAC&oi=fnd&pg=PR3&dq=ebxml+&ots=yYosABWG9D&sig=wjypDYsboxfGo7abUyoaQFyIBSg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=ebxml&f=false

ebXML RegRep OASIS reference:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:faeebde5-b5dd-4907-955c-1c60384e3e9f .

camssa:f64fb755-7478-41ea-bf1f-7d7c93a58de0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of UTF-8 is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore this criterion is not applicable specification.\r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:401318e0-da4b-492e-9ea9-0b3eb7bc6467 .

