    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f6e6cae8-339e-4619-87bb-fac10e6f4da2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Not enough pieces of evidence have been found to answer positively or negatively to this criterion. Moreover, it seems that the purpose of the specification is not related to the delivery.\r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00ec2c7c-7d59-4e27-bba3-99477a25817a .

camssa:f6e6d2d9-62e3-41d6-a63d-744e204845a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RDF allows for partial implementations in the sense that it allows for the creation and use of incomplete or partial data graphs.\r
\r
RDF primer document:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4670650-55b8-4d13-b879-9947ef6203b4 .

camssa:f6e7349d-3758-4656-9961-9ae41f698a47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The Open Digital Rights Language (ODRL) is a policy expression language that provides a flexible and interoperable information model, vocabulary, and encoding mechanisms for representing statements about the usage of content and services. Therefore, by implementing it, administrations can benefit from the common framework for representing the statements of digital public services and the provision of clear information. This is a powerful usage not only for administration-citizens interaction but also to enhance the cooperation between administrations. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8db84aec-0f6e-4a5c-ba56-d1ab2d0cbc5a .

camssa:f6e84e04-fc6e-4ee5-b740-84d547a43f59 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f7002996-3b35-4e19-8b9f-26a2abddab69 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-19598487b8ba278c3438dcfd74b74d9aad51beac08c53dbf40bf108ed09e72b2 ;
    cav:value "2" .

camssa:f7058988-e6d7-4f27-b53b-4a9302e0c6d8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"Assessments of the efficiency of the Dataspace Protocol primarily involve evaluating the performance, scalability, and practicality of implementations. For instance, a 2023-paper for Gaia-X Austria describes the main points to consider when building a dataspace and references for it. IDSA offers a dataspace reference architecture where a comprehensive dataspace protocol defines messages and API-bindings based on DCAT and ODRL, which highlights the specification's efficiency.

Building a Dataspace Gaia-X Austria: https://www.gaia-x.at/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/WhitepaperGaiaX.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7453e6f7-a185-43ae-9b01-598123bcfce2 .

camssa:f7060cca-f7ce-4dd6-876b-1d1815a33ef8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the main purpose of the DPV is to model the legal aspects of data portability, in order to link them with more technical aspects of electronic data exchange. DPV suggests mechanisms for the data to be protected, and data transfers in contexts where cross-border exchange is needed.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b16ff19c-8b9b-4219-81d4-0a1da22ee6e9 .

camssa:f70646b3-36af-4d73-8620-0e853d4eaad0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:f70ab6db-7075-4c6c-92c4-3bb8ac967866 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are existing documentation and studies assessing the effectiveness and efficiency of LDAP. It is a \r
comparison between LDAP 2 and LDAP 3. As well, the study shows the improvement of the different \r
versions over time as resulting in more efficient protocol.\r
\r
Difference between LDAP2 and LDAP3:\r
https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/desktop/ldap/differences-between-ldap-2-and\\x02ldap-3\r
\r
Assessment of LDAP services in high availability environment:\r
https://www.infona.pl/resource/bwmeta1.element.baztech-32ec800f-6db2-4a4a-be0a-bcb3fae16d23/tab\r
/summary'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd4a6e13-5401-4fa7-b940-f2c666488927 .

camssa:f70c26c1-7809-46cc-b12b-cf5f0e10f394 a cav:Score,
