camssa:f75ca5b7-39fb-4970-8d3f-44407479d438 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DIDs are designed to enable individuals and organizations to generate their own identifiers using systems they trust. These new identifiers enable entities to prove control over them by authenticating using cryptographic proofs such as digital signatures. Moreover, the specification also adresses the immutability of data. The more locked down a DID method is, while providing the same set of features, the less it can be manipulated by malicious actors.

DIDs cryptographic:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#introduction

DIDs immutability:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/#immutability'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2cd394bb-75dc-48ac-85fe-1839ae4f564a .

camssa:f75df8d2-d1ac-4adb-ae68-7fe02ac368cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating and Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all of the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:\r
- Technical excellence;\r
- prior implementation and testing;\r
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;\r
- openness and fairness; and \r
- timeliness.\r
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a644748-3746-4498-bccd-117f15b1e9cc .

camssa:f7619d41-3b03-4e49-9967-15efed832ea5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f767f4c9-2f4c-4c81-b372-ae1a1f434005 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f768510d-695d-4cc8-b8ac-2911efe21d2a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 itself does not provide an access control mechanism since it focuses primarily on the physical and data link layers of Ethernet networks. Access control is typically handled at higher layers of the OSI model.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:998978b2-d7e0-4324-810b-8ff7119ddd83 .

camssa:f76eab59-3f86-4878-9bef-3580500348a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Changes to the YAML language itself will be made using a "requests for comments (RFC)" process. The working group is currently engaged in finalising the remaining details of this process, with the intention of having them all resolved in the near future. Despite this, some ways to get involved are reporting typos, mistakes, bugs, discussing ideas and submitting fixes for the build system.

Contribution to YAML:
https://github.com/yaml/yaml-spec/blob/main/.github/contributing.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9bf9390-8bd2-48c8-ad64-cea349643471 .

camssa:f77f1e26-49d0-490c-bdd3-5fd9ea0688c2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SAML 2.0 is included in Portugal and Slovakian national catalogues of recommended specifications. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Slovakia and Portugal is fully aligned with at least 2 out of 3 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets.\r
\r
NIFO Factsheets:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2022\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss\r
/camss-list-standards\r
\r
Slovakia NIFO Factsheet:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/NIFO%20-%20Factsheet%20Slovakia_2016_v1_0.pdf\r
\r
SAML 2.0 Reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c367a456-d889-4db9-81fb-da19b58a28d4 .

camssa:f780968a-2dd3-401d-9e00-be9765fbae87 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-8c0e1d9d02fa1d534bed0962df3492708c99afbc6343ac8dc671bbabae75aca2 ;
    cav:value "None" .

camssa:f784ab4f-ee56-4bc8-8926-677eda891771 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Open Digital Rights Language (ODRL) specification is primarily designed for expressing digital rights \r
and permissions rather than specifically addressing data portability. However, the use of a standardized \r
language like ODRL can contribute to data portability efforts between systems and applications.\r
\r
W3C specification: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a79f024-66a8-4296-bcab-31085234a2c7 .

camssa:f78abfa0-553d-442a-bfd1-ed45c566c4a2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-483e8900c47b40bc67a6bd1cbfce07884b9ac5f2c85e0214f334cc37e4e65c35 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f79b868c-8557-4e9e-be95-f265364d4aef a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ba46c76c10ad769a23ce4a9a34cb4d96a00407d5fc14ad1c791a870be7563c2b ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f79e8edc-f553-41b2-b162-8b5608d27aae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
