    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f7a4cfe6-47e4-47bc-9a7a-66006ae46a34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of FTP is not related to restricting access to information/data. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0dc18064-7ce8-4df7-8fec-7ea4a3f0b5d6 .

camssa:f7a4e48a-6286-415c-bf06-a7b69dc31906 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The FTP (File Transfer Protocol) specification allows for partial implementations to some extent. It defines a set of core commands and behaviors that must be supported by all conforming FTP implementations to ensure basic interoperability.\r
\r
However, the FTP specification also includes optional features and extensions that allow for additional functionality beyond the core commands. These optional features can be selectively implemented based on the specific requirements and capabilities of the FTP server or client.\r
\r
FTP Specification Reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc959'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a17a20ad-3d09-4a3b-94c8-55a640f2c2be .

camssa:f7a69d92-5dc8-45fa-bd70-89065c04f9eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO/IEC 19944-1 has  been found recommended in a digitalisation report by the Spanish Standardisation Association (UNE) and the Louxembourg Institute for standardisation (ILNAS) as one of the specifications "addressing business challenges and supporting related ICT development".\r
\r
UNE digitalisation report:\r
https://www.une.org/normalizacion_documentos/Informe%20Transformaci%C3%B3n%20Digital_20201127.pdf\r
\r
ILNAS Technical standardisation report:\r
https://portail-qualite.public.lu/dam-assets/publications/normalisation/2022/report-technical-standardization-cloud-computing.pdf\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a1414657-3038-4632-999f-e66706d45959 .

camssa:f7a7e0d7-bd5b-4e8d-bc27-12502e0c6c48 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:f7af9313-17d7-48df-83fb-bdd275aa768b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f7b1023d-7bc8-40b7-b4df-60a73db09093 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Using mechanisms such as time-stamping authority, it is possible to ensure that data is secured and that only authorised persons have access to them. Moreover, there are other access control mechanisms that guarantee data is secured and changes are only allowed for authorised persons. 

ETSI TS 119 512:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119500_119599/119512/01.01.01_60/ts_119512v010101p.pdf

ETSI EN 319 401:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319401/02.03.01_60/en_319401v020301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:789b0212-966c-43ec-bc5d-8591954bc786 .

camssa:f7b3402e-9584-4f68-93fd-0966ce484c2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IEEE Std 802.3-2022 primarily focuses on the physical and data link layers for Ethernet networks, and while it doesn’t directly address e-accessibility, it supports the infrastructure that enables accessible digital services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.

IEEE Std 802.3-2022 Reference:
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9844436'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96c8cc7a-2e8a-4503-9cff-d3e97234ce62 .

camssa:f7b37e24-aae8-49b8-a573-3cf054a5beae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f7bb63aa-dd07-467f-a294-64a410b8a66c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:f7dbe535-b9f4-4fbd-818d-5be05a4bdae7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f7e4ea00-eb8e-4b48-b99f-eb7f56ba6652 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Tools & Libraries for assessing the conformance of datasets with DCAT or its extensions have been developed by the community.\r
\r
See: \r
http://www.dcat.be/validator/\r
https://www.npmjs.com/package/dcat-validator \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-ap-validator """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c1348852-4f74-4959-86fa-80299e2e607c .

camssa:f7e6ab9f-04a5-4309-ad84-4afa9f646b19 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "SOAP 1.2 is a sector domain agnostic specification that can be used independently from the business domain. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:63e2a73f-c35b-4c34-8d4a-275e8cf68f06 .

camssa:f7e8b633-2264-4765-bec8-8bf7794b6f88 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of MIME is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af581f13-caf7-4a0c-b318-27e3a1015f53 .

camssa:f7eae8e2-28b2-4f8b-bea5-c6fdb61d6f9b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DCAT-AP has a strong support from different communities. In fact, it is a joint initiative of the DCAT-AP Working  Group, which comprises the Directorate-General for Informatics: (DG DIGIT), in particular the SEMIC action of the ISA² programme, the Directorate-General for Communications Networks, Content & Technology (DG CONNECT), and The Publications Office of the EU.\r
\r
DCAT Application profiles for data portals in Europe:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe/about  \r
\r
DCAT-AP leaflet:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/leaflet_dcat-ap_lr_v13.pdf '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22e72e06-966b-4b94-a794-145f9666363e .

camssa:f7f01d2f-4f94-4912-b79e-0f54fce042a8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:f7f0fab1-78e1-42b3-a4fe-c7994d59e7ef a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the supporting documents of this specification is ETSI GR CIM 007, which identifies the security and privacy aspects that are relevant when building systems based on the NGSI-LD API and the NGSI-LD information model. Mechanisms for giving proof of authentication are described in ETSI TS 102 165-2, and in the context of attribute based cryptography in ETSI TR 103 719. In the NGSI-LD API context authentication is used in part to verify the identity of each actor in the NGSI-LD API system.

ETSI Context Information Management (CIM); Security and Privacy:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_gr/CIM/001_099/007/01.01.02_60/gr_cim007v010102p.pdf

ETSI TS 102 165-2: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102100_102199/10216502/04.02.01_60/ts_10216502v040201p.pdf

ETSI TR 103 719:
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_tr/103700_103799/103719/01.01.01_60/tr_103719v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b5bd4f1-18bf-40e0-8802-23bc839b8f75 .

camssa:f7f2ef4d-61cb-4d44-9002-8c3599e377f4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80" .

camssa:f7f3430a-7a95-4588-873f-a07d69ac38d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There is no reference to WAI-ARIA and a European use case explicitly stating that the specification allows relevant information and data to be reused. However, since WAI-ARIA can extend a host language, a grid can reuse the elements and attributes of an HTML table element. \r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference, section 5.4, Grid subsection:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:85217698-5fb2-42db-a203-9767a41dfe4e .

camssa:f7fa19e0-1491-493e-840b-644542ced578 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ADMS as a profile of DCAT, is an RDF vocabulary for representing data catalogues that allows data owners to provide metadata about the datasets they publish. By describing catalogues, datasets and resources, a publisher makes them easily searchable and discoverable.\r
\r
Following the previous statement it can be said that ADMS can simplify the delivery of European public services.\r
\r
ADMS Specification W3C:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-adms/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f67b0ad-bc4f-4474-851b-20204c2fdba2 .

camssa:f7ff01f7-a76c-4173-8df1-2e26d2868244 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard does not specifically mention the protection of personal data managed
by Public Administrations. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7390d149-9e30-4cd4-88db-30b30a6176c9 .

camssa:f801dfc6-faa5-478f-b4da-8a2f4c697844 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:f80320ae-dc06-44a8-b21b-d4c19437caf4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISO community, brings together experts to share knowledge and develop voluntary, consensus-based, market relevant International Standards that support innovation and provide solutions to global challenges.  All of ISO’s technical work, including the technical committees, is managed by the Technical Management Board (TMB). Some of the TMB’s tasks include setting up technical committees, appointing chairs and monitoring the progress of technical work. \r
\r
ISO developing standards:\r
https://www.iso.org/who-develops-standards.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:31bec05a-72d2-4765-93f2-f466718bbd93 .

camssa:f803e6db-15c2-4f6a-8c52-1c320e50b309 a cav:Statement,
