camssa:f8525716-545e-4906-bf23-64010ae3b2be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"While genericode's primary purpose is to provide a structured and consistent way to represent lists of values, by using Genericode-compliant code lists, organisations can ensure consistency in how these values are represented, improving data clarity, In addition, the inclusion of metadata can improve understanding and interpretation of the codes within various contexts.

Code List Representation (genericode): https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b6385250-12e8-4631-8b13-f5142a53acfe .

camssa:f853d279-cc7a-4fe5-9b57-c4b762a57adb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "76%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage",
        "89%AssessmentScoreAverage" .

camssa:f855bbb8-7928-44e2-88ec-dbd9bd003d71 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Section 4 of genericode defines that an XML instance conforms to the OASIS Code List Representation genericode document model if it does not violate any constraints expressed in the genericode.xsd schema associated with this version of the specification, including auxiliary rules marked as “document” rules. Furthermore, appendix E delves into testing select document conformance rules (non-normative), which specifies that some of the document conformance auxiliary rules prescribed in Section 4.2, “Category: document” can be tested using ISO/IEC 19757-3 Schematron.

Section 4 genericode: 
https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html#S-CONFORMANCE

Appendix D genericode:
https://docs.oasis-open.org/codelist/genericode/v1.0/os/genericode-v1.0-os.html#A-TESTING-SELECT-DOCUMENT-CONFORMANCE-RULES

ISO/IEC 19757-3:2020: https://www.iso.org/standard/74515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57f69024-e780-4916-a96b-7916fcadcbf5 .

camssa:f85ab39c-9e2e-4b94-a0eb-8d023a398d63 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f85c464a-1b52-4167-837f-dc9a53a23fe4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Indexed Database API specification allows to restrict access to information/data stored by some web that utilise the specification. In this context, only the website that created the data (from the same domain) can access it. If a website is loaded inside an iframe from a different domain, it can't access the data of the parent website. This rule helps protect your data from unauthorised access or manipulation.

Indexed Database API privacy:
https://www.w3.org/TR/2025/WD-IndexedDB-3-20250110/#privacy\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b873810d-1754-4605-acdc-5ae4b06b6339 .

camssa:f85d1615-953b-473c-9846-abdd306cc275 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By promoting standardized practices, Interoperability considerations, and compliance with relevant standards, the specifications guidelines and recommendations can enhance organisations interoperability with other systems and foster data exchanges.\r
\r
ISO/IEC 19944-1 specification:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/60545.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7b0e22c0-dab7-4e5b-9711-da4292dc2c8e .

camssa:f861ba91-8e23-4491-ad5b-9215fe42e0f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """After checking the assessments performed by CAMSS and the list of specifications identified by the MSP Multi-stakeholder-platform, no assessment verifying the compliance of the specification with the European standardisation regulation has been found.\r
\r
ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/industry/policy/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb28a9a3-eb2b-441a-b6b3-ddb13e6e5722 .

