camssa:f867d0d1-1e56-416d-9972-f516d59f7a86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "At the moment of performing the assessment, PNG is widely used in across sectors, it is one of the main image extension used. However, no evidences has been found to consider PNG as an asset to build innovative solutions."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f4544808-8015-4f58-8bb4-f258031b84b3 .

camssa:f86b09cd-03a0-4b89-ae28-8d0b93d17f8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'NUTS is intended to serve as a device to identify administrative zones in the EU and beyond the EU borders. There is no possibility of partial implementation of the specification, as NUTS has a single purpose.\r
\r
EUROSTAT reference, NUTS Principles and Characteristics section:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/principles-and-characteristics'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:44a5a486-e889-4cb9-8d7f-94fd0960a019 .

camssa:f86db8b6-32e3-4c9f-ac83-a79445b59d1f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By employing a common data model, adhering to platform-neutral principles, and supporting adaptable resolution processes, DIDs can be effectively implemented across a wide range of platforms.

DIDs W3C:
https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7731ef47-0354-4157-96e4-43d1f70531b2 .

camssa:f8807e5e-e7b4-48f4-a79c-8908009cd232 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The IETF is completely open to newcomers. There is no formal membership, no membership fee, and nothing to sign. The IETF's standards development work is organized into 8 Areas Each Area has 1 or more Area Directors (ADs), which together comprise the Internet Engineering Steering Group (IESG). The IESG is responsible for technical management of IETF activities, the Internet standards process, and for the actions associated with entry into and movement along the Internet ''standards track'', including final approval of specifications as Internet Standards and publication as an RFC. Within each Area there are multiple Working Groups (WG). Each WG has one or more chairs who manage the work, and a written charter defining what the work is and when it is due. There are more than 100 WGs. The WGs produce Internet Drafts (I-Ds) which often lead to the publication of an Internet standard as an RFC._x000D_\r
See: http://www.ietf.org/newcomers.html """@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:90637b3f-7576-4197-a999-d2bc0d2b1ffd .

camssa:f8905d4b-66cd-40fa-9265-c3aaa90b0172 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f890f437-5d28-4e65-b022-b3119b0b4358 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f893a4a0-ecb1-4507-9a2e-39b646994df3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are assessments that analyse and proving the effectiveness of the the usage of AMQP and other similar specifications. For a detailed explanation of AMQP's efficiency and comparison with other messaging protocols, refer to the document "Choice of Effective Messaging Protocols for IoT Systems: MQTT, CoAP, AMQP and HTTP."

Additionally, numerous real-world scenarios, products, and articles utilise and reference the AMQP specification, demonstrating its effectiveness. Examples of commercially available AMQP products include Microsoft's Azure Service Bus, JBoss A-MQ by Red Hat (built from Qpid), IBM’s MQlight, and many others.

Choice of Effective Messaging Protocols for IoT Systems: MQTT, CoAP, AMQP and HTTP Reference:
https://pure.port.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/12197128/IoT_Messaging_Protocols_Naik.pdf

Products and Success Stories - AMPQ.org Reference:
https://www.amqp.org/about/examples

Microsoft Windows Azure Reference:
http://www.windowsazure.com/en-us/develop/net/how-to-guides/service-bus-amqp-overview/

RedHat JBoss A-MQ Reference:
http://www.redhat.com/en/technologies/jboss-middleware/amq

IBM MQlight Reference:
https://developer.ibm.com/messaging/mq-light/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ece1ee47-d034-48b5-8478-fb51074c9c9b .

camssa:f89463d5-f573-4469-90dc-431c0ea32fe9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'MIME can play a role in authentication processes such as digital signatures, by specifying content types and headers to handle digitally signed or authenticated messages, but it does not provide the mechanisms for creating or verifying digital signatures or other authenticity features.\r
\r
MIME specification:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
S/MIME specification:\r
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5751.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f70646b3-36af-4d73-8620-0e853d4eaad0 .

camssa:f894f242-7fee-44e8-a212-5202ce180e2a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f897e8e0-4d1e-4e5d-b456-6dee8f51650b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The RFC 3161 Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) is widely used and involved in e-Signature services. This electronic signatures are part of digital public services, and also private in order to focus the development of digital environments avoiding the non-digital transactions. \r
\r
TSP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3161\r
\r
DigiStamp:\r
https://www.digistamp.com/\r
\r
FreeTSA:\r
https://www.freetsa.org/index_en.php"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9ac3054d-8a7c-4f26-a549-308c5ee03415 .

camssa:f89a8ee6-2011-47a9-9987-07f6ff6bda0b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The once-only principle is an e-government concept that aims to ensure that citizens, institutions, and \r
companies only have to provide certain standard information to the authorities and administrations once.\r
LDAP fosters the OOP in terms of accessibility by allowing administrations stakeholders to keep the contact \r
and access to different distributed services without providing personal data for authentication more than \r
strictly needed. \r
\r
LDAP IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:95df048b-e368-4a66-9814-ee7c3f4be1bc .

camssa:f89ab23e-3935-4c00-a401-b6bc4f5d26bb a cav:Score,
