camssa:f8e64480-a25a-456b-9c94-029c40dba638 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'This specification includes evaluations of verifiable credentials through a verifiable data registry. This role an entity may perform is the evaluation of whether a verifiable credential or verifiable presentation is an authentic and timely statement of the issuer or presenter, respectively includes checking that: the credential (or presentation) conforms to the specification; the proof method is satisfied; and, if present, the status is successfully checked. \r
\r
Verifiable Credentials: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/\r
\r
Verifiable Credentials conformance:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/#conformance'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c17085fb-ea37-465c-8ee6-f81acbe7e9cf .

camssa:f8ed7b04-0136-4031-bec2-3cd8e2212aab a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b6ba3f2f556446c68c55833e72b217be87ad5f0dd07744e2c39c6070aff6c10f ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f8f0b2a7-a0a4-4c22-97de-60cdde4f2cba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The TC(Technical Committe) is the primary group where OGC Standards and many Products are developed, discussed, approved, and maintained. The TC members are responsible for the development and maintenance of all Standards and related technical documents and supporting deliverables.

OGC Technical Committee Procedures:
https://www.ogc.org/join/

OGC Technical Committee Policies:
https://docs.ogc.org/pol/05-020r29/05-020r29.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:76390e3d-592e-48b8-888f-be75fd4633d7 .

camssa:f8f2d845-d4e4-4e37-96d1-a3cbd23c0c7b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-83d21357ecad07668ab7f2010aefed3cebb92dab384eeae6eb7aa77def06cfc3 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:f8f9956f-e92d-4616-8d1a-530437758007 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is widely adopted amongst others like SMTP for the exchange of data over the internet. It allows sharing several file formats, which makes the specification highly reusable. The specification has been implemented and it is supported by numerous mail services as Gmail amongst others, demonstrating the market acceptance of MIME.\r
\r
MIME reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045\r
\r
SMTP specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5321\r
\r
Gmail using MIME:\r
https://developers.google.com/gmail/api/guides/sending?hl=es-419'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54e68426-7eaf-4593-a47d-e4e5fb7b4e21 .

camssa:f8fb07b0-a88f-48bd-83d8-ca9d98946ca7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"As it can be seen in the example of 'data protection aspects of online shopping - a use case', DPV specifies the personal data that an order delivery has to take from the client, thus, ensuring efficient interactions between clients and citizens. For that matter, DPV can ease digitalisation and simplify the delivery of European public services.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

Data protection aspects of online shopping - a use case:
https://www.w3.org/community/dpvcg/2019/12/12/data-protection-aspects-of-online-shopping-a-use-case/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c04b4c4-a34b-471d-9e34-666808dba766 .

camssa:f8fd2742-561c-4656-8433-350cad9c41dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Implementing the Core Location Vocabulary enhances digital services by standardising location data, ensuring interoperability, and automating processes. This reduces reliance on non-digital document exchange, improves data integrity, and facilitates compliance with regulations. Overall, it fosters a more efficient, reliable, and user-friendly digital ecosystem.

Core Location Vocabulary:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/solution/core-location-vocabulary/release/100'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:847f9b8f-44bc-4fc0-a431-a469c42dbbcd .

camssa:f8fdf3de-1d84-4875-9f81-bae46e180767 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f903f477-e116-4cb0-af1f-4de143b95f8d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Up to date, there is no specific mechanism to assess the IPsec conformity in the IPsec documentation.\r
\r
IPSec reference, Conformance Requirements:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301#section-10\r
\r
IPSec reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca642e68-52e6-4e80-bd08-1d30a63bb783 .

camssa:f90bdc95-7129-4fc2-adf3-e8fed5e34a03 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:f91121fb-0651-44f2-902b-7f03ff23b17a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IPv4 specification plays a foundational role in enabling data portability between systems or applications in terms of network communication. Moreover, mechanisms such as IPsec ensures that data is secure transfered between systems.

IPv4 IETF:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791

IPsec protocol:
https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/network-layer/what-is-ipsec/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:78b06aea-af63-4920-b5ba-c3698d2897b4 .

camssa:f913b939-29d4-43a2-9302-497867ed2ed7 a cav:Score,
