camssa:f9e125a2-b95d-4ca2-a667-bb161167fdec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OASIS has defined a clear Technical Committee (hereby TC) process where all the stakeholders involved have the opportunity to participate in the development of the specification development process. \r
All the information related to a TC activity is hosted and can be consulted. \r
See: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process-2017-05-26"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:99593b93-e486-4185-b771-e648977e8213 .

camssa:f9e153f9-4ed5-47d1-8472-eae72e2d8939 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:515dd3bd-1d15-4638-a08e-0b23ca6aa066 .

camssa:f9e7d5f1-a498-4e48-bec9-8fe5ac88d19b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TOSCA is widely known in the field of cloud computing, since it runs on a container (or software unit) and specifies orchestration process models that enable the management of services independently of the application context. In this sense, the specification can be used beyond the business-specific domain and allows its implementation across any business domain.\r
\r
TOSCA reference:\r
https://docs.oasis-open.org/tosca/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML/v1.3/os/TOSCA-Simple-Profile-YAML-v1.3-os.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ed60b0a0-c47d-4dfd-8900-af8f4e13f795 .

camssa:f9fcdeee-d500-4716-a902-43a16d1983f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is relevant for administrations and services providers to be compliant with eIDAS. It is recommended and used in several services related to eIDAS compliance. Therefore, it is a clear specification that can be the center of discussions for the improvement of it and the services implementing it. \r
\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 422 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319400_319499/319422/01.01.01_60/en_319422v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7e99deb6-a5fe-4447-bf34-369ea7c0c6e8 .

