camssa:fa691bef-55d4-4a72-bfe6-7a84615d8721 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has been found few academic papers addressing the effectiveness and efficiency of E-ARK tools. One of them describes It describes E-ARK eco-system, analysing the E-ARK Specifications for Common Information Package, and shows some success stories from its implementation.\r
\r
Metadata profiles for interoperability : the E-ARK specifications for e-archiving:\r
https://www.torrossa.com/it/resources/an/5004900'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:229ca58e-f4f4-447f-b3d2-f5d8cbcaf482 .

camssa:fa6e1f1f-2b04-4aa1-9e52-69493af93a68 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SAMM includes recommendations on data protection and requirements for the proper protection and management of relevant data over their lifetime and also over time. More specifically, it is written down under the operational management and the first stream, which states the outcomes and need of establishing a data catalogue.\r
\r
SAMM webpage:\r
https://owaspsamm.org\r
\r
SAMM Documentation: \r
https://github.com/OWASP/samm/blob/master/Supporting%20Resources/v2.0/OWASP-SAMM-v2.0.pdf"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd05cfa1-0e5f-4006-b73a-cc985231ac65 .

camssa:fa6e343f-ea8e-44ed-b775-222ef44fb581 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of Ogg is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
Ogg XIPH reference:\r
https://xiph.org/ogg/doc/rfc3533.txt"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1107f61d-5d58-4980-b9e9-bce6d143fa21 .

camssa:fa7c5dcd-d2e3-466a-b312-263769d5bbbe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ISO 3166 Maintenance Agency is responsible for providing public support for any request regarding ISO 3166-1, but does not define the country names itself; the country names come from United Nations (UN) sources.\r
\r
ISO reference, ISO 3166 Country Codes:\r
https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html?msclkid=54aebe8ca9f611ec89ac280389b78309'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:77bb83ce-3abf-40cd-ac7a-9e0eff950e0c .

camssa:fa8070b2-9606-486c-a364-10194958f4b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) has some specific provisions regarding multilingualism mainly related at the naming of the assets and is characteristics but the specification per se is not multilingual.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dc6e7aa7-f6fd-4acb-ada7-c8f006c590fc .

camssa:fa847e68-10fa-4455-a775-4a7c23efe3ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While it uses the EU’s General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) as a guiding source for the creation and interpretation of concepts, the ambition and scope of DPV is to provide a broad globally useful vocabulary that can be extended to jurisdiction or domain specific applications.\r
\r
DPV primer document:\r
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/#introduction\r
\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c210fdd7-7149-44ab-9170-ae9ae53e3866 .

