camssa:fb05faf1-7924-45aa-a974-011dcfd6c6ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx is itself a tool to assess the conformity of RDF data graphs against correspondent schemas. Moreover, W3C provides the ShEx Simple Online Validator,  an online tool that allows performing RDF data validation using Shape Expressions.\r
\r
ShEx Simple Online Validator:\r
https://rawgit.com/shexSpec/shex.js/master/packages/shex-webapp/doc/shex-simple.html\r
\r
ShEx primer document:\r
https://shexspec.github.io/primer/\r
\r
ShEx Community Group:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/\r
\r
ShEx Github:\r
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues\r
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:14992c66-5d10-4120-8cbb-f60df4b78657 .

camssa:fb115485-a317-48d0-88c7-be7f02cd5c56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WAI-ARIA was conceived for assistive web technologies. As it was created to enhance e-accessibility and to simplify web navigation, it can be used in any other domain as a visibility enhancement. It is the case of Google Extensions with which the user can customise web content by means of the HTML Document Object Model (HTML DOM).\r
\r
WAI-ARIA reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria/\r
\r
WAI-ARIA Chrome Extension reference:\r
https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv3/a11y/#aria'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:36569494-93e7-48bb-835b-f2f9f488b122 .

camssa:fb1322a2-3df1-4cbb-a9db-b48204bb4e37 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "40" .

camssa:fb16397e-fe77-4980-b89e-dee7f7f6b2f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XHTML is maintained by the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C), an international community dedicated to
developing open standards. This collaboration ensures that web technologies remain accessible,
interoperable, and beneficial to users globally.

XHTML W3C reference
https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/

Developer community W3C:
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1386ba98-6d84-453b-aaaf-52702c777773 .

camssa:fb1784e4-e877-4aa7-bd44-e154de290ccb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'WSDL (Web Services Description Language) does enable the exposure of interfaces for web services, including those offered by public administrations. By defining a standardized way to describe the functionalities, operations, and communication protocols of a web service, WSDL makes these services accessible and usable by external systems and applications.  WSDL can be combined with other specifications and technologies to enable the exposure of interfaces for accessing services. WSDL, on its own, provides a standardized way to describe the interface and operations of a web service. However, the complete exposure of interfaces often requires additional components and considerations.\r
\r
W3C WSDL specification:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl20/#Interface'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cf310e44-50f6-4faf-aeb7-c7555bd23645 .

