camssa:0a488d85-d1a3-4f3c-8ed9-d9fdf4e6895c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML, which inherently supports customisation. In this context, UBL adopts a similar approach, allowing for tailored implementations while maintaining a core structure._x000D_
Certain elements within UBL are mandatory and cannot be customised, ensuring consistency and interoperability. However, once these required components are in place, users have the flexibility to select additional elements according to their specific needs, choosing the subset of UBL elements most relevant to their business transactions._x000D_
_x000D_
XML customisation:_x000D_
https://www.xml.com/articles/2017/01/01/what-is-ubl/#d0e126_x000D_
_x000D_
Customisation and extension of UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/guidelines/UBL2-Customization1.0cs01.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b33d841f-c147-4c20-a6e3-a7a821f2090d .

camssa:0d1f95bb-f27c-432f-a425-712d4ab515be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML, which supports a range of security mechanisms that are also compatible with UBL. One such mechanism is the XML Signature Syntax and Processing specification (XMLDSig), which is supported by both XML and UBL._x000D_
XMLDSig enables authentication of the document sender and verification of data integrity, ensuring that the content has not been altered during transmission and that the origin of the document can be reliably confirmed._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47b10db6-2f69-4dac-9d16-73fde07c189a .

