camssa:11e003ce-e6b4-4f2b-a049-d8fb5610ca0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is designed to integrate seamlessly with existing business, accounting, legal, auditing, and records management practices. By eliminating the need to re-key data, common in traditional fax, scanned-image, and paper-based supply chains, UBL offers a gateway to electronic business for small and medium-sized enterprises._x000D_
As a result, UBL enhances both internal and external visibility of administrative procedures and data. It also facilitates the delivery of European public services, as exemplified by its role in the ESPD project._x000D_
_x000D_
ESPD Project UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/technical/tech_architecture.html_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d493e98-c95b-4e83-981c-cb426b5a0e47 .

camssa:136ae6f4-c280-4b44-b07b-f750e1c7a89c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL was developed through the open and transparent work of an OASIS Technical Committee, involving contributions from numerous international and industry data standards bodies. First ratified as an OASIS Standard in 2004, it has since become one of the most established and widely implemented standards in the OASIS ecosystem._x000D_
_x000D_
In 2014, the European Commission declared UBL 2.1 officially eligible for referencing in tenders issued by public administrations. UBL is also integrated into the European Single Procurement Document (ESPD), a self-declaration form designed to simplify tendering procedures in public procurement at the EU level and adapted for use in national schemes._x000D_
_x000D_
Furthermore, UBL has been increasingly adopted by several countries for business transactions between enterprises and public administrations, as it provides a standardised and interoperable format for communication between organisations._x000D_
_x000D_
ESPD Project UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/technical/tech_architecture.html_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL adoption:_x000D_
https://www.b2brouter.net/global/what-is-ubl-format/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a64a1499-fcc8-4743-9d50-30164c571348 .

camssa:14891963-0f77-45f1-b4f9-a5a4244c3675 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is the product of the OASIS Technical Committee, with participation from a diverse range of international and industry data standards organisations. Originally approved as an OASIS Standard in 2004, it is now one of the most mature and widely implemented standards within the OASIS framework._x000D_
_x000D_
In 2014, the European Commission officially recognised UBL 2.1 as eligible for referencing in public sector tenders. The following year, UBL 2.1 was also approved as ISO/IEC 19845:2015, establishing it as a true international standard for use by governmental bodies worldwide. This endorsement represents the highest level of formal recognition attainable for an international standard._x000D_
_x000D_
The UBL 2.3 version, approved in 2021, introduced minor updates as part of a minor release. And the latest version, UBL 2.4, launched in 2024, follows the same incremental approach and increases the range of different business documents._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL history:_x000D_
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ubl_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d5dc81e-c5b6-45b0-a1bc-4f9cc028af1f .

camssa:153b0bbd-48aa-45c1-906c-a38ad32d6b32 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:159da9e0-4407-4aa5-a098-1e2090fe5245 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is primarily intended for use within the business domain. However, while it focuses on the exchange of business documents, it can also be effectively applied in other sectors such as healthcare, accounting, legal, auditing, and various areas of public administration._x000D_
In this context, it is worth highlighting that UBL is increasingly being used by businesses to communicate with public administrations, reflecting its versatility and growing adoption beyond its original scope._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:566e4f7c-2f35-4347-bdfb-8f667b17b773 .

camssa:1b98a39b-7848-41bf-98c2-b1010503faf3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is included in 5 Member States catalogues of recommended specifications. These _x000D_
Member States are Croatia, Denmark, Greece, Malta, and The Netherlands._x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Croatia:_x000D_
https://ssi.gov.hr/en/catalogue_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Denmark:_x000D_
https://arkitektur.digst.dk/sites/default/fileuploads/white_paper_on_a_common_public-sector_digital_architecture_pdfa.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Greece:_x000D_
https://www.e-gif.gov.gr/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/744027.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Malta:_x000D_
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of The Netherlands:_x000D_
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standard_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48618ad0-205a-4b72-a133-f8396644396c .

camssa:216611f9-76c1-478a-be69-077a02d94d7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'When existing UBL entities do not fully address specific business requirements, new entities can be introduced as extensions. These extensions build upon the original entities by linking to them and incorporating additional information, effectively creating an expanded version of the original structure._x000D_
_x000D_
Customisation and extension of UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/guidelines/UBL2-Customization1.0cs01.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cfb00802-8c3e-49c8-8751-ff9a7e69066f .

camssa:2207e2a2-f838-402c-89fd-03e87c208d3a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:304539fa-b5f4-40e8-ab1b-a5e378911a27 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is used by PEPPOL. PEPPOL (Pan European Public Procurement Online) is an international network that enables businesses worldwide to exchange electronic documents securely and easily, following a common standard adapted to the needs of each country. In this context, the UBL specification has been defined as a global standard to facilitate the exchange of electronic documents among companies from different countries._x000D_
In addition, the UBL specification is used in both the ESPD and OOTS projects. In the case of OOTS, public entities in the Netherlands use the specification to receive eInvoices. For this purpose, two UBL specialisations have been proposed for eInvoicing: UBL-OHNL and SI-UBL._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL OOTS:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/einvoicingCFS/pages/406257983/Netherlands+2021+eInvoicing+Country+Sheet_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL-OHNL reference:_x000D_
https://www.logius.nl/domeinen/gegevensuitwisseling/e-procurement/documentatie/ubl-ohnl_x000D_
_x000D_
SI-UBL reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/Peppolautoriteit-nl/validation_x000D_
_x000D_
PEPPOL reference:_x000D_
https://peppol.com/_x000D_
_x000D_
ESPD Project UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/technical/tech_architecture.html_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e357164b-dcea-47af-bb72-aade87783cab .

camssa:35ec3022-5b7f-4154-ae6e-474c4736b6c8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:36430f72-4560-4401-bc5d-b4be70c12b53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification facilitates digital service delivery channels by digitising processes that were previously carried out manually. Based on XML, it provides a standardised and interoperable data structure that enhances digital communication between users exchanging business documents, such as between public administrations and businesses. Consequently, the specification helps to streamline various procedures by enabling efficient digital service delivery._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5188dbea-8510-4bec-8b00-920e7cba71d1 .

camssa:38db271f-c7b1-4f0a-8ca6-02fa805df6d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the UBL specification has been assed by the Faculty of Engineering at the University of Porto. In the "A Business Language for a Distributed Simulation Framework" study, the UBL specification is proposed as a business language to promote semantic interoperability within a distributed simulation framework, facilitating communication between industrial simulation models._x000D_
_x000D_
"A Business language for a distributed simulation framework" study:_x000D_
https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Carlos-Braganca-3/publication/241186215_A_business_language_for_a_distributed_simulation_framework/links/0c96051c838d912f10000000/A-business-language-for-a-distributed-simulation-framework.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce1fe847-3893-434e-b340-5dea91c772be .

