camssa:640e8b85-6720-45fb-90a4-662e0b431e34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML. XML format, particularly through XAdES (XML Advanced Electronic Signatures), is recognised by the eIDAS Regulation as a compliant format for advanced electronic signatures. _x000D_
_x000D_
Overview of Standards for eIDAS document: https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/assessment-of-standards-related-to-eidas_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation: _x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb7059ad-28ff-400a-b256-2768555933b5 .

camssa:6476148c-ecbf-4878-9a85-466c16add90c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the UBL specification has been assed by the Fachhochschule Nordwestschweiz Olten (Basel), Switzerland, and the School of Science and Technology - University of Camerino, Italy. In the "The UBL Standard and its Potential in the Exchange of Industrial Data" study, it is concluded that UBL has significantly evolved to cover more detailed phases of business processes, especially in delivery and e-procurement._x000D_
_x000D_
"The UBL Standard and its Potential in the Exchange of Industrial Data" study:_x000D_
https://d1wqtxts1xzle7.cloudfront.net/89803279/EEE2893-libre.pdf?1660726010=&response-content-disposition=inline%3B+filename%3DThe_UBL_Standard_and_its_Potential_in_th.pdf&Expires=1754043009&Signature=WkPeZJ~ubx2R-yEDIsHD-RQ2LktCrT5LD~tKFp5fyM6i~soMhEekM-kfQATH5EpI6s-Ph4sh~Hd48iBALFUsQDIh9nB2BvBHRNrE6AmQWyRa2HVH46QlAhPlIN2ArNSUGGeH5mq~BbQkWk7hbN-PlPwhzIjKgkKyYX1apdxHDMXw-V0h1xIdb8D1DUD5xe0K04a~-10y7bukQeudWJ-mcROxPQv3YA5jad5~xzPRzMl29SCJE2aufZ7lYe86TjR8o-XtwTomJWRWrnyuzeZ9L6s4vZo~i~fZ~Upbbj9EqHiYEIpJ4zT5mz5CUGQ7xup0~XFvLd0jVz~QyEhlxzfBLw__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAJLOHF5GGSLRBV4ZA_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ceb99f4-ef88-407c-88a6-c752a907a68c .

camssa:66a98807-47d0-4c7d-bb39-230365813062 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6ee41e80-a8fb-4bb3-94ba-6ca7d34c40f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is developed by OASIS, a non-European organisation. However, it is used by many European countries and has also been adopted in different European projects. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OASIS organisation:_x000D_
https://www.oasis-open.org/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:10e1f2ec-32b6-4598-9a58-e5700729eddc .

camssa:70e219b0-17e9-4e1d-8c44-323c93c2c55a a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/2eda9b22-7b34-4bf0-af02-2a836637cfdb"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:71153bd8-ee0e-4b8e-b548-029091b1c825 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:72c3fcba-7b9d-49b4-a124-6a518d1dfe98 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7309f964-ee75-46d4-8895-628961d0e03c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification does not directly define or expose technical interfaces for accessing public administration services. However, it is built upon XML, which provides a standardised, machine-readable data structure that facilitates the development and exposure of such interfaces._x000D_
Additionally, UBL has been adopted by several countries to support the exchange of documents between businesses and public administrations, owing to its ease of readability and efficient data processing capabilities._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8ef58be-7408-487a-9087-1bf2e5f84185 .

camssa:78886b20-4959-4eea-998d-a006470adefe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As the UBL specification is based on XML, it supports multilingualism by accommodating all writing systems. Consequently, any language can be used within XML. In this sense, XML can be encoded using formats such as UTF-8, ensuring that all languages are accurately represented in XML documents. Furthermore, the UBL specification complements this by providing a defined structure to manage multilingual texts within the document itself._x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:153b0bbd-48aa-45c1-906c-a38ad32d6b32 .

camssa:7afff8ca-bd49-40cd-9dfa-cc603c10b961 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification, based on XML, does not itself include built-in mechanisms for guaranteeing the authenticity or authentication of the roles or agents involved in data transactions. However, complementary specifications such as XAdES, an extension of XMLDSig, can be employed to address this need. XAdES enables the authentication of agents participating in data exchanges, thereby enhancing trust and accountability in electronic transactions._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:66a98807-47d0-4c7d-bb39-230365813062 .

camssa:7ec81bd4-a02a-4913-8309-35b693ca4623 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7f95df88-c147-4ccc-8c2c-aeeee11aa7fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification does not offer any mechanism to provide access control. In this regard, there are complementary mechanisms and specifications that help to enhance data security, such as verifying whether data has been altered and protecting it, but none establishes access control mechanisms per se. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b6c2038-593f-4328-9e3c-88f441cf6d17 .

camssa:820c4c77-c3fd-4c98-89a4-042a372d64ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is intended to define a generic XML interchange format for business documents. In this context, XML serves as both a markup language and a file format for storing, transmitting, and reconstructing arbitrary data. It is particularly well-suited for publishing data on the web. In this regard, UBL supports the five stars in Tim Berners-Lee’s deployment scheme by enabling the linking of data to other resources. Specifically, the UBL specification allows attachments to be included, providing references to related documentation._x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11/_x000D_
_x000D_
Tim Berners-Lee 5 star open data: _x000D_
https://5stardata.info/en/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL Reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d6f70d11-664c-47bd-bbda-2111e451496d .

camssa:86674617-71ec-423f-87ad-2651d7f3ca0f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of UBL is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5900f725-117d-4f2d-ba9e-4666de1dcdf2 .

camssa:87e0ca12-a933-405f-af14-37501a396338 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The use of UBL offers many benefits for modelling business processes, including detailed textual descriptions, explanations, and examples for each of its specified functions and messages. It also provides clear rules for extension, alongside various subsets and tool resources._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a1c627a1-9ba7-4663-9339-2ea595db000e .

camssa:8b6c2038-593f-4328-9e3c-88f441cf6d17 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9aafadc8-055c-45e3-8518-342c82ea1ae8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More _x000D_
specifically, UBL can define the interoperability aspects of the "Controlled Vocabulary", "Data Model" and "Ontology" ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4399e8f6-f483-4915-b729-7a83dd6c8879 .

camssa:9c37af88-9e4c-4268-8bfb-13bebc22eb47 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a1c627a1-9ba7-4663-9339-2ea595db000e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a3ec8059-283b-491b-8bad-db1d752c4a34 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a64a1499-fcc8-4743-9d50-30164c571348 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a86a9498-245e-4d2a-9050-3700f6b708d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on the XML standard, which enables the separation of information through the use of tags and attributes. This approach makes the structure of data clearer and more accessible for users working with it._x000D_
By leveraging XML, the UBL specification promotes comprehensibility, offering a straightforward and user-friendly method for understanding business documents._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71153bd8-ee0e-4b8e-b548-029091b1c825 .

camssa:b034bc8a-fd9f-4524-ae91-457017611c27 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "90.95%AssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string,
        "100%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b04039d0-5647-4649-8ba3-33a38adf5941 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As defined by the OASIS Technical Committee (TC), the UBL TC plays an active role in the release lifecycle of the specification. External contributions to the committee are welcomed through open channels. To date, the UBL TC has announced several public reviews, each providing a specific period of time for users to submit comments. The most recent invitation for comment was issued in August 2025, concerning UBL v2.5 CSD01._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL OASIS Technical Committee reference:_x000D_
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ubl_x000D_
_x000D_
Invitation to comment on UBL v2.5 CSD01 reference:_x000D_
https://groups.oasis-open.org/discussion/invitation-to-comment-on-ubl-v25-csd01_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5047ea3e-5e7f-437c-b4e8-573ed8931ee3 .

camssa:b33d841f-c147-4c20-a6e3-a7a821f2090d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b3952f51-a82d-4fbf-b27c-190882d775d0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Similar to the XML specification, the UBL specification also supports partial implementations. While certain mandatory elements must be included, the specification offers over 4,000 business objects described as XML elements, which users can selectively adopt based on their specific requirements._x000D_
This flexibility allows implementers to include only the elements relevant to their use case, avoiding unnecessary complexity and streamlining integration._x000D_
_x000D_
XML customisation:_x000D_
https://www.xml.com/articles/2017/01/01/what-is-ubl/#d0e126_x000D_
_x000D_
Customisation and extension of UBL:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/guidelines/UBL2-Customization1.0cs01.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f7156f90-90bc-4bb3-96ff-eed2152c300c .

camssa:b454168a-6abe-4130-aeeb-7dbdd238f932 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification has been selected for referencing in public procurement, as it is mentioned in the Commission implementig decision of 31 October 2014 on the identification of Universal Business Language version 2.1 for referencing in public procurement._x000D_
_x000D_
"Commission implementig decision of 31 October 2014 on the identification of Universal Business Language version 2.1 for referencing in public procurement" document:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32014D0771&qid=1754043193358_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ec81bd4-a02a-4913-8309-35b693ca4623 .

camssa:b4a858e0-eb80-40aa-905e-25b7dc1cf386 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b81ec949-a8c1-4e0a-a270-9d90f5ce66c1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification, based on XML, does not inherently provide protection against unauthorised changes to the information it represents. However, specifications such as XAdES and XMLDsig can help verify whether data has been altered at any point during the transaction, ensuring that the data is intact and exactly as originally sent._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d286cf69-37da-4c8e-9c17-e522f1ca1ba4 .

camssa:bad0faaa-cd92-42e1-9a21-cfbe9d2c4191 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bc9f209a-0368-4f5e-8d13-a6e67362788e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bcfea64a-b4ab-4c86-af95-0f281fad5c9e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML and offers a standardised data structure that facilitates the exchange of business documents between organisations. Therefore, the specification is ideal for avoiding manual procedures, making the process more efficient, and ensuring that all organisations are capable of reading the exchanged data._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5db9e0e4-1d5d-4aa9-a0a3-e8f689820ffd .

camssa:bf7b4a61-cc4f-4321-9fe8-e570192c7b7f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bff2b20c-f467-47de-bee3-36222220a022 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL is based on the XML specification, which supports various mechanisms to protect data and enhance security against unauthorised changes. It can be complemented by other specifications such as XAdES and XMLDSig, which enable verification of whether data has been modified at any stage of the transaction. These complementary specifications and security mechanisms offer a range of capabilities to ensure that the data is as accurate and reliable as possible._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5144b390-0f2f-4a92-9f69-20ea59835979 .

camssa:c2d58a14-91de-4ac3-8162-c71407834077 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c7eeb894-3ba1-49b6-b322-da8d32bc7c20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML and, as such, supports security mechanisms applicable to XML, including XML Digital Signatures (XMLDSig), XAdES, and others._x000D_
To ensure a certain level of data protection, the specification allows for methods such as information encryption and digital signing. These measures help safeguard the integrity and confidentiality of the data exchanged, ensuring that documents are transmitted securely and remain unaltered by unauthorised parties._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4a858e0-eb80-40aa-905e-25b7dc1cf386 .

camssa:c8aabb75-63a2-449b-aaf4-29d4b78e3be7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification does not depend on any specific technology and is entirely agnostic with respect to web infrastructure. Moreover, as it is based on XML, which itself is technology-agnostic, the UBL specification is considered fully independent of underlying technological platforms._x000D_
This neutrality allows UBL to be implemented across a wide range of systems and environments, enhancing its adaptability and long-term relevance._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL technology and platform agnostic reference:_x000D_
https://www.ibiblio.org/bosak/ubl/pres/generic-ubl-overview.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:72c3fcba-7b9d-49b4-a124-6a518d1dfe98 .

camssa:c8ef58be-7408-487a-9087-1bf2e5f84185 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c9681c9a-8b5c-4037-8de8-3a5b1d6cd378 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cdb24f86-0d6f-48df-b102-15948a6a2e49 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification enables companies around the world to exchange electronic documents in a common language, while allowing adaptation to the fiscal requirements of each receiving country._x000D_
By conforming to UBL, all business document types remain machine-readable, thereby enhancing interoperability between systems. This standardised approach to document exchange ensures consistency, efficiency, and seamless integration across diverse platforms and jurisdictions._x000D_
_x000D_
b2brouter UBL:_x000D_
https://www.b2brouter.net/global/what-is-ubl-format/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3d03e3f1-0a85-4479-bea9-97b647e72a50 .

camssa:ce1fe847-3893-434e-b340-5dea91c772be a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cfb00802-8c3e-49c8-8751-ff9a7e69066f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cfd86d1a-d19b-4dbd-9171-27c6d0c14b1a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'UBL facilitates and simplifies the delivery of European public services by enabling automated data transactions. Additionally, the specification is based on XML, which provides a standardised data structure that eases interpretation by information systems. As a result, the need for manual intervention and more complex procedures can be avoided, thereby streamlining and simplifying the delivery of public services._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec8cd704-c879-4e5b-90e7-93467383a9bc .

camssa:d0a60760-27b6-48fa-963c-c370c6f3b691 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d286cf69-37da-4c8e-9c17-e522f1ca1ba4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d5c4dbf8-c25a-4445-b17f-eed13657f16d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification does not rely on any particular platform and is entirely agnostic in this regard. Additionally, as it is based on XML, which functions across all browsers and applications that support it, the UBL specification is considered platform-agnostic._x000D_
This broad compatibility ensures that UBL can be implemented in diverse technological environments without requiring platform-specific adaptations._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL technology and platform agnostic reference:_x000D_
https://www.ibiblio.org/bosak/ubl/pres/generic-ubl-overview.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c2d58a14-91de-4ac3-8162-c71407834077 .

camssa:d6ede308-610e-4781-b433-e359d9046369 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML, and therefore supports all mechanisms applicable to the XML standard. In this context, technologies such as encryption and the XML Signature Syntax and Processing specification (XMLDSig) can be applied to UBL documents. These mechanisms help ensure that data remains inaccessible to unauthorised parties during transmission and that the information received has not been altered in transit, thereby preserving both confidentiality and integrity._x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bad0faaa-cd92-42e1-9a21-cfbe9d2c4191 .

camssa:d6f70d11-664c-47bd-bbda-2111e451496d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:de45097f-b717-4bc3-8cd4-973e1ec9a872 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The UBL specification is based on XML, which supports other specifications such as XAdES. In this context, the digital signature features of UBL, particularly through integration with XAdES, provide the technical means to ensure the integrity, authenticity, and long-term validity of the data contained in UBL documents._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:35ec3022-5b7f-4154-ae6e-474c4736b6c8 .

camssa:e2b0f224-1418-4f0e-b865-564eeb09a909 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As an XML-based specification, UBL enables consistent data reuse across systems. Although it does not include explicit provisions dedicated to this topic, its foundation in XML inherently supports structured, repeatable data handling. The specification defines a set of rules for encoding documents in both human-readable and machine-readable formats, thereby enhancing data reusability and promoting interoperability between systems and services._x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0dd2cfad-6747-47d3-ae52-b0138f109b64 .

camssa:e2cc6fb4-a73b-46dc-905e-7797f8721879 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Implementations of the UBL specification can be assessed through the Interoperability Test Bed, available on the Interoperable Europe Portal. Specifically, the Interoperability Test Bed includes a dedicated page to validate UBL XML implementations. Additionally, there are other platforms available online for validating UBL implementations._x000D_
_x000D_
ITestBed UBL XML validator:_x000D_
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/ubl/upload_x000D_
_x000D_
UBL specification reference:_x000D_
https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.4/UBL-2.4.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a3ec8059-283b-491b-8bad-db1d752c4a34 .

