camssa:1fedecea-8dd0-48cd-82d8-701474a388a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile is based on XML and XML documents are based on Unicode, which supports all writing systems. Therefore, any language can be used in an XML document. Additionally, XML (both 1.0 and 1.1) can be encoded using formats like UTF-8, ensuring that all languages can be properly included and represented in XML documents. In addition, it is worth mentioning that in the XML 1.0 specification is mentioned that all XML processors must accept the UTF-8 and UTF-16 encodings of Unicode. However, certain Unicode encodings, like UTF-16, can result in larger file sizes compared to single-byte encodings, potentially impacting storage and transmission efficiency._x000D_
_x000D_
UTF-8 reference: _x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3629_x000D_
_x000D_
UTF-16 reference: https://www.iso.org/standard/76835.html _x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.0 reference: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/ _x000D_
_x000D_
XML 1.1 W3C reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml11_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:635c24c9-07c8-45ed-ac8e-2ae6d0a47957 .

