camssa:44710203-6d3e-41d2-b1f1-418533a572a3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XAdES was originally developed by W3C and has become one of the main ways to develop suitable security controls and mechanisms in place to protect digital transactions and to ensure trust and confidence among organisations. The XAdES Baseline Profile specification has evolved through several minor and one major releases to address emerging requirements and refine the specfication documentation (which can be superseeded by national recommendations in Europe). According to the change history section of the XAdES specification, the first official release dates back to December 2011, with continuous improvements. It is important to note that the latest version is 1.3.1 (released in July 2024), addressing bug fixes or incremental changes._x000D_
_x000D_
The version 1.2.1 includes core functionalities, but subsequent versions—culminating in 1.3.1—have introduced enhancements, particularly related to the ArchiveTimeStamp element. These updates improve the handling of the signature date in the counter-signature process, enhancing long-term validation and compliance with archival standards, which enables the evolution of electronic signature to evolving digital signature requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Advanced Electronic Signatures (XAdES): _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/XAdES/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dee3ee26-7d38-4c62-83d0-fb6edc985188 .

camssa:44bf8420-a17d-47e6-a28b-dcab2ba18422 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "91.11%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string,
        "92.68%AssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4bd06fb1-b1c6-47c5-a175-473d9fdb2b64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the XAdES baseline Profile is not related to data processing but with the usage of some XML based complimentary specifications like W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing it can be assured that data remains inaccessible and in the same form as it was sent._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Encryption Syntax and Processing reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/ _x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c8ed6cd-a35d-4c93-b83b-9e3534420cd8 .

camssa:4c8ed6cd-a35d-4c93-b83b-9e3534420cd8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4f4d4a5e-81a5-410e-aa6f-fb001d9ae6d7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES baseline Profile main purpose is to provide the stakeholders involved in any electronic transaction with the certainty that the exchanged documents are truthful for all. _x000D_
In this sense there are other XML based specifications that can complement XAdES, specifications like W3C XML Encryption Syntax and Processing, that provides the stakeholders with the capabilities to encrypt electronic transactions thus fostering security._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Encryption Syntax and Processing reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98f30edb-cede-4a4d-8596-09e556ab24fb .

camssa:50f84c11-46f6-4c85-92a4-b5385d61561f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XAdES Baseline Profile is a business sector agnostic specification which is reusable beyond the domain for which it was developed. Specifically, implemented to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a75bd2c-7245-40c5-a253-830fbdfba02a .

camssa:53e88d51-01fe-4bf4-b155-37215c9c9b09 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:551f0f8f-0093-453c-8f17-c29f2a1e59cc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The XAdES Baseline Profile is designed to guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the agents involved in data transactions. It achieves this by focusing on the signer's identity and their role, which is a core requirement of the eIDAS regulation._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a986f563-ac72-4b8a-8e11-b50cfff92597 .

camssa:596830dd-ea9b-49b2-bd07-c5172dc39bb6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5e3ee7e9-807f-4066-aa68-1f44b6c8f361 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile specifies profiles based on XMLDSig that ensure compliance with European legal requirements. XAdES guarantees that signed data remains authentic, integral, and legally defensible when transmitted or archived. Additionally, the specification can be combined with other mechanisms such as XML encryption or XMLDSig itself, allowing selective use of its XML-compliant parts to further enhance security capabilities._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C XML Signature Syntax and Processing Version 1.1: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c01b6791-3eef-4bf5-a747-2d87f782c582 .

camssa:624d194b-9014-4fe8-952c-a40cb2d7a787 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:635c24c9-07c8-45ed-ac8e-2ae6d0a47957 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:66ca3814-7f3b-44a2-a172-f0b8ee53b9b4 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/95a6d93a-505e-4f2c-9ede-9fe6071aa6ee"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:67832bd6-ed91-4105-885b-9a98bc9dbe57 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the XAdES Baseline Profile is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:399451ab-0a6b-4854-9cde-941b4e97cc0a .

camssa:6b092155-cf4f-4941-8fa4-3406e0eb8635 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile includes mechanisms for long-term validation, such as timestamps and embedded certificate information. This means that a signed public record or contract can be securely archived and remain legally verifiable for some time. In this sense the preservation of the date of signature is a partial preservation of the record._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3bb1dd77-1200-4d61-9d11-e6a149836211 .

camssa:6c83284d-58fc-43d3-9bda-548c2c75023d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:700dc454-b5c7-4f96-ab3a-44e47c9ca639 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:728a35b0-c7c4-4848-af65-efdbd67f0d8d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:77a9a670-037f-4b1a-bdbc-003003a6d902 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7a1e52f4-62e2-48cc-a080-0ff7fc89a0bd a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7e4aa8da-05ef-4f1e-8551-26f12847cc6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the XAdES specification has been assessed by several individual authors at the Open Identity Summit 2019, dedicated to link practical experiences and requirements with academic innovations. The "Security Analysis of XAdES Validation in the CEF Digital Signature Services (DSS)" study, addresses XAdES as a key functionality of the demonstration service of the Digital Signature Services (DSS) of the Connecting Europe Facility (CEF). The research focuses specifically on the signature verification functionality for XAdES implemented by this service, noting that DSS enables the validation of generic XAdES to verify arbitrarily signed XML documents. Furthermore, it highlights that XAdES is one of the signature formats supported by the DSS library, in line with the eIDAS regulation and compliant with the relevant ETSI standards._x000D_
_x000D_
"Security Analysis of XAdES Validation in the CEF Digital Signature Services (DSS)" study:_x000D_
https://dl.gi.de/items/17c4b8a1-e160-40a5-b598-28e27ae3018d_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:596830dd-ea9b-49b2-bd07-c5172dc39bb6 .

camssa:80a27284-b434-41e6-b7a8-aa7073e12a5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS regulation. The signature of a document can provide the involved stakeholders with the possibility to use the extensions (like XML encryption specification and other complementary specifications) on the schema in order to define specific legal or policy references relevant to the context of the signed document like confidentiality._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3fd53065-2c6d-4a46-bab1-abb5aef18365 .

camssa:81f1dda7-cc0d-4a0c-8e4a-ba141166d655 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:84c4db0b-2764-4185-b3be-5b9c88d757f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

