camssa:926a5f4e-23c4-4702-9b0a-e92b1191a584 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the XAdES Baseline Profile is not related to modelling business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:149b6a82-794c-4dbf-8e5e-a63f4b55ee9c .

camssa:9351dc9e-ef51-4338-b837-9242675c81a2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9539982c-476b-497c-a64a-1b258f45fc5f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile is a set of well-defined technical specifications developed by ETSI to ensure both interoperability and legal validity of electronic signatures across Europe, in line with the eIDAS Regulation._x000D_
_x000D_
The specification includes several signature levels: XAdES-B-B, XAdES-B-T, XAdES-B-LT, and XAdES-B-LT, which can be implemented individually based on the desired properties. These levels are designed to be incremental, meaning that a basic signature (e.g. XAdES-B-B) can be progressively enhanced to include additional features like timestamps or long-term validation data, depending on user or system requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation: https://digital-strategy._x000D_
ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8ff87603-7eb0-46a0-9161-ab7b51b986ee .

camssa:98f30edb-cede-4a4d-8596-09e556ab24fb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9d80af4f-14a7-46b9-90f5-135933918184 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"XAdES Baseline Profile guarantees authenticity by cryptographically linking the signature to a specific individual and their certificate. It enables the authentication of roles by providing a dedicated element for including this information within the signature, which is a powerful feature for applications where the signer's function is as important as their identity. In this sense the schema based on XML provides with enough flexibility to include some control mechanisms based on the signature identity._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53e88d51-01fe-4bf4-b155-37215c9c9b09 .

camssa:9e9ee75b-8afc-4b27-979a-a2209dc1f2a1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile provides the involved stakeholders with a legally binding signature structure to formalise interoperability agreements. In this sense it provides the foundation of any agreement among any kind of participants._x000D_
The specification also fosters and facilitates agreements by establishing a common method for signing documents and data in a secure and trustworthy manner. This enables documents to be exchanged in an interoperable way, ensuring that all parties can access the documents and trust the information or data contained within them. By providing a standardised approach, XAdES helps to build confidence between parties and supports the reliable execution of digital transactions._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:77a9a670-037f-4b1a-bdbc-003003a6d902 .

camssa:9eb084a6-1e17-4567-a218-44e886cec7ae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9ebc9e66-e281-4a6b-ae4a-ba9a89955175 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI IPR Policy which is part of the ETSI directives seeks to reduce the risk that our standards-making efforts might be wasted if SEPs are unavailable under Fair, Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory (FRAND) terms and conditions.
The main objective of the ETSI IPR Policy is to balance the rights and interests of IPR holders to be fairly and adequately rewarded for the use of their SEPs in the implementation of ETSI standards and the need for implementers to get access to the technology defined in ETSI standards under FRAND terms and conditions.

ETSI’s intellectual property rights policy:
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d32c314a-12fc-4c5b-8900-f3e6004c6393 .

camssa:a2d6037c-28a0-4035-a93c-f63c5272f3e2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES is not related to  data portability of data between systems/applications. Therefore this criterion is not applicable._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d9bcc3cb-0a8b-4fc3-9046-8b2eca4da5a1 .

camssa:a5d5b8a3-c9c6-4e6b-907a-0e65cbd6650a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:edf7b454-522d-4db9-a6db-01dd42d695ab .

camssa:a986f563-ac72-4b8a-8e11-b50cfff92597 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:aab93812-2220-466a-bbcb-fd74358e8d29 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS. In this sense,the specification provides with the "The Signing Certificate" element, which is the public key certificate of the person or entity who signed the document and the timestamp information. This means that a system receiving the signed document doesn't need to perform an entirely new validation process from scratch. It can reuse the included data to verify the signature's authenticity._x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cfe265a8-79a3-415a-898b-86e18251bbcc .

camssa:adb4047e-198a-436e-82fb-d043fb48134d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile helps users understand the logic behind electronic signatures. XAdES achieves this by organising information in the XML through the use of tags, which separate different pieces of data and provide a clear, structured format. This separation and clarity make it easier for users to comprehend the details of the signature._x000D_
Furthermore, XAdES builds upon the XMLDSig framework, which is widely supported by applications like PDF viewers. These applications enhance user understanding by visually displaying key information such as whether the signature is valid, the date it was timestamped, and other relevant properties in a simple and straightforward way._x000D_
A practical example of this is the CEF Digital Signature Service (DSS), which leverages XAdES to provide clear and verifiable electronic signatures. Through DSS, users can easily verify signature validity and timestamp information, helping improve trust and transparency in electronic communications._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
DSS reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XMLDSig reference_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmldsig-core1/_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a1e52f4-62e2-48cc-a080-0ff7fc89a0bd .

camssa:b09e8dbb-8679-4e62-bde9-22eaea8882d3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b14d92ba-a048-4f32-a231-894e00275336 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS regulation. In this sense, the specification, in conjuction with other specifications such as CAdES, ASiC and PAdES can enable the visibility of administrative procedures, as shown with the CEF Digital Signature Service (DSS). It is worth mentioning that the specification is encoded in a machine- and human-readable text format. Thus, it can be used in a variety of environments._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
DSS reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:728a35b0-c7c4-4848-af65-efdbd67f0d8d .

camssa:b5c29b78-e525-444c-b14e-0b19190d8e41 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XAdES does not directly define or expose technical interfaces for accessing public administration services._x000D_
However, the specification provides a standardised, machine- and human-readable structure for electronic signatures, which facilitates interaction between citizens and public administrations when submitting information through public administration portals. By using the XML format, the specification eases such communication and the presentation of information through interfaces._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
DSS reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86b520f2-12d8-41cc-b13c-22d07379a135 .

camssa:b93d76cf-5278-4906-9136-db5e5a3be81e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

