camssa:be393ee1-d9a1-4ec2-bb8b-6be7d05e0208 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the XAdES baseline Profile is not related to data accuracy but the specification can be complemented with other specifications like XML Encryption Syntax and Processing to ensure that signed data remains inaccessible to unauthorised changes and thus remains in the same form as sent by the sender. Apart from that, the specification allows verification of any changes made to the document. When a document is signed, a hash code is generated by XAdES, so if the document is modified, the hash will not match and the verification process will fail. This way, it can be detected if the document has been altered._x000D_
_x000D_
XML Encryption Syntax and Processing reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlenc-core1/ _x000D_
_x000D_
XAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31913201/01.02.01_60/en_31913201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e482973f-568c-4188-acd7-0806b2576fd2 .

