camssa:0d87e4dd-282b-4e1e-bf1e-d933b9d15a0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS supports the delivery of European public services by providing a clear structure for designing and describing APIs, including their security requirements. It helps reduce administrative burden by keeping API documentation aligned with the source code and enabling users to understand and use APIs without needing to know their technical implementation._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fd086ad0-4718-448e-9f96-2f9366f26a6b .

camssa:0e94d7b9-fb0a-4e65-8965-9d34e0c78c62 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0f16d739-8dd2-4b71-9d4b-1737d05114f0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Despite the OAS being adopted by numerous organisations and projects, it does not explicitly address or cover privacy aspects. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2912f6e2-3a01-4f56-90af-f5be07e655e6 .

camssa:12784605-d9a7-47d0-9a92-e992283619e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does not directly address long-term data preservation, but its standardised and technology-independent format helps maintain the accessibility and reuse of API documentation over time, preserving knowledge about data and system interactions._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:155d5984-3701-49df-9633-2fb3299a4f8d .

camssa:127d38b8-a4c4-4889-9f85-6ed019c60b96 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:129d7637-b7de-468c-b6ad-eb62a285d7d4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Many leading organisations and platforms use OpenAPI Specification (OAS) to achieve market acceptance for their APIs, as it provides a widely recognised, standardised way to describe RESTful services.The real-world examples of GitHub, Stripe, Postman, Netflix, Twilio, Kubernetes, Axway, MuleSoft, Nest, and Plaid underscore its versatility and effectiveness in diverse domains. _x000D_
_x000D_
A statement of some of this real world examples are Netfilx with having a complex microservices architecture that requires seamless communication between various services. The company uses OpenAPI to ensure well-defined contracts between their microservices, making it easier to manage and scale their infrastructure._x000D_
_x000D_
Another statement is Twilio, a cloud communications platform that provides a suite of communication APIs, leverages OpenAPI to help developers understand and use their APIs quickly. Through detailed documentation generated from OpenAPI definitions, Twilio ensures that new developers can get up to speed rapidly._x000D_
_x000D_
Examples of real-world usages:_x000D_
https://openapispec.com/docs/what/what-are-some-real-world-examples-of-openapi-usage/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f18ec484-3c98-4e96-88cf-8a2436a1e51f .

camssa:155d5984-3701-49df-9633-2fb3299a4f8d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:16c48370-1c23-41b4-80a5-7d180d12c840 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:183cd3df-52c5-446d-a45f-ecc83674b939 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1a0e3e02-93e5-4939-9336-68ee3059208c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does not implement security itself but provides a standardised description of the security mechanisms required to protect API resources. It allows API designers to specify authentication and authorisation methods, such as OAuth2, OpenID Connect, API keys, and HTTP authentication, through defined security schemes._x000D_
_x000D_
OAS Security Requirements Object:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#security-requirement-object_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22b70602-c6ef-4605-9b92-c1cb69e7ca15 .

camssa:1f3ff377-09c9-45f3-ac8f-17950d5c03b7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:22b70602-c6ef-4605-9b92-c1cb69e7ca15 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:246bccd0-2091-438a-a113-5b2cecb15474 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:24cbf1b7-efb9-4066-a5e1-bcb7e84c4af5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More _x000D_
specifically, OAS can define the interoperability aspects of the  "API", "API Manager", "Machine to Machine", "Data Space"  and "Web Service" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View-Application._x000D_
_x000D_
ELIS Refrence:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:73ddce0d-d333-4887-8597-3d15605a451d .

camssa:261ae63b-2962-45ec-975a-8f3a1819ee84 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:28b5c028-2bb4-4927-88a6-3e0f6dbb79b7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS is not related to the reuse of information, therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:62f57c26-6b0e-4a4c-b9bc-768f62b89f1c .

camssa:2912f6e2-3a01-4f56-90af-f5be07e655e6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2b87f820-afc2-42c9-8af0-74169b6ca993 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does not itself provide mechanisms to protect information against unauthorised changes. It serves to describe APIs and may include documentation of security measures. Therefore, this criterion is not directly applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ec3a00d2-d6e3-403a-9719-fb9db966ee56 .

camssa:2c16570b-5683-42d4-bff6-4c81a477877f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the OpenAPI specfication has been assed by the Institute of Electrical and_x000D_
Electronics Engineers (IEEE), dedicated to standardisation and development in technical areas.In the “Automatic Generation of Test Cases for REST APIs: A Specification-Based Approach” study, adresses how the REpresentation State Transfer (REST) has gained momentum as the preferred technique to design Web APIs but lacks of a specification to describe how to create/consume REST APIs, thus creating new challenges for their integration, testing and verification._x000D_
_x000D_
Automatic Generation of Test Cases for REST APIs: A Specification-Based Approach: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8536162_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9113d24-e9b0-4cc9-93d5-cdbeb03d38a8 .

camssa:2e9f0d1a-3a04-443f-a036-aacc967b1aa4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3004a41b-0c0c-4420-8b9b-52d8b423c0c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is included in two national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Malta and The Netherlands. The national interoperability framework of The Netherlands is fully alligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the European Interoperability Framework (EIF) according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. Malta, nonetheless, does not have a high performance, being aligned only with two sections of the EIF. _x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of The Netherlands:_x000D_
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Malta:_x000D_
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
NIFO Factsheets: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/iopeu-monitoring/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57a8596b-a984-452c-bc79-65fec80cc71f .

camssa:343a82ab-6972-4aea-b905-c0675e3c1b80 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3c828830-06d3-401d-82be-8fcf9f2a045c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:41fb5cea-b66d-4ab2-9308-ecc360c3e839 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS development is guided by the Techincal Steering Commitee (TSC) a group of committers in charge of _x000D_
implementing new versions of the specification. Moreover, the OAS has support from the community in _x000D_
Github, where anyone interested is encouraged to pull requests and give feedback on its implementation._x000D_
_x000D_
TSC Working Group Reference:_x000D_
https://www.openapis.org/about/technical-developer-community_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.2.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification in Github:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc33c527-dba6-4275-9801-8bde583fe2df .

camssa:4565cbd5-dade-425d-a617-5fd5dc270ab7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:486ba64e-68f3-43c8-8aed-fa825c355f3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Through the Github platform, the OAS community is encharged of reviewing all the releases as well as _x000D_
raising issues and proposing improvements. Although the specification does not contemplate a specific session or section to leave feedback about a specific minor or major release, it allows people to contribute by reviewing the contributing process so users can understand how the specification is evolving. Also, sessions where feedback is collected are open to the community, and all users can see the comments that have been made._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification in Github:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6408a49-c659-41f9-bf9f-b2d9f97dd0bb .

camssa:48c8d934-6086-4235-9c36-556f8622cb9f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4dd6a7ff-54a0-4280-a622-e4d9b6f1c6c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS specification is included in 2 Member States catalogues of recommended specifications. These _x000D_
Member States are Malta and The Netherlands._x000D_
_x000D_
Malta ICT National Catalogue Reference:_x000D_
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243_x000D_
_x000D_
Netherlands ICT National Catalogue Reference:_x000D_
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards:_x000D_
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:70abcba9-ff04-410e-80b5-696a3e8ed3b3 .

