camssa:56884f87-4525-4f4f-84d6-908ba17fd92d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Conformance of OpenAPI implementations is supported by the official conformance test suite maintained by Swagger with the support of SMARTBEAR. It provides a collection of valid and invalid example files used by tools to verify adherence to the specification. _x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Conformance Test Reference:_x000D_
https://swagger.io/solutions/api-testing/_x000D_
_x000D_
SMARTBEAR Reference:_x000D_
https://smartbear.com/solutions/api-lifecycle/openapi-spec/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c828830-06d3-401d-82be-8fcf9f2a045c .

camssa:57a8596b-a984-452c-bc79-65fec80cc71f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5a4df43c-611f-4c88-b17c-fcfacef725bf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5c2f4776-4118-4b01-ab50-3280541616be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does facilitate the publication of data on the Web since it defines a standard, language-agnostic interface to HTTP APIs which allows both humans and computers to discover and understand the capabilities of the service without access to source code or documentation, or through network traffic inspection. A use of OAS is the automated generation of API portals and documentation, generally by using JSON. This tooling automatically displays the API in a user-friendly format, effectively producing a detailed web interface or API portal that outlines every available endpoint._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://jsonapi.org/format/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:246bccd0-2091-438a-a113-5b2cecb15474 .

camssa:5c84556f-8838-4928-83a5-d07ec60df1b1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS serves as a framework for the development and documentation of APIs, it allows for customisation provided that the defined structure of the specification is respected. In this sense, the specification permits the inclusion of additional information or extensions while maintaining the core structure and integrity of the standard._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2e9f0d1a-3a04-443f-a036-aacc967b1aa4 .

camssa:61a15a79-c288-48e1-9add-ebfa63dbc2c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS simplifies the delivery of European public services by promoting interoperability and reuse of digital components. For example, the European Data Portal uses OAS-based APIs to expose and integrate open datasets across Member States, enabling consistent, secure, and efficient data exchange between public administrations and users._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
European Data Portal Reference:_x000D_
https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/pdf/documentation_data-europa-eu_V1.2.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d73f447c-45ed-47e6-94d6-1c8868201f78 .

camssa:62f57c26-6b0e-4a4c-b9bc-768f62b89f1c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6764384b-71b1-442a-809f-43abe02c5955 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the OpenAPI specfication has been assed by the Institute of Electrical and_x000D_
Electronics Engineers (IEEE), dedicated to standardisation and development in technical areas. In the “Analyzing OpenAPI Specifications for Security Design Issues” study, the OpenAPI specification is approached as the fundamental and standardised input for carrying out a semi-automatic design security analysis of web service APIs._x000D_
_x000D_
Analyzing OpenAPI Specifications for Security Design Issues:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/9652639_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1f3ff377-09c9-45f3-ac8f-17950d5c03b7 .

camssa:67b6ee20-a9c8-4ce8-a500-90bedb36a918 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Applications built on OpenAPI interface files can automatically generate documentation for methods, parameters, and models. This ensures that documentation, client libraries, and source code remain synchronised, therefore supporting data portability across systems._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:09563e6e-ca39-4c86-b1d7-b271dc622ec6 .

camssa:68d926ef-51db-41e9-9377-984d538d724d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6ef99ab4-5a7b-405e-bdd3-86a913d252ff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:70abcba9-ff04-410e-80b5-696a3e8ed3b3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:71383944-0dd1-4040-b311-b69785c81c7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Despite OAS is not included in an open repository/catalgue of standards at the European level, CENELEC provides a dedicated API portal where it publishes and manages a comprehensive catalogue of APIs, all of which are formally documented using the OpenAPI Specification (OAS) to ensure consistent, machine-readable definitions for developers._x000D_
_x000D_
CENELEC Catalogue of API Reference:_x000D_
https://api-portal.cenelec.eu/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fd8c27da-5bf0-4903-82c8-717b2acb05db .

camssa:73ddce0d-d333-4887-8597-3d15605a451d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7b218bf8-b940-4f45-aac9-239cd6cf935d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS can facilitate the interoperability agreements by providing a standardised description for APIs, enabling the documentation of security mechanisms, and streamlining the tasks required to work with APIs from other organisations._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:541609a4-1f92-4228-80a8-034fabd935b3 .

camssa:84975dd8-470f-4cb1-b667-f705ab47e007 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS facilitates the exposure of interfaces by supporting documentation tools that make APIs easy to understand and code generation tools that create clients and servers in multiple languages, simplifying public sector integration. When combined with other specifications and tools such as JSON Schema for data validation and documentation or code generation tools like Swagger UI, the specification enables interfaces to be both visible and usable across different contexts._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Schema Reference:_x000D_
https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-core_x000D_
_x000D_
Swagger UI Reference:_x000D_
https://swagger.io/tools/swagger-ui/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01c92199-a894-48a6-a533-30ea36636781 .

camssa:87153de0-0ab2-46ea-80c0-1c1d0deb8b30 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:88b3061a-7fc2-4409-8c47-ebdf40f6927f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "40"^^xsd:string .

camssa:89105a16-7124-4042-86f9-02e7a7e0c2b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:910e739e-4d4f-4c8a-954f-e3b1c8821da6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Currently, the OAS is maintained, evolved and promoted by the OpenAPI Initiative (OAI), a consortium of industry experts with an open governance structure under the Linux Foundation umbrella. There are different ways in which a user can participate: via GitHub, weekly discussions on Zoom, or by joining the Slack workspace. In addition, there are special interest groups that can be taken into account, as well as blog posts and questions through this mail: info@openapis.org._x000D_
_x000D_
Moreover,  the Technical Steering Committee (TSC) holds weekly web conferences to review open pull requests and discuss open issues related to the evolving OpenAPI Specification. Participation in weekly calls and scheduled working sessions is open to the community._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Initiative Reference:_x000D_
https://learn.openapis.org/introduction.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Participate Reference:_x000D_
https://www.openapis.org/participatehow-to-contribute_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Github Participation Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Github Community:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/community/blob/main/SPECIAL_INTEREST_GROUPS.md_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5e75b11-7778-4aa7-95c1-3936b9d2bcf7 .

camssa:91ef3d23-478d-483c-8e4b-c0de5aeacc2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Originating from Swagger in 2010 and formalised as OAS under the OpenAPI Initiative in 2016, the OAS is a mature and stable standard for defining RESTful APIs, widely adopted across the industry. Its tools for documentation, client generation, validation, and testing, combined with active governance by the Linux Foundation, ensures that it is reliable for both enterprise and production use. _x000D_
_x000D_
Updates, such as 3.2.0, revolve around enhanced support for multi-document descriptions and resolving references (Base URI management), expanded parameter and content encoding capabilities (especially for cookies and query strings), and improved data modeling for complex structures (such as XML)._x000D_
_x000D_
Linux Foundation OAS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.openapis.org/tag/oas_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI 3.2.0 Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d8cfddbe-bb64-4253-b7c8-7f92754a4e25 .

camssa:9295f59a-1d77-4af0-a985-07000a27b916 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS is not related to the modelling of business processes, therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:87153de0-0ab2-46ea-80c0-1c1d0deb8b30 .

camssa:9f96a79b-a985-4a2d-9ca1-11e194b1f795 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does not directly ensure data processing accuracy. Therefore, this criterion is not directly applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:261ae63b-2962-45ec-975a-8f3a1819ee84 .

camssa:a0d758eb-0e4f-40fb-a4d6-00b96e099cdb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS allows relevant information to be widely reused by defining reusable components such as schemas, parameters, responses, and security schemes. These can be referenced across multiple endpoints and operations, reducing duplication and ensuring consistency._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5219579-9e56-4d38-8b16-069edf41f1a9 .

camssa:a4ca2778-3c4f-40b3-9213-dbb49788ba3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is not a European Standard. It is an open specification developed and maintained by the OpenAPI Initiative under the Linux Foundation. However, it is widely recognised and adopted across Europe, including by EU institutions and national public administrations, to support interoperability and standardised API design._x000D_
_x000D_
Data Europa Reference:_x000D_
https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/pdf/documentation_data-europa-eu_V1.2.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3f1b96a-9abc-4925-8336-592627681a57 .

camssa:a627d911-5898-48e2-a15c-b8fa779627ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS has been found to be used in the Research Infrastructure for Science and Innovation Policy Studies (named as RISIS), where OpenAPI takes part in a project aiming to automatise query-centric APIs for accessing to linked data. Moreover, All APIs on data.europa.eu are documented via OpenAPI._x000D_
_x000D_
Automatic Query-centric API for Routine Access to Linked Data:_x000D_
https://iswc2017.semanticweb.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/MainProceedings/430.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Data Europa Reference:_x000D_
https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/pdf/documentation_data-europa-eu_V1.2.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
RISIS webpage:_x000D_
https://www.risis2.eu/about/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ef99ab4-5a7b-405e-bdd3-86a913d252ff .

camssa:a6408a49-c659-41f9-bf9f-b2d9f97dd0bb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a92bc5a8-df34-44f8-b556-0fb8875c6dd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Github platform hosts the OpenAPI guidelines and specifications, is as well as a space for contributions _x000D_
and proposals of improvements in which any individual interested is encouraged to participate and raise _x000D_
issues regarding OAS implementation. OAS has also been found in multiple platforms, such as Stackoverflow or the Central Digital and Data Office platform from the United Kingdom. In this platform, information about the use and implementation of OAS is shared and reviewed. Additionally, CENELEC mantains and distribute a Catalogue of APIs based on OAS._x000D_
_x000D_
UK API technical and data standards reference:_x000D_
https://www.gov.uk/guidance/gds-api-technical-and-data-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Stackoverflow refrence:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/48111459/how-to-define-a-property-that-can-be-string-or-null-in-openapi-swagger_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification CENELEC Catalogue of APIs Reference:_x000D_
https://api-portal.cenelec.eu/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification in Github:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/discussions'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16c48370-1c23-41b4-80a5-7d180d12c840 .

camssa:a94bb274-b28a-46ce-b6df-0ad115acbffb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:aa848a4b-c005-4f2b-8759-10be3d02242c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "84.44%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string,
        "92.63%AssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ae531502-e79a-4ccf-8722-3a0bb29fcc15 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'2 Member States are recommending OAS in their ICT National Catalogues. These Member States are Malta and The Netherlands._x000D_
_x000D_
Malta ICT National Catalogue Reference:_x000D_
https://mccaa.org.mt/Section/Content?contentId=1243_x000D_
_x000D_
Netherlands ICT National Catalogue Reference:_x000D_
https://www.forumstandaardisatie.nl/open-standaarden/lijst_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards:_x000D_
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68d926ef-51db-41e9-9377-984d538d724d .

camssa:b5e75b11-7778-4aa7-95c1-3936b9d2bcf7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b63386f1-daef-47ce-91b5-2f66671c0628 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS enables authentication and role identification to a high degree through the mandatory definition of security schemes and requirements, which inform users how to prove their identity. The specification uses the Security Scheme Object to define the types of security protocols the API supports, such as OAuth2, OpenID Connect, API keys, and HTTP authentication._x000D_
_x000D_
OAS Security Requirements Object:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#security-requirement-object_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:88b3061a-7fc2-4409-8c47-ebdf40f6927f .

camssa:b78d1460-4ea0-4eaa-af00-40fc0242b90d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is an open-source, royalty-free specification, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It is also available with any restrictions related to Fair, Reasonable, and Non Discriminatory (F/RAND) principles, and it can be accessed from its website and in the Github repository._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification in Github:_x000D_
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/#participation_x000D_
_x000D_
Apache License Version 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89105a16-7124-4042-86f9-02e7a7e0c2b1 .

camssa:b899309c-c439-445b-8fe2-e8f9aad1b225 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS seeks to cover most use cases, it also permits the inclusion of additional data through extensions at specific points. These extensions may not always be supported by existing tools, but internal or open-source tooling can likewise be extended to provide the required support. Moreover, OpenAPI can be complemented and extended through other OpenAPI Initiative specifications, such as Overlays, which enable modular and context-specific adaptations without altering the core definition._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Overlay Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/overlay/v1.0.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:343a82ab-6972-4aea-b905-c0675e3c1b80 .

camssa:bc33c527-dba6-4275-9801-8bde583fe2df a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c064def0-9556-478c-8773-47822e4b37ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS does not directly ensure the protection of personal data since it focuses more on the documentation and share of APIs. However, the specification does support the implementation of security measures with the inclusion of security schemes, such as OAuth2, OpenID Connect, or even metadada that can describe authentication, autherisation and encryption requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth 2.0 Authorization Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect Core Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4eef4394-4fa5-4a00-85d5-ccf85cd52fc6 .

camssa:c2453c47-cb59-4fb5-890f-1bb177541b02 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS allows the description of the security mechanisms used by an API, such as API Keys or OAuth2. This helps document how users authenticate to access resources, ensuring that only authorised users can retrieve or modify the data._x000D_
_x000D_
OAS Security Requirements Object:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#security-requirement-object_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a4df43c-611f-4c88-b17c-fcfacef725bf .

camssa:c9113d24-e9b0-4cc9-93d5-cdbeb03d38a8 a cav:Score,
