    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d73f447c-45ed-47e6-94d6-1c8868201f78 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d79455c6-284f-4ec9-8d0f-be5c3d56b643 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is intended to streamline the creation of APIs. Because the requirements of each API may differ, the specification permits partial implementations; however, a minimum level of implementation remains essential of an OpenAPI document (such as the openapi, info, and paths fields), valid schema definitions, correctly resolved references, and at least one properly defined operation. These elements ensure that even partial implementations remain compatible with OpenAPI tooling and maintain interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce2c6f89-b288-464a-96ad-d3b285624ea6 .

camssa:d82a0876-4936-40ab-9be5-fa173b081f69 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is independent of any specification and can be implemented without any dependency on platforms. This allows tools, clients, and documentation to work across platforms without modification, supporting interoperability and broad adoption._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a94bb274-b28a-46ce-b6df-0ad115acbffb .

camssa:d8cfddbe-bb64-4253-b7c8-7f92754a4e25 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:dcf5976c-48d6-49f2-940c-ac1bb83bf740 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS can serve as an effective tool for enhancing visibility when documenting and developing new APIs. The core of this function is defining a standard, programming language-agnostic interface description for HTTP APIs. This framework ensures that different systems can communicate effectively, thereby increasing interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
By enabling code generation for documentation, client applications, and server implementations, OAS improves the transparency of administrative processes. This standardisation facilitates API implementation, making them easier to understand and to interact._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48c8d934-6086-4235-9c36-556f8622cb9f .

camssa:e2642328-2bf7-489b-b423-5d20bc7104c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is independent of any specification and can be implemented without relying on other technologies. This allows OAS to standardise API descriptions across diverse technological environments, enabling consistent documentation, client generation, and interoperability regardless of the underlying tech._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:532a7281-428c-4c3d-8199-9a12cfa45df6 .

camssa:e5219579-9e56-4d38-8b16-069edf41f1a9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e948b9db-c5dc-4d3f-a631-401cba009d6a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS is designed to describe HTTP APIs regardless of the specific business domain or sector. Whether the API is for finance, healthcare, government, e‑commerce, or IoT, OAS can provide a standardised, programming language‑agnostic format to define endpoints, request/response schemas, authentication methods, and metadata._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c5d9f1e-c246-41b6-a866-007604af3f83 .

camssa:ec3a00d2-d6e3-403a-9719-fb9db966ee56 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ee58d454-025b-4d03-a0d8-b7c5209ebb5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS can be complemented with the Overlay specification, also from OpenAPI initiative. The Overlay specification allows to do modifications on an OpenAPI document without altering it. Among other functions, Overlay supports multi-language documentation._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Overlay Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/overlay/v1.0.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4565cbd5-dade-425d-a617-5fd5dc270ab7 .

camssa:f18ec484-3c98-4e96-88cf-8a2436a1e51f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f1f8223a-d208-4343-8dd4-a7252573eb6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS defines a standard, programming language-agnostic interface description for HTTP APIs. This core standard enables both humans and computers to discover and understand the capabilities of a service without requiring access to source code, additional documentation, or inspection of network traffic. _x000D_
_x000D_
The specification attempts to guide API authors to avoid ambiguous requirements in order to maximise interoperability. By defining a fixed format for how data should be exchanged and where resources can be found, the OAS ensures different clients and services can reliably communicate._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e94d7b9-fb0a-4e65-8965-9d34e0c78c62 .

camssa:f5ee6c71-7b93-464b-a53b-9d308a8006bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OAS does not provide means for restriction of access to information or data since it focuses more on the documentation and share of APIs. However, the specification does support the implementation of security measures with the inclusion of security schemes, such as OAuth2, OpenID Connect, or even metadada that can describe authentication, autherisation and encryption requirements. This allow to API designers to specify how information or data should be controlled. Thanks to this security schemes implementations the specification enables developers and tools to implement access restrictions in line with the intended security policies._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth 2.0 Authorization Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect Core Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:127d38b8-a4c4-4889-9f85-6ed019c60b96 .

camssa:fbe2feb1-25ac-4ff4-ae6a-4bdcce82cbbf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OAS does not directly provide an access control mechanism. Therefore, this criterion is not directly applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html#openapi-specification_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenAPI Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:183cd3df-52c5-446d-a45f-ecc83674b939 .

