camssa:5ec55c00-c68d-4712-ac9f-e0d9f495ec08 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"PAdES is intrinsically tied to the Portable Document Format (PDF) standard (ISO 32000-1). It defines extensions and restrictions on the PDF's internal data structures to support digital signatures. It is not designed to sign other document formats like Microsoft Word files or simple text files. In this regard Microsoft has developed their own proprietary alternative, OOXML._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
OOXML reference_x000D_
https://www.iso.org/standard/71691.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de5ed45f-5b53-43ba-8c0b-04ce70d00132 .

camssa:60639f49-e21b-4c4d-a98b-22d6f12fdaaa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the PAdES specification has been assessed in conjunction with other electronic signature specifications in an article on the "Special Issue Advanced Research in Technology and Information Systems" of the "Electronics" publication called "A Comprehensive and Privacy-Aware Approach for Remote Qualified Electronic Signatures". In the article the authors value the specification effectiveness in the integration with other cryptographic resources like blockchain and its eIDAS conformity._x000D_
_x000D_
A Comprehensive and Privacy-Aware Approach for Remote Qualified Electronic Signatures reference:_x000D_
https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics13040757_x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bba55e32-867e-4e8d-9267-312ca6836081 .

camssa:6070d1e5-5291-45f3-b952-02677e647b22 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6180f135-19f0-49f7-9458-3db731ccbb7c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'PAdES Baseline Profile function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS. The specification, through the "Long-Term Validation (LTV)" element and in conjunction with the Document Security Store (DSS), ensures the document remains self-contained and verifiable over long periods._x000D_
The DSS is a dictionary object within the PDF file itself, defined by the PAdES standard. Its purpose is to centralize and store the cryptographic data needed for validation. _x000D_
This means that a system receiving the signed document does not need to perform an entirely new validation process from scratch. It can reuse the included data to verify the signature's authenticity_x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5935db2b-46b1-485d-afda-8f027e020149 .

camssa:64c5ea1e-8469-4533-8fe6-9c27c68b25b3 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:68a3f02c-bbb1-4bf0-a4ef-04361e12129b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:829e7909-f8ae-4c91-ac36-92930ce91c8c .

camssa:6c5a3e70-b04d-4697-aeef-b0b6138b6418 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PAdES Baseline Profile is based on PDF and PDF documents are based on Unicode, which supports all writing systems. Therefore, any language can be used in an PDF document. In particular, ISO 32000-2 version officially introduced UTF-8 encoding on PDF as an allowed format for certain text strings (like metadata and comments), aligning the format more closely with web standards._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1d21f4f-f7f8-431d-893f-ac2628035329 .

camssa:70950f1e-901a-42c7-a50c-c2f08c67200a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef7e7cdb-eeaa-4a7b-ac71-e2b5f62f2019 .

camssa:75f6e33d-5f60-4073-9420-bf59eeeedd7b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"PAdES is included in 5 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Croatia, Cyprus, France, Poland and Spain. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Spain and France are aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets. _x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards: https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
NIFO Factsheets: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/iopeu-monitoring/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024_x000D_
_x000D_
France's catalogue: _x000D_
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/offre-accompagnement/reference-interoperabilite-rgi/_x000D_
_x000D_
Spains's catalogue:_x000D_
https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/pae_Home/dam/jcr:97912041-c1c3-47c4-b517f9f51db321d/Guia_aplicacion_Norma_Tecnica_Interoperabilidad_Catalogo_de_estandares.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Poland's catalogue: _x000D_
http://isap.sejm.gov.pl/isap.nsf/download.xsp/WDU20170002247/O/D20172247.pdf _x000D_
_x000D_
Cyprus catalogue: _x000D_
https://dits.dmrid.gov.cy/dmrid/dits/dits.nsf/all/B83AA8E4EB4EFD19C225855800288B10/$file/Cyprus%20eGovernment%20Interoperability%20Framework_new%20EIF_v2.0-To%20Publish.pdf _x000D_
_x000D_
Croatia's catalogue: _x000D_
https://ssi.gov.hr/en/catalogue_x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference: _x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dad3530c-9855-42e7-b112-5f0db0e706b7 .

