camssa:8630f9a7-5719-4eab-b588-64220e55de84 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PAdES specification can be found used in different European projects and also by Member States. Since it is suitable for advanced electronic signatures in PDF documents, it is used by companies and public administrations to sign this kind of format documents. In this sense, the specification has been selected within the CEF Digital Signature Service (DSS) along with CAdES, ASiC and XAdES Baseline profiles. Digital Signature Service is an open-source software library for electronic signature creation and validation supporting the interoperability of electronic signatures._x000D_
The initiative is an enabler for cross borders interoperability between administrations and businesses._x000D_
Applications such as eCoSignature from the Ministry of Industry and Commerce of Spain use PAdES as one of their base specifications._x000D_
_x000D_
eCoSignature reference: https://firmaelectronica.gob.es/en/ciudadanos/cosas-deberias-saber/formatos- firma DSS reference: https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html _x000D_
_x000D_
eSignatureHub - Digital Signature Service DSS: _x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/DIGITAL/pages/467109107/Digital+Signature+Service+-+DSS_x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0e2e8650-da31-40c8-a37b-da32f1f0878c .

camssa:8bd04cb0-bba7-4391-92e5-7e2ac4b5356b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the PAdES specification has been assessed on the thesis of Kiira Karonen from the Aalto University. The "PDF advanced electronic signature with smart cards" study describes a case example of a software implementation that signs PDF files according to the PAdES standard using smart cards as the signature creation device. The implementation described in this thesis is a low-abstraction solution that can be used to generate the signature structure required by the PAdES standard based on a raw cryptographic signature, thus showing that the PAdES specification can be efficiently implemented without dependencies on third party PDF reader software._x000D_
_x000D_
Karonen, K. (2025). PDF advanced electronic signature with smart cards. reference:_x000D_
