camssa:edf085e5-a916-44ad-b6b1-ff5b7fcab5fe a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PAdES Baseline Profile provides the involved stakeholders with a legally binding signature structure to formalise interoperability agreements. In this sense it provides the foundation of any agreement among any kind of participants. The specification also fosters and facilitates agreements by establishing a common method for signing PDF documents and data in a secure and trustworthy manner. This enables PDF documents to be exchanged in an interoperable way, ensuring that all parties can access the documents and trust the information or data contained within them. By providing a standardised approach, PAdES helps to build confidence between parties and supports the reliable execution of digital transactions._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d68fcf2-fc9e-4a0f-9a71-4d8001461678 .

camssa:ef7e7cdb-eeaa-4a7b-ac71-e2b5f62f2019 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f1cedb89-5165-4124-9322-7cb212adda86 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'PAdES guarantees that signed data on PDF format remains authentic, integral, and legally defensible when transmitted or archived._x000D_
PAdES signatures, especially when based on Qualified Certificates (which are common in Public Administrations under eIDAS), link the document directly to a verified identity._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cb22de4-d3a2-4727-afac-65877966ce60 .

camssa:f228a6fa-cc4a-4756-bd79-82bf8b7c74e0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the PAdES Baseline Profile is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81988a6b-af42-4811-9a42-1770deaff5c1 .

