camssa:fa3e8c88-9ca2-4738-a058-81172c45939d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The PAdES Baseline Profile includes mechanisms for long-term validation, such as timestamps and embedded certificate information. This means that a signed public record or contract can be securely archived and remain legally verifiable for some time. In this sense the preservation of the date of signature is a partial preservation of the record. _x000D_
The highest baseline level, PAdES-B-LTA (Long-Term Archival), facilitates  the long term data preservation through the Document Time-Stamp (Archive Time-Stamp) which is a cryptographic seal placed over the entire PDF document, including the Document Security Store (DSS) and all embedded signatures._x000D_
_x000D_
When a new Document Time-Stamp is applied (a form of periodic extension), it essentially reuses the integrity of all preceding data, including the Revocation Information (VRI) data already present in the Document Security Store (DSS)._x000D_
_x000D_
This proves that the validation data (certificates and revocation checks) existed and was valid at the time the Document Time-Stamp was applied, effectively "re-certifying" the entire package against the threat of future cryptographic breaking or certificate expiry._x000D_
_x000D_
PAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31914201/01.02.01_60/en_31914201v010201p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abe38a94-e4cd-4fab-a672-dfd0126d1994 .

