camssa:fbcd2d39-379f-489d-b709-46924978da0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DNS can be extended with several transport protocols to provide a safer data exchange. The Domain Name 
System Security Extensions (DNSSEC) modify DNS to add support for cryptographically signed responses, 
while other extensions such as Transaction Signature (TSIG), add support for cryptographic authentication 
between trusted peers and are commonly used to authorize zone transfer or dynamic update operations.

Resource Records for the DNS Security Extensions:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4034

Extension Mechanisms for DNS:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6891

DNS IETF reference:
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8499'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:162c6136-b211-47b9-8f47-fa63d88268d7 .

camssa:fbd3244f-8b0e-49c5-9ec1-06cbb47a2644 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:fbd46a93-d248-4dd9-b743-7da9ed0a9217 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """TSP is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications whose Member State NIF is fully aligned with at least 4 out of 5 sections of the EIF according to NIFO factsheets.\r
\r
CAMSS List of Standards:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c19a9bbd-7474-408d-a902-2675a4ac18fd .

camssa:fbd8381a-b554-40cd-b3aa-3fe1c9831285 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The specification is available for its use and implementation at the IETF's webpage. \r
\r
FTPS IETF reference:\r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4217"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8efc3400-5023-4b5a-9efc-b4abe1d682bc .

camssa:fbdd83c2-d43d-4c5e-a855-b2a451dae8da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.\r
\r
W3C Process document:\r
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e2ac5780-055e-4cb8-94f2-0e841c713b43 .

camssa:fbe0e1c1-40d8-4004-9554-2e703c666c4b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OASIS ebXML Core (ebCore) Technical Committee promotes the sharing of data and results and helps accelerate the specification adoption throughout the international community, particularly within government agencies. In this sense, the specification encourages both the creation of communities and the sharing of their data and results on national platforms.\r
\r
OASIS ebXML Core (ebCore) Technical Committee reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=ebcore'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0282d50a-9ca9-4093-a957-757b5cd72e66 .

camssa:fbe3faae-985a-4926-b223-6ad834bd22a3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fbe9a715-d0e6-4aad-858c-94abb8467074 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """By applying the OpenPM2 methodology into the development of initiatives, services or products aiming to implement the once-only principle, it can leverage and promote synergies between organisations working in the same area of application. \r
\r
European Institutions developing initiatives using OpenPM2 can help to develop efficient eGovernment initiatives implying the once-only principle. \r
\r
OpenPM2 specification reference:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/ac3e118a-cb6e-11e8-9424-01aa75ed71a1/language-en/format-PDF/source-83307127"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d301a44-9dc6-4a4c-9b23-675735424970 .

camssa:fbeef7c6-88b7-4ac1-b575-19f2c69a654f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:fbefae44-05f1-451d-969a-a0430b73b4d1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fbf669b7-df25-473b-959b-b187ee24ef05 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OGC TrainingDML-AI standard facilitates online access and retrieval of data, enhancing accessibility and potentially streamlining digital service delivery channels. By establishing a foundation for efficient AI/ML applications and guaranteeing interoperable, high-quality data, the standard indirectly fosters the advancement of digital services in diverse domains, including public administration and environmental management.

OGC TrainingDML-AI Standard:
https://docs.ogc.org/is/23-008r3/23-008r3.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c49120db-12c9-4de0-b5ba-e25f05aa1d27 .

camssa:fc07a3f8-0297-46fe-a8d6-34a373ec1dd5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fc09880d-8c4e-43d0-aa92-a91c204bb3d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The Asset Administration Shell (AAS) is  the standardized digital representation of an asset, the corner stone for the interoperability of Industrial components organized in Industry 4.0 systems. The AAS may be the logical representation of a simple component, a machine or a plant at any level of the equipment hierarchy. In this sense the specification can be used in other domains rather than the industrial manufacturing but it would be a complicated implementation.

Details of the Asset Administration Shell (AAS)
https://industrialdigitaltwin.org/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2024/06/IDTA-01001-3-0-1_SpecificationAssetAdministrationShell_Part1_Metamodel.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ada939c8-2c85-4429-ad58-d9b09757c588 .

camssa:fc0c946f-8a3c-4850-abba-7305f23602a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The OData specification is included in the EUOS European catalogue of standards.\r
\r
EUOS reference:\r
https://www.standict.eu/standards-repository'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b9bf162-3c67-4a2a-9afb-dbc9024e40b0 .

camssa:fc0d54bd-ef23-4b95-b2f2-78d82cd3df0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of ISO 639-2 is not related to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a024750c-9bd9-4917-99de-dff09b14e9a3 .

camssa:fc0dd52f-f4fc-4a74-9c89-8ec269c1ac1f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"HTTP is designed to allow extensibility, allowing specific needs while maintaining a foundation of interoperability. The specification provides the flexibility to introduce new methods, status codes, and header fields, enriching the protocol's vocabulary and functionality. 

HTTP /1.1 RFC 2616 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2616.html

HTTP/1.1 Semantics, RFC 7231 Reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7231\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54ce9fe8-471b-47f8-b052-7f0329846575 .

camssa:fc0e45cd-8fbf-4c30-9d68-13bbf24959c5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While EuroVoc was originally designed to facilitate data processing and classification within European Institutions, with a primary focus on eGovernment; it extends its coverage to various domains and subdomains, including but not limited to energy and transportation. Consequently, it can be regarded as adaptable and applicable across diverse business sectors.\r
\r
EuroVoc:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/dataset/-/resource?uri=http://publications.europa.eu/resource\r
/dataset/eurovoc'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:672b8ddc-c982-4a3c-8941-89a36bc1c799 .

