camssa:fc36fa37-1b34-45a3-a55d-02f246da2dc0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The JSON specification itself does not provide inherent mechanisms for secure processing of data. JSON is primarily a data interchange format that focuses on representing structured data in a readable and efficient manner. It does not include built-in features for secure processing, encryption, or access control. However, the security of data processing using JSON depends on the implementation and the systems handling the JSON data.\r
\r
How do you secure and encrypt JSON and XML data in web communication:\r
https://www.linkedin.com/advice/0/how-do-you-secure-encrypt-json-xml-data-web-communication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:52e45326-dcc4-4e5f-bee1-074e2db1f8ba .

