    cav:value "1" .

camssa:fc5fb249-d317-4e57-a775-d19b0fb1d995 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'An ebXML RegRep stores any type of electronic content, such as text documents, images, sound or video, and provides a set of protocols enabling data transfer among systems. For example, the ebXML specification has enabled the implementation of the e-SENS AS4 profile. Therefore, the specification enables data portability.\r
\r
ebXML reference:\r
http://docs.oasis-open.org/regrep/regrep-core/v4.0/os/regrep-core-overview-v4.0-os.html\r
\r
e-SENS AS4 profile reference:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/CEFDIGITAL/e-SENS+AS4+-+1.12'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:664e96ff-a59a-423d-84ef-8d5b7aa5d39c .

camssa:fc6971b0-efb3-42ee-a4c0-68d868c8d066 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """SHACL is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
See:\r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9dceab70-865e-4000-869f-d6a15188effc .

camssa:fc6c3736-e17e-45fd-9f78-8120fbc44be9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SOAP 1.2 is maintained by W3C which is an international community developing open standards. \r
\r
W3C Consortium Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/Consortium/\r
\r
SOAP Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12/  '"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:67cbafc0-c5ec-4ad3-a2f3-c5c17cd1e7ee .

camssa:fc7b657c-bbf9-4751-ae9a-e8194530dee8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of GraphQL is not related to enabling the secure exchange of data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification.\r
\r
GraphQL specification:\r
https://spec.graphql.org/October2021/#sec-Overview'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:141ad6b7-3a5b-4456-8c3a-e67a4ae75506 .

camssa:fc7c3d72-856a-4b18-b90b-86e4fa139f98 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'By establishing constraints on the creation and exchange of XML documents XSD fosters the trustworthy data exchange between administrations and stakeholders. However, XSD does not include security features in itself. Despite this, XML includes several recommendations in order to ensure the security of data and users.\r
\r
XSD Reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-xmlschema11-1-20120405/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:501d344c-b4b6-4c93-ab6a-bc89d54f282b .

camssa:fc7c4c3c-cd0c-49f1-87a9-afdf2f142851 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OData is maintained and developed by OASIS, which is an international community developing open\r
standards; specifically, by the Technical Committee (TC). The specification maintenance is transparent, and even if its development and the approval process is restricted to the specification TC, anyone can contribute by submitting feedback to the mailing list. All the contributions are publicly available.\r
\r
Developer community OASIS: \r
https://www.oasis-open.org/org/\r
\r
OASIS ebXML Registry Technical Committee reference:\r
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/tc_home.php?wg_abbrev=regrep'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:68549054-ee97-46da-8400-a5a445039646 .

