camssa:fcbd828b-9927-4311-b4eb-3ee9a6061467 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ODRL specification does not inherently provide features for ensuring the authenticity and authentication of \r
the roles of agents involved in data transactions. \r
\r
W3C specification reference: \r
https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/#vocab-core'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8bcf700c-e335-48c4-b2c0-f452383747e3 .

camssa:fcbe3f09-147a-4563-a7eb-ca19205ee591 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the EN 303 645 specification is not related to the comprehensibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. \r
\r
EN 303 645 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/303600_303699/303645/02.01.01_60/en_303645v020101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1fa8a10c-365a-4381-a43e-5f424b457f39 .

camssa:fcc45350-a57f-49aa-9104-e1bddf720294 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, the specification is not mapped with any EIRA ABBs and therefore it is not included in the ELIS v1.0.1. \r
\r
However, it has been associated with Legal ABBs from EIRA Legal View and is being included in the on-going version of the ELIS that will be released in May 2021.  The ABBs included are: Legal Act, Binding Instrument, Legislation On Data Information and Knowledge Exchange and Non-Binding Instrument.\r
\r
ELIS Solution: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis \r
\r
ELIS v1.0.1: \r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/v101-0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba822900-47e9-40d9-a27b-13bea9f91174 .

camssa:fcccd105-fead-45c1-a8d0-345a4e6b4d4d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "CSV is a text plain document which uses comma to separate values. Lines in a document are data records and records consists one or more fields. Therefore, CSV does not define a cross-sector reusable data model. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22e30eda-721e-4d50-b55b-1246f03e0dde .

camssa:fccd3f08-2026-433f-95c2-8597bd7c874f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Ecma International has clearly defined the procedures that have to be carried out in order to publish standards or technical reports. Although Ecma is the SDO that first developed the specification, it is currently being maintained by the IETF, thus, adhering to the development process defined by the organisation, which comprehends public reviews where stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
ECMA Directives:\r
http://www.ecma-international.org/memento/policies.htm\r
\r
Standard process IETF:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:19141704-146f-43b1-9e00-f2b20b0bc025 .

camssa:fcd115a7-ac6f-44ab-bf98-3019d8dc352d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fcd53e27-3ba8-46cb-ace4-41c70873b4a2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After searching in the different official European websites, there is no evidence of any cross-border project that use GITB TDL nor explicit agreements involving the usage of the specification.\r
\r
GITB TDL reference:\r
https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/docs/tdl/latest/introduction/index.html#introduction'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ca30012f-c181-4019-83d5-4af76bacaa68 .

camssa:fcdb22ae-64ac-47d3-9607-1a3088f77684 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of EN 16234-1 e-CF is not related to the secure exchange of data. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification.\r
\r
CEN reference, CEN/TC 428 - ICT Professionalism and Digital Competences (Published standards), EN 16234-1 e-CF:\r
https://standards.cencenelec.eu/dyn/www/f?p=205:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:67073&cs=15E62ED24D608A5F10D6BEE8E6D50FA10'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cd6e301d-3798-4319-8c48-a9a42607f874 .

camssa:fce06074-b79b-449a-a675-53868fe7c572 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Registered Organization Vocabulary is not protected against unauthorised changes. The main purpose of the specification is to define a standardised way of describing organisations that have gained legal entity status through a formal registration process. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification.

Registered Organization Vocabulary reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-regorg/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3a2cb40b-d19b-4254-94cd-11441728ff05 .

camssa:fce28153-ce70-4c79-9858-eb40ed42a7f2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The EIRA is a domain agnostic reference architecture that can be used to develop solutions in multiples domains. Some examples of that reusability across domains are the specialisations that the Interoperability Architecture solutions have: eGovERA Business Agnostic, eGovERA Tax, eGovERA Health, eGovERA Custom. These are specialisations based in EIRA, which demonstrates that it is domain agnostic and can be reused across domains. 

EIRA reference:
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira
/solution/eira/release/610

EIRA Github Repository: 
https://github.com/CarTool-EC/EIRA 

Interoperability Architecture Solutions Success Stories: 
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/european-interoperability-reference-architecture-eira/success-stories'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1edbc146-a85a-4537-ba4e-b28d8b877946 .

camssa:fce8422c-8561-48db-872a-ba4bbc073fce a cav:Score,
