camssa:fd2bbb95-a671-4163-ac4d-4ced5c6ee0ac a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The Web Services Security (WS-Security) main function is to reinforce integrity and confidentiality of the messages used by SOAP specification. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f78abfa0-553d-442a-bfd1-ed45c566c4a2 .

camssa:fd308359-6694-48e8-a3c0-17cd5d0468cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "The purpose of HTTPS is not related  to the modelling of business processes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:274db542-cafb-48d0-89d1-8447c1bfd8ad .

camssa:fd33f4f9-b178-426b-a341-fd6327bc96bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of TIFF/IT is not related to the implementation of the once-only principle. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
TIFF/IT ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/34342.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81cd0c3f-259c-4370-85b0-ee3b17e5a72c .

camssa:fd342bbf-5ff9-4dca-b95b-4c07bac4c66d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Since the specification is focused on testing the Trusted Lists established on web services and their schema according to the requirements established in  ETSI TS 119 612, the implementation and usage of the specification can increase the visibility and reliability of public organisations procedures and rules.\r
\r
ETSI TS 119 614-1 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119600_119699/11961401/01.01.01_60/ts_11961401v010101p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55dcf718-6746-4307-8a4c-5070db91e099 .

camssa:fd385919-1c06-4634-a21d-8a7e87a6a9f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There are some optional parts in the REM Structure, but it is not customizable itself.\r
\r
ETSI EN 319 532-3 reference:\r
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319500_319599/31953203/01.02.01_60/en_31953203v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:581ab796-b6d9-4259-8ee4-dc87bbf44ee9 .

camssa:fd39ef12-04f9-4e35-8484-da1e4a280f12 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'There has not been found any assessment addressing the efficiency of Domibus implementations.\r
\r
Domibus specification:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/Domibus'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83b85f6f-bcd1-49c2-9462-b479b32549bb .

camssa:fd3bc416-a9bb-4f2b-a875-a296dc97cbb6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'DPV is based on European Union legislative requirements such as the GDPR, which aims to harmonise data privacy laws across Europe. Therefore, public administrations benefit from the definition of a data model based on this regulation given that it promotes the transparency of the procedures and personal data handled by public administrations.

DPV specification:
https://w3c.github.io/dpv/primer/

GDPR reference:
https://gdpr.eu/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fdac66b8-478e-47a5-ade0-8506e1030e3b .

camssa:fd471a04-ec25-472d-916e-f9b01bd75267 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The Core Public Service Vocabulary Application Profile is a business domain agnostic specification, fostering the specification's use in any domain.\r
\r
CPSV-AP Joinup webpage:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/solution/core-public-service-vocabulary-application-profile/release/22\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a940094b-5200-4387-a28d-d03e3afa7ff8 .

camssa:fd4be95f-5b59-42ad-a5f6-b2cdf2de5a29 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of the Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary is not related to the availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Therefore, this criterion does not apply to this specification. \r
\r
CCCEV reference:\r
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/solution/e-government-core-vocabularies/core-criterion-and-core-evidence-vocabulary"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d76a0ba4-a959-4179-9518-4848838908a0 .

camssa:fd4f1c24-04b7-48e0-81ed-3ddd17aa9681 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "20" .

camssa:fd5120c8-a0a4-418a-8394-00e9ec175b20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Syslog is a widely used and standardized protocol for message logging, making it relatively versatile and applicable across different domains, including various business sectors. Its standardization allows different systems and devices to communicate using a common logging format. Therefore, it is abstract and can be implemented and/or used in any domain as long as it fulfills the requirements.

Syslog Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7c61608a-1c2d-42eb-92a8-751dd1ede188 .

camssa:fd537153-4770-44cc-b94c-5d60176e7e39 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ffdbd22af1ff3c1ebb100043d062a3df160007af761caf0a8c9f50f02e609c9e ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:fd58e935-cbfc-49f3-ad73-2a3e13f7e243 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f70d8bc1b4b6e186d69ea3f7f8cc7b2d75314b84e7f481ebe13b4e6ed8b36598 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:fd5cef57-4def-4942-ae1c-c20608e29030 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fd61306d-5460-47e1-aa5e-2211bc0e19d9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SFIA is a framework for defining skills and competences in digital communities. In this sense, the specification is domain-agnostic and can be implemented across business domains where the ICT sector can operate.\r
\r
SFIA reference:\r
https://sfia-online.org/en/sfia-8'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a07e3aee-9cc0-43f3-8ab9-c4784f9a93d6 .

camssa:fd61ac1f-2573-4b05-83d8-de349072d359 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """Eurovoc has the support of the Publication Office of the European Union as a developer community. \r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:29640a47-5cc2-4233-b03c-88f00af35d61 .

camssa:fd65c9f8-922f-4ab0-983e-56457ccb6f92 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ISO 3166-1 is intended to serve as a code list for the names of countries, dependent territories and special areas of geographical interest. Therefore, it is not designed to address nor prevent data long-term preservation.\r
\r
ISO 3166-1 reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/72482.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ada965e0-39bb-4db7-b028-8da4ba75358b .

camssa:fd669b5a-35ff-4767-a915-1511783a0c83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XSLT specification does not provide means for restriction of access to information/data. Therefore this criterion is considered not applicable specification.

XSLT Reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/xslt-30'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c35c6beb-6451-4775-b8ed-7ef08168cf94 .

camssa:fd70eceb-b9c9-4098-80bb-66cce42f091e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"TLS 1.3 is not classified as a European Standard but is instead an international standard developed by the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF), used by every public european organisation to provide the necessary security, interoperability, and performance to safeguard sensitive data and ensure trust in online interactions. 

Additionally, it is included in the ISO/IEC organisation, under the name ISO/IEC 20648:2016 - TLS specification for storage systems, which defines the requirements for utilising the TLS protocol within data storage systems. Furthermore, TLS 1.3 is widely recognised and adopted within Europe, including by the European Commission's Multi-Stakeholder Platform on ICT Standardisation.

European Multi-Stakeholder Platform on ICT Standardisation:
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/multi-stakeholder-platform-ict-standardisation

ISO/IEC 20648:2016 - TLS specification for storage systems Reference:
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso-iec:20648:ed-1:v1:en\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55e96d10-8ddc-4bd5-a38c-712ace304592 .

camssa:fd7599fe-5b61-44b3-a85b-557c748700cb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "PDF 1.7 does not defines a cross-sector reusable data model, but defines a file format for representing electronic documents. "@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a595d78-c17b-4c70-9bee-fd6e8d35bf63 .

camssa:fd78e57e-fac7-4578-90a8-4cf65e5c633d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fd7964a6-9db6-44fa-b643-f7122f440c00 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d28663fdb5deb361d5ad773d7b7ece3c6acf8d2eb7a1222a60cb08df4c93aac ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:fd79b422-7d81-44ff-911c-b9dd6c4641ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specifications promotes innovation as CSV Dialect to simplify the format to be able to describe various CSV dialects. Due to its simplicity, compatibility, and versatility, CSV is widely used across various industries and domains. It is commonly employed for data import/export, data integration, data migration, data transformation, and other scenarios where tabular data needs to be exchanged between different systems or processed programmatically. There are reports that justify the widespread use of CSV in public procurement.\r
\r
\r
CSV reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180\r
\r
'Utilizing open data: a primer for public procurement research" research document:\r
http://www.zbw.eu/econis-archiv/bitstream/11159/8918/1/180709300X_0.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a427897-a3a2-4d0c-b80b-f9487b9c58af .

camssa:fd79c7a3-1b3f-4541-bea9-a195588f87eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'After being evaluated compliant with the regulation on standardisation 1025/2012, IPsec has been identified by Commission Implementing Decision. The positive evaluation of IPsec and its identification is considered an interoperability agreement, although no specific provision are given to facilitate the drafting of such agreements.\r
\r
European Commission reference, ICT technical specifications:\r
https://ec.europa.eu/growth/single-market/european-standards/ict-standardisation/ict-technical-specifications_en\r
\r
IPSec reference:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4301'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3644b284-2496-40b6-b290-22ccbe9afd3c .

camssa:fd8e0c93-0659-4940-a09d-741599d385ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.\r
\r
W3C Patent practice:\r
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9cf2d992-3afb-44ca-9218-8a1ff7cc9ea2 .

camssa:fd8f9bce-a51a-48ad-9c32-9a058e5120a6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IPsec has been selected by several public administrations for secure data exchange over the internet. By allowing the secure exchange of data, the specification fosters the visibility of data across borders. An example of its implementation is the TESTA project, which provides a secure cross-border data communication network service for public administrations.

TESTA ISA2 project:
https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/testa_en/

IPSec reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6071.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fba390ee-3ddf-4708-93dd-331aabe4e53a .

camssa:fd95ff24-fc86-492f-a891-dc1958b1df42 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "60" .

camssa:fd9f2f9c-4a67-4b4c-b4bf-6721c6ba2448 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "http://data.europa.eu/w21/52db89ec-04b2-48d8-9a71-083de303993c"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:fd9f7b67-539e-4a05-beee-a7cacf877af1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The objective of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) is the creation of a common basis for the coordination of standards development for the purpose of systems interconnection.

OSI reference
https://www.iso.org/standard/20269.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0d8436b2-8a71-442e-a349-d8ecb1f6cd22 .

camssa:fda39c14-8d7a-4f4d-8bc6-fad8589fb70e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification explicitly addresses and enables long-term preservation as it allows clients to replicate the history of a dataset and efficiently synchronise with its latest changes.At the heart, a Linked Data Event Stream can be interpreted as a publishing strategy by which a data provider allows multiple third parties to stay in sync with the latest version of the data source in a resource and cost-effective manner.

LDES specification: 
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/linked-data-event-streams-ldes'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cca8b5c2-672d-42a5-b396-868a7c41744f .

camssa:fda501f0-f220-4f00-8300-64c8f18c2128 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """XForms specification became an official W3C Recommendation on 14 October 2003. It has been evolved over the years with versions updates demonstrating that it overcame the possible issues raised on the development and implementation.\r
\r
Xforms 2.0 W3C reference:\r
https://www.w3.org/community/xformsusers/wiki/XForms_2.0"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:017cce1d-e612-4329-8e24-4d46f68ea6b3 .

camssa:fdaaea8b-3c3c-4f46-adf0-ac5f934caa1b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7ab883158b51681c78f90d1a00bbb3840aa2c86e309a9abd1ad6e6eedb5e2735 ;
    cav:value "1" .

camssa:fdab763f-216f-4309-b909-aa2dd9062132 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'TSP can use TSA whose role is to time-stamp a datum to establish evidence indicating that a datum existed before a particular time.  This can then be used, for example, to verify that a digital signature was applied to a message before the corresponding certificate was revoked thus allowing a revoked public key certificate to be used for verifying signatures created prior to the time of revocation. Moreover, it provides a verifiable order of transactions, which is crucial for detecting unauthorised changes and supporting audits. While not encrypting data, when combined with other security measures like encryption, it strengthens overall data protection, especially in regulated environments like finance and healthcare.

TSP IETF reference:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3161

"Timestamp Authentication Protocol for RemoteMonitoring in eHealth" reference:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/4352969_Timestamp_Authentication_Protocol_for_Remote_Monitoring_in_eHealth'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:edef0a79-6881-4be0-862a-9f5d48de618e .

camssa:fdac66b8-478e-47a5-ade0-8506e1030e3b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100" .

camssa:fdaf5857-b6ef-49a2-91d0-bcf8d0509ad5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement "WS-Security helps defining a data model, which represents application-defined data structures and values as a directed edge-labelled graph of nodes."@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c50c672-9e3e-41b5-aa34-203d269b8ef9 .

