camssa:fe1a02e9-70d2-41aa-9370-44740531eeb4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of Standard for Public Code is the reuse of code for the creation of solutions with the most transparent and efficient process, independently from the project type or solution domain. Taking this as a basis, the specification can foster and help the availability of interfaces of internal information systems. \r
\r
The Standard for Public Code webpage:\r
https://standard.publiccode.net/\r
"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a47e1f96-2bff-443a-a11f-acdf4b57ee9c .

camssa:fe1dfd28-7e8b-4d2e-84a7-c1bc56e6d538 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """The purpose of JEPG is not related to organisational interoperability. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification. \r
\r
JEPG ISO reference:\r
https://www.iso.org/standard/18902.html\r
\r
JPEG public reference:\r
https://jpeg.org/jpeg/"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71236b02-3a41-483f-831c-7a7b08b42c03 .

camssa:fe1e9c8d-9903-421a-8a96-2a56e8e1fd64 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """At the moment of performing the assessment, LDAP is widely used at businesses and organizations worldwide for directory-based authentication. These types of resources are included in the development of platforms and services, including innovative solutions. \r
\r
LDAP with Active Directory:\r
https://www.windows-active-directory.com/active-directory-ldap.html"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4ed1ec22-8576-40a2-8eca-71c423631e83 .

camssa:fe1f0c78-6d19-4c94-b227-753b8264ff38 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.\r
\r
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.\r
\r
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.\r
\r
See:\r
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/ \r
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:829e91ff-2717-4da5-abe9-f3c914885448 .

camssa:fe210418-3197-4cf6-9e66-44c9c6ff873a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """OpenPM2 has the support of the Publication Office of the European Union as a developer community. \r
\r
Publication Office of the European Union:\r
https://op.europa.eu/en/home"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ba287076-5b6a-4d09-9e97-be86eb866ded .

