camssa:ff44d810-8752-466c-b1a2-6d30870cd1c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Although the SHACL specification is not addressed to enhance security mechanisms, it can play an important role in policy-based access control systems. In this context, SHACL can be utilised to define rules to determine whether access to certain data shuld be granted or denied. 

"SHACL-ACL: Access Control with SHACL" study:
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43458-7_4

SHACL W3C reference:
https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:724b489e-5e3c-41f2-bcbc-37613d289504 .

camssa:ff482586-d1e9-4ad5-b727-49aa63a13fdb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is an element with high relevance in the data and information exchange. UTF-8 as a specification to encoding data ensures that files, web applications and systems can be read by both parts implied in the communication ensuring the reliability of transferred data. Therefore, UTF-8 eases the trustworthy data exchange between administration and stakeholders. \r
\r
UTF-8 specification:\r
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3629'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:30e2f7f5-17dc-42ff-bfda-577d92e40716 .

