camssa:46e8e8db-6e89-4785-ae33-b8651937a7ce a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The CAdES Baseline signatures helps users simplify the usage of electronic signatures in electronic documents by (at the most basic signature level) using the SignedData.certificates attribute which includes the signed data itself, the signature value, and enough information to identify the signatory's certificate at the time of signing. This way, the users are provided with the relevant information about the document and it's signataires straightforward, thus enhancing user understanding of the document._x000D_
A practical example of this is the CEF Digital Signature Service (DSS), which leverages CAdES to provide clear and verifiable electronic signatures. Through DSS, users can easily verify signature validity and timestamp information, helping improve trust and transparency in_x000D_
electronic communications._x000D_
_x000D_
DSS reference: _x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html#CAdES_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation: _x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c9c07352-86b5-4a01-ab77-5aac89c2d33e .

camssa:4b096a17-0470-47e8-bbad-3aba3535e648 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CAdES started development as RFC 5126 by IETF, which  was built on the already existing standards RFC 5652, ISO/IEC 9594-8/ITU-T Recommendation X.509, RFC 3280 and RFC 3161 (as section-9.1 and 2 of the specification)._x000D_
_x000D_
The specification at that point introduced the concept of multiple signature forms to achieve increasing levels of security and preservation. With the enforcement of the eIDAS Regulation (EU No 910/2014) the CAdES specification was restructured and aligned with the core principles of the regulation by ETSI._x000D_
Therefore, the major difference with the previous release of the specification (ETSI TS 119 122-1) from 2015 is the aligment with the eIDAS Regulation but also the incorporation of technical updates to align with ETSI TS 119 312 (Cryptographic Suites) to support more secure algorithms and address the latest advances in cryptographic evolution._x000D_
Alongside this, CAdES has had a regular flow of minor releases to clarify certain technical aspects as it can be seen on the Annex F of the specification. This means CAdES is a consolidated and mature enough specification to use in the development of digital solutions and services. _x000D_
_x000D_
ETSI TS 119 312 (Cryptographic Suites) reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119300_119399/119312/01.04.03_60/ts_119312v010403p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG_x000D_
_x000D_
RFC 5652 Cryptographic Message Syntax (CMS) reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc5652.txt_x000D_
_x000D_
ISO/IEC 9594-8/ITU-T Recommendation X.509 Public-key and attribute certificate frameworks reference:_x000D_
https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso-iec:9594:-8:en_x000D_
_x000D_
RFC 3280 Certificate and Certificate Revocation List (CRL) Profile reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc3280_x000D_
_x000D_
RFC 3161 Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3161.txt_x000D_
_x000D_
RFC 5126 reference: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5126'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b9035001-6614-4cce-9836-2340fba2da01 .

camssa:4e38437e-3dfc-4cc4-b7c6-b86bbcc90f17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI has provided a conformance testing tool for electronic signatures. The conformity testing tool involves different standards applied in the development of eSignatures, including PAdES, CAdES and XAdES and their respective baseline profiles. _x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Conformance Checker reference _x000D_
https://signatures-conformance-checker.etsi.org/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5a8e73bd-e6a9-4136-9353-8d7161d3b03b .

camssa:4fe6529a-006e-449b-a918-c39da2444475 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES Baseline Signatures is a set of well-defined technical specifications developed by ETSI to ensure both interoperability and legal validity of electronic signatures across Europe, in line with the eIDAS Regulation. The specification includes several signature levels: CAdES-B, CAdES-T, CAdES-LT, and CAdES-LTA, which can be implemented individually based on the desired properties._x000D_
These levels are designed to be incremental, meaning that a basic signature (CAdES-B) can be progressively enhanced to include additional features like timestamps or long-term validation data, depending on user or system requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS regulation: _x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:467c22e0-94c4-4ac6-9b8a-814b6adf4ba5 .

camssa:52c9fc56-1a83-4935-a2fa-64c0c2332484 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES Baseline signatures function is to facilitate the electronic signature in compliance with eIDAS. In this sense, the specification provides with the "complete-certificate-references" attribute, which shall contain the reference to the certificate of the trust anchor if such certificate does exist._x000D_
This means that a system receiving the signed document doesn't need to perform an entirely new validation process from scratch. It can reuse the included data to verify the signature's authenticity._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9168a99-0ad4-4550-9069-a633afc73891 .

camssa:54758328-bad4-45df-bb4b-6c4d55666535 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

