camssa:6880690c-f3a2-43d9-b4b7-be7c99bbb1b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES Baseline Signatures includes mechanisms for long-term validation, such as timestamps and embedded certificate information. This means that a signed public record or contract can be securely archived and remain legally verifiable for some time. In this regard the preservation of the date of signature is a partial preservation of the record. The highest baseline level, CAdES-LTA (Long-Term Archival), facilitates the long term data preservation through the Document Time-Stamp (Archive Time-Stamp Token attribute) which is a cryptographic seal placed over the entire document structure and all embedded signatures._x000D_
When a new Document Time-Stamp is applied (a form of periodic extension), it essentially reuses the integrity of all preceding data, including the certificate data already present in the document certificate._x000D_
This proves that the validation data (certificates and revocation checks) existed and was valid at the time the Document Time-Stamp was applied, effectively "re-certifying" the entire package against the threat of future cryptographic breaking or certificate expiry._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b41e1d75-c4cf-4d23-ab6b-f50db17791d6 .

camssa:6c2dfc79-8622-43ae-9e52-bb15420149c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3221fede-643d-49a0-a3b5-42c944b801b5 .

camssa:6ebc611c-ca4d-49e9-94cc-3019ec8b8e5e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:70bbcd17-0f0f-4c24-8aa3-4fec6091f320 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES specification can be found used in different European projects and also by Member States. Since it is suitable for advanced electronic signatures in electronic documents, it is used by companies and public administrations to sign multiple documents. In this context, the specification has been selected within the CEF Digital Signature Service (DSS) along with PAdES, ASiC and XAdES Baseline profiles. Digital Signature Service is an open-source software library for electronic signature creation and validation supporting the interoperability of electronic signatures. The initiative is an enabler for cross borders interoperability between administrations and businesses. Applications such as eCoSignature from the Ministry of Industry and Commerce of Spain use CAdES as one of their base specifications. _x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
eCoSignature reference (EN):_x000D_
https://firmaelectronica.gob.es/en/ciudadanos/cosas-deberias-saber/formatos-firma_x000D_
 _x000D_
DSS reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/cefdigital/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html _x000D_
_x000D_
eSignatureHub - Digital Signature Service DSS:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/DIGITAL/pages/467109107/Digital+Signature+Service+-+DSS _x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:64c32237-66cf-458b-9f0b-ae3765f2f2e6 .

camssa:73dd3df0-01f7-4a09-9941-9685082e955d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:76f2bfec-c747-4036-a0ff-837206954f83 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES Baseline signatures guarantees authenticity by cryptographically linking the signature to a specific individual and their certificate. In this sense the signature must be applied after the file has been encrypted. So, while the encryption is done beforehand it will be intrinsically tied to the user signing the document._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:12b03c03-fa07-4a18-97fd-bc538bf519f0 .

camssa:7a6df5bb-db8a-4390-b831-dcda5830c206 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7ca5e863-2d36-4503-9a3e-48e6887e2a02 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CAdES is within the European eIDAS regulation which is legally binding for all EU members states. CAdES is also a core element of the EUDI Wallet initiative of the European Union, defined under the revised eIDAS Regulation 2.0. It is a secure, EU-backed digital wallet (typically a mobile application) designed to empower EU citizens, residents, and businesses with a universally recognised, user-centric, and privacy-preserving means of digital identification and authentication across the entire European single market. _x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/2979/oj_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7a6df5bb-db8a-4390-b831-dcda5830c206 .

camssa:7e5e2c07-73d0-4342-91de-c4e4794359b6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While the primary purpose of the CAdES Baseline Profile may not be focused on data integrity, its design supports mechanisms that uphold it. The different signature levels allow stakeholders to incorporate additional fields that can facilitate the detection of unauthorised changes, thereby reinforcing document integrity._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:baef537a-5e75-42b0-bbbd-2b51e93c39ae .

camssa:812bf3c1-4b34-4144-8f3c-7148425279db a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the CAdES Baseline Signatures is not related to modelling business processes. Therefore, this_x000D_
criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6ebc611c-ca4d-49e9-94cc-3019ec8b8e5e .

camssa:81dc8caa-a1e4-41a5-9452-bfbf9f65bcdf a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8fd9a13b-74d1-419e-b862-711eb57d667c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CAdES is maintained by ETSI, one of the European Agencies for Standardisation, specifically by the ETSI Technical Committee Electronic Signatures and Trust Infrastructures (ESI)._x000D_
_x000D_
ETSI reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/about _x000D_
_x000D_
Electronic Signatures and Trust Infrastructures (ESI) reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/committee/1399-esi_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a6f59da2-bd19-4c86-8af3-b975f65a2173 .

camssa:97df769e-8b8c-4904-ba6d-84be9a1cded1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI’s standards-making process has been clearly defined after years of experience. The organisation has adopted the open approach which means direct participation and consensus as a basis to develop standards. All the stakeholders have the opportunity to participate directly in the process of standardisation through the technical committees created to develop ETSI’s technical specifications and standards.

ETSI Standard-making process:
https://portal.etsi.org/Resources/Standards-Making-Process/Process'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:652e9ee7-5e88-4280-a76b-b6340e067654 .

camssa:9a0ef978-11c2-4eda-b512-59289459af47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ETSI is a European standards development organisation, and as such, all the specifications developed within the organisation are available and can be accessed through its website repository.

ETSI standards repository:
https://www.etsi.org/standards#page=1&search=ETSI%20TS%20319%20422&title=1&etsiNumber=1&content=1&version=0&onApproval=1&published=1&withdrawn=1&historical=1&isCurrent=1&superseded=1&startDate=1988-01-15&endDate=2022-07-25&harmonized=0&keyword=&TB=&stdType=&frequency=&mandate=&collection=&sort=1'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f9c2c0ed-a73e-44e0-9483-5f6e17b645cd .

