camssa:c47171c5-6fc7-4a6e-b853-bcab7f61a0a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'CAdES achieves multilingual support through its reliance on the Cryptographic Message Syntax (CMS) and the old  X.509 certificates, which are fundamentally based on international standards like Unicode/UTF-8._x000D_
_x000D_
In particular, the entire structure of a CMS object is defined using ASN.1 (Abstract Syntax Notation One) and then encoded into a binary format. ASN.1 encoding rules (GSER) include a string type called UTF8String, which ensures that the characters are encoded using UTF-8._x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
Generic String Encoding Rules (GSER) for ASN.1 Types reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3641_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1661830c-f6ee-4146-bbd9-4d20a0100e2e .

camssa:c765a5c9-dc34-4a43-bb2e-de47d21a94ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The CAdES baseline signatures has sparked some online communities that discuss the specification's implementation in regards to others as well as the data related to it. It also created numerous questions and debates on developer forums like stackoverflow._x000D_
_x000D_
Docusign community: https://community.docusign.com/esignature-111/xades-cades-or-pades-2917_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack-overflow communities and discussions:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/cades_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:be5a178f-e269-497c-a66f-8d244d35650e .

camssa:c8b1b963-ca92-4b7f-b720-00738cfafb7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the CAdES baseline signatures is not related to data processing. Therefore this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d168d16b-d30f-4177-a510-a44a8a7890da .

camssa:c8ccede3-635a-4d41-a1ac-234acaad2f8b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c9236590-0791-496d-b205-64aed2151f52 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ETSI IPR Policy which is part of the ETSI directives seeks to reduce the risk that our standards-making efforts might be wasted if SEPs are unavailable under Fair, Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory (FRAND) terms and conditions.
The main objective of the ETSI IPR Policy is to balance the rights and interests of IPR holders to be fairly and adequately rewarded for the use of their SEPs in the implementation of ETSI standards and the need for implementers to get access to the technology defined in ETSI standards under FRAND terms and conditions.

ETSI’s intellectual property rights policy:
https://www.etsi.org/intellectual-property-rights'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db3b32d4-973a-4886-bd2f-a20852e1c0b4 .

camssa:c9c07352-86b5-4a01-ab77-5aac89c2d33e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cd598d4a-590d-4900-9333-020d59795099 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of the CAdES Baseline Signatures is not related to e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:54758328-bad4-45df-bb4b-6c4d55666535 .

