camssa:f44413a9-3e91-45ef-aca4-58602b549251 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The CAdES Baseline Signatures main purpose is to provide the stakeholders involved in any electronic transaction with the certainty that the exchanged documents are truthful for all. In this sense the different signature levels (B Basic, T Time, LT Long-Term and LTA Long-Term Archive) provide a wide arrangement of security but it is not exhaustive._x000D_
_x000D_
It is worth mentioning that the specification is based on CMS, which enables data encryption and supports secure data exchange._x000D_
_x000D_
CMS reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5652_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e1e80ea9-b2eb-474a-bc84-7d9d814c4ba9 .

camssa:f6fd1bb8-b954-400e-b022-3051d819023a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The CAdES Baseline signature is designed to guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the agents involved in data transactions. It achieves this by focusing on the signer's identity and their role, which is a core requirement of the eIDAS regulation._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation: _x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidasregulation_x000D_
_x000D_
CAdES reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/319100_319199/31912201/01.03.01_60/en_31912201v010301p.pdf\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3b784e9-d904-42c1-af6b-e40527aff7c7 .

