camssa:222a8230-378c-43a1-bcdd-4b3001f0d70f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx is platform agnostic as it defines a language and validation framework independent of specific software environments or vendors. It can be implemented across different platforms and technologies that support RDF. However, its use is limited outside the RDF ecosystem._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C RDF Concepts and Abstract Data Model Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf12-concepts/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b226750e-ce64-4e76-bdaa-705aa5546a87 .

camssa:2ae3edae-5953-4f43-848e-73b1d3736e72 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2c53bf41-76e4-413e-9acd-69c834a575c8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx allows extensions. Mechanisms like semantic actions, custom datatypes, and annotations enable controlled, implementation-specific extensions without altering core validation semantics. For example, ShExMap supports mapping and transformation of RDF data. The official ShEx extensions catalogue collects such extensions, showing how ShEx provides flexibility for domain-specific needs._x000D_
_x000D_
ShEx Extensions Github reference:_x000D_
https://shexspec.github.io/extensions/_x000D_
_x000D_
ShExMap Extension Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/extensions/Map/_x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7dc9a76f-7068-4c28-8249-d083369c3bae .

camssa:2d31cad0-d1da-4a28-9865-e8d4a1b334ee a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx is technology-agnostic but depends on the RDF specification. It can be applied across platforms and domains that use RDF, ensuring data consistency and interoperability regardless of the technologies. However, its aplication outside the RDF ecosystem is limited._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C RDF Concepts and Abstract Data Model Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf12-concepts/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0bd46856-a645-455a-bc21-d5f654df4865 .

camssa:2e593e11-db37-4b0b-8ba6-647717634534 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2e7df028-1891-4128-98c5-3686405f01c4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The ShEx Community Group is an active W3C Community Group of developers, tasked with the maintenance and evolution of the ShEx specification. The group also operates via Github, where anyone interested can raise issues and pull requests about its implementation._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
ShEx Community Group:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/community/shex/_x000D_
_x000D_
ShEx Github:_x000D_
https://github.com/shexSpec/spec/issues'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:01a0daaa-5d9e-4f46-94d9-beb78be2d0a2 .

camssa:316deea2-c270-4a1c-8164-1da832dbc06d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:36f34208-1b9b-489c-a496-d8e2f6f87fbd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx allows the creation of core shape definitions that can be customised to fit specific business or domain requirements, ensuring interoperability without imposing technology-specific constraints._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c76ea2c0-7ea4-4b11-bbce-657514180c05 .

camssa:3845746a-1542-4756-b5cf-a02600213fc9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx specification does not provide mechanisms for restricting access to information or data, since it focuses more on data validation, ensuring that it conforms to predefined shapes and relationships. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89aa8bc2-6e66-4be7-ad17-cb1000c50184 .

camssa:3bff5a5a-9938-4ed7-bc27-40efb9f40fc3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3d7b9f2e-775c-4777-81d9-02d80f839ce6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx allows for partial implementations, as its specification is modular and focused on RDF validation semantics. Implementers can adopt only the core or relevant features needed for their use case without compromising overall interoperability. An example of partial implementation can be shex.js, a javascript implementation, its ideal for browser-based validation tools and lightweight RDF data checks, focusing on core ShEx functionality without full language complexity._x000D_
_x000D_
shex.js Javascript implementation reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/shexjs/shex.js_x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C RDF Concepts and Abstract Data Model Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf12-concepts/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:123d78fe-d7bf-444c-b523-9a4aa5909075 .

camssa:3ef812ad-ee2c-42ae-b935-21c76c5ff3a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx can be used in a multilingual context because it provides standardised, machine-readable validation for language information. Built upon RDF native support for language-tagged literals, the specification includes value sets that can also contain stems for IRIs, strings, and language tags. An IRI or string stem matches any IRI or string that starts with the stem._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/#value-sets'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b98c85f4-6381-4bfb-99d5-52b848057f90 .

camssa:4550bb13-8baf-44d7-a79d-cdd0954dff53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx acts as a language for validating semantic data and ensuring structural consistency within the Linked Data environment. By defining standardised Shapes (data contracts) for specific public service domains built upon RDF, different systems can exchange data that is not only structurally correct but also semantically reliable. _x000D_
_x000D_
For example, projects like the Yosemite project leverage ShEx to create a robust, interoperable data model for clinical data exchange, significantly reducing the administrative and technical burden of integrating health records across organisations and national systems. The Yosemite Project is a collaborative effort dedicated to healthcare information interoperability. It is comprised of experts in healthcare and technology and guided by a six-member steering committee._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
Yosemite Project Reference:_x000D_
https://yosemiteproject.org/interoperability-roadmap/_x000D_
_x000D_
Using Shape Expressions (ShEx) to Share RDF Data Models and to Guide Curation with Rigorous _x000D_
Validation:_x000D_
https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-21348-0_39'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b085bec-13d9-4da0-ae74-200b8752da0f .

camssa:4a27bc1f-ecba-4423-afb4-d7a866d8c234 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4ab50526-8ce1-41cf-96e0-70cc98e0ac15 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4d35d5b6-746c-459d-92a2-3680941a59f6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx validates RDF datasets, ensuring they conform to defined shapes and constraints. It is dependent on the RDF specification because it relies on the core concepts of triples, subjects, predicates, objects, and the definitions of RDF Terms (IRIs, blank nodes, and literals) to exist and be functional, without RDF data, ShEx has nothing to validate. By supporting the consistency, correctness, and structure of this foundational RDF data, ShEx can then enable the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services across public administrations._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C RDF Concepts and Abstract Data Model Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf12-concepts/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:200b7cd2-eae3-4362-8b6a-85f6eb70907a .

camssa:53f6c999-65dd-4add-9983-72246a72d9f3 a cav:Score,
