camssa:75f75c19-a3ed-4489-9015-63f8db08c4a0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The ShEx specification is not included in any Member States' catalogue of recommended specifications._x000D_
_x000D_
NIFO factsheets:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024_x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference: _x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b436bf8a-d37f-49f3-9d7a-cffabfc5fe94 .

camssa:7af7cae3-a086-499d-b5bf-b98b6494f036 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx demonstrates a good level of maturity and domain acceptance. It is maintained by an active W3C Community Group. Several research and implementation cases, in healthcare and linked-data validation, confirm its practical use._x000D_
_x000D_
Although ShEx is not a formal W3C Recommendation, it is considered a highly stable, community-driven specification. Its current "candidate" status for the Final 2.0 Release, combined with growing academic and technical uptake, makes it a viable and credible choice for RDF-based solutions._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/_x000D_
_x000D_
Modeling and validating HL7 FHIR profiles using semantic web Shape Expressions (ShEx):_x000D_
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28213144/_x000D_
_x000D_
Development of a FHIR RDF data transformation and validation framework and its evaluation:_x000D_
https://mayoclinic.elsevierpure.com/en/publications/development-of-a-fhir-rdf-data-transformation-and-validation-fram/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b517a6be-1a6f-4946-a498-6a5a4240ad6c .

camssa:7b6900cb-6a02-49ca-9647-ce76ee459510 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx main function is to facilitate data exhange in RDF format by providing the means to validate RDF data graphs and does not directly enable the secure processing of data. ShEx is a schema and validation language, not a security protocol, this criterion is not applicable to this specification. _x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d3925d94-c75a-44ed-9b7d-440b6acd06a3 .

camssa:7bb0824e-3469-43fa-905d-5ac7bdfe3502 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7dc9a76f-7068-4c28-8249-d083369c3bae a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8113d62f-6e08-42f8-9d7e-09199f0365a7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'ShEx specification itself does not guarantee the authenticity and authentication of the roles or agents involved in data transactions, since its a structural schema language for RDF graphs. Its function is strictly focused on data validation. Therefore this criterion does not apply to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
Shape Expressions (ShEx) 2.1 Reference:_x000D_
https://shex.io/shex-primer/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:56b0024e-56a6-40fa-ac4f-83e4d5d22eb8 .

