    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:27dab6e6-8ec8-4fdf-9ae2-7992388752c6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the XBRL GL language has been assessed by researchers from Mackenzie Presbyterian University and the University of São Paulo. In the "Use of the XBRL Language: potential benefits to brazilian companies" study, the XBRL language is proposed as a method to communicate financial information to the market, facilitating an increased perception of transparency and a reduction in informational asymmetry._x000D_
_x000D_
"Use of the XBRL Language: potential benefits to brazilian companies" study:_x000D_
https://periodicos.uninove.br/innovation/article/view/24011/10581_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e0ccaa0a-74d6-4179-8856-d0fdc2c5d624 .

camssa:2ad81050-e818-42ca-a2f7-fe6c820f790a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The specification enables reporting for various needs from a single data source. The foundational concept behind XBRL GL's creation, driven by its chief architect Eric Cohen, was to ensure that once a piece of business information is digitally recorded, it can move through the entire reporting supply chain without ever requiring manual re-entry._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL use cases:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-standard/_x000D_
_x000D_
Rutgers Accounting Research Center/CARLab - The Work of Eric Cohen:_x000D_
http://raw.rutgers.edu/carlab/Cohen.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0c12aaa9-6703-44d3-ada4-d7fa9f355a04 .

camssa:2f9e09a8-b85c-4256-8e24-6b4f3ce81cd9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL foresees sets of requirements that can be implemented separately. There are no requirements on the extent of the implementation of the specification, and the extent of the data contents being used should vary between use cases. This is achieved through its modular architecture, which allows implementers to select from a mandatory Core module and optional modules for specific needs, such as the Business module for customer details or the Tax Audit File module for providing data to tax authorities. It is recommended to publish sets of requirements per implementation._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL use cases:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-standard/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL Essentials (validation requirements):_x000D_
https://specifications.xbrl.org/xbrl-essentials.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:203fdb54-a8ec-4982-8a25-ba84b2a1ab35 .

camssa:35e6b838-9038-443e-970a-be0514bbdeb4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:38113909-c9a3-4bf5-99da-0b972927ea55 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL is recommended by European Member States both directly and indirectly. The foundational XBRL specification, on which XBRL GL is based, is officially recommended in the national catalogues of Ireland, Malta, and the Netherlands, as documented in the CAMSS List of Standards. More specifically, the Estonian Tax and Customs Board recommends the use of XBRL GL for the electronic submission of general ledger data as part of its "Reporting 3.0" initiative. This initiative is a core component of Estonia's "Real-Time Economy" vision, which aims to create a seamless, automated data exchange between businesses and the government. By using XBRL GL, the project enables companies to submit transaction-level data directly from their accounting systems, with the ultimate goal of creating a "no-tax-return" environment, demonstrating a deep and innovative recommendation of the specification for a core e-government service._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standars:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
Estonian Tax and Customs Board - Data-based reporting:_x000D_
https://www.emta.ee/en/business-client/board-news-and-contact/estonian-tax-and-customs-board/data-based-reporting_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cee4177-194d-4527-a272-bc84e5fd5f15 .

camssa:383a5231-60d7-49b1-b653-c611fecad4f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL specification is a pillar of the European Single Electronic Format (ESEF). This regulation requires all issuers on EU regulated markets to prepare their annual financial reports in a single electronic format (based on XBRL). Also it could operate entirely within the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), which can include personal data of individuals._x000D_
_x000D_
European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA) - ESEF:_x000D_
https://www.esma.europa.eu/policy-activities/corporate-disclosure/european-single-electronic-format_x000D_
_x000D_
EUR-Lex - General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3de0663b-a1c2-4894-a535-2c5db1ef8d65 .

camssa:394757a1-b2ed-47ff-82a0-94388eb11897 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:39a869b3-b234-4065-9318-0843cc387c20 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3b831e7f-6b52-45e1-8184-801f7cae24f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'On a technical level, developers and implementers actively discuss the XBRL GL specification, sharing solutions, implementations, and questions on general programming forums such as Stack Overflow , which has a dedicated “xbrl” tag._x000D_
_x000D_
Stack Overflow - XBRL Community_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/xbrl_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f6ec7845-3e80-4d29-87fb-34038a344bf2 .

camssa:3de0663b-a1c2-4894-a535-2c5db1ef8d65 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4aec3401-89e6-46db-9a03-e5d50e190690 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XBRL is not related to enable the secure processing of data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d17fffc2-7629-404d-a47b-4c23132c8175 .

camssa:4cee4177-194d-4527-a272-bc84e5fd5f15 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4d0d46a9-2e0c-45a4-a75a-6defea81989e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL specification is defined by a precise set of measurable rules that are designed for automated validation. To facilitate this, XBRL International provides and maintains official "XBRL Conformance Suites". These are comprehensive sets of test files and supporting documentation, including both valid and invalid instances, that software developers use as a resource to automatically test whether their applications correctly implement the rules of the core XBRL 2.1 specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2.1 Specification:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/Specification/XBRL-2.1/REC-2003-12-31/XBRL-2.1-REC-2003-12-31+corrected-errata-2013-02-20.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL Conformance Suites:_x000D_
https://specifications.xbrl.org/release-history-base-spec-conformance-suite.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b3f66fcb-8fb7-49de-9218-c3e5c0956334 .

camssa:4e2c2e23-573a-4566-a744-0fa134c33b93 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL GL specification is technology agnostic because it is built upon XML. This means that an XBRL GL document is a text-based file with a defined structure that can be created, read, and processed by any software, on any operating system, and using any programming language that has XML parsing capabilities._x000D_
_x000D_
XML specification:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee487592-7999-447b-a157-02ed5537d7ac .

camssa:4efbdb49-09e4-4ac3-9c92-cf1e8f6eb445 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL-GL is included in 3 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Ireland, Malta and Netherlands among others. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Ireland and the Netherlands are aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standars:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
NIFO Factsheets:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/nifo-national-interoperability-framework-observatory/digital-public-administration-factsheets-2024_x000D_
_x000D_
Ireland national catalogue:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/NIFO_2024_Supporting%20document_Ireland_vFINAL.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Netherlands national catalogue: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/NIFO_2024%20Supporting%20Document_Netherlands_vFinal_1.pdf_x000D_
