camssa:5533b458-5807-4800-92f2-27597c4e0dad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The primary function of XBRL GL is to create a standardised, machine-readable format for detailed financial and business data. This standardisation is the key to interoperability, allowing administrative bodies like tax agencies, regulators, and national treasuries to automate the collection, consolidation, and analysis of information. By enabling seamless data exchange and providing a clear, auditable trail from summary reports down to individual transactions, the specification inherently enhances the transparency of business operations for administrative oversight._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:208a0626-6763-43da-80a1-5f277abb8d31 .

camssa:558e7dc6-fc2f-45ad-9f80-66a29a7ca4f2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:55e88c05-8064-47dc-8d50-11c97dd409e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XBRL is not related to enable the secure exchange of data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7a48ea3-ee23-4587-b3ff-1225d2258ec4 .

camssa:56e9a2e8-ea79-4197-9792-419e26dfc46c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL GL specification is included in national catalogues and repositories. The foundational XBRL specification, on which XBRL GL is based, is officially recommended in the national catalogues of several Member States, including Ireland, Malta, and the Netherlands, as documented in the CAMSS List of Standards. Furthermore, Estonia's "Aruandlus 3.0" (Reporting 3.0) project, a key part of its national "Real-Time Economy" vision, is designed to automate data exchange between companies and the state. This project is built on the principle of using XBRL GL as the standard for machine-readable, transaction-level data for tax and statistical reporting._x000D_
_x000D_
The Baltic Course - Estonia plans wide use of XBRL-GL (Aruandlus 3.0):_x000D_
http://www.baltic-course.com/eng/good_for_business/?doc=159557_x000D_
_x000D_
Estonian Tax and Customs Board - Data-based Reporting:_x000D_
https://www.emta.ee/en/business-client/board-news-and-contact/estonian-tax-and-customs-board/data-based-reporting_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standars:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7ce3599a-09c6-4042-966b-4d45deaec327 .

camssa:576660f0-9fe3-41de-beb9-4a11b92e736c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XBRL GL is not related to the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe72bd7e-1482-436f-a855-26f749b7b18a .

camssa:59c60cc6-cf46-4188-9d6f-6986595cf1d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL specification was designed to permit not only the capture and expression of business_x000D_
reporting facts in all of the languages supported by ISO 639, but also the internal capture and expression of_x000D_
regulation and guidance related to the reporting content. The specification has support already for 8_x000D_
languages and the process for adding new ones is defined._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL International - Multilingual XBRL Guidance:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/guidance/multilingual-labels/#:~:text=XBRL%20supports%20multilingual%20taxonomies%20by%20allowing%20labels%20to,reader%20to%20view%20labels%20in%20their%20preferred%20language._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d47e0e49-de8f-45f3-b8de-ed24c55eb57a .

camssa:5b2c842e-54da-4896-baca-b9b957722828 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL specification does not include any mechanisms for confidentiality within the specification itself. The responsibility for implementing confidentiality rests with the systems and infrastructure handling the data, not with the data format._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL use cases:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-standard/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74fa3ac5-ac78-455a-9df9-d12ce38c5108 .

camssa:5b4893a2-7e1f-4945-b40d-8564342ecf8e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL-GL is already associated with EIRA ABBs. More specifically, XBRL-GL can define the interoperability aspects of the "Accounting" ABB of the EIRA Technical view and the "Data Representation" ABB of the EIRA Semantic view._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS) v6.1.1:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83875c93-6627-41f8-8261-75e27d92a7d2 .

camssa:5ce91237-998a-42ca-9e56-4ea03d4d0500 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:63b589ef-d698-405e-a7a7-20de80fe3423 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The principal purpose of the XBRL GL specification is to enable data portability. It achieves this by providing a standardised, open, and machine-readable format that is independent of any specific software or platform. This common format allows detailed business and financial data to be seamlessly moved between different applications without loss of meaning or the need for costly custom data transformations._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL International (Global Ledger overview):_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-standard/what/global-ledger/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:50828c36-4e72-4597-b3f0-e728b63e0a25 .

