camssa:850354f8-4704-4442-a016-347e3e478160 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL is the core technology for the European Single Electronic Format (ESEF), a major cross-border initiative mandated by the European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA). The purpose of XBRL within this project is to create a single, machine-readable format for the annual financial reports of all publicly listed companies across the entire European Union. Furthermore, specific national initiatives are using XBRL GL to build systems that facilitate cross-border interoperability; for example, Estonia's "Reporting 3.0" project uses XBRL GL to standardise the exchange of detailed transactional data with its Tax and Customs Board._x000D_
_x000D_
European Single Electronic Format (ESEF) Regulation:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_del/2019/815/oj_x000D_
_x000D_
Estonian Tax and Customs Board - Data-based Reporting:_x000D_
https://www.emta.ee/en/business-client/board-news-and-contact/estonian-tax-and-customs-board/data-based-reporting_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6e792f14-26ae-43d1-929e-7a4c318e38ff .

