camssa:96226ced-474e-4932-ace0-d020a8d55fa0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL GL specification enables data processing accuracy through its mandatory, built-in validation mechanisms. It uses XML Schema to ensure all data conforms to the correct structure and data types, preventing formatting errors. More powerfully, the specification includes a "Calculation Linkbase" which allows for the definition of business rules and mathematical relationships that are automatically checked by processing software._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2.1 Specification - Section 5.2.5.2: Calculation validation:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/Specification/XBRL-2.1/REC-2003-12-31/XBRL-2.1-REC-2003-12-31+corrected-errata-2013-02-20.html#_5.2.5.2_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98a3b3e3-46f8-4453-bedf-162508597f14 .

camssa:98a3b3e3-46f8-4453-bedf-162508597f14 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a048a71f-6270-41b1-97cf-f678d89f4e31 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification is explicitly designed to be extended. Users can create their own extension taxonomies to define new, specific concepts (elements) or relationships that are not included in the base XBRL GL standard._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL Essentials (Extensibility section):_x000D_
https://specifications.xbrl.org/xbrl-essentials.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:558e7dc6-fc2f-45ad-9f80-66a29a7ca4f2 .

camssa:a4c1e9a8-358d-4e66-a5da-c3da3504826a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL is fundamentally designed for the business and accounting domain. While it is a powerful and flexible standard within this context, its inherent semantics are not directly transferable to entirely different domains like healthcare, legal case management, or scientific research. Therefore, this specification is definetly tied to the business world._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a51afae4-c037-4cb0-ac1e-733b7b9ac965 .

camssa:a51afae4-c037-4cb0-ac1e-733b7b9ac965 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "40"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a6bacca6-599d-42b4-870d-d5f1930db0b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL specification simplifies the delivery of public services by enabling information to be exchanged between parties in a standardised way. When public administrations need to communicate with each other or with businesses, they can use a common, machine-readable format instead of relying on separate, proprietary solutions._x000D_
_x000D_
A prime example is the Danish Business Authority, which uses XBRL to receive all annual financial statements and share them with the public as open data, streamlining a core government service._x000D_
_x000D_
Danish Open Data Portal:_x000D_
https://datacvr.virk.dk/data_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7cb810f9-2fea-411e-9182-4beab093b8ec .

camssa:b1f8ac53-32ed-42a4-bab6-0910474209b3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b36ab0e8-10a1-45b0-8189-bf1f7bac957f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b3f66fcb-8fb7-49de-9218-c3e5c0956334 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b9497c6c-8197-4a6b-b489-564ad4756a47 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'XBRL GL provides the standardised, machine-readable data structure that serves as the essential payload for a public administration's digital services, such as tax filing or regulatory reporting. This standardised data format acts as the "contract" for any interface designed to receive this information. _x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f537749c-35d2-4a52-8989-dd3c5b3c1de0 .

camssa:bd3c49fc-b792-4421-a142-30aff949d2c2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bd76c72a-cf7b-411a-963f-c741cb72c8aa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the XBRL specification has been assessed by Noor Romy Rahwani of Politeknik Negeri Banjarmasin, Indonesia. In the "Adopting XBRL Efficiently: A Learning Curve-Based Strategic Framework" study, the XBRL specification is proposed as a technology whose implementation can be optimised over time, facilitating the identification of more efficient and cost-effective approaches for companies to adopt XBRL, ultimately enhancing their compliance and financial reporting practices._x000D_
_x000D_
"Adopting XBRL Efficiently: A Learning Curve-Based Strategic Framework" study:_x000D_
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/396890163_Adopting_XBRL_Efficiently_A_Learning_Curve-Based_Strategic_Framework_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:39a869b3-b234-4065-9318-0843cc387c20 .

camssa:bf77dc02-6263-4abe-9e27-b8440ffe69dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification facilitates business processes by providing a standard, interoperable format for the data that is exchanged at key points within those processes. While not a process modelling language itself, XBRL GL is designed to be implemented into standard business processes like "record-to-report" or "procure-to-pay." By standardising the data payload, it simplifies and enables the automation of these cross-organisational business processes._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7568825b-c021-4963-bf52-e8ab9f18b661 .

camssa:c00ea706-4b53-4550-9502-df5024af1333 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL GL specification does not include its own mechanisms for authentication, but it does address the topic by providing a standardised way to record information about the agents involved in a transaction. This gives implementers the chance to identify which person or entity is associated with a specific data entry. While these elements are not authentication themselves, they serve as a necessary foundation or "key" upon which external authentication systems can be built._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:394757a1-b2ed-47ff-82a0-94388eb11897 .

camssa:c9cea5d1-6663-4122-9192-c0b2ec1ca71c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The XBRL GL specification is developed, maintained, and published by XBRL International. This organisation itself constitutes the core community, which is composed of various member organisations, including companies, government agencies, and accounting professionals. Within XBRL International, specific working groups, such as the Global Ledger Working Group, are formally tasked with the ongoing maintenance, development, and support of the specification. _x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:16db7899-11a4-4e03-a63d-5c4f791a4664 .

camssa:cb4811e9-e2fe-4865-a3e5-5c97e274b403 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The first drafts of XBRL GL were developed in 1999 by its chief architect and contributed to XBRL, with the standards process leading to the first official version in 2005. From its inception, the specification was not developed in isolation. To ensure broad applicability and encourage harmonisation, its chief architect and other participants actively collaborated with other international standards bodies. This collaborative history is evident in its relationship with other specifications in overlapping spaces, including the OECD Standard Audit File for Taxation and ISO 21378:2019, proving the versatile capabilities of XBRL GL._x000D_
_x000D_
OECD Standard Audit File for Taxation (SAF-T):_x000D_
https://www.oecd.org/tax/forum-on-tax-administration/publications-and-products/standard-audit-file-for-tax.html_x000D_
_x000D_
ISO 21378:2019:_x000D_
https://www.iso.org/es/contents/data/standard/07/08/70823.html_x000D_
_x000D_
The Wacoal Story;_x000D_
http://www.xbrl.org/business/companies/breathing-new-life-into-old-systems.pdf _x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f259e7e8-21be-488f-ab4b-281fe979639d .

camssa:cce75c41-5e6f-4f43-8842-5227dc9c1d3b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification has achieved significant global market acceptance, a fact documented in numerous independent reports and academic literature reviews that analyse its widespread adoption. This is demonstrated by deep, national-level implementations that involve the specification in core digital solutions. A prime example is Turkey, where the government mandates the use of XBRL GL for its electronic bookkeeping system (e-Defter). An even more innovative use case is found in Estonia, where XBRL GL is a cornerstone of the "Reporting 3.0" initiative, a project designed to create a real-time, automated data ecosystem for businesses and government._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL implementations in Europe:_x000D_
https://www.revistatransparencia.com/ret/article/download/222/340/992_x000D_
_x000D_
Estonian Ministry of Economic Affairs - Real-Time Economy (Reporting 3.0):_x000D_
https://realtimeeconomy-bsr.eu/reporting-model-and-roadmap_x000D_
_x000D_
IFRS Foundation - Turkey Jurisdiction Profile (e-Defter Mandate):_x000D_
https://www.ifrs.org/content/dam/ifrs/publications/jurisdictions/filing-profiles/turkey-18-november-2015.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dbbfb289-1b9b-4b85-ad07-d2a008312555 .

camssa:cd7e49c0-f90f-4c35-80a5-0390e55642c7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XBRL is not related to enable the e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:74f03b9e-1796-4e29-af00-2119126e506b .

camssa:d02036d1-d212-4c08-b43e-639c2d84d2c8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "40"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d17fffc2-7629-404d-a47b-4c23132c8175 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d42c5b0d-bbea-4027-bfe2-59ad607dd084 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"The development of the XBRL GL specification is governed by XBRL International. Direct and ongoing participation in the XBRL GL Working Group is a benefit reserved for members of the consortium. To become a member, an organisation or individual must complete a formal application process (registration and approval) and pay an annual membership. Although non-members can contribute feedback during public review periods and participate in free Community Groups for discussion, they cannot join the working group's core development activities without formal membership._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL GL - Benefits from been part of the consortium:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-consortium/join/membership-benefits/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL GL - How to get involved in the consortium:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/the-consortium/get-involved/_x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d02036d1-d212-4c08-b43e-639c2d84d2c8 .

camssa:d47e0e49-de8f-45f3-b8de-ed24c55eb57a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:db0581ad-0550-4176-aede-c250678b11e5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The primary purpose of XBRL GL is to standardise the representation of detailed accounting and business data, not to define administrative procedures, rules, or services themselves. However, by providing a clear, unambiguous, and machine-readable structure for the data that flows through these administrative processes, it significantly contributes to making the overall process more transparent and comprehensible. _x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea85a2fa-124e-4ed1-81c9-9e44821930aa .

camssa:db130426-812a-49cd-99be-770e5dd8f479 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of XBRL is not related to the protection information against unauthorised changes. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
XBRL 2015 reference: _x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2015-03-25/GLTFTA-REC-2015-03-25.html_x000D_
 _x000D_
XBRL 2017 reference:_x000D_
https://www.xbrl.org/int/gl/2016-12-01/gl-framework-2017-PWD-2016-12-01.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:667f1b04-ffc8-41eb-ad82-c09773fb0e15 .

camssa:dbbfb289-1b9b-4b85-ad07-d2a008312555 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e0ccaa0a-74d6-4179-8856-d0fdc2c5d624 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
