camssa:07c8e3fc-e617-4efb-a050-acd9334997eb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC conformance can be effectively assessed through publicly available test tools, such as the OIDC Conformance Test Suite and OIDC Debugger, allow developers to validate flows (authentication, ID token validation, claims handling) against the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Conformance Suite:_x000D_
https://openid.net/certification/about-conformance-suite/_x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC debugger by Nate Barbettini: _x000D_
https://oidcdebugger.com/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a696c81d-b902-463f-b47f-e0a45e64ae17 .

camssa:0819bfac-f8fe-46a8-a5a8-f4d34f5faaaa a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:08f60f28-c963-422c-bc1d-81aa106df3e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:091e8fce-588c-4a8c-b963-bf80a11b9a98 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC enables secure transmission of identity information during authentication and identity services. It relies on established security mechanisms such as HTTPS, OAuth 2.0, and JWTs to ensure that data in transit is encrypted and tamper-resistant. The specification also enforces the principle of minimal disclosure by allowing only consented identity attributes to be shared with relying parties, supporting selective disclosure and user control._x000D_
_x000D_
Furthermore, OIDC’s optional parameters allow implementers to define precisely which data elements are exchanged, reducing unnecessary exposure of personal data._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Token - JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth 2.0 Client Authentication and Authorization Grants:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7521'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e134691-9bd3-40bc-a359-068710e423a4 .

camssa:120685fb-4bcd-4762-a102-f6eef2008e14 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:15a51943-18c2-4138-b719-d6359335127e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is included in the "Référentiel général d'interopérabilité", which is the French Catalogue of Standards._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a87c2602-2571-4552-891c-ae584c0b1865 .

camssa:16c4ba3b-2228-406f-ab0a-a7a346ea9785 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is a platform-agnostic specification built on widely adopted standards such as HTTP, JSON and OAuth 2.0. It enables interoperable authentication across operating systems, devices and environments, without reliance on specific hardware, software or vendor technologies._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:120685fb-4bcd-4762-a102-f6eef2008e14 .

camssa:1b11fe5b-4894-4fa0-8e9b-a12415487a6c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC enforces the restriction of access to user identity data through a combination of scopes, consent mechanisms, and authorisation tokens. Services can request only the specific information required for a given transaction, and users retain control over which attributes are shared. Access to data is further protected by standard security protocols, including HTTPS and OAuth 2.0 token validation, ensuring that only authorised parties can retrieve or use identity information. This approach supports the principles of data minimisation and purpose limitation, providing Public Administrations and other relying parties with a secure and privacy-preserving framework for identity management._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification Authentication reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#Authentication_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification Privacy reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#Privacy'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9f2a2679-d706-4755-97cc-3ec57d204a79 .

camssa:1e69fe29-2044-4e9c-89fc-d16e07ab9c8c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:27fdba46-3db3-45ac-a536-f5798a1dddc8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2b1155ec-6534-4454-922c-0e04655427fb a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:32e012aa-5da0-4955-817d-7f7ddc5aeb39 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:34c6a6c6-9cf2-4d6e-90d9-7c8acbc60773 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC specification is designed to maximise the reuse of relevant information across identity and authentication processes. Through standardised token formats (such as JWT), claims, scopes, endpoints, and metadata, information issued in one context can be reliably consumed in another without modification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Token (JWT) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7519'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32e012aa-5da0-4955-817d-7f7ddc5aeb39 .

camssa:380b9daf-8f8a-4ebf-8705-1216d13455b1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:390e849f-0f03-4872-b4a5-1e9bad606170 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC enables the secure exchange of identity data by ensuring confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity throughout authentication and authorisation processes. It relies on HTTPS to protect data in transit, signed tokens such as JWTs to guarantee data integrity and authenticity, and OAuth 2.0 authorisation mechanisms to control access. Together, these measures allow relying parties to securely obtain the information they need while preventing unauthorised access or tampering, providing a robust and interoperable framework for identity and credential exchange across public and private services._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification Security reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#ClientAuthentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:729d19d2-fd39-4acd-9a41-cc96c21ffa74 .

camssa:39a6aa5e-7a16-43ac-bf1e-7a5d057e513f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Public review is a stage of the OIDC release lifecycle, featuring fixed review periods of 45 days for Implementer’s Drafts and Errata, and 60 days for Final Specifications. During these windows, feedback is systematically incorporated to enhance clarity and interoperability. This process ensures transparency and community validation, as strictly mandated by the OpenID Foundation’s governance policies._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation OIDC Working Group:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/connect/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Intellectual Property & Contribution Agreements:_x000D_
https://openid.net/intellectual-property/openid-foundation-contribution-agreements/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb37a3ab-1ed5-4056-98f8-0ec6cbcaa43a .

camssa:3ce8b7e4-faa5-44dd-ae0d-4f18c9b30a54 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is used by major platforms (Google, Microsoft, Apple) and public administrations, indicating it can handle large-scale, high-frequency authentication efficiently. OIDC is built on OAuth 2.0 and uses lightweight JSON and HTTPS, reducing overhead and ensuring efficient performance in web, mobile, and API-based services. _x000D_
_x000D_
Additionally, several academic papers and industry reports discuss the efficiency and practical use of OIDC in large-scale deployments._x000D_
_x000D_
A Novel Secure and Privacy-Preserving Model for OpenID Connect Based on Blockchain:_x000D_
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/372115811_A_Novel_secure_and_privacy-preserving_model_for_OpenID_Connect_based_on_Blockchain#:~:text=Abstract%20and%20Figures,informally%20by%20discussing%20various%20attacks._x000D_
_x000D_
Understanding the Identity-Transformation Approach in OIDC-Compatible Privacy-Preserving SSO Services:_x000D_
https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.01325#:~:text=OpenID%20Connect%20(OIDC)%20enables%20a,variations%20of%20SSO%20security%20requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC²: Open Identity Certification with OpenID Connect_x000D_
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378896695_OIDC2_Open_Identity_Certification_With_OpenID_Connect'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b7d248e2-a611-4b0d-aae1-24e05852c283 .

camssa:3e39435c-bee7-46ce-8bff-c8393649005f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is a highly mature and globally recognised standard, recently formalised as ITU-T Recommendation X.1285. With multiple certified implementations and adoption by a high amount of users,since its the specification behind the "log in with" method. Its integration into the eIDAS 2.0 framework further confirms its suitability for building interoperable, high-assurance government ecosystems that are both future-proof and vendor-neutral._x000D_
_x000D_
ITU-T Recommendation X.1285 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-X.1285_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallets with OpenID for Verifiable Credentials (OpenID4VC):_x000D_
https://docs.igrant.io/concepts/openID4vc/_x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC Certified Implementations:_x000D_
https://openid.net/developers/certified-openid-connect-implementations/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:97b7cfef-5466-42d7-b62f-2bb247b8ca2e .

camssa:40be013a-632f-4df6-9552-baf721116552 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC specificacion provides a standarised way for digital authentication and identity verification, which organisations and service providers can use as a foundation to build their own access solutions. This specification can be applied across different sectors and use cases, without being tied to a specific business domain._x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC Adoption examples:_x000D_
https://openid.net/certification/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cb64f7cf-2dd4-4118-873e-17e5652ea102 .

