camssa:a0f1b539-5ce0-4d31-b04b-2ba0ca02f3dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC enables digital service delivery channels by providing a standardised and interoperable framework for secure authentication and identity verification. It allows users to access web portals, mobile applications, and digital wallets with a single, trusted identity, reducing friction and the need for multiple credentials. By supporting consent-based attribute sharing, extensible claims, and profiles such as OIDC4VC and OIDC4VP, OIDC facilitates seamless access to both national and cross-border public services, including eGovernment, healthcare, taxation, and social services._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC4VC Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/sg/openid4vc/_x000D_
_x000D_
OIDC4VP Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-presentations-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98e8056f-826c-4e80-b137-173d06d25ee1 .

camssa:a17d62de-8d9d-46aa-be63-ec6de660bddb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a3261e78-390a-49df-a102-c545678a07f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC simplifies the delivery of European public services by providing a secure user authentication and identity verification. It enables users to sign in to services such as cross‑border public administration platforms, eGovernment portals, and EU digital identity initiatives using trusted identity providers. For example, national digital identity schemes like itsme in Belgium (which supports government and citizen services), BankID in  Norway, Sweden, and Finland (used for eGovernment access and public services), and FranceConnect in France utilise OIDC‑based authentication models in alignment with eIDAS trust frameworks._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
itsme - Belgium service Reference:_x000D_
https://www.itsme-id.com/_x000D_
_x000D_
BankID from Norway, Sweden, and Finland service:_x000D_
https://www.bankid.com/_x000D_
_x000D_
FranceConnect - French Service:_x000D_
https://www.franceconnect.gouv.fr/_x000D_
_x000D_
The eKYC & IDA Working Group Welcomes the Proposal of the European Commission to Extend the Scope of eIDAS Trust Services - OpenID Fundation Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/the-ekyc-ida-working-group-welcomes-the-proposal-of-the-european-commission-to-extend-the-scope-of-eidas-trust-services/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a17d62de-8d9d-46aa-be63-ec6de660bddb .

camssa:a533f941-30ba-41cb-b0e6-d25b9f9b7616 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC specification focuses on secure authentication and identity management rather than enabling the e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6b20fe0-d996-469e-b399-5497e7e790de .

camssa:a603f9d4-6552-432b-b8a3-c6842db91f58 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC functions as an identity layer built on top of the OAuth 2.0 protocol, providing a standardised framework for verifying end-user identity and obtaining profile information. The specification exposes web-based interfaces, specifically the Authorization, Token, and UserInfo endpoints, which allow systems to handle identity and profile data consistently and securely._x000D_
_x000D_
In practice, OIDC is the protocol behind  “Log in with …” buttons on websites and applications. When a user chooses to log in with an external provider, OIDC manages the authentication process, allowing the service to redirect the user to a trusted identity provider, authenticate them, and then receive a secure confirmation of the user’s identity. This ensures interoperability between systems, enabling internal identity services to be reused across multiple applications while maintaining security and trust._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth 2.0 specification reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0819bfac-f8fe-46a8-a5a8-f4d34f5faaaa .

camssa:a696c81d-b902-463f-b47f-e0a45e64ae17 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a77d17a2-b005-487c-be90-2531d9c5d7ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC enables real time authentication, ensuring the user’s identity information is accurate at the time of login. OIDC retrieves identity data directly from a trusted identity provider, reducing the risk of using outdated or incorrect user information during authentication._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:557f63e1-8b62-43c8-ab20-5a7aef4487a2 .

camssa:a85cb9f0-dd69-476a-b38a-d0cadd3eefe3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC does not enable the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services as it instead focuses on providing a standard way to authenticate users and send identity information securely between parties. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f13c70c8-345a-4e1b-b524-628694d57429 .

camssa:a87c2602-2571-4552-891c-ae584c0b1865 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:aac8500f-b0f6-4bf7-b046-afe98bda0291 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC does not enable the long-term preservation of data/information/knowledge. Therefore, this criterion is considered not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:833696da-4f35-4c8c-8535-78cf43123f62 .

camssa:b65c3ebf-370e-4054-80d7-67a0ff95066b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of OIDC is not related to the publication of data on the web as it main purpose is the user authentication and identity management._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#Authentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1e69fe29-2044-4e9c-89fc-d16e07ab9c8c .

camssa:b6ff974c-fc04-42d1-9b16-85408de205da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC uses JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) with digital signatures, enabling receiving applications to verify both the integrity of the data and its origin from a trusted identity provider. In addition, OIDC requires the use of HTTPS to protect data from interception or modification during transit. Together, these mechanisms ensure that identity and credential data are exchanged securely, maintaining confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity throughout authentication and authorisation processes._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification  ID Token Validation reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#IDTokenValidation'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53251250-3736-4c16-bf26-8d8e85e62cd9 .

camssa:b7d248e2-a611-4b0d-aae1-24e05852c283 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b8b8ee14-094a-417b-b291-dca7b5e7a2fe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bb455012-1065-4149-b45d-690102a02832 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC defines a core set of mandatory and optional components while allowing additional functionality to be introduced through profiles, extensions, and optional parameters, without compromising the interoperability of the core specification. Its use of JSON-based structures, extensible token claims, scopes, endpoints, and metadata enables implementers and standards bodies to introduce new capabilities in a controlled and backwards-compatible manner._x000D_
_x000D_
This extensibility is demonstrated by several standardised profiles and extensions built on top of OIDC Core, including Identity Assurance, eKYC, and OpenID for Verifiable Credentials (OIDC4VC and OIDC4VP). These profiles leverage existing OIDC and OAuth 2.0 mechanisms while defining additional requirements, data models, and processing rules tailored to specific use cases. By doing so, they enable advanced identity scenarios, such as verifiable credentials and digital wallets, while preserving standards compliance, interoperability, and security._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
eKYC & IDA Working Group reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/ekyc-ida/_x000D_
_x000D_
IETF SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-oauth-selective-disclosure-jwt/22/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:06f8f79b-62ff-460e-9a36-72619bc9dc87 .

camssa:bc5cd6b3-24aa-44cf-b5c0-f483ccadada5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:befbaaff-f7aa-4cf8-8b84-49a4750744ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC ensures that identity data is transmitted securely during authentication by leveraging HTTPS for encrypted communication and signed tokens, such as JWTs, to guarantee integrity and authenticity. This allows applications to verify that the received data originates from a trusted identity provider, reducing the risk of impersonation or tampering. However, it does not regulate how applications handle or store user data after it has been received. Implementers are therefore responsible for applying additional privacy and security measures, such as secure storage, access restrictions, and compliance with data protection regulations, to safeguard user information throughout its lifecycle._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification Security reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#ClientAuthentication'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48619dc0-d7da-4db2-8c9f-339df643aafe .

camssa:c456f224-fca1-44b5-bd98-bbdf74fc22fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is included in European and national digital identity initiatives that cover privacy aspects, such as eSSIF-Lab (European Self-Sovereign Identity Framework Lab) or eIDAS projects, due to its support for secure, consent-based identity data sharing._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation welcomes eIDAS trust services expansion:_x000D_
https://openid.net/the-ekyc-ida-working-group-welcomes-the-proposal-of-the-european-commission-to-extend-the-scope-of-eidas-trust-services_x000D_
_x000D_
European Self-Sovereign Identity Framework Lab:_x000D_
https://essif-lab.github.io/framework/docs/essifLab-vision_x000D_
_x000D_
European Self-Sovereign Identity Framework Lab Standards used:_x000D_
https://tno-ssi-lab.github.io/standardisation-overview/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification Privacy reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#Privacy'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:63de7d5b-2bad-421d-a8b8-2f3f3da125db .

camssa:c6b20fe0-d996-469e-b399-5497e7e790de a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c71315f9-022c-435f-9a9d-204ed36ceb94 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is included in an italian repository that provides the specific technical consolidation, in accordance with National Guidelines, to improve the prospects of integration with the SPID and CIE id OIDC Federations for public and private Service Providers (RP), Identity Providers (OP), and Aggregators (SA)._x000D_
_x000D_
SPID/CIE OpenID Connect -  AgID + Team per la Trasformazione Digitale Reference:_x000D_
https://docs.italia.it/italia/spid/spid-cie-oidc-docs/it/versione-corrente/index.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6945a80f-583c-43f7-8788-4f2964f6c34d .

camssa:c77fa3f8-35a8-4aa4-a7bb-96b1d73a9153 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cb37a3ab-1ed5-4056-98f8-0ec6cbcaa43a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cb64f7cf-2dd4-4118-873e-17e5652ea102 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d1571c6c-3e32-41d0-b3a7-9c627a012fd2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e30ba8ea-380d-4fcd-960d-03470b60bde9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC does not include administrative procedures, rules, or service management as it instead focuses on providing a standard way to authenticate users and convey identity information securely between parties. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b8b8ee14-094a-417b-b291-dca7b5e7a2fe .

camssa:e3f37581-34ef-4d23-9a64-a42129750f09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC specification can be found in the OpenID Foundation Github where its development and maintenance can actively encourage and sustain open communities, discussions, and collaborative improvement of the specification and its implementations._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Github Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/openid'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8c177602-56bf-4fdd-b788-2b65f3cd06f2 .

camssa:e5061c9b-f4c9-43f4-be08-da6d4cf0e3e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC allows the customisation of claims, scopes and user flows to align with specific service requirements while maintaining compliance with the core protocol specifications. Through the controlled definition of customised scope values and claims structures, issuers can precisely indicate the type and semantic context of the credential being requested or issued. OIDC can support verifiable credential use cases and wallet-based authentication flows without compromising interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
This customisation enables selective disclosure mechanisms, allowing users to share only the specific attributes necessary for a given transaction. This approach reinforces privacy-by-design principles and ensures strict adherence to the principle of data minimisation, as required under European data protection frameworks._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#Claims'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4968e0d6-fea6-4710-b3e7-e0e83af9e716 .

camssa:e9e99faf-9047-4f18-bb82-46696d86a881 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is used in European cross-border initiatives and projects, including eIDAS 2.0 pilots and the European Digital Identity Wallet (EUDI Wallet) architecture, where it is utilised for secure authentication and authorisation. Its adoption in these initiatives is due to its maturity, interoperability, and alignment with web standards, making it suitable for cross-border identity federation and authentication scenarios._x000D_
_x000D_
EU Digital Identity Wallet Pilot implementation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eudi-wallet-implementation_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS 2.0 Roadmap:_x000D_
https://utimaco.com/news/blog-posts/eidas-20-roadmap-toolbox-and-european-digital-identity-wallet-architecture'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:43231c85-9f5f-4165-9dd1-cd8aa96f560d .

camssa:ec362bff-0049-4e7e-a160-216b33a85322 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is maintained by the OpenID Foundation (OIDF), an international non-profit standards organisation. The specification is developed and updated by the AB/Connect Working Group. The AB/Connect working group is a combined working group of the Artifact Binding (AB) Working Group and the Connect Working Group aimed at producing the OAuth 2.0 based “OpenID Connect” specifications. It also includes a project named OpenID for Verifiable Credentials which consists of three specifications. _x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID AB/Connect Working Group:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/connect/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Working Groups:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Mailing Lists:_x000D_
https://openid.net/community/mailing-lists/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7af9f340-3385-4f51-803a-738b7d90e29c .

camssa:f13c70c8-345a-4e1b-b524-628694d57429 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f3b8693f-0d96-4fb5-9b06-8b49ad99e13c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f5a7411c-3e0b-4054-9e34-71cd5cef19b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The development of the OIDC specification ensures broad technical input while maintaining a sustainable governance structure. At the technical level,  allows the participation of any stakeholder, including individual developers, private companies, and public administrations, to join working groups and contribute to the drafting of specifications without requiring a paid membership. Contributors only need to sign a Contribution Agreement. All working groups operate openly with decisions on specifications being consensus-led._x000D_
_x000D_
Formal influence and organizational governance, however, are managed through a tiered membership structure. While technical contribution is free, becoming a "Member" involves annual dues, which are scaled to be accessible for different entities (e.g., $250/year for governments and non-profits). This membership grants formal voting rights on the final approval of specifications and the election of the Board of Directors. This balanced approach ensures that while the technical evolution of OIDC is driven by a global community of experts, its long-term sustainability and strategic direction are overseen by a formal, representative body of invested stakeholders._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Working Groups:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation OIDC Working Group:_x000D_
https://openid.net/wg/connect/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation bylaws reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/oidf-updates-bylaws/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Membership reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/foundation/benefits-members/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Foundation Intellectual Property & Contribution Agreements:_x000D_
https://openid.net/intellectual-property/openid-foundation-contribution-agreements/_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6eb91dac-9834-44da-9a1f-8df43e72c115 .

camssa:f7961515-6cf2-41ab-8ea0-f3fd8fc90c97 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is a technology-agnostic specification, built on open standards such as HTTP, JSON, and OAuth 2.0. It enables interoperable authentication across a wide range of operating systems, devices, and programming environments. The specification defines a protocol for authentication and identity without imposing requirements on specific technologies, frameworks, or programming languages, allowing flexibility in implementation while ensuring consistency and compatibility._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d1571c6c-3e32-41d0-b3a7-9c627a012fd2 .

camssa:f93a4afc-dbef-46e6-9a90-8172d0051038 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is included in the French national catalogue of recommended specifications. The National Interoperability Framework of France is aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO) factsheets._x000D_
_x000D_
NIFO Factsheets France:_x000D_
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/NIFO_2024%20DPAF_France_vFinal_rev.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS list of standards:_x000D_
https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b2b0b93-4065-4f28-8e1f-59ff6221bb21 .

camssa:f99effff-7fb2-4c3c-b240-ce568ce25959 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:fae1c39d-571f-4a5c-af87-6a4146ea3cf0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC is not a European standard. It was developed by OpenID Foundation, a global non-profit organisation, and is based in the United States and supported by a worldwide community, including major industry stakeholders (e.g., Google, Microsoft, and others). However, OIDC has been adopted in Europe for authentication and identity federation, and is referenced in European cross-border initiatives (e.g., eIDAS 2.0, EUDI Wallet...) due to its interoperability and maturity._x000D_
_x000D_
EU Digital Identity Wallet Pilot implementation:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eudi-wallet-implementation_x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS 2.0 Roadmap:_x000D_
https://utimaco.com/news/blog-posts/eidas-20-roadmap-toolbox-and-european-digital-identity-wallet-architecture_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f99effff-7fb2-4c3c-b240-ce568ce25959 .

camssa:fe2a493e-4908-4cbe-9932-477baf14dfe1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'OIDC can be effectively used in a multilingual context. Authorization requests and error messages can include language preferences, enabling relying parties and identity providers to present interfaces and content in the user’s preferred language_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID Connect specification reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:08f60f28-c963-422c-bc1d-81aa106df3e9 .

