camssa:017c4201-5685-428b-9db6-29f0a9c3922b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT standard is not related with the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable for the standard._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a94fe47-a0a5-4c75-9a46-cca7d919238a .

camssa:02336f4c-b281-48e4-9667-eb2f22d3084c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:04de2a6e-5cbd-4641-8ead-356e89c65f00 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:06e1cfe4-ed29-4ab6-a953-61f9237d33da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT can carry information about a user, like their identity, roles, and permissions, which helps a system decide if they can access certain resources. When someone logs in, the system gives them a token with this information, and the token can be reused for Single Sign-On (SSO), so the user can access multiple apps or services without logging in again. _x000D_
_x000D_
JWT also has built-in claims to make it more secure: the audience (aud) claim makes sure only the right recipient can use the token; time-based claims (exp, nbf) limit when the token is valid; the issuer (iss) claim checks the token comes from a trusted source; and the JWT ID (jti) prevents the token from being used more than once. These features let JWT support access control methods like role-based (RBAC) and attribute-based (ABAC), giving a simple and secure way to handle who can do what across different apps and services. _x000D_
_x000D_
In addition, the JOSE framework allows JWTs to be encrypted through JWE, helping protect the confidentiality of the information carried inside the token._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:db30b117-4374-4e38-b28c-d24ddf71b236 .

camssa:0925b78b-ce25-4782-b24f-25cbe38c07dc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is discussed across both specialised forums and general developer platforms such as Stack Overflow. The big amount of questions about implementation, security discussions, and best-practice exchanges demonstrates active adoption and continuous community participation._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack Overflow JWT Questions Reference:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/jwt?tab=Newest'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bfa215e5-63a1-440d-ab14-accf77a7f222 .

camssa:0f2d3099-0921-4c92-8c1c-08b707cf108b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0fd8cc09-5c84-4404-9ca4-0d94c00a429f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is not related to comprehensively scope administrative procedures, rules, data, or services.The specification is focused on defining a compact token format for securely transmitting claims between parties. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2b93d063-3a10-44df-a338-02a7e17cf3df .

camssa:19d1a4c6-ed54-4195-8fd8-ab123bfd3c5b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'1 Member State is recommending JWT in its ICT National Catalogue. This Member State is Italy._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Italy Reference:_x000D_
https://www.agid.gov.it/sites/default/files/repository_files/linee_guida_interoperabilit_tecnica_pa.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57c045d4-4618-47a7-a851-81d32041a043 .

camssa:1bf193ad-dfbb-475c-8636-17eb6c2c5a2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is maintained by IETF which is an international organisation based in Fremont, California. More specifically, the standard is developed by the OAuth working group._x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth Working Group Reference:_x000D_
https://oauth.net/specs/_x000D_
_x000D_
IETF Reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/about/introduction/_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7135cb0-e3c2-4cd0-8c1c-8f4aeeba5b2d .

camssa:1d91c5d7-57af-44dc-92af-dd0fe5701e7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT enables digital service delivery channels by allowing claims and credentials to be transmitted securely in a digital form. Signed claims allow services to verify users and their permissions without maintaining server-side session state, supporting scenarios like SSO, APIs, and distributed digital services._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c574a09-6c64-40dc-815c-c0f20194b231 .

camssa:1ff97d48-67e0-4dea-a3d4-cce4a18d32ec a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:271e4bd6-ace2-46c6-aad0-9b73f50ff51d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is technology agnostic, it is defined as an open standard and is based on JSON, which is widely supported across programming languages and platforms. Any system capable of processing JSON and implementing the required cryptographic algorithms can issue or validate JWTs._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d7371a3-a003-49f1-aa61-47bf011c7204 .

camssa:2aae0d7d-6ddf-4bc7-a812-c57e758fda53 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2ac59b87-fa43-4f22-9881-ae6e442b25a9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is part of the JOSE framework and can be extended through signing, encryption, or custom claims. Its main extensions include JWS for ensuring integrity, JWE for confidentiality, JWA for specifying algorithms, and JWK for representing keys. These extensions make JWT a flexible and secure format that can be adapted to many different identity, authentication, and data exchange scenarios._x000D_
_x000D_
In addition, JWT can be extended through registered public claims maintained by IANA and through application-specific profiles, such as OpenID Connect ID Tokens and OAuth 2.0 access tokens, which define additional constraints and claim requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
IANA Reference:_x000D_
https://www.iana.org/assignments/jwt/jwt.xhtml_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Object Signing and Encryption(JOSE) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/jose/about/_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Signature (JWS) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7515_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Encryption (JWE) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7516_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Algorithms (JWA)_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7518_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Key (JWK) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7517_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e165e43b-5ba5-4536-aa17-4e467469952d .

camssa:2b93d063-3a10-44df-a338-02a7e17cf3df a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2bae6434-97b9-4835-acd2-697742f24c4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is language-neutral because it uses JSON to structure its data, meaning the format itself does not depend on any particular language or character set. Claims within a JWT can carry text in any language, allowing systems to transmit multilingual information such as names, addresses, or messages. A European public service could issue a JWT containing a claim for a user’s preferred language (e.g. "preferred_language": "fr"). The consuming application can read this claim and display the interface or messages in French._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Prefered Language Reference:_x000D_
https://openbao.org/api-docs/auth/jwt/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2eaf6ac2-6a79-43fc-b5b2-b8380f2eb53d .

camssa:2e1c88b1-0ec3-4ebd-8204-a09e43797818 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2eaf6ac2-6a79-43fc-b5b2-b8380f2eb53d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2f6a5791-0499-4919-94ab-a3c23d63e92c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:30161419-b624-475e-82bf-2ba8fceb0c5e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT standard is not related to the e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2aae0d7d-6ddf-4bc7-a812-c57e758fda53 .

camssa:306f85aa-cdae-4d0b-a66b-a5f04ac1d443 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:36531842-90bf-49cc-8331-850ada2d1b1f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT can be found in both relevant European regulations and European projects. In the case of relevant regulations, it can be found in the “Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/848 of 6 May 2025 laying down rules for the application of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards the registration of wallet-relying parties” . In this regulation, the JWT specification is adopted as the data exchange format, and the relying party registration certificate shall be represented as a signed JSON Web Token (JWT).  _x000D_
_x000D_
JWT also plays a key role in the implementation of the Mobile Driver’s Licence (mDL), where it is covered by ISO/IEC 18013-5:2021. In this context, it provides encryption mechanisms, including the use of signatures, to ensure the integrity and accuracy of the mDL. _x000D_
_x000D_
Mobile Driver’s Licence (mDL):_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/EUDIGITALIDENTITYWALLET/pages/929202846/The+Mobile+Driving+License+manual_x000D_
_x000D_
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/848 of 6 May 2025 laying down rules for the application of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards the registration of wallet-relying parties” reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32025R0848&qid=1766142281877  _x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0209b8b-45b5-4ad2-b9e5-e742518d124c .

