camssa:492d6001-b6e4-4b85-80d6-fdae8dc01936 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT conformance can be effectively assessed through publicly available test tools, such as the JSON Web Token (JWT) Debugger and Token Debugger from token.io. There test tools allow developers to validate tokens._x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Token (JWT) Debugger:_x000D_
https://www.jwt.io/_x000D_
_x000D_
Token Debugger:_x000D_
https://token.dev/jwt/_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e4688d8-3fc7-41d5-a509-ab1cb868a233 .

camssa:4ba83b8a-25d4-4b88-8c0b-033b0ae8450e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT allows customisation by the use of additional signing and encryption algorithms as defined in the related standards (JWS and JWE). Therefore, an implementation may choose algorithms according to its security requirements (e.g. ECDSA-based algorithms), provided they are compliant with the relevant RFCs._x000D_
_x000D_
However, proprietary algorithms can be used without constraint, to fit the application or service needs according to the organisations authentication and authorisation rules. The algorithm must be properly identified in the JWT header and must follow the rules defined by the JSON Web Algorithms (JWA) specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWE Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7516.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Best practices Algorithms reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8725#name-use-appropriate-algorithms_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab3b3484-6e5f-4046-ba53-524a73c390ac .

camssa:4e4688d8-3fc7-41d5-a509-ab1cb868a233 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:52088704-fef2-41d6-b428-fa30510bed55 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is included in 1 national catalogue of recommended specifications, which is Italy. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Italy is aligned with at least 3 out of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory factsheets._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
National Catalogue of Italy Reference:_x000D_
https://www.agid.gov.it/sites/default/files/repository_files/linee_guida_interoperabilit_tecnica_pa.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Italy Digital Public Administration Factsheet 2025:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/custom-page/attachment/2025-11/iopeu-monitoring_2025-dpaf_italy_vfinal.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f15f683e-be61-40db-ac0a-42aff90f16dc .

camssa:54e38134-e5ab-4caf-b7ec-e3246105cf06 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:56509729-970b-4cd4-83c8-f5f06b0b91f7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT can simplify the delivery of European public services by securely transmitting claims in a compact, URL-safe format between systems. This allows users to access multiple services without re-entering credentials and enables services to trust and reuse authentication information._x000D_
_x000D_
For example, a user that logs in via EU Login can access different EU services using the same token, which confirms their information securely._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1ff97d48-67e0-4dea-a3d4-cce4a18d32ec .

camssa:56872ad2-37d3-47f4-8aca-76c6c842e4b8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of JWT is not related to facilitating the publication of data on the web, as it is designed to securely transmit information between parties. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this standard._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04de2a6e-5cbd-4641-8ead-356e89c65f00 .

camssa:57c045d4-4618-47a7-a851-81d32041a043 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5a5fcb6c-14f4-413d-b80d-e2ce521bea8c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Together with JWS(digital signatures) and JWE(encryption), JWT allows applications to verify the integrity and authenticity of the data before processing it. This ensures that only trusted and untampered information is used in business logic, authorisation decisions, or service workflows._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Signature (JWS) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7515_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Encryption (JWE) Reference:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7516'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e5887e2-a692-4014-99f1-f9d339682217 .

camssa:5c574a09-6c64-40dc-815c-c0f20194b231 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5d7371a3-a003-49f1-aa61-47bf011c7204 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6432b033-3845-4373-a6a8-8f6230b5ea61 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is platform agnostic, it is defined as an open standard and is based on JSON, which is widely supported across programming languages and platforms. Any system capable of processing JSON and implementing the required cryptographic algorithms can issue or validate JWTs._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ac0afca6-d7f9-4586-8a88-e6e360274204 .

camssa:6990308f-3afd-4daf-8390-5465b012570c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6ef54108-f621-41a1-ac18-d34d43a74255 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"JWT only supports secure interaction with an existing interface, mainly for authentication and authorisation purposes. It is not related to enable the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f6a5791-0499-4919-94ab-a3c23d63e92c .

camssa:700a8997-8344-412a-bd8f-60086039a707 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:70f335be-1668-4b98-8d42-9df6a104eaf4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:72a1aab8-573c-4938-8b64-f2934df25e43 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT supports integrity and authenticity through digital signatures (JWS), ensuring that the data has not been altered and that the issuer can be verified. It also supports confidentiality when used with encryption (JWE), protecting the content from unauthorised disclosure during transmission._x000D_
_x000D_
In addition, JWT is designed to be compact and standardised, which facilitates secure token exchange across diverse systems and platforms._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3efed769-dc04-494e-892d-ba41f33097e4 .

camssa:7a997d81-2a7e-4b07-b26f-0fc41595c1e8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ee29589b-041c-4de1-84b2-663be1f645a3 .

camssa:847bdf20-a648-4842-bc04-1fe5a559ad6e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is domain-agnostic. It defines a technical mechanism for representing and securely transmitting claims, without sector-specific ties. The structure (header, payload, signature) is generic and does not impose business constraints. JWT can be used in any context where authentication and authorisation is needed._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:700a8997-8344-412a-bd8f-60086039a707 .

camssa:87e5110a-0893-4e02-9107-5d3ee9ecff53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT allows relevant information to be reused primarily in authentication and authorisation scenarios. When a user authenticates through a login page, the system issues a token containing identity-related claims, such as the user ID or email address. This token can then be used for Single Sign-On (SSO), allowing the user to access multiple websites or services without having to re-enter their credentials for each one. In this way, applications can rely on the existing authentication token and provide a smoother, more secure user experience._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e8a2105d-7039-4da0-bb0a-7cf7d2f4324b .

camssa:89086190-abab-4466-a143-e334791e6ba8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:900f5405-a613-45c7-9d8b-e9b4fe35c3d5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT can enable data portability between systems/applications supporting the implementation or evolution of European public services by providing a secure authentication and authorisation of data between systems and applications._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0077493b-c7c3-4014-8834-550cf45c8af6 .

camssa:915640e4-4aba-41c2-b4e7-d04668d85801 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is recognised by ENISA as an open standard for secure digital communication and is referenced in both European regulations and initiatives. In particular, the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/848 of 6 May 2025, which implements Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 for the registration of wallet-relying parties, specifies JWT as the required format for data exchange. According to this regulation, relying party registration certificates must be represented as signed JSON Web Tokens._x000D_
_x000D_
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/848 of 6 May 2025 laying down rules for the application of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards the registration of wallet-relying parties:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2025/848/oj/eng_x000D_
_x000D_
ENISA Security by Design and Default Playbook Reference:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2026-03/ENISA_Secure_By_Design_and_Default_Playbook_v0.4_draft_for_consultation.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9e1da65b-d3ca-4d3a-8e8d-e9118b1a6a1b .

camssa:96809464-6d7d-441c-8ce1-799de484a1f9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02336f4c-b281-48e4-9667-eb2f22d3084c .

camssa:9a94fe47-a0a5-4c75-9a46-cca7d919238a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9e1da65b-d3ca-4d3a-8e8d-e9118b1a6a1b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9eb5746a-8a73-401b-8eba-0f9d3182401d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT supports access control by carrying claims that describe the user’s roles, permissions, or attributes. For example, a token could indicate whether the user is an admin, a regular user, or has specific privileges. The application can then enforce access rules based on these claims. JWT itself does not define the roles or policies; it only provides a standard way to transmit the information that applications use to make access decisions._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f2d3099-0921-4c92-8c1c-08b707cf108b .

camssa:a0052141-1ae6-4db7-9f34-1e020eb5fc8a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT ensures that the data being processed is exactly what the trusted issuer sent and has not been altered, supporting reliable processing. However, it does not verify the real-world correctness of the data itself. As an example, when a user logs into a public service, the token contains claims such as the user ID or email. The service can trust that these claims so it can safely use the information to personalise the session or make authorisation decisions._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3e6de0e9-b184-4192-a3d9-7ad7556c4993 .

camssa:ab3b3484-6e5f-4046-ba53-524a73c390ac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:abf0c313-4819-4d3d-8cef-2c703bd75421 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT provides a secure and standardised mechanism for transmitting authentication and authorisation information, supporting organisational interoperability agreements. It is particularly suitable in environments that require both authentication and delegated authorisation._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c14fc1a0-5f83-48b1-a0b1-a45da160b410 .

camssa:ac0afca6-d7f9-4586-8a88-e6e360274204 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ada16e01-5d2b-4f9d-8e4b-a8ac5ab26fa0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT supports the simplification of business processes by enabling secure authentication and identity verification. It allows users to access digital services, such as cross-border public administration platforms, eGovernment portals, and EU digital identity initiatives._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:af3dccb2-9621-4582-8a7d-357da9cc8920 .

camssa:ae383fb0-3d1e-4aef-8811-bdf470d37114 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:af3dccb2-9621-4582-8a7d-357da9cc8920 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b7156119-60eb-47d0-823c-7cf4a529af0a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is not related to enabling the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Therefore, the criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c8540a9a-6ddc-4e87-8c2e-eb086f13f737 .

camssa:b85b37c7-a5ce-4d5c-8623-9dfe2129aa53 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the JWT specification has been assed by A. F. Nugraha, H. Kabetta, I. K. S. Buana and R. B. Hadiprakoso. In the "Performance and Security Comparison of Json Web Tokens (JWT) and Platform Agnostic Security Tokens (PASETO) on RESTful APIs" study. Performance tests show that JWT performs better than other token formats, such as PASETO. This advantage comes from its compact size, lightweight JSON encoding, and flexible support for efficient cryptographic algorithms within the JOSE framework, like HS256, RS256, and ES256._x000D_
_x000D_
"Performance and Security Comparison of Json Web Tokens (JWT) and Platform Agnostic Security Tokens (PASETO) on RESTful APIs" study:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10277377_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4018ab9c-e55b-47ab-be27-58c1684ff1bb .

camssa:ba60f100-810a-497b-a540-ff2b894a8393 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT allows partial implementations. An application that uses JWT for authentication and authorisation can implement a simplified version that handles only basic signed tokens and a limited set of claims, while omitting more complex or advanced requirements._x000D_
_x000D_
To be considered a conformant JWT implementation, a system is only required to support a small core set of features. Implementations must support the mandatory algorithms specified by the standard to ensure consistent and interoperable operation._x000D_
_x000D_
Implementation requirements Refrence:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7519#section-8_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ae383fb0-3d1e-4aef-8811-bdf470d37114 .

camssa:bfa0cb7e-af8a-4898-ba85-ddd08c4308e4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JSON Web Token (JWT), developed by the IETF and part of the JOSE family, was first drafted in 2012 and approved as RFC 7519 in 2015. JWT is a token format for carrying claims, secured via JWS (signing) and JWE (encryption)._x000D_
_x000D_
It is used for digital identity, authentication, authorisation, and secure data exchange, including in the European Digital Identity Wallet. Recent updates add stronger security checks, clearer separation of signed and encrypted tokens, and selective disclosure (SD-JWT) for privacy, making it more suitable for digital wallets and verifiable credentials._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/#architecture-and-reference-framework _x000D_
_x000D_
Github EU Digital Identity Wallet Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-doc-architecture-and-reference-framework/blob/main/docs/architecture-and-reference-framework-main.md'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e358eb43-24f8-4b86-bf9b-2d17c1ae0561 .

