camssa:e8a69da3-f9fc-4c3e-bbe0-9e19f68d342c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWTs are signed, compact tokens that let systems transmit identity and authorisation information securely without keeping session data on the server. They support stateless authorisation models like role-based (RBAC) and attribute-based (ABAC) access control. JWTs also provide strong protection against tampering: tokens signed with JWS let systems detect any changes to the data during transmission, ensuring that the information received is exactly the same as when it was issued._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3ef0a307-a926-4483-b58f-149475c1f2b6 .

camssa:e98b3534-d60f-4d9d-b879-20cc4494bc6b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT guarantees authenticity and identity verification to a significant extent through digital signatures, allowing systems to confirm the issuer and validity of claims._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe90e5e7-7659-4f67-8ca7-bafaaa1f99df .

