camssa:f8f0c58a-4549-4196-9590-14c4bfb6eb2c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the JWT standard has been assed by the International Journal of Recent Technology and Engineering (IJRTE). In the "Insights of JSON Web Token" study, the JWT has been shown to be effective for secure, interoperable, and compact token-based data exchange, particularly in authentication and authorisation scenarios. In addition, JWT ensures data integrity and authenticity when implemented with strong algorithms._x000D_
_x000D_
"Insights of JSON Web Token, 2020, International Journal of Recent Technology and Engineering (IJRTE)" study:_x000D_
https://www.academia.edu/100350122/Insights_of_JSON_Web_Token_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Standard Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:306f85aa-cdae-4d0b-a66b-a5f04ac1d443 .

camssa:f9e75d85-6988-47c4-b069-337044e04711 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWT is a token format used to carry claims between parties, secured through signing (JWS) and encryption (JWE). Its main purpose is to enable secure, interoperable, and verifiable data exchange, making it a dominant standard for identity and authentication. Popular implementations include platforms such as Keycloak and frameworks like the European Digital Identity (EUDI) Wallet._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT plays a key role in both European regulations and projects. For example, the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/848 specifies that relying party registration certificates must be represented as signed JWTs, establishing JWT as the official format for this data exchange._x000D_
_x000D_
In European projects, JWT is referenced in the EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF), where it is identified as a fit-for-purpose standard with no functional or technical gaps. Its adoption adds value by enabling interoperable, secure, and privacy-respecting identity solutions across different platforms and borders._x000D_
_x000D_
Eur-lex Registration of relying parties of European Digital Identity Wallets Reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32025R0848_x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/#architecture-and-reference-framework _x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Specification Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d488bea3-99ae-438a-9e7d-da73a60d0dea .

