camssa:00e6755c-82df-456c-a58a-ca2780fbf0f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Despite its relatively recent introduction and rapid standardisation, SD-JWT has already been adopted in European initiatives such as the European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI) and frameworks, such as IOTA Foundation, a Berlin-based open-source organisation developing technologies to support scalable and practical digital trust._x000D_
_x000D_
Additionally, it can be found in relevant European projects such as the EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF). SD-JWT is proposed as a technical specification relevant to both the “Attestation and PID Providers”  and “Protocols and Interoperability”  sections of the EUDI Wallet framework._x000D_
_x000D_
EBSI Hub Reference:_x000D_
https://hub.ebsi.eu/vc-framework/did/selective-disclosure-sd-jwt _x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT in EUDI Wallet reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.6.0/technical-specifications/_x000D_
_x000D_
IOTA Refence:_x000D_
https://docs.iota.org/developer/iota-identity/how-tos/verifiable-credentials/selective-disclosure#:~:text=The%20issuer%20makes%20the%20values%20of%20%22locality%22,,the%20address%20to%20be%20disclosed%20and%20presented._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04e798d2-036a-43e1-92b8-7c242f50e138 .

camssa:04e798d2-036a-43e1-92b8-7c242f50e138 a cav:Score,
