        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26aeec3cf5b3b4879325e85fcd751d0c17f62c6c3113109fb100883a553ec0af ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:09a4ff04-249e-4c3a-b96b-11eb256e2567 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT specification can enable the secure exchange of data between parties, ensuring that unnecessary data is not shared during specific procedures. Instead, the user can select which property is revealed, thereby avoiding the sharing of other personal data._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a2122e82-7f29-44b3-b9d9-6a6051eaddfe .

camssa:0b4b0282-976e-4b58-af4c-6e06e64408d4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b00b9b74de866ed2278d14d1b9d7ecf2c06950d296bb2f17013c7b710d6de41 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0c86413e-f9dd-47eb-bfc3-f27d9f1429b0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0f2aa3df-7c9c-4d64-9383-b37912c02730 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SD-JWT specification is not related to enable e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22a906aa-56f6-4aef-b74f-f5f20b0f5535 .

camssa:12aca6fc-b6f1-487e-a238-96fdd2b8dfe6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT supports the simplification of business processes by allowing a sender to selectively disclose claims of a signed JWT instead of sharing all data with every recipient._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7fe53706-709b-458b-8e51-d6ca3bfa7544 .

camssa:145fc25d-9df6-4c65-b8c3-03399df133f8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The specification first appeared as draft in June 2022 and, since November 2025, has been published as an RFC at Proposed Standard level. The available documentation provides clear details on all modifications introduced across the different released drafts._x000D_
_x000D_
Additionally, organisations have already begun adopting this standard. SD-JWT is an open specificacion utilised on multiple European projects and initiatives, such as European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI) meaning its sufficiently mature for its use in the development of digital solutions/services._x000D_
_x000D_
European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI) - SD-JWT reference:_x000D_
https://hub.ebsi.eu/arch-req/standards_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6607be79-b374-4cb0-a3b5-816b4fc8c67d .

camssa:1bc8ac58-be6a-420b-99a6-232d51e408c3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1beca20e-6d05-41b1-80fd-bb64fe40468b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1ceca10e-6486-4dee-a7cb-1167826e5348 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is domain-agnostic, as it is primarily focused on the secure and selective disclosure of claims between parties. It ensures integrity through digital signatures and enables selective disclosure without invalidating the original signature, while confidentiality can be achieved when combined with encryption mechanisms. This mechanisms can be applied in different domains, such as business, or health._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1beca20e-6d05-41b1-80fd-bb64fe40468b .

camssa:22a906aa-56f6-4aef-b74f-f5f20b0f5535 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:277b4bba-cfe8-4107-9878-38d5a3b2f3ec a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is maintained by IETF which is an international organisation based in Fremont, California. More specifically, the standard is developed by the OAuth working group._x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth Working Group Reference:_x000D_
https://oauth.net/specs/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b94277b-3af0-406c-acfe-3938539f460b .

camssa:2decb813-55a7-4941-94d4-21b3272d5cd0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT relies on the JOSE framework, using the same header structure and processing rules as JWT. It adds selective disclosure, which lets users share only the claims they need from a signed credential. This way, personal data can be kept private while still allowing verification, reducing unnecessary exposure of information._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a97fb5cf-8cb6-4bf0-a646-c4e104ee32b9 .

camssa:32256a4d-b985-4947-bacb-0e2bbadfc84f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, SD-JWT can define the interoperability aspects of the "Access Management Application Component" and "Access Management Application Service" ABBs of the EIRA Technical View._x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT standard:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f8e4014a-1aad-4df3-a562-310650e4c5c7 .

camssa:32f0594a-f25c-4357-b45b-23b67dfe798c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:357553e2-ac04-4ac5-8dab-7ffdba00ff3e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating and Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:
- Technical excellence;
- prior implementation and testing;
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;
- openness and fairness; and
- timeliness.
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4f535a5c-26f2-4585-8586-5f8fc5dc5e08 .

camssa:35c59517-c08e-4d6e-b515-4c28ca1ad627 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:37a54ceb-5c3b-4761-92d3-d055af83e1b8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3f6fa831-16e7-4421-b5e0-a8b4196ae7de a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:483ed482-e39f-4abd-8b06-b377a836cb0c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is not related to scope administrative procedures, rules, data, or services. The specification enables the selective disclosure of claims from a digitally signed credential, allowing the holders to reveal only specific information while keeping other claims private. _x000D_
_x000D_
However, the ongoing work from IETF on SD-JWT VC could indirectly support the visibility of procedures, as it introduces a standard way to represent and present digital credentials related to qualifications, permits, or other official attributes._x000D_
_x000D_
Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
IETF SD-JWT VC Reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-oauth-sd-jwt-vc-15.html_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4c1c9ee7-b596-44ae-8079-74ba3fdb8a97 .

camssa:48c6fed8-7732-425b-8064-540c88fce0b2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4c1c9ee7-b596-44ae-8079-74ba3fdb8a97 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4c5746c5-ff62-4379-b036-6aea1d8cc621 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT uses JSON to structure claims, which is inherently language-neutral and can carry text in any language or character set._x000D_
_x000D_
JSON specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8259_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:32f0594a-f25c-4357-b45b-23b67dfe798c .

camssa:4cad7ad2-451d-49ad-a0ca-0223e3097cf8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4d5ad3af-de14-45eb-b727-67af3497d6ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT contributes to secure and trustworthy data exchange by ensuring cryptographic integrity and authenticity. The issuer’s digital signature guarantees that data has not been altered, and selective disclosure mechanisms ensure that only verified claims from the original credential are processed. This supports protection against unauthorised modification during exchange._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e15d4348-e8c1-42b9-8695-d6e732bfbec3 .

camssa:4f535a5c-26f2-4585-8586-5f8fc5dc5e08 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:52201987-f7b2-4bf7-94d9-65359c0efa8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT specification issuer’s digital signature (via JWS) protects the integrity of the credential, ensuring that the signed payload cannot be modified without invalidating the signature. In addition, each selectively disclosable claim is protected through cryptographic digests bound to the signed JWT. When SD-JWT+KB is used, the disclosed claims are protected, preventing any intermediary from adding, removing, or modifying disclosures, ensuring that the data is intact and exactly as originally._x000D_
_x000D_
Integration of SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html#name-integrity-of-sd-jwts-and-sd_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f78f36a4-cbd6-49d0-9b17-262bf37dccbb .

camssa:53129717-cdcd-4a07-a94b-040858354162 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5734e752-6c0e-4d0e-baf3-bf49f450c718 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT allows users to share only the necessary information during specific procedures, revealing selected properties while keeping other personal data private, t hereby preventing unnecessary data exposure._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f6fa831-16e7-4421-b5e0-a8b4196ae7de .

camssa:579c3372-10e4-4b50-a973-28cad914a71c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0b4b0282-976e-4b58-af4c-6e06e64408d4 .

camssa:5b08a5da-dba7-4886-8558-a743f4be7896 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the SD-JWT specification has been assessed by the NTT Social Informatics Laboratories. In the "Multiparty Selective Disclosure using Attribute-Based Encryption" study, the SD-JWT is analysed by evaluating its feasibility in a virtualised environment through measuring the processing times for token generation, encryption, and decryption. Performance is further assessed by varying the count of disclosures to determine the impact of computational overhead on scalability and real-time applicability._x000D_
_x000D_
"Multiparty Selective Disclosure using Attribute-Based Encryption" study:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/11126722_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1bc8ac58-be6a-420b-99a6-232d51e408c3 .

camssa:5c9bedbf-e554-4bf2-8b30-fc359e5996d7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5ccbf238-c7e6-4570-8593-4d319dde8c91 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5cf5094b-4daa-4c22-9b82-3afbae52983f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5d427223-7b88-4d27-9718-6f5d88da4835 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT can be extended through profiles that enhance security or adapt it to specific ecosystems. In light of this, the base SD-JWT protects the issuer’s signature and the integrity of individual claims, but the set of disclosed claims is not itself protected, meaning disclosures could technically be added or removed without breaking the signature. The SD-JWT+KB (Key Binding) extension addresses this by adding a Key Binding JWT, which binds the disclosed claims to a specific holder key and cryptographically protects the exact set of disclosures. _x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f48aaed0-47ac-4d83-bbbe-8e10cf5ef9a5 .

camssa:5d457d45-a591-4929-8c8b-5c18099dde3a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT supports secure access to services, but it is not designed to enable the visibility of administrative procedures, rules data, and services. Its main purpose is to securely exchange and verify claims between parties, ensuring integrity through signatures and, optionally, confidentiality through encryption._x000D_
_x000D_
However, the ongoing work from IETF on SD-JWT VC could indirectly support the visibility of procedures, as it introduces a standard way to represent and present digital credentials related to qualifications, permits, or other official attributes._x000D_
_x000D_
Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
IETF SD-JWT VC Reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-oauth-sd-jwt-vc-15.html_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:05981b5e-2339-4321-9e40-2f861db4e060 .

camssa:5d7d5b1c-9a5d-441b-837b-00d4b1cc5747 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

