camssa:993f17be-cc86-488a-a2a2-f4519e97396e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:99d3c7d0-2d6b-47b1-a29a-656ef3d3b705 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT enables data portability, allowing claims to be used across different systems and applications. This makes it easier for services to share and verify information, while selective disclosure or encryption can be applied without affecting the underlying data._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48c6fed8-7732-425b-8064-540c88fce0b2 .

camssa:9d6678aa-6f49-4dc9-b495-881f426991ca a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT can simplify the delivery of European public services by securely transmitting selectively disclosed claims. This allows users to share only the information required for a specific procedure, reducing unnecessary data exposure and simplifying the collection and processing of information by public services._x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/EUDIGITALIDENTITYWALLET/pages/694487811/Benefits _x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5d7d5b1c-9a5d-441b-837b-00d4b1cc5747 .

camssa:9e3ad4d7-3b1a-4c66-88f2-02ba9bd31a89 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is developed by IETF, a non-European organisation. However, it is used by many European countries and has also been adopted in different European projects. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
IETF Organisation:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:61841b73-5019-4f2c-a3b9-be942ce1e88b .

camssa:a2122e82-7f29-44b3-b9d9-6a6051eaddfe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a3d39397-ae30-451b-85b5-fadc02a16992 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is adopted and reflected in relevant legal frameworks, such as the PID Rulebook of the EUDI Wallet Architecture Reference Framework (ARF). In this context, the specification covers privacy appears covering certain aspects ensuring selective disclosure of information and keeping undisclosed claims hidden while maintain signature validity._x000D_
_x000D_
ANNEX 3.1 - PID Rulebook; SD-JWT reference_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/1.4.0/annexes/annex-3/annex-3.01-pid-rulebook/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fe9f102f-bfcb-4f0c-8668-b4df6ab7a6f1 .

camssa:a52e783e-a296-491c-8afd-7d4ecc7748ba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the SD-JWT specification has been assessed by the Wilfrid Laurier University. In the "Selective-Disclosure in Decentralised Identity: A Comparative Evaluation of BBS+ and SD-JWT" study, the SD-JWT specification is analysed through a systematic literature review that evaluates its security guarantees, empirical performance metrics like verification latency and proof size, and ecosystem maturity. It employs quantitative synthesis and qualitative assessment to compare these features against BBS+ signatures, highlighting SD-JWT's integration efficiency and standardisation status alongside its privacy trade-offs._x000D_
_x000D_
"Selective-Disclosure in Decentralised Identity: A Comparative Evaluation of BBS+ and SD-JWT" study:_x000D_
https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5360529_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c3b174e4-9283-4e1a-9936-8b417ea70b1d .

camssa:a97fb5cf-8cb6-4bf0-a646-c4e104ee32b9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:abeef9de-b8ec-4463-905a-c204713fc28c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b69d33b7-a799-4ee1-b992-e9869bedf5f4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5cf5094b-4daa-4c22-9b82-3afbae52983f .

camssa:b7195a56-d858-464c-94a5-6bbd1845d63f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT allow the reuse of verified claims to be presented across multiple systems and contexts, enhancing interoperability without compromising confidentiality. The disclosed data comes from a single trusted source, and the same claim can be safely reused in different applications without requiring a new credential. For example, a citizen could prove they are over 18 to multiple public services without revealing their full date of birth or address._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e3acf877-b688-4282-bd01-a0b52b25fe58 .

camssa:b756e8d2-4249-4a07-bf40-f21a344da22b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is platform agnostic since it is based on open standards such as JSON to structure the data, JSON Web Token (JWT) as the base format, JSON Web Signature (JWS) for signing and verification, and JSON Web Key (JWK) for handling keys, which is widely supported across programming languages and platforms. It works with Node.js on the backend, in web browsers using JavaScript, and in mobile frameworks like React Native._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JWK Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7517.html_x000D_
_x000D_
Open wallet Foundation Github Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/openwallet-foundation/sd-jwt-js_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ce3935e1-2a29-4fcd-bf86-e38b0e530cb8 .

camssa:b7f302fe-b9af-4586-a5fc-2b0fd141d890 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is used within the EU eIDAS 2.0 framework to secure verifiable credentials. This allows users to share only the necessary information, reducing data exposure and supporting efficient, interoperable digital public service delivery._x000D_
_x000D_
Moreover, the EUDI Wallet Architecture Reference Framework recommends the use of SD-JWT for the selective disclosure of claims from a JWS-protected JWT. In this context, the specification can also be extended with Key Binding (SD-JWT+KB) , providing additional security features and ensuring that the sender of the information is verified._x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Architecture Reference Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/_x000D_
_x000D_
EU eIDAS 2.0 Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2f3d8cf-364b-4d18-9b73-4f68fdce4940 .

camssa:b81af555-9d9c-4f2f-aadf-0f0d04904eb5 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:b8bc09f9-0ad4-47f6-ae24-7fa96a0744b5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "100%AssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string,
        "73.33%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ba978a4f-779c-4250-8492-466254a0d103 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT allows customization within its specification. Its JWT and JSON structure lets issuers define custom claims, control which claims are disclosed, and optionally implement holder binding. As an example, the working draft of SD-JWT VC applies this same mechanism to Verifiable Credentials, enabling secure issuance and selective disclosure of claims in a VC context while keeping the core process simple and interoperable._x000D_
_x000D_
IETF SD-JWT VC Reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-oauth-sd-jwt-vc-15.html_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:89ab1c48-0acb-4dc4-91cf-7ddf63f4824d .

camssa:c3b174e4-9283-4e1a-9936-8b417ea70b1d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c5aa3eb0-19ab-4138-a1a9-bf5da55e270d a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c87a50c6-a80f-493a-a76e-dfdd6796f627 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cb8fddac-1ce7-423f-b013-b26b5927fc3c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT provides a secure and standardised mechanism for representing claims that can be exchanged between organisations. By extending JWT and JWS, it enables cryptographically verifiable selective disclosure, allowing each organisation to share only the claims necessary for a specific agreement, reducing unnecessary data exposure and supporting trust and compliance across organisational boundaries._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4cad7ad2-451d-49ad-a0ca-0223e3097cf8 .

camssa:ce3935e1-2a29-4fcd-bf86-e38b0e530cb8 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:cfdcc7bc-da27-4791-95fb-9ea7cc4cd957 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT specification enables selective disclosure of claims, allowing users to share only the data they chose. This specification is builded on JWT and JWS by enabling cryptographically verifiable selective disclosure of individual claims from a signed payload. These mechanisms help ensure that data remains inaccessible to unauthorised parties during transmission and that the information received has not been altered in transit, thereby preserving both confidentiality and integrity._x000D_
_x000D_
JWT specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS specification:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ccbf238-c7e6-4570-8593-4d319dde8c91 .

camssa:d2f3d8cf-364b-4d18-9b73-4f68fdce4940 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d4a4a039-18f5-4c46-afc0-4e4e8c91bbc6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is not included within the catalogue of any Member State. However, it is used by many European countries and has also been adopted in different European projects. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:53129717-cdcd-4a07-a94b-040858354162 .

camssa:d5ad539a-1865-4976-a4c0-5a9388e6fcd3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT requires implementation of the core selective disclosure mechanism. From there, disclosures can be simple or more complex._x000D_
_x000D_
For example, in the EUDI Wallet, the full SD-JWT feature set is not used. Instead, the implementation relies on a signed JSON Web Token (JWT), the basic selective disclosure mechanism, and simple presentations derived from claims._x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:94f13efa-c808-4252-acb6-09e5716bc9b2 .

camssa:d71745bb-31a5-4afc-9985-f31fe24c7f10 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is not intended to provide access control mechanisms. Its purpose is to represent claims for secure transfer between two parties. The specification extends related standards such as JWT and JWS by adding cryptographically verifiable selective disclosure, allowing individual claims within a signed payload to be revealed without compromising the integrity of the remaining data. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9825f596-b808-47d9-8743-e2c98bbeeaee .

camssa:e15d4348-e8c1-42b9-8695-d6e732bfbec3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e247db8c-6d3d-4cbe-8c87-464242849bdc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT conformance can be effectively assessed through publicly available test tools, such as the SD-JWT Debugger. This test tool allows developers to validate selective disclosure claims._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Debugger test tool reference:_x000D_
https://www.sdjwt.co/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5e507c76-5f99-4032-93d3-da6dde27f676 .

camssa:e3acf877-b688-4282-bd01-a0b52b25fe58 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e75a4230-d0c4-463c-9b57-a03ae075dc24 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is technology agnostic since it is defined as an open specification and is based on JSON, which is widely supported across programming languages and platforms, and guarantees technological neutrality and broad compatibility across diverse systems_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c87a50c6-a80f-493a-a76e-dfdd6796f627 .

camssa:eeea24ec-f6da-4917-a0b0-c6ee13fc7114 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f033a75a-9a27-4199-af56-2ffa5c46437f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT is not related to enable long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:abeef9de-b8ec-4463-905a-c204713fc28c .

camssa:f48aaed0-47ac-4d83-bbbe-8e10cf5ef9a5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f6bbdb83-9e63-44ad-b63b-a5aabecd4890 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"SD-JWT is not addressed to enable the exposure of interfaces to access the public administration's services. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:993f17be-cc86-488a-a2a2-f4519e97396e .

camssa:f78f36a4-cbd6-49d0-9b17-262bf37dccbb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f8e4014a-1aad-4df3-a562-310650e4c5c7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:fe2adfa1-7389-4e96-9341-fd85513fb18a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The SD-JWT specification is listed as one of the specifications used in the EUDI Architecture Reference Framework. Specifically, it is cited as a candidate standard for use in the EUDI Wallet, with no gaps identified in its applicability. Within this context, SD-JWT is applied to Verifiable Credentials, enabling the assurance of authenticity and integrity for PIDs or attestations, while also supporting selective disclosure of attributes._x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT in EUDI Wallet reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.6.0/technical-specifications/_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eeea24ec-f6da-4917-a0b0-c6ee13fc7114 .

camssa:fe9f102f-bfcb-4f0c-8668-b4df6ab7a6f1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ff14f9f2-d2b7-4309-8da8-3a023613a9c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SD-JWT supports digital service delivery channels by ensuring privacy and control over personal data, as only the necessary information is disclosed. This aligns with eIDAS 2.0, which promotes secure access to services based on verified digital proofs by giving individuals more control over how their personal information is shared._x000D_
_x000D_
eIDAS Regulation Reference:_x000D_
https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation_x000D_
_x000D_
Regulation on electronic identification and trust services Reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv:OJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG_x000D_
_x000D_
SD-JWT Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9901.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c9bedbf-e554-4bf2-8b30-fc359e5996d7 .

