camssa:02fe284b-92a6-4bc9-bb28-cc5bd73676f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is not related to enable the long-term preservation of data, information, or knowledge. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2b14ba23-6e0c-49eb-900d-12fff6cf36d6 .

camssa:0662e484-839e-43bd-97a3-b8a84a513e9a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0dc1872b-fe54-4c45-8c22-caf6f7476caf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Like all the IETF standards, this specification is a free and open technical specification, built on IETF standards and licenses from the Open Web Foundation. Therefore it is licensed on a royalty-free basis.
No IPR disclosures have been submitted directly on this RFC.

Intellectual Property Rights in IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8179'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:de650950-c17c-4a7e-b858-31d54ef9d425 .

camssa:0f0c8c34-2db3-46f7-8f8a-13c27257dc17 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is platform agnostic. It defines a standardised, JSON-based mechanism for digitally signing data and does not depend on any specific software platform, infrastructure environment, cloud provider, or deployment model. As a result, it can be implemented and operated across different platforms without restriction._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9a11f74f-28f1-4014-afba-5611953c6ec0 .

camssa:124d7a17-3bf5-4189-8bf4-21fb9c1e5c34 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS enables secure exchange of data in terms of integrity and authenticity, but it does not provide confidentiality. It guarantees that data has not been altered and that it originates from a trusted signer, but anyone with access to the token can read the payload._x000D_
_x000D_
If confidentiality is required (so that only authorised recipients can read the data), JWE or another encryption mechanism must be used in combination with JWS._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c0e9a4a6-7471-4054-96da-dafaf5fcd381 .

camssa:18bad783-226d-4a63-b9dc-9cea950c272b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"JWS is not related to enable the exposure of interfaces to access public administration's services. Therefore, the criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d29b6a0c-7779-48ca-83a0-06de43c206a1 .

camssa:196d7a54-8938-4eff-9bb6-b96ec17eb130 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS provides a standardised, interoperable format for signing data, ensuring that the integrity and authenticity of the information are preserved when exchanged between different systems. _x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c8b7e74-9762-443c-8dd5-5f81b0f07e6a .

camssa:1995e531-0a07-460f-ba4c-72c2bbae1351 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-51782b9aa4b92f4aba322a549b9d3972e304ca68f9353073c29add782502d910 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:21832615-23cc-47ea-82a9-3608b356ad0c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:24d88aec-ff7d-48bf-b6f8-9cef64251397 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS ensures that the sender of a JSON payload can be verified through the cryptographic signature, confirming that the data originates from a party in possession of the correct private key or shared secret. This provides authentication of the sender and integrity of the data._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:baf36809-7a13-4c61-93d6-54fb8aa7ebcd .

camssa:2954c5ec-fade-4eb0-a4d8-b50457f2fe4a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f71a6871-f244-40de-9564-a623f038b0d8 .

camssa:2b14ba23-6e0c-49eb-900d-12fff6cf36d6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2c8b7e74-9762-443c-8dd5-5f81b0f07e6a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2dd308d7-92f3-47f3-8d63-42a82b47ec7b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:36bac39c-bf50-4f9b-9780-4442444439fb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:38ab9342-ebfc-4fed-8f46-40bc1d9dcd67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is developed by IETF, a non-European organisation. However, JAdES is built on top of JWS and adds what is needed to use it in official European electronic signatures. JWS provides a way to sign data, while JAdES adds extra features like identifying the signer, adding trusted timestamps, applying signature rules, and supporting long-term validation._x000D_
_x000D_
IETF Organisation:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JAdES Reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119100_119199/11918201/01.02.01_60/ts_11918201v010201p.pdf'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2dd308d7-92f3-47f3-8d63-42a82b47ec7b .

camssa:3c551f9d-5473-48e7-b71b-1e80333308e7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is maintained by IETF which is an international organisation based in Fremont, California. More specifically, the standard is developed by the OAuth working group._x000D_
_x000D_
OAuth Working Group Reference:_x000D_
https://oauth.net/specs/_x000D_
_x000D_
JOSE Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/ietf-wg-jose_x000D_
_x000D_
IETF Reference:_x000D_
https://www.ietf.org/_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:507567c8-d7ca-428d-8784-29051b2da099 .

camssa:3c7b82d6-374e-4a24-8b45-6358be1625c4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:3f3b5f0d-d2df-4870-a627-2575e1315d97 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:40c8c39b-cac9-48f0-9afc-0cb6e07bcbbc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS ensures data integrity and authenticity through digital signatures, providing a standard mechanism that enables interoperability between organisations. It is particularly useful in environments that require authentication and the secure exchange of data to support authorisation decisions._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1995e531-0a07-460f-ba4c-72c2bbae1351 .

camssa:43e82229-ba8a-47cf-ac31-80ab0fe9b931 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can be found in both relevant European regulations and European projects. In the case of relevant regulations, it can be found in the “CIR 2025/2531 regarding reference standards and specifications for qualified electronic ledgers” Commission Implementing Regulation. In this regulation, JWS is proposed to provide a standardised, interoperable mechanism for ensuring data integrity and authenticity across different systems, platforms, and organisations._x000D_
_x000D_
Furthermore, the specification is referenced in the EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF). Specifically, the specification is mentioned in section 6.3.4, “Attestation revocation” , of the ARF discussion topic. According to this section, the specification provides the cryptographic integrity and authenticity over the attestation data, and the SD-JWT structure is extended so that revocation status can be independently checked by the verifier._x000D_
_x000D_
CIR 2025/2531 regarding reference standards and specifications for qualified electronic ledgers:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2025/2531/oj_x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/_x000D_
_x000D_
Section “Attestation revocation”, in EUDI Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF): https://eudi.dev/1.3.0/arf/#634-attestation-revocation_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9c3ffe91-3a7c-4e8f-bc72-83af140469b6 .

camssa:489e0b61-7cc2-4186-9ab9-eb585aa61fd2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4aa44500-c66c-430c-bf8c-7e306e949488 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS enables secure processing of data in terms of integrity and authenticity. Any system processing a JWS-protected payload can verify that the data has not been altered and that it comes from a trusted source. This ensures that decisions or operations based on the data are reliable._x000D_
_x000D_
However, the content is readable by anyone who has the token. For secure processing that requires limiting access to authorised parties, JWE or additional encryption mechanisms must be used alongside JWS._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b95cc6ed-7466-45ef-bd51-169d1b36af4e .

camssa:4fe6d9d0-407c-4583-9755-0a3cc51829f6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ceebc7042ff4b3525981f67e306167d9711ac0bce6ea07a067cdb4881854db97 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:507567c8-d7ca-428d-8784-29051b2da099 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:532f1b34-cf3b-45f3-ad11-a0ab19e2c8f7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:582bd330-80cc-4249-9bfa-0185fdf3431c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS allows tokens to be digitally signed, ensuring the integrity and authenticity of the information they contain. If any part of the token is modified, signature verification will fail, indicating that the data has been altered and is no longer trustworthy. Successful verification confirms that the token was issued by the trusted signing authority and has not been tampered with._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:489e0b61-7cc2-4186-9ab9-eb585aa61fd2 .

camssa:58515f75-ff82-4cda-9f8a-54a0d7b45692 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d83a73b3287a82d85b1bd3f5b18089e9794b091b6c6457992a77d5be6bc1500a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5951007b-935b-49ed-8264-8a094b06b6dd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS ensures that the data received has not been altered during transmission by providing cryptographic integrity checks. Because the payload is signed, systems can trust that the information they process is exactly what the sender intended, reducing errors caused by tampering or corruption._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b855119d-561f-4a7b-85fb-f5c0ea4ec789 .

camssa:6011bcb4-39d7-4426-87be-2188649ada0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is not currently included in most Member States’ catalogues of recommended specifications. _x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0662e484-839e-43bd-97a3-b8a84a513e9a .

camssa:637cffef-d2cb-4887-93e6-44419846d633 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of the JWS specification has been assed by the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE). The "A JSON Web Signature Based Adaptive Authentication Modality for Healthcare Applications" study, proposes an open standards based authentication modality that can seamlessly integrate with an Adaptive Authentication system. The proposed authentication modality uses JSON, JWS, and supports a means of verifying the authenticity of the requesting client._x000D_
_x000D_
"A JSON Web Signature Based Adaptive Authentication Modality for Healthcare Applications" study:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9952258_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e7cab9a6-83eb-4a19-bbc3-7202fdc31da2 .

camssa:662770e3-2921-4fc0-b95f-3f9843a9faf8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS supports the simplification of business processes by enabling secure data integrity and authenticity through digital signatures. It allows users to access digital services, such as cross-border public administration platforms, eGovernment portals, and EU digital identity initiatives._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d25eb534-0d2d-461a-ad49-9790fa265cd1 .

camssa:6a48538d-3205-44f0-a20a-411d69d4b8a5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS conformance can be effectively assessed through publicly available test tools. JWT Validator tools let users decode and validate signed tokens (JWS) by checking structure, signature correctness, and claims such as issuer and expiration and JWS Parser/Decoder tools provide decoding of the header, payload, and signature for inspection._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Parser/Decoder Reference:_x000D_
https://8gwifi.org/jwsparse.jsp_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT Validator Reference:_x000D_
https://jwtsecrets.com/tools/jwt-validator_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e765d361-9afb-4b7f-8511-598259539761 .

camssa:6fa72868-98c8-4a56-8900-0fe8e639bbc0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:714ff3ef-14e7-434b-b1b9-ad6dcbbaa607 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS allows extensions by the inclusion of new header parameters, registration of additional cryptographic algorithms and the creation of application specific profiles built on top of the core specification. _x000D_
_x000D_
For example, custom header parameters can be included for domain specific requirements. These extensions can be formally registered through the IANA registries defined by the specification, ensuring uniqueness, transparency, and interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
IANA Considerations JWS reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html#section-9_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:58515f75-ff82-4cda-9f8a-54a0d7b45692 .

camssa:73f48787-c11a-485f-920e-9567681e6b56 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can help enable digital service delivery channels by protecting the integrity and authenticity of information contained within tokens through digital signatures. By allowing public administrations to verify that data has not been altered and was issued by a trusted authority, JWS supports secure digital procedures. This reduces the need for in-person processes by ensuring that electronic exchanges are reliable and based on verified information._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:84b0e590-f07e-4d72-aba8-a93b236f83e0 .

camssa:7a2e1e95-aa83-4e88-94b5-99b8cb7475ff a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3b3b2febe9a7e3ad44bdefc47b0bbcafc7a2e677e9570d6ad822efbe1f7d41e2 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7a4ea8c8-196c-4d67-a568-10ef802ae470 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can be found in the EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF). Specifically, the specification is mentioned in the standards used for the EUDI Wallet. _x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b065e0cb-78be-4be0-9d17-4a6474b51dfe .

camssa:7c935a30-53d8-4f0d-8d0a-fd9a4260845e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:7d6dd190-8f5d-4642-a92e-08c9410a0049 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:value "100%StrengthOfAssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string,
        "89.19%AssessmentScoreAverage"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8097a34d-5d31-46c5-81f0-136caeb8e269 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is addressed to ensure that data is trustworthy, but the decision to grant or deny access is handled by the surrounding system (application, API, or authorisation server). Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7c935a30-53d8-4f0d-8d0a-fd9a4260845e .

camssa:84b0e590-f07e-4d72-aba8-a93b236f83e0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:86ba9020-4b11-45c6-b564-667661a2e5a8 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is widely used in European regulations and cross-border projects. It provides cryptographic integrity and authenticity in the EUDI Wallet, where it protects attestation data, and is considered a stable candidate specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS is also a core component of the eSignature Building Block and Digital Signature Services (DSS), enabling advanced and qualified electronic signatures in line with eIDAS. Within DSS, JAdES extends JWS for JSON-based signatures with features like signatory binding, modification detection, trusted timestamps, and long-term validation._x000D_
_x000D_
eSignature Building Block Reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/DIGITAL/pages/467109036/eSignature_x000D_
_x000D_
DSS (Digital Signature Services) Reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/DIGITAL/pages/467109107/Digital+Signature+Service+-+DSS_x000D_
_x000D_
JAdES Reference:_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/DSS/webapp-demo/doc/dss-documentation.html#_jades_signature_jws_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3f3b5f0d-d2df-4870-a627-2575e1315d97 .

camssa:8a190a83-b990-48c2-9976-dab07d4be55a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-26d7b17ff73e55cbf2e7b90ec0eaca8627f132b000e1c8f2de8e5157d8ebe216 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8a3e7267-8066-414a-8062-d26146b8b7be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is not related to provide an access control mechanism. Therefore, this criterion is not related to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d829e8f-af74-4cd7-b38e-b36a66257e08 .

camssa:8c3f1cbe-5598-457b-8a6e-b9230290c6bc a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the JWS has been assed by the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE). In the "Validating a Modified JSON Web Signature Format using the Scenario of Ammunition Issuance for Training Purposes" study, the JWS has been shown to be effective for secure identities exchange data directly with each other. _x000D_
_x000D_
"Validating a Modified JSON Web Signature Format using the Scenario of Ammunition Issuance for Training Purposes" study:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/10356342_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6fa72868-98c8-4a56-8900-0fe8e639bbc0 .

camssa:8c94b7b7-c2ce-43f9-b549-4bf6f528c926 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can simplify the delivery of European public services by ensuring the integrity and authenticity of information exchanged between different systems. By digitally signing data, JWS allows public administrations to verify that the information was issued by a trusted authority and has not been modified during transmission. This supports more reliable and accurate service delivery based on verified information._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f07758a8-978c-43b6-9079-f54a67cca042 .

camssa:8d829e8f-af74-4cd7-b38e-b36a66257e08 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8dfdfbcf-5782-451d-9fb7-26b7f791c2c9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is not related to the publication of data on the web, as it is designed to ensure the integrity and authenticity of data by applying a cryptographic digital signature to a JSON payload. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:90c35b87-5b8d-494f-964e-935dbde17c78 .

camssa:8e1bb7ce-94b6-49d6-99a6-578e7e5e5c92 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS supports customisation through custom header parameters and application-specific claims. This flexibility allows implementations to adapt JWS to specific business or organisational requirements while still remaining compatible with the core specification. JAdES extends JWS by adding features required for advanced electronic signatures, such as trusted timestamps, signature policies, and long-term validation support._x000D_
_x000D_
JAdES Reference:_x000D_
https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/119100_119199/11918201/01.01.01_60/ts_11918201v010101p.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21832615-23cc-47ea-82a9-3608b356ad0c .

camssa:8eda97c8-fddc-43e6-92b3-966891079a90 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can be used in a multilingual context, because it simply signs a JSON payload. The payload can contain text in any language, encoded in UTF‑8, and JWS will preserve the integrity and authenticity regardless of language._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8a190a83-b990-48c2-9976-dab07d4be55a .

camssa:90c35b87-5b8d-494f-964e-935dbde17c78 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:92cb3597-22ff-4fe0-b1b4-693b045c5704 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS first appeared as draft in March 2011 and, since May 2025, has been published as an_x000D_
RFC at Proposed Standard level. The available documentation provides clear details on all modifications_x000D_
introduced across the different released drafts._x000D_
_x000D_
Additionally, organisations have already begun adopting this standard. JWS is an open specificacion_x000D_
utilised on multiple European projects and initiatives, such as European Blockchain Services Infrastructure_x000D_
(EBSI) meaning its sufficiently mature for its use in the development of digital solutions/services._x000D_
_x000D_
European Blockchain Services Infrastructure (EBSI) - JWS reference:_x000D_
https://hub.ebsi.eu/arch-req/standards_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d657a0a8-a8ae-453f-b9df-e0d805e668d6 .

camssa:93a32c51-c887-417c-8133-594a08203db7 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is not related to scope comprehensively scope administrative procedures, rules, data, and services. Therefore, the criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ecc519a1-1908-4a02-b419-27246dd25daf .

camssa:96afa36a-f108-474c-a670-3903f98e7444 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9a11f74f-28f1-4014-afba-5611953c6ec0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9c3ffe91-3a7c-4e8f-bc72-83af140469b6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9f34cc6a-794d-42d5-b956-19c6a9cf7aa2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a0b60bc0-8e6d-4703-b89f-b9f435b87ff5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is technology agnostic. It is based on JSON mechanism for digitally signing data. It does not mandate any specific programming language, operating system, hardware environment, or vendor implementation._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96afa36a-f108-474c-a670-3903f98e7444 .

camssa:a6e0503b-21a9-4813-9d04-5949084aa386 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS specification is not included in any national catalogue of recommended specifications._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
Digital Public Administration factsheets - 2025: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/iopeu-monitoring/digital-public-administration-factsheets_x000D_
_x000D_
JWT standard:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:3c7b82d6-374e-4a24-8b45-6358be1625c4 .

camssa:ac74bed0-d2e3-4125-bf3e-cae9c5182103 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, JWS can define the interoperability aspects of the "eSignature Verification and Validation" and "e-Seal Verification and Validation" ABBs of the EIRA Technical-view application._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:dd56da3b-fdf8-4d4b-a62f-740561f00aca .

camssa:affa5fa7-415e-4a6f-85bd-727c6a2246c3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS can support the reuse of relevant information because it allows verified claims or evidence to be exchanged between administrations without requiring the citizen to provide the same data again._x000D_
_x000D_
For example, a JWS could contain signed information such as identity details, proof of residence, qualifications, permits, or business registration data. Once signed by the issuing authority, that information can be reused by other administrations because they can verify its authenticity and integrity directly, without asking the citizen to resubmit the same evidence._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4fe6d9d0-407c-4583-9755-0a3cc51829f6 .

camssa:b065e0cb-78be-4be0-9d17-4a6474b51dfe a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b51b7844-dbd0-4200-9023-28a4b544581f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'JWS is discussed across both specialised forums and general developer platforms such as Stack Overflow. The big amount of questions about implementation, security discussions, and best-practice exchanges demonstrates active adoption and continuous community participation._x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Stack Overflow Reference:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=JWS&s=56cbb160-cc05-4349-a221-1f5b487e167a_x000D_
_x000D_
JWS Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html_x000D_
_x000D_
JOSE Framework Reference:_x000D_
https://jose.readthedocs.io/en/latest/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c6b88bcc-fcd6-44c5-880e-21abb5719eb0 .

camssa:b855119d-561f-4a7b-85fb-f5c0ea4ec789 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

