camssa:08de5dc7-92ba-4a21-8667-50d8eb6d0773 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style that defines how systems should interact, and it is intrinsically linked to the HTTP protocol. While REST provides the design principles, HTTP provides the actual methods to carry them out. This close relationship means that as the HTTP standards evolve and mature, RESTful implementations become more robust and efficient for public services._x000D_
_x000D_
The latest minor updates to the HTTP/3 specification (RFC 9114) address specific transport-layer efficiencies and security patches._x000D_
_x000D_
The most recent major milestone for RESTful implementations was the release of the RFC 9110 series in June 2022. This major update consolidated and standardised HTTP semantics into a single, mature document, providing a stable and well-documented foundation for developers to plan and implement digital solutions for years to come._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Major 2022 Update):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5c765e98-df7e-4cad-a462-8a31332e5bfa .

camssa:0f2122db-d389-485e-b1fc-8f7740f0f167 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-583a0f52df591048a41be40620830a70260e77855364174d91ba159970d8488e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:102425ab-33a4-4351-8045-ec6ce34a3367 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1a842477-4169-4565-9dd0-530f3fab46bb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:1abe9ea9-66fa-450c-9dfa-aa968dd76af5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is a sofware architectural style which defines a set of costraints for how the architecture of an internet-scale distributed hypermedia system should behave. REST architectural constraints are designed to provide efficient and scalable client-server applications through a URI resource approach. In this regard, REST allows for a greater interoperability, explicitly addressing and enabling data portability between systems or  applications._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d64f1a6-0b3c-4c77-9026-faac12253b99 .

camssa:2425e2dc-ba7a-4e31-aefe-7fbe0a02bc18 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2c5d212e-23e0-4f1c-8a0c-e41311cc8f1f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2f9abf6c-b6e9-4613-b9ba-6f4a281bb501 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:31bcd44a-5803-414d-b27f-2327a9ca467a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of REST's architectural properties is the modifiability of components to meet changing needs. While the core architectural constraints remain fixed to ensure consistency, users have the flexibility to choose different media types (such as JSON, XML, or HTML) and decide which optional features, such as "Code on Demand," to include. This ability to select optional elements based on requirements makes the style adaptable to a wide range of digital services._x000D_
_x000D_
REST "Code on demand" reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/#code-on-demand_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:102425ab-33a4-4351-8045-ec6ce34a3367 .

camssa:320c47ae-d20d-4d6e-b9c7-57e14d31d194 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST relies on the underlying HTTP protocol to ensure that data is protected from unauthorised changes. While it does not define its own encryption, it is designed to work with secure transport layers like HTTPS to safeguard information during transit. Additionally, RESTful systems often use mechanisms such as "ETags" or digital signatures to verify at the final stage that a resource has not been tampered with._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Conditional Requests and ETags):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-13_x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5ea24587-d013-4012-b1e4-cce7a63ddab6 .

camssa:34ca5e56-5f7e-44cd-811b-4bf7a2bb5897 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:36124f6c-cd91-4278-af97-caea6c71f064 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is a domain-agnostic architectural style. Its six core constraints emphasise the scalability of interactions between components, uniform interfaces, independent deployment of components and the creation of layered architecture to facilitate its usage across business domains._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bac527ee-0f4d-4a90-a965-1b005b62bacc .

camssa:390c6adb-5d25-4a17-ba22-1d6be13cbaba a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST represents a set of design principles and constraints rather than a document being actively developed by a committee, there is no evidence found of any working group contributing to the development of REST. _x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:693b54b6-ff88-430b-a98d-fa055914c98e .

camssa:3955af07-5023-416a-9f63-99385f1b529e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The purpose of REST is not related to the delivery of multilingual public services. Therefore, this criterion is_x000D_
not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83cf5a5e-5d96-4328-8ac8-67155d610172 .

camssa:39fbcb3d-6627-4d5a-9a88-46eaa6899d4c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of the REST specification has been assessed by the VNR Vignana Jyothi Institute of Engineering and Technology. In the "Performance evaluation of RESTful web services" study, the REST specification is proposed as a lightweight architectural style for building web services, facilitating better performance and lower resource consumption compared to traditional protocols._x000D_
_x000D_
"Performance evaluation of RESTful web services" study:_x000D_
https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8103450_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0761260c-c24e-4215-8823-0259ef620d4f .

camssa:3b524e0e-8f7d-4180-bf88-6b8c3577990d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style focused on how systems interact rather than a security or privacy protocol. It does not natively include mechanisms to ensure the protection of personal data or specific alignment with regulations. However, it is designed to be implemented over secure transport layers such as HTTPS (TLS), which provides the encryption and integrity needed to protect data during transmission._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Security Considerations):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-17_x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:414491c6-c995-4d34-b08e-47eb93c6bc9b .

camssa:3ffc6d21-1fbb-4dc5-ab15-31712f958613 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
    dcat:accessURL "https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss"^^xsd:anyURI .

camssa:414491c6-c995-4d34-b08e-47eb93c6bc9b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3dd3a1fb1ac7d78d162dab36230e70a34459f38a795e765cc5fdd304c8c04907 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:45221212-f864-4f92-860d-112ec34476dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-69e927013383f3944a629c01e930a6663b8304aa5f3137b9a5de3c02d34da401 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:46eb64d4-fb34-48ea-a19f-3681dac80688 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST as an architectural style, relies on universal web standards such as HTTP and URI, which means it can be implemented using any programming language or framework. This flexibility allows different systems to communicate seamlessly, regardless of the specific technology stack they use in the background._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (HTTP Standard):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
Uniform Resource Identifier (URI): Generic Syntax:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3986.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:45221212-f864-4f92-860d-112ec34476dc .

camssa:4907a70f-f6bf-43d5-89e0-8d4e9e2a367d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The REST specification provides RESTful APIs that are built on key security design principles that ensure data is processed and exchanged in a secure and trustworthy manner. By following these principles, such as using secure transport layers like HTTPS, public administrations can ensure that sensitive information remains protected and unaltered during transit._x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (HTTP Standard):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c7734307-a62f-4ffa-8a11-0a5721b19c7e .

camssa:4a8d0dde-d6fc-442d-a9e2-9c2718997aaa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is included in several open repositories and catalogues at the European level. It is a fundamental part of the "API Framework for European Public Administrations" published by the Joint Research Centre (JRC), which provides the standard guidelines for building interoperable digital services. Additionally, it is listed on the CAMSS List of Standards further confirms its recognised status at the European level._x000D_
_x000D_
JRC Publications Repository - API Framework for European Public Administrations:_x000D_
https://publications.jrc.ec.europa.eu/repository/handle/JRC115049_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d2c7b0fc-4907-4558-8b18-e3f55099ec12 .

camssa:4ade5910-c2ea-4816-beb2-ea32ef96dea1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is a software architectural style based on standard HTTP methods. Its principles can be applied in any case and, therefore, it is a resource not subject to royalties or any kind of proprietary restrictions. This open nature ensures that any organisation can implement RESTful services freely, without legal barriers or costs, which has led to its universal adoption across the web._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6bc2919d-9899-4d4c-aa6b-5eff95388c64 .

camssa:4d77bae4-d041-475a-88c1-269735f53162 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style rather than a technical specification, and there is no evidence found of any working group contributing to the development of REST_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fcd7747c-59ca-425b-8e10-fe4c05466b5f .

