camssa:86faef64-594d-4c38-8f9b-1aa55c03e126 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST uses the standard features of the HTTP protocol to handle access to information. It does not have its own built-in access control system, but it relies on standard HTTP headers and status codes to make sure only authorised people can access or change data. This allows public administrations to set up their own security rules while using a common, well-known way to manage permissions._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Authentication and Authorization):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-11_x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/_x000D_
'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:93b9dff3-a427-4a50-bcbb-fd9a40e07812 .

camssa:8d64f1a6-0b3c-4c77-9026-faac12253b99 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8d8e4520-510e-4d8e-a250-b8aea299bf90 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8f2737a3-2efe-4524-a1f4-9fd22a4253c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:8fabb408-251b-454b-bce7-cca2628b0fc6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'RESTful systems are built on core security principles that ensure data is handled safely. By using secure transport protocols like HTTPS, REST ensures that information stays private and cannot be tampered with while moving between systems. This approach allows public administrations to process sensitive data with confidence, knowing it is protected from unauthorised access and remains exactly as it was sent._x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (HTTP Standard):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8d8e4520-510e-4d8e-a250-b8aea299bf90 .

camssa:907dc68a-34cb-4e19-b215-50de7659a099 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:90acd49d-771e-4708-a67e-db50173485d2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST relies on the underlying HTTP protocol to manage access to resources. It does not define its own specific security or encryption mechanisms, but it uses standard HTTP features, to enable controlled access. This ensures that confidentiality can be maintained by integrating with standard authentication and authorisation frameworks._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Security Considerations):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-17_x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:bc88d5da-2cc1-4e91-8371-d13ab89a49dc .

camssa:927911f8-ac3c-486b-b60b-587740cb90e9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9c03a344765a6b8da57c4a7d40647791b737e3e1feecc14e3d59f2c69bdb246b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:93b9dff3-a427-4a50-bcbb-fd9a40e07812 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a16c678a586cf542d2ae1d6cd8a987bd6ed0b2af52ba0e04d8872fe616a9b7bd ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:98909529-1d07-4449-bafe-35e5132e5ac4 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style rather than a technical specification maintained by a specific organisation. However, it is a fundamental technology used in many relevant European projects and initiatives, such as the Once-Only Technical System (OOTS) and the Interoperable Europe Portal._x000D_
_x000D_
European Commission - Once-Only Technical System (OOTS):_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/OOTS/overview_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e255f6af-051c-48de-85e1-d1d4039ecfa7 .

camssa:9b55a727-3401-46c8-9212-6f0d6c780ab9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:9c5146d4-1362-4e41-aaa0-3259209de4e1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style that defines how different systems should interact. REST APIs provide a simple and flexible way to access web services, which helps in creating digital interfaces that can be easily used by assistive technologies. By simplifying how data is accessed and shared, it explicitly supports the goal of making public services accessible to all citizens._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2f9abf6c-b6e9-4613-b9ba-6f4a281bb501 .

camssa:a83e7260-dafb-447b-9a5e-2719c21e3055 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is a key technology used in major European projects that focus on privacy and data protection. For instance, the Once-Only Technical System (OOTS), which powers the "Your Europe" portal's data exchange, relies on RESTful APIs. This initiative is strictly governed by the Single Digital Gateway Regulation and the GDPR, ensuring that personal information is handled securely and privately across European borders._x000D_
_x000D_
General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng_x000D_
_x000D_
European Commission - Once-Only Technical System (OOTS) - REST reference:_x000D_
https://oots.pages.code.europa.eu/tdd/apidoc/_x000D_
_x000D_
Single Digital Gateway (SDG):_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32018R1724_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f98e6d28-3af4-47cf-befd-b6ce86614ff6 .

camssa:ad37806e-5d2c-47be-ae0c-ce6623bdceac a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ae5f5930-9277-4b3c-bb09-0a665fada16b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is designed to ensure that different systems can work together smoothly by following a set of clear architectural rules. Because it provides a standardised way for systems to communicate, it makes it much simpler for organisations to create interoperability agreements. By referencing RESTful principles, public administrations can easily define the technical terms of their collaboration, ensuring that their digital services remain efficient and easy to manage across different departments or borders._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Standard for RESTful communication):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:59d2b028-df5e-4181-84d6-367536322d45 .

camssa:b1a0997e-e373-43ea-b6e4-6a4857803752 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The uniform interface constraint is fundamental to the design of any RESTful system. It simplifies and decouples the architecture, which enables each part to evolve independently. For that reason, the REST architectural style ensures the standardised transfer of information between software systems, effectively enabling the exposure of interfaces that allow citizens and other organisations to access public services._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad37806e-5d2c-47be-ae0c-ce6623bdceac .

camssa:b7779533-688b-482b-96fb-076ac9a7ba18 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "60"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b91734ee-f05e-400d-a4cf-e69300575745 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"REST is an architectural style that defines how different systems should interact, allowing for greater interoperability between clients and servers. By providing a simple and flexible way to access web services through machine-readable formats, it ensures that administrative data and services are highly visible and easy to discover. A prime example of this is the French government's open data portal,  which uses REST APIs to host and share public datasets, making government information transparent and accessible to everyone._x000D_
_x000D_
French government's open data portal:_x000D_
https://doc.data.gouv.fr/api/intro/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57d11989-9cdf-49d3-a902-4a8a66bcf205 .

camssa:bac4a64c-71e1-47c5-bb96-a96a2fe1a169 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Finland and Slovakia. Its recommendation by these Member States highlights its recognised value as a mature architectural style for building interoperable digital services across Europe._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
National catalogue of Finland:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Finland%20Factsheet%20Validated.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:02c361f9-00b1-4122-915c-f69bd9f39f9f .

camssa:bac527ee-0f4d-4a90-a965-1b005b62bacc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-50ab6a29689585b917f7b2972d2c41e8c8c52723c2d58eb9b92109c938d4e825 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bc39396b-5142-449f-9ba9-3a582f246c0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST relies on standard web protocols, such as HTTP, to manage the identification and authentication of users. While it does not provide its own specific tools for this, it defines how standard headers should be used to carry authentication data._x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:57603f6b-8c5e-4b79-8466-705c7fd3aa6e .

camssa:bc4e327f-57b5-4d38-b023-fca38d3cd965 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is included in 2 national catalogues of recommended specifications. They belong to Finland and_x000D_
Slovakia. The National Interoperability Framework (NIF) of Finland and Slovakia are aligned with at least 3 out_x000D_
of 4 scoreboards of the EIF Monitoring according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory_x000D_
(NIFO) factsheets._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
National catalogue of Finland:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Finland%20Factsheet%20Validated.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c5d212e-23e0-4f1c-8a0c-e41311cc8f1f .

camssa:bc88d5da-2cc1-4e91-8371-d13ab89a49dc a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bf0eebc1-ce76-4111-9372-7193dd4dfa48 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'Through the caching architectural principle, REST has the ability to store copies of frequently accessed data_x000D_
in several places along the requeest-response path. The Cache Control Headers can indicate when a representation never expires, meaning that the data of the representation is well preserved._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:907dc68a-34cb-4e19-b215-50de7659a099 .

camssa:c2f2edd8-b3a1-4d9b-9848-82c5377e0f79 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The REST architectural style is the primary way digital service delivery channels are built. By using RESTful APIs, public administrations can digitise procedures that used to be done in person, such as applying for permits or accessing health records. This approach streamlines communication between different government systems and ensures that services are available through various channels such as mobile apps and web portals._x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:927911f8-ac3c-486b-b60b-587740cb90e9 .

camssa:c7734307-a62f-4ffa-8a11-0a5721b19c7e a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-3beae22dd24b0dbc955ce74a9fe755390983d8436a45b401461ceaaa7a5d1609 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:c82a84b9-f80f-43c9-8523-dfb141b450b9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'One of the key properties of REST is the modifiability of its components to meet changing needs. Specifically, the "Code on demand" constraint allows a server to extend or customise the functionality of a client by transferring executable code, such as JavaScript. This ensures that the system can be extended with new features at runtime without needing to manually update the client software, making the architecture highly flexible._x000D_
_x000D_
REST "Code on demand" reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/#code-on-demand_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:70f228cf-eb3d-4634-bf8c-38ab342fb122 .

camssa:cbebf260-54a8-4bec-b4ea-df93d5df4920 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is an architectural style defined by a specific set of core constraints. For a system to be considered truly RESTful, it must conform to all of these rules together, as they are designed to work as a complete set to ensure performance and scalability. Because missing any of these constraints means the system no longer follows the REST model, the specification is meant to be implemented as a whole._x000D_
_x000D_
REST architectural constraints reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/rest-architectural-constraints/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:55c9cfc4-04a4-4c02-81b2-047b54fa8e23 .

camssa:d0fc91b5-02db-42a4-ba33-f57ab8046fda a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"REST helps ensure data processing accuracy by using standard HTTP features like ETags and conditional headers. These tools allow a system to verify that it is working with the most recent version of a resource before making any changes, which prevents errors such as overwriting someone else's updates. When combined with secure transport layers like HTTPS to prevent unauthorised modifications, these mechanisms ensure that the data remains accurate throughout the entire process._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (Conditional Requests and ETags):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-13_x000D_
_x000D_
REST API Tutorial - REST Security Essentials:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/security-essentials/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f19b4ba5-4939-4588-bc0e-55d6fac745d1 .

camssa:d2c7b0fc-4907-4558-8b18-e3f55099ec12 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-549e39fc635763b9466e09688714b2908fcf7a349d4f4f0fe2a761bd6f502733 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d5259188-6e1f-4b16-b9ee-bdcfd5805ee0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The REST architectural style simplifies the delivery of public services by providing a common and flexible way for different government systems to communicate. By using RESTful APIs, public administrations can build digital services that are easy for citizens to access from any device, reducing the need for paper-based processes and in-person visits. A practical example is the Once-Only Technical System (OOTS), which relies on REST to help citizens and businesses share information across the EU more efficiently._x000D_
_x000D_
Once-Only Technical System (OOTS):_x000D_
https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/sites/spaces/OOTS/overview_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1a842477-4169-4565-9dd0-530f3fab46bb .

camssa:d8348a56-9f28-453a-a5cf-865a6d6073b0 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is included in 1 national catalogue of recommended specifications, it belongs to Finland. Its inclusion in these national repositories demonstrates its recognised value as a standard for building interoperable digital services at a national level._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
National catalogue of Finland:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Finland%20Factsheet%20Validated.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e01740b4-860a-4308-961c-72638ae0f67b .

camssa:dd4c2a64-3240-462f-878a-570cff86e6ae a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"REST is an architectural style that defines how different systems should interact, providing a simple and flexible way to access web services. By providing consistent resource structures with well-defined properties and metadata, the API ensures that clients can easily interpret the data, supporting clearer understanding of administrative procedures and services. A practical example is the French government's open data portal, which is built using REST principles to ensure its datasets are presented in a comprehensible and logical way for the public._x000D_
_x000D_
French government's open data portal:_x000D_
https://doc.data.gouv.fr/api/intro/_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8f2737a3-2efe-4524-a1f4-9fd22a4253c9 .

camssa:e01740b4-860a-4308-961c-72638ae0f67b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e255f6af-051c-48de-85e1-d1d4039ecfa7 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-17a2b7a0ca372f407c300b69049faf9d92cbf274964290ba278b18cf10bf5dbf ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e71a6db8-2499-42db-9c0a-33829f87f4a3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST has a wide-spread market acceptance as it is a common method to connect components in_x000D_
microservice architectures. Major global businesses like IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS) rely on RESTful APIs to power their cloud platforms and manage complex data exchanges. Furthermore, open-source projects such as Spree Commerce use REST APIs to allow external applications to interact with their e-commerce engine, facilitating the management of products and orders in a standardised way._x000D_
_x000D_
Amazon Web Services reference:_x000D_
https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-rest-api.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST IBM reference:_x000D_
https://www.ibm.com/es-es/cloud/learn/rest-apis_x000D_
_x000D_
Spree Commerce - REST API Reference:_x000D_
https://spreecommerce.org/docs/api-reference/store-api/introduction_x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f0a04d53-574b-4184-af74-622c4c9bebd5 .

camssa:edf75128-4a09-4559-8b05-b0525065b257 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is platform agnostic as it is not tied to any specific operating system or hardware. It is designed to be a universal architectural style that works across all devices and environments that support standard web protocols such as HTTP. This ensures that digital content and services remain accessible and consistent regardless of the underlying platform being used by the client or the server._x000D_
_x000D_
HTTP Semantics (HTTP Standard):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:34ca5e56-5f7e-44cd-811b-4bf7a2bb5897 .

camssa:f0a04d53-574b-4184-af74-622c4c9bebd5 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f19b4ba5-4939-4588-bc0e-55d6fac745d1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f1ee4f38-a65d-45f8-be2a-b6021be32112 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'REST is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, REST can define the interoperability aspects of the "Web Service", "Machine to Machine Interface", "API", and "Data Exchange" ABBs of the EIRA Technical Application View._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
_x000D_
REST reference:_x000D_
https://restfulapi.net/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0f2122db-d389-485e-b1fc-8f7740f0f167 .

camssa:f98e6d28-3af4-47cf-befd-b6ce86614ff6 a cav:Score,
