camssa:146b06be-17e6-4852-9568-7e8c43096501 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH employs a DNS-based naming convention (e.g., name@domainname) for algorithms and methods, allowing anyone to define and use extensions in a local namespace without central registration. This capability is further enhanced by RFC 8308, which defines a formal mechanism for extension negotiation within the protocol._x000D_
_x000D_
Extension Negotiation in the Secure Shell (SSH) Protocol (RFC8308):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8308_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4991e9d-9caa-416a-a894-d3108467c845 .

camssa:15302d44-0922-4279-a271-48ba010fd3fd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is a low-level technical specification for secure remote login and encrypted transport. It does not provide the commonly accepted modelling techniques required to document or align administrative business processes for the delivery of public services._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b325de36-b57d-4bf4-8efd-2269aec4175a .

camssa:17e317de-0b8e-478e-92f5-a69494161b73 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH facilitates the technical movement of data by providing secure communication channels, multiplexed logical channels, and TCP/IP port forwarding, which allow data to be moved securely between disparate systems. However, SSH does not enable data portability on its own; as a low-level transport protocol, it is "binary-transparent" and does not define the structure, format, or semantics of the data being transmitted._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:833413df-24e7-4360-8053-ab92838d202b .

camssa:18eaca67-e3af-4053-87cc-f567b708eafa a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is technology agnostic because it is designed to work over any 8-bit clean, binary-transparent transport. While it typically runs over TCP/IP, the specification explicitly states it can be used on top of any other reliable data stream. Furthermore, it does not mandate a single cryptographic technology; instead, it uses a negotiation mechanism where parties agree on encryption, integrity, and key exchange algorithms from a broad list of supported standards._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8399e8e7-a849-4e94-9068-729295f4e682 .

camssa:19e6989f-f326-4de5-8343-d16821ffda09 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is selected for use in European initiatives as a foundational cryptographic protocol. It is specifically included in the ENISA Technical implementation guidance on cybersecurity risk management measures to assist entities in meeting the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2690. This guidance is designed for essential and important entities across the EU, facilitating secure cross-border digital operations_x000D_
_x000D_
ENISA Technical implementation guidance on cybersecurity risk management measures:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2025-06/ENISA_Technical_implementation_guidance_on_cybersecurity_risk_management_measures_version_1.0.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2690:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/2690/oj/eng_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:90356ad7-ee72-4459-9dfe-55a6a9eaf2f1 .

camssa:1e2565bd-48c5-4560-8f0b-ed243595af9b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """"SSH has been included in the CAMSS List of Standards, notably the French Référentiel Général d’Interopérabilité (RGI), which is a Member State's catalogue with high performance on interoperability according to the National Interoperability Framework Observatory (NIFO)._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
Référentiel général d'interopérabilité (RGI) Reference:_x000D_
https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/uploads/Referentiel_General_Interoperabilite_V2.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html\""""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b5e9cf3a-cb74-4c14-b9e9-5794aa9e248f .

