camssa:317fd1d2-bd19-4ed9-946d-2556a723b9bd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SSH is a globally recognized protocol for secure remote administration, its status within specific national catalogues is not documented in the provided RFCs or ENISA guidance._x000D_
_x000D_
ENISA:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/#contentList_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:c4cae551-c3b1-4122-9df1-1f32fd603f31 .

camssa:32a0505e-4526-458a-a86a-4004d6073157 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SSH is an international specification, the protocol is a foundational element in European initiatives focused on the security and privacy of digital public services, providing guidance to public administrations on implementing secure remote access and encrypted communication. By providing strong encryption, cryptographic host authentication, and integrity protection, SSH acts as a critical technical enabler for the secure exchange of information._x000D_
_x000D_
ENISA Technical implementation guidance on cybersecurity risk management measures:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2025-06/ENISA_Technical_implementation_guidance_on_cybersecurity_risk_management_measures_version_1.0.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47ea9f09-8fda-474e-8469-8e95a76955c9 .

camssa:364429d7-e97e-4433-b937-fb65491db0b5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH provides extensive means for access control through its User Authentication Protocol and its ability to enforce local security policies. The specification mandates that the server must ensure the local policy permits the user the specific access requested (e.g., shell access vs. file transfer). Additionally, it provides administrative mechanisms to restrict which services are exposed to a user, including the ability to disable features like TCP/IP port forwarding or X11 forwarding based on the level of trust._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:990ae32a-181a-476c-854e-be8030fd4028 .

camssa:40146117-c800-4898-bcb9-2bfc7d3e5a81 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:42b5859f-6f5e-4eb2-ab4e-af40a75e9f67 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is supported by a robust Internet community, originally organised through the Secsh Working Group and maintained via active mailing list discussions. Furthermore, because it utilises well-known, well-established cryptographic algorithms, it benefits from the support and scrutiny of the broader global security and research community._x000D_
_x000D_
Secsh Working Group:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/secsh/about/_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:8b2f15c0-2bb8-45ab-ab12-3c0587942c72 .

camssa:455969eb-ef29-433f-bda3-5b49082dd509 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The IETF is a consensus-based group, and authority to act on behalf of the community requires a high degree of consensus and the continued consent of the community. The process of creating and Internet Standard is straightforward: a specification undergoes a period of development and several iterations of review by the Internet community and revision based upon experience, is adopted as a Standard by the appropriate body... and is published. In practice, the process is more complicated, due to (1) the difficulty of creating specifications of high technical quality; (2) the need to consider the interests of all the affected parties; (3) the importance of establishing widespread community consensus; and (4) the difficulty of evaluating the utility of a particular specification for the Internet community. The goals of the Internet Standards Process are:
- Technical excellence;
- prior implementation and testing;
- clear, concise, and easily understood documentation;
- openness and fairness; and
- timeliness.
The goal of technical competence, the requirement for prior implementation and testing, and the need to allow all interested parties to comment all require significant time and effort. The Internet Standards Process is intended to balance these conflicting goals. The process is believed to be as short and simple as possible without sacrificing technical excellence, thorough testing before adoption of a standard, or openness and fairness.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:9b54f3b0-4a48-4615-8d93-9ec55757435d .

camssa:47bd1f3d-19d8-4c6f-acb3-a35462cdbe59 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:47ea9f09-8fda-474e-8469-8e95a76955c9 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4867dc37-04bd-4bfe-888b-c5aa65e178be a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH specification was developed specifically for the Internet community and explicitly requests discussion and suggestions for improvements. This has resulted in a robust support community, originally through the secsh Working Group and ongoing mailing list discussions, involving a wide array of academic and corporate contributors. While its focus is on technical evolution rather than sharing administrative results on national platforms, its open status fosters a global community of developers and researchers._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b725f671-7651-4436-a893-b62e64c400c0 .

camssa:48bb2477-1916-44c1-8f5a-48bd054c1722 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d2c939f8f97b2a02c254da4add5fcbea1311d465178344adc029d82366a0f642 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

