camssa:527abffa-6e7c-4660-8a73-c2fbe37f3da1 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH provides precise data type representations, standardised message formats, and assigned message numbers, which allow developers and auditors to verify that an implementation aligns with the architectural standard. However, because practical implementation is often dependent on the target environment, many systems provide their own tools for conformance and validation testing. For example, GitHub provides specific documentation and procedures for "Testing your SSH connection" to ensure that a user's local configuration and keys are correctly implemented and authenticated within their specific network and security infrastructure. This indicates that while the protocol defines the baseline, the final validation of conformance often occurs through system-specific testing platforms tailored to the operational environment._x000D_
_x000D_
Connecting to GitHub with SSH:_x000D_
https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/connecting-to-github-with-ssh_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fc0820ea-b547-4af5-b602-c1862d276056 .

camssa:57349d75-4a89-4d6f-9a59-bd20a2971256 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH provides the technical foundation for protecting data through strong encryption and integrity protection, which are essential components for securing the exchange of personal data. It mandates cryptographic host authentication to ensure that data is only shared with verified entities. However, as a low-level transport protocol, SSH does not define procedures for the management, classification, or long-term storage of personal data, nor does it explicitly reference specific European privacy regulations like the GDPR._x000D_
_x000D_
GDPR:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj/eng_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:86038970-7c8d-4773-9bd1-c9e8cfb9e9fc .

camssa:5b353037-7b1b-4085-bfa8-01b92bdab821 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'As an Internet standards track protocol, the SSH specification has been subject to rigorous and continuous assessment by the IETF (secsh Working Group) and the broader global security community. Its effectiveness is documented through the publication of updating RFCs (such as RFC 8308 and RFC 9142) and the systematic reporting of errata, which demonstrate an ongoing evaluation of its ability to reach its expected security goals. Furthermore, its status as the de facto standard for secure remote administration—evidenced by its universal assignment to TCP port 22—serves as a practical assessment of its effectiveness in real-world environments._x000D_
_x000D_
Secsh Working Group:_x000D_
https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/secsh/about/_x000D_
_x000D_
Extension Negotiation in the Secure Shell (SSH) Protocol (RFC 8308):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8308_x000D_
_x000D_
Key Exchange (KEX) Method Updates and Recommendations for Secure Shell (SSH) (RFC 9142):_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9142_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:695ca27d-bc44-4594-a38d-42ae399a8cd2 .

camssa:5be72260-66df-4fb1-b51e-b9dc1c160ce3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-bb5b5da7c1dc98a64c6a6f22f8fc539a8f80702f896697e985dd2c06d4ab68aa ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:5f39afab-07c8-4c73-9e87-e7238943540c a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d9b9ce1d270550422a8ea6097d2ffa1d923267fd681c56280e3b7810a14a580a ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:614ae18f-da63-4518-a6f5-69c438d2e096 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH demonstrates extensive market acceptance, evidenced by the fact that TCP/IP port 22 is officially and universally assigned for SSH services. To ensure global interoperability, the specification mandates that all implementations must support a minimal set of required algorithms, which has led to its inclusion in virtually all modern network operating systems._x000D_
_x000D_
TCP/IP port 22 reference (iOS):_x000D_
https://support.apple.com/en-us/103229_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:11e1f2c9-a8f4-4424-9e9f-9cd6fcb6bdf2 .

camssa:62f44091-7c87-42ce-8ccf-5dbf82fb7cbb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is platform agnostic, intended to be portable across different environments. It achieves this by defining standardised message formats, data types (like uint32 and string), and terminal modes that allow some degree of independence of specific hardware or operating systems._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:146353fc-b39f-4936-bb4b-7424dd646974 .

camssa:695ca27d-bc44-4594-a38d-42ae399a8cd2 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6a65b100-4afc-4554-9e1a-0efa610b3f08 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:71afc2bf-6e3c-4bfd-bc47-4f510e982606 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is defined as a secure remote login and low-level transport protocol designed for encrypted communication over insecure networks, this criterion is therefore not applicable._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:83e16490-f49a-4ce5-926e-4ebc3c7bba47 .

camssa:741b2328-bc8e-402a-8a1c-8c38a3c60357 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is defined as a secure remote login and low-level transport protocol designed for encrypted communication over insecure networks, this criterion is therefore not applicable._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5be72260-66df-4fb1-b51e-b9dc1c160ce3 .

camssa:79caa0a7-b1ec-45ce-9696-14a08463703e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH has already been added to the ELIS, specifically under EIRA Data Exchange Application Service and Component ABB._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-andspecifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611_x000D_
