camssa:ca2c5b1d-8a45-4617-a784-fd43c855f922 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'IETF has a formal review and approval so that all the relevant stakeholders can formally appeal or raise objections to the development and approval of specifications.
Each distinct version of an Internet standards-related specification is published as part of the "Request for Comments" (RFC) document series. This archival series is the official publication channel for Internet standards documents and other publications.
During the development of a specification, draft versions of the document are made available for informal review and comment by placing them in the IETF's "Internet-Drafts" directory, which is replicated on a number of Internet hosts. This makes an evolving working document readily available to a wide audience, facilitating the process of review and revision.

Standard process IETF:
https://www.ietf.org/standards/process/

Internet Best Current Practices IETF:
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2026'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a362a836-6d55-4ff5-8ee0-4a13e256a0a9 .

camssa:cdec074a-b1e7-4367-a039-1ad195eb1637 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SSH provides a secure "encrypted tunnel" for data transmission, its primary focus is on the transport rather than the processing of data, meaning that the protocol provides the means for the "remote execution of commands," but it assumes "end point security". In other words, while the data is protected while moving, the security of the actual processing on the remote host depends on local security policies and the server's environment rather than the protocol's internal mechanics._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:47bd1f3d-19d8-4c6f-acb3-a35462cdbe59 .

camssa:cefb1783-35a7-4cfb-b104-df92842f3ab0 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-ec3f8a897147f530040ab94fb9bbee9fdad56e7256b2ce6fbb63cf1465315d91 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:d3fd9b53-a23e-4dcb-bdf3-2db3b7fa7caf a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH explicitly includes assessments of its own efficiency, specifically regarding packet size and overhead. The specification provides a technical analysis of how the protocol's headers and Message Authentication Codes (MAC) affect data fields, concluding that the increase is "negligible" for standard Ethernet and TCP/IP packets. Additionally, the protocol is designed to minimize the number of round-trips required for key exchange and authentication, ensuring an efficient connection setup process even in high-latency environments._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:48bb2477-1916-44c1-8f5a-48bd054c1722 .

camssa:d406717f-b8e3-4b97-a8a2-f00e7b90a20c a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH allows for partial implementations due to its modular architecture, which is divided into three distinct layers: the Transport Layer Protocol, the User Authentication Protocol, and the Connection Protocol. For instance, a developer could implement the Transport Layer to provide a secure, encrypted pipe without necessarily implementing the multiplexing features of the Connection Protocol._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:cefb1783-35a7-4cfb-b104-df92842f3ab0 .

camssa:d75aa4ab-5eb5-4d17-9cff-d98c4e330124 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b37687b8bb3dbd4c6f96969358cf5d70900d1ccd01402cea7668da6303bec4b4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:dad0dbaa-71a4-4acf-99ec-e403892aa661 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH includes a dedicated User Authentication Protocol designed to authenticate clients to the server using multiple secure methods, including public key authentication, passwords, and host-based authentication. Furthermore, its architecture allows for the enforcement of local security policies, enabling administrations to restrict the specific operations a user is permitted to perform (such as limiting a user to file transfers while denying interactive shell access). These features, combined with negotiated confidentiality algorithms (e.g., AES), provide robust means for restricting access to data._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ea02ee60-ea9f-4622-b3f0-e31af8f05fa1 .

camssa:dfca2222-6ad7-49c8-bef5-4cceebd0acd2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is included in the ENISA guidance as a reference example of a cryptographic protocol for secure communications. As this guidance supports European regulation and is accessible to all relevant entities, it serves as a European-level repository for technical security standards._x000D_
_x000D_
ENISA Technical implementation guidance on cybersecurity risk management measures:_x000D_
https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2025-06/ENISA_Technical_implementation_guidance_on_cybersecurity_risk_management_measures_version_1.0.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:1275dd99-3677-4e7b-baa2-a49aa9af0fcf .

camssa:e3c912a4-e025-4010-8553-b36a963a9320 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-c2d03f19521389763921ce9c758a3697caa22bed98c2c11c3b10344b11c468bb ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:e49fef25-b802-4bd8-91b1-38f19e325840 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is a highly mature specification with a stable, modular architecture divided into the Transport Layer, User Authentication, and Connection protocols. Originally published in its current form in 2006, it has undergone continuous evolution and hardening through multiple extensions and updates to ensure it remains effective against modern cryptographic threats._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6a65b100-4afc-4554-9e1a-0efa610b3f08 .

camssa:e4d1e541-33b5-4f84-b423-665871f358f3 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'While SSH is an internationally recognised standard, it is published by the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) as a Proposed Standard. According to the sources, European Standards are those specifically developed and published by organisations such as CEN, CENELEC, or ETSI for the European region._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a147ed8c-3d93-478b-ac5c-3b7d9153c16a .

camssa:ea02ee60-ea9f-4622-b3f0-e31af8f05fa1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:f04fd84a-af1f-4680-a585-22530b46b9ab a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is designed to provide technical security properties such as confidentiality and integrity. It does not define the organisational elements, such as Memorandums of Understanding (MoUs) or Service Level Agreements (SLAs), necessary to clarify and formalise relationships between public administrations as required for organisational interoperability._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b4a01603-3bdc-470b-b890-911d32a0bfb0 .

camssa:f63d077f-f03d-488d-afd0-6fffe11c08da a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is to establish technical security properties like confidentiality, integrity, and host authentication for network services. Its scope is restricted to the technical transport and connection layers and does not involve the design of user-facing interfaces. Consequently, the specification does not address e-accessibility requirements, such as those found in WCAG or WAI-ARIA, designed to ensure digital public services are accessible to persons with disabilities or the elderly._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d75aa4ab-5eb5-4d17-9cff-d98c4e330124 .

camssa:f86e0f5a-765b-4d0d-9331-d5d4507ad017 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:fc0820ea-b547-4af5-b602-c1862d276056 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:fd3d0734-7fc7-4aed-8a51-33c36a91c3b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH is defined as a secure remote login and low-level transport protocol designed for encrypted communication over insecure networks, this criterion is therefore not applicable._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:40146117-c800-4898-bcb9-2bfc7d3e5a81 .

camssa:fe3f0ede-309a-4d41-826c-dff2b4ec3494 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'SSH allows for extensive customisation through the negotiation of parameters. Implementations can be configured to support specific sets of encryption, integrity, and compression algorithms based on local security policies. Additionally, it provides a system for naming algorithms and methods that allows organizations to implement their own proprietary or experimental features without conflicting with the base protocol._x000D_
_x000D_
SSH Transport Layer:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4253.html_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:5f39afab-07c8-4c73-9e87-e7238943540c .

