camssa:00998345-79a7-474c-971b-7f1d6645539b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is technology agnostic, as it defines an abstract and extensible data model for expressing verifiable credentials without mandating a specific implementation technology, protocol, or infrastructure. Therefore, different cryptographic methods, proof formats, and transport mechanisms can be used._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e17c67a8-0e04-4318-982f-b99f45a40daa .

camssa:00ecc578-eebf-4df9-8cd0-420fccf305ce a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9694ffda6be83e507b6d3395cb411581d91419db0107726873a0a9018eab6a54 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0308645e-f659-4212-b26b-a890c199b582 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is not related with enable the long-term preservation of data/information/knowledge (electronic records included). Therefore, this criterion is not related to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:942f67a0-8d0c-4bee-ad02-36477bb58136 .

camssa:04e12ec0-d71e-4f85-a844-0b279076b5cb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-d520eae57650560dd54723cdcdd166243c9a0b1458a4afdc331175b5c1cada7e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:07aca5e1-1f9d-447c-b389-1665899b2df4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a60f86e868fe2bdcf0c5c47111455d1d5b59498172688e36f23a77baa347d916 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:07b561ac-30e4-4d65-8b5f-ad022f1c8793 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 can enable the exposure of interfaces if combined with other specifications. Therefore, additional specifications are required, such as OpenID for Verifiable Credential Issuance and OpenID for Verifiable Presentations._x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID for Verifiable Presentations Reference:_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-presentations-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
OpenID for Verifiable Credential Issuance Reference: v_x000D_
https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-credential-issuance-1_0.html_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f950e7f2-4a0d-4f00-ad80-c2aa9ce6bb21 .

camssa:0a016b77-a476-476b-b240-af047322fc97 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6184fb705cfed44856c7b9594b492926f7a63a128a5a2be7b896294d8c79838 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:0a8b663f-db05-4880-955f-a0c0891ec8d6 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 simplifies the delivery of European public services by providing a standard format for the digital representation of credentials that are secure, machine-verifiable, and privacy-preserving. Verifiable credentials can help simplify administrative procedures by allowing individuals to easily present trusted information about their identity, qualifications, residence, permits, or other personal circumstances. Public administrations and authorities can then automatically verify this information without relying on paper documents or repeated manual checks. This can make procedures faster and more efficient, while helping individuals gain access to public services, benefits, or administrative processes in a more secure and user-friendly way._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:96586193-40b1-4124-8dca-4836881e59f6 .

camssa:0e83f747-3eac-4c93-8f0a-b17d035f2bfb a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is not related to enable the e-accessibility. Therefore, this criterion is not related to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:82a485e9-262e-46f6-8837-a8fc9b759758 .

camssa:1430fbc7-b7b0-42bc-83ca-4b58e3a4a46b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a2e2820561158593079cf28230b73b9b7f1cb83da49b04d2317790e20c0c706f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:19c1358d-d76c-4060-ad62-a8c8cc09f56a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 supports interoperability and standard compliance by providing evaluations and validation tools for verifiable credentials. Several frameworks are available to test implementations against W3C requirements. For example, the W3C VC Test Suite, hosted on GitHub, provides automated Node.js tests to ensure that applications generate Verifiable Credentials compliant with the VC Data Model 1.0. Additionally, the EBSI VC Validator is a web-based tool that allows manual validation of Verifiable Credentials or Verifiable Presentations in JWT format by directly pasting the credential content._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/_x000D_
_x000D_
EBSI VC Validator Reference:_x000D_
https://hub.ebsi.eu/tools/vc-validator_x000D_
_x000D_
Verifiable Credentials conformance:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/#conformance_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Working Group Test Suite: _x000D_
https://github.com/w3c/vc-test-suite'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:69e4c63c-dd71-4f5b-bf1d-2867d1a4a5ef .

camssa:1dc4b148-9f9b-4962-b7d1-f06eaeb975cd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 allows partial implementations. This means that implementers can adopt only the components they need, such as specific proof types, credential features, or data structures, without having to support the full specification or ecosystem. Core mechanisms like selective disclosure or credential status checking are optional, not mandatory. Selective disclosure allows holders to reveal only parts of a credential, and credential status enables verification of revocation, but neither is required for a compliant implementation of VC DM._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C RDF Dataset Canonicalization Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-canon/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e55d6982-6a8c-4678-9a00-865f026dab6d .

camssa:200df19b-ac36-42ee-a5b0-2a4ae4bed1ad a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 is not recommended by any European Member State._x000D_
_x000D_
However, VC DM has several implementations at the US Home Security, California Driving Licenses, GS1, work done by the Government of Singapore. It will be used for the UNECE work on the supply chains and Digital Product Passports. _x000D_
_x000D_
Moreover, VC DM 2.0 is also used in the Spanish Cartera Digital for Age Verification, implying there is a broad adoption worldwide. In this project, VCDM 2.0 is recommended. Since this project is from the Ministry for Digital Transformation and Civil Service, the specification is indirectly recommended by Spain. See the comment in the Spanish Consolidated Legislation reference._x000D_
_x000D_
UNECE Digital Product Passport Reference:_x000D_
https://untp.unece.org/docs/0.6.0/specification/DigitalProductPassport/#:~:text=All%20DPPs%20are%20issued%20as%20W3C%20Verifiable%20Credentials%20and%20MUST%20conform%20to%20the%20VCDM%202%2E0%2E_x000D_
_x000D_
Age verification system for access to online content Reference:_x000D_
https://digital.gob.es/content/dam/portal-mtdfp/especificaciones-t%C3%A9cnicas/2024-06-30_Protocolo_de_verificacion_de_edad-v1_0eng.pdf.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
Spanish Consolidated Legislation: _x000D_
https://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-2023-16284'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:00ecc578-eebf-4df9-8cd0-420fccf305ce .

camssa:21d34aa5-b6f0-4a4d-b01b-a76af6928df1 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
