    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2769e6db-d180-4860-82b7-8e88c288f7fb a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-497a81dae06c1d53b4cfe96c1f998f6f65d46354d68a83d29a2950c984fc1166 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:29d000b3-8906-4087-aeba-ffaa3430a77d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 ensures the protection of personal data by giving individuals control over their credentials, allowing them to decide when and with whom to share information. _x000D_
_x000D_
Selective disclosure further enhances privacy by transmitting only the specific information required for a transaction, so public administrations cannot access sensitive or unnecessary personal data, supporting both data minimisation and privacy-preserving interactions._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/#privacy-considerations'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d7606fa3-349a-4644-ab3b-2de1e0adafb7 .

camssa:2c17647f-8788-486d-a806-6332410cee87 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9420538a5a92af199b492414dd056ab7134e456f005895261b1a5b15a3f2814e ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:2e91a0a5-2d79-4771-9db4-4aa38c48657a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 ensures data processing accuracy by making credentials tamper-evident: since they are digitally signed, any alteration after issuance is detectable, so the data remains exactly as the issuer intended._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:71b9d764-0f9a-4a20-a141-52a25f7d1f3a .

camssa:36ca6a35-89b7-4657-81d2-27446ab3d428 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 facilitates aspects of business process modelling by providing a standardised way to represent, share, and verify credentials across different systems and organisations._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6f46f094-8fb7-45fe-a82b-397031b8c72b .

camssa:3827812f-a6cf-4fc2-9991-b274ae33da1f a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-f53dee88cf8529a93a68be781005e903c270057da1a72e2f89e8cb154be0c51b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:39a41a31-99ac-4321-ab68-92c1f5c9fa0e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 allows credential holders to control which information is shared through a mechanism called Selective Disclosure. This means holders can reveal only specific claims from a credential without exposing the entire content, enhancing privacy and data minimisation. _x000D_
_x000D_
In addition, verifiable credentials rely on cryptographic mechanisms and digital signatures, which ensure the integrity, authenticity, and tamper-evidence of the credential. Together, these mechanisms make credentials trustworthy while allowing holders to retain control over their personal data._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:98c2d738-f534-4dc4-aed3-7b26e7c894b6 .

camssa:3b3d89ad-18b8-41c3-8a3d-4453a16d5b20 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 enables the secure exchange of data by defining a framework for credentials that can be cryptographically verified. Credentials can be digitally signed using proof mechanisms such as Verifiable Credentials Data Integrity (VCDI) or JSON Web Signature (JWS), allowing receiving parties to verify the authenticity and integrity of the data._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credential Data Integrity reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-integrity/_x000D_
_x000D_
JSON Web Signature Reference:_x000D_
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7515.html'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:21d34aa5-b6f0-4a4d-b01b-a76af6928df1 .

camssa:3c89f282-f012-468e-babb-6a13fe739215 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The W3C Royalty-Free IPR licenses granted under the W3C Patent Policy apply to all W3C specifications, including this specification.

W3C Patent practice:
https://www.w3.org/TR/patent-practice#ref-AC'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7523c364-8588-4101-9840-10b8b3fe2360 .

camssa:3ef90edd-2d73-4ec5-a1ae-3972d709760b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 guarantees the authenticity and authentication of roles involved in data transactions by enabling credentials and presentations to include cryptographic proofs. These proofs allow verifiers to confirm the identity of the issuer and verify that the data has not been altered._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:fb91ec4b-5330-4464-beaf-5fcccb526de3 .

camssa:3fef4d31-08a1-4176-aaa5-99ba7588505f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is not yet included in European repositories or catalogues of standards. However, VC DM 1.1 is referenced in the Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation in the area of electronic identification and trust services, including electronic signatures._x000D_
_x000D_
Since VC DM 2.0 is the direct successor of VC DM 1.1 and remains compatible with it, this reference can also be considered indirectly relevant to VC DM 2.0. In practice, some systems, such as the EUDI Wallet OOTS PoC, still use VC DM 1.1, and the transition to VC DM 2.0 is expected to occur because both versions are backward compatible when the newer features of VC DM 2.0 are not used._x000D_
_x000D_
Rolling Plan for ICT Standardisation: _x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/custom-page/attachment/2025-04/RollingPlan_ICT_2025.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6310e08d-9cd3-4ff1-a475-0839fa99d7f4 .

camssa:4388cb91-23fa-4291-ab97-eb350959ba86 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0b122f4f42ca2089ee158a31d932d6a0332aa3a4d04acce1e2e7aa140815a0ec ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:4488af8f-6169-4d0b-ac85-79cccb063a66 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard. Also, a clear Release Notes tracking the changes of the different versions is archived.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:04e12ec0-d71e-4f85-a844-0b279076b5cb .

camssa:4580bfab-6ae5-41b5-b2fe-35a8184c6137 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-812668363d8f0cc562041fae6c588e1555372bf0bf5c16835be996dd72070013 ;
    cav:value "20"^^xsd:string .

camssa:49344523-0581-4f90-b071-c66bc4ca00ff a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 has not been included within the catalogue of any Member State._x000D_
_x000D_
CAMSS List of Standards:_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/camss-list-standards_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4580bfab-6ae5-41b5-b2fe-35a8184c6137 .

camssa:4dbfe407-92c9-45d9-9ecd-b05446f51661 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is developed by W3C, a standard development organisation based in the US. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to this specification._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Organisation Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/about/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2637f97d-4fbc-4c60-9539-614a388fdcad .

camssa:4e805a28-8d61-4df3-a630-dd3994dc3563 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-fb2c0a4ddb03b09ecd5450c5a1d6aeed4e51c2a0387709a95a89cd850a7dd180 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:55961d40-5f43-4895-99a3-9079ba289a0d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 supports secure management of credentials by enabling holders to store them in protected repositories, such as digital wallets, which limits exposure and reduces the risk of unauthorised access or tampering._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:eb2d2b78-58f5-4656-8b7f-78c5becfdd48 .

camssa:559a40dd-5340-47b0-9bd0-ade202664e61 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 allows customisation. Developers can define custom properties using JSON-LD. The specification provides extension points for essential features (credential status, data schemas, proofs, refreshing, terms of use, evidence) and reserved points for experimental properties (e.g., confidenceMethod, renderMethod). This flexibility allows verifiers to apply their own business rules and ensures credentials can be adapted for specific use cases while remaining interoperable._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:e5f09355-895f-462a-93fe-ac40aa766b59 .

camssa:5656ee04-2705-44c1-9e3d-44a3f99eef91 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is maintained by the W3C Verifiable Credentials Working Group. This group is responsible for developing, maintaining, and updating the specification and its related standards within the Verifiable Credentials family. VC DM 2.0 was officially published as a W3C Recommendation on 15 May 2025 and is intended to be used for new implementations, while VC DM 1.1 remains valid mainly for existing deployments._x000D_
_x000D_
VC DM 2.0 is also within the EU Digital Identity Wallet standards and technical specifications repository, where addresses the adoption of VC DM 2.0 and its relationship with VC DM 1.1. The repository notes that VC DM 2.0 is fully backwards compatible with VC DM 1.1 provided that the new features introduced in v2.0 are not used_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Organisation Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/_x000D_
_x000D_
Verifiable Credentials WG Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/groups/wg/vc/_x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Github reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-doc-standards-and-technical-specifications/issues/115 _x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:4e805a28-8d61-4df3-a630-dd3994dc3563 .

camssa:579d8598-7f2d-45fa-a442-e65a7d308a94 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        dcat:Distribution ;
