camssa:6594b85c-c8ba-48ad-80fd-2898c158d72e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM defines a data model for verifiable credentials and their exchange. It does not address the facilitation of the publication of data on the web. Therefore, this criterion is not applicable to the specification._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:b954993e-35bd-4714-9c57-321d4c671b16 .

camssa:67b84fff-066a-4dd7-8326-2115e51828f5 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is designed to be domain-neutral, enabling its use across diverse sectors. It can be used to represent and express digital credentials from different domains, such as identity, education, health, transport, finance, and professional qualifications. This flexibility ensures interoperability across ecosystems and supports broad adoption beyond any one specific use case or industry._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:6331dd68-1e39-409e-b046-b07518e26b8d .

camssa:67c2eded-2184-47df-af21-cac7e2ffb7e9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 has been selected and adopted in multiple large-scale and cross-border initiatives. It is used by organisations such as the US Department of Homeland Security, in California digital driving licences, by GS1, and in projects led by the Government of Singapore. It is also being applied in initiatives of the United Nations Economic Commission for Europe related to supply chains, traceability, and Digital Product Passports._x000D_
_x000D_
In the context of UNECE, VC DM provides a secure and machine-verifiable way to represent digital credentials about products, facilities, organisations, certifications, and traceability events. This allows trusted information to be exchanged across different actors and systems without relying on paper documents or isolated databases. For example, a Digital Product Passport can include verifiable information about a product’s origin, materials, environmental impact, repairability, recycling characteristics, and compliance with sustainability or regulatory requirements. This supports transparency, due diligence, and regulatory compliance across complex international supply chains._x000D_
_x000D_
UNECE UN Transparency Protocol Reference:_x000D_
https://untp.unece.org/docs/about/Goals_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:0a016b77-a476-476b-b240-af047322fc97 .

camssa:69e4c63c-dd71-4f5b-bf1d-2867d1a4a5ef a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-a6fa642bc8eceff2b1d333dc1123748399264c028fde2fd78308f0a0209ae21b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6a9027f9-d93b-4fc4-9550-eeb2ed22ee7e a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is widely used in public and private sector initiatives and is one of the main specifications used within the European Digital Identity Wallet ecosystem. In this context, verifiable credentials are used to represent digital attestations, such as identity data, educational qualifications, health information, and driving licences, which can be securely stored and presented by the user._x000D_
_x000D_
Within the EUDI Wallet, VC DM enables issuers to provide digitally signed credentials and allows holders to selectively disclose only the information required for a specific transaction._x000D_
_x000D_
VC DM 1.1 is expected to be progressively replaced by VC DM 2.0, as the newer version provides improved security, privacy, and support for selective disclosure and zero-knowledge proof mechanisms._x000D_
_x000D_
VC DM is also used in initiatives such as the United States Department of Homeland Security, California mobile driving licences, GS1, the Government of Singapore, Digital Product Passports, and supply chain traceability projects._x000D_
_x000D_
In the Spanish Cartera Digital age verification initiative, VC DM is used to allow users to prove that they are of legal age without providing information that would allow their identification or tracking on the Internet. Content platforms are only allowed to obtain the minimum information necessary to verify that the user is above the required age threshold, following the principle of data minimisation._x000D_
_x000D_
The system is based on verifiable credentials securely stored in a digital wallet. Instead of sharing a full identity document or exact date of birth, the user presents a cryptographic proof that they are over 18. This proof can be verified by the platform without revealing additional personal information._x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet Reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.2.0/architecture-and-reference-framework-main/#534-w3c-verifiable-credentials_x000D_
_x000D_
UNECE Digital Product Passport Reference:_x000D_
https://untp.unece.org/docs/0.6.0/specification/DigitalProductPassport/#:~:text=All%20DPPs%20are%20issued%20as%20W3C%20Verifiable%20Credentials%20and%20MUST%20conform%20to%20the%20VCDM%202%2E0%2E_x000D_
_x000D_
Age verification system for access to online content Reference:_x000D_
https://digital.gob.es/content/dam/portal-mtdfp/especificaciones-t%C3%A9cnicas/2024-06-30_Protocolo_de_verificacion_de_edad-v1_0eng.pdf.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:07aca5e1-1f9d-447c-b389-1665899b2df4 .

camssa:6f46f094-8fb7-45fe-a82b-397031b8c72b a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-22c3c5b40201f4ab2cb64a2d34b7665f8d0d1562f2a3e1a493dd3312608c7537 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:6fe24b62-c49f-4277-8440-95ed4b06ba7f a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is designed to use JSON-LD, which enhances data portability by combining the widely adopted JSON format with linked data semantics. This allows credential information to be consistently shared, interpreted, and understood across diverse and heterogeneous systems._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0  reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ab51ec2c-4c3c-4fd1-8353-ceb8ded8daf3 .

camssa:71b9d764-0f9a-4a20-a141-52a25f7d1f3a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-9b3cb1ef128e2a87386258a5812c05b520024e6e4a404d1f1d6f0e35707e8a7b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:721e109a-bd08-44e0-8eb1-edf3f4250f94 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is used in the Spanish Cartera Digital age verification initiative, where verifiable credentials allow users to prove that they are above the required age threshold without revealing unnecessary personal information. Through selective disclosure and privacy-preserving cryptographic mechanisms, only the minimum information required for the transaction is shared, reducing the risk of profiling, tracking, or unnecessary disclosure of personal data. This reflects the privacy principles established in Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2979, which promotes user control, confidentiality, and data minimisation in European Digital Identity Wallets, ensuring that users remain in control of their credentials and can decide which information to share. _x000D_
_x000D_
Moreover, VC DM 2.0 will also be used in the work of the United Nations Economic Commission for Europe on supply chains and Digital Product Passports. In this context, verifiable credentials can be used to represent trusted information about products, such as origin, sustainability, conformity, repairability, and traceability. Privacy is also relevant in these scenarios, as only the necessary information about a product, supplier, or supply chain step may be disclosed, while commercially sensitive or confidential information can remain protected. This helps ensure transparency and traceability without exposing unnecessary business data._x000D_
_x000D_
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2979 Reference:_x000D_
https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2024/2979/oj/eng_x000D_
_x000D_
UNECE Digital Product Passport Reference:_x000D_
https://untp.unece.org/docs/0.6.0/specification/DigitalProductPassport/#:~:text=All%20DPPs%20are%20issued%20as%20W3C%20Verifiable%20Credentials%20and%20MUST%20conform%20to%20the%20VCDM%202%2E0%2E_x000D_
_x000D_
Age verification system for access to online content Reference:_x000D_
https://digital.gob.es/content/dam/portal-mtdfp/especificaciones-t%C3%A9cnicas/2024-06-30_Protocolo_de_verificacion_de_edad-v1_0eng.pdf.pdf_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2769e6db-d180-4860-82b7-8e88c288f7fb .

