camssa:85093e44-a70a-4d27-8fa0-0c8eaa50a560 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is platform-agnostic and can be implemented across different systems and infrastructures without dependence on a specific platform._x000D_
_x000D_
VC DM can be represented using both plain JSON and JSON-LD. Through the use of JSON-LD, it allows different systems to interpret credential data in the same way, even when credentials are issued by different organisations or sectors. This is particularly useful in cross-border and cross-domain environments, such as the EUDI Wallet, ensuring a structured and interoperable data exchange, but introducing complexity._x000D_
_x000D_
EUDI Wallet JSON-LD Reference:_x000D_
https://eudi.dev/2.8.0/architecture-and-reference-framework-main/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:2c17647f-8788-486d-a806-6332410cee87 .

camssa:885900ab-15fd-473f-aded-b2e0bba218b4 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-847f0d7b5b56f9491b75fadd87efa1d6bdb112bcbb660d2ec7b6d786d403360f ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:885bbd94-1d92-4074-a739-9e23dd973db9 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is already associated to EIRA ABBs in the EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS). More specifically, VC DM can define the interoperability aspects of the "Data Model", "Open Data"  ABBs of the EIRA Semantic View and "Data Exchange" and "Integrity Verification" ABBs of the EIRA Technical Application Views._x000D_
_x000D_
EIRA Library of Interoperability Specifications (ELIS):_x000D_
https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss/solution/elis/release/611'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:7d4e1e4e-cc60-426f-9dcc-a37dce7b9cf0 .

camssa:918ef0c7-7809-4ba2-955a-552b4d288ddd a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 facilitates organisational interoperability by providing a common and standardised way to issue, share, and verify credentials across different systems and organisations. This helps organisations establish trust, reduce administrative work, and support interoperability across sectors and borders. For example, a university can issue a digital diploma that an employer or public authority can easily verify and accept as proof of qualification._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d176fde2-e3dd-4d82-8612-fa8fdae89f76 .

camssa:939a5134-f1db-472c-ba59-25b306a1b2ed a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 enables digital service delivery channels and supports digitalisation and administrative simplification. Government-issued identity documents, such as national ID cards, can be represented as verifiable credentials, allowing them to be securely managed, presented, and verified while the individual remains in control of their personal data._x000D_
_x000D_
It can also simplify manual procedures by replacing paper-based or document-based processes with trusted digital channels. For example, a driving licence can be presented as a verifiable credential instead of requiring the user to upload or send a scanned PDF. The receiving authority can then verify the authenticity and validity of the credential directly, reducing manual checks, fraud risks, and administrative burden._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:f8f5dd51-4ebe-4d61-94f9-e7565c344f9b .

camssa:942f67a0-8d0c-4bee-ad02-36477bb58136 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-245e5eb8db3a19aebfdf9ccc2c2ac0467bebccc76339696f519452e8bbd393ad ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:94eb6712-d1f4-4352-b6fd-9a6b52d1f90a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 enables the visibility and comprehensibility of public administrations data and services. This is achieved with VCDM because it standardises how credentials are expressed in a machine-readable format (typically JSON-LD) and how they include cryptographic proofs, enabling independent verification of their authenticity._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C JSON-LD Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:d02e3c7b-1090-4f20-988a-2ea2b7bbe107 .

camssa:96586193-40b1-4124-8dca-4836881e59f6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-e225f44a0b0939b1b30a1ab03b2f38baeca8699c0cd44b4e39adbe19ffbb3542 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:98c2d738-f534-4dc4-aed3-7b26e7c894b6 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-29023937877d658f898d48a06b2648e283306a041137cc58af4f79f061e1de4b ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a0e53bdf-6f25-40ed-8c91-150484af4a04 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The effectiveness of VC DM 2.0 has been assessed through practical implementations, pilot projects, academic studies, and community feedback. In the study “Towards a Standardized Model for Privacy-Preserving Verifiable Credentials,” researchers concluded that Verifiable Credentials can be enhanced to support privacy-preserving features, such as predicates and selective disclosure mechanisms. The study also provided guidance and validation tools to adapt these mechanisms to the VC Data Model and demonstrated their applicability through a proof-of-concept implementation, highlighting the potential for secure and privacy-aware credential exchange across diverse use cases._x000D_
_x000D_
Towards a standardized model for privacy-preserving Verifiable Credentials Reference:_x000D_
https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3465481.3469204_x000D_
_x000D_
Verifiable Credentials Use Cases: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-use-cases_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a4ff08d9-67ac-4ff3-9417-6b3f020d7eb3 .

camssa:a4ff08d9-67ac-4ff3-9417-6b3f020d7eb3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-0e9bb259b84413d890a0fd548e40f255bb983a3add2eb7a737283f711e23d523 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a584578a-8177-421b-a23e-7bb0c391e97a a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-5a7323988b5d96da801e2abd4d95248af758fe9adbbafd09dd76114629567ff4 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:a5972762-cfd1-46a6-80eb-f040c877675d a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM is designed to be extensible. Implementers can define additional credential types, claims, and vocabularies through JSON-LD contexts, which allow external vocabularies to be referenced. This enables new properties and credential types to be introduced without modifying the core data model._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C JSON-LD 1.1 reference: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11/#the-context'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:25685c49-695c-49e3-8aa2-1674aac38135 .

camssa:a7e9248b-82d3-4c4f-89fe-5e9308cce9b2 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 with JSON-LD organises credential data into clear, semantically defined properties, which improves readability, interoperability, and machine processing. Therefore, it fosters the visibility and comprehensibility of public administrations data and services_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C JSON-LD Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11/_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ad118641-a66e-4867-a190-2bcb2b56b691 .

camssa:ab51ec2c-4c3c-4fd1-8353-ceb8ded8daf3 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b71e04068a444f6ee23c0863df43f19957762528381d6edece40e35c0efab242 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:ad118641-a66e-4867-a190-2bcb2b56b691 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-7d12b846c487e7201dbcf395866b5abc0bb5fa040b1f519127b6a5f56d447257 ;
    cav:value "80"^^xsd:string .

camssa:b3d21ec7-66af-492c-b1db-e36e0ee3f90b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 is discussed across both specialised forums and general developer platforms such as Stack Overflow, LinkedIn and many more. The questions about implementation, security discussions, and best-practice exchanges demonstrates active adoption and continuous community participation_x000D_
_x000D_
LinkedIn Reference:_x000D_
https://www.linkedin.com/posts/pierregronlier_w3c-verifiable-credentials-20-specifications-activity-7329031162352332800-ZlJy/?skipRedirect=true_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack Overflow Reference:_x000D_
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/58882523/decentralised-identity-management/58883753#58883753_x000D_
_x000D_
Stack Exchange Network Reference:_x000D_
https://security.stackexchange.com/questions/263367/can-my-name-be-revealed-from-a-stolen-verifiable-credential/266361#266361_x000D_
_x000D_
eu-digital-identity-wallet / eudi-doc-standards-and-technical-specifications Github Reference:_x000D_
https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-doc-standards-and-technical-specifications/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20VCDM_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 Reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:885900ab-15fd-473f-aded-b2e0bba218b4 .

camssa:b954993e-35bd-4714-9c57-321d4c671b16 a cav:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:assignedTo sc:c-b433a6dd6682476829a60de6a4fb771395c4baf637aa496ba6bca9bd6766d933 ;
    cav:value "100"^^xsd:string .

camssa:bd676112-f8df-4709-938c-ba17617d2982 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'W3C has a defined and publicly available Process for the Development and approval process of the specification as a recommended standard, including a public review.

W3C Process document:
https://www.w3.org/2018/Process-20180201/#Policies'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:81406a82-c752-4adf-bacf-ae6b85d25054 .

camssa:bfa7c8c9-8060-4a0d-9889-b7a7311aec7a a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'The efficiency of VC DM 2.0 has been assessed by researchers from different academic institutions. In the “Certifying Provenance of Scientific Datasets with Self-sovereign Identity and Verifiable Credentials” study, it is concluded that Verifiable Credentials can provide a secure and efficient way to certify the provenance and authenticity of scientific datasets. The study also highlights that Verifiable Credentials can improve trust, scalability, and the verification of data quality across different environments and use cases._x000D_
_x000D_
Certifying Provenance of Scientific Datasets with Self-sovereign Identity and Verifiable Credentials Reference:_x000D_
https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.02796_x000D_
_x000D_
Verifiable Credentials Use Cases: _x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-use-cases_x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:22c06a02-fe33-49d5-85be-54c4cac87a4a .

camssa:c3154b0c-03ec-4d7d-b18e-efa827ac8b8b a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VC DM 2.0 can be used in a multilingual context as it supports expressing data in different languages and scripts, encouraging the use of standardised language tags and direction metadata to ensure correct interpretation. It also enables multiple language representations for the same data element (e.g. via language-tagged values or arrays), enhancing flexibility and interoperability across systems and formats._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:ef022754-a461-4956-b540-9c25527a5e59 .

camssa:ca214045-dae2-4c91-aa41-aa32ad344374 a cav:Statement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    cav:judgement """'VCDM 2.0 protects information against unauthorised changes through cryptographic signatures. When a credential is issued, it is digitally signed by the issuer, so any modification to the credential after issuance can be detected._x000D_
_x000D_
W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 reference:_x000D_
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0'"""@en ;
    cav:refersTo camssa:a584578a-8177-421b-a23e-7bb0c391e97a .

